window.TARL = window.TARL || {};
TARL.literacy = {"meta":{"name":"TARL Literacy","levels":["Beginner","Letter","Word","Para","Story"],"duration":70,"dailyStructure":[["Warm-up (games, rhymes)","5 min","Whole class"],["Oral discussion","10 min","Whole class"],["Story (read, discuss, retell, drama on Saturday)","20 min","Whole class, small groups, individual"],["Sound-symbol games / Barakhadi / language games","10 min","Whole class, small groups"],["Mind mapping (Day 1) / Self-writing (Day 2)","15 min","Whole class, small groups, individual"],["Daily reading with a library book","10 min","Individual"]],"assessmentSteps":[["Start","Begin from the paragraph. The learner reads the paragraph fluently, as sentences and not word by word."],["Para level","If the learner reads three sentences correctly and fluently, ask them to read the story."],["Story level","If the learner reads the story fluently with correct punctuation and expression for at least five consecutive lines, mark the Story level. Bonus: ask two questions about the story; mark Y if both are answered correctly, otherwise N."],["Word level","If the learner cannot read three sentences correctly and fluently in the paragraph, ask them to read words: any 5 of the 10 words; at least 4 must be correct. Then ask them to read the paragraph again; if they still cannot read it after the second attempt, mark the Word level."],["Letter level","If the learner cannot read at least 4 words, ask them to identify any 5 of the 10 letters; at least 4 must be correct. Mark the Letter level."],["Beginner level","If the learner cannot identify at least 4 letters, mark the Beginner level."]],"toolLetters":"c, j, x, n, p, u, s, o, k, h","toolWords":"run, book, cat, tall, fan, jump, cup, rope, bag, nice","samples":[{"n":1,"story":"Rohit lived in a small village. He lived with his mother. His brother Ajay lived in a city. Rohit was happy when Ajay came home. They played games and had fun. Their mother made them lots of food. Rohit was sad when Ajay left. He told Ajay to come back soon. His mother was sad too.","questions":["Where did Rohit live?","How did Rohit feel when Ajay came home?"],"paras":["Rani is a tall girl. She loves to drink milk. Rani likes to run fast. She runs to school every day.","Aamir has a big dog. The dog is called Raja. They play every day. They like to play outside."]},{"n":2,"story":"On Monday, Alia was very happy. She went to school for the first time. She had a new school bag for her books. She put a red flower on the bag. Alia went to school with her sister. Their mother also went with them. The school was not far from their house. Alia made many new friends in school.","questions":["Who went to school with Alia?","Can you tell me why Alia was happy on Monday?"],"paras":["Ramu has a new ball. His father gave him the ball. Ramu plays with it every day. He loves his new ball.","Aamir has a big dog. The dog is called Raja. They play every day. They like to play outside."]},{"n":3,"story":"One day, Samir was in school. He saw some old books on a table. Samir picked up a big book. The book had many stories. Samir took it home to show his mother. He read the book with his mother. His mother was very happy. Samir was happy too. Then Samir took the book back to school.","questions":["Where did Samir find the old books?","Why was Samir's mother happy?"],"paras":["Sana lives in a village. Her home is near a river. Gita likes to swim. Her sister swims with her.","Anil loves to eat sweets. He buys sweets from the shop. Anil gives some to his friends. They also like eating sweets."]},{"n":4,"story":"Nina was a little girl. She lived near a big garden. One day, she went to the garden. She saw a man selling flowers. Nina asked him for a flower. The man gave her two big red flowers. Then Nina ran back to her home. She gave the flowers to her mother. They both felt very happy.","questions":["Where did Nina go one day?","Can you tell me what Nina gave to her mother?"],"paras":["Amit lives with his mother. He wakes up very early. He helps his mother cook food. Then he goes to school.","Abdul loves to play cricket. He goes to the big park. He meets his friends there. They play cricket in the park."]}],"gaps":["The manual does not contain a 90-day schedule, a 45-day phase split, or day-by-day lesson plans. It gives the method, the daily timetable, the activity descriptions and the order in which new topics should be introduced. The day-by-day order in these plans is a professional interpretation of that material and is marked as such.","The manual describes one assessment tool (used before teaching starts) and four sample test sets. It does not give a separate midline or endline procedure, scoring or timing. These plans reuse the same tool for the midline and endline; which sample set is used for which checkpoint is an interpretation (baseline: Sample 1, midline: Sample 2, endline: Sample 3, Sample 4 spare).","The manual does not give a materials list; the TLM in each plan are the materials the manual names in the activity descriptions (stick bundles, number table, number cards, Barakhadi / alphabet or phonics chart, picture cards, story books, textbooks, library books).","The manual does not state which weekday the programme starts on. These plans assume six teaching days a week with Saturday as the drama day.","The manual does not name specific stories. The plans suggest a story theme for each story pair; use any suitable story from the school library or textbook.","The manual describes writing by level only (draw and write, words, sentences, paragraph or story). It does not describe separate pre-writing, pencil-grip or letter-formation stages, so none are invented; support for learners who reverse or confuse letters follows the manual's tracing advice.","The letter and word games (manual p.18-21) are not tied to a place in the daily timetable. They are placed in the 10-minute sound-symbol / alphabet slot and are marked as interpretation.","For Day 2 of a story, the manual gives tasks for Para and Story level and for word-level learners only; the Beginner and Letter level group tasks on that day are interpreted from the group-reading task and marked in the text.","Component times: the five timetable components of a literacy lesson (warm-up 5, oral discussion 10, story 20, sound symbol games 10, mind mapping or individual writing 15 = 60 minutes) are taken from manual p.7. The manual adds the 10-minute daily reading session as a note 'at the end of the reading class' and does not state one overall class length. These plans therefore show the daily reading as a sixth component with a total of 70 minutes. Please confirm with your training whether the 10 minutes fall inside or after the 60-minute class; the total is computed from the component times, so it changes automatically if you change them.","The manual gives the time of each component only. It does not split a component into big-group, small-group and individual minutes (for example the 20-minute Story session). The split shown for each activity inside a component is a suggested split (interpretation) and always adds up to the manual's component time.","The manual does not give different timings for different learning levels or days; the same timetable is used for all levels, and Saturday drama replaces the story activities inside the 20-minute Story component."],"prescribed":[["warmup","Warm-up activities",5,"p.7"],["oral","Oral Discussion",10,"p.7"],["story","Story",20,"p.7"],["sound","Sound symbol games, Sound separation-pairing",10,"p.7"],["mindwrite","Mind Mapping (Day 1) / Individual-Writing (Day 2)",15,"p.7"],["reading","Daily reading",10,"p.7 (note)"]],"checkpoints":{"baseline":{"name":"Baseline assessment","when":"Before Day 1","sample":1,"purpose":"Find out each learner's current level before teaching starts, then form level-wise groups (manual p.4, p.23). Assess each learner individually.","afterwards":"Form the groups for Day 1 and seat learners in a 'U' shape by level. Keep a daily progress record for each learner in a notebook."},"midline":{"name":"Midline assessment","when":"After Day 45 (before Day 46)","sample":2,"purpose":"Check each learner's level after Phase 1. The manual's only assessment tool is reused (see the note on gaps).","afterwards":"Re-group learners by their new levels and move learners who have improved to the next level group; Day 46 starts with regrouping."},"endline":{"name":"Endline assessment","when":"After Day 90","sample":3,"purpose":"Final check of each learner's level at the end of the programme using the same tool (see the note on gaps).","afterwards":"Compare each learner's final level with the baseline and the midline."}}},"days":[{"programme":"TARL Literacy","id":"lit-001","day":1,"phase":1,"phaseLabel":"Phase 1 (Days 1-45)","title":"Story: an animal friendship story (Day 1)","dayType":"Story Day 1 + Mind mapping","focus":"Hearing the different sounds in words (bed, run, zip) | Mind map: shop","duration":70,"objectives":["Listen, speak and answer in the oral conversation (conversation on a picture).","Listen to and read a story with understanding; discuss it in big and small groups and respond at their own level.","Develop sound-symbol skills: Hearing the different sounds in words (bed, run, zip).","Build vocabulary through a mind map ('shop') and use the words at their own level.","Read independently for 10 minutes every day."],"sequence":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Rain clapping","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Everyone stands in a circle with eyes closed and keeps clapping: first one finger, then two, three, four and finally five fingers. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Stand in a circle, close the eyes and clap with 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 fingers.","tlm":"After the activity ask: What did the sound remind you of?","source":"M","ref":"p.8","n":1},{"activity":"Oral conversation: conversation on a picture","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Show a picture of a busy village market and ask what is happening, who is doing what and what is happening around them. Let learners think creatively and even make up a story. In the initial days use the learners' home language so that they feel comfortable.","learners":"Look at the picture, answer questions and make up their own story about it.","tlm":"Picture card of a busy village market","source":"M","ref":"p.9","n":2},{"activity":"Story (Day 1 of the story): reading aloud and discussion","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":8,"teacher":"Discuss the title or picture of the story with the learners. Read the story aloud with expression and voice modulation (learners do not repeat after you). Discuss it, with emphasis on factual questions. Read it again slowly, pointing to each word.","learners":"Talk about the title/picture; listen; answer questions; follow each word with a finger in their own copy.","tlm":"A story from the school library (an animal friendship story), a copy for each learner","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":3},{"activity":"Story: reading in small groups","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":7,"teacher":"Form level-wise groups with a group leader. Learners read the story one sentence at a time while the others follow with their fingers. Para and Story level learners practise reading with emotion and expression.","learners":"Read the story sentence by sentence, supporting each other; the group leader helps.","tlm":"Story book copies","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":4},{"activity":"Story: level-wise individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":5,"teacher":"Give each learner the task for their level (see level table) and support those who need it.","learners":"Beginner/Letter: find and write favourite words or letters. Word: find consonant clusters. Para/Story: silently read, find unfamiliar and rhyming words.","tlm":"Story book, notebooks, board","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":5},{"activity":"Sound-symbol activity: oral sound awareness","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":4,"teacher":"Say 10-12 simple words aloud ('bed, run, zip, cat, pen, hot, sun, bag, dig, mud, top, net') and ask learners to identify the different sounds in them. This builds phonemic awareness.","learners":"Listen to each word and tell its sounds.","tlm":"None (oral activity)","source":"M","ref":"p.12","n":6},{"activity":"Sound-symbol games by level","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":6,"teacher":"Give each level group its game (see level table). Move among the groups and help those who need support; say each word clearly.","learners":"Play the game for their level in small groups.","tlm":"Board, chalk, letter cards","source":"M","ref":"p.12","n":7},{"activity":"Mind mapping (Day 1): the word 'shop'","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Ask: 'What words come to your mind when you hear the word shop?' Write learners' answers on the board or floor (Para and Story level learners write the words themselves). Guide the map towards the learning objective. Example words: shoes, pant, t-shirt, bangles, milk, sweets, rice, flour, sand, iron, cement, stone.","learners":"Say words connected with 'shop'; share the meaning and feeling of words.","tlm":"Board, chalk (or floor)","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":8},{"activity":"Mind mapping: classify the words","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":4,"teacher":"Ask learners to classify the words in groups, for example: Clothing: shoes, pant, t-shirt, bangles; Food: milk, sweets, rice, flour; House construction: sand, iron, cement, stone.","learners":"Sort the words into groups and say why.","tlm":"Board, chalk, word cards (optional)","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":9},{"activity":"Mind mapping: level-wise individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":6,"teacher":"Give each learner the individual task for their level; observe closely and give individual support. Display corrected stories on the wall.","learners":"Complete the task for their level (see level table).","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":10},{"activity":"Daily reading (10 minutes)","grouping":"Individual","minutes":10,"teacher":"Give each learner a library book or any storybook. Move around, listen to individual readers and note their level.","learners":"Read independently a book of their choice.","tlm":"Library books or storybooks","source":"M","ref":"p.7","n":11}],"procedures":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Rain clapping","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","steps":[{"teacher":"Stand the learners in a circle and ask them to close their eyes. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Stand in a circle and close their eyes."},{"teacher":"Start clapping with one finger; then two fingers, three, four and finally five fingers.","learners":"Keep clapping, copying the change of fingers."},{"teacher":"After the activity ask: What did the sound remind you of?","learners":"Tell how they felt and what the sounds reminded them of."}]},{"activity":"Oral conversation: conversation on a picture","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.9","steps":[{"teacher":"Show the picture of a busy village market.","learners":"Look carefully."},{"teacher":"Ask: What is happening in the picture? Who is doing what? What is happening around them? Then: What might happen next?","learners":"Answer in their own words; every learner gets a chance."},{"teacher":"Let learners imagine and make up a short story from the picture.","learners":"Tell their stories to the class."}]},{"activity":"Story - Day 1 (an animal friendship story)","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.10","steps":[{"teacher":"Discuss the title or picture of the story with the learners.","learners":"Talk about what they see and what the story may be about."},{"teacher":"Read the story aloud with expression and proper voice modulation. Learners should not simply repeat after you.","learners":"Listen carefully and enjoy the story."},{"teacher":"Discuss the story: factual, logical, vocabulary-based, judgment or opinion questions (today's focus: factual: Who was in the story? Where did it happen? What did the character do first?). Begin in the home language if needed.","learners":"Think and respond thoughtfully; every learner takes part."},{"teacher":"Read the story again slowly, pointing to each word. Make sure each learner has a copy and follows with a finger.","learners":"Follow each word with their finger."},{"teacher":"Ask learners to read in small groups; select a group leader who helps the others. Learners read one sentence at a time while the others point with fingers.","learners":"Read with the help of one another."}]},{"activity":"Sound-symbol: oral and level games","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.12","steps":[{"teacher":"Say 10-12 simple words aloud ('bed, run, zip, cat, pen, hot, sun, bag, dig, mud, top, net') and ask learners to identify the different sounds in them. This builds phonemic awareness.","learners":"Listen to each word and tell its sounds."},{"teacher":"Write the sounds or words for the day on the board and give each level group its task (see the level table).","learners":"Work in small groups and share their answers."},{"teacher":"Say each word clearly with distinct pronunciation. Give learners enough time to respond and think; use words learners commonly use at home (regional language and the medium of instruction).","learners":"Think, say and write the sounds."}]},{"activity":"Mind mapping: 'shop'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Small group (level-wise) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.14","steps":[{"teacher":"Choose a word that can generate many related words: 'shop'. Ask: 'What words come to your mind when you hear the word shop?' Write the answers on the board or floor.","learners":"Say words they link with 'shop'."},{"teacher":"Discuss the words: what they mean and how they are connected.","learners":"Explain their words and listen to others."},{"teacher":"In small groups, let the learners classify the words (Clothing: shoes, pant, t-shirt, bangles; Food: milk, sweets, rice, flour; House construction: sand, iron, cement, stone).","learners":"Sort the words into groups."},{"teacher":"Give the individual tasks by level and help each learner.","learners":"Work individually; read the work aloud at the end if time allows."}]}],"levelTasks":[{"activity":"Story - Day 1: individual tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.10","tasks":{"Beginner":"Circle or search for a favourite word or letter in the story and say it aloud. If a learner cannot draw a circle, write words on the board and ask them to identify them.","Letter":"Find, read and write favourite words from the story.","Word":"Find the consonant clusters in the story, read them and write them in the notebook.","Para":"Silently read the story from the textbook; find unfamiliar words and try to understand them; find rhyming words, use them in sentences and write in the notebook; ask other groups for meanings; make questions in groups.","Story":"Silently read the story; find unfamiliar words and rhyming words; practise reading with emotion; one group reads sentences formed with consonant clusters to the other group; ask and answer group questions (information, thinking and opinion questions)."}},{"activity":"Sound-symbol games by level (small groups)","source":"M","ref":"p.12","tasks":{"Beginner":"'What is the first sound in the word ball?' 'Is there a letter that makes the sound /b/?' 'Can you name objects that start with the letter B?' Learners think and share names in the group.","Letter":"Write the rhyming ending -at on the board and ask learners to add new letters to form words: c + at = cat, h + at = hat, m + at = mat.","Word":"Say a word and tell its sounds, for example 'sun' = /s/ + /u/ + /n/. Then tell what word is formed if /r/ is put before 'at': r + at = rat. Do 8-10 such combinations; at first learners may form meaningless words, later only meaningful words.","Para":"Write two or three sounds on the board (for example Br, cl, st) and let the learners form words that start with those sounds; this builds a word list for the learner.","Story":"Write two or three sounds on the board (for example Br, cl, st) and let the learners form words that start with those sounds; this builds a word list for the learner."}},{"activity":"Mind mapping 'shop': level tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.14","tasks":{"Beginner":"Circle all the words that contain the letter 'E' on the board; make a list. See how many learners find the most words.","Letter":"Circle all the words that contain the letter 'E' and make a list of them.","Word":"Use 4-5 words (for example iron, milk, pant, rice, sand) to form sentences, starting with words of one or two syllables. Example: Dream - I had a dream last night.","Para":"Choose any five words from the map and create a story with them. Use consonant clusters correctly, read the story aloud, correct mistakes of sentence structure, spelling or grammar, then display it on the wall.","Story":"Choose any five words from the map and create a story with them. Use consonant clusters correctly, read the story aloud, correct mistakes of sentence structure, spelling or grammar, then display it on the wall."}}],"organisation":[{"grouping":"Whole class (big group)","how":"All learners of all levels sit in a 'U' shape arranged by level (Beginner, Letter, Word, Para, Story) so that the move to small groups is easy.","activities":["Warm-up: Rain clapping","Oral conversation: conversation on a picture","Story (Day 1 of the story): reading aloud and discussion","Sound-symbol activity: oral sound awareness","Mind mapping (Day 1): the word 'shop'"]},{"grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","how":"Learners of similar levels work together; the teacher gives each group a task for its level and spends more time with learners who need support. Rotate responsibilities (for example group leader).","activities":["Story: reading in small groups","Sound-symbol games by level","Mind mapping: classify the words"]},{"grouping":"Individual","how":"Each learner works on a task for their own level; the teacher moves around, observes difficulties and supports individuals.","activities":["Story: level-wise individual tasks","Mind mapping: level-wise individual tasks","Daily reading (10 minutes)"]}],"materials":["After the activity ask: What did the sound remind you of?","Picture card of a busy village market","A story from the school library (an animal friendship story)","a copy for each learner","Story book copies","Story book","notebooks","board","Board","chalk","letter cards","chalk (or floor)","word cards (optional)","Notebooks","Library books or storybooks"],"outcomes":["Learners take part in the oral conversation and speak without fear.","Learners show understanding of the story in the discussion and complete the task for their level.","Learners respond to the sound-symbol task for today (Hearing the different sounds in words (bed, run, zip)) at their own level.","Learners add words to the mind map and use them in sentences or a story at their level.","Each learner reads a book for 10 minutes."],"observation":["Observe each learner's reading and writing during the individual tasks; note who needs individual support and how many learners share the same difficulty.","Note any learner whose level is improving; move the learner to the next level group when you see steady progress (manual p.5).","Record each learner's progress for the day in the notebook, according to the learner's level (manual p.4).","Use today's observations to adjust tomorrow's plan (manual p.5)."],"teacherNotes":["Story selection: the manual asks teachers to use picture story books or stories in the school library. Today's suggested theme (an animal friendship story) is a planning suggestion; use any suitable story you have.","Sound-symbol: for the first 4-5 days, play sound-based games with the learners at word level. Include the sounds learners find difficult when you prepare the Class Transaction Plan.","Mind mapping topic for this day: 'shop'. The manual's example uses the word 'shop'; today's topic follows the same method.","Before Day 1 the baseline assessment is done individually; its results decide the groups (manual p.4-5).","Pace: the manual says not to assume all learners progress at the same speed. Repeat a day's activity with the groups that need it before moving on.","Special needs: give extra time and prepare materials for slower learners; seat learners with hearing or vision difficulty at the front; for learners who reverse or confuse letters, trace letters on the letter card with a finger and write with dots to trace with a pencil (manual p.6)."],"components":[{"no":1,"key":"warmup","name":"Warm-up activities","keywords":["Rain clapping","two learners lead"],"rows":[1]},{"no":2,"key":"oral","name":"Oral Discussion","keywords":["conversation on a picture","every learner speaks","home language"],"rows":[2]},{"no":3,"key":"story","name":"Story","keywords":["Day 1","title / picture talk","read aloud with expression","factual questions","re-read pointing","group reading","level tasks"],"rows":[3,4,5]},{"no":4,"key":"sound","name":"Sound symbol games, Sound separation-pairing","keywords":["oral sound awareness","say the different sounds","level games in small groups"],"rows":[6,7]},{"no":5,"key":"mindwrite","name":"Mind Mapping (Day 1)","keywords":["mind map: shop","classify the words","level task: circle letter E / sentences / story"],"rows":[8,9,10]},{"no":6,"key":"reading","name":"Daily reading","keywords":["library book","read alone","teacher listens"],"rows":[11]}],"preLesson":"Before the timed lesson (not part of the lesson time): form level-wise groups from the baseline results, seat learners in a 'U' shape arranged by level, and set the ground rules (wait for your turn, work as a team, raise your hand). Manual p.4-6."},{"programme":"TARL Literacy","id":"lit-002","day":2,"phase":1,"phaseLabel":"Phase 1 (Days 1-45)","title":"Story: an animal friendship story (Day 2)","dayType":"Story Day 2 + Self-writing","focus":"Barakhadi / alphabet and phonics chart (line 3, letter 'm') | Self-writing: my favourite festival","duration":70,"objectives":["Listen, speak and answer in the oral conversation (listening and storytelling).","Retell the story, read it with expression, ask and answer questions about it and write answers.","Develop sound-symbol skills: Barakhadi / alphabet and phonics chart (line 3, letter 'm').","Write about a topic at their own level and review the writing (my favourite festival).","Read independently for 10 minutes every day."],"sequence":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Writing with body parts","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Learners stand in a circle. Demonstrate writing their names in the air with a finger, then ask them to write it with different body parts. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Write their names in the air with the finger, then with the head, shoulders, knees or elbows.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.8","n":1},{"activity":"Oral conversation: listening and storytelling","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Tell an interesting story starter and involve the learners: 'Yesterday I grabbed an elephant's tail and flew into the sky. What do you think happened next?' Let learners imagine and continue the story. In the initial days use the learners' home language so that they feel comfortable.","learners":"Listen to the teacher, then imagine and continue the story. Learners can also recite a rhyme or story they know.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.9","n":2},{"activity":"Story (Day 2 of the story): retelling","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":6,"teacher":"Ask learners to retell yesterday's story in their own words. Prompt with questions on the beginning, middle and end.","learners":"Retell the story using their own words.","tlm":"The same story book as yesterday","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":3},{"activity":"Story: reading with actions and group questions","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":9,"teacher":"Learners practise reading with actions and expressions; one learner per group reads aloud to the class. Guide groups to make questions about the story (guide initially). Groups take turns to ask and answer each other's questions. Word-level learners also read aloud the consonants learned on the first day.","learners":"Read with actions; make questions (word-level learners help write them); ask and answer questions with another group.","tlm":"Story book, slate or paper for questions","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":4},{"activity":"Story: writing answers individually","grouping":"Individual","minutes":5,"teacher":"Para and Story level learners write answers to all questions individually; read and correct their responses after they finish.","learners":"Write the answers in their notebooks; Beginner/Letter/Word learners read or listen and answer orally.","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":5},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart: big group reading","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":3,"teacher":"Show the Barakhadi chart and ask which letter they like. Read the letter 'm' on the chart; learners listen carefully and point to it on their own chart (they do not repeat after you).","learners":"Listen and point to the letter on their own chart.","tlm":"Barakhadi chart, alphabet or phonics chart","source":"M","ref":"p.13","n":6},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart: small-group practice","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Learners practise reading the alphabet or phonics chart in groups and help each other. One learner per group reads aloud. Occasionally ask learners to identify the sounds of letters. Give each level its group task.","learners":"Read the chart in groups; one learner reads aloud; do the level task.","tlm":"Alphabet or phonics chart, board or floor","source":"M","ref":"p.13","n":7},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart: individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":2,"teacher":"Give each learner an individual task for their level and observe closely; assist any learner who needs individual support.","learners":"Say and write a letter or word, a sentence or a short paragraph (by level).","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.13","n":8},{"activity":"Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on my favourite festival","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Start a conversation about a picture card: 'my favourite festival'. Involve all learners and ask open-ended questions.","learners":"Take part in the discussion and share thoughts freely.","tlm":"Picture card or topic on the board","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":9},{"activity":"Self-writing: individual writing","grouping":"Individual","minutes":7,"teacher":"Give each level its task (see level table). Let learners take ownership of what they draw and write; mistakes are fine.","learners":"Draw and write about the topic at their level.","tlm":"Notebooks, crayons or pencils","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":10},{"activity":"Self-writing: review and reading back","grouping":"Individual","minutes":3,"teacher":"Ask each learner 'What did you draw or write?' and have them read it aloud once. Word-level learners read to the group; discuss spelling, punctuation and sentence structure. Help beginners by writing their text in the notebook for them if needed.","learners":"Read what they wrote; correct mistakes after listening to their own reading.","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":11},{"activity":"Daily reading (10 minutes)","grouping":"Individual","minutes":10,"teacher":"Give each learner a library book or any storybook. Move around, listen to individual readers and note their level.","learners":"Read independently a book of their choice.","tlm":"Library books or storybooks","source":"M","ref":"p.7","n":12}],"procedures":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Writing with body parts","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","steps":[{"teacher":"Stand the learners in a circle. Demonstrate writing their names in the air with your finger.","learners":"Watch and then copy with their own finger."},{"teacher":"Ask them to write it again using head and other body parts (head, shoulders, knees, ...).","learners":"Write the letters in the air with the named body part."},{"teacher":"Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Take turns to lead."}]},{"activity":"Oral conversation: listening and storytelling","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.9","steps":[{"teacher":"Say the starter: 'Yesterday I grabbed an elephant's tail and flew into the sky. What do you think happened next?'","learners":"Listen and imagine."},{"teacher":"Ask learners to continue the story one by one. Encourage those who speak less.","learners":"Add ideas to the story."},{"teacher":"Invite a learner to recite a poem or rhyme they know.","learners":"Recite and listen to others."}]},{"activity":"Story - Day 2 (an animal friendship story)","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.11","steps":[{"teacher":"Ask learners to retell the story they read yesterday in their own words.","learners":"Retell, helping each other remember."},{"teacher":"In small groups learners practise reading the story using actions and expressions; one learner from each group then reads aloud to the class.","learners":"Read with actions and expression; a representative reads aloud."},{"teacher":"Guide the groups to come up with questions about the story (guide initially). Word-level learners can support by helping write them down.","learners":"Make questions together."},{"teacher":"Groups take turns to ask and answer each other's questions. Useful kinds: questions whose answer is not in the text; questions needing thinking beyond the text; questions asking for an opinion.","learners":"Ask, answer and discuss in the groups."},{"teacher":"Word-level learners also read aloud the consonants they learned on the first day.","learners":"Read the consonant clusters aloud."}]},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart activity (line 3)","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Small group (level-wise) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.13","steps":[{"teacher":"Show the Barakhadi chart and ask the learners which letter they like. Where is the letter 'm'?","learners":"Look for the letter on the chart."},{"teacher":"Read the letter 'm' on the chart. Learners listen and point to it on their own chart. Make sure they do not repeat after you.","learners":"Listen and point to the letter."},{"teacher":"Learners read the alphabet or phonics chart in their groups and help each other; one learner from each group comes forward to read aloud.","learners":"Read in groups; the representative reads aloud."},{"teacher":"Occasionally ask them to identify the sounds of letters from the chart.","learners":"Say the sound of the letter you point to."},{"teacher":"As an extra activity, write some letters on the floor, call out each letter one by one and let the learners jump onto the correct letter.","learners":"Jump onto the letter that is called."}]},{"activity":"Self-writing: 'Discussion, Writing, Self-review'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.15","steps":[{"teacher":"Start a conversation about a picture card: 'my favourite festival'. Involve all learners and ask open-ended questions.","learners":"Discuss and answer questions."},{"teacher":"Give writing time at each level: draw then write (Beginner), write about what they liked (Letter), a sentence (Word), a paragraph or story on a topic of their choice (Para/Story).","learners":"Write at their level and take ownership of the work."},{"teacher":"Review: ask 'What did you draw or write?' Have each learner read the text aloud once. Support with writing if needed.","learners":"Read aloud, listen to their pronunciation and correct mistakes."}]}],"levelTasks":[{"activity":"Story - Day 2: level-wise tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.11","tasks":{"Beginner":"Retell with the group by pointing to pictures or words; read aloud with group support (interpretation of the manual's group reading task).","Letter":"Read with the group, pointing to words; say the letters and words they know (interpretation of the manual's group reading task).","Word":"Support the group in writing the questions; read aloud the consonant clusters learned on the first day.","Para":"Ask the group's questions to another group, discuss them, then write answers to all questions individually; the teacher reads and corrects.","Story":"Ask the group's questions to another group, discuss them, then write answers to all questions individually; the teacher reads and corrects."}},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart: level tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.13","tasks":{"Beginner":"Small group: read the chart in the group; find and write favourite letters from the line. Individual: say and write a letter of their choice.","Letter":"Small group: read the chart; find and write favourite letters or words from any line. Individual: say a word on their own that begins with any letter.","Word":"Small group: write one or two lines of letters on the board or floor and use them to form words. Individual: speak and write sentences using words they know.","Para":"Small group: prepare word lists using the Barakhadi chart (for example items found in a shop or in the kitchen). Individual: write short paragraphs using the words formed with the Barakhadi chart.","Story":"Small group: prepare word lists using the Barakhadi chart. Individual: write short paragraphs using the words formed with the Barakhadi chart."}},{"activity":"Self-writing: level tasks and review","source":"M","ref":"p.15","tasks":{"Beginner":"Draw a picture about the discussion and then write a few sentences about it, expressing thoughts freely. Review: say what they drew or wrote; read the text aloud once; the teacher may write the text in the notebook for them.","Letter":"Write about what they liked, using drawing and writing; write any words or sentences they can. Review: read the text aloud once; correct punctuation mistakes using the Barakhadi chart.","Word":"Write a sentence based on the conversation. Mistakes in spelling, punctuation and sentence structure are fine. Review: read it to the group; discuss and correct mistakes together.","Para":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation.","Story":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation."}}],"organisation":[{"grouping":"Whole class (big group)","how":"All learners of all levels sit in a 'U' shape arranged by level (Beginner, Letter, Word, Para, Story) so that the move to small groups is easy.","activities":["Warm-up: Writing with body parts","Oral conversation: listening and storytelling","Story (Day 2 of the story): retelling","Barakhadi chart: big group reading","Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on my favourite festival"]},{"grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","how":"Learners of similar levels work together; the teacher gives each group a task for its level and spends more time with learners who need support. Rotate responsibilities (for example group leader).","activities":["Story: reading with actions and group questions","Barakhadi chart: small-group practice"]},{"grouping":"Individual","how":"Each learner works on a task for their own level; the teacher moves around, observes difficulties and supports individuals.","activities":["Story: writing answers individually","Barakhadi chart: individual tasks","Self-writing: individual writing","Self-writing: review and reading back","Daily reading (10 minutes)"]}],"materials":["The same story book as yesterday","Story book","slate or paper for questions","Notebooks","Barakhadi chart","alphabet or phonics chart","Alphabet or phonics chart","board or floor","Picture card or topic on the board","crayons or pencils","Library books or storybooks"],"outcomes":["Learners take part in the oral conversation and speak without fear.","Learners retell the story, read with expression and ask or answer questions at their level.","Learners respond to the sound-symbol task for today (Barakhadi / alphabet and phonics chart (line 3, letter 'm')) at their own level.","Learners write about the topic at their level and read it aloud.","Each learner reads a book for 10 minutes."],"observation":["Observe each learner's reading and writing during the individual tasks; note who needs individual support and how many learners share the same difficulty.","Note any learner whose level is improving; move the learner to the next level group when you see steady progress (manual p.5).","Record each learner's progress for the day in the notebook, according to the learner's level (manual p.4).","Use today's observations to adjust tomorrow's plan (manual p.5)."],"teacherNotes":["Questions to elicit on Day 2: information questions (answer not in the text), thinking questions (needs knowledge beyond the text) and opinion questions (feedback on something in the text).","Barakhadi: learners who need extra time should get repeated practice using one or two sound units at a time. Topic-based discussion helps oral expression, thinking and understanding.","Writing has two parts, content and sequence: encourage learners to read what they wrote, improve it and rewrite it for clarity and correctness (manual p.15).","Pace: the manual says not to assume all learners progress at the same speed. Repeat a day's activity with the groups that need it before moving on.","Special needs: give extra time and prepare materials for slower learners; seat learners with hearing or vision difficulty at the front; for learners who reverse or confuse letters, trace letters on the letter card with a finger and write with dots to trace with a pencil (manual p.6)."],"components":[{"no":1,"key":"warmup","name":"Warm-up activities","keywords":["Writing with body parts","two learners lead"],"rows":[1]},{"no":2,"key":"oral","name":"Oral Discussion","keywords":["listening and storytelling","every learner speaks","home language"],"rows":[2]},{"no":3,"key":"story","name":"Story","keywords":["Day 2","retell","read with actions","group questions","ask and answer","write answers (Para/Story)"],"rows":[3,4,5]},{"no":4,"key":"sound","name":"Sound symbol games, Sound separation-pairing","keywords":["Barakhadi / alphabet chart","listen and point (no repeating)","group reading","level tasks"],"rows":[6,7,8]},{"no":5,"key":"mindwrite","name":"Individual-Writing (Day 2)","keywords":["discussion","write at own level","self-review (read aloud)"],"rows":[9,10,11]},{"no":6,"key":"reading","name":"Daily reading","keywords":["library book","read alone","teacher listens"],"rows":[12]}],"preLesson":null},{"programme":"TARL Literacy","id":"lit-003","day":3,"phase":1,"phaseLabel":"Phase 1 (Days 1-45)","title":"Story: a story about a farmer and his field (Day 1)","dayType":"Story Day 1 + Mind mapping","focus":"Blending sounds to form words (pig, hat, pen) | Mind map: market","duration":70,"objectives":["Listen, speak and answer in the oral conversation (What did you see on your way?).","Listen to and read a story with understanding; discuss it in big and small groups and respond at their own level.","Develop sound-symbol skills: Blending sounds to form words (pig, hat, pen).","Build vocabulary through a mind map ('market') and use the words at their own level.","Read independently for 10 minutes every day."],"sequence":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Alphabet song (last-letter word chain)","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Say a word to the big group, for example 'tree'. Learners say a word that starts with the last letter ('e'). A learner who cannot say a word is out. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Say a word that starts with the last letter of the previous word; step out if unable to.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.8","n":1},{"activity":"Oral conversation: What did you see on your way?","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Ask learners to describe what they saw on their way to school. If they are hesitant, begin yourself: 'When I arrived today, I saw two cats chasing each other, a farmer ploughing in the field, and goats grazing on the river bank. What did you see?' In the initial days use the learners' home language so that they feel comfortable.","learners":"Describe what they saw on the way to school and connect with what others share.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.9","n":2},{"activity":"Story (Day 1 of the story): reading aloud and discussion","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":8,"teacher":"Discuss the title or picture of the story with the learners. Read the story aloud with expression and voice modulation (learners do not repeat after you). Discuss it, with emphasis on logical questions. Read it again slowly, pointing to each word.","learners":"Talk about the title/picture; listen; answer questions; follow each word with a finger in their own copy.","tlm":"A story from the school library (a story about a farmer and his field), a copy for each learner","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":3},{"activity":"Story: reading in small groups","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":7,"teacher":"Form level-wise groups with a group leader. Learners read the story one sentence at a time while the others follow with their fingers. Para and Story level learners practise reading with emotion and expression.","learners":"Read the story sentence by sentence, supporting each other; the group leader helps.","tlm":"Story book copies","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":4},{"activity":"Story: level-wise individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":5,"teacher":"Give each learner the task for their level (see level table) and support those who need it.","learners":"Beginner/Letter: find and write favourite words or letters. Word: find consonant clusters. Para/Story: silently read, find unfamiliar and rhyming words.","tlm":"Story book, notebooks, board","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":5},{"activity":"Sound-symbol activity: oral sound awareness","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":4,"teacher":"Say separate sounds from 10-12 words (pig: p - i - g; hat: h - a - t; pen: p - e - n; bus: b - u - s) and ask learners to blend the sounds into the complete word.","learners":"Listen to the separate sounds and blend them to say the whole word.","tlm":"None (oral activity)","source":"M","ref":"p.12","n":6},{"activity":"Sound-symbol games by level","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":6,"teacher":"Give each level group its game (see level table). Move among the groups and help those who need support; say each word clearly.","learners":"Play the game for their level in small groups.","tlm":"Board, chalk, letter cards","source":"M","ref":"p.12","n":7},{"activity":"Mind mapping (Day 1): the word 'market'","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Ask: 'What words come to your mind when you hear the word market?' Write learners' answers on the board or floor (Para and Story level learners write the words themselves). Guide the map towards the learning objective. Example words: potato, pumpkin, tomato, brinjal, banana, papaya, pineapple, guava, basket, spice, fish, eggs.","learners":"Say words connected with 'market'; share the meaning and feeling of words.","tlm":"Board, chalk (or floor)","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":8},{"activity":"Mind mapping: classify the words","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":4,"teacher":"Ask learners to classify the words in groups, for example: Vegetables: potato, pumpkin, tomato, brinjal; Fruits: banana, papaya, pineapple, guava; Things sold: basket, spice, fish, eggs.","learners":"Sort the words into groups and say why.","tlm":"Board, chalk, word cards (optional)","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":9},{"activity":"Mind mapping: level-wise individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":6,"teacher":"Give each learner the individual task for their level; observe closely and give individual support. Display corrected stories on the wall.","learners":"Complete the task for their level (see level table).","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":10},{"activity":"Daily reading (10 minutes)","grouping":"Individual","minutes":10,"teacher":"Give each learner a library book or any storybook. Move around, listen to individual readers and note their level.","learners":"Read independently a book of their choice.","tlm":"Library books or storybooks","source":"M","ref":"p.7","n":11}],"procedures":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Alphabet song (last-letter word chain)","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","steps":[{"teacher":"Say the word 'tree' to the big group and show that its last letter is 'e'.","learners":"Listen and think of a word starting with 'e'."},{"teacher":"Ask learners in turn to say a word that starts with the last letter of the previous word. Example: rain -> nest.","learners":"Say a word in turn; anyone who cannot say a word is out of the game."},{"teacher":"Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Lead the game when it is their turn."}]},{"activity":"Oral conversation: What did you see on your way?","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.9","steps":[{"teacher":"Ask: 'What did you see on your way to school today?'","learners":"Think about the way to school."},{"teacher":"If learners hesitate, start: 'When I arrived today, I saw two cats chasing each other, a farmer ploughing in the field, and goats grazing on the river bank. What did you see?'","learners":"Listen to the model and then share their own observations."},{"teacher":"Connect learners' answers with each other.","learners":"Listen and add what they noticed."}]},{"activity":"Story - Day 1 (a story about a farmer and his field)","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.10","steps":[{"teacher":"Discuss the title or picture of the story with the learners.","learners":"Talk about what they see and what the story may be about."},{"teacher":"Read the story aloud with expression and proper voice modulation. Learners should not simply repeat after you.","learners":"Listen carefully and enjoy the story."},{"teacher":"Discuss the story: factual, logical, vocabulary-based, judgment or opinion questions (today's focus: logical: Why did the character do that? What would have happened if ...?). Begin in the home language if needed.","learners":"Think and respond thoughtfully; every learner takes part."},{"teacher":"Read the story again slowly, pointing to each word. Make sure each learner has a copy and follows with a finger.","learners":"Follow each word with their finger."},{"teacher":"Ask learners to read in small groups; select a group leader who helps the others. Learners read one sentence at a time while the others point with fingers.","learners":"Read with the help of one another."}]},{"activity":"Sound-symbol: oral and level games","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.12","steps":[{"teacher":"Say separate sounds from 10-12 words (pig: p - i - g; hat: h - a - t; pen: p - e - n; bus: b - u - s) and ask learners to blend the sounds into the complete word.","learners":"Listen to the separate sounds and blend them to say the whole word."},{"teacher":"Write the sounds or words for the day on the board and give each level group its task (see the level table).","learners":"Work in small groups and share their answers."},{"teacher":"Say each word clearly with distinct pronunciation. Give learners enough time to respond and think; use words learners commonly use at home (regional language and the medium of instruction).","learners":"Think, say and write the sounds."}]},{"activity":"Mind mapping: 'market'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Small group (level-wise) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.14","steps":[{"teacher":"Choose a word that can generate many related words: 'market'. Ask: 'What words come to your mind when you hear the word market?' Write the answers on the board or floor.","learners":"Say words they link with 'market'."},{"teacher":"Discuss the words: what they mean and how they are connected.","learners":"Explain their words and listen to others."},{"teacher":"In small groups, let the learners classify the words (Vegetables: potato, pumpkin, tomato, brinjal; Fruits: banana, papaya, pineapple, guava; Things sold: basket, spice, fish, eggs).","learners":"Sort the words into groups."},{"teacher":"Give the individual tasks by level and help each learner.","learners":"Work individually; read the work aloud at the end if time allows."}]}],"levelTasks":[{"activity":"Story - Day 1: individual tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.10","tasks":{"Beginner":"Circle or search for a favourite word or letter in the story and say it aloud. If a learner cannot draw a circle, write words on the board and ask them to identify them.","Letter":"Find, read and write favourite words from the story.","Word":"Find the consonant clusters in the story, read them and write them in the notebook.","Para":"Silently read the story from the textbook; find unfamiliar words and try to understand them; find rhyming words, use them in sentences and write in the notebook; ask other groups for meanings; make questions in groups.","Story":"Silently read the story; find unfamiliar words and rhyming words; practise reading with emotion; one group reads sentences formed with consonant clusters to the other group; ask and answer group questions (information, thinking and opinion questions)."}},{"activity":"Sound-symbol games by level (small groups)","source":"M","ref":"p.12","tasks":{"Beginner":"'What is the first sound in the word sun?' 'Is there a letter that makes the sound /s/?' 'Can you name objects that start with the letter S?' Learners think and share names in the group.","Letter":"Write the rhyming ending -og on the board and ask learners to add new letters to form words: d + og = dog, l + og = log, f + og = fog.","Word":"Say a word and tell its sounds, for example 'sun' = /s/ + /u/ + /n/. Then tell what word is formed if /r/ is put before 'at': r + at = rat. Do 8-10 such combinations; at first learners may form meaningless words, later only meaningful words.","Para":"Write two or three sounds on the board (for example Br, cl, st) and let the learners form words that start with those sounds; this builds a word list for the learner.","Story":"Write two or three sounds on the board (for example Br, cl, st) and let the learners form words that start with those sounds; this builds a word list for the learner."}},{"activity":"Mind mapping 'market': level tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.14","tasks":{"Beginner":"Circle all the words that contain the letter 'A' on the board; make a list. See how many learners find the most words.","Letter":"Circle all the words that contain the letter 'A' and make a list of them.","Word":"Use 4-5 words (for example eggs, fish, guava, spice, banana) to form sentences, starting with words of one or two syllables. Example: Dream - I had a dream last night.","Para":"Choose any five words from the map and create a story with them. Use consonant clusters correctly, read the story aloud, correct mistakes of sentence structure, spelling or grammar, then display it on the wall.","Story":"Choose any five words from the map and create a story with them. Use consonant clusters correctly, read the story aloud, correct mistakes of sentence structure, spelling or grammar, then display it on the wall."}}],"organisation":[{"grouping":"Whole class (big group)","how":"All learners of all levels sit in a 'U' shape arranged by level (Beginner, Letter, Word, Para, Story) so that the move to small groups is easy.","activities":["Warm-up: Alphabet song (last-letter word chain)","Oral conversation: What did you see on your way?","Story (Day 1 of the story): reading aloud and discussion","Sound-symbol activity: oral sound awareness","Mind mapping (Day 1): the word 'market'"]},{"grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","how":"Learners of similar levels work together; the teacher gives each group a task for its level and spends more time with learners who need support. Rotate responsibilities (for example group leader).","activities":["Story: reading in small groups","Sound-symbol games by level","Mind mapping: classify the words"]},{"grouping":"Individual","how":"Each learner works on a task for their own level; the teacher moves around, observes difficulties and supports individuals.","activities":["Story: level-wise individual tasks","Mind mapping: level-wise individual tasks","Daily reading (10 minutes)"]}],"materials":["A story from the school library (a story about a farmer","his field)","a copy for each learner","Story book copies","Story book","notebooks","board","Board","chalk","letter cards","chalk (or floor)","word cards (optional)","Notebooks","Library books or storybooks"],"outcomes":["Learners take part in the oral conversation and speak without fear.","Learners show understanding of the story in the discussion and complete the task for their level.","Learners respond to the sound-symbol task for today (Blending sounds to form words (pig, hat, pen)) at their own level.","Learners add words to the mind map and use them in sentences or a story at their level.","Each learner reads a book for 10 minutes."],"observation":["Observe each learner's reading and writing during the individual tasks; note who needs individual support and how many learners share the same difficulty.","Note any learner whose level is improving; move the learner to the next level group when you see steady progress (manual p.5).","Record each learner's progress for the day in the notebook, according to the learner's level (manual p.4).","Use today's observations to adjust tomorrow's plan (manual p.5)."],"teacherNotes":["Story selection: the manual asks teachers to use picture story books or stories in the school library. Today's suggested theme (a story about a farmer and his field) is a planning suggestion; use any suitable story you have.","Sound-symbol: for the first 4-5 days, play sound-based games with the learners at word level. Include the sounds learners find difficult when you prepare the Class Transaction Plan.","Mind mapping topic for this day: 'market'. The manual's example uses the word 'shop'; today's topic follows the same method.","Pace: the manual says not to assume all learners progress at the same speed. Repeat a day's activity with the groups that need it before moving on.","Special needs: give extra time and prepare materials for slower learners; seat learners with hearing or vision difficulty at the front; for learners who reverse or confuse letters, trace letters on the letter card with a finger and write with dots to trace with a pencil (manual p.6)."],"components":[{"no":1,"key":"warmup","name":"Warm-up activities","keywords":["Alphabet song (last-letter word chain)","two learners lead"],"rows":[1]},{"no":2,"key":"oral","name":"Oral Discussion","keywords":["What did you see on your way?","every learner speaks","home language"],"rows":[2]},{"no":3,"key":"story","name":"Story","keywords":["Day 1","title / picture talk","read aloud with expression","logical questions","re-read pointing","group reading","level tasks"],"rows":[3,4,5]},{"no":4,"key":"sound","name":"Sound symbol games, Sound separation-pairing","keywords":["oral sound awareness","blend sounds to a word","level games in small groups"],"rows":[6,7]},{"no":5,"key":"mindwrite","name":"Mind Mapping (Day 1)","keywords":["mind map: market","classify the words","level task: circle letter A / sentences / story"],"rows":[8,9,10]},{"no":6,"key":"reading","name":"Daily reading","keywords":["library book","read alone","teacher listens"],"rows":[11]}],"preLesson":null},{"programme":"TARL Literacy","id":"lit-004","day":4,"phase":1,"phaseLabel":"Phase 1 (Days 1-45)","title":"Story: a story about a farmer and his field (Day 2)","dayType":"Story Day 2 + Self-writing","focus":"Language game: Letter Matching Game | Self-writing: a picture of a busy market","duration":70,"objectives":["Listen, speak and answer in the oral conversation (familiar topic).","Retell the story, read it with expression, ask and answer questions about it and write answers.","Develop sound-symbol skills: Language game: Letter Matching Game.","Write about a topic at their own level and review the writing (a picture of a busy market).","Read independently for 10 minutes every day."],"sequence":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Handkerchief game","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Learners sit in a circle and clap while singing a rhyme ('I saw a Little Bird'). One learner runs outside the circle with a handkerchief and secretly places it behind another learner, who must chase the runner. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Sit in a circle, clap and sing; run, place the handkerchief or chase as the game requires.","tlm":"A handkerchief","source":"M","ref":"p.8","n":1},{"activity":"Oral conversation: familiar topic","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Hold a conversation on the topic 'my favourite food and who cooks it'. Give each learner a chance to speak; be patient with learners who need extra time. In the initial days use the learners' home language so that they feel comfortable.","learners":"Talk about the topic and listen to others.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.9","n":2},{"activity":"Story (Day 2 of the story): retelling","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":6,"teacher":"Ask learners to retell yesterday's story in their own words. Prompt with questions on the beginning, middle and end.","learners":"Retell the story using their own words.","tlm":"The same story book as yesterday","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":3},{"activity":"Story: reading with actions and group questions","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":9,"teacher":"Learners practise reading with actions and expressions; one learner per group reads aloud to the class. Guide groups to make questions about the story (guide initially). Groups take turns to ask and answer each other's questions. Word-level learners also read aloud the consonants learned on the first day.","learners":"Read with actions; make questions (word-level learners help write them); ask and answer questions with another group.","tlm":"Story book, slate or paper for questions","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":4},{"activity":"Story: writing answers individually","grouping":"Individual","minutes":5,"teacher":"Para and Story level learners write answers to all questions individually; read and correct their responses after they finish.","learners":"Write the answers in their notebooks; Beginner/Letter/Word learners read or listen and answer orally.","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":5},{"activity":"Language game: Letter Matching Game","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Two cards for each letter, face down; learners pick two at a time and keep matching pairs. Observe each learner and give help where needed.","learners":"Play the game, take turns and read or say the words they make.","tlm":"Letter cards (two of each letter)","source":"M","ref":"p.18","n":6},{"activity":"Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on a picture of a busy market","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Start a conversation about a topic: 'a picture of a busy market'. Involve all learners and ask open-ended questions.","learners":"Take part in the discussion and share thoughts freely.","tlm":"Picture card or topic on the board","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":7},{"activity":"Self-writing: individual writing","grouping":"Individual","minutes":7,"teacher":"Give each level its task (see level table). Let learners take ownership of what they draw and write; mistakes are fine.","learners":"Draw and write about the topic at their level.","tlm":"Notebooks, crayons or pencils","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":8},{"activity":"Self-writing: review and reading back","grouping":"Individual","minutes":3,"teacher":"Ask each learner 'What did you draw or write?' and have them read it aloud once. Word-level learners read to the group; discuss spelling, punctuation and sentence structure. Help beginners by writing their text in the notebook for them if needed.","learners":"Read what they wrote; correct mistakes after listening to their own reading.","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":9},{"activity":"Daily reading (10 minutes)","grouping":"Individual","minutes":10,"teacher":"Give each learner a library book or any storybook. Move around, listen to individual readers and note their level.","learners":"Read independently a book of their choice.","tlm":"Library books or storybooks","source":"M","ref":"p.7","n":10}],"procedures":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Handkerchief game","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","steps":[{"teacher":"Seat the learners in a circle and start clapping and singing the rhyme 'I saw a Little Bird'.","learners":"Clap and sing together."},{"teacher":"One learner runs outside the circle holding a handkerchief and secretly places it behind another learner.","learners":"Everyone keeps clapping; the learner who finds the handkerchief behind them takes it and chases the runner."},{"teacher":"If the runner sits in the chaser's place before being caught, they stay in the game; if caught, they are out. Continue in this way.","learners":"Play fairly and take turns."}]},{"activity":"Oral conversation: familiar topic","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.9","steps":[{"teacher":"Introduce the topic: 'my favourite food and who cooks it'.","learners":"Think about their own experience."},{"teacher":"Ask open questions; give every learner a chance. Involve learners who speak less.","learners":"Speak freely and without fear."},{"teacher":"Praise efforts and sum up.","learners":"Listen and respect each other's ideas."}]},{"activity":"Story - Day 2 (a story about a farmer and his field)","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.11","steps":[{"teacher":"Ask learners to retell the story they read yesterday in their own words.","learners":"Retell, helping each other remember."},{"teacher":"In small groups learners practise reading the story using actions and expressions; one learner from each group then reads aloud to the class.","learners":"Read with actions and expression; a representative reads aloud."},{"teacher":"Guide the groups to come up with questions about the story (guide initially). Word-level learners can support by helping write them down.","learners":"Make questions together."},{"teacher":"Groups take turns to ask and answer each other's questions. Useful kinds: questions whose answer is not in the text; questions needing thinking beyond the text; questions asking for an opinion.","learners":"Ask, answer and discuss in the groups."},{"teacher":"Word-level learners also read aloud the consonants they learned on the first day.","learners":"Read the consonant clusters aloud."}]},{"activity":"Language game: Letter Matching Game","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.18","steps":[{"teacher":"Make two cards for each letter (use the letters being practised). Mix them and place them face down on the floor.","learners":"Watch the teacher and sit around the cards."},{"teacher":"Call the learners one by one to turn over two cards. If they do not match, they are turned face down again.","learners":"Remember where each letter is placed; pick the next pair."},{"teacher":"Continue until all pairs are matched. The learner with the most pairs wins.","learners":"Count pairs, cheer and say each matched letter aloud."}]},{"activity":"Self-writing: 'Discussion, Writing, Self-review'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.15","steps":[{"teacher":"Start a conversation about a topic: 'a picture of a busy market'. Involve all learners and ask open-ended questions.","learners":"Discuss and answer questions."},{"teacher":"Give writing time at each level: draw then write (Beginner), write about what they liked (Letter), a sentence (Word), a paragraph or story on a topic of their choice (Para/Story).","learners":"Write at their level and take ownership of the work."},{"teacher":"Review: ask 'What did you draw or write?' Have each learner read the text aloud once. Support with writing if needed.","learners":"Read aloud, listen to their pronunciation and correct mistakes."}]}],"levelTasks":[{"activity":"Story - Day 2: level-wise tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.11","tasks":{"Beginner":"Retell with the group by pointing to pictures or words; read aloud with group support (interpretation of the manual's group reading task).","Letter":"Read with the group, pointing to words; say the letters and words they know (interpretation of the manual's group reading task).","Word":"Support the group in writing the questions; read aloud the consonant clusters learned on the first day.","Para":"Ask the group's questions to another group, discuss them, then write answers to all questions individually; the teacher reads and corrects.","Story":"Ask the group's questions to another group, discuss them, then write answers to all questions individually; the teacher reads and corrects."}},{"activity":"Language game: Letter Matching Game - level support","source":"I","ref":"p.18","tasks":{"Beginner":"Take part by saying or pointing to the letters involved and by listening carefully; Para and Story level partners help.","Letter":"Say the letters/sounds and give simple words they know.","Word":"Say and write words and short sentences for the game.","Para":"Write sentences with the words; help groups to record answers.","Story":"Write sentences or short stories with the words; help groups to record answers."}},{"activity":"Self-writing: level tasks and review","source":"M","ref":"p.15","tasks":{"Beginner":"Draw a picture about the discussion and then write a few sentences about it, expressing thoughts freely. Review: say what they drew or wrote; read the text aloud once; the teacher may write the text in the notebook for them.","Letter":"Write about what they liked, using drawing and writing; write any words or sentences they can. Review: read the text aloud once; correct punctuation mistakes using the Barakhadi chart.","Word":"Write a sentence based on the conversation. Mistakes in spelling, punctuation and sentence structure are fine. Review: read it to the group; discuss and correct mistakes together.","Para":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation.","Story":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation."}}],"organisation":[{"grouping":"Whole class (big group)","how":"All learners of all levels sit in a 'U' shape arranged by level (Beginner, Letter, Word, Para, Story) so that the move to small groups is easy.","activities":["Warm-up: Handkerchief game","Oral conversation: familiar topic","Story (Day 2 of the story): retelling","Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on a picture of a busy market"]},{"grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","how":"Learners of similar levels work together; the teacher gives each group a task for its level and spends more time with learners who need support. Rotate responsibilities (for example group leader).","activities":["Story: reading with actions and group questions","Language game: Letter Matching Game"]},{"grouping":"Individual","how":"Each learner works on a task for their own level; the teacher moves around, observes difficulties and supports individuals.","activities":["Story: writing answers individually","Self-writing: individual writing","Self-writing: review and reading back","Daily reading (10 minutes)"]}],"materials":["A handkerchief","The same story book as yesterday","Story book","slate or paper for questions","Notebooks","Letter cards (two of each letter)","Picture card or topic on the board","crayons or pencils","Library books or storybooks"],"outcomes":["Learners take part in the oral conversation and speak without fear.","Learners retell the story, read with expression and ask or answer questions at their level.","Learners respond to the sound-symbol task for today (Language game: Letter Matching Game) at their own level.","Learners write about the topic at their level and read it aloud.","Each learner reads a book for 10 minutes."],"observation":["Observe each learner's reading and writing during the individual tasks; note who needs individual support and how many learners share the same difficulty.","Note any learner whose level is improving; move the learner to the next level group when you see steady progress (manual p.5).","Record each learner's progress for the day in the notebook, according to the learner's level (manual p.4).","Use today's observations to adjust tomorrow's plan (manual p.5)."],"teacherNotes":["Questions to elicit on Day 2: information questions (answer not in the text), thinking questions (needs knowledge beyond the text) and opinion questions (feedback on something in the text).","The manual lists the letter and word games but does not fix the slot in the daily timetable where they are used. This plan places them in the 10-minute sound-symbol / alphabet slot (interpretation).","Writing has two parts, content and sequence: encourage learners to read what they wrote, improve it and rewrite it for clarity and correctness (manual p.15).","Pace: the manual says not to assume all learners progress at the same speed. Repeat a day's activity with the groups that need it before moving on.","Special needs: give extra time and prepare materials for slower learners; seat learners with hearing or vision difficulty at the front; for learners who reverse or confuse letters, trace letters on the letter card with a finger and write with dots to trace with a pencil (manual p.6)."],"components":[{"no":1,"key":"warmup","name":"Warm-up activities","keywords":["Handkerchief game","two learners lead"],"rows":[1]},{"no":2,"key":"oral","name":"Oral Discussion","keywords":["familiar topic","every learner speaks","home language"],"rows":[2]},{"no":3,"key":"story","name":"Story","keywords":["Day 2","retell","read with actions","group questions","ask and answer","write answers (Para/Story)"],"rows":[3,4,5]},{"no":4,"key":"sound","name":"Sound symbol games, Sound separation-pairing","keywords":["Letter Matching Game","play in turns","level support"],"rows":[6]},{"no":5,"key":"mindwrite","name":"Individual-Writing (Day 2)","keywords":["discussion","write at own level","self-review (read aloud)"],"rows":[7,8,9]},{"no":6,"key":"reading","name":"Daily reading","keywords":["library book","read alone","teacher listens"],"rows":[10]}],"preLesson":null},{"programme":"TARL Literacy","id":"lit-005","day":5,"phase":1,"phaseLabel":"Phase 1 (Days 1-45)","title":"Story: a folk tale about a clever fox or rabbit (Day 1)","dayType":"Story Day 1 + Mind mapping","focus":"Barakhadi / alphabet and phonics chart (line 6, letter 'p') | Mind map: school","duration":70,"objectives":["Listen, speak and answer in the oral conversation (conversation on a picture).","Listen to and read a story with understanding; discuss it in big and small groups and respond at their own level.","Develop sound-symbol skills: Barakhadi / alphabet and phonics chart (line 6, letter 'p').","Build vocabulary through a mind map ('school') and use the words at their own level.","Read independently for 10 minutes every day."],"sequence":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Rhyme - 'I caught a Fish Alive'","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Say the rhyme with actions, then say it together. Lines: One, two, three, four, five, once I caught a fish alive. / Six, seven, eight, nine, ten, then I let it go again. / Why did you let it go? Because it bit my finger so. / Which finger did it bite? This little finger on my right. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Listen, then say the rhyme with actions.","tlm":"Rhyme chart or board (optional)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","n":1},{"activity":"Oral conversation: conversation on a picture","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Show a picture of children playing in the rain and ask what is happening, who is doing what and what is happening around them. Let learners think creatively and even make up a story. In the initial days use the learners' home language so that they feel comfortable.","learners":"Look at the picture, answer questions and make up their own story about it.","tlm":"Picture card of children playing in the rain","source":"M","ref":"p.9","n":2},{"activity":"Story (Day 1 of the story): reading aloud and discussion","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":8,"teacher":"Discuss the title or picture of the story with the learners. Read the story aloud with expression and voice modulation (learners do not repeat after you). Discuss it, with emphasis on vocabulary-based questions. Read it again slowly, pointing to each word.","learners":"Talk about the title/picture; listen; answer questions; follow each word with a finger in their own copy.","tlm":"A story from the school library (a folk tale about a clever fox or rabbit), a copy for each learner","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":3},{"activity":"Story: reading in small groups","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":7,"teacher":"Form level-wise groups with a group leader. Learners read the story one sentence at a time while the others follow with their fingers. Para and Story level learners practise reading with emotion and expression.","learners":"Read the story sentence by sentence, supporting each other; the group leader helps.","tlm":"Story book copies","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":4},{"activity":"Story: level-wise individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":5,"teacher":"Give each learner the task for their level (see level table) and support those who need it.","learners":"Beginner/Letter: find and write favourite words or letters. Word: find consonant clusters. Para/Story: silently read, find unfamiliar and rhyming words.","tlm":"Story book, notebooks, board","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":5},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart: big group reading","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":3,"teacher":"Show the Barakhadi chart and ask which letter they like. Read the letter 'p' on the chart; learners listen carefully and point to it on their own chart (they do not repeat after you).","learners":"Listen and point to the letter on their own chart.","tlm":"Barakhadi chart, alphabet or phonics chart","source":"M","ref":"p.13","n":6},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart: small-group practice","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Learners practise reading the alphabet or phonics chart in groups and help each other. One learner per group reads aloud. Occasionally ask learners to identify the sounds of letters. Give each level its group task.","learners":"Read the chart in groups; one learner reads aloud; do the level task.","tlm":"Alphabet or phonics chart, board or floor","source":"M","ref":"p.13","n":7},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart: individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":2,"teacher":"Give each learner an individual task for their level and observe closely; assist any learner who needs individual support.","learners":"Say and write a letter or word, a sentence or a short paragraph (by level).","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.13","n":8},{"activity":"Mind mapping (Day 1): the word 'school'","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Ask: 'What words come to your mind when you hear the word school?' Write learners' answers on the board or floor (Para and Story level learners write the words themselves). Guide the map towards the learning objective. Example words: book, pencil, notebook, eraser, playground, classroom, library, office, teacher, student, principal, cook.","learners":"Say words connected with 'school'; share the meaning and feeling of words.","tlm":"Board, chalk (or floor)","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":9},{"activity":"Mind mapping: classify the words","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":4,"teacher":"Ask learners to classify the words in groups, for example: Things in the bag: book, pencil, notebook, eraser; Places: playground, classroom, library, office; People: teacher, student, principal, cook.","learners":"Sort the words into groups and say why.","tlm":"Board, chalk, word cards (optional)","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":10},{"activity":"Mind mapping: level-wise individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":6,"teacher":"Give each learner the individual task for their level; observe closely and give individual support. Display corrected stories on the wall.","learners":"Complete the task for their level (see level table).","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":11},{"activity":"Daily reading (10 minutes)","grouping":"Individual","minutes":10,"teacher":"Give each learner a library book or any storybook. Move around, listen to individual readers and note their level.","learners":"Read independently a book of their choice.","tlm":"Library books or storybooks","source":"M","ref":"p.7","n":12}],"procedures":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Rhyme - 'I caught a Fish Alive'","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","steps":[{"teacher":"Say the rhyme 'I caught a Fish Alive' slowly with actions: One, two, three, four, five, once I caught a fish alive. / Six, seven, eight, nine, ten, then I let it go again. / Why did you let it go? Because it bit my finger so. / Which finger did it bite? This little finger on my right.","learners":"Listen and watch the actions."},{"teacher":"Say it again; invite learners to join with actions.","learners":"Say the rhyme together with actions."},{"teacher":"Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Choose a rhyme they like and lead."}]},{"activity":"Oral conversation: conversation on a picture","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.9","steps":[{"teacher":"Show the picture of children playing in the rain.","learners":"Look carefully."},{"teacher":"Ask: What is happening in the picture? Who is doing what? What is happening around them? Then: How do the people feel? How can you tell?","learners":"Answer in their own words; every learner gets a chance."},{"teacher":"Let learners imagine and make up a short story from the picture.","learners":"Tell their stories to the class."}]},{"activity":"Story - Day 1 (a folk tale about a clever fox or rabbit)","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.10","steps":[{"teacher":"Discuss the title or picture of the story with the learners.","learners":"Talk about what they see and what the story may be about."},{"teacher":"Read the story aloud with expression and proper voice modulation. Learners should not simply repeat after you.","learners":"Listen carefully and enjoy the story."},{"teacher":"Discuss the story: factual, logical, vocabulary-based, judgment or opinion questions (today's focus: vocabulary-based: What does this word mean? Which word in the story means the same as ...?). Begin in the home language if needed.","learners":"Think and respond thoughtfully; every learner takes part."},{"teacher":"Read the story again slowly, pointing to each word. Make sure each learner has a copy and follows with a finger.","learners":"Follow each word with their finger."},{"teacher":"Ask learners to read in small groups; select a group leader who helps the others. Learners read one sentence at a time while the others point with fingers.","learners":"Read with the help of one another."}]},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart activity (line 6)","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Small group (level-wise) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.13","steps":[{"teacher":"Show the Barakhadi chart and ask the learners which letter they like. Where is the letter 'p'?","learners":"Look for the letter on the chart."},{"teacher":"Read the letter 'p' on the chart. Learners listen and point to it on their own chart. Make sure they do not repeat after you.","learners":"Listen and point to the letter."},{"teacher":"Learners read the alphabet or phonics chart in their groups and help each other; one learner from each group comes forward to read aloud.","learners":"Read in groups; the representative reads aloud."},{"teacher":"Occasionally ask them to identify the sounds of letters from the chart.","learners":"Say the sound of the letter you point to."},{"teacher":"As an extra activity, write some letters on the floor, call out each letter one by one and let the learners jump onto the correct letter.","learners":"Jump onto the letter that is called."}]},{"activity":"Mind mapping: 'school'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Small group (level-wise) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.14","steps":[{"teacher":"Choose a word that can generate many related words: 'school'. Ask: 'What words come to your mind when you hear the word school?' Write the answers on the board or floor.","learners":"Say words they link with 'school'."},{"teacher":"Discuss the words: what they mean and how they are connected.","learners":"Explain their words and listen to others."},{"teacher":"In small groups, let the learners classify the words (Things in the bag: book, pencil, notebook, eraser; Places: playground, classroom, library, office; People: teacher, student, principal, cook).","learners":"Sort the words into groups."},{"teacher":"Give the individual tasks by level and help each learner.","learners":"Work individually; read the work aloud at the end if time allows."}]}],"levelTasks":[{"activity":"Story - Day 1: individual tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.10","tasks":{"Beginner":"Circle or search for a favourite word or letter in the story and say it aloud. If a learner cannot draw a circle, write words on the board and ask them to identify them.","Letter":"Find, read and write favourite words from the story.","Word":"Find the consonant clusters in the story, read them and write them in the notebook.","Para":"Silently read the story from the textbook; find unfamiliar words and try to understand them; find rhyming words, use them in sentences and write in the notebook; ask other groups for meanings; make questions in groups.","Story":"Silently read the story; find unfamiliar words and rhyming words; practise reading with emotion; one group reads sentences formed with consonant clusters to the other group; ask and answer group questions (information, thinking and opinion questions)."}},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart: level tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.13","tasks":{"Beginner":"Small group: read the chart in the group; find and write favourite letters from the line. Individual: say and write a letter of their choice.","Letter":"Small group: read the chart; find and write favourite letters or words from any line. Individual: say a word on their own that begins with any letter.","Word":"Small group: write one or two lines of letters on the board or floor and use them to form words. Individual: speak and write sentences using words they know.","Para":"Small group: prepare word lists using the Barakhadi chart (for example items found in a shop or in the kitchen). Individual: write short paragraphs using the words formed with the Barakhadi chart.","Story":"Small group: prepare word lists using the Barakhadi chart. Individual: write short paragraphs using the words formed with the Barakhadi chart."}},{"activity":"Mind mapping 'school': level tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.14","tasks":{"Beginner":"Circle all the words that contain the letter 'A' on the board; make a list. See how many learners find the most words.","Letter":"Circle all the words that contain the letter 'A' and make a list of them.","Word":"Use 4-5 words (for example book, cook, eraser, office, pencil) to form sentences, starting with words of one or two syllables. Example: Dream - I had a dream last night.","Para":"Choose any five words from the map and create a story with them. Use consonant clusters correctly, read the story aloud, correct mistakes of sentence structure, spelling or grammar, then display it on the wall.","Story":"Choose any five words from the map and create a story with them. Use consonant clusters correctly, read the story aloud, correct mistakes of sentence structure, spelling or grammar, then display it on the wall."}}],"organisation":[{"grouping":"Whole class (big group)","how":"All learners of all levels sit in a 'U' shape arranged by level (Beginner, Letter, Word, Para, Story) so that the move to small groups is easy.","activities":["Warm-up: Rhyme - 'I caught a Fish Alive'","Oral conversation: conversation on a picture","Story (Day 1 of the story): reading aloud and discussion","Barakhadi chart: big group reading","Mind mapping (Day 1): the word 'school'"]},{"grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","how":"Learners of similar levels work together; the teacher gives each group a task for its level and spends more time with learners who need support. Rotate responsibilities (for example group leader).","activities":["Story: reading in small groups","Barakhadi chart: small-group practice","Mind mapping: classify the words"]},{"grouping":"Individual","how":"Each learner works on a task for their own level; the teacher moves around, observes difficulties and supports individuals.","activities":["Story: level-wise individual tasks","Barakhadi chart: individual tasks","Mind mapping: level-wise individual tasks","Daily reading (10 minutes)"]}],"materials":["Rhyme chart or board (optional)","Picture card of children playing in the rain","A story from the school library (a folk tale about a clever fox or rabbit)","a copy for each learner","Story book copies","Story book","notebooks","board","Barakhadi chart","alphabet or phonics chart","Alphabet or phonics chart","board or floor","Notebooks","Board","chalk (or floor)","chalk","word cards (optional)","Library books or storybooks"],"outcomes":["Learners take part in the oral conversation and speak without fear.","Learners show understanding of the story in the discussion and complete the task for their level.","Learners respond to the sound-symbol task for today (Barakhadi / alphabet and phonics chart (line 6, letter 'p')) at their own level.","Learners add words to the mind map and use them in sentences or a story at their level.","Each learner reads a book for 10 minutes."],"observation":["Observe each learner's reading and writing during the individual tasks; note who needs individual support and how many learners share the same difficulty.","Note any learner whose level is improving; move the learner to the next level group when you see steady progress (manual p.5).","Record each learner's progress for the day in the notebook, according to the learner's level (manual p.4).","Use today's observations to adjust tomorrow's plan (manual p.5)."],"teacherNotes":["Story selection: the manual asks teachers to use picture story books or stories in the school library. Today's suggested theme (a folk tale about a clever fox or rabbit) is a planning suggestion; use any suitable story you have.","Barakhadi: learners who need extra time should get repeated practice using one or two sound units at a time. Topic-based discussion helps oral expression, thinking and understanding.","Mind mapping topic for this day: 'school'. The manual's example uses the word 'shop'; today's topic follows the same method.","Pace: the manual says not to assume all learners progress at the same speed. Repeat a day's activity with the groups that need it before moving on.","Special needs: give extra time and prepare materials for slower learners; seat learners with hearing or vision difficulty at the front; for learners who reverse or confuse letters, trace letters on the letter card with a finger and write with dots to trace with a pencil (manual p.6)."],"components":[{"no":1,"key":"warmup","name":"Warm-up activities","keywords":["Rhyme - 'I caught a Fish Alive'","two learners lead"],"rows":[1]},{"no":2,"key":"oral","name":"Oral Discussion","keywords":["conversation on a picture","every learner speaks","home language"],"rows":[2]},{"no":3,"key":"story","name":"Story","keywords":["Day 1","title / picture talk","read aloud with expression","vocabulary-based questions","re-read pointing","group reading","level tasks"],"rows":[3,4,5]},{"no":4,"key":"sound","name":"Sound symbol games, Sound separation-pairing","keywords":["Barakhadi / alphabet chart","listen and point (no repeating)","group reading","level tasks"],"rows":[6,7,8]},{"no":5,"key":"mindwrite","name":"Mind Mapping (Day 1)","keywords":["mind map: school","classify the words","level task: circle letter A / sentences / story"],"rows":[9,10,11]},{"no":6,"key":"reading","name":"Daily reading","keywords":["library book","read alone","teacher listens"],"rows":[12]}],"preLesson":null},{"programme":"TARL Literacy","id":"lit-006","day":6,"phase":1,"phaseLabel":"Phase 1 (Days 1-45)","title":"Saturday: drama presentation","dayType":"Saturday drama + Self-writing","focus":"Hearing the different sounds in words (pig, hat, cup) | Self-writing: the story we acted out (a folk tale about a clever fox or rabbit)","duration":70,"objectives":["Listen, speak and answer in the oral conversation (listening and storytelling).","Express a story through role play, using voice, facial expressions and gestures.","Develop sound-symbol skills: Hearing the different sounds in words (pig, hat, cup).","Write about the story and review the writing.","Read independently for 10 minutes every day."],"sequence":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Singing and Spinning","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Learners sit in a circle and pass a small object while you clap with your back turned; when the clapping stops, the learner holding it sings a song, recites a poem or tells a joke. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Pass the object round the circle; sing, recite or tell a joke when the clapping stops.","tlm":"A small object (chalk or pencil)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","n":1},{"activity":"Oral conversation: listening and storytelling","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Tell an interesting story starter and involve the learners: 'One morning a tiny door appeared in the school wall. What was behind it?' Let learners imagine and continue the story.","learners":"Listen to the teacher, then imagine and continue the story. Learners can also recite a rhyme or story they know.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.9","n":2},{"activity":"Dramatic presentation: introduction and reading","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Explain what a dramatic presentation is and how it is done. Provide stories discussed during the week and read one aloud once more. Para and Story level learners support Beginner and Letter level learners in reading.","learners":"Listen, read along, then each learner chooses a character.","tlm":"Stories discussed in the week (a story about a farmer and his field; a folk tale about a clever fox or rabbit)","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":3},{"activity":"Dramatic presentation: planning in small groups","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":8,"teacher":"Each group discusses and plans dialogues; Para or Story level learners write the dialogues. Groups prepare their dramatic presentation.","learners":"Choose characters, plan and rehearse dialogues with facial expressions and gestures.","tlm":"Story, paper for dialogues","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":4},{"activity":"Dramatic presentation: performances and feedback","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":7,"teacher":"Learners sit in a U shape. Each group presents; after each performance, watching learners say what they enjoyed and what could be improved.","learners":"Perform in turn; watch; give feedback.","tlm":"Open space (U-shape seating)","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":5},{"activity":"Sound-symbol activity: oral sound awareness","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":4,"teacher":"Say 10-12 simple words aloud ('pig, hat, cup, log, jam, fan, red, bus, sit, map, wet, van') and ask learners to identify the different sounds in them. This builds phonemic awareness.","learners":"Listen to each word and tell its sounds.","tlm":"None (oral activity)","source":"M","ref":"p.12","n":6},{"activity":"Sound-symbol games by level","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":6,"teacher":"Give each level group its game (see level table). Move among the groups and help those who need support; say each word clearly.","learners":"Play the game for their level in small groups.","tlm":"Board, chalk, letter cards","source":"M","ref":"p.12","n":7},{"activity":"Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on the story we acted out (a folk tale about a clever fox or rabbit)","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Start a conversation about the story used for the drama: 'the story we acted out (a folk tale about a clever fox or rabbit)'. Involve all learners with open-ended questions.","learners":"Take part in the discussion and share thoughts freely.","tlm":"Picture card or topic on the board","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":8},{"activity":"Self-writing: individual writing","grouping":"Individual","minutes":7,"teacher":"Give each level its task (see level table). Let learners take ownership of what they draw and write; mistakes are fine.","learners":"Draw and write about the topic at their level.","tlm":"Notebooks, crayons or pencils","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":9},{"activity":"Self-writing: review and reading back","grouping":"Individual","minutes":3,"teacher":"Ask each learner 'What did you draw or write?' and have them read it aloud once. Word-level learners read to the group; discuss spelling, punctuation and sentence structure. Help beginners by writing their text in the notebook for them if needed.","learners":"Read what they wrote; correct mistakes after listening to their own reading.","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":10},{"activity":"Daily reading (10 minutes)","grouping":"Individual","minutes":10,"teacher":"Give each learner a library book or any storybook. Move around, listen to individual readers and note their level.","learners":"Read independently a book of their choice.","tlm":"Library books or storybooks","source":"M","ref":"p.7","n":11}],"procedures":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Singing and Spinning","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","steps":[{"teacher":"Seat the learners in a circle; give a small object to one learner.","learners":"Sit in a circle."},{"teacher":"Stand outside the circle with your back to them and clap steadily; they pass the object.","learners":"Pass the object while the clapping continues."},{"teacher":"Stop clapping; the learner holding the object sings, recites or tells a joke.","learners":"Perform, and everybody claps."}]},{"activity":"Oral conversation: listening and storytelling","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.9","steps":[{"teacher":"Say the starter: 'One morning a tiny door appeared in the school wall. What was behind it?'","learners":"Listen and imagine."},{"teacher":"Ask learners to continue the story one by one. Encourage those who speak less.","learners":"Add ideas to the story."},{"teacher":"Invite a learner to recite a poem or rhyme they know.","learners":"Recite and listen to others."}]},{"activity":"Saturday special: dramatic presentation","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.11","steps":[{"teacher":"Explain what a dramatic presentation is and how it can be done. Give the groups the stories discussed during the week.","learners":"Listen to the explanation."},{"teacher":"Read a story aloud once more. Learners at story and paragraph level support those at beginner and letter level in reading.","learners":"Read along; helpers support their friends."},{"teacher":"After reading, each learner chooses a character from the story.","learners":"Choose a role (boys may play girl roles and girls may play boy roles)."},{"teacher":"In groups, learners discuss and plan the dialogues; paragraph or story level learners write the dialogues.","learners":"Plan and write dialogues together."},{"teacher":"Learners sit in a U shape. Each group presents its drama. After each performance, ask what the audience enjoyed and what could be improved.","learners":"Perform, watch and give kind feedback."}]},{"activity":"Sound-symbol: oral and level games","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.12","steps":[{"teacher":"Say 10-12 simple words aloud ('pig, hat, cup, log, jam, fan, red, bus, sit, map, wet, van') and ask learners to identify the different sounds in them. This builds phonemic awareness.","learners":"Listen to each word and tell its sounds."},{"teacher":"Write the sounds or words for the day on the board and give each level group its task (see the level table).","learners":"Work in small groups and share their answers."},{"teacher":"Say each word clearly with distinct pronunciation. Give learners enough time to respond and think; use words learners commonly use at home (regional language and the medium of instruction).","learners":"Think, say and write the sounds."}]},{"activity":"Self-writing: 'Discussion, Writing, Self-review'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.15","steps":[{"teacher":"Start a conversation about the story used for the drama: 'the story we acted out (a folk tale about a clever fox or rabbit)'. Involve all learners with open-ended questions.","learners":"Discuss and answer questions."},{"teacher":"Give writing time at each level: draw then write (Beginner), write about what they liked (Letter), a sentence (Word), a paragraph or story on a topic of their choice (Para/Story).","learners":"Write at their level and take ownership of the work."},{"teacher":"Review: ask 'What did you draw or write?' Have each learner read the text aloud once. Support with writing if needed.","learners":"Read aloud, listen to their pronunciation and correct mistakes."}]}],"levelTasks":[{"activity":"Drama: roles by level","source":"M","ref":"p.11","tasks":{"Beginner":"Take a character role and say or act short lines with help from Para and Story level learners.","Letter":"Take a character role and say or act short lines with help from Para and Story level learners.","Word":"Take a role and speak the dialogues; help rehearse.","Para":"Write the dialogues for the group and support Beginner, Letter and Word level learners throughout.","Story":"Write the dialogues for the group and support Beginner, Letter and Word level learners throughout."}},{"activity":"Sound-symbol games by level (small groups)","source":"M","ref":"p.12","tasks":{"Beginner":"'What is the first sound in the word nest?' 'Is there a letter that makes the sound /n/?' 'Can you name objects that start with the letter N?' Learners think and share names in the group.","Letter":"Write the rhyming ending -en on the board and ask learners to add new letters to form words: p + en = pen, t + en = ten, h + en = hen.","Word":"Say a word and tell its sounds, for example 'sun' = /s/ + /u/ + /n/. Then tell what word is formed if /r/ is put before 'at': r + at = rat. Do 8-10 such combinations; at first learners may form meaningless words, later only meaningful words.","Para":"Write two or three sounds on the board (for example Br, cl, st) and let the learners form words that start with those sounds; this builds a word list for the learner.","Story":"Write two or three sounds on the board (for example Br, cl, st) and let the learners form words that start with those sounds; this builds a word list for the learner."}},{"activity":"Self-writing: level tasks and review","source":"M","ref":"p.15","tasks":{"Beginner":"Draw a picture about the discussion and then write a few sentences about it, expressing thoughts freely. Review: say what they drew or wrote; read the text aloud once; the teacher may write the text in the notebook for them.","Letter":"Write about what they liked, using drawing and writing; write any words or sentences they can. Review: read the text aloud once; correct punctuation mistakes using the Barakhadi chart.","Word":"Write a sentence based on the conversation. Mistakes in spelling, punctuation and sentence structure are fine. Review: read it to the group; discuss and correct mistakes together.","Para":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation.","Story":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation."}}],"organisation":[{"grouping":"Whole class (big group)","how":"All learners of all levels sit in a 'U' shape arranged by level (Beginner, Letter, Word, Para, Story) so that the move to small groups is easy.","activities":["Warm-up: Singing and Spinning","Oral conversation: listening and storytelling","Dramatic presentation: introduction and reading","Dramatic presentation: performances and feedback","Sound-symbol activity: oral sound awareness","Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on the story we acted out (a folk tale about a clever fox or rabbit)"]},{"grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","how":"Learners of similar levels work together; the teacher gives each group a task for its level and spends more time with learners who need support. Rotate responsibilities (for example group leader).","activities":["Dramatic presentation: planning in small groups","Sound-symbol games by level"]},{"grouping":"Individual","how":"Each learner works on a task for their own level; the teacher moves around, observes difficulties and supports individuals.","activities":["Self-writing: individual writing","Self-writing: review and reading back","Daily reading (10 minutes)"]}],"materials":["A small object (chalk or pencil)","Stories discussed in the week (a story about a farmer","his field; a folk tale about a clever fox or rabbit)","Story","paper for dialogues","Open space (U-shape seating)","Board","chalk","letter cards","Picture card or topic on the board","Notebooks","crayons or pencils","Library books or storybooks"],"outcomes":["Learners take part in the oral conversation and speak without fear.","Learners present a role in the group drama and give feedback to others.","Learners respond to the sound-symbol task for today (Hearing the different sounds in words (pig, hat, cup)) at their own level.","Learners write about the story at their level and read it aloud.","Each learner reads a book for 10 minutes."],"observation":["Observe each learner's reading and writing during the individual tasks; note who needs individual support and how many learners share the same difficulty.","Note any learner whose level is improving; move the learner to the next level group when you see steady progress (manual p.5).","Record each learner's progress for the day in the notebook, according to the learner's level (manual p.4).","Use today's observations to adjust tomorrow's plan (manual p.5)."],"teacherNotes":["Saturday: this plan assumes Day 1 is a Monday (six teaching days per week). If your school week is different, hold the drama presentation on your Saturday and keep the other days in sequence.","Sound-symbol: for the first 4-5 days, play sound-based games with the learners at word level. Include the sounds learners find difficult when you prepare the Class Transaction Plan.","Writing has two parts, content and sequence: encourage learners to read what they wrote, improve it and rewrite it for clarity and correctness (manual p.15).","Pace: the manual says not to assume all learners progress at the same speed. Repeat a day's activity with the groups that need it before moving on.","Special needs: give extra time and prepare materials for slower learners; seat learners with hearing or vision difficulty at the front; for learners who reverse or confuse letters, trace letters on the letter card with a finger and write with dots to trace with a pencil (manual p.6)."],"components":[{"no":1,"key":"warmup","name":"Warm-up activities","keywords":["Singing and Spinning","two learners lead"],"rows":[1]},{"no":2,"key":"oral","name":"Oral Discussion","keywords":["listening and storytelling","every learner speaks"],"rows":[2]},{"no":3,"key":"story","name":"Story (Saturday: dramatic presentation)","keywords":["Saturday drama","choose a character","plan dialogues","perform in U shape","feedback"],"rows":[3,4,5]},{"no":4,"key":"sound","name":"Sound symbol games, Sound separation-pairing","keywords":["oral sound awareness","say the different sounds","level games in small groups"],"rows":[6,7]},{"no":5,"key":"mindwrite","name":"Individual-Writing (Day 2)","keywords":["discussion","write at own level","self-review (read aloud)"],"rows":[8,9,10]},{"no":6,"key":"reading","name":"Daily reading","keywords":["library book","read alone","teacher listens"],"rows":[11]}],"preLesson":null},{"programme":"TARL Literacy","id":"lit-007","day":7,"phase":1,"phaseLabel":"Phase 1 (Days 1-45)","title":"Story: a folk tale about a clever fox or rabbit (Day 2)","dayType":"Story Day 2 + Self-writing","focus":"Language game: Matching Words (rhyme) | Self-writing: what I did last Sunday","duration":70,"objectives":["Listen, speak and answer in the oral conversation (What did you see on your way?).","Retell the story, read it with expression, ask and answer questions about it and write answers.","Develop sound-symbol skills: Language game: Matching Words (rhyme).","Write about a topic at their own level and review the writing (what I did last Sunday).","Read independently for 10 minutes every day."],"sequence":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Rain clapping","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Everyone stands in a circle with eyes closed and keeps clapping: first one finger, then two, three, four and finally five fingers. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Stand in a circle, close the eyes and clap with 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 fingers.","tlm":"After the activity ask: Was it a gentle rain or a storm? How did you feel?","source":"M","ref":"p.8","n":1},{"activity":"Oral conversation: What did you see on your way?","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Ask learners to describe what they saw on their way to school. If they are hesitant, begin yourself: 'On my way I saw a bus full of people, a boy on a bicycle and an old man selling guavas. What did you see?'","learners":"Describe what they saw on the way to school and connect with what others share.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.9","n":2},{"activity":"Story (Day 2 of the story): retelling","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":6,"teacher":"Ask learners to retell yesterday's story in their own words. Prompt with questions on the beginning, middle and end.","learners":"Retell the story using their own words.","tlm":"The same story book as yesterday","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":3},{"activity":"Story: reading with actions and group questions","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":9,"teacher":"Learners practise reading with actions and expressions; one learner per group reads aloud to the class. Guide groups to make questions about the story (guide initially). Groups take turns to ask and answer each other's questions. Word-level learners also read aloud the consonants learned on the first day.","learners":"Read with actions; make questions (word-level learners help write them); ask and answer questions with another group.","tlm":"Story book, slate or paper for questions","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":4},{"activity":"Story: writing answers individually","grouping":"Individual","minutes":5,"teacher":"Para and Story level learners write answers to all questions individually; read and correct their responses after they finish.","learners":"Write the answers in their notebooks; Beginner/Letter/Word learners read or listen and answer orally.","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":5},{"activity":"Language game: Matching Words (rhyme)","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"A word is written on the board and learners hear words that rhyme with it, for example pen, den, men, ten. Observe each learner and give help where needed.","learners":"Play the game, take turns and read or say the words they make.","tlm":"Board and chalk","source":"M","ref":"p.18","n":6},{"activity":"Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on what I did last Sunday","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Start a conversation about a situation: 'what I did last Sunday'. Involve all learners and ask open-ended questions.","learners":"Take part in the discussion and share thoughts freely.","tlm":"Picture card or topic on the board","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":7},{"activity":"Self-writing: individual writing","grouping":"Individual","minutes":7,"teacher":"Give each level its task (see level table). Let learners take ownership of what they draw and write; mistakes are fine.","learners":"Draw and write about the topic at their level.","tlm":"Notebooks, crayons or pencils","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":8},{"activity":"Self-writing: review and reading back","grouping":"Individual","minutes":3,"teacher":"Ask each learner 'What did you draw or write?' and have them read it aloud once. Word-level learners read to the group; discuss spelling, punctuation and sentence structure. Help beginners by writing their text in the notebook for them if needed.","learners":"Read what they wrote; correct mistakes after listening to their own reading.","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":9},{"activity":"Daily reading (10 minutes)","grouping":"Individual","minutes":10,"teacher":"Give each learner a library book or any storybook. Move around, listen to individual readers and note their level.","learners":"Read independently a book of their choice.","tlm":"Library books or storybooks","source":"M","ref":"p.7","n":10}],"procedures":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Rain clapping","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","steps":[{"teacher":"Stand the learners in a circle and ask them to close their eyes. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Stand in a circle and close their eyes."},{"teacher":"Start clapping with one finger; then two fingers, three, four and finally five fingers.","learners":"Keep clapping, copying the change of fingers."},{"teacher":"After the activity ask: Was it a gentle rain or a storm? How did you feel?","learners":"Tell how they felt and what the sounds reminded them of."}]},{"activity":"Oral conversation: What did you see on your way?","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.9","steps":[{"teacher":"Ask: 'What did you see on your way to school today?'","learners":"Think about the way to school."},{"teacher":"If learners hesitate, start: 'On my way I saw a bus full of people, a boy on a bicycle and an old man selling guavas. What did you see?'","learners":"Listen to the model and then share their own observations."},{"teacher":"Connect learners' answers with each other.","learners":"Listen and add what they noticed."}]},{"activity":"Story - Day 2 (a folk tale about a clever fox or rabbit)","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.11","steps":[{"teacher":"Ask learners to retell the story they read yesterday in their own words.","learners":"Retell, helping each other remember."},{"teacher":"In small groups learners practise reading the story using actions and expressions; one learner from each group then reads aloud to the class.","learners":"Read with actions and expression; a representative reads aloud."},{"teacher":"Guide the groups to come up with questions about the story (guide initially). Word-level learners can support by helping write them down.","learners":"Make questions together."},{"teacher":"Groups take turns to ask and answer each other's questions. Useful kinds: questions whose answer is not in the text; questions needing thinking beyond the text; questions asking for an opinion.","learners":"Ask, answer and discuss in the groups."},{"teacher":"Word-level learners also read aloud the consonants they learned on the first day.","learners":"Read the consonant clusters aloud."}]},{"activity":"Language game: Matching Words (rhyme)","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.18","steps":[{"teacher":"Write a word on the board and say a few words that rhyme with it, for example pen, den, men, ten. Read the rhyming words aloud.","learners":"Listen and say the rhyming words after the teacher has read them."},{"teacher":"Repeat with a different word each day; rhyming words can be meaningful or meaningless.","learners":"Suggest more words that sound the same at the end."},{"teacher":"Ask learners to match words that sound alike.","learners":"Match rhyming words and read them aloud."}]},{"activity":"Self-writing: 'Discussion, Writing, Self-review'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.15","steps":[{"teacher":"Start a conversation about a situation: 'what I did last Sunday'. Involve all learners and ask open-ended questions.","learners":"Discuss and answer questions."},{"teacher":"Give writing time at each level: draw then write (Beginner), write about what they liked (Letter), a sentence (Word), a paragraph or story on a topic of their choice (Para/Story).","learners":"Write at their level and take ownership of the work."},{"teacher":"Review: ask 'What did you draw or write?' Have each learner read the text aloud once. Support with writing if needed.","learners":"Read aloud, listen to their pronunciation and correct mistakes."}]}],"levelTasks":[{"activity":"Story - Day 2: level-wise tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.11","tasks":{"Beginner":"Retell with the group by pointing to pictures or words; read aloud with group support (interpretation of the manual's group reading task).","Letter":"Read with the group, pointing to words; say the letters and words they know (interpretation of the manual's group reading task).","Word":"Support the group in writing the questions; read aloud the consonant clusters learned on the first day.","Para":"Ask the group's questions to another group, discuss them, then write answers to all questions individually; the teacher reads and corrects.","Story":"Ask the group's questions to another group, discuss them, then write answers to all questions individually; the teacher reads and corrects."}},{"activity":"Language game: Matching Words (rhyme) - level support","source":"I","ref":"p.18","tasks":{"Beginner":"Take part by saying or pointing to the letters involved and by listening carefully; Para and Story level partners help.","Letter":"Say the letters/sounds and give simple words they know.","Word":"Say and write words and short sentences for the game.","Para":"Write sentences with the words; help groups to record answers.","Story":"Write sentences or short stories with the words; help groups to record answers."}},{"activity":"Self-writing: level tasks and review","source":"M","ref":"p.15","tasks":{"Beginner":"Draw a picture about the discussion and then write a few sentences about it, expressing thoughts freely. Review: say what they drew or wrote; read the text aloud once; the teacher may write the text in the notebook for them.","Letter":"Write about what they liked, using drawing and writing; write any words or sentences they can. Review: read the text aloud once; correct punctuation mistakes using the Barakhadi chart.","Word":"Write a sentence based on the conversation. Mistakes in spelling, punctuation and sentence structure are fine. Review: read it to the group; discuss and correct mistakes together.","Para":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation.","Story":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation."}}],"organisation":[{"grouping":"Whole class (big group)","how":"All learners of all levels sit in a 'U' shape arranged by level (Beginner, Letter, Word, Para, Story) so that the move to small groups is easy.","activities":["Warm-up: Rain clapping","Oral conversation: What did you see on your way?","Story (Day 2 of the story): retelling","Language game: Matching Words (rhyme)","Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on what I did last Sunday"]},{"grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","how":"Learners of similar levels work together; the teacher gives each group a task for its level and spends more time with learners who need support. Rotate responsibilities (for example group leader).","activities":["Story: reading with actions and group questions"]},{"grouping":"Individual","how":"Each learner works on a task for their own level; the teacher moves around, observes difficulties and supports individuals.","activities":["Story: writing answers individually","Self-writing: individual writing","Self-writing: review and reading back","Daily reading (10 minutes)"]}],"materials":["After the activity ask: Was it a gentle rain or a storm? How did you feel?","The same story book as yesterday","Story book","slate or paper for questions","Notebooks","Board","chalk","Picture card or topic on the board","crayons or pencils","Library books or storybooks"],"outcomes":["Learners take part in the oral conversation and speak without fear.","Learners retell the story, read with expression and ask or answer questions at their level.","Learners respond to the sound-symbol task for today (Language game: Matching Words (rhyme)) at their own level.","Learners write about the topic at their level and read it aloud.","Each learner reads a book for 10 minutes."],"observation":["Observe each learner's reading and writing during the individual tasks; note who needs individual support and how many learners share the same difficulty.","Note any learner whose level is improving; move the learner to the next level group when you see steady progress (manual p.5).","Record each learner's progress for the day in the notebook, according to the learner's level (manual p.4).","Use today's observations to adjust tomorrow's plan (manual p.5)."],"teacherNotes":["Questions to elicit on Day 2: information questions (answer not in the text), thinking questions (needs knowledge beyond the text) and opinion questions (feedback on something in the text).","The manual lists the letter and word games but does not fix the slot in the daily timetable where they are used. This plan places them in the 10-minute sound-symbol / alphabet slot (interpretation).","Writing has two parts, content and sequence: encourage learners to read what they wrote, improve it and rewrite it for clarity and correctness (manual p.15).","Pace: the manual says not to assume all learners progress at the same speed. Repeat a day's activity with the groups that need it before moving on.","Special needs: give extra time and prepare materials for slower learners; seat learners with hearing or vision difficulty at the front; for learners who reverse or confuse letters, trace letters on the letter card with a finger and write with dots to trace with a pencil (manual p.6)."],"components":[{"no":1,"key":"warmup","name":"Warm-up activities","keywords":["Rain clapping","two learners lead"],"rows":[1]},{"no":2,"key":"oral","name":"Oral Discussion","keywords":["What did you see on your way?","every learner speaks"],"rows":[2]},{"no":3,"key":"story","name":"Story","keywords":["Day 2","retell","read with actions","group questions","ask and answer","write answers (Para/Story)"],"rows":[3,4,5]},{"no":4,"key":"sound","name":"Sound symbol games, Sound separation-pairing","keywords":["Matching Words (rhyme)","play in turns","level support"],"rows":[6]},{"no":5,"key":"mindwrite","name":"Individual-Writing (Day 2)","keywords":["discussion","write at own level","self-review (read aloud)"],"rows":[7,8,9]},{"no":6,"key":"reading","name":"Daily reading","keywords":["library book","read alone","teacher listens"],"rows":[10]}],"preLesson":null},{"programme":"TARL Literacy","id":"lit-008","day":8,"phase":1,"phaseLabel":"Phase 1 (Days 1-45)","title":"Story: a story about a village festival (Day 1)","dayType":"Story Day 1 + Mind mapping","focus":"Barakhadi / alphabet and phonics chart (line 9, letter 'd') | Mind map: farm","duration":70,"objectives":["Listen, speak and answer in the oral conversation (familiar topic).","Listen to and read a story with understanding; discuss it in big and small groups and respond at their own level.","Develop sound-symbol skills: Barakhadi / alphabet and phonics chart (line 9, letter 'd').","Build vocabulary through a mind map ('farm') and use the words at their own level.","Read independently for 10 minutes every day."],"sequence":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Writing with body parts","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Learners stand in a circle. Demonstrate writing the word 'sun' in the air with a finger, then ask them to write it with different body parts. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Write the word 'sun' in the air with the finger, then with the head, shoulders, knees or elbows.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.8","n":1},{"activity":"Oral conversation: familiar topic","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Hold a conversation on the topic 'my best friend and what we play'. Give each learner a chance to speak; be patient with learners who need extra time.","learners":"Talk about the topic and listen to others.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.9","n":2},{"activity":"Story (Day 1 of the story): reading aloud and discussion","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":8,"teacher":"Discuss the title or picture of the story with the learners. Read the story aloud with expression and voice modulation (learners do not repeat after you). Discuss it, with emphasis on judgment questions. Read it again slowly, pointing to each word.","learners":"Talk about the title/picture; listen; answer questions; follow each word with a finger in their own copy.","tlm":"A story from the school library (a story about a village festival), a copy for each learner","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":3},{"activity":"Story: reading in small groups","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":7,"teacher":"Form level-wise groups with a group leader. Learners read the story one sentence at a time while the others follow with their fingers. Para and Story level learners practise reading with emotion and expression.","learners":"Read the story sentence by sentence, supporting each other; the group leader helps.","tlm":"Story book copies","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":4},{"activity":"Story: level-wise individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":5,"teacher":"Give each learner the task for their level (see level table) and support those who need it.","learners":"Beginner/Letter: find and write favourite words or letters. Word: find consonant clusters. Para/Story: silently read, find unfamiliar and rhyming words.","tlm":"Story book, notebooks, board","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":5},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart: big group reading","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":3,"teacher":"Show the Barakhadi chart and ask which letter they like. Read the letter 'd' on the chart; learners listen carefully and point to it on their own chart (they do not repeat after you).","learners":"Listen and point to the letter on their own chart.","tlm":"Barakhadi chart, alphabet or phonics chart","source":"M","ref":"p.13","n":6},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart: small-group practice","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Learners practise reading the alphabet or phonics chart in groups and help each other. One learner per group reads aloud. Occasionally ask learners to identify the sounds of letters. Give each level its group task.","learners":"Read the chart in groups; one learner reads aloud; do the level task.","tlm":"Alphabet or phonics chart, board or floor","source":"M","ref":"p.13","n":7},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart: individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":2,"teacher":"Give each learner an individual task for their level and observe closely; assist any learner who needs individual support.","learners":"Say and write a letter or word, a sentence or a short paragraph (by level).","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.13","n":8},{"activity":"Mind mapping (Day 1): the word 'farm'","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Ask: 'What words come to your mind when you hear the word farm?' Write learners' answers on the board or floor (Para and Story level learners write the words themselves). Guide the map towards the learning objective. Example words: paddy, wheat, mustard, sugarcane, plough, spade, sickle, rope, cow, bullock, goat, hen.","learners":"Say words connected with 'farm'; share the meaning and feeling of words.","tlm":"Board, chalk (or floor)","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":9},{"activity":"Mind mapping: classify the words","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":4,"teacher":"Ask learners to classify the words in groups, for example: Crops: paddy, wheat, mustard, sugarcane; Tools: plough, spade, sickle, rope; Animals: cow, bullock, goat, hen.","learners":"Sort the words into groups and say why.","tlm":"Board, chalk, word cards (optional)","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":10},{"activity":"Mind mapping: level-wise individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":6,"teacher":"Give each learner the individual task for their level; observe closely and give individual support. Display corrected stories on the wall.","learners":"Complete the task for their level (see level table).","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":11},{"activity":"Daily reading (10 minutes)","grouping":"Individual","minutes":10,"teacher":"Give each learner a library book or any storybook. Move around, listen to individual readers and note their level.","learners":"Read independently a book of their choice.","tlm":"Library books or storybooks","source":"M","ref":"p.7","n":12}],"procedures":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Writing with body parts","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","steps":[{"teacher":"Stand the learners in a circle. Demonstrate writing the word 'sun' in the air with your finger.","learners":"Watch and then copy with their own finger."},{"teacher":"Ask them to write it again using shoulders and other body parts (head, shoulders, knees, ...).","learners":"Write the letters in the air with the named body part."},{"teacher":"Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Take turns to lead."}]},{"activity":"Oral conversation: familiar topic","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.9","steps":[{"teacher":"Introduce the topic: 'my best friend and what we play'.","learners":"Think about their own experience."},{"teacher":"Ask open questions; give every learner a chance. Involve learners who speak less.","learners":"Speak freely and without fear."},{"teacher":"Praise efforts and sum up.","learners":"Listen and respect each other's ideas."}]},{"activity":"Story - Day 1 (a story about a village festival)","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.10","steps":[{"teacher":"Discuss the title or picture of the story with the learners.","learners":"Talk about what they see and what the story may be about."},{"teacher":"Read the story aloud with expression and proper voice modulation. Learners should not simply repeat after you.","learners":"Listen carefully and enjoy the story."},{"teacher":"Discuss the story: factual, logical, vocabulary-based, judgment or opinion questions (today's focus: judgment: Was the character right or wrong? Was that a good thing to do? Why?). Begin in the home language if needed.","learners":"Think and respond thoughtfully; every learner takes part."},{"teacher":"Read the story again slowly, pointing to each word. Make sure each learner has a copy and follows with a finger.","learners":"Follow each word with their finger."},{"teacher":"Ask learners to read in small groups; select a group leader who helps the others. Learners read one sentence at a time while the others point with fingers.","learners":"Read with the help of one another."}]},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart activity (line 9)","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Small group (level-wise) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.13","steps":[{"teacher":"Show the Barakhadi chart and ask the learners which letter they like. Where is the letter 'd'?","learners":"Look for the letter on the chart."},{"teacher":"Read the letter 'd' on the chart. Learners listen and point to it on their own chart. Make sure they do not repeat after you.","learners":"Listen and point to the letter."},{"teacher":"Learners read the alphabet or phonics chart in their groups and help each other; one learner from each group comes forward to read aloud.","learners":"Read in groups; the representative reads aloud."},{"teacher":"Occasionally ask them to identify the sounds of letters from the chart.","learners":"Say the sound of the letter you point to."},{"teacher":"As an extra activity, write some letters on the floor, call out each letter one by one and let the learners jump onto the correct letter.","learners":"Jump onto the letter that is called."}]},{"activity":"Mind mapping: 'farm'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Small group (level-wise) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.14","steps":[{"teacher":"Choose a word that can generate many related words: 'farm'. Ask: 'What words come to your mind when you hear the word farm?' Write the answers on the board or floor.","learners":"Say words they link with 'farm'."},{"teacher":"Discuss the words: what they mean and how they are connected.","learners":"Explain their words and listen to others."},{"teacher":"In small groups, let the learners classify the words (Crops: paddy, wheat, mustard, sugarcane; Tools: plough, spade, sickle, rope; Animals: cow, bullock, goat, hen).","learners":"Sort the words into groups."},{"teacher":"Give the individual tasks by level and help each learner.","learners":"Work individually; read the work aloud at the end if time allows."}]}],"levelTasks":[{"activity":"Story - Day 1: individual tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.10","tasks":{"Beginner":"Circle or search for a favourite word or letter in the story and say it aloud. If a learner cannot draw a circle, write words on the board and ask them to identify them.","Letter":"Find, read and write favourite words from the story.","Word":"Find the consonant clusters in the story, read them and write them in the notebook.","Para":"Silently read the story from the textbook; find unfamiliar words and try to understand them; find rhyming words, use them in sentences and write in the notebook; ask other groups for meanings; make questions in groups.","Story":"Silently read the story; find unfamiliar words and rhyming words; practise reading with emotion; one group reads sentences formed with consonant clusters to the other group; ask and answer group questions (information, thinking and opinion questions)."}},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart: level tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.13","tasks":{"Beginner":"Small group: read the chart in the group; find and write favourite letters from the line. Individual: say and write a letter of their choice.","Letter":"Small group: read the chart; find and write favourite letters or words from any line. Individual: say a word on their own that begins with any letter.","Word":"Small group: write one or two lines of letters on the board or floor and use them to form words. Individual: speak and write sentences using words they know.","Para":"Small group: prepare word lists using the Barakhadi chart (for example items found in a shop or in the kitchen). Individual: write short paragraphs using the words formed with the Barakhadi chart.","Story":"Small group: prepare word lists using the Barakhadi chart. Individual: write short paragraphs using the words formed with the Barakhadi chart."}},{"activity":"Mind mapping 'farm': level tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.14","tasks":{"Beginner":"Circle all the words that contain the letter 'A' on the board; make a list. See how many learners find the most words.","Letter":"Circle all the words that contain the letter 'A' and make a list of them.","Word":"Use 4-5 words (for example cow, hen, goat, rope, paddy) to form sentences, starting with words of one or two syllables. Example: Dream - I had a dream last night.","Para":"Choose any five words from the map and create a story with them. Use consonant clusters correctly, read the story aloud, correct mistakes of sentence structure, spelling or grammar, then display it on the wall.","Story":"Choose any five words from the map and create a story with them. Use consonant clusters correctly, read the story aloud, correct mistakes of sentence structure, spelling or grammar, then display it on the wall."}}],"organisation":[{"grouping":"Whole class (big group)","how":"All learners of all levels sit in a 'U' shape arranged by level (Beginner, Letter, Word, Para, Story) so that the move to small groups is easy.","activities":["Warm-up: Writing with body parts","Oral conversation: familiar topic","Story (Day 1 of the story): reading aloud and discussion","Barakhadi chart: big group reading","Mind mapping (Day 1): the word 'farm'"]},{"grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","how":"Learners of similar levels work together; the teacher gives each group a task for its level and spends more time with learners who need support. Rotate responsibilities (for example group leader).","activities":["Story: reading in small groups","Barakhadi chart: small-group practice","Mind mapping: classify the words"]},{"grouping":"Individual","how":"Each learner works on a task for their own level; the teacher moves around, observes difficulties and supports individuals.","activities":["Story: level-wise individual tasks","Barakhadi chart: individual tasks","Mind mapping: level-wise individual tasks","Daily reading (10 minutes)"]}],"materials":["A story from the school library (a story about a village festival)","a copy for each learner","Story book copies","Story book","notebooks","board","Barakhadi chart","alphabet or phonics chart","Alphabet or phonics chart","board or floor","Notebooks","Board","chalk (or floor)","chalk","word cards (optional)","Library books or storybooks"],"outcomes":["Learners take part in the oral conversation and speak without fear.","Learners show understanding of the story in the discussion and complete the task for their level.","Learners respond to the sound-symbol task for today (Barakhadi / alphabet and phonics chart (line 9, letter 'd')) at their own level.","Learners add words to the mind map and use them in sentences or a story at their level.","Each learner reads a book for 10 minutes."],"observation":["Observe each learner's reading and writing during the individual tasks; note who needs individual support and how many learners share the same difficulty.","Note any learner whose level is improving; move the learner to the next level group when you see steady progress (manual p.5).","Record each learner's progress for the day in the notebook, according to the learner's level (manual p.4).","Use today's observations to adjust tomorrow's plan (manual p.5)."],"teacherNotes":["Story selection: the manual asks teachers to use picture story books or stories in the school library. Today's suggested theme (a story about a village festival) is a planning suggestion; use any suitable story you have.","Barakhadi: learners who need extra time should get repeated practice using one or two sound units at a time. Topic-based discussion helps oral expression, thinking and understanding.","Mind mapping topic for this day: 'farm'. The manual's example uses the word 'shop'; today's topic follows the same method.","Pace: the manual says not to assume all learners progress at the same speed. Repeat a day's activity with the groups that need it before moving on.","Special needs: give extra time and prepare materials for slower learners; seat learners with hearing or vision difficulty at the front; for learners who reverse or confuse letters, trace letters on the letter card with a finger and write with dots to trace with a pencil (manual p.6)."],"components":[{"no":1,"key":"warmup","name":"Warm-up activities","keywords":["Writing with body parts","two learners lead"],"rows":[1]},{"no":2,"key":"oral","name":"Oral Discussion","keywords":["familiar topic","every learner speaks"],"rows":[2]},{"no":3,"key":"story","name":"Story","keywords":["Day 1","title / picture talk","read aloud with expression","judgment questions","re-read pointing","group reading","level tasks"],"rows":[3,4,5]},{"no":4,"key":"sound","name":"Sound symbol games, Sound separation-pairing","keywords":["Barakhadi / alphabet chart","listen and point (no repeating)","group reading","level tasks"],"rows":[6,7,8]},{"no":5,"key":"mindwrite","name":"Mind Mapping (Day 1)","keywords":["mind map: farm","classify the words","level task: circle letter A / sentences / story"],"rows":[9,10,11]},{"no":6,"key":"reading","name":"Daily reading","keywords":["library book","read alone","teacher listens"],"rows":[12]}],"preLesson":null},{"programme":"TARL Literacy","id":"lit-009","day":9,"phase":1,"phaseLabel":"Phase 1 (Days 1-45)","title":"Story: a story about a village festival (Day 2)","dayType":"Story Day 2 + Self-writing","focus":"Blending sounds to form words (map, jam, fox) | Self-writing: my best friend","duration":70,"objectives":["Listen, speak and answer in the oral conversation (conversation on a picture).","Retell the story, read it with expression, ask and answer questions about it and write answers.","Develop sound-symbol skills: Blending sounds to form words (map, jam, fox).","Write about a topic at their own level and review the writing (my best friend).","Read independently for 10 minutes every day."],"sequence":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Alphabet song (last-letter word chain)","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Say a word to the big group, for example 'road'. Learners say a word that starts with the last letter ('d'). A learner who cannot say a word is out. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Say a word that starts with the last letter of the previous word; step out if unable to.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.8","n":1},{"activity":"Oral conversation: conversation on a picture","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Show a picture of a farmer ploughing his field and ask what is happening, who is doing what and what is happening around them. Let learners think creatively and even make up a story.","learners":"Look at the picture, answer questions and make up their own story about it.","tlm":"Picture card of a farmer ploughing his field","source":"M","ref":"p.9","n":2},{"activity":"Story (Day 2 of the story): retelling","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":6,"teacher":"Ask learners to retell yesterday's story in their own words. Prompt with questions on the beginning, middle and end.","learners":"Retell the story using their own words.","tlm":"The same story book as yesterday","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":3},{"activity":"Story: reading with actions and group questions","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":9,"teacher":"Learners practise reading with actions and expressions; one learner per group reads aloud to the class. Guide groups to make questions about the story (guide initially). Groups take turns to ask and answer each other's questions. Word-level learners also read aloud the consonants learned on the first day.","learners":"Read with actions; make questions (word-level learners help write them); ask and answer questions with another group.","tlm":"Story book, slate or paper for questions","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":4},{"activity":"Story: writing answers individually","grouping":"Individual","minutes":5,"teacher":"Para and Story level learners write answers to all questions individually; read and correct their responses after they finish.","learners":"Write the answers in their notebooks; Beginner/Letter/Word learners read or listen and answer orally.","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":5},{"activity":"Sound-symbol activity: oral sound awareness","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":4,"teacher":"Say separate sounds from 10-12 words (map: m - a - p; jam: j - a - m; fox: f - o - x; bed: b - e - d) and ask learners to blend the sounds into the complete word.","learners":"Listen to the separate sounds and blend them to say the whole word.","tlm":"None (oral activity)","source":"M","ref":"p.12","n":6},{"activity":"Sound-symbol games by level","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":6,"teacher":"Give each level group its game (see level table). Move among the groups and help those who need support; say each word clearly.","learners":"Play the game for their level in small groups.","tlm":"Board, chalk, letter cards","source":"M","ref":"p.12","n":7},{"activity":"Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on my best friend","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Start a conversation about a picture card: 'my best friend'. Involve all learners and ask open-ended questions.","learners":"Take part in the discussion and share thoughts freely.","tlm":"Picture card or topic on the board","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":8},{"activity":"Self-writing: individual writing","grouping":"Individual","minutes":7,"teacher":"Give each level its task (see level table). Let learners take ownership of what they draw and write; mistakes are fine.","learners":"Draw and write about the topic at their level.","tlm":"Notebooks, crayons or pencils","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":9},{"activity":"Self-writing: review and reading back","grouping":"Individual","minutes":3,"teacher":"Ask each learner 'What did you draw or write?' and have them read it aloud once. Word-level learners read to the group; discuss spelling, punctuation and sentence structure. Help beginners by writing their text in the notebook for them if needed.","learners":"Read what they wrote; correct mistakes after listening to their own reading.","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":10},{"activity":"Daily reading (10 minutes)","grouping":"Individual","minutes":10,"teacher":"Give each learner a library book or any storybook. Move around, listen to individual readers and note their level.","learners":"Read independently a book of their choice.","tlm":"Library books or storybooks","source":"M","ref":"p.7","n":11}],"procedures":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Alphabet song (last-letter word chain)","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","steps":[{"teacher":"Say the word 'road' to the big group and show that its last letter is 'd'.","learners":"Listen and think of a word starting with 'd'."},{"teacher":"Ask learners in turn to say a word that starts with the last letter of the previous word. Example: rain -> nest.","learners":"Say a word in turn; anyone who cannot say a word is out of the game."},{"teacher":"Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Lead the game when it is their turn."}]},{"activity":"Oral conversation: conversation on a picture","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.9","steps":[{"teacher":"Show the picture of a farmer ploughing his field.","learners":"Look carefully."},{"teacher":"Ask: What is happening in the picture? Who is doing what? What is happening around them? Then: What might happen next?","learners":"Answer in their own words; every learner gets a chance."},{"teacher":"Let learners imagine and make up a short story from the picture.","learners":"Tell their stories to the class."}]},{"activity":"Story - Day 2 (a story about a village festival)","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.11","steps":[{"teacher":"Ask learners to retell the story they read yesterday in their own words.","learners":"Retell, helping each other remember."},{"teacher":"In small groups learners practise reading the story using actions and expressions; one learner from each group then reads aloud to the class.","learners":"Read with actions and expression; a representative reads aloud."},{"teacher":"Guide the groups to come up with questions about the story (guide initially). Word-level learners can support by helping write them down.","learners":"Make questions together."},{"teacher":"Groups take turns to ask and answer each other's questions. Useful kinds: questions whose answer is not in the text; questions needing thinking beyond the text; questions asking for an opinion.","learners":"Ask, answer and discuss in the groups."},{"teacher":"Word-level learners also read aloud the consonants they learned on the first day.","learners":"Read the consonant clusters aloud."}]},{"activity":"Sound-symbol: oral and level games","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.12","steps":[{"teacher":"Say separate sounds from 10-12 words (map: m - a - p; jam: j - a - m; fox: f - o - x; bed: b - e - d) and ask learners to blend the sounds into the complete word.","learners":"Listen to the separate sounds and blend them to say the whole word."},{"teacher":"Write the sounds or words for the day on the board and give each level group its task (see the level table).","learners":"Work in small groups and share their answers."},{"teacher":"Say each word clearly with distinct pronunciation. Give learners enough time to respond and think; use words learners commonly use at home (regional language and the medium of instruction).","learners":"Think, say and write the sounds."}]},{"activity":"Self-writing: 'Discussion, Writing, Self-review'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.15","steps":[{"teacher":"Start a conversation about a picture card: 'my best friend'. Involve all learners and ask open-ended questions.","learners":"Discuss and answer questions."},{"teacher":"Give writing time at each level: draw then write (Beginner), write about what they liked (Letter), a sentence (Word), a paragraph or story on a topic of their choice (Para/Story).","learners":"Write at their level and take ownership of the work."},{"teacher":"Review: ask 'What did you draw or write?' Have each learner read the text aloud once. Support with writing if needed.","learners":"Read aloud, listen to their pronunciation and correct mistakes."}]}],"levelTasks":[{"activity":"Story - Day 2: level-wise tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.11","tasks":{"Beginner":"Retell with the group by pointing to pictures or words; read aloud with group support (interpretation of the manual's group reading task).","Letter":"Read with the group, pointing to words; say the letters and words they know (interpretation of the manual's group reading task).","Word":"Support the group in writing the questions; read aloud the consonant clusters learned on the first day.","Para":"Ask the group's questions to another group, discuss them, then write answers to all questions individually; the teacher reads and corrects.","Story":"Ask the group's questions to another group, discuss them, then write answers to all questions individually; the teacher reads and corrects."}},{"activity":"Sound-symbol games by level (small groups)","source":"M","ref":"p.12","tasks":{"Beginner":"'What is the first sound in the word apple?' 'Is there a letter that makes the sound /a/?' 'Can you name objects that start with the letter A?' Learners think and share names in the group.","Letter":"Write the rhyming ending -un on the board and ask learners to add new letters to form words: s + un = sun, r + un = run, f + un = fun.","Word":"Say a word and tell its sounds, for example 'sun' = /s/ + /u/ + /n/. Then tell what word is formed if /r/ is put before 'at': r + at = rat. Do 8-10 such combinations; at first learners may form meaningless words, later only meaningful words.","Para":"Write two or three sounds on the board (for example Br, cl, st) and let the learners form words that start with those sounds; this builds a word list for the learner.","Story":"Write two or three sounds on the board (for example Br, cl, st) and let the learners form words that start with those sounds; this builds a word list for the learner."}},{"activity":"Self-writing: level tasks and review","source":"M","ref":"p.15","tasks":{"Beginner":"Draw a picture about the discussion and then write a few sentences about it, expressing thoughts freely. Review: say what they drew or wrote; read the text aloud once; the teacher may write the text in the notebook for them.","Letter":"Write about what they liked, using drawing and writing; write any words or sentences they can. Review: read the text aloud once; correct punctuation mistakes using the Barakhadi chart.","Word":"Write a sentence based on the conversation. Mistakes in spelling, punctuation and sentence structure are fine. Review: read it to the group; discuss and correct mistakes together.","Para":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation.","Story":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation."}}],"organisation":[{"grouping":"Whole class (big group)","how":"All learners of all levels sit in a 'U' shape arranged by level (Beginner, Letter, Word, Para, Story) so that the move to small groups is easy.","activities":["Warm-up: Alphabet song (last-letter word chain)","Oral conversation: conversation on a picture","Story (Day 2 of the story): retelling","Sound-symbol activity: oral sound awareness","Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on my best friend"]},{"grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","how":"Learners of similar levels work together; the teacher gives each group a task for its level and spends more time with learners who need support. Rotate responsibilities (for example group leader).","activities":["Story: reading with actions and group questions","Sound-symbol games by level"]},{"grouping":"Individual","how":"Each learner works on a task for their own level; the teacher moves around, observes difficulties and supports individuals.","activities":["Story: writing answers individually","Self-writing: individual writing","Self-writing: review and reading back","Daily reading (10 minutes)"]}],"materials":["Picture card of a farmer ploughing his field","The same story book as yesterday","Story book","slate or paper for questions","Notebooks","Board","chalk","letter cards","Picture card or topic on the board","crayons or pencils","Library books or storybooks"],"outcomes":["Learners take part in the oral conversation and speak without fear.","Learners retell the story, read with expression and ask or answer questions at their level.","Learners respond to the sound-symbol task for today (Blending sounds to form words (map, jam, fox)) at their own level.","Learners write about the topic at their level and read it aloud.","Each learner reads a book for 10 minutes."],"observation":["Observe each learner's reading and writing during the individual tasks; note who needs individual support and how many learners share the same difficulty.","Note any learner whose level is improving; move the learner to the next level group when you see steady progress (manual p.5).","Record each learner's progress for the day in the notebook, according to the learner's level (manual p.4).","Use today's observations to adjust tomorrow's plan (manual p.5)."],"teacherNotes":["Questions to elicit on Day 2: information questions (answer not in the text), thinking questions (needs knowledge beyond the text) and opinion questions (feedback on something in the text).","Sound-symbol: for the first 4-5 days, play sound-based games with the learners at word level. Include the sounds learners find difficult when you prepare the Class Transaction Plan.","Writing has two parts, content and sequence: encourage learners to read what they wrote, improve it and rewrite it for clarity and correctness (manual p.15).","Pace: the manual says not to assume all learners progress at the same speed. Repeat a day's activity with the groups that need it before moving on.","Special needs: give extra time and prepare materials for slower learners; seat learners with hearing or vision difficulty at the front; for learners who reverse or confuse letters, trace letters on the letter card with a finger and write with dots to trace with a pencil (manual p.6)."],"components":[{"no":1,"key":"warmup","name":"Warm-up activities","keywords":["Alphabet song (last-letter word chain)","two learners lead"],"rows":[1]},{"no":2,"key":"oral","name":"Oral Discussion","keywords":["conversation on a picture","every learner speaks"],"rows":[2]},{"no":3,"key":"story","name":"Story","keywords":["Day 2","retell","read with actions","group questions","ask and answer","write answers (Para/Story)"],"rows":[3,4,5]},{"no":4,"key":"sound","name":"Sound symbol games, Sound separation-pairing","keywords":["oral sound awareness","blend sounds to a word","level games in small groups"],"rows":[6,7]},{"no":5,"key":"mindwrite","name":"Individual-Writing (Day 2)","keywords":["discussion","write at own level","self-review (read aloud)"],"rows":[8,9,10]},{"no":6,"key":"reading","name":"Daily reading","keywords":["library book","read alone","teacher listens"],"rows":[11]}],"preLesson":null},{"programme":"TARL Literacy","id":"lit-010","day":10,"phase":1,"phaseLabel":"Phase 1 (Days 1-45)","title":"Story: a story about helping a neighbour (Day 1)","dayType":"Story Day 1 + Mind mapping","focus":"Language game: Matching Words (rhyme) | Mind map: river","duration":70,"objectives":["Listen, speak and answer in the oral conversation (listening and storytelling).","Listen to and read a story with understanding; discuss it in big and small groups and respond at their own level.","Develop sound-symbol skills: Language game: Matching Words (rhyme).","Build vocabulary through a mind map ('river') and use the words at their own level.","Read independently for 10 minutes every day."],"sequence":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Handkerchief game","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Learners sit in a circle and clap while singing a rhyme ('I caught a Fish Alive'). One learner runs outside the circle with a handkerchief and secretly places it behind another learner, who must chase the runner. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Sit in a circle, clap and sing; run, place the handkerchief or chase as the game requires.","tlm":"A handkerchief","source":"M","ref":"p.8","n":1},{"activity":"Oral conversation: listening and storytelling","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Tell an interesting story starter and involve the learners: 'A little cloud fell into our courtyard. What did we do?' Let learners imagine and continue the story.","learners":"Listen to the teacher, then imagine and continue the story. Learners can also recite a rhyme or story they know.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.9","n":2},{"activity":"Story (Day 1 of the story): reading aloud and discussion","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":8,"teacher":"Discuss the title or picture of the story with the learners. Read the story aloud with expression and voice modulation (learners do not repeat after you). Discuss it, with emphasis on opinion questions. Read it again slowly, pointing to each word.","learners":"Talk about the title/picture; listen; answer questions; follow each word with a finger in their own copy.","tlm":"A story from the school library (a story about helping a neighbour), a copy for each learner","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":3},{"activity":"Story: reading in small groups","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":7,"teacher":"Form level-wise groups with a group leader. Learners read the story one sentence at a time while the others follow with their fingers. Para and Story level learners practise reading with emotion and expression.","learners":"Read the story sentence by sentence, supporting each other; the group leader helps.","tlm":"Story book copies","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":4},{"activity":"Story: level-wise individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":5,"teacher":"Give each learner the task for their level (see level table) and support those who need it.","learners":"Beginner/Letter: find and write favourite words or letters. Word: find consonant clusters. Para/Story: silently read, find unfamiliar and rhyming words.","tlm":"Story book, notebooks, board","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":5},{"activity":"Language game: Matching Words (rhyme)","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"A word is written on the board and learners hear words that rhyme with it, for example pen, den, men, ten. Observe each learner and give help where needed.","learners":"Play the game, take turns and read or say the words they make.","tlm":"Board and chalk","source":"M","ref":"p.18","n":6},{"activity":"Mind mapping (Day 1): the word 'river'","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Ask: 'What words come to your mind when you hear the word river?' Write learners' answers on the board or floor (Para and Story level learners write the words themselves). Guide the map towards the learning objective. Example words: fish, crab, frog, duck, boat, oar, net, rope, sand, bank, bridge, reed.","learners":"Say words connected with 'river'; share the meaning and feeling of words.","tlm":"Board, chalk (or floor)","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":7},{"activity":"Mind mapping: classify the words","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":4,"teacher":"Ask learners to classify the words in groups, for example: Creatures: fish, crab, frog, duck; Boats and ropes: boat, oar, net, rope; Around the river: sand, bank, bridge, reed.","learners":"Sort the words into groups and say why.","tlm":"Board, chalk, word cards (optional)","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":8},{"activity":"Mind mapping: level-wise individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":6,"teacher":"Give each learner the individual task for their level; observe closely and give individual support. Display corrected stories on the wall.","learners":"Complete the task for their level (see level table).","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":9},{"activity":"Daily reading (10 minutes)","grouping":"Individual","minutes":10,"teacher":"Give each learner a library book or any storybook. Move around, listen to individual readers and note their level.","learners":"Read independently a book of their choice.","tlm":"Library books or storybooks","source":"M","ref":"p.7","n":10}],"procedures":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Handkerchief game","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","steps":[{"teacher":"Seat the learners in a circle and start clapping and singing the rhyme 'I caught a Fish Alive'.","learners":"Clap and sing together."},{"teacher":"One learner runs outside the circle holding a handkerchief and secretly places it behind another learner.","learners":"Everyone keeps clapping; the learner who finds the handkerchief behind them takes it and chases the runner."},{"teacher":"If the runner sits in the chaser's place before being caught, they stay in the game; if caught, they are out. Continue in this way.","learners":"Play fairly and take turns."}]},{"activity":"Oral conversation: listening and storytelling","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.9","steps":[{"teacher":"Say the starter: 'A little cloud fell into our courtyard. What did we do?'","learners":"Listen and imagine."},{"teacher":"Ask learners to continue the story one by one. Encourage those who speak less.","learners":"Add ideas to the story."},{"teacher":"Invite a learner to recite a poem or rhyme they know.","learners":"Recite and listen to others."}]},{"activity":"Story - Day 1 (a story about helping a neighbour)","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.10","steps":[{"teacher":"Discuss the title or picture of the story with the learners.","learners":"Talk about what they see and what the story may be about."},{"teacher":"Read the story aloud with expression and proper voice modulation. Learners should not simply repeat after you.","learners":"Listen carefully and enjoy the story."},{"teacher":"Discuss the story: factual, logical, vocabulary-based, judgment or opinion questions (today's focus: opinion: What did you like best? What would you have done in the story?). Begin in the home language if needed.","learners":"Think and respond thoughtfully; every learner takes part."},{"teacher":"Read the story again slowly, pointing to each word. Make sure each learner has a copy and follows with a finger.","learners":"Follow each word with their finger."},{"teacher":"Ask learners to read in small groups; select a group leader who helps the others. Learners read one sentence at a time while the others point with fingers.","learners":"Read with the help of one another."}]},{"activity":"Language game: Matching Words (rhyme)","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.18","steps":[{"teacher":"Write a word on the board and say a few words that rhyme with it, for example pen, den, men, ten. Read the rhyming words aloud.","learners":"Listen and say the rhyming words after the teacher has read them."},{"teacher":"Repeat with a different word each day; rhyming words can be meaningful or meaningless.","learners":"Suggest more words that sound the same at the end."},{"teacher":"Ask learners to match words that sound alike.","learners":"Match rhyming words and read them aloud."}]},{"activity":"Mind mapping: 'river'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Small group (level-wise) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.14","steps":[{"teacher":"Choose a word that can generate many related words: 'river'. Ask: 'What words come to your mind when you hear the word river?' Write the answers on the board or floor.","learners":"Say words they link with 'river'."},{"teacher":"Discuss the words: what they mean and how they are connected.","learners":"Explain their words and listen to others."},{"teacher":"In small groups, let the learners classify the words (Creatures: fish, crab, frog, duck; Boats and ropes: boat, oar, net, rope; Around the river: sand, bank, bridge, reed).","learners":"Sort the words into groups."},{"teacher":"Give the individual tasks by level and help each learner.","learners":"Work individually; read the work aloud at the end if time allows."}]}],"levelTasks":[{"activity":"Story - Day 1: individual tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.10","tasks":{"Beginner":"Circle or search for a favourite word or letter in the story and say it aloud. If a learner cannot draw a circle, write words on the board and ask them to identify them.","Letter":"Find, read and write favourite words from the story.","Word":"Find the consonant clusters in the story, read them and write them in the notebook.","Para":"Silently read the story from the textbook; find unfamiliar words and try to understand them; find rhyming words, use them in sentences and write in the notebook; ask other groups for meanings; make questions in groups.","Story":"Silently read the story; find unfamiliar words and rhyming words; practise reading with emotion; one group reads sentences formed with consonant clusters to the other group; ask and answer group questions (information, thinking and opinion questions)."}},{"activity":"Language game: Matching Words (rhyme) - level support","source":"I","ref":"p.18","tasks":{"Beginner":"Take part by saying or pointing to the letters involved and by listening carefully; Para and Story level partners help.","Letter":"Say the letters/sounds and give simple words they know.","Word":"Say and write words and short sentences for the game.","Para":"Write sentences with the words; help groups to record answers.","Story":"Write sentences or short stories with the words; help groups to record answers."}},{"activity":"Mind mapping 'river': level tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.14","tasks":{"Beginner":"Circle all the words that contain the letter 'R' on the board; make a list. See how many learners find the most words.","Letter":"Circle all the words that contain the letter 'R' and make a list of them.","Word":"Use 4-5 words (for example net, oar, bank, boat, crab) to form sentences, starting with words of one or two syllables. Example: Dream - I had a dream last night.","Para":"Choose any five words from the map and create a story with them. Use consonant clusters correctly, read the story aloud, correct mistakes of sentence structure, spelling or grammar, then display it on the wall.","Story":"Choose any five words from the map and create a story with them. Use consonant clusters correctly, read the story aloud, correct mistakes of sentence structure, spelling or grammar, then display it on the wall."}}],"organisation":[{"grouping":"Whole class (big group)","how":"All learners of all levels sit in a 'U' shape arranged by level (Beginner, Letter, Word, Para, Story) so that the move to small groups is easy.","activities":["Warm-up: Handkerchief game","Oral conversation: listening and storytelling","Story (Day 1 of the story): reading aloud and discussion","Language game: Matching Words (rhyme)","Mind mapping (Day 1): the word 'river'"]},{"grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","how":"Learners of similar levels work together; the teacher gives each group a task for its level and spends more time with learners who need support. Rotate responsibilities (for example group leader).","activities":["Story: reading in small groups","Mind mapping: classify the words"]},{"grouping":"Individual","how":"Each learner works on a task for their own level; the teacher moves around, observes difficulties and supports individuals.","activities":["Story: level-wise individual tasks","Mind mapping: level-wise individual tasks","Daily reading (10 minutes)"]}],"materials":["A handkerchief","A story from the school library (a story about helping a neighbour)","a copy for each learner","Story book copies","Story book","notebooks","board","Board","chalk","chalk (or floor)","word cards (optional)","Notebooks","Library books or storybooks"],"outcomes":["Learners take part in the oral conversation and speak without fear.","Learners show understanding of the story in the discussion and complete the task for their level.","Learners respond to the sound-symbol task for today (Language game: Matching Words (rhyme)) at their own level.","Learners add words to the mind map and use them in sentences or a story at their level.","Each learner reads a book for 10 minutes."],"observation":["Observe each learner's reading and writing during the individual tasks; note who needs individual support and how many learners share the same difficulty.","Note any learner whose level is improving; move the learner to the next level group when you see steady progress (manual p.5).","Record each learner's progress for the day in the notebook, according to the learner's level (manual p.4).","Use today's observations to adjust tomorrow's plan (manual p.5)."],"teacherNotes":["Story selection: the manual asks teachers to use picture story books or stories in the school library. Today's suggested theme (a story about helping a neighbour) is a planning suggestion; use any suitable story you have.","The manual lists the letter and word games but does not fix the slot in the daily timetable where they are used. This plan places them in the 10-minute sound-symbol / alphabet slot (interpretation).","Mind mapping topic for this day: 'river'. The manual's example uses the word 'shop'; today's topic follows the same method.","Level check: if learners have moved up to a new level, celebrate with an appreciation-oriented game (word level to para level): 'Word formation by arranging jumbled letters' or 'Activities with Picture Cards' (manual p.42-45). Teachers may use such activities on their own.","Pace: the manual says not to assume all learners progress at the same speed. Repeat a day's activity with the groups that need it before moving on.","Special needs: give extra time and prepare materials for slower learners; seat learners with hearing or vision difficulty at the front; for learners who reverse or confuse letters, trace letters on the letter card with a finger and write with dots to trace with a pencil (manual p.6)."],"components":[{"no":1,"key":"warmup","name":"Warm-up activities","keywords":["Handkerchief game","two learners lead"],"rows":[1]},{"no":2,"key":"oral","name":"Oral Discussion","keywords":["listening and storytelling","every learner speaks"],"rows":[2]},{"no":3,"key":"story","name":"Story","keywords":["Day 1","title / picture talk","read aloud with expression","opinion questions","re-read pointing","group reading","level tasks"],"rows":[3,4,5]},{"no":4,"key":"sound","name":"Sound symbol games, Sound separation-pairing","keywords":["Matching Words (rhyme)","play in turns","level support"],"rows":[6]},{"no":5,"key":"mindwrite","name":"Mind Mapping (Day 1)","keywords":["mind map: river","classify the words","level task: circle letter R / sentences / story"],"rows":[7,8,9]},{"no":6,"key":"reading","name":"Daily reading","keywords":["library book","read alone","teacher listens"],"rows":[10]}],"preLesson":null},{"programme":"TARL Literacy","id":"lit-011","day":11,"phase":1,"phaseLabel":"Phase 1 (Days 1-45)","title":"Story: a story about helping a neighbour (Day 2)","dayType":"Story Day 2 + Self-writing","focus":"Identifying the first, second and last sound (dog, sun, pig) | Self-writing: a rainy day","duration":70,"objectives":["Listen, speak and answer in the oral conversation (What did you see on your way?).","Retell the story, read it with expression, ask and answer questions about it and write answers.","Develop sound-symbol skills: Identifying the first, second and last sound (dog, sun, pig).","Write about a topic at their own level and review the writing (a rainy day).","Read independently for 10 minutes every day."],"sequence":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Rhyme - 'I saw a Little Bird'","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Say the rhyme with actions, then say it together. Lines: I saw a little bird go hop, hop, hop / I told the little bird to stop, stop, stop. / I went to the window to say 'How do you do?' / He wagged his little tail and far away he flew! Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Listen, then say the rhyme with actions.","tlm":"Rhyme chart or board (optional)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","n":1},{"activity":"Oral conversation: What did you see on your way?","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Ask learners to describe what they saw on their way to school. If they are hesitant, begin yourself: 'This morning I saw a flock of ducks crossing the road and a girl carrying water. What did you see?'","learners":"Describe what they saw on the way to school and connect with what others share.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.9","n":2},{"activity":"Story (Day 2 of the story): retelling","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":6,"teacher":"Ask learners to retell yesterday's story in their own words. Prompt with questions on the beginning, middle and end.","learners":"Retell the story using their own words.","tlm":"The same story book as yesterday","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":3},{"activity":"Story: reading with actions and group questions","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":9,"teacher":"Learners practise reading with actions and expressions; one learner per group reads aloud to the class. Guide groups to make questions about the story (guide initially). Groups take turns to ask and answer each other's questions. Word-level learners also read aloud the consonants learned on the first day.","learners":"Read with actions; make questions (word-level learners help write them); ask and answer questions with another group.","tlm":"Story book, slate or paper for questions","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":4},{"activity":"Story: writing answers individually","grouping":"Individual","minutes":5,"teacher":"Para and Story level learners write answers to all questions individually; read and correct their responses after they finish.","learners":"Write the answers in their notebooks; Beginner/Letter/Word learners read or listen and answer orally.","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":5},{"activity":"Sound-symbol activity: oral sound awareness","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":4,"teacher":"Say words and ask learners to identify the first, second or last sound. Example: pan - first sound p, second sound a, third sound n; log: l, o, g; cup: c, u, p.","learners":"Say the first, second or last sound of the word.","tlm":"None (oral activity)","source":"M","ref":"p.12","n":6},{"activity":"Sound-symbol games by level","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":6,"teacher":"Give each level group its game (see level table). Move among the groups and help those who need support; say each word clearly.","learners":"Play the game for their level in small groups.","tlm":"Board, chalk, letter cards","source":"M","ref":"p.12","n":7},{"activity":"Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on a rainy day","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Start a conversation about a topic: 'a rainy day'. Involve all learners and ask open-ended questions.","learners":"Take part in the discussion and share thoughts freely.","tlm":"Picture card or topic on the board","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":8},{"activity":"Self-writing: individual writing","grouping":"Individual","minutes":7,"teacher":"Give each level its task (see level table). Let learners take ownership of what they draw and write; mistakes are fine.","learners":"Draw and write about the topic at their level.","tlm":"Notebooks, crayons or pencils","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":9},{"activity":"Self-writing: review and reading back","grouping":"Individual","minutes":3,"teacher":"Ask each learner 'What did you draw or write?' and have them read it aloud once. Word-level learners read to the group; discuss spelling, punctuation and sentence structure. Help beginners by writing their text in the notebook for them if needed.","learners":"Read what they wrote; correct mistakes after listening to their own reading.","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":10},{"activity":"Daily reading (10 minutes)","grouping":"Individual","minutes":10,"teacher":"Give each learner a library book or any storybook. Move around, listen to individual readers and note their level.","learners":"Read independently a book of their choice.","tlm":"Library books or storybooks","source":"M","ref":"p.7","n":11}],"procedures":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Rhyme - 'I saw a Little Bird'","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","steps":[{"teacher":"Say the rhyme 'I saw a Little Bird' slowly with actions: I saw a little bird go hop, hop, hop / I told the little bird to stop, stop, stop. / I went to the window to say 'How do you do?' / He wagged his little tail and far away he flew!","learners":"Listen and watch the actions."},{"teacher":"Say it again; invite learners to join with actions.","learners":"Say the rhyme together with actions."},{"teacher":"Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Choose a rhyme they like and lead."}]},{"activity":"Oral conversation: What did you see on your way?","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.9","steps":[{"teacher":"Ask: 'What did you see on your way to school today?'","learners":"Think about the way to school."},{"teacher":"If learners hesitate, start: 'This morning I saw a flock of ducks crossing the road and a girl carrying water. What did you see?'","learners":"Listen to the model and then share their own observations."},{"teacher":"Connect learners' answers with each other.","learners":"Listen and add what they noticed."}]},{"activity":"Story - Day 2 (a story about helping a neighbour)","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.11","steps":[{"teacher":"Ask learners to retell the story they read yesterday in their own words.","learners":"Retell, helping each other remember."},{"teacher":"In small groups learners practise reading the story using actions and expressions; one learner from each group then reads aloud to the class.","learners":"Read with actions and expression; a representative reads aloud."},{"teacher":"Guide the groups to come up with questions about the story (guide initially). Word-level learners can support by helping write them down.","learners":"Make questions together."},{"teacher":"Groups take turns to ask and answer each other's questions. Useful kinds: questions whose answer is not in the text; questions needing thinking beyond the text; questions asking for an opinion.","learners":"Ask, answer and discuss in the groups."},{"teacher":"Word-level learners also read aloud the consonants they learned on the first day.","learners":"Read the consonant clusters aloud."}]},{"activity":"Sound-symbol: oral and level games","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.12","steps":[{"teacher":"Say words and ask learners to identify the first, second or last sound. Example: pan - first sound p, second sound a, third sound n; log: l, o, g; cup: c, u, p.","learners":"Say the first, second or last sound of the word."},{"teacher":"Write the sounds or words for the day on the board and give each level group its task (see the level table).","learners":"Work in small groups and share their answers."},{"teacher":"Say each word clearly with distinct pronunciation. Give learners enough time to respond and think; use words learners commonly use at home (regional language and the medium of instruction).","learners":"Think, say and write the sounds."}]},{"activity":"Self-writing: 'Discussion, Writing, Self-review'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.15","steps":[{"teacher":"Start a conversation about a topic: 'a rainy day'. Involve all learners and ask open-ended questions.","learners":"Discuss and answer questions."},{"teacher":"Give writing time at each level: draw then write (Beginner), write about what they liked (Letter), a sentence (Word), a paragraph or story on a topic of their choice (Para/Story).","learners":"Write at their level and take ownership of the work."},{"teacher":"Review: ask 'What did you draw or write?' Have each learner read the text aloud once. Support with writing if needed.","learners":"Read aloud, listen to their pronunciation and correct mistakes."}]}],"levelTasks":[{"activity":"Story - Day 2: level-wise tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.11","tasks":{"Beginner":"Retell with the group by pointing to pictures or words; read aloud with group support (interpretation of the manual's group reading task).","Letter":"Read with the group, pointing to words; say the letters and words they know (interpretation of the manual's group reading task).","Word":"Support the group in writing the questions; read aloud the consonant clusters learned on the first day.","Para":"Ask the group's questions to another group, discuss them, then write answers to all questions individually; the teacher reads and corrects.","Story":"Ask the group's questions to another group, discuss them, then write answers to all questions individually; the teacher reads and corrects."}},{"activity":"Sound-symbol games by level (small groups)","source":"M","ref":"p.12","tasks":{"Beginner":"'What is the first sound in the word fish?' 'Is there a letter that makes the sound /f/?' 'Can you name objects that start with the letter F?' Learners think and share names in the group.","Letter":"Write the rhyming ending -ed on the board and ask learners to add new letters to form words: b + ed = bed, r + ed = red, f + ed = fed.","Word":"Say a word and tell its sounds, for example 'sun' = /s/ + /u/ + /n/. Then tell what word is formed if /r/ is put before 'at': r + at = rat. Do 8-10 such combinations; at first learners may form meaningless words, later only meaningful words.","Para":"Write two or three sounds on the board (for example Br, cl, st) and let the learners form words that start with those sounds; this builds a word list for the learner.","Story":"Write two or three sounds on the board (for example Br, cl, st) and let the learners form words that start with those sounds; this builds a word list for the learner."}},{"activity":"Self-writing: level tasks and review","source":"M","ref":"p.15","tasks":{"Beginner":"Draw a picture about the discussion and then write a few sentences about it, expressing thoughts freely. Review: say what they drew or wrote; read the text aloud once; the teacher may write the text in the notebook for them.","Letter":"Write about what they liked, using drawing and writing; write any words or sentences they can. Review: read the text aloud once; correct punctuation mistakes using the Barakhadi chart.","Word":"Write a sentence based on the conversation. Mistakes in spelling, punctuation and sentence structure are fine. Review: read it to the group; discuss and correct mistakes together.","Para":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation.","Story":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation."}}],"organisation":[{"grouping":"Whole class (big group)","how":"All learners of all levels sit in a 'U' shape arranged by level (Beginner, Letter, Word, Para, Story) so that the move to small groups is easy.","activities":["Warm-up: Rhyme - 'I saw a Little Bird'","Oral conversation: What did you see on your way?","Story (Day 2 of the story): retelling","Sound-symbol activity: oral sound awareness","Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on a rainy day"]},{"grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","how":"Learners of similar levels work together; the teacher gives each group a task for its level and spends more time with learners who need support. Rotate responsibilities (for example group leader).","activities":["Story: reading with actions and group questions","Sound-symbol games by level"]},{"grouping":"Individual","how":"Each learner works on a task for their own level; the teacher moves around, observes difficulties and supports individuals.","activities":["Story: writing answers individually","Self-writing: individual writing","Self-writing: review and reading back","Daily reading (10 minutes)"]}],"materials":["Rhyme chart or board (optional)","The same story book as yesterday","Story book","slate or paper for questions","Notebooks","Board","chalk","letter cards","Picture card or topic on the board","crayons or pencils","Library books or storybooks"],"outcomes":["Learners take part in the oral conversation and speak without fear.","Learners retell the story, read with expression and ask or answer questions at their level.","Learners respond to the sound-symbol task for today (Identifying the first, second and last sound (dog, sun, pig)) at their own level.","Learners write about the topic at their level and read it aloud.","Each learner reads a book for 10 minutes."],"observation":["Observe each learner's reading and writing during the individual tasks; note who needs individual support and how many learners share the same difficulty.","Note any learner whose level is improving; move the learner to the next level group when you see steady progress (manual p.5).","Record each learner's progress for the day in the notebook, according to the learner's level (manual p.4).","Use today's observations to adjust tomorrow's plan (manual p.5)."],"teacherNotes":["Questions to elicit on Day 2: information questions (answer not in the text), thinking questions (needs knowledge beyond the text) and opinion questions (feedback on something in the text).","Sound-symbol: for the first 4-5 days, play sound-based games with the learners at word level. Include the sounds learners find difficult when you prepare the Class Transaction Plan.","Writing has two parts, content and sequence: encourage learners to read what they wrote, improve it and rewrite it for clarity and correctness (manual p.15).","Pace: the manual says not to assume all learners progress at the same speed. Repeat a day's activity with the groups that need it before moving on.","Special needs: give extra time and prepare materials for slower learners; seat learners with hearing or vision difficulty at the front; for learners who reverse or confuse letters, trace letters on the letter card with a finger and write with dots to trace with a pencil (manual p.6)."],"components":[{"no":1,"key":"warmup","name":"Warm-up activities","keywords":["Rhyme - 'I saw a Little Bird'","two learners lead"],"rows":[1]},{"no":2,"key":"oral","name":"Oral Discussion","keywords":["What did you see on your way?","every learner speaks"],"rows":[2]},{"no":3,"key":"story","name":"Story","keywords":["Day 2","retell","read with actions","group questions","ask and answer","write answers (Para/Story)"],"rows":[3,4,5]},{"no":4,"key":"sound","name":"Sound symbol games, Sound separation-pairing","keywords":["oral sound awareness","first / second / last sound","level games in small groups"],"rows":[6,7]},{"no":5,"key":"mindwrite","name":"Individual-Writing (Day 2)","keywords":["discussion","write at own level","self-review (read aloud)"],"rows":[8,9,10]},{"no":6,"key":"reading","name":"Daily reading","keywords":["library book","read alone","teacher listens"],"rows":[11]}],"preLesson":null},{"programme":"TARL Literacy","id":"lit-012","day":12,"phase":1,"phaseLabel":"Phase 1 (Days 1-45)","title":"Saturday: drama presentation","dayType":"Saturday drama + Self-writing","focus":"Barakhadi / alphabet and phonics chart (line 4, letter 'g') | Self-writing: the story we acted out (a story about helping a neighbour)","duration":70,"objectives":["Listen, speak and answer in the oral conversation (familiar topic).","Express a story through role play, using voice, facial expressions and gestures.","Develop sound-symbol skills: Barakhadi / alphabet and phonics chart (line 4, letter 'g').","Write about the story and review the writing.","Read independently for 10 minutes every day."],"sequence":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Singing and Spinning","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Learners sit in a circle and pass a small object while you clap with your back turned; when the clapping stops, the learner holding it sings a song, recites a poem or tells a joke. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Pass the object round the circle; sing, recite or tell a joke when the clapping stops.","tlm":"A small object (chalk or pencil)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","n":1},{"activity":"Oral conversation: familiar topic","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Hold a conversation on the topic 'my family and what each person does'. Give each learner a chance to speak; be patient with learners who need extra time.","learners":"Talk about the topic and listen to others.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.9","n":2},{"activity":"Dramatic presentation: introduction and reading","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Explain what a dramatic presentation is and how it is done. Provide stories discussed during the week and read one aloud once more. Para and Story level learners support Beginner and Letter level learners in reading.","learners":"Listen, read along, then each learner chooses a character.","tlm":"Stories discussed in the week (a story about a village festival; a story about helping a neighbour)","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":3},{"activity":"Dramatic presentation: planning in small groups","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":8,"teacher":"Each group discusses and plans dialogues; Para or Story level learners write the dialogues. Groups prepare their dramatic presentation.","learners":"Choose characters, plan and rehearse dialogues with facial expressions and gestures.","tlm":"Story, paper for dialogues","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":4},{"activity":"Dramatic presentation: performances and feedback","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":7,"teacher":"Learners sit in a U shape. Each group presents; after each performance, watching learners say what they enjoyed and what could be improved.","learners":"Perform in turn; watch; give feedback.","tlm":"Open space (U-shape seating)","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":5},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart: big group reading","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":3,"teacher":"Show the Barakhadi chart and ask which letter they like. Read the letter 'g' on the chart; learners listen carefully and point to it on their own chart (they do not repeat after you).","learners":"Listen and point to the letter on their own chart.","tlm":"Barakhadi chart, alphabet or phonics chart","source":"M","ref":"p.13","n":6},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart: small-group practice","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Learners practise reading the alphabet or phonics chart in groups and help each other. One learner per group reads aloud. Occasionally ask learners to identify the sounds of letters. Give each level its group task.","learners":"Read the chart in groups; one learner reads aloud; do the level task.","tlm":"Alphabet or phonics chart, board or floor","source":"M","ref":"p.13","n":7},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart: individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":2,"teacher":"Give each learner an individual task for their level and observe closely; assist any learner who needs individual support.","learners":"Say and write a letter or word, a sentence or a short paragraph (by level).","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.13","n":8},{"activity":"Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on the story we acted out (a story about helping a neighbour)","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Start a conversation about the story used for the drama: 'the story we acted out (a story about helping a neighbour)'. Involve all learners with open-ended questions.","learners":"Take part in the discussion and share thoughts freely.","tlm":"Picture card or topic on the board","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":9},{"activity":"Self-writing: individual writing","grouping":"Individual","minutes":7,"teacher":"Give each level its task (see level table). Let learners take ownership of what they draw and write; mistakes are fine.","learners":"Draw and write about the topic at their level.","tlm":"Notebooks, crayons or pencils","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":10},{"activity":"Self-writing: review and reading back","grouping":"Individual","minutes":3,"teacher":"Ask each learner 'What did you draw or write?' and have them read it aloud once. Word-level learners read to the group; discuss spelling, punctuation and sentence structure. Help beginners by writing their text in the notebook for them if needed.","learners":"Read what they wrote; correct mistakes after listening to their own reading.","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":11},{"activity":"Daily reading (10 minutes)","grouping":"Individual","minutes":10,"teacher":"Give each learner a library book or any storybook. Move around, listen to individual readers and note their level.","learners":"Read independently a book of their choice.","tlm":"Library books or storybooks","source":"M","ref":"p.7","n":12}],"procedures":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Singing and Spinning","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","steps":[{"teacher":"Seat the learners in a circle; give a small object to one learner.","learners":"Sit in a circle."},{"teacher":"Stand outside the circle with your back to them and clap steadily; they pass the object.","learners":"Pass the object while the clapping continues."},{"teacher":"Stop clapping; the learner holding the object sings, recites or tells a joke.","learners":"Perform, and everybody claps."}]},{"activity":"Oral conversation: familiar topic","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.9","steps":[{"teacher":"Introduce the topic: 'my family and what each person does'.","learners":"Think about their own experience."},{"teacher":"Ask open questions; give every learner a chance. Involve learners who speak less.","learners":"Speak freely and without fear."},{"teacher":"Praise efforts and sum up.","learners":"Listen and respect each other's ideas."}]},{"activity":"Saturday special: dramatic presentation","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.11","steps":[{"teacher":"Explain what a dramatic presentation is and how it can be done. Give the groups the stories discussed during the week.","learners":"Listen to the explanation."},{"teacher":"Read a story aloud once more. Learners at story and paragraph level support those at beginner and letter level in reading.","learners":"Read along; helpers support their friends."},{"teacher":"After reading, each learner chooses a character from the story.","learners":"Choose a role (boys may play girl roles and girls may play boy roles)."},{"teacher":"In groups, learners discuss and plan the dialogues; paragraph or story level learners write the dialogues.","learners":"Plan and write dialogues together."},{"teacher":"Learners sit in a U shape. Each group presents its drama. After each performance, ask what the audience enjoyed and what could be improved.","learners":"Perform, watch and give kind feedback."}]},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart activity (line 4)","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Small group (level-wise) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.13","steps":[{"teacher":"Show the Barakhadi chart and ask the learners which letter they like. Where is the letter 'g'?","learners":"Look for the letter on the chart."},{"teacher":"Read the letter 'g' on the chart. Learners listen and point to it on their own chart. Make sure they do not repeat after you.","learners":"Listen and point to the letter."},{"teacher":"Learners read the alphabet or phonics chart in their groups and help each other; one learner from each group comes forward to read aloud.","learners":"Read in groups; the representative reads aloud."},{"teacher":"Occasionally ask them to identify the sounds of letters from the chart.","learners":"Say the sound of the letter you point to."},{"teacher":"As an extra activity, write some letters on the floor, call out each letter one by one and let the learners jump onto the correct letter.","learners":"Jump onto the letter that is called."}]},{"activity":"Self-writing: 'Discussion, Writing, Self-review'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.15","steps":[{"teacher":"Start a conversation about the story used for the drama: 'the story we acted out (a story about helping a neighbour)'. Involve all learners with open-ended questions.","learners":"Discuss and answer questions."},{"teacher":"Give writing time at each level: draw then write (Beginner), write about what they liked (Letter), a sentence (Word), a paragraph or story on a topic of their choice (Para/Story).","learners":"Write at their level and take ownership of the work."},{"teacher":"Review: ask 'What did you draw or write?' Have each learner read the text aloud once. Support with writing if needed.","learners":"Read aloud, listen to their pronunciation and correct mistakes."}]}],"levelTasks":[{"activity":"Drama: roles by level","source":"M","ref":"p.11","tasks":{"Beginner":"Take a character role and say or act short lines with help from Para and Story level learners.","Letter":"Take a character role and say or act short lines with help from Para and Story level learners.","Word":"Take a role and speak the dialogues; help rehearse.","Para":"Write the dialogues for the group and support Beginner, Letter and Word level learners throughout.","Story":"Write the dialogues for the group and support Beginner, Letter and Word level learners throughout."}},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart: level tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.13","tasks":{"Beginner":"Small group: read the chart in the group; find and write favourite letters from the line. Individual: say and write a letter of their choice.","Letter":"Small group: read the chart; find and write favourite letters or words from any line. Individual: say a word on their own that begins with any letter.","Word":"Small group: write one or two lines of letters on the board or floor and use them to form words. Individual: speak and write sentences using words they know.","Para":"Small group: prepare word lists using the Barakhadi chart (for example items found in a shop or in the kitchen). Individual: write short paragraphs using the words formed with the Barakhadi chart.","Story":"Small group: prepare word lists using the Barakhadi chart. Individual: write short paragraphs using the words formed with the Barakhadi chart."}},{"activity":"Self-writing: level tasks and review","source":"M","ref":"p.15","tasks":{"Beginner":"Draw a picture about the discussion and then write a few sentences about it, expressing thoughts freely. Review: say what they drew or wrote; read the text aloud once; the teacher may write the text in the notebook for them.","Letter":"Write about what they liked, using drawing and writing; write any words or sentences they can. Review: read the text aloud once; correct punctuation mistakes using the Barakhadi chart.","Word":"Write a sentence based on the conversation. Mistakes in spelling, punctuation and sentence structure are fine. Review: read it to the group; discuss and correct mistakes together.","Para":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation.","Story":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation."}}],"organisation":[{"grouping":"Whole class (big group)","how":"All learners of all levels sit in a 'U' shape arranged by level (Beginner, Letter, Word, Para, Story) so that the move to small groups is easy.","activities":["Warm-up: Singing and Spinning","Oral conversation: familiar topic","Dramatic presentation: introduction and reading","Dramatic presentation: performances and feedback","Barakhadi chart: big group reading","Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on the story we acted out (a story about helping a neighbour)"]},{"grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","how":"Learners of similar levels work together; the teacher gives each group a task for its level and spends more time with learners who need support. Rotate responsibilities (for example group leader).","activities":["Dramatic presentation: planning in small groups","Barakhadi chart: small-group practice"]},{"grouping":"Individual","how":"Each learner works on a task for their own level; the teacher moves around, observes difficulties and supports individuals.","activities":["Barakhadi chart: individual tasks","Self-writing: individual writing","Self-writing: review and reading back","Daily reading (10 minutes)"]}],"materials":["A small object (chalk or pencil)","Stories discussed in the week (a story about a village festival; a story about helping a neighbour)","Story","paper for dialogues","Open space (U-shape seating)","Barakhadi chart","alphabet or phonics chart","Alphabet or phonics chart","board or floor","Notebooks","Picture card or topic on the board","crayons or pencils","Library books or storybooks"],"outcomes":["Learners take part in the oral conversation and speak without fear.","Learners present a role in the group drama and give feedback to others.","Learners respond to the sound-symbol task for today (Barakhadi / alphabet and phonics chart (line 4, letter 'g')) at their own level.","Learners write about the story at their level and read it aloud.","Each learner reads a book for 10 minutes."],"observation":["Observe each learner's reading and writing during the individual tasks; note who needs individual support and how many learners share the same difficulty.","Note any learner whose level is improving; move the learner to the next level group when you see steady progress (manual p.5).","Record each learner's progress for the day in the notebook, according to the learner's level (manual p.4).","Use today's observations to adjust tomorrow's plan (manual p.5)."],"teacherNotes":["Saturday: this plan assumes Day 1 is a Monday (six teaching days per week). If your school week is different, hold the drama presentation on your Saturday and keep the other days in sequence.","Barakhadi: learners who need extra time should get repeated practice using one or two sound units at a time. Topic-based discussion helps oral expression, thinking and understanding.","Writing has two parts, content and sequence: encourage learners to read what they wrote, improve it and rewrite it for clarity and correctness (manual p.15).","Pace: the manual says not to assume all learners progress at the same speed. Repeat a day's activity with the groups that need it before moving on.","Special needs: give extra time and prepare materials for slower learners; seat learners with hearing or vision difficulty at the front; for learners who reverse or confuse letters, trace letters on the letter card with a finger and write with dots to trace with a pencil (manual p.6)."],"components":[{"no":1,"key":"warmup","name":"Warm-up activities","keywords":["Singing and Spinning","two learners lead"],"rows":[1]},{"no":2,"key":"oral","name":"Oral Discussion","keywords":["familiar topic","every learner speaks"],"rows":[2]},{"no":3,"key":"story","name":"Story (Saturday: dramatic presentation)","keywords":["Saturday drama","choose a character","plan dialogues","perform in U shape","feedback"],"rows":[3,4,5]},{"no":4,"key":"sound","name":"Sound symbol games, Sound separation-pairing","keywords":["Barakhadi / alphabet chart","listen and point (no repeating)","group reading","level tasks"],"rows":[6,7,8]},{"no":5,"key":"mindwrite","name":"Individual-Writing (Day 2)","keywords":["discussion","write at own level","self-review (read aloud)"],"rows":[9,10,11]},{"no":6,"key":"reading","name":"Daily reading","keywords":["library book","read alone","teacher listens"],"rows":[12]}],"preLesson":null},{"programme":"TARL Literacy","id":"lit-013","day":13,"phase":1,"phaseLabel":"Phase 1 (Days 1-45)","title":"Story: a story set near a river (Day 1)","dayType":"Story Day 1 + Mind mapping","focus":"Language game: Find My Word | Mind map: kitchen","duration":70,"objectives":["Listen, speak and answer in the oral conversation (conversation on a picture).","Listen to and read a story with understanding; discuss it in big and small groups and respond at their own level.","Develop sound-symbol skills: Language game: Find My Word.","Build vocabulary through a mind map ('kitchen') and use the words at their own level.","Read independently for 10 minutes every day."],"sequence":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Rain clapping","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Everyone stands in a circle with eyes closed and keeps clapping: first one finger, then two, three, four and finally five fingers. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Stand in a circle, close the eyes and clap with 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 fingers.","tlm":"After the activity ask: Where were you when you last heard real rain?","source":"M","ref":"p.8","n":1},{"activity":"Oral conversation: conversation on a picture","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Show a picture of boats on a river and ask what is happening, who is doing what and what is happening around them. Let learners think creatively and even make up a story.","learners":"Look at the picture, answer questions and make up their own story about it.","tlm":"Picture card of boats on a river","source":"M","ref":"p.9","n":2},{"activity":"Story (Day 1 of the story): reading aloud and discussion","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":8,"teacher":"Discuss the title or picture of the story with the learners. Read the story aloud with expression and voice modulation (learners do not repeat after you). Discuss it, with emphasis on factual questions. Read it again slowly, pointing to each word.","learners":"Talk about the title/picture; listen; answer questions; follow each word with a finger in their own copy.","tlm":"A story from the school library (a story set near a river), a copy for each learner","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":3},{"activity":"Story: reading in small groups","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":7,"teacher":"Form level-wise groups with a group leader. Learners read the story one sentence at a time while the others follow with their fingers. Para and Story level learners practise reading with emotion and expression.","learners":"Read the story sentence by sentence, supporting each other; the group leader helps.","tlm":"Story book copies","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":4},{"activity":"Story: level-wise individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":5,"teacher":"Give each learner the task for their level (see level table) and support those who need it.","learners":"Beginner/Letter: find and write favourite words or letters. Word: find consonant clusters. Para/Story: silently read, find unfamiliar and rhyming words.","tlm":"Story book, notebooks, board","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":5},{"activity":"Language game: Find My Word","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Learners search their book pages for words beginning with a letter chosen by a classmate. Observe each learner and give help where needed.","learners":"Play the game, take turns and read or say the words they make.","tlm":"Textbooks or storybooks","source":"M","ref":"p.19","n":6},{"activity":"Mind mapping (Day 1): the word 'kitchen'","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Ask: 'What words come to your mind when you hear the word kitchen?' Write learners' answers on the board or floor (Para and Story level learners write the words themselves). Guide the map towards the learning objective. Example words: plate, spoon, pan, bowl, rice, dal, curry, pitha, stove, wood, water, matches.","learners":"Say words connected with 'kitchen'; share the meaning and feeling of words.","tlm":"Board, chalk (or floor)","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":7},{"activity":"Mind mapping: classify the words","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":4,"teacher":"Ask learners to classify the words in groups, for example: Utensils: plate, spoon, pan, bowl; Food: rice, dal, curry, pitha; Fuel and water: stove, wood, water, matches.","learners":"Sort the words into groups and say why.","tlm":"Board, chalk, word cards (optional)","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":8},{"activity":"Mind mapping: level-wise individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":6,"teacher":"Give each learner the individual task for their level; observe closely and give individual support. Display corrected stories on the wall.","learners":"Complete the task for their level (see level table).","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":9},{"activity":"Daily reading (10 minutes)","grouping":"Individual","minutes":10,"teacher":"Give each learner a library book or any storybook. Move around, listen to individual readers and note their level.","learners":"Read independently a book of their choice.","tlm":"Library books or storybooks","source":"M","ref":"p.7","n":10}],"procedures":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Rain clapping","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","steps":[{"teacher":"Stand the learners in a circle and ask them to close their eyes. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Stand in a circle and close their eyes."},{"teacher":"Start clapping with one finger; then two fingers, three, four and finally five fingers.","learners":"Keep clapping, copying the change of fingers."},{"teacher":"After the activity ask: Where were you when you last heard real rain?","learners":"Tell how they felt and what the sounds reminded them of."}]},{"activity":"Oral conversation: conversation on a picture","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.9","steps":[{"teacher":"Show the picture of boats on a river.","learners":"Look carefully."},{"teacher":"Ask: What is happening in the picture? Who is doing what? What is happening around them? Then: How do the people feel? How can you tell?","learners":"Answer in their own words; every learner gets a chance."},{"teacher":"Let learners imagine and make up a short story from the picture.","learners":"Tell their stories to the class."}]},{"activity":"Story - Day 1 (a story set near a river)","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.10","steps":[{"teacher":"Discuss the title or picture of the story with the learners.","learners":"Talk about what they see and what the story may be about."},{"teacher":"Read the story aloud with expression and proper voice modulation. Learners should not simply repeat after you.","learners":"Listen carefully and enjoy the story."},{"teacher":"Discuss the story: factual, logical, vocabulary-based, judgment or opinion questions (today's focus: factual: Who was in the story? Where did it happen? What did the character do first?). Begin in the home language if needed.","learners":"Think and respond thoughtfully; every learner takes part."},{"teacher":"Read the story again slowly, pointing to each word. Make sure each learner has a copy and follows with a finger.","learners":"Follow each word with their finger."},{"teacher":"Ask learners to read in small groups; select a group leader who helps the others. Learners read one sentence at a time while the others point with fingers.","learners":"Read with the help of one another."}]},{"activity":"Language game: Find My Word","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.19","steps":[{"teacher":"Ask the learners to open any page of their books. Choose a learner to say a letter, for example 'b'.","learners":"Open a book page and listen for the letter."},{"teacher":"The others look through the page to find and say words that begin with that letter (book, ball, bat).","learners":"Find words and read them aloud."},{"teacher":"The learner who finds the most words wins the round. Another learner picks a new letter.","learners":"Choose a new letter and play again."}]},{"activity":"Mind mapping: 'kitchen'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Small group (level-wise) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.14","steps":[{"teacher":"Choose a word that can generate many related words: 'kitchen'. Ask: 'What words come to your mind when you hear the word kitchen?' Write the answers on the board or floor.","learners":"Say words they link with 'kitchen'."},{"teacher":"Discuss the words: what they mean and how they are connected.","learners":"Explain their words and listen to others."},{"teacher":"In small groups, let the learners classify the words (Utensils: plate, spoon, pan, bowl; Food: rice, dal, curry, pitha; Fuel and water: stove, wood, water, matches).","learners":"Sort the words into groups."},{"teacher":"Give the individual tasks by level and help each learner.","learners":"Work individually; read the work aloud at the end if time allows."}]}],"levelTasks":[{"activity":"Story - Day 1: individual tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.10","tasks":{"Beginner":"Circle or search for a favourite word or letter in the story and say it aloud. If a learner cannot draw a circle, write words on the board and ask them to identify them.","Letter":"Find, read and write favourite words from the story.","Word":"Find the consonant clusters in the story, read them and write them in the notebook.","Para":"Silently read the story from the textbook; find unfamiliar words and try to understand them; find rhyming words, use them in sentences and write in the notebook; ask other groups for meanings; make questions in groups.","Story":"Silently read the story; find unfamiliar words and rhyming words; practise reading with emotion; one group reads sentences formed with consonant clusters to the other group; ask and answer group questions (information, thinking and opinion questions)."}},{"activity":"Language game: Find My Word - level support","source":"I","ref":"p.19","tasks":{"Beginner":"Take part by saying or pointing to the letters involved and by listening carefully; Para and Story level partners help.","Letter":"Say the letters/sounds and give simple words they know.","Word":"Say and write words and short sentences for the game.","Para":"Write sentences with the words; help groups to record answers.","Story":"Write sentences or short stories with the words; help groups to record answers."}},{"activity":"Mind mapping 'kitchen': level tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.14","tasks":{"Beginner":"Circle all the words that contain the letter 'A' on the board; make a list. See how many learners find the most words.","Letter":"Circle all the words that contain the letter 'A' and make a list of them.","Word":"Use 4-5 words (for example dal, pan, bowl, rice, wood) to form sentences, starting with words of one or two syllables. Example: Dream - I had a dream last night.","Para":"Choose any five words from the map and create a story with them. Use consonant clusters correctly, read the story aloud, correct mistakes of sentence structure, spelling or grammar, then display it on the wall.","Story":"Choose any five words from the map and create a story with them. Use consonant clusters correctly, read the story aloud, correct mistakes of sentence structure, spelling or grammar, then display it on the wall."}}],"organisation":[{"grouping":"Whole class (big group)","how":"All learners of all levels sit in a 'U' shape arranged by level (Beginner, Letter, Word, Para, Story) so that the move to small groups is easy.","activities":["Warm-up: Rain clapping","Oral conversation: conversation on a picture","Story (Day 1 of the story): reading aloud and discussion","Mind mapping (Day 1): the word 'kitchen'"]},{"grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","how":"Learners of similar levels work together; the teacher gives each group a task for its level and spends more time with learners who need support. Rotate responsibilities (for example group leader).","activities":["Story: reading in small groups","Language game: Find My Word","Mind mapping: classify the words"]},{"grouping":"Individual","how":"Each learner works on a task for their own level; the teacher moves around, observes difficulties and supports individuals.","activities":["Story: level-wise individual tasks","Mind mapping: level-wise individual tasks","Daily reading (10 minutes)"]}],"materials":["After the activity ask: Where were you when you last heard real rain?","Picture card of boats on a river","A story from the school library (a story set near a river)","a copy for each learner","Story book copies","Story book","notebooks","board","Textbooks or storybooks","Board","chalk (or floor)","chalk","word cards (optional)","Notebooks","Library books or storybooks"],"outcomes":["Learners take part in the oral conversation and speak without fear.","Learners show understanding of the story in the discussion and complete the task for their level.","Learners respond to the sound-symbol task for today (Language game: Find My Word) at their own level.","Learners add words to the mind map and use them in sentences or a story at their level.","Each learner reads a book for 10 minutes."],"observation":["Observe each learner's reading and writing during the individual tasks; note who needs individual support and how many learners share the same difficulty.","Note any learner whose level is improving; move the learner to the next level group when you see steady progress (manual p.5).","Record each learner's progress for the day in the notebook, according to the learner's level (manual p.4).","Use today's observations to adjust tomorrow's plan (manual p.5)."],"teacherNotes":["Story selection: the manual asks teachers to use picture story books or stories in the school library. Today's suggested theme (a story set near a river) is a planning suggestion; use any suitable story you have.","The manual lists the letter and word games but does not fix the slot in the daily timetable where they are used. This plan places them in the 10-minute sound-symbol / alphabet slot (interpretation).","Mind mapping topic for this day: 'kitchen'. The manual's example uses the word 'shop'; today's topic follows the same method.","Pace: the manual says not to assume all learners progress at the same speed. Repeat a day's activity with the groups that need it before moving on.","Special needs: give extra time and prepare materials for slower learners; seat learners with hearing or vision difficulty at the front; for learners who reverse or confuse letters, trace letters on the letter card with a finger and write with dots to trace with a pencil (manual p.6)."],"components":[{"no":1,"key":"warmup","name":"Warm-up activities","keywords":["Rain clapping","two learners lead"],"rows":[1]},{"no":2,"key":"oral","name":"Oral Discussion","keywords":["conversation on a picture","every learner speaks"],"rows":[2]},{"no":3,"key":"story","name":"Story","keywords":["Day 1","title / picture talk","read aloud with expression","factual questions","re-read pointing","group reading","level tasks"],"rows":[3,4,5]},{"no":4,"key":"sound","name":"Sound symbol games, Sound separation-pairing","keywords":["Find My Word","play in turns","level support"],"rows":[6]},{"no":5,"key":"mindwrite","name":"Mind Mapping (Day 1)","keywords":["mind map: kitchen","classify the words","level task: circle letter A / sentences / story"],"rows":[7,8,9]},{"no":6,"key":"reading","name":"Daily reading","keywords":["library book","read alone","teacher listens"],"rows":[10]}],"preLesson":null},{"programme":"TARL Literacy","id":"lit-014","day":14,"phase":1,"phaseLabel":"Phase 1 (Days 1-45)","title":"Story: a story set near a river (Day 2)","dayType":"Story Day 2 + Self-writing","focus":"Blending sounds to form words (sun, pig, hat) | Self-writing: my village","duration":70,"objectives":["Listen, speak and answer in the oral conversation (listening and storytelling).","Retell the story, read it with expression, ask and answer questions about it and write answers.","Develop sound-symbol skills: Blending sounds to form words (sun, pig, hat).","Write about a topic at their own level and review the writing (my village).","Read independently for 10 minutes every day."],"sequence":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Writing with body parts","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Learners stand in a circle. Demonstrate writing the word 'cat' in the air with a finger, then ask them to write it with different body parts. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Write the word 'cat' in the air with the finger, then with the head, shoulders, knees or elbows.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.8","n":1},{"activity":"Oral conversation: listening and storytelling","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Tell an interesting story starter and involve the learners: 'My shadow got up and walked away without me. Where did it go?' Let learners imagine and continue the story.","learners":"Listen to the teacher, then imagine and continue the story. Learners can also recite a rhyme or story they know.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.9","n":2},{"activity":"Story (Day 2 of the story): retelling","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":6,"teacher":"Ask learners to retell yesterday's story in their own words. Prompt with questions on the beginning, middle and end.","learners":"Retell the story using their own words.","tlm":"The same story book as yesterday","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":3},{"activity":"Story: reading with actions and group questions","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":9,"teacher":"Learners practise reading with actions and expressions; one learner per group reads aloud to the class. Guide groups to make questions about the story (guide initially). Groups take turns to ask and answer each other's questions. Word-level learners also read aloud the consonants learned on the first day.","learners":"Read with actions; make questions (word-level learners help write them); ask and answer questions with another group.","tlm":"Story book, slate or paper for questions","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":4},{"activity":"Story: writing answers individually","grouping":"Individual","minutes":5,"teacher":"Para and Story level learners write answers to all questions individually; read and correct their responses after they finish.","learners":"Write the answers in their notebooks; Beginner/Letter/Word learners read or listen and answer orally.","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":5},{"activity":"Sound-symbol activity: oral sound awareness","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":4,"teacher":"Say separate sounds from 10-12 words (sun: s - u - n; pig: p - i - g; hat: h - a - t; pen: p - e - n) and ask learners to blend the sounds into the complete word.","learners":"Listen to the separate sounds and blend them to say the whole word.","tlm":"None (oral activity)","source":"M","ref":"p.12","n":6},{"activity":"Sound-symbol games by level","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":6,"teacher":"Give each level group its game (see level table). Move among the groups and help those who need support; say each word clearly.","learners":"Play the game for their level in small groups.","tlm":"Board, chalk, letter cards","source":"M","ref":"p.12","n":7},{"activity":"Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on my village","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Start a conversation about a situation: 'my village'. Involve all learners and ask open-ended questions.","learners":"Take part in the discussion and share thoughts freely.","tlm":"Picture card or topic on the board","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":8},{"activity":"Self-writing: individual writing","grouping":"Individual","minutes":7,"teacher":"Give each level its task (see level table). Let learners take ownership of what they draw and write; mistakes are fine.","learners":"Draw and write about the topic at their level.","tlm":"Notebooks, crayons or pencils","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":9},{"activity":"Self-writing: review and reading back","grouping":"Individual","minutes":3,"teacher":"Ask each learner 'What did you draw or write?' and have them read it aloud once. Word-level learners read to the group; discuss spelling, punctuation and sentence structure. Help beginners by writing their text in the notebook for them if needed.","learners":"Read what they wrote; correct mistakes after listening to their own reading.","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":10},{"activity":"Daily reading (10 minutes)","grouping":"Individual","minutes":10,"teacher":"Give each learner a library book or any storybook. Move around, listen to individual readers and note their level.","learners":"Read independently a book of their choice.","tlm":"Library books or storybooks","source":"M","ref":"p.7","n":11}],"procedures":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Writing with body parts","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","steps":[{"teacher":"Stand the learners in a circle. Demonstrate writing the word 'cat' in the air with your finger.","learners":"Watch and then copy with their own finger."},{"teacher":"Ask them to write it again using knees and other body parts (head, shoulders, knees, ...).","learners":"Write the letters in the air with the named body part."},{"teacher":"Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Take turns to lead."}]},{"activity":"Oral conversation: listening and storytelling","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.9","steps":[{"teacher":"Say the starter: 'My shadow got up and walked away without me. Where did it go?'","learners":"Listen and imagine."},{"teacher":"Ask learners to continue the story one by one. Encourage those who speak less.","learners":"Add ideas to the story."},{"teacher":"Invite a learner to recite a poem or rhyme they know.","learners":"Recite and listen to others."}]},{"activity":"Story - Day 2 (a story set near a river)","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.11","steps":[{"teacher":"Ask learners to retell the story they read yesterday in their own words.","learners":"Retell, helping each other remember."},{"teacher":"In small groups learners practise reading the story using actions and expressions; one learner from each group then reads aloud to the class.","learners":"Read with actions and expression; a representative reads aloud."},{"teacher":"Guide the groups to come up with questions about the story (guide initially). Word-level learners can support by helping write them down.","learners":"Make questions together."},{"teacher":"Groups take turns to ask and answer each other's questions. Useful kinds: questions whose answer is not in the text; questions needing thinking beyond the text; questions asking for an opinion.","learners":"Ask, answer and discuss in the groups."},{"teacher":"Word-level learners also read aloud the consonants they learned on the first day.","learners":"Read the consonant clusters aloud."}]},{"activity":"Sound-symbol: oral and level games","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.12","steps":[{"teacher":"Say separate sounds from 10-12 words (sun: s - u - n; pig: p - i - g; hat: h - a - t; pen: p - e - n) and ask learners to blend the sounds into the complete word.","learners":"Listen to the separate sounds and blend them to say the whole word."},{"teacher":"Write the sounds or words for the day on the board and give each level group its task (see the level table).","learners":"Work in small groups and share their answers."},{"teacher":"Say each word clearly with distinct pronunciation. Give learners enough time to respond and think; use words learners commonly use at home (regional language and the medium of instruction).","learners":"Think, say and write the sounds."}]},{"activity":"Self-writing: 'Discussion, Writing, Self-review'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.15","steps":[{"teacher":"Start a conversation about a situation: 'my village'. Involve all learners and ask open-ended questions.","learners":"Discuss and answer questions."},{"teacher":"Give writing time at each level: draw then write (Beginner), write about what they liked (Letter), a sentence (Word), a paragraph or story on a topic of their choice (Para/Story).","learners":"Write at their level and take ownership of the work."},{"teacher":"Review: ask 'What did you draw or write?' Have each learner read the text aloud once. Support with writing if needed.","learners":"Read aloud, listen to their pronunciation and correct mistakes."}]}],"levelTasks":[{"activity":"Story - Day 2: level-wise tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.11","tasks":{"Beginner":"Retell with the group by pointing to pictures or words; read aloud with group support (interpretation of the manual's group reading task).","Letter":"Read with the group, pointing to words; say the letters and words they know (interpretation of the manual's group reading task).","Word":"Support the group in writing the questions; read aloud the consonant clusters learned on the first day.","Para":"Ask the group's questions to another group, discuss them, then write answers to all questions individually; the teacher reads and corrects.","Story":"Ask the group's questions to another group, discuss them, then write answers to all questions individually; the teacher reads and corrects."}},{"activity":"Sound-symbol games by level (small groups)","source":"M","ref":"p.12","tasks":{"Beginner":"'What is the first sound in the word lamp?' 'Is there a letter that makes the sound /l/?' 'Can you name objects that start with the letter L?' Learners think and share names in the group.","Letter":"Write the rhyming ending -ub on the board and ask learners to add new letters to form words: t + ub = tub, r + ub = rub, c + ub = cub.","Word":"Say a word and tell its sounds, for example 'sun' = /s/ + /u/ + /n/. Then tell what word is formed if /r/ is put before 'at': r + at = rat. Do 8-10 such combinations; at first learners may form meaningless words, later only meaningful words.","Para":"Write two or three sounds on the board (for example Br, cl, st) and let the learners form words that start with those sounds; this builds a word list for the learner.","Story":"Write two or three sounds on the board (for example Br, cl, st) and let the learners form words that start with those sounds; this builds a word list for the learner."}},{"activity":"Self-writing: level tasks and review","source":"M","ref":"p.15","tasks":{"Beginner":"Draw a picture about the discussion and then write a few sentences about it, expressing thoughts freely. Review: say what they drew or wrote; read the text aloud once; the teacher may write the text in the notebook for them.","Letter":"Write about what they liked, using drawing and writing; write any words or sentences they can. Review: read the text aloud once; correct punctuation mistakes using the Barakhadi chart.","Word":"Write a sentence based on the conversation. Mistakes in spelling, punctuation and sentence structure are fine. Review: read it to the group; discuss and correct mistakes together.","Para":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation.","Story":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation."}}],"organisation":[{"grouping":"Whole class (big group)","how":"All learners of all levels sit in a 'U' shape arranged by level (Beginner, Letter, Word, Para, Story) so that the move to small groups is easy.","activities":["Warm-up: Writing with body parts","Oral conversation: listening and storytelling","Story (Day 2 of the story): retelling","Sound-symbol activity: oral sound awareness","Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on my village"]},{"grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","how":"Learners of similar levels work together; the teacher gives each group a task for its level and spends more time with learners who need support. Rotate responsibilities (for example group leader).","activities":["Story: reading with actions and group questions","Sound-symbol games by level"]},{"grouping":"Individual","how":"Each learner works on a task for their own level; the teacher moves around, observes difficulties and supports individuals.","activities":["Story: writing answers individually","Self-writing: individual writing","Self-writing: review and reading back","Daily reading (10 minutes)"]}],"materials":["The same story book as yesterday","Story book","slate or paper for questions","Notebooks","Board","chalk","letter cards","Picture card or topic on the board","crayons or pencils","Library books or storybooks"],"outcomes":["Learners take part in the oral conversation and speak without fear.","Learners retell the story, read with expression and ask or answer questions at their level.","Learners respond to the sound-symbol task for today (Blending sounds to form words (sun, pig, hat)) at their own level.","Learners write about the topic at their level and read it aloud.","Each learner reads a book for 10 minutes."],"observation":["Observe each learner's reading and writing during the individual tasks; note who needs individual support and how many learners share the same difficulty.","Note any learner whose level is improving; move the learner to the next level group when you see steady progress (manual p.5).","Record each learner's progress for the day in the notebook, according to the learner's level (manual p.4).","Use today's observations to adjust tomorrow's plan (manual p.5)."],"teacherNotes":["Questions to elicit on Day 2: information questions (answer not in the text), thinking questions (needs knowledge beyond the text) and opinion questions (feedback on something in the text).","Sound-symbol: for the first 4-5 days, play sound-based games with the learners at word level. Include the sounds learners find difficult when you prepare the Class Transaction Plan.","Writing has two parts, content and sequence: encourage learners to read what they wrote, improve it and rewrite it for clarity and correctness (manual p.15).","Pace: the manual says not to assume all learners progress at the same speed. Repeat a day's activity with the groups that need it before moving on.","Special needs: give extra time and prepare materials for slower learners; seat learners with hearing or vision difficulty at the front; for learners who reverse or confuse letters, trace letters on the letter card with a finger and write with dots to trace with a pencil (manual p.6)."],"components":[{"no":1,"key":"warmup","name":"Warm-up activities","keywords":["Writing with body parts","two learners lead"],"rows":[1]},{"no":2,"key":"oral","name":"Oral Discussion","keywords":["listening and storytelling","every learner speaks"],"rows":[2]},{"no":3,"key":"story","name":"Story","keywords":["Day 2","retell","read with actions","group questions","ask and answer","write answers (Para/Story)"],"rows":[3,4,5]},{"no":4,"key":"sound","name":"Sound symbol games, Sound separation-pairing","keywords":["oral sound awareness","blend sounds to a word","level games in small groups"],"rows":[6,7]},{"no":5,"key":"mindwrite","name":"Individual-Writing (Day 2)","keywords":["discussion","write at own level","self-review (read aloud)"],"rows":[8,9,10]},{"no":6,"key":"reading","name":"Daily reading","keywords":["library book","read alone","teacher listens"],"rows":[11]}],"preLesson":null},{"programme":"TARL Literacy","id":"lit-015","day":15,"phase":1,"phaseLabel":"Phase 1 (Days 1-45)","title":"Story: a story about a school day (Day 1)","dayType":"Story Day 1 + Mind mapping","focus":"Barakhadi / alphabet and phonics chart (line 7, letter 'r') | Mind map: Bihu festival","duration":70,"objectives":["Listen, speak and answer in the oral conversation (What did you see on your way?).","Listen to and read a story with understanding; discuss it in big and small groups and respond at their own level.","Develop sound-symbol skills: Barakhadi / alphabet and phonics chart (line 7, letter 'r').","Build vocabulary through a mind map ('Bihu festival') and use the words at their own level.","Read independently for 10 minutes every day."],"sequence":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Alphabet song (last-letter word chain)","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Say a word to the big group, for example 'tea'. Learners say a word that starts with the last letter ('a'). A learner who cannot say a word is out. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Say a word that starts with the last letter of the previous word; step out if unable to.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.8","n":1},{"activity":"Oral conversation: What did you see on your way?","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Ask learners to describe what they saw on their way to school. If they are hesitant, begin yourself: 'I saw smoke rising from a kitchen, a dog sleeping under a tree and children walking to school together. What did you see?'","learners":"Describe what they saw on the way to school and connect with what others share.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.9","n":2},{"activity":"Story (Day 1 of the story): reading aloud and discussion","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":8,"teacher":"Discuss the title or picture of the story with the learners. Read the story aloud with expression and voice modulation (learners do not repeat after you). Discuss it, with emphasis on logical questions. Read it again slowly, pointing to each word.","learners":"Talk about the title/picture; listen; answer questions; follow each word with a finger in their own copy.","tlm":"A story from the school library (a story about a school day), a copy for each learner","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":3},{"activity":"Story: reading in small groups","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":7,"teacher":"Form level-wise groups with a group leader. Learners read the story one sentence at a time while the others follow with their fingers. Para and Story level learners practise reading with emotion and expression.","learners":"Read the story sentence by sentence, supporting each other; the group leader helps.","tlm":"Story book copies","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":4},{"activity":"Story: level-wise individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":5,"teacher":"Give each learner the task for their level (see level table) and support those who need it.","learners":"Beginner/Letter: find and write favourite words or letters. Word: find consonant clusters. Para/Story: silently read, find unfamiliar and rhyming words.","tlm":"Story book, notebooks, board","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":5},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart: big group reading","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":3,"teacher":"Show the Barakhadi chart and ask which letter they like. Read the letter 'r' on the chart; learners listen carefully and point to it on their own chart (they do not repeat after you).","learners":"Listen and point to the letter on their own chart.","tlm":"Barakhadi chart, alphabet or phonics chart","source":"M","ref":"p.13","n":6},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart: small-group practice","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Learners practise reading the alphabet or phonics chart in groups and help each other. One learner per group reads aloud. Occasionally ask learners to identify the sounds of letters. Give each level its group task.","learners":"Read the chart in groups; one learner reads aloud; do the level task.","tlm":"Alphabet or phonics chart, board or floor","source":"M","ref":"p.13","n":7},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart: individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":2,"teacher":"Give each learner an individual task for their level and observe closely; assist any learner who needs individual support.","learners":"Say and write a letter or word, a sentence or a short paragraph (by level).","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.13","n":8},{"activity":"Mind mapping (Day 1): the word 'Bihu festival'","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Ask: 'What words come to your mind when you hear the word Bihu festival?' Write learners' answers on the board or floor (Para and Story level learners write the words themselves). Guide the map towards the learning objective. Example words: mekhela, gamosa, chador, flower, pitha, laru, rice, jolpan, dance, drum, song, pepa.","learners":"Say words connected with 'Bihu festival'; share the meaning and feeling of words.","tlm":"Board, chalk (or floor)","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":9},{"activity":"Mind mapping: classify the words","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":4,"teacher":"Ask learners to classify the words in groups, for example: Dress: mekhela, gamosa, chador, flower; Food: pitha, laru, rice, jolpan; Fun: dance, drum, song, pepa.","learners":"Sort the words into groups and say why.","tlm":"Board, chalk, word cards (optional)","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":10},{"activity":"Mind mapping: level-wise individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":6,"teacher":"Give each learner the individual task for their level; observe closely and give individual support. Display corrected stories on the wall.","learners":"Complete the task for their level (see level table).","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":11},{"activity":"Daily reading (10 minutes)","grouping":"Individual","minutes":10,"teacher":"Give each learner a library book or any storybook. Move around, listen to individual readers and note their level.","learners":"Read independently a book of their choice.","tlm":"Library books or storybooks","source":"M","ref":"p.7","n":12}],"procedures":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Alphabet song (last-letter word chain)","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","steps":[{"teacher":"Say the word 'tea' to the big group and show that its last letter is 'a'.","learners":"Listen and think of a word starting with 'a'."},{"teacher":"Ask learners in turn to say a word that starts with the last letter of the previous word. Example: rain -> nest.","learners":"Say a word in turn; anyone who cannot say a word is out of the game."},{"teacher":"Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Lead the game when it is their turn."}]},{"activity":"Oral conversation: What did you see on your way?","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.9","steps":[{"teacher":"Ask: 'What did you see on your way to school today?'","learners":"Think about the way to school."},{"teacher":"If learners hesitate, start: 'I saw smoke rising from a kitchen, a dog sleeping under a tree and children walking to school together. What did you see?'","learners":"Listen to the model and then share their own observations."},{"teacher":"Connect learners' answers with each other.","learners":"Listen and add what they noticed."}]},{"activity":"Story - Day 1 (a story about a school day)","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.10","steps":[{"teacher":"Discuss the title or picture of the story with the learners.","learners":"Talk about what they see and what the story may be about."},{"teacher":"Read the story aloud with expression and proper voice modulation. Learners should not simply repeat after you.","learners":"Listen carefully and enjoy the story."},{"teacher":"Discuss the story: factual, logical, vocabulary-based, judgment or opinion questions (today's focus: logical: Why did the character do that? What would have happened if ...?). Begin in the home language if needed.","learners":"Think and respond thoughtfully; every learner takes part."},{"teacher":"Read the story again slowly, pointing to each word. Make sure each learner has a copy and follows with a finger.","learners":"Follow each word with their finger."},{"teacher":"Ask learners to read in small groups; select a group leader who helps the others. Learners read one sentence at a time while the others point with fingers.","learners":"Read with the help of one another."}]},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart activity (line 7)","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Small group (level-wise) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.13","steps":[{"teacher":"Show the Barakhadi chart and ask the learners which letter they like. Where is the letter 'r'?","learners":"Look for the letter on the chart."},{"teacher":"Read the letter 'r' on the chart. Learners listen and point to it on their own chart. Make sure they do not repeat after you.","learners":"Listen and point to the letter."},{"teacher":"Learners read the alphabet or phonics chart in their groups and help each other; one learner from each group comes forward to read aloud.","learners":"Read in groups; the representative reads aloud."},{"teacher":"Occasionally ask them to identify the sounds of letters from the chart.","learners":"Say the sound of the letter you point to."},{"teacher":"As an extra activity, write some letters on the floor, call out each letter one by one and let the learners jump onto the correct letter.","learners":"Jump onto the letter that is called."}]},{"activity":"Mind mapping: 'Bihu festival'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Small group (level-wise) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.14","steps":[{"teacher":"Choose a word that can generate many related words: 'Bihu festival'. Ask: 'What words come to your mind when you hear the word Bihu festival?' Write the answers on the board or floor.","learners":"Say words they link with 'Bihu festival'."},{"teacher":"Discuss the words: what they mean and how they are connected.","learners":"Explain their words and listen to others."},{"teacher":"In small groups, let the learners classify the words (Dress: mekhela, gamosa, chador, flower; Food: pitha, laru, rice, jolpan; Fun: dance, drum, song, pepa).","learners":"Sort the words into groups."},{"teacher":"Give the individual tasks by level and help each learner.","learners":"Work individually; read the work aloud at the end if time allows."}]}],"levelTasks":[{"activity":"Story - Day 1: individual tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.10","tasks":{"Beginner":"Circle or search for a favourite word or letter in the story and say it aloud. If a learner cannot draw a circle, write words on the board and ask them to identify them.","Letter":"Find, read and write favourite words from the story.","Word":"Find the consonant clusters in the story, read them and write them in the notebook.","Para":"Silently read the story from the textbook; find unfamiliar words and try to understand them; find rhyming words, use them in sentences and write in the notebook; ask other groups for meanings; make questions in groups.","Story":"Silently read the story; find unfamiliar words and rhyming words; practise reading with emotion; one group reads sentences formed with consonant clusters to the other group; ask and answer group questions (information, thinking and opinion questions)."}},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart: level tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.13","tasks":{"Beginner":"Small group: read the chart in the group; find and write favourite letters from the line. Individual: say and write a letter of their choice.","Letter":"Small group: read the chart; find and write favourite letters or words from any line. Individual: say a word on their own that begins with any letter.","Word":"Small group: write one or two lines of letters on the board or floor and use them to form words. Individual: speak and write sentences using words they know.","Para":"Small group: prepare word lists using the Barakhadi chart (for example items found in a shop or in the kitchen). Individual: write short paragraphs using the words formed with the Barakhadi chart.","Story":"Small group: prepare word lists using the Barakhadi chart. Individual: write short paragraphs using the words formed with the Barakhadi chart."}},{"activity":"Mind mapping 'Bihu festival': level tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.14","tasks":{"Beginner":"Circle all the words that contain the letter 'A' on the board; make a list. See how many learners find the most words.","Letter":"Circle all the words that contain the letter 'A' and make a list of them.","Word":"Use 4-5 words (for example drum, laru, pepa, rice, song) to form sentences, starting with words of one or two syllables. Example: Dream - I had a dream last night.","Para":"Choose any five words from the map and create a story with them. Use consonant clusters correctly, read the story aloud, correct mistakes of sentence structure, spelling or grammar, then display it on the wall.","Story":"Choose any five words from the map and create a story with them. Use consonant clusters correctly, read the story aloud, correct mistakes of sentence structure, spelling or grammar, then display it on the wall."}}],"organisation":[{"grouping":"Whole class (big group)","how":"All learners of all levels sit in a 'U' shape arranged by level (Beginner, Letter, Word, Para, Story) so that the move to small groups is easy.","activities":["Warm-up: Alphabet song (last-letter word chain)","Oral conversation: What did you see on your way?","Story (Day 1 of the story): reading aloud and discussion","Barakhadi chart: big group reading","Mind mapping (Day 1): the word 'Bihu festival'"]},{"grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","how":"Learners of similar levels work together; the teacher gives each group a task for its level and spends more time with learners who need support. Rotate responsibilities (for example group leader).","activities":["Story: reading in small groups","Barakhadi chart: small-group practice","Mind mapping: classify the words"]},{"grouping":"Individual","how":"Each learner works on a task for their own level; the teacher moves around, observes difficulties and supports individuals.","activities":["Story: level-wise individual tasks","Barakhadi chart: individual tasks","Mind mapping: level-wise individual tasks","Daily reading (10 minutes)"]}],"materials":["A story from the school library (a story about a school day)","a copy for each learner","Story book copies","Story book","notebooks","board","Barakhadi chart","alphabet or phonics chart","Alphabet or phonics chart","board or floor","Notebooks","Board","chalk (or floor)","chalk","word cards (optional)","Library books or storybooks"],"outcomes":["Learners take part in the oral conversation and speak without fear.","Learners show understanding of the story in the discussion and complete the task for their level.","Learners respond to the sound-symbol task for today (Barakhadi / alphabet and phonics chart (line 7, letter 'r')) at their own level.","Learners add words to the mind map and use them in sentences or a story at their level.","Each learner reads a book for 10 minutes."],"observation":["Observe each learner's reading and writing during the individual tasks; note who needs individual support and how many learners share the same difficulty.","Note any learner whose level is improving; move the learner to the next level group when you see steady progress (manual p.5).","Record each learner's progress for the day in the notebook, according to the learner's level (manual p.4).","Use today's observations to adjust tomorrow's plan (manual p.5)."],"teacherNotes":["Story selection: the manual asks teachers to use picture story books or stories in the school library. Today's suggested theme (a story about a school day) is a planning suggestion; use any suitable story you have.","Barakhadi: learners who need extra time should get repeated practice using one or two sound units at a time. Topic-based discussion helps oral expression, thinking and understanding.","Mind mapping topic for this day: 'Bihu festival'. The manual's example uses the word 'shop'; today's topic follows the same method.","Pace: the manual says not to assume all learners progress at the same speed. Repeat a day's activity with the groups that need it before moving on.","Special needs: give extra time and prepare materials for slower learners; seat learners with hearing or vision difficulty at the front; for learners who reverse or confuse letters, trace letters on the letter card with a finger and write with dots to trace with a pencil (manual p.6)."],"components":[{"no":1,"key":"warmup","name":"Warm-up activities","keywords":["Alphabet song (last-letter word chain)","two learners lead"],"rows":[1]},{"no":2,"key":"oral","name":"Oral Discussion","keywords":["What did you see on your way?","every learner speaks"],"rows":[2]},{"no":3,"key":"story","name":"Story","keywords":["Day 1","title / picture talk","read aloud with expression","logical questions","re-read pointing","group reading","level tasks"],"rows":[3,4,5]},{"no":4,"key":"sound","name":"Sound symbol games, Sound separation-pairing","keywords":["Barakhadi / alphabet chart","listen and point (no repeating)","group reading","level tasks"],"rows":[6,7,8]},{"no":5,"key":"mindwrite","name":"Mind Mapping (Day 1)","keywords":["mind map: Bihu festival","classify the words","level task: circle letter A / sentences / story"],"rows":[9,10,11]},{"no":6,"key":"reading","name":"Daily reading","keywords":["library book","read alone","teacher listens"],"rows":[12]}],"preLesson":null},{"programme":"TARL Literacy","id":"lit-016","day":16,"phase":1,"phaseLabel":"Phase 1 (Days 1-45)","title":"Story: a story about a school day (Day 2)","dayType":"Story Day 2 + Self-writing","focus":"Language game: Find My Word | Self-writing: my school","duration":70,"objectives":["Listen, speak and answer in the oral conversation (familiar topic).","Retell the story, read it with expression, ask and answer questions about it and write answers.","Develop sound-symbol skills: Language game: Find My Word.","Write about a topic at their own level and review the writing (my school).","Read independently for 10 minutes every day."],"sequence":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Handkerchief game","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Learners sit in a circle and clap while singing a rhyme ('I saw a Little Bird'). One learner runs outside the circle with a handkerchief and secretly places it behind another learner, who must chase the runner. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Sit in a circle, clap and sing; run, place the handkerchief or chase as the game requires.","tlm":"A handkerchief","source":"M","ref":"p.8","n":1},{"activity":"Oral conversation: familiar topic","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Hold a conversation on the topic 'a festival we celebrate at home'. Give each learner a chance to speak; be patient with learners who need extra time.","learners":"Talk about the topic and listen to others.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.9","n":2},{"activity":"Story (Day 2 of the story): retelling","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":6,"teacher":"Ask learners to retell yesterday's story in their own words. Prompt with questions on the beginning, middle and end.","learners":"Retell the story using their own words.","tlm":"The same story book as yesterday","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":3},{"activity":"Story: reading with actions and group questions","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":9,"teacher":"Learners practise reading with actions and expressions; one learner per group reads aloud to the class. Guide groups to make questions about the story (guide initially). Groups take turns to ask and answer each other's questions. Word-level learners also read aloud the consonants learned on the first day.","learners":"Read with actions; make questions (word-level learners help write them); ask and answer questions with another group.","tlm":"Story book, slate or paper for questions","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":4},{"activity":"Story: writing answers individually","grouping":"Individual","minutes":5,"teacher":"Para and Story level learners write answers to all questions individually; read and correct their responses after they finish.","learners":"Write the answers in their notebooks; Beginner/Letter/Word learners read or listen and answer orally.","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":5},{"activity":"Language game: Find My Word","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Learners search their book pages for words beginning with a letter chosen by a classmate. Observe each learner and give help where needed.","learners":"Play the game, take turns and read or say the words they make.","tlm":"Textbooks or storybooks","source":"M","ref":"p.19","n":6},{"activity":"Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on my school","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Start a conversation about a picture card: 'my school'. Involve all learners and ask open-ended questions.","learners":"Take part in the discussion and share thoughts freely.","tlm":"Picture card or topic on the board","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":7},{"activity":"Self-writing: individual writing","grouping":"Individual","minutes":7,"teacher":"Give each level its task (see level table). Let learners take ownership of what they draw and write; mistakes are fine.","learners":"Draw and write about the topic at their level.","tlm":"Notebooks, crayons or pencils","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":8},{"activity":"Self-writing: review and reading back","grouping":"Individual","minutes":3,"teacher":"Ask each learner 'What did you draw or write?' and have them read it aloud once. Word-level learners read to the group; discuss spelling, punctuation and sentence structure. Help beginners by writing their text in the notebook for them if needed.","learners":"Read what they wrote; correct mistakes after listening to their own reading.","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":9},{"activity":"Daily reading (10 minutes)","grouping":"Individual","minutes":10,"teacher":"Give each learner a library book or any storybook. Move around, listen to individual readers and note their level.","learners":"Read independently a book of their choice.","tlm":"Library books or storybooks","source":"M","ref":"p.7","n":10}],"procedures":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Handkerchief game","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","steps":[{"teacher":"Seat the learners in a circle and start clapping and singing the rhyme 'I saw a Little Bird'.","learners":"Clap and sing together."},{"teacher":"One learner runs outside the circle holding a handkerchief and secretly places it behind another learner.","learners":"Everyone keeps clapping; the learner who finds the handkerchief behind them takes it and chases the runner."},{"teacher":"If the runner sits in the chaser's place before being caught, they stay in the game; if caught, they are out. Continue in this way.","learners":"Play fairly and take turns."}]},{"activity":"Oral conversation: familiar topic","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.9","steps":[{"teacher":"Introduce the topic: 'a festival we celebrate at home'.","learners":"Think about their own experience."},{"teacher":"Ask open questions; give every learner a chance. Involve learners who speak less.","learners":"Speak freely and without fear."},{"teacher":"Praise efforts and sum up.","learners":"Listen and respect each other's ideas."}]},{"activity":"Story - Day 2 (a story about a school day)","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.11","steps":[{"teacher":"Ask learners to retell the story they read yesterday in their own words.","learners":"Retell, helping each other remember."},{"teacher":"In small groups learners practise reading the story using actions and expressions; one learner from each group then reads aloud to the class.","learners":"Read with actions and expression; a representative reads aloud."},{"teacher":"Guide the groups to come up with questions about the story (guide initially). Word-level learners can support by helping write them down.","learners":"Make questions together."},{"teacher":"Groups take turns to ask and answer each other's questions. Useful kinds: questions whose answer is not in the text; questions needing thinking beyond the text; questions asking for an opinion.","learners":"Ask, answer and discuss in the groups."},{"teacher":"Word-level learners also read aloud the consonants they learned on the first day.","learners":"Read the consonant clusters aloud."}]},{"activity":"Language game: Find My Word","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.19","steps":[{"teacher":"Ask the learners to open any page of their books. Choose a learner to say a letter, for example 'b'.","learners":"Open a book page and listen for the letter."},{"teacher":"The others look through the page to find and say words that begin with that letter (book, ball, bat).","learners":"Find words and read them aloud."},{"teacher":"The learner who finds the most words wins the round. Another learner picks a new letter.","learners":"Choose a new letter and play again."}]},{"activity":"Self-writing: 'Discussion, Writing, Self-review'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.15","steps":[{"teacher":"Start a conversation about a picture card: 'my school'. Involve all learners and ask open-ended questions.","learners":"Discuss and answer questions."},{"teacher":"Give writing time at each level: draw then write (Beginner), write about what they liked (Letter), a sentence (Word), a paragraph or story on a topic of their choice (Para/Story).","learners":"Write at their level and take ownership of the work."},{"teacher":"Review: ask 'What did you draw or write?' Have each learner read the text aloud once. Support with writing if needed.","learners":"Read aloud, listen to their pronunciation and correct mistakes."}]}],"levelTasks":[{"activity":"Story - Day 2: level-wise tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.11","tasks":{"Beginner":"Retell with the group by pointing to pictures or words; read aloud with group support (interpretation of the manual's group reading task).","Letter":"Read with the group, pointing to words; say the letters and words they know (interpretation of the manual's group reading task).","Word":"Support the group in writing the questions; read aloud the consonant clusters learned on the first day.","Para":"Ask the group's questions to another group, discuss them, then write answers to all questions individually; the teacher reads and corrects.","Story":"Ask the group's questions to another group, discuss them, then write answers to all questions individually; the teacher reads and corrects."}},{"activity":"Language game: Find My Word - level support","source":"I","ref":"p.19","tasks":{"Beginner":"Take part by saying or pointing to the letters involved and by listening carefully; Para and Story level partners help.","Letter":"Say the letters/sounds and give simple words they know.","Word":"Say and write words and short sentences for the game.","Para":"Write sentences with the words; help groups to record answers.","Story":"Write sentences or short stories with the words; help groups to record answers."}},{"activity":"Self-writing: level tasks and review","source":"M","ref":"p.15","tasks":{"Beginner":"Draw a picture about the discussion and then write a few sentences about it, expressing thoughts freely. Review: say what they drew or wrote; read the text aloud once; the teacher may write the text in the notebook for them.","Letter":"Write about what they liked, using drawing and writing; write any words or sentences they can. Review: read the text aloud once; correct punctuation mistakes using the Barakhadi chart.","Word":"Write a sentence based on the conversation. Mistakes in spelling, punctuation and sentence structure are fine. Review: read it to the group; discuss and correct mistakes together.","Para":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation.","Story":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation."}}],"organisation":[{"grouping":"Whole class (big group)","how":"All learners of all levels sit in a 'U' shape arranged by level (Beginner, Letter, Word, Para, Story) so that the move to small groups is easy.","activities":["Warm-up: Handkerchief game","Oral conversation: familiar topic","Story (Day 2 of the story): retelling","Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on my school"]},{"grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","how":"Learners of similar levels work together; the teacher gives each group a task for its level and spends more time with learners who need support. Rotate responsibilities (for example group leader).","activities":["Story: reading with actions and group questions","Language game: Find My Word"]},{"grouping":"Individual","how":"Each learner works on a task for their own level; the teacher moves around, observes difficulties and supports individuals.","activities":["Story: writing answers individually","Self-writing: individual writing","Self-writing: review and reading back","Daily reading (10 minutes)"]}],"materials":["A handkerchief","The same story book as yesterday","Story book","slate or paper for questions","Notebooks","Textbooks or storybooks","Picture card or topic on the board","crayons or pencils","Library books or storybooks"],"outcomes":["Learners take part in the oral conversation and speak without fear.","Learners retell the story, read with expression and ask or answer questions at their level.","Learners respond to the sound-symbol task for today (Language game: Find My Word) at their own level.","Learners write about the topic at their level and read it aloud.","Each learner reads a book for 10 minutes."],"observation":["Observe each learner's reading and writing during the individual tasks; note who needs individual support and how many learners share the same difficulty.","Note any learner whose level is improving; move the learner to the next level group when you see steady progress (manual p.5).","Record each learner's progress for the day in the notebook, according to the learner's level (manual p.4).","Use today's observations to adjust tomorrow's plan (manual p.5)."],"teacherNotes":["Questions to elicit on Day 2: information questions (answer not in the text), thinking questions (needs knowledge beyond the text) and opinion questions (feedback on something in the text).","The manual lists the letter and word games but does not fix the slot in the daily timetable where they are used. This plan places them in the 10-minute sound-symbol / alphabet slot (interpretation).","Writing has two parts, content and sequence: encourage learners to read what they wrote, improve it and rewrite it for clarity and correctness (manual p.15).","Pace: the manual says not to assume all learners progress at the same speed. Repeat a day's activity with the groups that need it before moving on.","Special needs: give extra time and prepare materials for slower learners; seat learners with hearing or vision difficulty at the front; for learners who reverse or confuse letters, trace letters on the letter card with a finger and write with dots to trace with a pencil (manual p.6)."],"components":[{"no":1,"key":"warmup","name":"Warm-up activities","keywords":["Handkerchief game","two learners lead"],"rows":[1]},{"no":2,"key":"oral","name":"Oral Discussion","keywords":["familiar topic","every learner speaks"],"rows":[2]},{"no":3,"key":"story","name":"Story","keywords":["Day 2","retell","read with actions","group questions","ask and answer","write answers (Para/Story)"],"rows":[3,4,5]},{"no":4,"key":"sound","name":"Sound symbol games, Sound separation-pairing","keywords":["Find My Word","play in turns","level support"],"rows":[6]},{"no":5,"key":"mindwrite","name":"Individual-Writing (Day 2)","keywords":["discussion","write at own level","self-review (read aloud)"],"rows":[7,8,9]},{"no":6,"key":"reading","name":"Daily reading","keywords":["library book","read alone","teacher listens"],"rows":[10]}],"preLesson":null},{"programme":"TARL Literacy","id":"lit-017","day":17,"phase":1,"phaseLabel":"Phase 1 (Days 1-45)","title":"Story: a story about a brave child (Day 1)","dayType":"Story Day 1 + Mind mapping","focus":"Identifying the first, second and last sound (bed, run, zip) | Mind map: garden","duration":70,"objectives":["Listen, speak and answer in the oral conversation (conversation on a picture).","Listen to and read a story with understanding; discuss it in big and small groups and respond at their own level.","Develop sound-symbol skills: Identifying the first, second and last sound (bed, run, zip).","Build vocabulary through a mind map ('garden') and use the words at their own level.","Read independently for 10 minutes every day."],"sequence":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Rhyme - 'I caught a Fish Alive'","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Say the rhyme with actions, then say it together. Lines: One, two, three, four, five, once I caught a fish alive. / Six, seven, eight, nine, ten, then I let it go again. / Why did you let it go? Because it bit my finger so. / Which finger did it bite? This little finger on my right. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Listen, then say the rhyme with actions.","tlm":"Rhyme chart or board (optional)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","n":1},{"activity":"Oral conversation: conversation on a picture","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Show a picture of a school assembly in the morning and ask what is happening, who is doing what and what is happening around them. Let learners think creatively and even make up a story.","learners":"Look at the picture, answer questions and make up their own story about it.","tlm":"Picture card of a school assembly in the morning","source":"M","ref":"p.9","n":2},{"activity":"Story (Day 1 of the story): reading aloud and discussion","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":8,"teacher":"Discuss the title or picture of the story with the learners. Read the story aloud with expression and voice modulation (learners do not repeat after you). Discuss it, with emphasis on vocabulary-based questions. Read it again slowly, pointing to each word.","learners":"Talk about the title/picture; listen; answer questions; follow each word with a finger in their own copy.","tlm":"A story from the school library (a story about a brave child), a copy for each learner","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":3},{"activity":"Story: reading in small groups","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":7,"teacher":"Form level-wise groups with a group leader. Learners read the story one sentence at a time while the others follow with their fingers. Para and Story level learners practise reading with emotion and expression.","learners":"Read the story sentence by sentence, supporting each other; the group leader helps.","tlm":"Story book copies","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":4},{"activity":"Story: level-wise individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":5,"teacher":"Give each learner the task for their level (see level table) and support those who need it.","learners":"Beginner/Letter: find and write favourite words or letters. Word: find consonant clusters. Para/Story: silently read, find unfamiliar and rhyming words.","tlm":"Story book, notebooks, board","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":5},{"activity":"Sound-symbol activity: oral sound awareness","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":4,"teacher":"Say words and ask learners to identify the first, second or last sound. Example: pan - first sound p, second sound a, third sound n; log: l, o, g; cup: c, u, p.","learners":"Say the first, second or last sound of the word.","tlm":"None (oral activity)","source":"M","ref":"p.12","n":6},{"activity":"Sound-symbol games by level","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":6,"teacher":"Give each level group its game (see level table). Move among the groups and help those who need support; say each word clearly.","learners":"Play the game for their level in small groups.","tlm":"Board, chalk, letter cards","source":"M","ref":"p.12","n":7},{"activity":"Mind mapping (Day 1): the word 'garden'","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Ask: 'What words come to your mind when you hear the word garden?' Write learners' answers on the board or floor (Para and Story level learners write the words themselves). Guide the map towards the learning objective. Example words: rose, lily, marigold, jasmine, bee, ant, butterfly, spider, spade, water, seed, fence.","learners":"Say words connected with 'garden'; share the meaning and feeling of words.","tlm":"Board, chalk (or floor)","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":8},{"activity":"Mind mapping: classify the words","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":4,"teacher":"Ask learners to classify the words in groups, for example: Flowers: rose, lily, marigold, jasmine; Insects: bee, ant, butterfly, spider; Things: spade, water, seed, fence.","learners":"Sort the words into groups and say why.","tlm":"Board, chalk, word cards (optional)","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":9},{"activity":"Mind mapping: level-wise individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":6,"teacher":"Give each learner the individual task for their level; observe closely and give individual support. Display corrected stories on the wall.","learners":"Complete the task for their level (see level table).","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":10},{"activity":"Daily reading (10 minutes)","grouping":"Individual","minutes":10,"teacher":"Give each learner a library book or any storybook. Move around, listen to individual readers and note their level.","learners":"Read independently a book of their choice.","tlm":"Library books or storybooks","source":"M","ref":"p.7","n":11}],"procedures":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Rhyme - 'I caught a Fish Alive'","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","steps":[{"teacher":"Say the rhyme 'I caught a Fish Alive' slowly with actions: One, two, three, four, five, once I caught a fish alive. / Six, seven, eight, nine, ten, then I let it go again. / Why did you let it go? Because it bit my finger so. / Which finger did it bite? This little finger on my right.","learners":"Listen and watch the actions."},{"teacher":"Say it again; invite learners to join with actions.","learners":"Say the rhyme together with actions."},{"teacher":"Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Choose a rhyme they like and lead."}]},{"activity":"Oral conversation: conversation on a picture","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.9","steps":[{"teacher":"Show the picture of a school assembly in the morning.","learners":"Look carefully."},{"teacher":"Ask: What is happening in the picture? Who is doing what? What is happening around them? Then: What might happen next?","learners":"Answer in their own words; every learner gets a chance."},{"teacher":"Let learners imagine and make up a short story from the picture.","learners":"Tell their stories to the class."}]},{"activity":"Story - Day 1 (a story about a brave child)","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.10","steps":[{"teacher":"Discuss the title or picture of the story with the learners.","learners":"Talk about what they see and what the story may be about."},{"teacher":"Read the story aloud with expression and proper voice modulation. Learners should not simply repeat after you.","learners":"Listen carefully and enjoy the story."},{"teacher":"Discuss the story: factual, logical, vocabulary-based, judgment or opinion questions (today's focus: vocabulary-based: What does this word mean? Which word in the story means the same as ...?). Begin in the home language if needed.","learners":"Think and respond thoughtfully; every learner takes part."},{"teacher":"Read the story again slowly, pointing to each word. Make sure each learner has a copy and follows with a finger.","learners":"Follow each word with their finger."},{"teacher":"Ask learners to read in small groups; select a group leader who helps the others. Learners read one sentence at a time while the others point with fingers.","learners":"Read with the help of one another."}]},{"activity":"Sound-symbol: oral and level games","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.12","steps":[{"teacher":"Say words and ask learners to identify the first, second or last sound. Example: pan - first sound p, second sound a, third sound n; log: l, o, g; cup: c, u, p.","learners":"Say the first, second or last sound of the word."},{"teacher":"Write the sounds or words for the day on the board and give each level group its task (see the level table).","learners":"Work in small groups and share their answers."},{"teacher":"Say each word clearly with distinct pronunciation. Give learners enough time to respond and think; use words learners commonly use at home (regional language and the medium of instruction).","learners":"Think, say and write the sounds."}]},{"activity":"Mind mapping: 'garden'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Small group (level-wise) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.14","steps":[{"teacher":"Choose a word that can generate many related words: 'garden'. Ask: 'What words come to your mind when you hear the word garden?' Write the answers on the board or floor.","learners":"Say words they link with 'garden'."},{"teacher":"Discuss the words: what they mean and how they are connected.","learners":"Explain their words and listen to others."},{"teacher":"In small groups, let the learners classify the words (Flowers: rose, lily, marigold, jasmine; Insects: bee, ant, butterfly, spider; Things: spade, water, seed, fence).","learners":"Sort the words into groups."},{"teacher":"Give the individual tasks by level and help each learner.","learners":"Work individually; read the work aloud at the end if time allows."}]}],"levelTasks":[{"activity":"Story - Day 1: individual tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.10","tasks":{"Beginner":"Circle or search for a favourite word or letter in the story and say it aloud. If a learner cannot draw a circle, write words on the board and ask them to identify them.","Letter":"Find, read and write favourite words from the story.","Word":"Find the consonant clusters in the story, read them and write them in the notebook.","Para":"Silently read the story from the textbook; find unfamiliar words and try to understand them; find rhyming words, use them in sentences and write in the notebook; ask other groups for meanings; make questions in groups.","Story":"Silently read the story; find unfamiliar words and rhyming words; practise reading with emotion; one group reads sentences formed with consonant clusters to the other group; ask and answer group questions (information, thinking and opinion questions)."}},{"activity":"Sound-symbol games by level (small groups)","source":"M","ref":"p.12","tasks":{"Beginner":"'What is the first sound in the word jug?' 'Is there a letter that makes the sound /j/?' 'Can you name objects that start with the letter J?' Learners think and share names in the group.","Letter":"Write the rhyming ending -in on the board and ask learners to add new letters to form words: p + in = pin, b + in = bin, f + in = fin.","Word":"Say a word and tell its sounds, for example 'sun' = /s/ + /u/ + /n/. Then tell what word is formed if /r/ is put before 'at': r + at = rat. Do 8-10 such combinations; at first learners may form meaningless words, later only meaningful words.","Para":"Write two or three sounds on the board (for example Br, cl, st) and let the learners form words that start with those sounds; this builds a word list for the learner.","Story":"Write two or three sounds on the board (for example Br, cl, st) and let the learners form words that start with those sounds; this builds a word list for the learner."}},{"activity":"Mind mapping 'garden': level tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.14","tasks":{"Beginner":"Circle all the words that contain the letter 'E' on the board; make a list. See how many learners find the most words.","Letter":"Circle all the words that contain the letter 'E' and make a list of them.","Word":"Use 4-5 words (for example ant, bee, lily, rose, seed) to form sentences, starting with words of one or two syllables. Example: Dream - I had a dream last night.","Para":"Choose any five words from the map and create a story with them. Use consonant clusters correctly, read the story aloud, correct mistakes of sentence structure, spelling or grammar, then display it on the wall.","Story":"Choose any five words from the map and create a story with them. Use consonant clusters correctly, read the story aloud, correct mistakes of sentence structure, spelling or grammar, then display it on the wall."}}],"organisation":[{"grouping":"Whole class (big group)","how":"All learners of all levels sit in a 'U' shape arranged by level (Beginner, Letter, Word, Para, Story) so that the move to small groups is easy.","activities":["Warm-up: Rhyme - 'I caught a Fish Alive'","Oral conversation: conversation on a picture","Story (Day 1 of the story): reading aloud and discussion","Sound-symbol activity: oral sound awareness","Mind mapping (Day 1): the word 'garden'"]},{"grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","how":"Learners of similar levels work together; the teacher gives each group a task for its level and spends more time with learners who need support. Rotate responsibilities (for example group leader).","activities":["Story: reading in small groups","Sound-symbol games by level","Mind mapping: classify the words"]},{"grouping":"Individual","how":"Each learner works on a task for their own level; the teacher moves around, observes difficulties and supports individuals.","activities":["Story: level-wise individual tasks","Mind mapping: level-wise individual tasks","Daily reading (10 minutes)"]}],"materials":["Rhyme chart or board (optional)","Picture card of a school assembly in the morning","A story from the school library (a story about a brave child)","a copy for each learner","Story book copies","Story book","notebooks","board","Board","chalk","letter cards","chalk (or floor)","word cards (optional)","Notebooks","Library books or storybooks"],"outcomes":["Learners take part in the oral conversation and speak without fear.","Learners show understanding of the story in the discussion and complete the task for their level.","Learners respond to the sound-symbol task for today (Identifying the first, second and last sound (bed, run, zip)) at their own level.","Learners add words to the mind map and use them in sentences or a story at their level.","Each learner reads a book for 10 minutes."],"observation":["Observe each learner's reading and writing during the individual tasks; note who needs individual support and how many learners share the same difficulty.","Note any learner whose level is improving; move the learner to the next level group when you see steady progress (manual p.5).","Record each learner's progress for the day in the notebook, according to the learner's level (manual p.4).","Use today's observations to adjust tomorrow's plan (manual p.5)."],"teacherNotes":["Story selection: the manual asks teachers to use picture story books or stories in the school library. Today's suggested theme (a story about a brave child) is a planning suggestion; use any suitable story you have.","Sound-symbol: for the first 4-5 days, play sound-based games with the learners at word level. Include the sounds learners find difficult when you prepare the Class Transaction Plan.","Mind mapping topic for this day: 'garden'. The manual's example uses the word 'shop'; today's topic follows the same method.","Pace: the manual says not to assume all learners progress at the same speed. Repeat a day's activity with the groups that need it before moving on.","Special needs: give extra time and prepare materials for slower learners; seat learners with hearing or vision difficulty at the front; for learners who reverse or confuse letters, trace letters on the letter card with a finger and write with dots to trace with a pencil (manual p.6)."],"components":[{"no":1,"key":"warmup","name":"Warm-up activities","keywords":["Rhyme - 'I caught a Fish Alive'","two learners lead"],"rows":[1]},{"no":2,"key":"oral","name":"Oral Discussion","keywords":["conversation on a picture","every learner speaks"],"rows":[2]},{"no":3,"key":"story","name":"Story","keywords":["Day 1","title / picture talk","read aloud with expression","vocabulary-based questions","re-read pointing","group reading","level tasks"],"rows":[3,4,5]},{"no":4,"key":"sound","name":"Sound symbol games, Sound separation-pairing","keywords":["oral sound awareness","first / second / last sound","level games in small groups"],"rows":[6,7]},{"no":5,"key":"mindwrite","name":"Mind Mapping (Day 1)","keywords":["mind map: garden","classify the words","level task: circle letter E / sentences / story"],"rows":[8,9,10]},{"no":6,"key":"reading","name":"Daily reading","keywords":["library book","read alone","teacher listens"],"rows":[11]}],"preLesson":null},{"programme":"TARL Literacy","id":"lit-018","day":18,"phase":1,"phaseLabel":"Phase 1 (Days 1-45)","title":"Saturday: drama presentation","dayType":"Saturday drama + Self-writing","focus":"Barakhadi / alphabet and phonics chart (line 1, letter 'w') | Self-writing: the story we acted out (a story about a brave child)","duration":70,"objectives":["Listen, speak and answer in the oral conversation (listening and storytelling).","Express a story through role play, using voice, facial expressions and gestures.","Develop sound-symbol skills: Barakhadi / alphabet and phonics chart (line 1, letter 'w').","Write about the story and review the writing.","Read independently for 10 minutes every day."],"sequence":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Singing and Spinning","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Learners sit in a circle and pass a small object while you clap with your back turned; when the clapping stops, the learner holding it sings a song, recites a poem or tells a joke. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Pass the object round the circle; sing, recite or tell a joke when the clapping stops.","tlm":"A small object (chalk or pencil)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","n":1},{"activity":"Oral conversation: listening and storytelling","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Tell an interesting story starter and involve the learners: 'I found a talking fish in the village pond. What did it say?' Let learners imagine and continue the story.","learners":"Listen to the teacher, then imagine and continue the story. Learners can also recite a rhyme or story they know.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.9","n":2},{"activity":"Dramatic presentation: introduction and reading","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Explain what a dramatic presentation is and how it is done. Provide stories discussed during the week and read one aloud once more. Para and Story level learners support Beginner and Letter level learners in reading.","learners":"Listen, read along, then each learner chooses a character.","tlm":"Stories discussed in the week (a story about a school day; a story about a brave child)","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":3},{"activity":"Dramatic presentation: planning in small groups","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":8,"teacher":"Each group discusses and plans dialogues; Para or Story level learners write the dialogues. Groups prepare their dramatic presentation.","learners":"Choose characters, plan and rehearse dialogues with facial expressions and gestures.","tlm":"Story, paper for dialogues","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":4},{"activity":"Dramatic presentation: performances and feedback","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":7,"teacher":"Learners sit in a U shape. Each group presents; after each performance, watching learners say what they enjoyed and what could be improved.","learners":"Perform in turn; watch; give feedback.","tlm":"Open space (U-shape seating)","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":5},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart: big group reading","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":3,"teacher":"Show the Barakhadi chart and ask which letter they like. Read the letter 'w' on the chart; learners listen carefully and point to it on their own chart (they do not repeat after you).","learners":"Listen and point to the letter on their own chart.","tlm":"Barakhadi chart, alphabet or phonics chart","source":"M","ref":"p.13","n":6},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart: small-group practice","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Learners practise reading the alphabet or phonics chart in groups and help each other. One learner per group reads aloud. Occasionally ask learners to identify the sounds of letters. Give each level its group task.","learners":"Read the chart in groups; one learner reads aloud; do the level task.","tlm":"Alphabet or phonics chart, board or floor","source":"M","ref":"p.13","n":7},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart: individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":2,"teacher":"Give each learner an individual task for their level and observe closely; assist any learner who needs individual support.","learners":"Say and write a letter or word, a sentence or a short paragraph (by level).","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.13","n":8},{"activity":"Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on the story we acted out (a story about a brave child)","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Start a conversation about the story used for the drama: 'the story we acted out (a story about a brave child)'. Involve all learners with open-ended questions.","learners":"Take part in the discussion and share thoughts freely.","tlm":"Picture card or topic on the board","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":9},{"activity":"Self-writing: individual writing","grouping":"Individual","minutes":7,"teacher":"Give each level its task (see level table). Let learners take ownership of what they draw and write; mistakes are fine.","learners":"Draw and write about the topic at their level.","tlm":"Notebooks, crayons or pencils","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":10},{"activity":"Self-writing: review and reading back","grouping":"Individual","minutes":3,"teacher":"Ask each learner 'What did you draw or write?' and have them read it aloud once. Word-level learners read to the group; discuss spelling, punctuation and sentence structure. Help beginners by writing their text in the notebook for them if needed.","learners":"Read what they wrote; correct mistakes after listening to their own reading.","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":11},{"activity":"Daily reading (10 minutes)","grouping":"Individual","minutes":10,"teacher":"Give each learner a library book or any storybook. Move around, listen to individual readers and note their level.","learners":"Read independently a book of their choice.","tlm":"Library books or storybooks","source":"M","ref":"p.7","n":12}],"procedures":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Singing and Spinning","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","steps":[{"teacher":"Seat the learners in a circle; give a small object to one learner.","learners":"Sit in a circle."},{"teacher":"Stand outside the circle with your back to them and clap steadily; they pass the object.","learners":"Pass the object while the clapping continues."},{"teacher":"Stop clapping; the learner holding the object sings, recites or tells a joke.","learners":"Perform, and everybody claps."}]},{"activity":"Oral conversation: listening and storytelling","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.9","steps":[{"teacher":"Say the starter: 'I found a talking fish in the village pond. What did it say?'","learners":"Listen and imagine."},{"teacher":"Ask learners to continue the story one by one. Encourage those who speak less.","learners":"Add ideas to the story."},{"teacher":"Invite a learner to recite a poem or rhyme they know.","learners":"Recite and listen to others."}]},{"activity":"Saturday special: dramatic presentation","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.11","steps":[{"teacher":"Explain what a dramatic presentation is and how it can be done. Give the groups the stories discussed during the week.","learners":"Listen to the explanation."},{"teacher":"Read a story aloud once more. Learners at story and paragraph level support those at beginner and letter level in reading.","learners":"Read along; helpers support their friends."},{"teacher":"After reading, each learner chooses a character from the story.","learners":"Choose a role (boys may play girl roles and girls may play boy roles)."},{"teacher":"In groups, learners discuss and plan the dialogues; paragraph or story level learners write the dialogues.","learners":"Plan and write dialogues together."},{"teacher":"Learners sit in a U shape. Each group presents its drama. After each performance, ask what the audience enjoyed and what could be improved.","learners":"Perform, watch and give kind feedback."}]},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart activity (line 1)","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Small group (level-wise) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.13","steps":[{"teacher":"Show the Barakhadi chart and ask the learners which letter they like. Where is the letter 'w'?","learners":"Look for the letter on the chart."},{"teacher":"Read the letter 'w' on the chart. Learners listen and point to it on their own chart. Make sure they do not repeat after you.","learners":"Listen and point to the letter."},{"teacher":"Learners read the alphabet or phonics chart in their groups and help each other; one learner from each group comes forward to read aloud.","learners":"Read in groups; the representative reads aloud."},{"teacher":"Occasionally ask them to identify the sounds of letters from the chart.","learners":"Say the sound of the letter you point to."},{"teacher":"As an extra activity, write some letters on the floor, call out each letter one by one and let the learners jump onto the correct letter.","learners":"Jump onto the letter that is called."}]},{"activity":"Self-writing: 'Discussion, Writing, Self-review'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.15","steps":[{"teacher":"Start a conversation about the story used for the drama: 'the story we acted out (a story about a brave child)'. Involve all learners with open-ended questions.","learners":"Discuss and answer questions."},{"teacher":"Give writing time at each level: draw then write (Beginner), write about what they liked (Letter), a sentence (Word), a paragraph or story on a topic of their choice (Para/Story).","learners":"Write at their level and take ownership of the work."},{"teacher":"Review: ask 'What did you draw or write?' Have each learner read the text aloud once. Support with writing if needed.","learners":"Read aloud, listen to their pronunciation and correct mistakes."}]}],"levelTasks":[{"activity":"Drama: roles by level","source":"M","ref":"p.11","tasks":{"Beginner":"Take a character role and say or act short lines with help from Para and Story level learners.","Letter":"Take a character role and say or act short lines with help from Para and Story level learners.","Word":"Take a role and speak the dialogues; help rehearse.","Para":"Write the dialogues for the group and support Beginner, Letter and Word level learners throughout.","Story":"Write the dialogues for the group and support Beginner, Letter and Word level learners throughout."}},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart: level tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.13","tasks":{"Beginner":"Small group: read the chart in the group; find and write favourite letters from the line. Individual: say and write a letter of their choice.","Letter":"Small group: read the chart; find and write favourite letters or words from any line. Individual: say a word on their own that begins with any letter.","Word":"Small group: write one or two lines of letters on the board or floor and use them to form words. Individual: speak and write sentences using words they know.","Para":"Small group: prepare word lists using the Barakhadi chart (for example items found in a shop or in the kitchen). Individual: write short paragraphs using the words formed with the Barakhadi chart.","Story":"Small group: prepare word lists using the Barakhadi chart. Individual: write short paragraphs using the words formed with the Barakhadi chart."}},{"activity":"Self-writing: level tasks and review","source":"M","ref":"p.15","tasks":{"Beginner":"Draw a picture about the discussion and then write a few sentences about it, expressing thoughts freely. Review: say what they drew or wrote; read the text aloud once; the teacher may write the text in the notebook for them.","Letter":"Write about what they liked, using drawing and writing; write any words or sentences they can. Review: read the text aloud once; correct punctuation mistakes using the Barakhadi chart.","Word":"Write a sentence based on the conversation. Mistakes in spelling, punctuation and sentence structure are fine. Review: read it to the group; discuss and correct mistakes together.","Para":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation.","Story":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation."}}],"organisation":[{"grouping":"Whole class (big group)","how":"All learners of all levels sit in a 'U' shape arranged by level (Beginner, Letter, Word, Para, Story) so that the move to small groups is easy.","activities":["Warm-up: Singing and Spinning","Oral conversation: listening and storytelling","Dramatic presentation: introduction and reading","Dramatic presentation: performances and feedback","Barakhadi chart: big group reading","Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on the story we acted out (a story about a brave child)"]},{"grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","how":"Learners of similar levels work together; the teacher gives each group a task for its level and spends more time with learners who need support. Rotate responsibilities (for example group leader).","activities":["Dramatic presentation: planning in small groups","Barakhadi chart: small-group practice"]},{"grouping":"Individual","how":"Each learner works on a task for their own level; the teacher moves around, observes difficulties and supports individuals.","activities":["Barakhadi chart: individual tasks","Self-writing: individual writing","Self-writing: review and reading back","Daily reading (10 minutes)"]}],"materials":["A small object (chalk or pencil)","Stories discussed in the week (a story about a school day; a story about a brave child)","Story","paper for dialogues","Open space (U-shape seating)","Barakhadi chart","alphabet or phonics chart","Alphabet or phonics chart","board or floor","Notebooks","Picture card or topic on the board","crayons or pencils","Library books or storybooks"],"outcomes":["Learners take part in the oral conversation and speak without fear.","Learners present a role in the group drama and give feedback to others.","Learners respond to the sound-symbol task for today (Barakhadi / alphabet and phonics chart (line 1, letter 'w')) at their own level.","Learners write about the story at their level and read it aloud.","Each learner reads a book for 10 minutes."],"observation":["Observe each learner's reading and writing during the individual tasks; note who needs individual support and how many learners share the same difficulty.","Note any learner whose level is improving; move the learner to the next level group when you see steady progress (manual p.5).","Record each learner's progress for the day in the notebook, according to the learner's level (manual p.4).","Use today's observations to adjust tomorrow's plan (manual p.5)."],"teacherNotes":["Saturday: this plan assumes Day 1 is a Monday (six teaching days per week). If your school week is different, hold the drama presentation on your Saturday and keep the other days in sequence.","Barakhadi: learners who need extra time should get repeated practice using one or two sound units at a time. Topic-based discussion helps oral expression, thinking and understanding.","Writing has two parts, content and sequence: encourage learners to read what they wrote, improve it and rewrite it for clarity and correctness (manual p.15).","Pace: the manual says not to assume all learners progress at the same speed. Repeat a day's activity with the groups that need it before moving on.","Special needs: give extra time and prepare materials for slower learners; seat learners with hearing or vision difficulty at the front; for learners who reverse or confuse letters, trace letters on the letter card with a finger and write with dots to trace with a pencil (manual p.6)."],"components":[{"no":1,"key":"warmup","name":"Warm-up activities","keywords":["Singing and Spinning","two learners lead"],"rows":[1]},{"no":2,"key":"oral","name":"Oral Discussion","keywords":["listening and storytelling","every learner speaks"],"rows":[2]},{"no":3,"key":"story","name":"Story (Saturday: dramatic presentation)","keywords":["Saturday drama","choose a character","plan dialogues","perform in U shape","feedback"],"rows":[3,4,5]},{"no":4,"key":"sound","name":"Sound symbol games, Sound separation-pairing","keywords":["Barakhadi / alphabet chart","listen and point (no repeating)","group reading","level tasks"],"rows":[6,7,8]},{"no":5,"key":"mindwrite","name":"Individual-Writing (Day 2)","keywords":["discussion","write at own level","self-review (read aloud)"],"rows":[9,10,11]},{"no":6,"key":"reading","name":"Daily reading","keywords":["library book","read alone","teacher listens"],"rows":[12]}],"preLesson":null},{"programme":"TARL Literacy","id":"lit-019","day":19,"phase":1,"phaseLabel":"Phase 1 (Days 1-45)","title":"Story: a story about a brave child (Day 2)","dayType":"Story Day 2 + Self-writing","focus":"Consonant clusters: nn (funny, dinner) | Self-writing: the animal I like most","duration":70,"objectives":["Listen, speak and answer in the oral conversation (What did you see on your way?).","Retell the story, read it with expression, ask and answer questions about it and write answers.","Develop sound-symbol skills: Consonant clusters: nn (funny, dinner).","Write about a topic at their own level and review the writing (the animal I like most).","Read independently for 10 minutes every day."],"sequence":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Rain clapping","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Everyone stands in a circle with eyes closed and keeps clapping: first one finger, then two, three, four and finally five fingers. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Stand in a circle, close the eyes and clap with 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 fingers.","tlm":"After the activity ask: What sound came after the last clap?","source":"M","ref":"p.8","n":1},{"activity":"Oral conversation: What did you see on your way?","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Ask learners to describe what they saw on their way to school. If they are hesitant, begin yourself: 'On the road I saw a bullock cart, a tea stall and a boy flying a kite. What did you see?'","learners":"Describe what they saw on the way to school and connect with what others share.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.9","n":2},{"activity":"Story (Day 2 of the story): retelling","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":6,"teacher":"Ask learners to retell yesterday's story in their own words. Prompt with questions on the beginning, middle and end.","learners":"Retell the story using their own words.","tlm":"The same story book as yesterday","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":3},{"activity":"Story: reading with actions and group questions","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":9,"teacher":"Learners practise reading with actions and expressions; one learner per group reads aloud to the class. Guide groups to make questions about the story (guide initially). Groups take turns to ask and answer each other's questions. Word-level learners also read aloud the consonants learned on the first day.","learners":"Read with actions; make questions (word-level learners help write them); ask and answer questions with another group.","tlm":"Story book, slate or paper for questions","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":4},{"activity":"Story: writing answers individually","grouping":"Individual","minutes":5,"teacher":"Para and Story level learners write answers to all questions individually; read and correct their responses after they finish.","learners":"Write the answers in their notebooks; Beginner/Letter/Word learners read or listen and answer orally.","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":5},{"activity":"Consonant clusters: introduction","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":4,"teacher":"Same-letter clusters: familiarise learners with clusters made of the same letter ('nn' as in funny, dinner, runner). Ask them to pronounce them and find such words in the text and write them down.","learners":"Listen, pronounce the cluster and say words that contain it.","tlm":"Board and chalk, words list (funny dinner runner penny tunnel)","source":"M","ref":"p.16","n":6},{"activity":"Consonant cluster game: Looking for Similar Ones","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":6,"teacher":"Write some words with the same conjunct consonants on the board, for example bl, tr, st. Observe closely and help learners who need support.","learners":"Match words that have the same conjunct consonant (black, blue, blanket, blow, blink).","tlm":"Words on the board","source":"M","ref":"p.17","n":7},{"activity":"Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on the animal I like most","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Start a conversation about a topic: 'the animal I like most'. Involve all learners and ask open-ended questions.","learners":"Take part in the discussion and share thoughts freely.","tlm":"Picture card or topic on the board","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":8},{"activity":"Self-writing: individual writing","grouping":"Individual","minutes":7,"teacher":"Give each level its task (see level table). Let learners take ownership of what they draw and write; mistakes are fine.","learners":"Draw and write about the topic at their level.","tlm":"Notebooks, crayons or pencils","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":9},{"activity":"Self-writing: review and reading back","grouping":"Individual","minutes":3,"teacher":"Ask each learner 'What did you draw or write?' and have them read it aloud once. Word-level learners read to the group; discuss spelling, punctuation and sentence structure. Help beginners by writing their text in the notebook for them if needed.","learners":"Read what they wrote; correct mistakes after listening to their own reading.","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":10},{"activity":"Daily reading (10 minutes)","grouping":"Individual","minutes":10,"teacher":"Give each learner a library book or any storybook. Move around, listen to individual readers and note their level.","learners":"Read independently a book of their choice.","tlm":"Library books or storybooks","source":"M","ref":"p.7","n":11}],"procedures":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Rain clapping","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","steps":[{"teacher":"Stand the learners in a circle and ask them to close their eyes. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Stand in a circle and close their eyes."},{"teacher":"Start clapping with one finger; then two fingers, three, four and finally five fingers.","learners":"Keep clapping, copying the change of fingers."},{"teacher":"After the activity ask: What sound came after the last clap?","learners":"Tell how they felt and what the sounds reminded them of."}]},{"activity":"Oral conversation: What did you see on your way?","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.9","steps":[{"teacher":"Ask: 'What did you see on your way to school today?'","learners":"Think about the way to school."},{"teacher":"If learners hesitate, start: 'On the road I saw a bullock cart, a tea stall and a boy flying a kite. What did you see?'","learners":"Listen to the model and then share their own observations."},{"teacher":"Connect learners' answers with each other.","learners":"Listen and add what they noticed."}]},{"activity":"Story - Day 2 (a story about a brave child)","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.11","steps":[{"teacher":"Ask learners to retell the story they read yesterday in their own words.","learners":"Retell, helping each other remember."},{"teacher":"In small groups learners practise reading the story using actions and expressions; one learner from each group then reads aloud to the class.","learners":"Read with actions and expression; a representative reads aloud."},{"teacher":"Guide the groups to come up with questions about the story (guide initially). Word-level learners can support by helping write them down.","learners":"Make questions together."},{"teacher":"Groups take turns to ask and answer each other's questions. Useful kinds: questions whose answer is not in the text; questions needing thinking beyond the text; questions asking for an opinion.","learners":"Ask, answer and discuss in the groups."},{"teacher":"Word-level learners also read aloud the consonants they learned on the first day.","learners":"Read the consonant clusters aloud."}]},{"activity":"Consonant clusters (nn) and the game 'Looking for Similar Ones'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.16-17","steps":[{"teacher":"Same-letter clusters: familiarise learners with clusters made of the same letter ('nn' as in funny, dinner, runner). Ask them to pronounce them and find such words in the text and write them down.","learners":"Listen, pronounce and find words in the text."},{"teacher":"Write the words on the board: funny dinner runner penny tunnel. Read them aloud with distinct pronunciation of the cluster.","learners":"Read the words aloud; point to the cluster in each word."},{"teacher":"Write some words with the same conjunct consonants on the board, for example bl, tr, st.","learners":"Match words that have the same conjunct consonant (black, blue, blanket, blow, blink)."}]},{"activity":"Self-writing: 'Discussion, Writing, Self-review'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.15","steps":[{"teacher":"Start a conversation about a topic: 'the animal I like most'. Involve all learners and ask open-ended questions.","learners":"Discuss and answer questions."},{"teacher":"Give writing time at each level: draw then write (Beginner), write about what they liked (Letter), a sentence (Word), a paragraph or story on a topic of their choice (Para/Story).","learners":"Write at their level and take ownership of the work."},{"teacher":"Review: ask 'What did you draw or write?' Have each learner read the text aloud once. Support with writing if needed.","learners":"Read aloud, listen to their pronunciation and correct mistakes."}]}],"levelTasks":[{"activity":"Story - Day 2: level-wise tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.11","tasks":{"Beginner":"Retell with the group by pointing to pictures or words; read aloud with group support (interpretation of the manual's group reading task).","Letter":"Read with the group, pointing to words; say the letters and words they know (interpretation of the manual's group reading task).","Word":"Support the group in writing the questions; read aloud the consonant clusters learned on the first day.","Para":"Ask the group's questions to another group, discuss them, then write answers to all questions individually; the teacher reads and corrects.","Story":"Ask the group's questions to another group, discuss them, then write answers to all questions individually; the teacher reads and corrects."}},{"activity":"Consonant clusters (nn): level tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.16-17","tasks":{"Beginner":"Listen to the sound of the cluster and point to it in a word; continue with letter-sound work (interpretation: the manual describes clusters for learners lagging in reading words and sentences).","Letter":"Listen to the cluster sound and pick words with the cluster from a word card (interpretation).","Word":"Find the cluster in the story or textbook words, read the words and write them in the notebook.","Para":"Form words and sentences using the cluster; read the sentences aloud.","Story":"Form words and sentences using the cluster; read the sentences aloud; use them in the story writing."}},{"activity":"Self-writing: level tasks and review","source":"M","ref":"p.15","tasks":{"Beginner":"Draw a picture about the discussion and then write a few sentences about it, expressing thoughts freely. Review: say what they drew or wrote; read the text aloud once; the teacher may write the text in the notebook for them.","Letter":"Write about what they liked, using drawing and writing; write any words or sentences they can. Review: read the text aloud once; correct punctuation mistakes using the Barakhadi chart.","Word":"Write a sentence based on the conversation. Mistakes in spelling, punctuation and sentence structure are fine. Review: read it to the group; discuss and correct mistakes together.","Para":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation.","Story":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation."}}],"organisation":[{"grouping":"Whole class (big group)","how":"All learners of all levels sit in a 'U' shape arranged by level (Beginner, Letter, Word, Para, Story) so that the move to small groups is easy.","activities":["Warm-up: Rain clapping","Oral conversation: What did you see on your way?","Story (Day 2 of the story): retelling","Consonant clusters: introduction","Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on the animal I like most"]},{"grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","how":"Learners of similar levels work together; the teacher gives each group a task for its level and spends more time with learners who need support. Rotate responsibilities (for example group leader).","activities":["Story: reading with actions and group questions","Consonant cluster game: Looking for Similar Ones"]},{"grouping":"Individual","how":"Each learner works on a task for their own level; the teacher moves around, observes difficulties and supports individuals.","activities":["Story: writing answers individually","Self-writing: individual writing","Self-writing: review and reading back","Daily reading (10 minutes)"]}],"materials":["After the activity ask: What sound came after the last clap?","The same story book as yesterday","Story book","slate or paper for questions","Notebooks","Board","chalk","words list (funny dinner runner penny tunnel)","Words on the board","Picture card or topic on the board","crayons or pencils","Library books or storybooks"],"outcomes":["Learners take part in the oral conversation and speak without fear.","Learners retell the story, read with expression and ask or answer questions at their level.","Learners respond to the sound-symbol task for today (Consonant clusters: nn (funny, dinner)) at their own level.","Learners write about the topic at their level and read it aloud.","Each learner reads a book for 10 minutes."],"observation":["Observe each learner's reading and writing during the individual tasks; note who needs individual support and how many learners share the same difficulty.","Note any learner whose level is improving; move the learner to the next level group when you see steady progress (manual p.5).","Record each learner's progress for the day in the notebook, according to the learner's level (manual p.4).","Use today's observations to adjust tomorrow's plan (manual p.5)."],"teacherNotes":["Questions to elicit on Day 2: information questions (answer not in the text), thinking questions (needs knowledge beyond the text) and opinion questions (feedback on something in the text).","Consonant clusters: do these activities daily for learners who find reading complex words hard; the aim is to remove the fear of reading clusters. Teachers may carry out similar activities on their own.","Writing has two parts, content and sequence: encourage learners to read what they wrote, improve it and rewrite it for clarity and correctness (manual p.15).","Pace: the manual says not to assume all learners progress at the same speed. Repeat a day's activity with the groups that need it before moving on.","Special needs: give extra time and prepare materials for slower learners; seat learners with hearing or vision difficulty at the front; for learners who reverse or confuse letters, trace letters on the letter card with a finger and write with dots to trace with a pencil (manual p.6)."],"components":[{"no":1,"key":"warmup","name":"Warm-up activities","keywords":["Rain clapping","two learners lead"],"rows":[1]},{"no":2,"key":"oral","name":"Oral Discussion","keywords":["What did you see on your way?","every learner speaks"],"rows":[2]},{"no":3,"key":"story","name":"Story","keywords":["Day 2","retell","read with actions","group questions","ask and answer","write answers (Para/Story)"],"rows":[3,4,5]},{"no":4,"key":"sound","name":"Sound symbol games, Sound separation-pairing","keywords":["consonant cluster 'nn'","pronounce and find words","game: Looking for Similar Ones"],"rows":[6,7]},{"no":5,"key":"mindwrite","name":"Individual-Writing (Day 2)","keywords":["discussion","write at own level","self-review (read aloud)"],"rows":[8,9,10]},{"no":6,"key":"reading","name":"Daily reading","keywords":["library book","read alone","teacher listens"],"rows":[11]}],"preLesson":null},{"programme":"TARL Literacy","id":"lit-020","day":20,"phase":1,"phaseLabel":"Phase 1 (Days 1-45)","title":"Story: a story about sharing food (Day 1)","dayType":"Story Day 1 + Mind mapping","focus":"Language game: Word Builders | Mind map: zoo","duration":70,"objectives":["Listen, speak and answer in the oral conversation (familiar topic).","Listen to and read a story with understanding; discuss it in big and small groups and respond at their own level.","Develop sound-symbol skills: Language game: Word Builders.","Build vocabulary through a mind map ('zoo') and use the words at their own level.","Read independently for 10 minutes every day."],"sequence":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Writing with body parts","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Learners stand in a circle. Demonstrate writing the word 'moon' in the air with a finger, then ask them to write it with different body parts. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Write the word 'moon' in the air with the finger, then with the head, shoulders, knees or elbows.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.8","n":1},{"activity":"Oral conversation: familiar topic","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Hold a conversation on the topic 'my favourite animal and why I like it'. Give each learner a chance to speak; be patient with learners who need extra time.","learners":"Talk about the topic and listen to others.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.9","n":2},{"activity":"Story (Day 1 of the story): reading aloud and discussion","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":8,"teacher":"Discuss the title or picture of the story with the learners. Read the story aloud with expression and voice modulation (learners do not repeat after you). Discuss it, with emphasis on judgment questions. Read it again slowly, pointing to each word.","learners":"Talk about the title/picture; listen; answer questions; follow each word with a finger in their own copy.","tlm":"A story from the school library (a story about sharing food), a copy for each learner","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":3},{"activity":"Story: reading in small groups","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":7,"teacher":"Form level-wise groups with a group leader. Learners read the story one sentence at a time while the others follow with their fingers. Para and Story level learners practise reading with emotion and expression.","learners":"Read the story sentence by sentence, supporting each other; the group leader helps.","tlm":"Story book copies","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":4},{"activity":"Story: level-wise individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":5,"teacher":"Give each learner the task for their level (see level table) and support those who need it.","learners":"Beginner/Letter: find and write favourite words or letters. Word: find consonant clusters. Para/Story: silently read, find unfamiliar and rhyming words.","tlm":"Story book, notebooks, board","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":5},{"activity":"Language game: Word Builders","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Groups of 4-5 pick four folded letter slips and form as many words as they can. Observe each learner and give help where needed.","learners":"Play the game, take turns and read or say the words they make.","tlm":"Folded letter slips, a container","source":"M","ref":"p.19","n":6},{"activity":"Mind mapping (Day 1): the word 'zoo'","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Ask: 'What words come to your mind when you hear the word zoo?' Write learners' answers on the board or floor (Para and Story level learners write the words themselves). Guide the map towards the learning objective. Example words: elephant, tiger, lion, rhinoceros, monkey, rabbit, deer, parrot, ticket, cage, keeper, gate.","learners":"Say words connected with 'zoo'; share the meaning and feeling of words.","tlm":"Board, chalk (or floor)","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":7},{"activity":"Mind mapping: classify the words","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":4,"teacher":"Ask learners to classify the words in groups, for example: Big animals: elephant, tiger, lion, rhinoceros; Small animals: monkey, rabbit, deer, parrot; People and things: ticket, cage, keeper, gate.","learners":"Sort the words into groups and say why.","tlm":"Board, chalk, word cards (optional)","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":8},{"activity":"Mind mapping: level-wise individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":6,"teacher":"Give each learner the individual task for their level; observe closely and give individual support. Display corrected stories on the wall.","learners":"Complete the task for their level (see level table).","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":9},{"activity":"Daily reading (10 minutes)","grouping":"Individual","minutes":10,"teacher":"Give each learner a library book or any storybook. Move around, listen to individual readers and note their level.","learners":"Read independently a book of their choice.","tlm":"Library books or storybooks","source":"M","ref":"p.7","n":10}],"procedures":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Writing with body parts","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","steps":[{"teacher":"Stand the learners in a circle. Demonstrate writing the word 'moon' in the air with your finger.","learners":"Watch and then copy with their own finger."},{"teacher":"Ask them to write it again using elbows and other body parts (head, shoulders, knees, ...).","learners":"Write the letters in the air with the named body part."},{"teacher":"Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Take turns to lead."}]},{"activity":"Oral conversation: familiar topic","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.9","steps":[{"teacher":"Introduce the topic: 'my favourite animal and why I like it'.","learners":"Think about their own experience."},{"teacher":"Ask open questions; give every learner a chance. Involve learners who speak less.","learners":"Speak freely and without fear."},{"teacher":"Praise efforts and sum up.","learners":"Listen and respect each other's ideas."}]},{"activity":"Story - Day 1 (a story about sharing food)","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.10","steps":[{"teacher":"Discuss the title or picture of the story with the learners.","learners":"Talk about what they see and what the story may be about."},{"teacher":"Read the story aloud with expression and proper voice modulation. Learners should not simply repeat after you.","learners":"Listen carefully and enjoy the story."},{"teacher":"Discuss the story: factual, logical, vocabulary-based, judgment or opinion questions (today's focus: judgment: Was the character right or wrong? Was that a good thing to do? Why?). Begin in the home language if needed.","learners":"Think and respond thoughtfully; every learner takes part."},{"teacher":"Read the story again slowly, pointing to each word. Make sure each learner has a copy and follows with a finger.","learners":"Follow each word with their finger."},{"teacher":"Ask learners to read in small groups; select a group leader who helps the others. Learners read one sentence at a time while the others point with fingers.","learners":"Read with the help of one another."}]},{"activity":"Language game: Word Builders","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.19","steps":[{"teacher":"Write different letters on small pieces of paper, fold them and put them in a container. Make groups of 4-5.","learners":"Sit in groups."},{"teacher":"Let each group pick four folded pieces and form as many words as possible with the letters.","learners":"Discuss and write words together."},{"teacher":"The group with the most correct words wins. Give new letter sets for the next round.","learners":"Read the words the group formed aloud."}]},{"activity":"Mind mapping: 'zoo'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Small group (level-wise) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.14","steps":[{"teacher":"Choose a word that can generate many related words: 'zoo'. Ask: 'What words come to your mind when you hear the word zoo?' Write the answers on the board or floor.","learners":"Say words they link with 'zoo'."},{"teacher":"Discuss the words: what they mean and how they are connected.","learners":"Explain their words and listen to others."},{"teacher":"In small groups, let the learners classify the words (Big animals: elephant, tiger, lion, rhinoceros; Small animals: monkey, rabbit, deer, parrot; People and things: ticket, cage, keeper, gate).","learners":"Sort the words into groups."},{"teacher":"Give the individual tasks by level and help each learner.","learners":"Work individually; read the work aloud at the end if time allows."}]}],"levelTasks":[{"activity":"Story - Day 1: individual tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.10","tasks":{"Beginner":"Circle or search for a favourite word or letter in the story and say it aloud. If a learner cannot draw a circle, write words on the board and ask them to identify them.","Letter":"Find, read and write favourite words from the story.","Word":"Find the consonant clusters in the story, read them and write them in the notebook.","Para":"Silently read the story from the textbook; find unfamiliar words and try to understand them; find rhyming words, use them in sentences and write in the notebook; ask other groups for meanings; make questions in groups.","Story":"Silently read the story; find unfamiliar words and rhyming words; practise reading with emotion; one group reads sentences formed with consonant clusters to the other group; ask and answer group questions (information, thinking and opinion questions)."}},{"activity":"Language game: Word Builders - level support","source":"I","ref":"p.19","tasks":{"Beginner":"Take part by saying or pointing to the letters involved and by listening carefully; Para and Story level partners help.","Letter":"Say the letters/sounds and give simple words they know.","Word":"Say and write words and short sentences for the game.","Para":"Write sentences with the words; help groups to record answers.","Story":"Write sentences or short stories with the words; help groups to record answers."}},{"activity":"Mind mapping 'zoo': level tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.14","tasks":{"Beginner":"Circle all the words that contain the letter 'E' on the board; make a list. See how many learners find the most words.","Letter":"Circle all the words that contain the letter 'E' and make a list of them.","Word":"Use 4-5 words (for example cage, deer, gate, lion, tiger) to form sentences, starting with words of one or two syllables. Example: Dream - I had a dream last night.","Para":"Choose any five words from the map and create a story with them. Use consonant clusters correctly, read the story aloud, correct mistakes of sentence structure, spelling or grammar, then display it on the wall.","Story":"Choose any five words from the map and create a story with them. Use consonant clusters correctly, read the story aloud, correct mistakes of sentence structure, spelling or grammar, then display it on the wall."}}],"organisation":[{"grouping":"Whole class (big group)","how":"All learners of all levels sit in a 'U' shape arranged by level (Beginner, Letter, Word, Para, Story) so that the move to small groups is easy.","activities":["Warm-up: Writing with body parts","Oral conversation: familiar topic","Story (Day 1 of the story): reading aloud and discussion","Mind mapping (Day 1): the word 'zoo'"]},{"grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","how":"Learners of similar levels work together; the teacher gives each group a task for its level and spends more time with learners who need support. Rotate responsibilities (for example group leader).","activities":["Story: reading in small groups","Language game: Word Builders","Mind mapping: classify the words"]},{"grouping":"Individual","how":"Each learner works on a task for their own level; the teacher moves around, observes difficulties and supports individuals.","activities":["Story: level-wise individual tasks","Mind mapping: level-wise individual tasks","Daily reading (10 minutes)"]}],"materials":["A story from the school library (a story about sharing food)","a copy for each learner","Story book copies","Story book","notebooks","board","Folded letter slips","a container","Board","chalk (or floor)","chalk","word cards (optional)","Notebooks","Library books or storybooks"],"outcomes":["Learners take part in the oral conversation and speak without fear.","Learners show understanding of the story in the discussion and complete the task for their level.","Learners respond to the sound-symbol task for today (Language game: Word Builders) at their own level.","Learners add words to the mind map and use them in sentences or a story at their level.","Each learner reads a book for 10 minutes."],"observation":["Observe each learner's reading and writing during the individual tasks; note who needs individual support and how many learners share the same difficulty.","Note any learner whose level is improving; move the learner to the next level group when you see steady progress (manual p.5).","Record each learner's progress for the day in the notebook, according to the learner's level (manual p.4).","Use today's observations to adjust tomorrow's plan (manual p.5)."],"teacherNotes":["Story selection: the manual asks teachers to use picture story books or stories in the school library. Today's suggested theme (a story about sharing food) is a planning suggestion; use any suitable story you have.","The manual lists the letter and word games but does not fix the slot in the daily timetable where they are used. This plan places them in the 10-minute sound-symbol / alphabet slot (interpretation).","Mind mapping topic for this day: 'zoo'. The manual's example uses the word 'shop'; today's topic follows the same method.","Level check: if learners have moved up to a new level, celebrate with an appreciation-oriented game (beginner level to letter level): 'Look for Me' or 'What's Your Name?' (manual p.42-45). Teachers may use such activities on their own.","Pace: the manual says not to assume all learners progress at the same speed. Repeat a day's activity with the groups that need it before moving on.","Special needs: give extra time and prepare materials for slower learners; seat learners with hearing or vision difficulty at the front; for learners who reverse or confuse letters, trace letters on the letter card with a finger and write with dots to trace with a pencil (manual p.6)."],"components":[{"no":1,"key":"warmup","name":"Warm-up activities","keywords":["Writing with body parts","two learners lead"],"rows":[1]},{"no":2,"key":"oral","name":"Oral Discussion","keywords":["familiar topic","every learner speaks"],"rows":[2]},{"no":3,"key":"story","name":"Story","keywords":["Day 1","title / picture talk","read aloud with expression","judgment questions","re-read pointing","group reading","level tasks"],"rows":[3,4,5]},{"no":4,"key":"sound","name":"Sound symbol games, Sound separation-pairing","keywords":["Word Builders","play in turns","level support"],"rows":[6]},{"no":5,"key":"mindwrite","name":"Mind Mapping (Day 1)","keywords":["mind map: zoo","classify the words","level task: circle letter E / sentences / story"],"rows":[7,8,9]},{"no":6,"key":"reading","name":"Daily reading","keywords":["library book","read alone","teacher listens"],"rows":[10]}],"preLesson":null},{"programme":"TARL Literacy","id":"lit-021","day":21,"phase":1,"phaseLabel":"Phase 1 (Days 1-45)","title":"Story: a story about sharing food (Day 2)","dayType":"Story Day 2 + Self-writing","focus":"Barakhadi / alphabet and phonics chart (line 4, letter 'z') | Self-writing: a picture of children at play","duration":70,"objectives":["Listen, speak and answer in the oral conversation (conversation on a picture).","Retell the story, read it with expression, ask and answer questions about it and write answers.","Develop sound-symbol skills: Barakhadi / alphabet and phonics chart (line 4, letter 'z').","Write about a topic at their own level and review the writing (a picture of children at play).","Read independently for 10 minutes every day."],"sequence":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Alphabet song (last-letter word chain)","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Say a word to the big group, for example 'yak'. Learners say a word that starts with the last letter ('k'). A learner who cannot say a word is out. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Say a word that starts with the last letter of the previous word; step out if unable to.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.8","n":1},{"activity":"Oral conversation: conversation on a picture","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Show a picture of a family having dinner together and ask what is happening, who is doing what and what is happening around them. Let learners think creatively and even make up a story.","learners":"Look at the picture, answer questions and make up their own story about it.","tlm":"Picture card of a family having dinner together","source":"M","ref":"p.9","n":2},{"activity":"Story (Day 2 of the story): retelling","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":6,"teacher":"Ask learners to retell yesterday's story in their own words. Prompt with questions on the beginning, middle and end.","learners":"Retell the story using their own words.","tlm":"The same story book as yesterday","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":3},{"activity":"Story: reading with actions and group questions","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":9,"teacher":"Learners practise reading with actions and expressions; one learner per group reads aloud to the class. Guide groups to make questions about the story (guide initially). Groups take turns to ask and answer each other's questions. Word-level learners also read aloud the consonants learned on the first day.","learners":"Read with actions; make questions (word-level learners help write them); ask and answer questions with another group.","tlm":"Story book, slate or paper for questions","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":4},{"activity":"Story: writing answers individually","grouping":"Individual","minutes":5,"teacher":"Para and Story level learners write answers to all questions individually; read and correct their responses after they finish.","learners":"Write the answers in their notebooks; Beginner/Letter/Word learners read or listen and answer orally.","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":5},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart: big group reading","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":3,"teacher":"Show the Barakhadi chart and ask which letter they like. Read the letter 'z' on the chart; learners listen carefully and point to it on their own chart (they do not repeat after you).","learners":"Listen and point to the letter on their own chart.","tlm":"Barakhadi chart, alphabet or phonics chart","source":"M","ref":"p.13","n":6},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart: small-group practice","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Learners practise reading the alphabet or phonics chart in groups and help each other. One learner per group reads aloud. Occasionally ask learners to identify the sounds of letters. Give each level its group task.","learners":"Read the chart in groups; one learner reads aloud; do the level task.","tlm":"Alphabet or phonics chart, board or floor","source":"M","ref":"p.13","n":7},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart: individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":2,"teacher":"Give each learner an individual task for their level and observe closely; assist any learner who needs individual support.","learners":"Say and write a letter or word, a sentence or a short paragraph (by level).","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.13","n":8},{"activity":"Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on a picture of children at play","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Start a conversation about a situation: 'a picture of children at play'. Involve all learners and ask open-ended questions.","learners":"Take part in the discussion and share thoughts freely.","tlm":"Picture card or topic on the board","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":9},{"activity":"Self-writing: individual writing","grouping":"Individual","minutes":7,"teacher":"Give each level its task (see level table). Let learners take ownership of what they draw and write; mistakes are fine.","learners":"Draw and write about the topic at their level.","tlm":"Notebooks, crayons or pencils","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":10},{"activity":"Self-writing: review and reading back","grouping":"Individual","minutes":3,"teacher":"Ask each learner 'What did you draw or write?' and have them read it aloud once. Word-level learners read to the group; discuss spelling, punctuation and sentence structure. Help beginners by writing their text in the notebook for them if needed.","learners":"Read what they wrote; correct mistakes after listening to their own reading.","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":11},{"activity":"Daily reading (10 minutes)","grouping":"Individual","minutes":10,"teacher":"Give each learner a library book or any storybook. Move around, listen to individual readers and note their level.","learners":"Read independently a book of their choice.","tlm":"Library books or storybooks","source":"M","ref":"p.7","n":12}],"procedures":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Alphabet song (last-letter word chain)","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","steps":[{"teacher":"Say the word 'yak' to the big group and show that its last letter is 'k'.","learners":"Listen and think of a word starting with 'k'."},{"teacher":"Ask learners in turn to say a word that starts with the last letter of the previous word. Example: rain -> nest.","learners":"Say a word in turn; anyone who cannot say a word is out of the game."},{"teacher":"Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Lead the game when it is their turn."}]},{"activity":"Oral conversation: conversation on a picture","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.9","steps":[{"teacher":"Show the picture of a family having dinner together.","learners":"Look carefully."},{"teacher":"Ask: What is happening in the picture? Who is doing what? What is happening around them? Then: How do the people feel? How can you tell?","learners":"Answer in their own words; every learner gets a chance."},{"teacher":"Let learners imagine and make up a short story from the picture.","learners":"Tell their stories to the class."}]},{"activity":"Story - Day 2 (a story about sharing food)","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.11","steps":[{"teacher":"Ask learners to retell the story they read yesterday in their own words.","learners":"Retell, helping each other remember."},{"teacher":"In small groups learners practise reading the story using actions and expressions; one learner from each group then reads aloud to the class.","learners":"Read with actions and expression; a representative reads aloud."},{"teacher":"Guide the groups to come up with questions about the story (guide initially). Word-level learners can support by helping write them down.","learners":"Make questions together."},{"teacher":"Groups take turns to ask and answer each other's questions. Useful kinds: questions whose answer is not in the text; questions needing thinking beyond the text; questions asking for an opinion.","learners":"Ask, answer and discuss in the groups."},{"teacher":"Word-level learners also read aloud the consonants they learned on the first day.","learners":"Read the consonant clusters aloud."}]},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart activity (line 4)","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Small group (level-wise) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.13","steps":[{"teacher":"Show the Barakhadi chart and ask the learners which letter they like. Where is the letter 'z'?","learners":"Look for the letter on the chart."},{"teacher":"Read the letter 'z' on the chart. Learners listen and point to it on their own chart. Make sure they do not repeat after you.","learners":"Listen and point to the letter."},{"teacher":"Learners read the alphabet or phonics chart in their groups and help each other; one learner from each group comes forward to read aloud.","learners":"Read in groups; the representative reads aloud."},{"teacher":"Occasionally ask them to identify the sounds of letters from the chart.","learners":"Say the sound of the letter you point to."},{"teacher":"As an extra activity, write some letters on the floor, call out each letter one by one and let the learners jump onto the correct letter.","learners":"Jump onto the letter that is called."}]},{"activity":"Self-writing: 'Discussion, Writing, Self-review'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.15","steps":[{"teacher":"Start a conversation about a situation: 'a picture of children at play'. Involve all learners and ask open-ended questions.","learners":"Discuss and answer questions."},{"teacher":"Give writing time at each level: draw then write (Beginner), write about what they liked (Letter), a sentence (Word), a paragraph or story on a topic of their choice (Para/Story).","learners":"Write at their level and take ownership of the work."},{"teacher":"Review: ask 'What did you draw or write?' Have each learner read the text aloud once. Support with writing if needed.","learners":"Read aloud, listen to their pronunciation and correct mistakes."}]}],"levelTasks":[{"activity":"Story - Day 2: level-wise tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.11","tasks":{"Beginner":"Retell with the group by pointing to pictures or words; read aloud with group support (interpretation of the manual's group reading task).","Letter":"Read with the group, pointing to words; say the letters and words they know (interpretation of the manual's group reading task).","Word":"Support the group in writing the questions; read aloud the consonant clusters learned on the first day.","Para":"Ask the group's questions to another group, discuss them, then write answers to all questions individually; the teacher reads and corrects.","Story":"Ask the group's questions to another group, discuss them, then write answers to all questions individually; the teacher reads and corrects."}},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart: level tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.13","tasks":{"Beginner":"Small group: read the chart in the group; find and write favourite letters from the line. Individual: say and write a letter of their choice.","Letter":"Small group: read the chart; find and write favourite letters or words from any line. Individual: say a word on their own that begins with any letter.","Word":"Small group: write one or two lines of letters on the board or floor and use them to form words. Individual: speak and write sentences using words they know.","Para":"Small group: prepare word lists using the Barakhadi chart (for example items found in a shop or in the kitchen). Individual: write short paragraphs using the words formed with the Barakhadi chart.","Story":"Small group: prepare word lists using the Barakhadi chart. Individual: write short paragraphs using the words formed with the Barakhadi chart."}},{"activity":"Self-writing: level tasks and review","source":"M","ref":"p.15","tasks":{"Beginner":"Draw a picture about the discussion and then write a few sentences about it, expressing thoughts freely. Review: say what they drew or wrote; read the text aloud once; the teacher may write the text in the notebook for them.","Letter":"Write about what they liked, using drawing and writing; write any words or sentences they can. Review: read the text aloud once; correct punctuation mistakes using the Barakhadi chart.","Word":"Write a sentence based on the conversation. Mistakes in spelling, punctuation and sentence structure are fine. Review: read it to the group; discuss and correct mistakes together.","Para":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation.","Story":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation."}}],"organisation":[{"grouping":"Whole class (big group)","how":"All learners of all levels sit in a 'U' shape arranged by level (Beginner, Letter, Word, Para, Story) so that the move to small groups is easy.","activities":["Warm-up: Alphabet song (last-letter word chain)","Oral conversation: conversation on a picture","Story (Day 2 of the story): retelling","Barakhadi chart: big group reading","Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on a picture of children at play"]},{"grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","how":"Learners of similar levels work together; the teacher gives each group a task for its level and spends more time with learners who need support. Rotate responsibilities (for example group leader).","activities":["Story: reading with actions and group questions","Barakhadi chart: small-group practice"]},{"grouping":"Individual","how":"Each learner works on a task for their own level; the teacher moves around, observes difficulties and supports individuals.","activities":["Story: writing answers individually","Barakhadi chart: individual tasks","Self-writing: individual writing","Self-writing: review and reading back","Daily reading (10 minutes)"]}],"materials":["Picture card of a family having dinner together","The same story book as yesterday","Story book","slate or paper for questions","Notebooks","Barakhadi chart","alphabet or phonics chart","Alphabet or phonics chart","board or floor","Picture card or topic on the board","crayons or pencils","Library books or storybooks"],"outcomes":["Learners take part in the oral conversation and speak without fear.","Learners retell the story, read with expression and ask or answer questions at their level.","Learners respond to the sound-symbol task for today (Barakhadi / alphabet and phonics chart (line 4, letter 'z')) at their own level.","Learners write about the topic at their level and read it aloud.","Each learner reads a book for 10 minutes."],"observation":["Observe each learner's reading and writing during the individual tasks; note who needs individual support and how many learners share the same difficulty.","Note any learner whose level is improving; move the learner to the next level group when you see steady progress (manual p.5).","Record each learner's progress for the day in the notebook, according to the learner's level (manual p.4).","Use today's observations to adjust tomorrow's plan (manual p.5)."],"teacherNotes":["Questions to elicit on Day 2: information questions (answer not in the text), thinking questions (needs knowledge beyond the text) and opinion questions (feedback on something in the text).","Barakhadi: learners who need extra time should get repeated practice using one or two sound units at a time. Topic-based discussion helps oral expression, thinking and understanding.","Writing has two parts, content and sequence: encourage learners to read what they wrote, improve it and rewrite it for clarity and correctness (manual p.15).","Pace: the manual says not to assume all learners progress at the same speed. Repeat a day's activity with the groups that need it before moving on.","Special needs: give extra time and prepare materials for slower learners; seat learners with hearing or vision difficulty at the front; for learners who reverse or confuse letters, trace letters on the letter card with a finger and write with dots to trace with a pencil (manual p.6)."],"components":[{"no":1,"key":"warmup","name":"Warm-up activities","keywords":["Alphabet song (last-letter word chain)","two learners lead"],"rows":[1]},{"no":2,"key":"oral","name":"Oral Discussion","keywords":["conversation on a picture","every learner speaks"],"rows":[2]},{"no":3,"key":"story","name":"Story","keywords":["Day 2","retell","read with actions","group questions","ask and answer","write answers (Para/Story)"],"rows":[3,4,5]},{"no":4,"key":"sound","name":"Sound symbol games, Sound separation-pairing","keywords":["Barakhadi / alphabet chart","listen and point (no repeating)","group reading","level tasks"],"rows":[6,7,8]},{"no":5,"key":"mindwrite","name":"Individual-Writing (Day 2)","keywords":["discussion","write at own level","self-review (read aloud)"],"rows":[9,10,11]},{"no":6,"key":"reading","name":"Daily reading","keywords":["library book","read alone","teacher listens"],"rows":[12]}],"preLesson":null},{"programme":"TARL Literacy","id":"lit-022","day":22,"phase":1,"phaseLabel":"Phase 1 (Days 1-45)","title":"Story: a story about a bird and its nest (Day 1)","dayType":"Story Day 1 + Mind mapping","focus":"Consonant clusters: dd (ladder, middle) | Mind map: forest","duration":70,"objectives":["Listen, speak and answer in the oral conversation (listening and storytelling).","Listen to and read a story with understanding; discuss it in big and small groups and respond at their own level.","Develop sound-symbol skills: Consonant clusters: dd (ladder, middle).","Build vocabulary through a mind map ('forest') and use the words at their own level.","Read independently for 10 minutes every day."],"sequence":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Handkerchief game","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Learners sit in a circle and clap while singing a rhyme ('I caught a Fish Alive'). One learner runs outside the circle with a handkerchief and secretly places it behind another learner, who must chase the runner. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Sit in a circle, clap and sing; run, place the handkerchief or chase as the game requires.","tlm":"A handkerchief","source":"M","ref":"p.8","n":1},{"activity":"Oral conversation: listening and storytelling","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Tell an interesting story starter and involve the learners: 'The moon came down to drink water from our well. What happened then?' Let learners imagine and continue the story.","learners":"Listen to the teacher, then imagine and continue the story. Learners can also recite a rhyme or story they know.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.9","n":2},{"activity":"Story (Day 1 of the story): reading aloud and discussion","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":8,"teacher":"Discuss the title or picture of the story with the learners. Read the story aloud with expression and voice modulation (learners do not repeat after you). Discuss it, with emphasis on opinion questions. Read it again slowly, pointing to each word.","learners":"Talk about the title/picture; listen; answer questions; follow each word with a finger in their own copy.","tlm":"A story from the school library (a story about a bird and its nest), a copy for each learner","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":3},{"activity":"Story: reading in small groups","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":7,"teacher":"Form level-wise groups with a group leader. Learners read the story one sentence at a time while the others follow with their fingers. Para and Story level learners practise reading with emotion and expression.","learners":"Read the story sentence by sentence, supporting each other; the group leader helps.","tlm":"Story book copies","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":4},{"activity":"Story: level-wise individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":5,"teacher":"Give each learner the task for their level (see level table) and support those who need it.","learners":"Beginner/Letter: find and write favourite words or letters. Word: find consonant clusters. Para/Story: silently read, find unfamiliar and rhyming words.","tlm":"Story book, notebooks, board","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":5},{"activity":"Consonant clusters: introduction","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":4,"teacher":"Same-letter clusters: familiarise learners with clusters made of the same letter ('dd' as in ladder, middle, sudden). Ask them to pronounce them and find such words in the text and write them down.","learners":"Listen, pronounce the cluster and say words that contain it.","tlm":"Board and chalk, words list (ladder middle sudden puddle paddy)","source":"M","ref":"p.16","n":6},{"activity":"Consonant cluster game: Who is Whose Friend?","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":6,"teacher":"Prepare cards: some with broken parts of conjunct consonants (b + l, c + r, s + t) and some with the full form (bl as in black, cr as in crab, st as in star). Take out all the cards. Observe closely and help learners who need support.","learners":"Match each full form with its broken parts and discover 'who is whose friend'.","tlm":"Broken-part cards and full-form cards","source":"M","ref":"p.17","n":7},{"activity":"Mind mapping (Day 1): the word 'forest'","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Ask: 'What words come to your mind when you hear the word forest?' Write learners' answers on the board or floor (Para and Story level learners write the words themselves). Guide the map towards the learning objective. Example words: teak, bamboo, banyan, mango, deer, bear, snake, owl, leaf, branch, nest, fruit.","learners":"Say words connected with 'forest'; share the meaning and feeling of words.","tlm":"Board, chalk (or floor)","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":8},{"activity":"Mind mapping: classify the words","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":4,"teacher":"Ask learners to classify the words in groups, for example: Trees: teak, bamboo, banyan, mango; Animals: deer, bear, snake, owl; Things: leaf, branch, nest, fruit.","learners":"Sort the words into groups and say why.","tlm":"Board, chalk, word cards (optional)","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":9},{"activity":"Mind mapping: level-wise individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":6,"teacher":"Give each learner the individual task for their level; observe closely and give individual support. Display corrected stories on the wall.","learners":"Complete the task for their level (see level table).","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":10},{"activity":"Daily reading (10 minutes)","grouping":"Individual","minutes":10,"teacher":"Give each learner a library book or any storybook. Move around, listen to individual readers and note their level.","learners":"Read independently a book of their choice.","tlm":"Library books or storybooks","source":"M","ref":"p.7","n":11}],"procedures":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Handkerchief game","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","steps":[{"teacher":"Seat the learners in a circle and start clapping and singing the rhyme 'I caught a Fish Alive'.","learners":"Clap and sing together."},{"teacher":"One learner runs outside the circle holding a handkerchief and secretly places it behind another learner.","learners":"Everyone keeps clapping; the learner who finds the handkerchief behind them takes it and chases the runner."},{"teacher":"If the runner sits in the chaser's place before being caught, they stay in the game; if caught, they are out. Continue in this way.","learners":"Play fairly and take turns."}]},{"activity":"Oral conversation: listening and storytelling","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.9","steps":[{"teacher":"Say the starter: 'The moon came down to drink water from our well. What happened then?'","learners":"Listen and imagine."},{"teacher":"Ask learners to continue the story one by one. Encourage those who speak less.","learners":"Add ideas to the story."},{"teacher":"Invite a learner to recite a poem or rhyme they know.","learners":"Recite and listen to others."}]},{"activity":"Story - Day 1 (a story about a bird and its nest)","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.10","steps":[{"teacher":"Discuss the title or picture of the story with the learners.","learners":"Talk about what they see and what the story may be about."},{"teacher":"Read the story aloud with expression and proper voice modulation. Learners should not simply repeat after you.","learners":"Listen carefully and enjoy the story."},{"teacher":"Discuss the story: factual, logical, vocabulary-based, judgment or opinion questions (today's focus: opinion: What did you like best? What would you have done in the story?). Begin in the home language if needed.","learners":"Think and respond thoughtfully; every learner takes part."},{"teacher":"Read the story again slowly, pointing to each word. Make sure each learner has a copy and follows with a finger.","learners":"Follow each word with their finger."},{"teacher":"Ask learners to read in small groups; select a group leader who helps the others. Learners read one sentence at a time while the others point with fingers.","learners":"Read with the help of one another."}]},{"activity":"Consonant clusters (dd) and the game 'Who is Whose Friend?'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.16-17","steps":[{"teacher":"Same-letter clusters: familiarise learners with clusters made of the same letter ('dd' as in ladder, middle, sudden). Ask them to pronounce them and find such words in the text and write them down.","learners":"Listen, pronounce and find words in the text."},{"teacher":"Write the words on the board: ladder middle sudden puddle paddy. Read them aloud with distinct pronunciation of the cluster.","learners":"Read the words aloud; point to the cluster in each word."},{"teacher":"Prepare cards: some with broken parts of conjunct consonants (b + l, c + r, s + t) and some with the full form (bl as in black, cr as in crab, st as in star). Take out all the cards.","learners":"Match each full form with its broken parts and discover 'who is whose friend'."}]},{"activity":"Mind mapping: 'forest'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Small group (level-wise) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.14","steps":[{"teacher":"Choose a word that can generate many related words: 'forest'. Ask: 'What words come to your mind when you hear the word forest?' Write the answers on the board or floor.","learners":"Say words they link with 'forest'."},{"teacher":"Discuss the words: what they mean and how they are connected.","learners":"Explain their words and listen to others."},{"teacher":"In small groups, let the learners classify the words (Trees: teak, bamboo, banyan, mango; Animals: deer, bear, snake, owl; Things: leaf, branch, nest, fruit).","learners":"Sort the words into groups."},{"teacher":"Give the individual tasks by level and help each learner.","learners":"Work individually; read the work aloud at the end if time allows."}]}],"levelTasks":[{"activity":"Story - Day 1: individual tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.10","tasks":{"Beginner":"Circle or search for a favourite word or letter in the story and say it aloud. If a learner cannot draw a circle, write words on the board and ask them to identify them.","Letter":"Find, read and write favourite words from the story.","Word":"Find the consonant clusters in the story, read them and write them in the notebook.","Para":"Silently read the story from the textbook; find unfamiliar words and try to understand them; find rhyming words, use them in sentences and write in the notebook; ask other groups for meanings; make questions in groups.","Story":"Silently read the story; find unfamiliar words and rhyming words; practise reading with emotion; one group reads sentences formed with consonant clusters to the other group; ask and answer group questions (information, thinking and opinion questions)."}},{"activity":"Consonant clusters (dd): level tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.16-17","tasks":{"Beginner":"Listen to the sound of the cluster and point to it in a word; continue with letter-sound work (interpretation: the manual describes clusters for learners lagging in reading words and sentences).","Letter":"Listen to the cluster sound and pick words with the cluster from a word card (interpretation).","Word":"Find the cluster in the story or textbook words, read the words and write them in the notebook.","Para":"Form words and sentences using the cluster; read the sentences aloud.","Story":"Form words and sentences using the cluster; read the sentences aloud; use them in the story writing."}},{"activity":"Mind mapping 'forest': level tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.14","tasks":{"Beginner":"Circle all the words that contain the letter 'A' on the board; make a list. See how many learners find the most words.","Letter":"Circle all the words that contain the letter 'A' and make a list of them.","Word":"Use 4-5 words (for example owl, bear, deer, leaf, nest) to form sentences, starting with words of one or two syllables. Example: Dream - I had a dream last night.","Para":"Choose any five words from the map and create a story with them. Use consonant clusters correctly, read the story aloud, correct mistakes of sentence structure, spelling or grammar, then display it on the wall.","Story":"Choose any five words from the map and create a story with them. Use consonant clusters correctly, read the story aloud, correct mistakes of sentence structure, spelling or grammar, then display it on the wall."}}],"organisation":[{"grouping":"Whole class (big group)","how":"All learners of all levels sit in a 'U' shape arranged by level (Beginner, Letter, Word, Para, Story) so that the move to small groups is easy.","activities":["Warm-up: Handkerchief game","Oral conversation: listening and storytelling","Story (Day 1 of the story): reading aloud and discussion","Consonant clusters: introduction","Mind mapping (Day 1): the word 'forest'"]},{"grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","how":"Learners of similar levels work together; the teacher gives each group a task for its level and spends more time with learners who need support. Rotate responsibilities (for example group leader).","activities":["Story: reading in small groups","Consonant cluster game: Who is Whose Friend?","Mind mapping: classify the words"]},{"grouping":"Individual","how":"Each learner works on a task for their own level; the teacher moves around, observes difficulties and supports individuals.","activities":["Story: level-wise individual tasks","Mind mapping: level-wise individual tasks","Daily reading (10 minutes)"]}],"materials":["A handkerchief","A story from the school library (a story about a bird","its nest)","a copy for each learner","Story book copies","Story book","notebooks","board","Board","chalk","words list (ladder middle sudden puddle paddy)","Broken-part cards","full-form cards","chalk (or floor)","word cards (optional)","Notebooks","Library books or storybooks"],"outcomes":["Learners take part in the oral conversation and speak without fear.","Learners show understanding of the story in the discussion and complete the task for their level.","Learners respond to the sound-symbol task for today (Consonant clusters: dd (ladder, middle)) at their own level.","Learners add words to the mind map and use them in sentences or a story at their level.","Each learner reads a book for 10 minutes."],"observation":["Observe each learner's reading and writing during the individual tasks; note who needs individual support and how many learners share the same difficulty.","Note any learner whose level is improving; move the learner to the next level group when you see steady progress (manual p.5).","Record each learner's progress for the day in the notebook, according to the learner's level (manual p.4).","Use today's observations to adjust tomorrow's plan (manual p.5)."],"teacherNotes":["Story selection: the manual asks teachers to use picture story books or stories in the school library. Today's suggested theme (a story about a bird and its nest) is a planning suggestion; use any suitable story you have.","Consonant clusters: do these activities daily for learners who find reading complex words hard; the aim is to remove the fear of reading clusters. Teachers may carry out similar activities on their own.","Mind mapping topic for this day: 'forest'. The manual's example uses the word 'shop'; today's topic follows the same method.","Pace: the manual says not to assume all learners progress at the same speed. Repeat a day's activity with the groups that need it before moving on.","Special needs: give extra time and prepare materials for slower learners; seat learners with hearing or vision difficulty at the front; for learners who reverse or confuse letters, trace letters on the letter card with a finger and write with dots to trace with a pencil (manual p.6)."],"components":[{"no":1,"key":"warmup","name":"Warm-up activities","keywords":["Handkerchief game","two learners lead"],"rows":[1]},{"no":2,"key":"oral","name":"Oral Discussion","keywords":["listening and storytelling","every learner speaks"],"rows":[2]},{"no":3,"key":"story","name":"Story","keywords":["Day 1","title / picture talk","read aloud with expression","opinion questions","re-read pointing","group reading","level tasks"],"rows":[3,4,5]},{"no":4,"key":"sound","name":"Sound symbol games, Sound separation-pairing","keywords":["consonant cluster 'dd'","pronounce and find words","game: Who is Whose Friend?"],"rows":[6,7]},{"no":5,"key":"mindwrite","name":"Mind Mapping (Day 1)","keywords":["mind map: forest","classify the words","level task: circle letter A / sentences / story"],"rows":[8,9,10]},{"no":6,"key":"reading","name":"Daily reading","keywords":["library book","read alone","teacher listens"],"rows":[11]}],"preLesson":null},{"programme":"TARL Literacy","id":"lit-023","day":23,"phase":1,"phaseLabel":"Phase 1 (Days 1-45)","title":"Story: a story about a bird and its nest (Day 2)","dayType":"Story Day 2 + Self-writing","focus":"Identifying the first, second and last sound (dog, sun, pig) | Self-writing: what I want to be","duration":70,"objectives":["Listen, speak and answer in the oral conversation (What did you see on your way?).","Retell the story, read it with expression, ask and answer questions about it and write answers.","Develop sound-symbol skills: Identifying the first, second and last sound (dog, sun, pig).","Write about a topic at their own level and review the writing (what I want to be).","Read independently for 10 minutes every day."],"sequence":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Rhyme - 'I saw a Little Bird'","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Say the rhyme with actions, then say it together. Lines: I saw a little bird go hop, hop, hop / I told the little bird to stop, stop, stop. / I went to the window to say 'How do you do?' / He wagged his little tail and far away he flew! Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Listen, then say the rhyme with actions.","tlm":"Rhyme chart or board (optional)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","n":1},{"activity":"Oral conversation: What did you see on your way?","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Ask learners to describe what they saw on their way to school. If they are hesitant, begin yourself: 'I saw the river shining, a boat leaving the bank and two birds on a bamboo pole. What did you see on your way?'","learners":"Describe what they saw on the way to school and connect with what others share.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.9","n":2},{"activity":"Story (Day 2 of the story): retelling","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":6,"teacher":"Ask learners to retell yesterday's story in their own words. Prompt with questions on the beginning, middle and end.","learners":"Retell the story using their own words.","tlm":"The same story book as yesterday","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":3},{"activity":"Story: reading with actions and group questions","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":9,"teacher":"Learners practise reading with actions and expressions; one learner per group reads aloud to the class. Guide groups to make questions about the story (guide initially). Groups take turns to ask and answer each other's questions. Word-level learners also read aloud the consonants learned on the first day.","learners":"Read with actions; make questions (word-level learners help write them); ask and answer questions with another group.","tlm":"Story book, slate or paper for questions","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":4},{"activity":"Story: writing answers individually","grouping":"Individual","minutes":5,"teacher":"Para and Story level learners write answers to all questions individually; read and correct their responses after they finish.","learners":"Write the answers in their notebooks; Beginner/Letter/Word learners read or listen and answer orally.","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":5},{"activity":"Sound-symbol activity: oral sound awareness","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":4,"teacher":"Say words and ask learners to identify the first, second or last sound. Example: pan - first sound p, second sound a, third sound n; log: l, o, g; cup: c, u, p.","learners":"Say the first, second or last sound of the word.","tlm":"None (oral activity)","source":"M","ref":"p.12","n":6},{"activity":"Sound-symbol games by level","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":6,"teacher":"Give each level group its game (see level table). Move among the groups and help those who need support; say each word clearly.","learners":"Play the game for their level in small groups.","tlm":"Board, chalk, letter cards","source":"M","ref":"p.12","n":7},{"activity":"Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on what I want to be","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Start a conversation about a picture card: 'what I want to be'. Involve all learners and ask open-ended questions.","learners":"Take part in the discussion and share thoughts freely.","tlm":"Picture card or topic on the board","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":8},{"activity":"Self-writing: individual writing","grouping":"Individual","minutes":7,"teacher":"Give each level its task (see level table). Let learners take ownership of what they draw and write; mistakes are fine.","learners":"Draw and write about the topic at their level.","tlm":"Notebooks, crayons or pencils","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":9},{"activity":"Self-writing: review and reading back","grouping":"Individual","minutes":3,"teacher":"Ask each learner 'What did you draw or write?' and have them read it aloud once. Word-level learners read to the group; discuss spelling, punctuation and sentence structure. Help beginners by writing their text in the notebook for them if needed.","learners":"Read what they wrote; correct mistakes after listening to their own reading.","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":10},{"activity":"Daily reading (10 minutes)","grouping":"Individual","minutes":10,"teacher":"Give each learner a library book or any storybook. Move around, listen to individual readers and note their level.","learners":"Read independently a book of their choice.","tlm":"Library books or storybooks","source":"M","ref":"p.7","n":11}],"procedures":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Rhyme - 'I saw a Little Bird'","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","steps":[{"teacher":"Say the rhyme 'I saw a Little Bird' slowly with actions: I saw a little bird go hop, hop, hop / I told the little bird to stop, stop, stop. / I went to the window to say 'How do you do?' / He wagged his little tail and far away he flew!","learners":"Listen and watch the actions."},{"teacher":"Say it again; invite learners to join with actions.","learners":"Say the rhyme together with actions."},{"teacher":"Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Choose a rhyme they like and lead."}]},{"activity":"Oral conversation: What did you see on your way?","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.9","steps":[{"teacher":"Ask: 'What did you see on your way to school today?'","learners":"Think about the way to school."},{"teacher":"If learners hesitate, start: 'I saw the river shining, a boat leaving the bank and two birds on a bamboo pole. What did you see on your way?'","learners":"Listen to the model and then share their own observations."},{"teacher":"Connect learners' answers with each other.","learners":"Listen and add what they noticed."}]},{"activity":"Story - Day 2 (a story about a bird and its nest)","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.11","steps":[{"teacher":"Ask learners to retell the story they read yesterday in their own words.","learners":"Retell, helping each other remember."},{"teacher":"In small groups learners practise reading the story using actions and expressions; one learner from each group then reads aloud to the class.","learners":"Read with actions and expression; a representative reads aloud."},{"teacher":"Guide the groups to come up with questions about the story (guide initially). Word-level learners can support by helping write them down.","learners":"Make questions together."},{"teacher":"Groups take turns to ask and answer each other's questions. Useful kinds: questions whose answer is not in the text; questions needing thinking beyond the text; questions asking for an opinion.","learners":"Ask, answer and discuss in the groups."},{"teacher":"Word-level learners also read aloud the consonants they learned on the first day.","learners":"Read the consonant clusters aloud."}]},{"activity":"Sound-symbol: oral and level games","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.12","steps":[{"teacher":"Say words and ask learners to identify the first, second or last sound. Example: pan - first sound p, second sound a, third sound n; log: l, o, g; cup: c, u, p.","learners":"Say the first, second or last sound of the word."},{"teacher":"Write the sounds or words for the day on the board and give each level group its task (see the level table).","learners":"Work in small groups and share their answers."},{"teacher":"Say each word clearly with distinct pronunciation. Give learners enough time to respond and think; use words learners commonly use at home (regional language and the medium of instruction).","learners":"Think, say and write the sounds."}]},{"activity":"Self-writing: 'Discussion, Writing, Self-review'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.15","steps":[{"teacher":"Start a conversation about a picture card: 'what I want to be'. Involve all learners and ask open-ended questions.","learners":"Discuss and answer questions."},{"teacher":"Give writing time at each level: draw then write (Beginner), write about what they liked (Letter), a sentence (Word), a paragraph or story on a topic of their choice (Para/Story).","learners":"Write at their level and take ownership of the work."},{"teacher":"Review: ask 'What did you draw or write?' Have each learner read the text aloud once. Support with writing if needed.","learners":"Read aloud, listen to their pronunciation and correct mistakes."}]}],"levelTasks":[{"activity":"Story - Day 2: level-wise tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.11","tasks":{"Beginner":"Retell with the group by pointing to pictures or words; read aloud with group support (interpretation of the manual's group reading task).","Letter":"Read with the group, pointing to words; say the letters and words they know (interpretation of the manual's group reading task).","Word":"Support the group in writing the questions; read aloud the consonant clusters learned on the first day.","Para":"Ask the group's questions to another group, discuss them, then write answers to all questions individually; the teacher reads and corrects.","Story":"Ask the group's questions to another group, discuss them, then write answers to all questions individually; the teacher reads and corrects."}},{"activity":"Sound-symbol games by level (small groups)","source":"M","ref":"p.12","tasks":{"Beginner":"'What is the first sound in the word egg?' 'Is there a letter that makes the sound /e/?' 'Can you name objects that start with the letter E?' Learners think and share names in the group.","Letter":"Write the rhyming ending -ap on the board and ask learners to add new letters to form words: c + ap = cap, m + ap = map, t + ap = tap.","Word":"Say a word and tell its sounds, for example 'sun' = /s/ + /u/ + /n/. Then tell what word is formed if /r/ is put before 'at': r + at = rat. Do 8-10 such combinations; at first learners may form meaningless words, later only meaningful words.","Para":"Write two or three sounds on the board (for example Br, cl, st) and let the learners form words that start with those sounds; this builds a word list for the learner.","Story":"Write two or three sounds on the board (for example Br, cl, st) and let the learners form words that start with those sounds; this builds a word list for the learner."}},{"activity":"Self-writing: level tasks and review","source":"M","ref":"p.15","tasks":{"Beginner":"Draw a picture about the discussion and then write a few sentences about it, expressing thoughts freely. Review: say what they drew or wrote; read the text aloud once; the teacher may write the text in the notebook for them.","Letter":"Write about what they liked, using drawing and writing; write any words or sentences they can. Review: read the text aloud once; correct punctuation mistakes using the Barakhadi chart.","Word":"Write a sentence based on the conversation. Mistakes in spelling, punctuation and sentence structure are fine. Review: read it to the group; discuss and correct mistakes together.","Para":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation.","Story":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation."}}],"organisation":[{"grouping":"Whole class (big group)","how":"All learners of all levels sit in a 'U' shape arranged by level (Beginner, Letter, Word, Para, Story) so that the move to small groups is easy.","activities":["Warm-up: Rhyme - 'I saw a Little Bird'","Oral conversation: What did you see on your way?","Story (Day 2 of the story): retelling","Sound-symbol activity: oral sound awareness","Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on what I want to be"]},{"grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","how":"Learners of similar levels work together; the teacher gives each group a task for its level and spends more time with learners who need support. Rotate responsibilities (for example group leader).","activities":["Story: reading with actions and group questions","Sound-symbol games by level"]},{"grouping":"Individual","how":"Each learner works on a task for their own level; the teacher moves around, observes difficulties and supports individuals.","activities":["Story: writing answers individually","Self-writing: individual writing","Self-writing: review and reading back","Daily reading (10 minutes)"]}],"materials":["Rhyme chart or board (optional)","The same story book as yesterday","Story book","slate or paper for questions","Notebooks","Board","chalk","letter cards","Picture card or topic on the board","crayons or pencils","Library books or storybooks"],"outcomes":["Learners take part in the oral conversation and speak without fear.","Learners retell the story, read with expression and ask or answer questions at their level.","Learners respond to the sound-symbol task for today (Identifying the first, second and last sound (dog, sun, pig)) at their own level.","Learners write about the topic at their level and read it aloud.","Each learner reads a book for 10 minutes."],"observation":["Observe each learner's reading and writing during the individual tasks; note who needs individual support and how many learners share the same difficulty.","Note any learner whose level is improving; move the learner to the next level group when you see steady progress (manual p.5).","Record each learner's progress for the day in the notebook, according to the learner's level (manual p.4).","Use today's observations to adjust tomorrow's plan (manual p.5)."],"teacherNotes":["Questions to elicit on Day 2: information questions (answer not in the text), thinking questions (needs knowledge beyond the text) and opinion questions (feedback on something in the text).","Sound-symbol: for the first 4-5 days, play sound-based games with the learners at word level. Include the sounds learners find difficult when you prepare the Class Transaction Plan.","Writing has two parts, content and sequence: encourage learners to read what they wrote, improve it and rewrite it for clarity and correctness (manual p.15).","Pace: the manual says not to assume all learners progress at the same speed. Repeat a day's activity with the groups that need it before moving on.","Special needs: give extra time and prepare materials for slower learners; seat learners with hearing or vision difficulty at the front; for learners who reverse or confuse letters, trace letters on the letter card with a finger and write with dots to trace with a pencil (manual p.6)."],"components":[{"no":1,"key":"warmup","name":"Warm-up activities","keywords":["Rhyme - 'I saw a Little Bird'","two learners lead"],"rows":[1]},{"no":2,"key":"oral","name":"Oral Discussion","keywords":["What did you see on your way?","every learner speaks"],"rows":[2]},{"no":3,"key":"story","name":"Story","keywords":["Day 2","retell","read with actions","group questions","ask and answer","write answers (Para/Story)"],"rows":[3,4,5]},{"no":4,"key":"sound","name":"Sound symbol games, Sound separation-pairing","keywords":["oral sound awareness","first / second / last sound","level games in small groups"],"rows":[6,7]},{"no":5,"key":"mindwrite","name":"Individual-Writing (Day 2)","keywords":["discussion","write at own level","self-review (read aloud)"],"rows":[8,9,10]},{"no":6,"key":"reading","name":"Daily reading","keywords":["library book","read alone","teacher listens"],"rows":[11]}],"preLesson":null},{"programme":"TARL Literacy","id":"lit-024","day":24,"phase":1,"phaseLabel":"Phase 1 (Days 1-45)","title":"Saturday: drama presentation","dayType":"Saturday drama + Self-writing","focus":"Language game: Singing and Spinning | Self-writing: the story we acted out (a story about a bird and its nest)","duration":70,"objectives":["Listen, speak and answer in the oral conversation (familiar topic).","Express a story through role play, using voice, facial expressions and gestures.","Develop sound-symbol skills: Language game: Singing and Spinning.","Write about the story and review the writing.","Read independently for 10 minutes every day."],"sequence":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Singing and Spinning","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Learners sit in a circle and pass a small object while you clap with your back turned; when the clapping stops, the learner holding it sings a song, recites a poem or tells a joke. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Pass the object round the circle; sing, recite or tell a joke when the clapping stops.","tlm":"A small object (chalk or pencil)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","n":1},{"activity":"Oral conversation: familiar topic","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Hold a conversation on the topic 'what I want to be when I grow up'. Give each learner a chance to speak; be patient with learners who need extra time.","learners":"Talk about the topic and listen to others.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.9","n":2},{"activity":"Dramatic presentation: introduction and reading","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Explain what a dramatic presentation is and how it is done. Provide stories discussed during the week and read one aloud once more. Para and Story level learners support Beginner and Letter level learners in reading.","learners":"Listen, read along, then each learner chooses a character.","tlm":"Stories discussed in the week (a story about sharing food; a story about a bird and its nest)","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":3},{"activity":"Dramatic presentation: planning in small groups","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":8,"teacher":"Each group discusses and plans dialogues; Para or Story level learners write the dialogues. Groups prepare their dramatic presentation.","learners":"Choose characters, plan and rehearse dialogues with facial expressions and gestures.","tlm":"Story, paper for dialogues","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":4},{"activity":"Dramatic presentation: performances and feedback","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":7,"teacher":"Learners sit in a U shape. Each group presents; after each performance, watching learners say what they enjoyed and what could be improved.","learners":"Perform in turn; watch; give feedback.","tlm":"Open space (U-shape seating)","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":5},{"activity":"Language game: Singing and Spinning","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Learners sit in a circle; a small object (chalk, pencil) is passed around while the teacher, back turned, claps steadily. Observe each learner and give help where needed.","learners":"Play the game, take turns and read or say the words they make.","tlm":"A small object (chalk or pencil)","source":"M","ref":"p.18","n":6},{"activity":"Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on the story we acted out (a story about a bird and its nest)","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Start a conversation about the story used for the drama: 'the story we acted out (a story about a bird and its nest)'. Involve all learners with open-ended questions.","learners":"Take part in the discussion and share thoughts freely.","tlm":"Picture card or topic on the board","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":7},{"activity":"Self-writing: individual writing","grouping":"Individual","minutes":7,"teacher":"Give each level its task (see level table). Let learners take ownership of what they draw and write; mistakes are fine.","learners":"Draw and write about the topic at their level.","tlm":"Notebooks, crayons or pencils","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":8},{"activity":"Self-writing: review and reading back","grouping":"Individual","minutes":3,"teacher":"Ask each learner 'What did you draw or write?' and have them read it aloud once. Word-level learners read to the group; discuss spelling, punctuation and sentence structure. Help beginners by writing their text in the notebook for them if needed.","learners":"Read what they wrote; correct mistakes after listening to their own reading.","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":9},{"activity":"Daily reading (10 minutes)","grouping":"Individual","minutes":10,"teacher":"Give each learner a library book or any storybook. Move around, listen to individual readers and note their level.","learners":"Read independently a book of their choice.","tlm":"Library books or storybooks","source":"M","ref":"p.7","n":10}],"procedures":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Singing and Spinning","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","steps":[{"teacher":"Seat the learners in a circle; give a small object to one learner.","learners":"Sit in a circle."},{"teacher":"Stand outside the circle with your back to them and clap steadily; they pass the object.","learners":"Pass the object while the clapping continues."},{"teacher":"Stop clapping; the learner holding the object sings, recites or tells a joke.","learners":"Perform, and everybody claps."}]},{"activity":"Oral conversation: familiar topic","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.9","steps":[{"teacher":"Introduce the topic: 'what I want to be when I grow up'.","learners":"Think about their own experience."},{"teacher":"Ask open questions; give every learner a chance. Involve learners who speak less.","learners":"Speak freely and without fear."},{"teacher":"Praise efforts and sum up.","learners":"Listen and respect each other's ideas."}]},{"activity":"Saturday special: dramatic presentation","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.11","steps":[{"teacher":"Explain what a dramatic presentation is and how it can be done. Give the groups the stories discussed during the week.","learners":"Listen to the explanation."},{"teacher":"Read a story aloud once more. Learners at story and paragraph level support those at beginner and letter level in reading.","learners":"Read along; helpers support their friends."},{"teacher":"After reading, each learner chooses a character from the story.","learners":"Choose a role (boys may play girl roles and girls may play boy roles)."},{"teacher":"In groups, learners discuss and plan the dialogues; paragraph or story level learners write the dialogues.","learners":"Plan and write dialogues together."},{"teacher":"Learners sit in a U shape. Each group presents its drama. After each performance, ask what the audience enjoyed and what could be improved.","learners":"Perform, watch and give kind feedback."}]},{"activity":"Language game: Singing and Spinning","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.18","steps":[{"teacher":"Seat the learners in a circle. Give one learner a small object such as a piece of chalk.","learners":"Sit in a circle and listen for the clapping."},{"teacher":"Stand outside the circle with your back to the learners and clap steadily. Stop clapping without warning.","learners":"Pass the object round while the clapping continues."},{"teacher":"Ask the learner holding the object when you stop to sing a song, recite a poem or tell a joke.","learners":"Sing, recite or tell a joke; the others listen and clap."}]},{"activity":"Self-writing: 'Discussion, Writing, Self-review'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.15","steps":[{"teacher":"Start a conversation about the story used for the drama: 'the story we acted out (a story about a bird and its nest)'. Involve all learners with open-ended questions.","learners":"Discuss and answer questions."},{"teacher":"Give writing time at each level: draw then write (Beginner), write about what they liked (Letter), a sentence (Word), a paragraph or story on a topic of their choice (Para/Story).","learners":"Write at their level and take ownership of the work."},{"teacher":"Review: ask 'What did you draw or write?' Have each learner read the text aloud once. Support with writing if needed.","learners":"Read aloud, listen to their pronunciation and correct mistakes."}]}],"levelTasks":[{"activity":"Drama: roles by level","source":"M","ref":"p.11","tasks":{"Beginner":"Take a character role and say or act short lines with help from Para and Story level learners.","Letter":"Take a character role and say or act short lines with help from Para and Story level learners.","Word":"Take a role and speak the dialogues; help rehearse.","Para":"Write the dialogues for the group and support Beginner, Letter and Word level learners throughout.","Story":"Write the dialogues for the group and support Beginner, Letter and Word level learners throughout."}},{"activity":"Language game: Singing and Spinning - level support","source":"I","ref":"p.18","tasks":{"Beginner":"Take part by saying or pointing to the letters involved and by listening carefully; Para and Story level partners help.","Letter":"Say the letters/sounds and give simple words they know.","Word":"Say and write words and short sentences for the game.","Para":"Write sentences with the words; help groups to record answers.","Story":"Write sentences or short stories with the words; help groups to record answers."}},{"activity":"Self-writing: level tasks and review","source":"M","ref":"p.15","tasks":{"Beginner":"Draw a picture about the discussion and then write a few sentences about it, expressing thoughts freely. Review: say what they drew or wrote; read the text aloud once; the teacher may write the text in the notebook for them.","Letter":"Write about what they liked, using drawing and writing; write any words or sentences they can. Review: read the text aloud once; correct punctuation mistakes using the Barakhadi chart.","Word":"Write a sentence based on the conversation. Mistakes in spelling, punctuation and sentence structure are fine. Review: read it to the group; discuss and correct mistakes together.","Para":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation.","Story":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation."}}],"organisation":[{"grouping":"Whole class (big group)","how":"All learners of all levels sit in a 'U' shape arranged by level (Beginner, Letter, Word, Para, Story) so that the move to small groups is easy.","activities":["Warm-up: Singing and Spinning","Oral conversation: familiar topic","Dramatic presentation: introduction and reading","Dramatic presentation: performances and feedback","Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on the story we acted out (a story about a bird and its nest)"]},{"grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","how":"Learners of similar levels work together; the teacher gives each group a task for its level and spends more time with learners who need support. Rotate responsibilities (for example group leader).","activities":["Dramatic presentation: planning in small groups","Language game: Singing and Spinning"]},{"grouping":"Individual","how":"Each learner works on a task for their own level; the teacher moves around, observes difficulties and supports individuals.","activities":["Self-writing: individual writing","Self-writing: review and reading back","Daily reading (10 minutes)"]}],"materials":["A small object (chalk or pencil)","Stories discussed in the week (a story about sharing food; a story about a bird","its nest)","Story","paper for dialogues","Open space (U-shape seating)","Picture card or topic on the board","Notebooks","crayons or pencils","Library books or storybooks"],"outcomes":["Learners take part in the oral conversation and speak without fear.","Learners present a role in the group drama and give feedback to others.","Learners respond to the sound-symbol task for today (Language game: Singing and Spinning) at their own level.","Learners write about the story at their level and read it aloud.","Each learner reads a book for 10 minutes."],"observation":["Observe each learner's reading and writing during the individual tasks; note who needs individual support and how many learners share the same difficulty.","Note any learner whose level is improving; move the learner to the next level group when you see steady progress (manual p.5).","Record each learner's progress for the day in the notebook, according to the learner's level (manual p.4).","Use today's observations to adjust tomorrow's plan (manual p.5)."],"teacherNotes":["Saturday: this plan assumes Day 1 is a Monday (six teaching days per week). If your school week is different, hold the drama presentation on your Saturday and keep the other days in sequence.","The manual lists the letter and word games but does not fix the slot in the daily timetable where they are used. This plan places them in the 10-minute sound-symbol / alphabet slot (interpretation).","Writing has two parts, content and sequence: encourage learners to read what they wrote, improve it and rewrite it for clarity and correctness (manual p.15).","Pace: the manual says not to assume all learners progress at the same speed. Repeat a day's activity with the groups that need it before moving on.","Special needs: give extra time and prepare materials for slower learners; seat learners with hearing or vision difficulty at the front; for learners who reverse or confuse letters, trace letters on the letter card with a finger and write with dots to trace with a pencil (manual p.6)."],"components":[{"no":1,"key":"warmup","name":"Warm-up activities","keywords":["Singing and Spinning","two learners lead"],"rows":[1]},{"no":2,"key":"oral","name":"Oral Discussion","keywords":["familiar topic","every learner speaks"],"rows":[2]},{"no":3,"key":"story","name":"Story (Saturday: dramatic presentation)","keywords":["Saturday drama","choose a character","plan dialogues","perform in U shape","feedback"],"rows":[3,4,5]},{"no":4,"key":"sound","name":"Sound symbol games, Sound separation-pairing","keywords":["Singing and Spinning","play in turns","level support"],"rows":[6]},{"no":5,"key":"mindwrite","name":"Individual-Writing (Day 2)","keywords":["discussion","write at own level","self-review (read aloud)"],"rows":[7,8,9]},{"no":6,"key":"reading","name":"Daily reading","keywords":["library book","read alone","teacher listens"],"rows":[10]}],"preLesson":null},{"programme":"TARL Literacy","id":"lit-025","day":25,"phase":1,"phaseLabel":"Phase 1 (Days 1-45)","title":"Story: a story about the rain and the seasons (Day 1)","dayType":"Story Day 1 + Mind mapping","focus":"Consonant clusters: gg (egg, bigger) | Mind map: village","duration":70,"objectives":["Listen, speak and answer in the oral conversation (conversation on a picture).","Listen to and read a story with understanding; discuss it in big and small groups and respond at their own level.","Develop sound-symbol skills: Consonant clusters: gg (egg, bigger).","Build vocabulary through a mind map ('village') and use the words at their own level.","Read independently for 10 minutes every day."],"sequence":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Rain clapping","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Everyone stands in a circle with eyes closed and keeps clapping: first one finger, then two, three, four and finally five fingers. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Stand in a circle, close the eyes and clap with 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 fingers.","tlm":"After the activity ask: Which finger sound was your favourite?","source":"M","ref":"p.8","n":1},{"activity":"Oral conversation: conversation on a picture","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Show a picture of a railway station with a waiting train and ask what is happening, who is doing what and what is happening around them. Let learners think creatively and even make up a story.","learners":"Look at the picture, answer questions and make up their own story about it.","tlm":"Picture card of a railway station with a waiting train","source":"M","ref":"p.9","n":2},{"activity":"Story (Day 1 of the story): reading aloud and discussion","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":8,"teacher":"Discuss the title or picture of the story with the learners. Read the story aloud with expression and voice modulation (learners do not repeat after you). Discuss it, with emphasis on factual questions. Read it again slowly, pointing to each word.","learners":"Talk about the title/picture; listen; answer questions; follow each word with a finger in their own copy.","tlm":"A story from the school library (a story about the rain and the seasons), a copy for each learner","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":3},{"activity":"Story: reading in small groups","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":7,"teacher":"Form level-wise groups with a group leader. Learners read the story one sentence at a time while the others follow with their fingers. Para and Story level learners practise reading with emotion and expression.","learners":"Read the story sentence by sentence, supporting each other; the group leader helps.","tlm":"Story book copies","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":4},{"activity":"Story: level-wise individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":5,"teacher":"Give each learner the task for their level (see level table) and support those who need it.","learners":"Beginner/Letter: find and write favourite words or letters. Word: find consonant clusters. Para/Story: silently read, find unfamiliar and rhyming words.","tlm":"Story book, notebooks, board","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":5},{"activity":"Consonant clusters: introduction","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":4,"teacher":"Same-letter clusters: familiarise learners with clusters made of the same letter ('gg' as in egg, bigger, jogging). Ask them to pronounce them and find such words in the text and write them down.","learners":"Listen, pronounce the cluster and say words that contain it.","tlm":"Board and chalk, words list (egg bigger jogging wagging buggy)","source":"M","ref":"p.16","n":6},{"activity":"Consonant cluster game: Conjunct Consonant Game","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":6,"teacher":"Give each child a set of conjunct consonant cards. Observe closely and help learners who need support.","learners":"Choose one conjunct consonant and form five words with it. Learners at paragraph or story level can make sentences with the words they formed.","tlm":"Conjunct consonant cards","source":"M","ref":"p.17","n":7},{"activity":"Mind mapping (Day 1): the word 'village'","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Ask: 'What words come to your mind when you hear the word village?' Write learners' answers on the board or floor (Para and Story level learners write the words themselves). Guide the map towards the learning objective. Example words: hut, roof, wall, door, pond, field, temple, school, farmer, potter, weaver, fisherman.","learners":"Say words connected with 'village'; share the meaning and feeling of words.","tlm":"Board, chalk (or floor)","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":8},{"activity":"Mind mapping: classify the words","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":4,"teacher":"Ask learners to classify the words in groups, for example: Houses: hut, roof, wall, door; Places: pond, field, temple, school; Work: farmer, potter, weaver, fisherman.","learners":"Sort the words into groups and say why.","tlm":"Board, chalk, word cards (optional)","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":9},{"activity":"Mind mapping: level-wise individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":6,"teacher":"Give each learner the individual task for their level; observe closely and give individual support. Display corrected stories on the wall.","learners":"Complete the task for their level (see level table).","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":10},{"activity":"Daily reading (10 minutes)","grouping":"Individual","minutes":10,"teacher":"Give each learner a library book or any storybook. Move around, listen to individual readers and note their level.","learners":"Read independently a book of their choice.","tlm":"Library books or storybooks","source":"M","ref":"p.7","n":11}],"procedures":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Rain clapping","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","steps":[{"teacher":"Stand the learners in a circle and ask them to close their eyes. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Stand in a circle and close their eyes."},{"teacher":"Start clapping with one finger; then two fingers, three, four and finally five fingers.","learners":"Keep clapping, copying the change of fingers."},{"teacher":"After the activity ask: Which finger sound was your favourite?","learners":"Tell how they felt and what the sounds reminded them of."}]},{"activity":"Oral conversation: conversation on a picture","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.9","steps":[{"teacher":"Show the picture of a railway station with a waiting train.","learners":"Look carefully."},{"teacher":"Ask: What is happening in the picture? Who is doing what? What is happening around them? Then: What might happen next?","learners":"Answer in their own words; every learner gets a chance."},{"teacher":"Let learners imagine and make up a short story from the picture.","learners":"Tell their stories to the class."}]},{"activity":"Story - Day 1 (a story about the rain and the seasons)","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.10","steps":[{"teacher":"Discuss the title or picture of the story with the learners.","learners":"Talk about what they see and what the story may be about."},{"teacher":"Read the story aloud with expression and proper voice modulation. Learners should not simply repeat after you.","learners":"Listen carefully and enjoy the story."},{"teacher":"Discuss the story: factual, logical, vocabulary-based, judgment or opinion questions (today's focus: factual: Who was in the story? Where did it happen? What did the character do first?). Begin in the home language if needed.","learners":"Think and respond thoughtfully; every learner takes part."},{"teacher":"Read the story again slowly, pointing to each word. Make sure each learner has a copy and follows with a finger.","learners":"Follow each word with their finger."},{"teacher":"Ask learners to read in small groups; select a group leader who helps the others. Learners read one sentence at a time while the others point with fingers.","learners":"Read with the help of one another."}]},{"activity":"Consonant clusters (gg) and the game 'Conjunct Consonant Game'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.16-17","steps":[{"teacher":"Same-letter clusters: familiarise learners with clusters made of the same letter ('gg' as in egg, bigger, jogging). Ask them to pronounce them and find such words in the text and write them down.","learners":"Listen, pronounce and find words in the text."},{"teacher":"Write the words on the board: egg bigger jogging wagging buggy. Read them aloud with distinct pronunciation of the cluster.","learners":"Read the words aloud; point to the cluster in each word."},{"teacher":"Give each child a set of conjunct consonant cards.","learners":"Choose one conjunct consonant and form five words with it. Learners at paragraph or story level can make sentences with the words they formed."}]},{"activity":"Mind mapping: 'village'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Small group (level-wise) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.14","steps":[{"teacher":"Choose a word that can generate many related words: 'village'. Ask: 'What words come to your mind when you hear the word village?' Write the answers on the board or floor.","learners":"Say words they link with 'village'."},{"teacher":"Discuss the words: what they mean and how they are connected.","learners":"Explain their words and listen to others."},{"teacher":"In small groups, let the learners classify the words (Houses: hut, roof, wall, door; Places: pond, field, temple, school; Work: farmer, potter, weaver, fisherman).","learners":"Sort the words into groups."},{"teacher":"Give the individual tasks by level and help each learner.","learners":"Work individually; read the work aloud at the end if time allows."}]}],"levelTasks":[{"activity":"Story - Day 1: individual tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.10","tasks":{"Beginner":"Circle or search for a favourite word or letter in the story and say it aloud. If a learner cannot draw a circle, write words on the board and ask them to identify them.","Letter":"Find, read and write favourite words from the story.","Word":"Find the consonant clusters in the story, read them and write them in the notebook.","Para":"Silently read the story from the textbook; find unfamiliar words and try to understand them; find rhyming words, use them in sentences and write in the notebook; ask other groups for meanings; make questions in groups.","Story":"Silently read the story; find unfamiliar words and rhyming words; practise reading with emotion; one group reads sentences formed with consonant clusters to the other group; ask and answer group questions (information, thinking and opinion questions)."}},{"activity":"Consonant clusters (gg): level tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.16-17","tasks":{"Beginner":"Listen to the sound of the cluster and point to it in a word; continue with letter-sound work (interpretation: the manual describes clusters for learners lagging in reading words and sentences).","Letter":"Listen to the cluster sound and pick words with the cluster from a word card (interpretation).","Word":"Find the cluster in the story or textbook words, read the words and write them in the notebook.","Para":"Form words and sentences using the cluster; read the sentences aloud.","Story":"Form words and sentences using the cluster; read the sentences aloud; use them in the story writing."}},{"activity":"Mind mapping 'village': level tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.14","tasks":{"Beginner":"Circle all the words that contain the letter 'E' on the board; make a list. See how many learners find the most words.","Letter":"Circle all the words that contain the letter 'E' and make a list of them.","Word":"Use 4-5 words (for example hut, door, pond, roof, wall) to form sentences, starting with words of one or two syllables. Example: Dream - I had a dream last night.","Para":"Choose any five words from the map and create a story with them. Use consonant clusters correctly, read the story aloud, correct mistakes of sentence structure, spelling or grammar, then display it on the wall.","Story":"Choose any five words from the map and create a story with them. Use consonant clusters correctly, read the story aloud, correct mistakes of sentence structure, spelling or grammar, then display it on the wall."}}],"organisation":[{"grouping":"Whole class (big group)","how":"All learners of all levels sit in a 'U' shape arranged by level (Beginner, Letter, Word, Para, Story) so that the move to small groups is easy.","activities":["Warm-up: Rain clapping","Oral conversation: conversation on a picture","Story (Day 1 of the story): reading aloud and discussion","Consonant clusters: introduction","Mind mapping (Day 1): the word 'village'"]},{"grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","how":"Learners of similar levels work together; the teacher gives each group a task for its level and spends more time with learners who need support. Rotate responsibilities (for example group leader).","activities":["Story: reading in small groups","Consonant cluster game: Conjunct Consonant Game","Mind mapping: classify the words"]},{"grouping":"Individual","how":"Each learner works on a task for their own level; the teacher moves around, observes difficulties and supports individuals.","activities":["Story: level-wise individual tasks","Mind mapping: level-wise individual tasks","Daily reading (10 minutes)"]}],"materials":["After the activity ask: Which finger sound was your favourite?","Picture card of a railway station with a waiting train","A story from the school library (a story about the rain","the seasons)","a copy for each learner","Story book copies","Story book","notebooks","board","Board","chalk","words list (egg bigger jogging wagging buggy)","Conjunct consonant cards","chalk (or floor)","word cards (optional)","Notebooks","Library books or storybooks"],"outcomes":["Learners take part in the oral conversation and speak without fear.","Learners show understanding of the story in the discussion and complete the task for their level.","Learners respond to the sound-symbol task for today (Consonant clusters: gg (egg, bigger)) at their own level.","Learners add words to the mind map and use them in sentences or a story at their level.","Each learner reads a book for 10 minutes."],"observation":["Observe each learner's reading and writing during the individual tasks; note who needs individual support and how many learners share the same difficulty.","Note any learner whose level is improving; move the learner to the next level group when you see steady progress (manual p.5).","Record each learner's progress for the day in the notebook, according to the learner's level (manual p.4).","Use today's observations to adjust tomorrow's plan (manual p.5)."],"teacherNotes":["Story selection: the manual asks teachers to use picture story books or stories in the school library. Today's suggested theme (a story about the rain and the seasons) is a planning suggestion; use any suitable story you have.","Consonant clusters: do these activities daily for learners who find reading complex words hard; the aim is to remove the fear of reading clusters. Teachers may carry out similar activities on their own.","Mind mapping topic for this day: 'village'. The manual's example uses the word 'shop'; today's topic follows the same method.","Pace: the manual says not to assume all learners progress at the same speed. Repeat a day's activity with the groups that need it before moving on.","Special needs: give extra time and prepare materials for slower learners; seat learners with hearing or vision difficulty at the front; for learners who reverse or confuse letters, trace letters on the letter card with a finger and write with dots to trace with a pencil (manual p.6)."],"components":[{"no":1,"key":"warmup","name":"Warm-up activities","keywords":["Rain clapping","two learners lead"],"rows":[1]},{"no":2,"key":"oral","name":"Oral Discussion","keywords":["conversation on a picture","every learner speaks"],"rows":[2]},{"no":3,"key":"story","name":"Story","keywords":["Day 1","title / picture talk","read aloud with expression","factual questions","re-read pointing","group reading","level tasks"],"rows":[3,4,5]},{"no":4,"key":"sound","name":"Sound symbol games, Sound separation-pairing","keywords":["consonant cluster 'gg'","pronounce and find words","game: Conjunct Consonant Game"],"rows":[6,7]},{"no":5,"key":"mindwrite","name":"Mind Mapping (Day 1)","keywords":["mind map: village","classify the words","level task: circle letter E / sentences / story"],"rows":[8,9,10]},{"no":6,"key":"reading","name":"Daily reading","keywords":["library book","read alone","teacher listens"],"rows":[11]}],"preLesson":null},{"programme":"TARL Literacy","id":"lit-026","day":26,"phase":1,"phaseLabel":"Phase 1 (Days 1-45)","title":"Story: a story about the rain and the seasons (Day 2)","dayType":"Story Day 2 + Self-writing","focus":"Barakhadi / alphabet and phonics chart (line 9, letter 'x') | Self-writing: a day at the river","duration":70,"objectives":["Listen, speak and answer in the oral conversation (listening and storytelling).","Retell the story, read it with expression, ask and answer questions about it and write answers.","Develop sound-symbol skills: Barakhadi / alphabet and phonics chart (line 9, letter 'x').","Write about a topic at their own level and review the writing (a day at the river).","Read independently for 10 minutes every day."],"sequence":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Writing with body parts","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Learners stand in a circle. Demonstrate writing the word 'book' in the air with a finger, then ask them to write it with different body parts. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Write the word 'book' in the air with the finger, then with the head, shoulders, knees or elbows.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.8","n":1},{"activity":"Oral conversation: listening and storytelling","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Tell an interesting story starter and involve the learners: 'A kite came to my window and asked me to hold on. Where did we fly?' Let learners imagine and continue the story.","learners":"Listen to the teacher, then imagine and continue the story. Learners can also recite a rhyme or story they know.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.9","n":2},{"activity":"Story (Day 2 of the story): retelling","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":6,"teacher":"Ask learners to retell yesterday's story in their own words. Prompt with questions on the beginning, middle and end.","learners":"Retell the story using their own words.","tlm":"The same story book as yesterday","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":3},{"activity":"Story: reading with actions and group questions","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":9,"teacher":"Learners practise reading with actions and expressions; one learner per group reads aloud to the class. Guide groups to make questions about the story (guide initially). Groups take turns to ask and answer each other's questions. Word-level learners also read aloud the consonants learned on the first day.","learners":"Read with actions; make questions (word-level learners help write them); ask and answer questions with another group.","tlm":"Story book, slate or paper for questions","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":4},{"activity":"Story: writing answers individually","grouping":"Individual","minutes":5,"teacher":"Para and Story level learners write answers to all questions individually; read and correct their responses after they finish.","learners":"Write the answers in their notebooks; Beginner/Letter/Word learners read or listen and answer orally.","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":5},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart: big group reading","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":3,"teacher":"Show the Barakhadi chart and ask which letter they like. Read the letter 'x' on the chart; learners listen carefully and point to it on their own chart (they do not repeat after you).","learners":"Listen and point to the letter on their own chart.","tlm":"Barakhadi chart, alphabet or phonics chart","source":"M","ref":"p.13","n":6},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart: small-group practice","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Learners practise reading the alphabet or phonics chart in groups and help each other. One learner per group reads aloud. Occasionally ask learners to identify the sounds of letters. Give each level its group task.","learners":"Read the chart in groups; one learner reads aloud; do the level task.","tlm":"Alphabet or phonics chart, board or floor","source":"M","ref":"p.13","n":7},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart: individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":2,"teacher":"Give each learner an individual task for their level and observe closely; assist any learner who needs individual support.","learners":"Say and write a letter or word, a sentence or a short paragraph (by level).","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.13","n":8},{"activity":"Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on a day at the river","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Start a conversation about a topic: 'a day at the river'. Involve all learners and ask open-ended questions.","learners":"Take part in the discussion and share thoughts freely.","tlm":"Picture card or topic on the board","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":9},{"activity":"Self-writing: individual writing","grouping":"Individual","minutes":7,"teacher":"Give each level its task (see level table). Let learners take ownership of what they draw and write; mistakes are fine.","learners":"Draw and write about the topic at their level.","tlm":"Notebooks, crayons or pencils","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":10},{"activity":"Self-writing: review and reading back","grouping":"Individual","minutes":3,"teacher":"Ask each learner 'What did you draw or write?' and have them read it aloud once. Word-level learners read to the group; discuss spelling, punctuation and sentence structure. Help beginners by writing their text in the notebook for them if needed.","learners":"Read what they wrote; correct mistakes after listening to their own reading.","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":11},{"activity":"Daily reading (10 minutes)","grouping":"Individual","minutes":10,"teacher":"Give each learner a library book or any storybook. Move around, listen to individual readers and note their level.","learners":"Read independently a book of their choice.","tlm":"Library books or storybooks","source":"M","ref":"p.7","n":12}],"procedures":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Writing with body parts","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","steps":[{"teacher":"Stand the learners in a circle. Demonstrate writing the word 'book' in the air with your finger.","learners":"Watch and then copy with their own finger."},{"teacher":"Ask them to write it again using toes and other body parts (head, shoulders, knees, ...).","learners":"Write the letters in the air with the named body part."},{"teacher":"Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Take turns to lead."}]},{"activity":"Oral conversation: listening and storytelling","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.9","steps":[{"teacher":"Say the starter: 'A kite came to my window and asked me to hold on. Where did we fly?'","learners":"Listen and imagine."},{"teacher":"Ask learners to continue the story one by one. Encourage those who speak less.","learners":"Add ideas to the story."},{"teacher":"Invite a learner to recite a poem or rhyme they know.","learners":"Recite and listen to others."}]},{"activity":"Story - Day 2 (a story about the rain and the seasons)","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.11","steps":[{"teacher":"Ask learners to retell the story they read yesterday in their own words.","learners":"Retell, helping each other remember."},{"teacher":"In small groups learners practise reading the story using actions and expressions; one learner from each group then reads aloud to the class.","learners":"Read with actions and expression; a representative reads aloud."},{"teacher":"Guide the groups to come up with questions about the story (guide initially). Word-level learners can support by helping write them down.","learners":"Make questions together."},{"teacher":"Groups take turns to ask and answer each other's questions. Useful kinds: questions whose answer is not in the text; questions needing thinking beyond the text; questions asking for an opinion.","learners":"Ask, answer and discuss in the groups."},{"teacher":"Word-level learners also read aloud the consonants they learned on the first day.","learners":"Read the consonant clusters aloud."}]},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart activity (line 9)","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Small group (level-wise) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.13","steps":[{"teacher":"Show the Barakhadi chart and ask the learners which letter they like. Where is the letter 'x'?","learners":"Look for the letter on the chart."},{"teacher":"Read the letter 'x' on the chart. Learners listen and point to it on their own chart. Make sure they do not repeat after you.","learners":"Listen and point to the letter."},{"teacher":"Learners read the alphabet or phonics chart in their groups and help each other; one learner from each group comes forward to read aloud.","learners":"Read in groups; the representative reads aloud."},{"teacher":"Occasionally ask them to identify the sounds of letters from the chart.","learners":"Say the sound of the letter you point to."},{"teacher":"As an extra activity, write some letters on the floor, call out each letter one by one and let the learners jump onto the correct letter.","learners":"Jump onto the letter that is called."}]},{"activity":"Self-writing: 'Discussion, Writing, Self-review'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.15","steps":[{"teacher":"Start a conversation about a topic: 'a day at the river'. Involve all learners and ask open-ended questions.","learners":"Discuss and answer questions."},{"teacher":"Give writing time at each level: draw then write (Beginner), write about what they liked (Letter), a sentence (Word), a paragraph or story on a topic of their choice (Para/Story).","learners":"Write at their level and take ownership of the work."},{"teacher":"Review: ask 'What did you draw or write?' Have each learner read the text aloud once. Support with writing if needed.","learners":"Read aloud, listen to their pronunciation and correct mistakes."}]}],"levelTasks":[{"activity":"Story - Day 2: level-wise tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.11","tasks":{"Beginner":"Retell with the group by pointing to pictures or words; read aloud with group support (interpretation of the manual's group reading task).","Letter":"Read with the group, pointing to words; say the letters and words they know (interpretation of the manual's group reading task).","Word":"Support the group in writing the questions; read aloud the consonant clusters learned on the first day.","Para":"Ask the group's questions to another group, discuss them, then write answers to all questions individually; the teacher reads and corrects.","Story":"Ask the group's questions to another group, discuss them, then write answers to all questions individually; the teacher reads and corrects."}},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart: level tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.13","tasks":{"Beginner":"Small group: read the chart in the group; find and write favourite letters from the line. Individual: say and write a letter of their choice.","Letter":"Small group: read the chart; find and write favourite letters or words from any line. Individual: say a word on their own that begins with any letter.","Word":"Small group: write one or two lines of letters on the board or floor and use them to form words. Individual: speak and write sentences using words they know.","Para":"Small group: prepare word lists using the Barakhadi chart (for example items found in a shop or in the kitchen). Individual: write short paragraphs using the words formed with the Barakhadi chart.","Story":"Small group: prepare word lists using the Barakhadi chart. Individual: write short paragraphs using the words formed with the Barakhadi chart."}},{"activity":"Self-writing: level tasks and review","source":"M","ref":"p.15","tasks":{"Beginner":"Draw a picture about the discussion and then write a few sentences about it, expressing thoughts freely. Review: say what they drew or wrote; read the text aloud once; the teacher may write the text in the notebook for them.","Letter":"Write about what they liked, using drawing and writing; write any words or sentences they can. Review: read the text aloud once; correct punctuation mistakes using the Barakhadi chart.","Word":"Write a sentence based on the conversation. Mistakes in spelling, punctuation and sentence structure are fine. Review: read it to the group; discuss and correct mistakes together.","Para":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation.","Story":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation."}}],"organisation":[{"grouping":"Whole class (big group)","how":"All learners of all levels sit in a 'U' shape arranged by level (Beginner, Letter, Word, Para, Story) so that the move to small groups is easy.","activities":["Warm-up: Writing with body parts","Oral conversation: listening and storytelling","Story (Day 2 of the story): retelling","Barakhadi chart: big group reading","Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on a day at the river"]},{"grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","how":"Learners of similar levels work together; the teacher gives each group a task for its level and spends more time with learners who need support. Rotate responsibilities (for example group leader).","activities":["Story: reading with actions and group questions","Barakhadi chart: small-group practice"]},{"grouping":"Individual","how":"Each learner works on a task for their own level; the teacher moves around, observes difficulties and supports individuals.","activities":["Story: writing answers individually","Barakhadi chart: individual tasks","Self-writing: individual writing","Self-writing: review and reading back","Daily reading (10 minutes)"]}],"materials":["The same story book as yesterday","Story book","slate or paper for questions","Notebooks","Barakhadi chart","alphabet or phonics chart","Alphabet or phonics chart","board or floor","Picture card or topic on the board","crayons or pencils","Library books or storybooks"],"outcomes":["Learners take part in the oral conversation and speak without fear.","Learners retell the story, read with expression and ask or answer questions at their level.","Learners respond to the sound-symbol task for today (Barakhadi / alphabet and phonics chart (line 9, letter 'x')) at their own level.","Learners write about the topic at their level and read it aloud.","Each learner reads a book for 10 minutes."],"observation":["Observe each learner's reading and writing during the individual tasks; note who needs individual support and how many learners share the same difficulty.","Note any learner whose level is improving; move the learner to the next level group when you see steady progress (manual p.5).","Record each learner's progress for the day in the notebook, according to the learner's level (manual p.4).","Use today's observations to adjust tomorrow's plan (manual p.5)."],"teacherNotes":["Questions to elicit on Day 2: information questions (answer not in the text), thinking questions (needs knowledge beyond the text) and opinion questions (feedback on something in the text).","Barakhadi: learners who need extra time should get repeated practice using one or two sound units at a time. Topic-based discussion helps oral expression, thinking and understanding.","Writing has two parts, content and sequence: encourage learners to read what they wrote, improve it and rewrite it for clarity and correctness (manual p.15).","Pace: the manual says not to assume all learners progress at the same speed. Repeat a day's activity with the groups that need it before moving on.","Special needs: give extra time and prepare materials for slower learners; seat learners with hearing or vision difficulty at the front; for learners who reverse or confuse letters, trace letters on the letter card with a finger and write with dots to trace with a pencil (manual p.6)."],"components":[{"no":1,"key":"warmup","name":"Warm-up activities","keywords":["Writing with body parts","two learners lead"],"rows":[1]},{"no":2,"key":"oral","name":"Oral Discussion","keywords":["listening and storytelling","every learner speaks"],"rows":[2]},{"no":3,"key":"story","name":"Story","keywords":["Day 2","retell","read with actions","group questions","ask and answer","write answers (Para/Story)"],"rows":[3,4,5]},{"no":4,"key":"sound","name":"Sound symbol games, Sound separation-pairing","keywords":["Barakhadi / alphabet chart","listen and point (no repeating)","group reading","level tasks"],"rows":[6,7,8]},{"no":5,"key":"mindwrite","name":"Individual-Writing (Day 2)","keywords":["discussion","write at own level","self-review (read aloud)"],"rows":[9,10,11]},{"no":6,"key":"reading","name":"Daily reading","keywords":["library book","read alone","teacher listens"],"rows":[12]}],"preLesson":null},{"programme":"TARL Literacy","id":"lit-027","day":27,"phase":1,"phaseLabel":"Phase 1 (Days 1-45)","title":"Story: a story about a family journey (Day 1)","dayType":"Story Day 1 + Mind mapping","focus":"Language game: Jumping on Letters | Mind map: hospital","duration":70,"objectives":["Listen, speak and answer in the oral conversation (What did you see on your way?).","Listen to and read a story with understanding; discuss it in big and small groups and respond at their own level.","Develop sound-symbol skills: Language game: Jumping on Letters.","Build vocabulary through a mind map ('hospital') and use the words at their own level.","Read independently for 10 minutes every day."],"sequence":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Alphabet song (last-letter word chain)","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Say a word to the big group, for example 'earth'. Learners say a word that starts with the last letter ('h'). A learner who cannot say a word is out. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Say a word that starts with the last letter of the previous word; step out if unable to.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.8","n":1},{"activity":"Oral conversation: What did you see on your way?","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Ask learners to describe what they saw on their way to school. If they are hesitant, begin yourself: 'Today I saw a rainbow over the school, wet leaves on the path and a frog near the drain. What did you see?'","learners":"Describe what they saw on the way to school and connect with what others share.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.9","n":2},{"activity":"Story (Day 1 of the story): reading aloud and discussion","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":8,"teacher":"Discuss the title or picture of the story with the learners. Read the story aloud with expression and voice modulation (learners do not repeat after you). Discuss it, with emphasis on logical questions. Read it again slowly, pointing to each word.","learners":"Talk about the title/picture; listen; answer questions; follow each word with a finger in their own copy.","tlm":"A story from the school library (a story about a family journey), a copy for each learner","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":3},{"activity":"Story: reading in small groups","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":7,"teacher":"Form level-wise groups with a group leader. Learners read the story one sentence at a time while the others follow with their fingers. Para and Story level learners practise reading with emotion and expression.","learners":"Read the story sentence by sentence, supporting each other; the group leader helps.","tlm":"Story book copies","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":4},{"activity":"Story: level-wise individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":5,"teacher":"Give each learner the task for their level (see level table) and support those who need it.","learners":"Beginner/Letter: find and write favourite words or letters. Word: find consonant clusters. Para/Story: silently read, find unfamiliar and rhyming words.","tlm":"Story book, notebooks, board","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":5},{"activity":"Language game: Jumping on Letters","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Big boxes with one letter each are drawn on the ground; learners jump onto the letter the teacher calls. Observe each learner and give help where needed.","learners":"Play the game, take turns and read or say the words they make.","tlm":"Chalk, ground or floor","source":"M","ref":"p.18","n":6},{"activity":"Mind mapping (Day 1): the word 'hospital'","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Ask: 'What words come to your mind when you hear the word hospital?' Write learners' answers on the board or floor (Para and Story level learners write the words themselves). Guide the map towards the learning objective. Example words: doctor, nurse, patient, visitor, medicine, bed, injection, bandage, ward, pharmacy, ambulance, gate.","learners":"Say words connected with 'hospital'; share the meaning and feeling of words.","tlm":"Board, chalk (or floor)","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":7},{"activity":"Mind mapping: classify the words","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":4,"teacher":"Ask learners to classify the words in groups, for example: People: doctor, nurse, patient, visitor; Things: medicine, bed, injection, bandage; Places: ward, pharmacy, ambulance, gate.","learners":"Sort the words into groups and say why.","tlm":"Board, chalk, word cards (optional)","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":8},{"activity":"Mind mapping: level-wise individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":6,"teacher":"Give each learner the individual task for their level; observe closely and give individual support. Display corrected stories on the wall.","learners":"Complete the task for their level (see level table).","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":9},{"activity":"Daily reading (10 minutes)","grouping":"Individual","minutes":10,"teacher":"Give each learner a library book or any storybook. Move around, listen to individual readers and note their level.","learners":"Read independently a book of their choice.","tlm":"Library books or storybooks","source":"M","ref":"p.7","n":10}],"procedures":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Alphabet song (last-letter word chain)","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","steps":[{"teacher":"Say the word 'earth' to the big group and show that its last letter is 'h'.","learners":"Listen and think of a word starting with 'h'."},{"teacher":"Ask learners in turn to say a word that starts with the last letter of the previous word. Example: rain -> nest.","learners":"Say a word in turn; anyone who cannot say a word is out of the game."},{"teacher":"Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Lead the game when it is their turn."}]},{"activity":"Oral conversation: What did you see on your way?","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.9","steps":[{"teacher":"Ask: 'What did you see on your way to school today?'","learners":"Think about the way to school."},{"teacher":"If learners hesitate, start: 'Today I saw a rainbow over the school, wet leaves on the path and a frog near the drain. What did you see?'","learners":"Listen to the model and then share their own observations."},{"teacher":"Connect learners' answers with each other.","learners":"Listen and add what they noticed."}]},{"activity":"Story - Day 1 (a story about a family journey)","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.10","steps":[{"teacher":"Discuss the title or picture of the story with the learners.","learners":"Talk about what they see and what the story may be about."},{"teacher":"Read the story aloud with expression and proper voice modulation. Learners should not simply repeat after you.","learners":"Listen carefully and enjoy the story."},{"teacher":"Discuss the story: factual, logical, vocabulary-based, judgment or opinion questions (today's focus: logical: Why did the character do that? What would have happened if ...?). Begin in the home language if needed.","learners":"Think and respond thoughtfully; every learner takes part."},{"teacher":"Read the story again slowly, pointing to each word. Make sure each learner has a copy and follows with a finger.","learners":"Follow each word with their finger."},{"teacher":"Ask learners to read in small groups; select a group leader who helps the others. Learners read one sentence at a time while the others point with fingers.","learners":"Read with the help of one another."}]},{"activity":"Language game: Jumping on Letters","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.18","steps":[{"teacher":"Draw large boxes on the ground with chalk and write one letter inside each box.","learners":"Look at the letters in the boxes."},{"teacher":"Call learners one by one and say a letter aloud, for example p, m, t, n.","learners":"Listen to the sound and jump onto the correct letter."},{"teacher":"Repeat with new letters and let learners take turns to be the caller.","learners":"Take turns to jump and to call out letters."}]},{"activity":"Mind mapping: 'hospital'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Small group (level-wise) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.14","steps":[{"teacher":"Choose a word that can generate many related words: 'hospital'. Ask: 'What words come to your mind when you hear the word hospital?' Write the answers on the board or floor.","learners":"Say words they link with 'hospital'."},{"teacher":"Discuss the words: what they mean and how they are connected.","learners":"Explain their words and listen to others."},{"teacher":"In small groups, let the learners classify the words (People: doctor, nurse, patient, visitor; Things: medicine, bed, injection, bandage; Places: ward, pharmacy, ambulance, gate).","learners":"Sort the words into groups."},{"teacher":"Give the individual tasks by level and help each learner.","learners":"Work individually; read the work aloud at the end if time allows."}]}],"levelTasks":[{"activity":"Story - Day 1: individual tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.10","tasks":{"Beginner":"Circle or search for a favourite word or letter in the story and say it aloud. If a learner cannot draw a circle, write words on the board and ask them to identify them.","Letter":"Find, read and write favourite words from the story.","Word":"Find the consonant clusters in the story, read them and write them in the notebook.","Para":"Silently read the story from the textbook; find unfamiliar words and try to understand them; find rhyming words, use them in sentences and write in the notebook; ask other groups for meanings; make questions in groups.","Story":"Silently read the story; find unfamiliar words and rhyming words; practise reading with emotion; one group reads sentences formed with consonant clusters to the other group; ask and answer group questions (information, thinking and opinion questions)."}},{"activity":"Language game: Jumping on Letters - level support","source":"I","ref":"p.18","tasks":{"Beginner":"Take part by saying or pointing to the letters involved and by listening carefully; Para and Story level partners help.","Letter":"Say the letters/sounds and give simple words they know.","Word":"Say and write words and short sentences for the game.","Para":"Write sentences with the words; help groups to record answers.","Story":"Write sentences or short stories with the words; help groups to record answers."}},{"activity":"Mind mapping 'hospital': level tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.14","tasks":{"Beginner":"Circle all the words that contain the letter 'E' on the board; make a list. See how many learners find the most words.","Letter":"Circle all the words that contain the letter 'E' and make a list of them.","Word":"Use 4-5 words (for example bed, gate, ward, nurse, doctor) to form sentences, starting with words of one or two syllables. Example: Dream - I had a dream last night.","Para":"Choose any five words from the map and create a story with them. Use consonant clusters correctly, read the story aloud, correct mistakes of sentence structure, spelling or grammar, then display it on the wall.","Story":"Choose any five words from the map and create a story with them. Use consonant clusters correctly, read the story aloud, correct mistakes of sentence structure, spelling or grammar, then display it on the wall."}}],"organisation":[{"grouping":"Whole class (big group)","how":"All learners of all levels sit in a 'U' shape arranged by level (Beginner, Letter, Word, Para, Story) so that the move to small groups is easy.","activities":["Warm-up: Alphabet song (last-letter word chain)","Oral conversation: What did you see on your way?","Story (Day 1 of the story): reading aloud and discussion","Language game: Jumping on Letters","Mind mapping (Day 1): the word 'hospital'"]},{"grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","how":"Learners of similar levels work together; the teacher gives each group a task for its level and spends more time with learners who need support. Rotate responsibilities (for example group leader).","activities":["Story: reading in small groups","Mind mapping: classify the words"]},{"grouping":"Individual","how":"Each learner works on a task for their own level; the teacher moves around, observes difficulties and supports individuals.","activities":["Story: level-wise individual tasks","Mind mapping: level-wise individual tasks","Daily reading (10 minutes)"]}],"materials":["A story from the school library (a story about a family journey)","a copy for each learner","Story book copies","Story book","notebooks","board","Chalk","ground or floor","Board","chalk (or floor)","chalk","word cards (optional)","Notebooks","Library books or storybooks"],"outcomes":["Learners take part in the oral conversation and speak without fear.","Learners show understanding of the story in the discussion and complete the task for their level.","Learners respond to the sound-symbol task for today (Language game: Jumping on Letters) at their own level.","Learners add words to the mind map and use them in sentences or a story at their level.","Each learner reads a book for 10 minutes."],"observation":["Observe each learner's reading and writing during the individual tasks; note who needs individual support and how many learners share the same difficulty.","Note any learner whose level is improving; move the learner to the next level group when you see steady progress (manual p.5).","Record each learner's progress for the day in the notebook, according to the learner's level (manual p.4).","Use today's observations to adjust tomorrow's plan (manual p.5)."],"teacherNotes":["Story selection: the manual asks teachers to use picture story books or stories in the school library. Today's suggested theme (a story about a family journey) is a planning suggestion; use any suitable story you have.","The manual lists the letter and word games but does not fix the slot in the daily timetable where they are used. This plan places them in the 10-minute sound-symbol / alphabet slot (interpretation).","Mind mapping topic for this day: 'hospital'. The manual's example uses the word 'shop'; today's topic follows the same method.","Pace: the manual says not to assume all learners progress at the same speed. Repeat a day's activity with the groups that need it before moving on.","Special needs: give extra time and prepare materials for slower learners; seat learners with hearing or vision difficulty at the front; for learners who reverse or confuse letters, trace letters on the letter card with a finger and write with dots to trace with a pencil (manual p.6)."],"components":[{"no":1,"key":"warmup","name":"Warm-up activities","keywords":["Alphabet song (last-letter word chain)","two learners lead"],"rows":[1]},{"no":2,"key":"oral","name":"Oral Discussion","keywords":["What did you see on your way?","every learner speaks"],"rows":[2]},{"no":3,"key":"story","name":"Story","keywords":["Day 1","title / picture talk","read aloud with expression","logical questions","re-read pointing","group reading","level tasks"],"rows":[3,4,5]},{"no":4,"key":"sound","name":"Sound symbol games, Sound separation-pairing","keywords":["Jumping on Letters","play in turns","level support"],"rows":[6]},{"no":5,"key":"mindwrite","name":"Mind Mapping (Day 1)","keywords":["mind map: hospital","classify the words","level task: circle letter E / sentences / story"],"rows":[7,8,9]},{"no":6,"key":"reading","name":"Daily reading","keywords":["library book","read alone","teacher listens"],"rows":[10]}],"preLesson":null},{"programme":"TARL Literacy","id":"lit-028","day":28,"phase":1,"phaseLabel":"Phase 1 (Days 1-45)","title":"Story: a story about a family journey (Day 2)","dayType":"Story Day 2 + Self-writing","focus":"Consonant clusters: sn (snake, snow) | Self-writing: my favourite food","duration":70,"objectives":["Listen, speak and answer in the oral conversation (familiar topic).","Retell the story, read it with expression, ask and answer questions about it and write answers.","Develop sound-symbol skills: Consonant clusters: sn (snake, snow).","Write about a topic at their own level and review the writing (my favourite food).","Read independently for 10 minutes every day."],"sequence":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Handkerchief game","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Learners sit in a circle and clap while singing a rhyme ('I saw a Little Bird'). One learner runs outside the circle with a handkerchief and secretly places it behind another learner, who must chase the runner. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Sit in a circle, clap and sing; run, place the handkerchief or chase as the game requires.","tlm":"A handkerchief","source":"M","ref":"p.8","n":1},{"activity":"Oral conversation: familiar topic","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Hold a conversation on the topic 'what I did last Sunday'. Give each learner a chance to speak; be patient with learners who need extra time.","learners":"Talk about the topic and listen to others.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.9","n":2},{"activity":"Story (Day 2 of the story): retelling","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":6,"teacher":"Ask learners to retell yesterday's story in their own words. Prompt with questions on the beginning, middle and end.","learners":"Retell the story using their own words.","tlm":"The same story book as yesterday","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":3},{"activity":"Story: reading with actions and group questions","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":9,"teacher":"Learners practise reading with actions and expressions; one learner per group reads aloud to the class. Guide groups to make questions about the story (guide initially). Groups take turns to ask and answer each other's questions. Word-level learners also read aloud the consonants learned on the first day.","learners":"Read with actions; make questions (word-level learners help write them); ask and answer questions with another group.","tlm":"Story book, slate or paper for questions","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":4},{"activity":"Story: writing answers individually","grouping":"Individual","minutes":5,"teacher":"Para and Story level learners write answers to all questions individually; read and correct their responses after they finish.","learners":"Write the answers in their notebooks; Beginner/Letter/Word learners read or listen and answer orally.","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":5},{"activity":"Consonant clusters: introduction","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":4,"teacher":"Two-letter clusters: after same-letter clusters, familiarise learners with clusters of two different letters ('sn' as in snake, snow, snack). Discuss the words, ask learners to pronounce them and to frame sentences using them.","learners":"Listen, pronounce the cluster and say words that contain it.","tlm":"Board and chalk, words list (snake snow snack snail snap)","source":"M","ref":"p.16","n":6},{"activity":"Consonant cluster game: List of Conjunct Consonants","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":6,"teacher":"Write the names of the children in the class on the board and list those that contain conjunct consonants. If no names contain them, say words or sentences with conjunct consonants and write them on the board. Observe closely and help learners who need support.","learners":"Try to form new words using those conjunct consonants.","tlm":"Names, words or sentences on the board","source":"M","ref":"p.17","n":7},{"activity":"Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on my favourite food","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Start a conversation about a situation: 'my favourite food'. Involve all learners and ask open-ended questions.","learners":"Take part in the discussion and share thoughts freely.","tlm":"Picture card or topic on the board","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":8},{"activity":"Self-writing: individual writing","grouping":"Individual","minutes":7,"teacher":"Give each level its task (see level table). Let learners take ownership of what they draw and write; mistakes are fine.","learners":"Draw and write about the topic at their level.","tlm":"Notebooks, crayons or pencils","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":9},{"activity":"Self-writing: review and reading back","grouping":"Individual","minutes":3,"teacher":"Ask each learner 'What did you draw or write?' and have them read it aloud once. Word-level learners read to the group; discuss spelling, punctuation and sentence structure. Help beginners by writing their text in the notebook for them if needed.","learners":"Read what they wrote; correct mistakes after listening to their own reading.","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":10},{"activity":"Daily reading (10 minutes)","grouping":"Individual","minutes":10,"teacher":"Give each learner a library book or any storybook. Move around, listen to individual readers and note their level.","learners":"Read independently a book of their choice.","tlm":"Library books or storybooks","source":"M","ref":"p.7","n":11}],"procedures":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Handkerchief game","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","steps":[{"teacher":"Seat the learners in a circle and start clapping and singing the rhyme 'I saw a Little Bird'.","learners":"Clap and sing together."},{"teacher":"One learner runs outside the circle holding a handkerchief and secretly places it behind another learner.","learners":"Everyone keeps clapping; the learner who finds the handkerchief behind them takes it and chases the runner."},{"teacher":"If the runner sits in the chaser's place before being caught, they stay in the game; if caught, they are out. Continue in this way.","learners":"Play fairly and take turns."}]},{"activity":"Oral conversation: familiar topic","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.9","steps":[{"teacher":"Introduce the topic: 'what I did last Sunday'.","learners":"Think about their own experience."},{"teacher":"Ask open questions; give every learner a chance. Involve learners who speak less.","learners":"Speak freely and without fear."},{"teacher":"Praise efforts and sum up.","learners":"Listen and respect each other's ideas."}]},{"activity":"Story - Day 2 (a story about a family journey)","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.11","steps":[{"teacher":"Ask learners to retell the story they read yesterday in their own words.","learners":"Retell, helping each other remember."},{"teacher":"In small groups learners practise reading the story using actions and expressions; one learner from each group then reads aloud to the class.","learners":"Read with actions and expression; a representative reads aloud."},{"teacher":"Guide the groups to come up with questions about the story (guide initially). Word-level learners can support by helping write them down.","learners":"Make questions together."},{"teacher":"Groups take turns to ask and answer each other's questions. Useful kinds: questions whose answer is not in the text; questions needing thinking beyond the text; questions asking for an opinion.","learners":"Ask, answer and discuss in the groups."},{"teacher":"Word-level learners also read aloud the consonants they learned on the first day.","learners":"Read the consonant clusters aloud."}]},{"activity":"Consonant clusters (sn) and the game 'List of Conjunct Consonants'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.16-17","steps":[{"teacher":"Two-letter clusters: after same-letter clusters, familiarise learners with clusters of two different letters ('sn' as in snake, snow, snack). Discuss the words, ask learners to pronounce them and to frame sentences using them.","learners":"Listen, pronounce and find words in the text."},{"teacher":"Write the words on the board: snake snow snack snail snap. Read them aloud with distinct pronunciation of the cluster.","learners":"Read the words aloud; point to the cluster in each word."},{"teacher":"Write the names of the children in the class on the board and list those that contain conjunct consonants. If no names contain them, say words or sentences with conjunct consonants and write them on the board.","learners":"Try to form new words using those conjunct consonants."}]},{"activity":"Self-writing: 'Discussion, Writing, Self-review'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.15","steps":[{"teacher":"Start a conversation about a situation: 'my favourite food'. Involve all learners and ask open-ended questions.","learners":"Discuss and answer questions."},{"teacher":"Give writing time at each level: draw then write (Beginner), write about what they liked (Letter), a sentence (Word), a paragraph or story on a topic of their choice (Para/Story).","learners":"Write at their level and take ownership of the work."},{"teacher":"Review: ask 'What did you draw or write?' Have each learner read the text aloud once. Support with writing if needed.","learners":"Read aloud, listen to their pronunciation and correct mistakes."}]}],"levelTasks":[{"activity":"Story - Day 2: level-wise tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.11","tasks":{"Beginner":"Retell with the group by pointing to pictures or words; read aloud with group support (interpretation of the manual's group reading task).","Letter":"Read with the group, pointing to words; say the letters and words they know (interpretation of the manual's group reading task).","Word":"Support the group in writing the questions; read aloud the consonant clusters learned on the first day.","Para":"Ask the group's questions to another group, discuss them, then write answers to all questions individually; the teacher reads and corrects.","Story":"Ask the group's questions to another group, discuss them, then write answers to all questions individually; the teacher reads and corrects."}},{"activity":"Consonant clusters (sn): level tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.16-17","tasks":{"Beginner":"Listen to the sound of the cluster and point to it in a word; continue with letter-sound work (interpretation: the manual describes clusters for learners lagging in reading words and sentences).","Letter":"Listen to the cluster sound and pick words with the cluster from a word card (interpretation).","Word":"Find the cluster in the story or textbook words, read the words and write them in the notebook.","Para":"Form words and sentences using the cluster; read the sentences aloud.","Story":"Form words and sentences using the cluster; read the sentences aloud; use them in the story writing."}},{"activity":"Self-writing: level tasks and review","source":"M","ref":"p.15","tasks":{"Beginner":"Draw a picture about the discussion and then write a few sentences about it, expressing thoughts freely. Review: say what they drew or wrote; read the text aloud once; the teacher may write the text in the notebook for them.","Letter":"Write about what they liked, using drawing and writing; write any words or sentences they can. Review: read the text aloud once; correct punctuation mistakes using the Barakhadi chart.","Word":"Write a sentence based on the conversation. Mistakes in spelling, punctuation and sentence structure are fine. Review: read it to the group; discuss and correct mistakes together.","Para":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation.","Story":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation."}}],"organisation":[{"grouping":"Whole class (big group)","how":"All learners of all levels sit in a 'U' shape arranged by level (Beginner, Letter, Word, Para, Story) so that the move to small groups is easy.","activities":["Warm-up: Handkerchief game","Oral conversation: familiar topic","Story (Day 2 of the story): retelling","Consonant clusters: introduction","Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on my favourite food"]},{"grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","how":"Learners of similar levels work together; the teacher gives each group a task for its level and spends more time with learners who need support. Rotate responsibilities (for example group leader).","activities":["Story: reading with actions and group questions","Consonant cluster game: List of Conjunct Consonants"]},{"grouping":"Individual","how":"Each learner works on a task for their own level; the teacher moves around, observes difficulties and supports individuals.","activities":["Story: writing answers individually","Self-writing: individual writing","Self-writing: review and reading back","Daily reading (10 minutes)"]}],"materials":["A handkerchief","The same story book as yesterday","Story book","slate or paper for questions","Notebooks","Board","chalk","words list (snake snow snack snail snap)","Names","words or sentences on the board","Picture card or topic on the board","crayons or pencils","Library books or storybooks"],"outcomes":["Learners take part in the oral conversation and speak without fear.","Learners retell the story, read with expression and ask or answer questions at their level.","Learners respond to the sound-symbol task for today (Consonant clusters: sn (snake, snow)) at their own level.","Learners write about the topic at their level and read it aloud.","Each learner reads a book for 10 minutes."],"observation":["Observe each learner's reading and writing during the individual tasks; note who needs individual support and how many learners share the same difficulty.","Note any learner whose level is improving; move the learner to the next level group when you see steady progress (manual p.5).","Record each learner's progress for the day in the notebook, according to the learner's level (manual p.4).","Use today's observations to adjust tomorrow's plan (manual p.5)."],"teacherNotes":["Questions to elicit on Day 2: information questions (answer not in the text), thinking questions (needs knowledge beyond the text) and opinion questions (feedback on something in the text).","Consonant clusters: do these activities daily for learners who find reading complex words hard; the aim is to remove the fear of reading clusters. Teachers may carry out similar activities on their own.","Writing has two parts, content and sequence: encourage learners to read what they wrote, improve it and rewrite it for clarity and correctness (manual p.15).","Pace: the manual says not to assume all learners progress at the same speed. Repeat a day's activity with the groups that need it before moving on.","Special needs: give extra time and prepare materials for slower learners; seat learners with hearing or vision difficulty at the front; for learners who reverse or confuse letters, trace letters on the letter card with a finger and write with dots to trace with a pencil (manual p.6)."],"components":[{"no":1,"key":"warmup","name":"Warm-up activities","keywords":["Handkerchief game","two learners lead"],"rows":[1]},{"no":2,"key":"oral","name":"Oral Discussion","keywords":["familiar topic","every learner speaks"],"rows":[2]},{"no":3,"key":"story","name":"Story","keywords":["Day 2","retell","read with actions","group questions","ask and answer","write answers (Para/Story)"],"rows":[3,4,5]},{"no":4,"key":"sound","name":"Sound symbol games, Sound separation-pairing","keywords":["consonant cluster 'sn'","pronounce and find words","game: List of Conjunct Consonants"],"rows":[6,7]},{"no":5,"key":"mindwrite","name":"Individual-Writing (Day 2)","keywords":["discussion","write at own level","self-review (read aloud)"],"rows":[8,9,10]},{"no":6,"key":"reading","name":"Daily reading","keywords":["library book","read alone","teacher listens"],"rows":[11]}],"preLesson":null},{"programme":"TARL Literacy","id":"lit-029","day":29,"phase":1,"phaseLabel":"Phase 1 (Days 1-45)","title":"Story: a story about a market day (Day 1)","dayType":"Story Day 1 + Mind mapping","focus":"Language game: Jumping on Letters | Mind map: railway station","duration":70,"objectives":["Listen, speak and answer in the oral conversation (conversation on a picture).","Listen to and read a story with understanding; discuss it in big and small groups and respond at their own level.","Develop sound-symbol skills: Language game: Jumping on Letters.","Build vocabulary through a mind map ('railway station') and use the words at their own level.","Read independently for 10 minutes every day."],"sequence":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Rhyme - 'I caught a Fish Alive'","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Say the rhyme with actions, then say it together. Lines: One, two, three, four, five, once I caught a fish alive. / Six, seven, eight, nine, ten, then I let it go again. / Why did you let it go? Because it bit my finger so. / Which finger did it bite? This little finger on my right. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Listen, then say the rhyme with actions.","tlm":"Rhyme chart or board (optional)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","n":1},{"activity":"Oral conversation: conversation on a picture","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Show a picture of a festival procession with drums and ask what is happening, who is doing what and what is happening around them. Let learners think creatively and even make up a story.","learners":"Look at the picture, answer questions and make up their own story about it.","tlm":"Picture card of a festival procession with drums","source":"M","ref":"p.9","n":2},{"activity":"Story (Day 1 of the story): reading aloud and discussion","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":8,"teacher":"Discuss the title or picture of the story with the learners. Read the story aloud with expression and voice modulation (learners do not repeat after you). Discuss it, with emphasis on vocabulary-based questions. Read it again slowly, pointing to each word.","learners":"Talk about the title/picture; listen; answer questions; follow each word with a finger in their own copy.","tlm":"A story from the school library (a story about a market day), a copy for each learner","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":3},{"activity":"Story: reading in small groups","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":7,"teacher":"Form level-wise groups with a group leader. Learners read the story one sentence at a time while the others follow with their fingers. Para and Story level learners practise reading with emotion and expression.","learners":"Read the story sentence by sentence, supporting each other; the group leader helps.","tlm":"Story book copies","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":4},{"activity":"Story: level-wise individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":5,"teacher":"Give each learner the task for their level (see level table) and support those who need it.","learners":"Beginner/Letter: find and write favourite words or letters. Word: find consonant clusters. Para/Story: silently read, find unfamiliar and rhyming words.","tlm":"Story book, notebooks, board","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":5},{"activity":"Language game: Jumping on Letters","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Big boxes with one letter each are drawn on the ground; learners jump onto the letter the teacher calls. Observe each learner and give help where needed.","learners":"Play the game, take turns and read or say the words they make.","tlm":"Chalk, ground or floor","source":"M","ref":"p.18","n":6},{"activity":"Mind mapping (Day 1): the word 'railway station'","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Ask: 'What words come to your mind when you hear the word railway station?' Write learners' answers on the board or floor (Para and Story level learners write the words themselves). Guide the map towards the learning objective. Example words: porter, passenger, driver, guard, train, ticket, platform, signal, whistle, bell, flag, clock.","learners":"Say words connected with 'railway station'; share the meaning and feeling of words.","tlm":"Board, chalk (or floor)","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":7},{"activity":"Mind mapping: classify the words","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":4,"teacher":"Ask learners to classify the words in groups, for example: People: porter, passenger, driver, guard; Things: train, ticket, platform, signal; Sounds and signs: whistle, bell, flag, clock.","learners":"Sort the words into groups and say why.","tlm":"Board, chalk, word cards (optional)","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":8},{"activity":"Mind mapping: level-wise individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":6,"teacher":"Give each learner the individual task for their level; observe closely and give individual support. Display corrected stories on the wall.","learners":"Complete the task for their level (see level table).","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":9},{"activity":"Daily reading (10 minutes)","grouping":"Individual","minutes":10,"teacher":"Give each learner a library book or any storybook. Move around, listen to individual readers and note their level.","learners":"Read independently a book of their choice.","tlm":"Library books or storybooks","source":"M","ref":"p.7","n":10}],"procedures":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Rhyme - 'I caught a Fish Alive'","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","steps":[{"teacher":"Say the rhyme 'I caught a Fish Alive' slowly with actions: One, two, three, four, five, once I caught a fish alive. / Six, seven, eight, nine, ten, then I let it go again. / Why did you let it go? Because it bit my finger so. / Which finger did it bite? This little finger on my right.","learners":"Listen and watch the actions."},{"teacher":"Say it again; invite learners to join with actions.","learners":"Say the rhyme together with actions."},{"teacher":"Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Choose a rhyme they like and lead."}]},{"activity":"Oral conversation: conversation on a picture","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.9","steps":[{"teacher":"Show the picture of a festival procession with drums.","learners":"Look carefully."},{"teacher":"Ask: What is happening in the picture? Who is doing what? What is happening around them? Then: How do the people feel? How can you tell?","learners":"Answer in their own words; every learner gets a chance."},{"teacher":"Let learners imagine and make up a short story from the picture.","learners":"Tell their stories to the class."}]},{"activity":"Story - Day 1 (a story about a market day)","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.10","steps":[{"teacher":"Discuss the title or picture of the story with the learners.","learners":"Talk about what they see and what the story may be about."},{"teacher":"Read the story aloud with expression and proper voice modulation. Learners should not simply repeat after you.","learners":"Listen carefully and enjoy the story."},{"teacher":"Discuss the story: factual, logical, vocabulary-based, judgment or opinion questions (today's focus: vocabulary-based: What does this word mean? Which word in the story means the same as ...?). Begin in the home language if needed.","learners":"Think and respond thoughtfully; every learner takes part."},{"teacher":"Read the story again slowly, pointing to each word. Make sure each learner has a copy and follows with a finger.","learners":"Follow each word with their finger."},{"teacher":"Ask learners to read in small groups; select a group leader who helps the others. Learners read one sentence at a time while the others point with fingers.","learners":"Read with the help of one another."}]},{"activity":"Language game: Jumping on Letters","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.18","steps":[{"teacher":"Draw large boxes on the ground with chalk and write one letter inside each box.","learners":"Look at the letters in the boxes."},{"teacher":"Call learners one by one and say a letter aloud, for example p, m, t, n.","learners":"Listen to the sound and jump onto the correct letter."},{"teacher":"Repeat with new letters and let learners take turns to be the caller.","learners":"Take turns to jump and to call out letters."}]},{"activity":"Mind mapping: 'railway station'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Small group (level-wise) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.14","steps":[{"teacher":"Choose a word that can generate many related words: 'railway station'. Ask: 'What words come to your mind when you hear the word railway station?' Write the answers on the board or floor.","learners":"Say words they link with 'railway station'."},{"teacher":"Discuss the words: what they mean and how they are connected.","learners":"Explain their words and listen to others."},{"teacher":"In small groups, let the learners classify the words (People: porter, passenger, driver, guard; Things: train, ticket, platform, signal; Sounds and signs: whistle, bell, flag, clock).","learners":"Sort the words into groups."},{"teacher":"Give the individual tasks by level and help each learner.","learners":"Work individually; read the work aloud at the end if time allows."}]}],"levelTasks":[{"activity":"Story - Day 1: individual tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.10","tasks":{"Beginner":"Circle or search for a favourite word or letter in the story and say it aloud. If a learner cannot draw a circle, write words on the board and ask them to identify them.","Letter":"Find, read and write favourite words from the story.","Word":"Find the consonant clusters in the story, read them and write them in the notebook.","Para":"Silently read the story from the textbook; find unfamiliar words and try to understand them; find rhyming words, use them in sentences and write in the notebook; ask other groups for meanings; make questions in groups.","Story":"Silently read the story; find unfamiliar words and rhyming words; practise reading with emotion; one group reads sentences formed with consonant clusters to the other group; ask and answer group questions (information, thinking and opinion questions)."}},{"activity":"Language game: Jumping on Letters - level support","source":"I","ref":"p.18","tasks":{"Beginner":"Take part by saying or pointing to the letters involved and by listening carefully; Para and Story level partners help.","Letter":"Say the letters/sounds and give simple words they know.","Word":"Say and write words and short sentences for the game.","Para":"Write sentences with the words; help groups to record answers.","Story":"Write sentences or short stories with the words; help groups to record answers."}},{"activity":"Mind mapping 'railway station': level tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.14","tasks":{"Beginner":"Circle all the words that contain the letter 'A' on the board; make a list. See how many learners find the most words.","Letter":"Circle all the words that contain the letter 'A' and make a list of them.","Word":"Use 4-5 words (for example bell, flag, clock, guard, train) to form sentences, starting with words of one or two syllables. Example: Dream - I had a dream last night.","Para":"Choose any five words from the map and create a story with them. Use consonant clusters correctly, read the story aloud, correct mistakes of sentence structure, spelling or grammar, then display it on the wall.","Story":"Choose any five words from the map and create a story with them. Use consonant clusters correctly, read the story aloud, correct mistakes of sentence structure, spelling or grammar, then display it on the wall."}}],"organisation":[{"grouping":"Whole class (big group)","how":"All learners of all levels sit in a 'U' shape arranged by level (Beginner, Letter, Word, Para, Story) so that the move to small groups is easy.","activities":["Warm-up: Rhyme - 'I caught a Fish Alive'","Oral conversation: conversation on a picture","Story (Day 1 of the story): reading aloud and discussion","Language game: Jumping on Letters","Mind mapping (Day 1): the word 'railway station'"]},{"grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","how":"Learners of similar levels work together; the teacher gives each group a task for its level and spends more time with learners who need support. Rotate responsibilities (for example group leader).","activities":["Story: reading in small groups","Mind mapping: classify the words"]},{"grouping":"Individual","how":"Each learner works on a task for their own level; the teacher moves around, observes difficulties and supports individuals.","activities":["Story: level-wise individual tasks","Mind mapping: level-wise individual tasks","Daily reading (10 minutes)"]}],"materials":["Rhyme chart or board (optional)","Picture card of a festival procession with drums","A story from the school library (a story about a market day)","a copy for each learner","Story book copies","Story book","notebooks","board","Chalk","ground or floor","Board","chalk (or floor)","chalk","word cards (optional)","Notebooks","Library books or storybooks"],"outcomes":["Learners take part in the oral conversation and speak without fear.","Learners show understanding of the story in the discussion and complete the task for their level.","Learners respond to the sound-symbol task for today (Language game: Jumping on Letters) at their own level.","Learners add words to the mind map and use them in sentences or a story at their level.","Each learner reads a book for 10 minutes."],"observation":["Observe each learner's reading and writing during the individual tasks; note who needs individual support and how many learners share the same difficulty.","Note any learner whose level is improving; move the learner to the next level group when you see steady progress (manual p.5).","Record each learner's progress for the day in the notebook, according to the learner's level (manual p.4).","Use today's observations to adjust tomorrow's plan (manual p.5)."],"teacherNotes":["Story selection: the manual asks teachers to use picture story books or stories in the school library. Today's suggested theme (a story about a market day) is a planning suggestion; use any suitable story you have.","The manual lists the letter and word games but does not fix the slot in the daily timetable where they are used. This plan places them in the 10-minute sound-symbol / alphabet slot (interpretation).","Mind mapping topic for this day: 'railway station'. The manual's example uses the word 'shop'; today's topic follows the same method.","Pace: the manual says not to assume all learners progress at the same speed. Repeat a day's activity with the groups that need it before moving on.","Special needs: give extra time and prepare materials for slower learners; seat learners with hearing or vision difficulty at the front; for learners who reverse or confuse letters, trace letters on the letter card with a finger and write with dots to trace with a pencil (manual p.6)."],"components":[{"no":1,"key":"warmup","name":"Warm-up activities","keywords":["Rhyme - 'I caught a Fish Alive'","two learners lead"],"rows":[1]},{"no":2,"key":"oral","name":"Oral Discussion","keywords":["conversation on a picture","every learner speaks"],"rows":[2]},{"no":3,"key":"story","name":"Story","keywords":["Day 1","title / picture talk","read aloud with expression","vocabulary-based questions","re-read pointing","group reading","level tasks"],"rows":[3,4,5]},{"no":4,"key":"sound","name":"Sound symbol games, Sound separation-pairing","keywords":["Jumping on Letters","play in turns","level support"],"rows":[6]},{"no":5,"key":"mindwrite","name":"Mind Mapping (Day 1)","keywords":["mind map: railway station","classify the words","level task: circle letter A / sentences / story"],"rows":[7,8,9]},{"no":6,"key":"reading","name":"Daily reading","keywords":["library book","read alone","teacher listens"],"rows":[10]}],"preLesson":null},{"programme":"TARL Literacy","id":"lit-030","day":30,"phase":1,"phaseLabel":"Phase 1 (Days 1-45)","title":"Saturday: drama presentation","dayType":"Saturday drama + Self-writing","focus":"Hearing the different sounds in words (pig, hat, cup) | Self-writing: the story we acted out (a story about a market day)","duration":70,"objectives":["Listen, speak and answer in the oral conversation (listening and storytelling).","Express a story through role play, using voice, facial expressions and gestures.","Develop sound-symbol skills: Hearing the different sounds in words (pig, hat, cup).","Write about the story and review the writing.","Read independently for 10 minutes every day."],"sequence":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Singing and Spinning","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Learners sit in a circle and pass a small object while you clap with your back turned; when the clapping stops, the learner holding it sings a song, recites a poem or tells a joke. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Pass the object round the circle; sing, recite or tell a joke when the clapping stops.","tlm":"A small object (chalk or pencil)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","n":1},{"activity":"Oral conversation: listening and storytelling","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Tell an interesting story starter and involve the learners: 'My schoolbag started to sing in the middle of the class. What did the teacher say?' Let learners imagine and continue the story.","learners":"Listen to the teacher, then imagine and continue the story. Learners can also recite a rhyme or story they know.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.9","n":2},{"activity":"Dramatic presentation: introduction and reading","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Explain what a dramatic presentation is and how it is done. Provide stories discussed during the week and read one aloud once more. Para and Story level learners support Beginner and Letter level learners in reading.","learners":"Listen, read along, then each learner chooses a character.","tlm":"Stories discussed in the week (a story about a family journey; a story about a market day)","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":3},{"activity":"Dramatic presentation: planning in small groups","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":8,"teacher":"Each group discusses and plans dialogues; Para or Story level learners write the dialogues. Groups prepare their dramatic presentation.","learners":"Choose characters, plan and rehearse dialogues with facial expressions and gestures.","tlm":"Story, paper for dialogues","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":4},{"activity":"Dramatic presentation: performances and feedback","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":7,"teacher":"Learners sit in a U shape. Each group presents; after each performance, watching learners say what they enjoyed and what could be improved.","learners":"Perform in turn; watch; give feedback.","tlm":"Open space (U-shape seating)","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":5},{"activity":"Sound-symbol activity: oral sound awareness","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":4,"teacher":"Say 10-12 simple words aloud ('pig, hat, cup, log, jam, fan, red, bus, sit, map, wet, van') and ask learners to identify the different sounds in them. This builds phonemic awareness.","learners":"Listen to each word and tell its sounds.","tlm":"None (oral activity)","source":"M","ref":"p.12","n":6},{"activity":"Sound-symbol games by level","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":6,"teacher":"Give each level group its game (see level table). Move among the groups and help those who need support; say each word clearly.","learners":"Play the game for their level in small groups.","tlm":"Board, chalk, letter cards","source":"M","ref":"p.12","n":7},{"activity":"Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on the story we acted out (a story about a market day)","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Start a conversation about the story used for the drama: 'the story we acted out (a story about a market day)'. Involve all learners with open-ended questions.","learners":"Take part in the discussion and share thoughts freely.","tlm":"Picture card or topic on the board","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":8},{"activity":"Self-writing: individual writing","grouping":"Individual","minutes":7,"teacher":"Give each level its task (see level table). Let learners take ownership of what they draw and write; mistakes are fine.","learners":"Draw and write about the topic at their level.","tlm":"Notebooks, crayons or pencils","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":9},{"activity":"Self-writing: review and reading back","grouping":"Individual","minutes":3,"teacher":"Ask each learner 'What did you draw or write?' and have them read it aloud once. Word-level learners read to the group; discuss spelling, punctuation and sentence structure. Help beginners by writing their text in the notebook for them if needed.","learners":"Read what they wrote; correct mistakes after listening to their own reading.","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":10},{"activity":"Daily reading (10 minutes)","grouping":"Individual","minutes":10,"teacher":"Give each learner a library book or any storybook. Move around, listen to individual readers and note their level.","learners":"Read independently a book of their choice.","tlm":"Library books or storybooks","source":"M","ref":"p.7","n":11}],"procedures":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Singing and Spinning","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","steps":[{"teacher":"Seat the learners in a circle; give a small object to one learner.","learners":"Sit in a circle."},{"teacher":"Stand outside the circle with your back to them and clap steadily; they pass the object.","learners":"Pass the object while the clapping continues."},{"teacher":"Stop clapping; the learner holding the object sings, recites or tells a joke.","learners":"Perform, and everybody claps."}]},{"activity":"Oral conversation: listening and storytelling","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.9","steps":[{"teacher":"Say the starter: 'My schoolbag started to sing in the middle of the class. What did the teacher say?'","learners":"Listen and imagine."},{"teacher":"Ask learners to continue the story one by one. Encourage those who speak less.","learners":"Add ideas to the story."},{"teacher":"Invite a learner to recite a poem or rhyme they know.","learners":"Recite and listen to others."}]},{"activity":"Saturday special: dramatic presentation","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.11","steps":[{"teacher":"Explain what a dramatic presentation is and how it can be done. Give the groups the stories discussed during the week.","learners":"Listen to the explanation."},{"teacher":"Read a story aloud once more. Learners at story and paragraph level support those at beginner and letter level in reading.","learners":"Read along; helpers support their friends."},{"teacher":"After reading, each learner chooses a character from the story.","learners":"Choose a role (boys may play girl roles and girls may play boy roles)."},{"teacher":"In groups, learners discuss and plan the dialogues; paragraph or story level learners write the dialogues.","learners":"Plan and write dialogues together."},{"teacher":"Learners sit in a U shape. Each group presents its drama. After each performance, ask what the audience enjoyed and what could be improved.","learners":"Perform, watch and give kind feedback."}]},{"activity":"Sound-symbol: oral and level games","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.12","steps":[{"teacher":"Say 10-12 simple words aloud ('pig, hat, cup, log, jam, fan, red, bus, sit, map, wet, van') and ask learners to identify the different sounds in them. This builds phonemic awareness.","learners":"Listen to each word and tell its sounds."},{"teacher":"Write the sounds or words for the day on the board and give each level group its task (see the level table).","learners":"Work in small groups and share their answers."},{"teacher":"Say each word clearly with distinct pronunciation. Give learners enough time to respond and think; use words learners commonly use at home (regional language and the medium of instruction).","learners":"Think, say and write the sounds."}]},{"activity":"Self-writing: 'Discussion, Writing, Self-review'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.15","steps":[{"teacher":"Start a conversation about the story used for the drama: 'the story we acted out (a story about a market day)'. Involve all learners with open-ended questions.","learners":"Discuss and answer questions."},{"teacher":"Give writing time at each level: draw then write (Beginner), write about what they liked (Letter), a sentence (Word), a paragraph or story on a topic of their choice (Para/Story).","learners":"Write at their level and take ownership of the work."},{"teacher":"Review: ask 'What did you draw or write?' Have each learner read the text aloud once. Support with writing if needed.","learners":"Read aloud, listen to their pronunciation and correct mistakes."}]}],"levelTasks":[{"activity":"Drama: roles by level","source":"M","ref":"p.11","tasks":{"Beginner":"Take a character role and say or act short lines with help from Para and Story level learners.","Letter":"Take a character role and say or act short lines with help from Para and Story level learners.","Word":"Take a role and speak the dialogues; help rehearse.","Para":"Write the dialogues for the group and support Beginner, Letter and Word level learners throughout.","Story":"Write the dialogues for the group and support Beginner, Letter and Word level learners throughout."}},{"activity":"Sound-symbol games by level (small groups)","source":"M","ref":"p.12","tasks":{"Beginner":"'What is the first sound in the word tree?' 'Is there a letter that makes the sound /t/?' 'Can you name objects that start with the letter T?' Learners think and share names in the group.","Letter":"Write the rhyming ending -et on the board and ask learners to add new letters to form words: n + et = net, p + et = pet, w + et = wet.","Word":"Say a word and tell its sounds, for example 'sun' = /s/ + /u/ + /n/. Then tell what word is formed if /r/ is put before 'at': r + at = rat. Do 8-10 such combinations; at first learners may form meaningless words, later only meaningful words.","Para":"Write two or three sounds on the board (for example Br, cl, st) and let the learners form words that start with those sounds; this builds a word list for the learner.","Story":"Write two or three sounds on the board (for example Br, cl, st) and let the learners form words that start with those sounds; this builds a word list for the learner."}},{"activity":"Self-writing: level tasks and review","source":"M","ref":"p.15","tasks":{"Beginner":"Draw a picture about the discussion and then write a few sentences about it, expressing thoughts freely. Review: say what they drew or wrote; read the text aloud once; the teacher may write the text in the notebook for them.","Letter":"Write about what they liked, using drawing and writing; write any words or sentences they can. Review: read the text aloud once; correct punctuation mistakes using the Barakhadi chart.","Word":"Write a sentence based on the conversation. Mistakes in spelling, punctuation and sentence structure are fine. Review: read it to the group; discuss and correct mistakes together.","Para":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation.","Story":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation."}}],"organisation":[{"grouping":"Whole class (big group)","how":"All learners of all levels sit in a 'U' shape arranged by level (Beginner, Letter, Word, Para, Story) so that the move to small groups is easy.","activities":["Warm-up: Singing and Spinning","Oral conversation: listening and storytelling","Dramatic presentation: introduction and reading","Dramatic presentation: performances and feedback","Sound-symbol activity: oral sound awareness","Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on the story we acted out (a story about a market day)"]},{"grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","how":"Learners of similar levels work together; the teacher gives each group a task for its level and spends more time with learners who need support. Rotate responsibilities (for example group leader).","activities":["Dramatic presentation: planning in small groups","Sound-symbol games by level"]},{"grouping":"Individual","how":"Each learner works on a task for their own level; the teacher moves around, observes difficulties and supports individuals.","activities":["Self-writing: individual writing","Self-writing: review and reading back","Daily reading (10 minutes)"]}],"materials":["A small object (chalk or pencil)","Stories discussed in the week (a story about a family journey; a story about a market day)","Story","paper for dialogues","Open space (U-shape seating)","Board","chalk","letter cards","Picture card or topic on the board","Notebooks","crayons or pencils","Library books or storybooks"],"outcomes":["Learners take part in the oral conversation and speak without fear.","Learners present a role in the group drama and give feedback to others.","Learners respond to the sound-symbol task for today (Hearing the different sounds in words (pig, hat, cup)) at their own level.","Learners write about the story at their level and read it aloud.","Each learner reads a book for 10 minutes."],"observation":["Observe each learner's reading and writing during the individual tasks; note who needs individual support and how many learners share the same difficulty.","Note any learner whose level is improving; move the learner to the next level group when you see steady progress (manual p.5).","Record each learner's progress for the day in the notebook, according to the learner's level (manual p.4).","Use today's observations to adjust tomorrow's plan (manual p.5)."],"teacherNotes":["Saturday: this plan assumes Day 1 is a Monday (six teaching days per week). If your school week is different, hold the drama presentation on your Saturday and keep the other days in sequence.","Sound-symbol: for the first 4-5 days, play sound-based games with the learners at word level. Include the sounds learners find difficult when you prepare the Class Transaction Plan.","Writing has two parts, content and sequence: encourage learners to read what they wrote, improve it and rewrite it for clarity and correctness (manual p.15).","Level check: if learners have moved up to a new level, celebrate with an appreciation-oriented game (word level to para level): 'Write Sentences from Words' or 'Rearranging Sentences' (manual p.42-45). Teachers may use such activities on their own.","Pace: the manual says not to assume all learners progress at the same speed. Repeat a day's activity with the groups that need it before moving on.","Special needs: give extra time and prepare materials for slower learners; seat learners with hearing or vision difficulty at the front; for learners who reverse or confuse letters, trace letters on the letter card with a finger and write with dots to trace with a pencil (manual p.6)."],"components":[{"no":1,"key":"warmup","name":"Warm-up activities","keywords":["Singing and Spinning","two learners lead"],"rows":[1]},{"no":2,"key":"oral","name":"Oral Discussion","keywords":["listening and storytelling","every learner speaks"],"rows":[2]},{"no":3,"key":"story","name":"Story (Saturday: dramatic presentation)","keywords":["Saturday drama","choose a character","plan dialogues","perform in U shape","feedback"],"rows":[3,4,5]},{"no":4,"key":"sound","name":"Sound symbol games, Sound separation-pairing","keywords":["oral sound awareness","say the different sounds","level games in small groups"],"rows":[6,7]},{"no":5,"key":"mindwrite","name":"Individual-Writing (Day 2)","keywords":["discussion","write at own level","self-review (read aloud)"],"rows":[8,9,10]},{"no":6,"key":"reading","name":"Daily reading","keywords":["library book","read alone","teacher listens"],"rows":[11]}],"preLesson":null},{"programme":"TARL Literacy","id":"lit-031","day":31,"phase":1,"phaseLabel":"Phase 1 (Days 1-45)","title":"Story: a story about a market day (Day 2)","dayType":"Story Day 2 + Self-writing","focus":"Consonant clusters: st (star, stone) | Self-writing: a picture of a farmer at work","duration":70,"objectives":["Listen, speak and answer in the oral conversation (What did you see on your way?).","Retell the story, read it with expression, ask and answer questions about it and write answers.","Develop sound-symbol skills: Consonant clusters: st (star, stone).","Write about a topic at their own level and review the writing (a picture of a farmer at work).","Read independently for 10 minutes every day."],"sequence":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Rain clapping","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Everyone stands in a circle with eyes closed and keeps clapping: first one finger, then two, three, four and finally five fingers. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Stand in a circle, close the eyes and clap with 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 fingers.","tlm":"After the activity ask: What does the rain do to the fields?","source":"M","ref":"p.8","n":1},{"activity":"Oral conversation: What did you see on your way?","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Ask learners to describe what they saw on their way to school. If they are hesitant, begin yourself: 'I saw a shop opening, a bus stopping and a mother holding her child's hand. What did you see?'","learners":"Describe what they saw on the way to school and connect with what others share.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.9","n":2},{"activity":"Story (Day 2 of the story): retelling","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":6,"teacher":"Ask learners to retell yesterday's story in their own words. Prompt with questions on the beginning, middle and end.","learners":"Retell the story using their own words.","tlm":"The same story book as yesterday","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":3},{"activity":"Story: reading with actions and group questions","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":9,"teacher":"Learners practise reading with actions and expressions; one learner per group reads aloud to the class. Guide groups to make questions about the story (guide initially). Groups take turns to ask and answer each other's questions. Word-level learners also read aloud the consonants learned on the first day.","learners":"Read with actions; make questions (word-level learners help write them); ask and answer questions with another group.","tlm":"Story book, slate or paper for questions","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":4},{"activity":"Story: writing answers individually","grouping":"Individual","minutes":5,"teacher":"Para and Story level learners write answers to all questions individually; read and correct their responses after they finish.","learners":"Write the answers in their notebooks; Beginner/Letter/Word learners read or listen and answer orally.","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":5},{"activity":"Consonant clusters: introduction","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":4,"teacher":"Two-letter clusters: after same-letter clusters, familiarise learners with clusters of two different letters ('st' as in star, stone, stand). Discuss the words, ask learners to pronounce them and to frame sentences using them.","learners":"Listen, pronounce the cluster and say words that contain it.","tlm":"Board and chalk, words list (star stone stand stick storm)","source":"M","ref":"p.16","n":6},{"activity":"Consonant cluster game: Looking for Similar Ones","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":6,"teacher":"Write some words with the same conjunct consonants on the board, for example bl, tr, st. Observe closely and help learners who need support.","learners":"Match words that have the same conjunct consonant (black, blue, blanket, blow, blink).","tlm":"Words on the board","source":"M","ref":"p.17","n":7},{"activity":"Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on a picture of a farmer at work","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Start a conversation about a picture card: 'a picture of a farmer at work'. Involve all learners and ask open-ended questions.","learners":"Take part in the discussion and share thoughts freely.","tlm":"Picture card or topic on the board","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":8},{"activity":"Self-writing: individual writing","grouping":"Individual","minutes":7,"teacher":"Give each level its task (see level table). Let learners take ownership of what they draw and write; mistakes are fine.","learners":"Draw and write about the topic at their level.","tlm":"Notebooks, crayons or pencils","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":9},{"activity":"Self-writing: review and reading back","grouping":"Individual","minutes":3,"teacher":"Ask each learner 'What did you draw or write?' and have them read it aloud once. Word-level learners read to the group; discuss spelling, punctuation and sentence structure. Help beginners by writing their text in the notebook for them if needed.","learners":"Read what they wrote; correct mistakes after listening to their own reading.","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":10},{"activity":"Daily reading (10 minutes)","grouping":"Individual","minutes":10,"teacher":"Give each learner a library book or any storybook. Move around, listen to individual readers and note their level.","learners":"Read independently a book of their choice.","tlm":"Library books or storybooks","source":"M","ref":"p.7","n":11}],"procedures":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Rain clapping","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","steps":[{"teacher":"Stand the learners in a circle and ask them to close their eyes. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Stand in a circle and close their eyes."},{"teacher":"Start clapping with one finger; then two fingers, three, four and finally five fingers.","learners":"Keep clapping, copying the change of fingers."},{"teacher":"After the activity ask: What does the rain do to the fields?","learners":"Tell how they felt and what the sounds reminded them of."}]},{"activity":"Oral conversation: What did you see on your way?","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.9","steps":[{"teacher":"Ask: 'What did you see on your way to school today?'","learners":"Think about the way to school."},{"teacher":"If learners hesitate, start: 'I saw a shop opening, a bus stopping and a mother holding her child's hand. What did you see?'","learners":"Listen to the model and then share their own observations."},{"teacher":"Connect learners' answers with each other.","learners":"Listen and add what they noticed."}]},{"activity":"Story - Day 2 (a story about a market day)","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.11","steps":[{"teacher":"Ask learners to retell the story they read yesterday in their own words.","learners":"Retell, helping each other remember."},{"teacher":"In small groups learners practise reading the story using actions and expressions; one learner from each group then reads aloud to the class.","learners":"Read with actions and expression; a representative reads aloud."},{"teacher":"Guide the groups to come up with questions about the story (guide initially). Word-level learners can support by helping write them down.","learners":"Make questions together."},{"teacher":"Groups take turns to ask and answer each other's questions. Useful kinds: questions whose answer is not in the text; questions needing thinking beyond the text; questions asking for an opinion.","learners":"Ask, answer and discuss in the groups."},{"teacher":"Word-level learners also read aloud the consonants they learned on the first day.","learners":"Read the consonant clusters aloud."}]},{"activity":"Consonant clusters (st) and the game 'Looking for Similar Ones'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.16-17","steps":[{"teacher":"Two-letter clusters: after same-letter clusters, familiarise learners with clusters of two different letters ('st' as in star, stone, stand). Discuss the words, ask learners to pronounce them and to frame sentences using them.","learners":"Listen, pronounce and find words in the text."},{"teacher":"Write the words on the board: star stone stand stick storm. Read them aloud with distinct pronunciation of the cluster.","learners":"Read the words aloud; point to the cluster in each word."},{"teacher":"Write some words with the same conjunct consonants on the board, for example bl, tr, st.","learners":"Match words that have the same conjunct consonant (black, blue, blanket, blow, blink)."}]},{"activity":"Self-writing: 'Discussion, Writing, Self-review'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.15","steps":[{"teacher":"Start a conversation about a picture card: 'a picture of a farmer at work'. Involve all learners and ask open-ended questions.","learners":"Discuss and answer questions."},{"teacher":"Give writing time at each level: draw then write (Beginner), write about what they liked (Letter), a sentence (Word), a paragraph or story on a topic of their choice (Para/Story).","learners":"Write at their level and take ownership of the work."},{"teacher":"Review: ask 'What did you draw or write?' Have each learner read the text aloud once. Support with writing if needed.","learners":"Read aloud, listen to their pronunciation and correct mistakes."}]}],"levelTasks":[{"activity":"Story - Day 2: level-wise tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.11","tasks":{"Beginner":"Retell with the group by pointing to pictures or words; read aloud with group support (interpretation of the manual's group reading task).","Letter":"Read with the group, pointing to words; say the letters and words they know (interpretation of the manual's group reading task).","Word":"Support the group in writing the questions; read aloud the consonant clusters learned on the first day.","Para":"Ask the group's questions to another group, discuss them, then write answers to all questions individually; the teacher reads and corrects.","Story":"Ask the group's questions to another group, discuss them, then write answers to all questions individually; the teacher reads and corrects."}},{"activity":"Consonant clusters (st): level tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.16-17","tasks":{"Beginner":"Listen to the sound of the cluster and point to it in a word; continue with letter-sound work (interpretation: the manual describes clusters for learners lagging in reading words and sentences).","Letter":"Listen to the cluster sound and pick words with the cluster from a word card (interpretation).","Word":"Find the cluster in the story or textbook words, read the words and write them in the notebook.","Para":"Form words and sentences using the cluster; read the sentences aloud.","Story":"Form words and sentences using the cluster; read the sentences aloud; use them in the story writing."}},{"activity":"Self-writing: level tasks and review","source":"M","ref":"p.15","tasks":{"Beginner":"Draw a picture about the discussion and then write a few sentences about it, expressing thoughts freely. Review: say what they drew or wrote; read the text aloud once; the teacher may write the text in the notebook for them.","Letter":"Write about what they liked, using drawing and writing; write any words or sentences they can. Review: read the text aloud once; correct punctuation mistakes using the Barakhadi chart.","Word":"Write a sentence based on the conversation. Mistakes in spelling, punctuation and sentence structure are fine. Review: read it to the group; discuss and correct mistakes together.","Para":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation.","Story":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation."}}],"organisation":[{"grouping":"Whole class (big group)","how":"All learners of all levels sit in a 'U' shape arranged by level (Beginner, Letter, Word, Para, Story) so that the move to small groups is easy.","activities":["Warm-up: Rain clapping","Oral conversation: What did you see on your way?","Story (Day 2 of the story): retelling","Consonant clusters: introduction","Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on a picture of a farmer at work"]},{"grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","how":"Learners of similar levels work together; the teacher gives each group a task for its level and spends more time with learners who need support. Rotate responsibilities (for example group leader).","activities":["Story: reading with actions and group questions","Consonant cluster game: Looking for Similar Ones"]},{"grouping":"Individual","how":"Each learner works on a task for their own level; the teacher moves around, observes difficulties and supports individuals.","activities":["Story: writing answers individually","Self-writing: individual writing","Self-writing: review and reading back","Daily reading (10 minutes)"]}],"materials":["After the activity ask: What does the rain do to the fields?","The same story book as yesterday","Story book","slate or paper for questions","Notebooks","Board","chalk","words list (star stone stand stick storm)","Words on the board","Picture card or topic on the board","crayons or pencils","Library books or storybooks"],"outcomes":["Learners take part in the oral conversation and speak without fear.","Learners retell the story, read with expression and ask or answer questions at their level.","Learners respond to the sound-symbol task for today (Consonant clusters: st (star, stone)) at their own level.","Learners write about the topic at their level and read it aloud.","Each learner reads a book for 10 minutes."],"observation":["Observe each learner's reading and writing during the individual tasks; note who needs individual support and how many learners share the same difficulty.","Note any learner whose level is improving; move the learner to the next level group when you see steady progress (manual p.5).","Record each learner's progress for the day in the notebook, according to the learner's level (manual p.4).","Use today's observations to adjust tomorrow's plan (manual p.5)."],"teacherNotes":["Questions to elicit on Day 2: information questions (answer not in the text), thinking questions (needs knowledge beyond the text) and opinion questions (feedback on something in the text).","Consonant clusters: do these activities daily for learners who find reading complex words hard; the aim is to remove the fear of reading clusters. Teachers may carry out similar activities on their own.","Writing has two parts, content and sequence: encourage learners to read what they wrote, improve it and rewrite it for clarity and correctness (manual p.15).","Pace: the manual says not to assume all learners progress at the same speed. Repeat a day's activity with the groups that need it before moving on.","Special needs: give extra time and prepare materials for slower learners; seat learners with hearing or vision difficulty at the front; for learners who reverse or confuse letters, trace letters on the letter card with a finger and write with dots to trace with a pencil (manual p.6)."],"components":[{"no":1,"key":"warmup","name":"Warm-up activities","keywords":["Rain clapping","two learners lead"],"rows":[1]},{"no":2,"key":"oral","name":"Oral Discussion","keywords":["What did you see on your way?","every learner speaks"],"rows":[2]},{"no":3,"key":"story","name":"Story","keywords":["Day 2","retell","read with actions","group questions","ask and answer","write answers (Para/Story)"],"rows":[3,4,5]},{"no":4,"key":"sound","name":"Sound symbol games, Sound separation-pairing","keywords":["consonant cluster 'st'","pronounce and find words","game: Looking for Similar Ones"],"rows":[6,7]},{"no":5,"key":"mindwrite","name":"Individual-Writing (Day 2)","keywords":["discussion","write at own level","self-review (read aloud)"],"rows":[8,9,10]},{"no":6,"key":"reading","name":"Daily reading","keywords":["library book","read alone","teacher listens"],"rows":[11]}],"preLesson":null},{"programme":"TARL Literacy","id":"lit-032","day":32,"phase":1,"phaseLabel":"Phase 1 (Days 1-45)","title":"Story: a story about honesty (Day 1)","dayType":"Story Day 1 + Mind mapping","focus":"Barakhadi / alphabet and phonics chart (line 6, letter 'n') | Mind map: rain","duration":70,"objectives":["Listen, speak and answer in the oral conversation (familiar topic).","Listen to and read a story with understanding; discuss it in big and small groups and respond at their own level.","Develop sound-symbol skills: Barakhadi / alphabet and phonics chart (line 6, letter 'n').","Build vocabulary through a mind map ('rain') and use the words at their own level.","Read independently for 10 minutes every day."],"sequence":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Writing with body parts","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Learners stand in a circle. Demonstrate writing the word 'pen' in the air with a finger, then ask them to write it with different body parts. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Write the word 'pen' in the air with the finger, then with the head, shoulders, knees or elbows.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.8","n":1},{"activity":"Oral conversation: familiar topic","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Hold a conversation on the topic 'my favourite game'. Give each learner a chance to speak; be patient with learners who need extra time.","learners":"Talk about the topic and listen to others.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.9","n":2},{"activity":"Story (Day 1 of the story): reading aloud and discussion","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":8,"teacher":"Discuss the title or picture of the story with the learners. Read the story aloud with expression and voice modulation (learners do not repeat after you). Discuss it, with emphasis on judgment questions. Read it again slowly, pointing to each word.","learners":"Talk about the title/picture; listen; answer questions; follow each word with a finger in their own copy.","tlm":"A story from the school library (a story about honesty), a copy for each learner","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":3},{"activity":"Story: reading in small groups","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":7,"teacher":"Form level-wise groups with a group leader. Learners read the story one sentence at a time while the others follow with their fingers. Para and Story level learners practise reading with emotion and expression.","learners":"Read the story sentence by sentence, supporting each other; the group leader helps.","tlm":"Story book copies","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":4},{"activity":"Story: level-wise individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":5,"teacher":"Give each learner the task for their level (see level table) and support those who need it.","learners":"Beginner/Letter: find and write favourite words or letters. Word: find consonant clusters. Para/Story: silently read, find unfamiliar and rhyming words.","tlm":"Story book, notebooks, board","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":5},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart: big group reading","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":3,"teacher":"Show the Barakhadi chart and ask which letter they like. Read the letter 'n' on the chart; learners listen carefully and point to it on their own chart (they do not repeat after you).","learners":"Listen and point to the letter on their own chart.","tlm":"Barakhadi chart, alphabet or phonics chart","source":"M","ref":"p.13","n":6},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart: small-group practice","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Learners practise reading the alphabet or phonics chart in groups and help each other. One learner per group reads aloud. Occasionally ask learners to identify the sounds of letters. Give each level its group task.","learners":"Read the chart in groups; one learner reads aloud; do the level task.","tlm":"Alphabet or phonics chart, board or floor","source":"M","ref":"p.13","n":7},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart: individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":2,"teacher":"Give each learner an individual task for their level and observe closely; assist any learner who needs individual support.","learners":"Say and write a letter or word, a sentence or a short paragraph (by level).","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.13","n":8},{"activity":"Mind mapping (Day 1): the word 'rain'","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Ask: 'What words come to your mind when you hear the word rain?' Write learners' answers on the board or floor (Para and Story level learners write the words themselves). Guide the map towards the learning objective. Example words: cloud, lightning, puddle, rainbow, umbrella, raincoat, boots, boat, cold, wet, cool, happy.","learners":"Say words connected with 'rain'; share the meaning and feeling of words.","tlm":"Board, chalk (or floor)","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":9},{"activity":"Mind mapping: classify the words","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":4,"teacher":"Ask learners to classify the words in groups, for example: Things we see: cloud, lightning, puddle, rainbow; Things we use: umbrella, raincoat, boots, boat; Things we feel: cold, wet, cool, happy.","learners":"Sort the words into groups and say why.","tlm":"Board, chalk, word cards (optional)","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":10},{"activity":"Mind mapping: level-wise individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":6,"teacher":"Give each learner the individual task for their level; observe closely and give individual support. Display corrected stories on the wall.","learners":"Complete the task for their level (see level table).","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":11},{"activity":"Daily reading (10 minutes)","grouping":"Individual","minutes":10,"teacher":"Give each learner a library book or any storybook. Move around, listen to individual readers and note their level.","learners":"Read independently a book of their choice.","tlm":"Library books or storybooks","source":"M","ref":"p.7","n":12}],"procedures":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Writing with body parts","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","steps":[{"teacher":"Stand the learners in a circle. Demonstrate writing the word 'pen' in the air with your finger.","learners":"Watch and then copy with their own finger."},{"teacher":"Ask them to write it again using nose and other body parts (head, shoulders, knees, ...).","learners":"Write the letters in the air with the named body part."},{"teacher":"Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Take turns to lead."}]},{"activity":"Oral conversation: familiar topic","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.9","steps":[{"teacher":"Introduce the topic: 'my favourite game'.","learners":"Think about their own experience."},{"teacher":"Ask open questions; give every learner a chance. Involve learners who speak less.","learners":"Speak freely and without fear."},{"teacher":"Praise efforts and sum up.","learners":"Listen and respect each other's ideas."}]},{"activity":"Story - Day 1 (a story about honesty)","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.10","steps":[{"teacher":"Discuss the title or picture of the story with the learners.","learners":"Talk about what they see and what the story may be about."},{"teacher":"Read the story aloud with expression and proper voice modulation. Learners should not simply repeat after you.","learners":"Listen carefully and enjoy the story."},{"teacher":"Discuss the story: factual, logical, vocabulary-based, judgment or opinion questions (today's focus: judgment: Was the character right or wrong? Was that a good thing to do? Why?). Begin in the home language if needed.","learners":"Think and respond thoughtfully; every learner takes part."},{"teacher":"Read the story again slowly, pointing to each word. Make sure each learner has a copy and follows with a finger.","learners":"Follow each word with their finger."},{"teacher":"Ask learners to read in small groups; select a group leader who helps the others. Learners read one sentence at a time while the others point with fingers.","learners":"Read with the help of one another."}]},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart activity (line 6)","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Small group (level-wise) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.13","steps":[{"teacher":"Show the Barakhadi chart and ask the learners which letter they like. Where is the letter 'n'?","learners":"Look for the letter on the chart."},{"teacher":"Read the letter 'n' on the chart. Learners listen and point to it on their own chart. Make sure they do not repeat after you.","learners":"Listen and point to the letter."},{"teacher":"Learners read the alphabet or phonics chart in their groups and help each other; one learner from each group comes forward to read aloud.","learners":"Read in groups; the representative reads aloud."},{"teacher":"Occasionally ask them to identify the sounds of letters from the chart.","learners":"Say the sound of the letter you point to."},{"teacher":"As an extra activity, write some letters on the floor, call out each letter one by one and let the learners jump onto the correct letter.","learners":"Jump onto the letter that is called."}]},{"activity":"Mind mapping: 'rain'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Small group (level-wise) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.14","steps":[{"teacher":"Choose a word that can generate many related words: 'rain'. Ask: 'What words come to your mind when you hear the word rain?' Write the answers on the board or floor.","learners":"Say words they link with 'rain'."},{"teacher":"Discuss the words: what they mean and how they are connected.","learners":"Explain their words and listen to others."},{"teacher":"In small groups, let the learners classify the words (Things we see: cloud, lightning, puddle, rainbow; Things we use: umbrella, raincoat, boots, boat; Things we feel: cold, wet, cool, happy).","learners":"Sort the words into groups."},{"teacher":"Give the individual tasks by level and help each learner.","learners":"Work individually; read the work aloud at the end if time allows."}]}],"levelTasks":[{"activity":"Story - Day 1: individual tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.10","tasks":{"Beginner":"Circle or search for a favourite word or letter in the story and say it aloud. If a learner cannot draw a circle, write words on the board and ask them to identify them.","Letter":"Find, read and write favourite words from the story.","Word":"Find the consonant clusters in the story, read them and write them in the notebook.","Para":"Silently read the story from the textbook; find unfamiliar words and try to understand them; find rhyming words, use them in sentences and write in the notebook; ask other groups for meanings; make questions in groups.","Story":"Silently read the story; find unfamiliar words and rhyming words; practise reading with emotion; one group reads sentences formed with consonant clusters to the other group; ask and answer group questions (information, thinking and opinion questions)."}},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart: level tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.13","tasks":{"Beginner":"Small group: read the chart in the group; find and write favourite letters from the line. Individual: say and write a letter of their choice.","Letter":"Small group: read the chart; find and write favourite letters or words from any line. Individual: say a word on their own that begins with any letter.","Word":"Small group: write one or two lines of letters on the board or floor and use them to form words. Individual: speak and write sentences using words they know.","Para":"Small group: prepare word lists using the Barakhadi chart (for example items found in a shop or in the kitchen). Individual: write short paragraphs using the words formed with the Barakhadi chart.","Story":"Small group: prepare word lists using the Barakhadi chart. Individual: write short paragraphs using the words formed with the Barakhadi chart."}},{"activity":"Mind mapping 'rain': level tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.14","tasks":{"Beginner":"Circle all the words that contain the letter 'O' on the board; make a list. See how many learners find the most words.","Letter":"Circle all the words that contain the letter 'O' and make a list of them.","Word":"Use 4-5 words (for example wet, boat, cold, cool, boots) to form sentences, starting with words of one or two syllables. Example: Dream - I had a dream last night.","Para":"Choose any five words from the map and create a story with them. Use consonant clusters correctly, read the story aloud, correct mistakes of sentence structure, spelling or grammar, then display it on the wall.","Story":"Choose any five words from the map and create a story with them. Use consonant clusters correctly, read the story aloud, correct mistakes of sentence structure, spelling or grammar, then display it on the wall."}}],"organisation":[{"grouping":"Whole class (big group)","how":"All learners of all levels sit in a 'U' shape arranged by level (Beginner, Letter, Word, Para, Story) so that the move to small groups is easy.","activities":["Warm-up: Writing with body parts","Oral conversation: familiar topic","Story (Day 1 of the story): reading aloud and discussion","Barakhadi chart: big group reading","Mind mapping (Day 1): the word 'rain'"]},{"grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","how":"Learners of similar levels work together; the teacher gives each group a task for its level and spends more time with learners who need support. Rotate responsibilities (for example group leader).","activities":["Story: reading in small groups","Barakhadi chart: small-group practice","Mind mapping: classify the words"]},{"grouping":"Individual","how":"Each learner works on a task for their own level; the teacher moves around, observes difficulties and supports individuals.","activities":["Story: level-wise individual tasks","Barakhadi chart: individual tasks","Mind mapping: level-wise individual tasks","Daily reading (10 minutes)"]}],"materials":["A story from the school library (a story about honesty)","a copy for each learner","Story book copies","Story book","notebooks","board","Barakhadi chart","alphabet or phonics chart","Alphabet or phonics chart","board or floor","Notebooks","Board","chalk (or floor)","chalk","word cards (optional)","Library books or storybooks"],"outcomes":["Learners take part in the oral conversation and speak without fear.","Learners show understanding of the story in the discussion and complete the task for their level.","Learners respond to the sound-symbol task for today (Barakhadi / alphabet and phonics chart (line 6, letter 'n')) at their own level.","Learners add words to the mind map and use them in sentences or a story at their level.","Each learner reads a book for 10 minutes."],"observation":["Observe each learner's reading and writing during the individual tasks; note who needs individual support and how many learners share the same difficulty.","Note any learner whose level is improving; move the learner to the next level group when you see steady progress (manual p.5).","Record each learner's progress for the day in the notebook, according to the learner's level (manual p.4).","Use today's observations to adjust tomorrow's plan (manual p.5)."],"teacherNotes":["Story selection: the manual asks teachers to use picture story books or stories in the school library. Today's suggested theme (a story about honesty) is a planning suggestion; use any suitable story you have.","Barakhadi: learners who need extra time should get repeated practice using one or two sound units at a time. Topic-based discussion helps oral expression, thinking and understanding.","Mind mapping topic for this day: 'rain'. The manual's example uses the word 'shop'; today's topic follows the same method.","Pace: the manual says not to assume all learners progress at the same speed. Repeat a day's activity with the groups that need it before moving on.","Special needs: give extra time and prepare materials for slower learners; seat learners with hearing or vision difficulty at the front; for learners who reverse or confuse letters, trace letters on the letter card with a finger and write with dots to trace with a pencil (manual p.6)."],"components":[{"no":1,"key":"warmup","name":"Warm-up activities","keywords":["Writing with body parts","two learners lead"],"rows":[1]},{"no":2,"key":"oral","name":"Oral Discussion","keywords":["familiar topic","every learner speaks"],"rows":[2]},{"no":3,"key":"story","name":"Story","keywords":["Day 1","title / picture talk","read aloud with expression","judgment questions","re-read pointing","group reading","level tasks"],"rows":[3,4,5]},{"no":4,"key":"sound","name":"Sound symbol games, Sound separation-pairing","keywords":["Barakhadi / alphabet chart","listen and point (no repeating)","group reading","level tasks"],"rows":[6,7,8]},{"no":5,"key":"mindwrite","name":"Mind Mapping (Day 1)","keywords":["mind map: rain","classify the words","level task: circle letter O / sentences / story"],"rows":[9,10,11]},{"no":6,"key":"reading","name":"Daily reading","keywords":["library book","read alone","teacher listens"],"rows":[12]}],"preLesson":null},{"programme":"TARL Literacy","id":"lit-033","day":33,"phase":1,"phaseLabel":"Phase 1 (Days 1-45)","title":"Story: a story about honesty (Day 2)","dayType":"Story Day 2 + Self-writing","focus":"Language game: The Wind is Blowing | Self-writing: a trip I enjoyed","duration":70,"objectives":["Listen, speak and answer in the oral conversation (conversation on a picture).","Retell the story, read it with expression, ask and answer questions about it and write answers.","Develop sound-symbol skills: Language game: The Wind is Blowing.","Write about a topic at their own level and review the writing (a trip I enjoyed).","Read independently for 10 minutes every day."],"sequence":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Alphabet song (last-letter word chain)","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Say a word to the big group, for example 'tree'. Learners say a word that starts with the last letter ('e'). A learner who cannot say a word is out. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Say a word that starts with the last letter of the previous word; step out if unable to.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.8","n":1},{"activity":"Oral conversation: conversation on a picture","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Show a picture of a tea garden with pickers and ask what is happening, who is doing what and what is happening around them. Let learners think creatively and even make up a story.","learners":"Look at the picture, answer questions and make up their own story about it.","tlm":"Picture card of a tea garden with pickers","source":"M","ref":"p.9","n":2},{"activity":"Story (Day 2 of the story): retelling","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":6,"teacher":"Ask learners to retell yesterday's story in their own words. Prompt with questions on the beginning, middle and end.","learners":"Retell the story using their own words.","tlm":"The same story book as yesterday","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":3},{"activity":"Story: reading with actions and group questions","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":9,"teacher":"Learners practise reading with actions and expressions; one learner per group reads aloud to the class. Guide groups to make questions about the story (guide initially). Groups take turns to ask and answer each other's questions. Word-level learners also read aloud the consonants learned on the first day.","learners":"Read with actions; make questions (word-level learners help write them); ask and answer questions with another group.","tlm":"Story book, slate or paper for questions","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":4},{"activity":"Story: writing answers individually","grouping":"Individual","minutes":5,"teacher":"Para and Story level learners write answers to all questions individually; read and correct their responses after they finish.","learners":"Write the answers in their notebooks; Beginner/Letter/Word learners read or listen and answer orally.","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":5},{"activity":"Language game: The Wind is Blowing","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Learners hold a secret letter card; the one whose letter the teacher names says words beginning with it. Observe each learner and give help where needed.","learners":"Play the game, take turns and read or say the words they make.","tlm":"Letter flashcards","source":"M","ref":"p.19","n":6},{"activity":"Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on a trip I enjoyed","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Start a conversation about a topic: 'a trip I enjoyed'. Involve all learners and ask open-ended questions.","learners":"Take part in the discussion and share thoughts freely.","tlm":"Picture card or topic on the board","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":7},{"activity":"Self-writing: individual writing","grouping":"Individual","minutes":7,"teacher":"Give each level its task (see level table). Let learners take ownership of what they draw and write; mistakes are fine.","learners":"Draw and write about the topic at their level.","tlm":"Notebooks, crayons or pencils","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":8},{"activity":"Self-writing: review and reading back","grouping":"Individual","minutes":3,"teacher":"Ask each learner 'What did you draw or write?' and have them read it aloud once. Word-level learners read to the group; discuss spelling, punctuation and sentence structure. Help beginners by writing their text in the notebook for them if needed.","learners":"Read what they wrote; correct mistakes after listening to their own reading.","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":9},{"activity":"Daily reading (10 minutes)","grouping":"Individual","minutes":10,"teacher":"Give each learner a library book or any storybook. Move around, listen to individual readers and note their level.","learners":"Read independently a book of their choice.","tlm":"Library books or storybooks","source":"M","ref":"p.7","n":10}],"procedures":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Alphabet song (last-letter word chain)","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","steps":[{"teacher":"Say the word 'tree' to the big group and show that its last letter is 'e'.","learners":"Listen and think of a word starting with 'e'."},{"teacher":"Ask learners in turn to say a word that starts with the last letter of the previous word. Example: rain -> nest.","learners":"Say a word in turn; anyone who cannot say a word is out of the game."},{"teacher":"Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Lead the game when it is their turn."}]},{"activity":"Oral conversation: conversation on a picture","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.9","steps":[{"teacher":"Show the picture of a tea garden with pickers.","learners":"Look carefully."},{"teacher":"Ask: What is happening in the picture? Who is doing what? What is happening around them? Then: What might happen next?","learners":"Answer in their own words; every learner gets a chance."},{"teacher":"Let learners imagine and make up a short story from the picture.","learners":"Tell their stories to the class."}]},{"activity":"Story - Day 2 (a story about honesty)","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.11","steps":[{"teacher":"Ask learners to retell the story they read yesterday in their own words.","learners":"Retell, helping each other remember."},{"teacher":"In small groups learners practise reading the story using actions and expressions; one learner from each group then reads aloud to the class.","learners":"Read with actions and expression; a representative reads aloud."},{"teacher":"Guide the groups to come up with questions about the story (guide initially). Word-level learners can support by helping write them down.","learners":"Make questions together."},{"teacher":"Groups take turns to ask and answer each other's questions. Useful kinds: questions whose answer is not in the text; questions needing thinking beyond the text; questions asking for an opinion.","learners":"Ask, answer and discuss in the groups."},{"teacher":"Word-level learners also read aloud the consonants they learned on the first day.","learners":"Read the consonant clusters aloud."}]},{"activity":"Language game: The Wind is Blowing","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.19","steps":[{"teacher":"Stand all learners in a circle and give each one a letter flashcard, which they must not show to anyone.","learners":"Hold the card against the chest; do not show it."},{"teacher":"Say: 'The wind is blowing.' Learners answer: 'Which way is it blowing?' Say: 'The wind is blowing towards T.'","learners":"Reply together; the learner with the letter T steps to the centre."},{"teacher":"Ask the learner in the centre to say a few words that start with T. Continue with other letters.","learners":"Say words such as tree, tiger, toy."}]},{"activity":"Self-writing: 'Discussion, Writing, Self-review'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.15","steps":[{"teacher":"Start a conversation about a topic: 'a trip I enjoyed'. Involve all learners and ask open-ended questions.","learners":"Discuss and answer questions."},{"teacher":"Give writing time at each level: draw then write (Beginner), write about what they liked (Letter), a sentence (Word), a paragraph or story on a topic of their choice (Para/Story).","learners":"Write at their level and take ownership of the work."},{"teacher":"Review: ask 'What did you draw or write?' Have each learner read the text aloud once. Support with writing if needed.","learners":"Read aloud, listen to their pronunciation and correct mistakes."}]}],"levelTasks":[{"activity":"Story - Day 2: level-wise tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.11","tasks":{"Beginner":"Retell with the group by pointing to pictures or words; read aloud with group support (interpretation of the manual's group reading task).","Letter":"Read with the group, pointing to words; say the letters and words they know (interpretation of the manual's group reading task).","Word":"Support the group in writing the questions; read aloud the consonant clusters learned on the first day.","Para":"Ask the group's questions to another group, discuss them, then write answers to all questions individually; the teacher reads and corrects.","Story":"Ask the group's questions to another group, discuss them, then write answers to all questions individually; the teacher reads and corrects."}},{"activity":"Language game: The Wind is Blowing - level support","source":"I","ref":"p.19","tasks":{"Beginner":"Take part by saying or pointing to the letters involved and by listening carefully; Para and Story level partners help.","Letter":"Say the letters/sounds and give simple words they know.","Word":"Say and write words and short sentences for the game.","Para":"Write sentences with the words; help groups to record answers.","Story":"Write sentences or short stories with the words; help groups to record answers."}},{"activity":"Self-writing: level tasks and review","source":"M","ref":"p.15","tasks":{"Beginner":"Draw a picture about the discussion and then write a few sentences about it, expressing thoughts freely. Review: say what they drew or wrote; read the text aloud once; the teacher may write the text in the notebook for them.","Letter":"Write about what they liked, using drawing and writing; write any words or sentences they can. Review: read the text aloud once; correct punctuation mistakes using the Barakhadi chart.","Word":"Write a sentence based on the conversation. Mistakes in spelling, punctuation and sentence structure are fine. Review: read it to the group; discuss and correct mistakes together.","Para":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation.","Story":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation."}}],"organisation":[{"grouping":"Whole class (big group)","how":"All learners of all levels sit in a 'U' shape arranged by level (Beginner, Letter, Word, Para, Story) so that the move to small groups is easy.","activities":["Warm-up: Alphabet song (last-letter word chain)","Oral conversation: conversation on a picture","Story (Day 2 of the story): retelling","Language game: The Wind is Blowing","Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on a trip I enjoyed"]},{"grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","how":"Learners of similar levels work together; the teacher gives each group a task for its level and spends more time with learners who need support. Rotate responsibilities (for example group leader).","activities":["Story: reading with actions and group questions"]},{"grouping":"Individual","how":"Each learner works on a task for their own level; the teacher moves around, observes difficulties and supports individuals.","activities":["Story: writing answers individually","Self-writing: individual writing","Self-writing: review and reading back","Daily reading (10 minutes)"]}],"materials":["Picture card of a tea garden with pickers","The same story book as yesterday","Story book","slate or paper for questions","Notebooks","Letter flashcards","Picture card or topic on the board","crayons or pencils","Library books or storybooks"],"outcomes":["Learners take part in the oral conversation and speak without fear.","Learners retell the story, read with expression and ask or answer questions at their level.","Learners respond to the sound-symbol task for today (Language game: The Wind is Blowing) at their own level.","Learners write about the topic at their level and read it aloud.","Each learner reads a book for 10 minutes."],"observation":["Observe each learner's reading and writing during the individual tasks; note who needs individual support and how many learners share the same difficulty.","Note any learner whose level is improving; move the learner to the next level group when you see steady progress (manual p.5).","Record each learner's progress for the day in the notebook, according to the learner's level (manual p.4).","Use today's observations to adjust tomorrow's plan (manual p.5)."],"teacherNotes":["Questions to elicit on Day 2: information questions (answer not in the text), thinking questions (needs knowledge beyond the text) and opinion questions (feedback on something in the text).","The manual lists the letter and word games but does not fix the slot in the daily timetable where they are used. This plan places them in the 10-minute sound-symbol / alphabet slot (interpretation).","Writing has two parts, content and sequence: encourage learners to read what they wrote, improve it and rewrite it for clarity and correctness (manual p.15).","Pace: the manual says not to assume all learners progress at the same speed. Repeat a day's activity with the groups that need it before moving on.","Special needs: give extra time and prepare materials for slower learners; seat learners with hearing or vision difficulty at the front; for learners who reverse or confuse letters, trace letters on the letter card with a finger and write with dots to trace with a pencil (manual p.6)."],"components":[{"no":1,"key":"warmup","name":"Warm-up activities","keywords":["Alphabet song (last-letter word chain)","two learners lead"],"rows":[1]},{"no":2,"key":"oral","name":"Oral Discussion","keywords":["conversation on a picture","every learner speaks"],"rows":[2]},{"no":3,"key":"story","name":"Story","keywords":["Day 2","retell","read with actions","group questions","ask and answer","write answers (Para/Story)"],"rows":[3,4,5]},{"no":4,"key":"sound","name":"Sound symbol games, Sound separation-pairing","keywords":["The Wind is Blowing","play in turns","level support"],"rows":[6]},{"no":5,"key":"mindwrite","name":"Individual-Writing (Day 2)","keywords":["discussion","write at own level","self-review (read aloud)"],"rows":[7,8,9]},{"no":6,"key":"reading","name":"Daily reading","keywords":["library book","read alone","teacher listens"],"rows":[10]}],"preLesson":null},{"programme":"TARL Literacy","id":"lit-034","day":34,"phase":1,"phaseLabel":"Phase 1 (Days 1-45)","title":"Story: a story about a forest and its animals (Day 1)","dayType":"Story Day 1 + Mind mapping","focus":"Consonant clusters: sw (swim, sweet) | Mind map: summer","duration":70,"objectives":["Listen, speak and answer in the oral conversation (listening and storytelling).","Listen to and read a story with understanding; discuss it in big and small groups and respond at their own level.","Develop sound-symbol skills: Consonant clusters: sw (swim, sweet).","Build vocabulary through a mind map ('summer') and use the words at their own level.","Read independently for 10 minutes every day."],"sequence":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Handkerchief game","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Learners sit in a circle and clap while singing a rhyme ('I caught a Fish Alive'). One learner runs outside the circle with a handkerchief and secretly places it behind another learner, who must chase the runner. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Sit in a circle, clap and sing; run, place the handkerchief or chase as the game requires.","tlm":"A handkerchief","source":"M","ref":"p.8","n":1},{"activity":"Oral conversation: listening and storytelling","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Tell an interesting story starter and involve the learners: 'A small bird knocked on my door and asked for a story. Which story did I tell?' Let learners imagine and continue the story.","learners":"Listen to the teacher, then imagine and continue the story. Learners can also recite a rhyme or story they know.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.9","n":2},{"activity":"Story (Day 1 of the story): reading aloud and discussion","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":8,"teacher":"Discuss the title or picture of the story with the learners. Read the story aloud with expression and voice modulation (learners do not repeat after you). Discuss it, with emphasis on opinion questions. Read it again slowly, pointing to each word.","learners":"Talk about the title/picture; listen; answer questions; follow each word with a finger in their own copy.","tlm":"A story from the school library (a story about a forest and its animals), a copy for each learner","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":3},{"activity":"Story: reading in small groups","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":7,"teacher":"Form level-wise groups with a group leader. Learners read the story one sentence at a time while the others follow with their fingers. Para and Story level learners practise reading with emotion and expression.","learners":"Read the story sentence by sentence, supporting each other; the group leader helps.","tlm":"Story book copies","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":4},{"activity":"Story: level-wise individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":5,"teacher":"Give each learner the task for their level (see level table) and support those who need it.","learners":"Beginner/Letter: find and write favourite words or letters. Word: find consonant clusters. Para/Story: silently read, find unfamiliar and rhyming words.","tlm":"Story book, notebooks, board","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":5},{"activity":"Consonant clusters: introduction","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":4,"teacher":"Two-letter clusters: after same-letter clusters, familiarise learners with clusters of two different letters ('sw' as in swim, sweet, swing). Discuss the words, ask learners to pronounce them and to frame sentences using them.","learners":"Listen, pronounce the cluster and say words that contain it.","tlm":"Board and chalk, words list (swim sweet swing sweep swan)","source":"M","ref":"p.16","n":6},{"activity":"Consonant cluster game: Who is Whose Friend?","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":6,"teacher":"Prepare cards: some with broken parts of conjunct consonants (b + l, c + r, s + t) and some with the full form (bl as in black, cr as in crab, st as in star). Take out all the cards. Observe closely and help learners who need support.","learners":"Match each full form with its broken parts and discover 'who is whose friend'.","tlm":"Broken-part cards and full-form cards","source":"M","ref":"p.17","n":7},{"activity":"Mind mapping (Day 1): the word 'summer'","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Ask: 'What words come to your mind when you hear the word summer?' Write learners' answers on the board or floor (Para and Story level learners write the words themselves). Guide the map towards the learning objective. Example words: mango, ice cream, lemon water, watermelon, cap, cotton, shorts, sandals, fan, sun, shade, sweat.","learners":"Say words connected with 'summer'; share the meaning and feeling of words.","tlm":"Board, chalk (or floor)","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":8},{"activity":"Mind mapping: classify the words","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":4,"teacher":"Ask learners to classify the words in groups, for example: Foods: mango, ice cream, lemon water, watermelon; Clothes: cap, cotton, shorts, sandals; Things: fan, sun, shade, sweat.","learners":"Sort the words into groups and say why.","tlm":"Board, chalk, word cards (optional)","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":9},{"activity":"Mind mapping: level-wise individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":6,"teacher":"Give each learner the individual task for their level; observe closely and give individual support. Display corrected stories on the wall.","learners":"Complete the task for their level (see level table).","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":10},{"activity":"Daily reading (10 minutes)","grouping":"Individual","minutes":10,"teacher":"Give each learner a library book or any storybook. Move around, listen to individual readers and note their level.","learners":"Read independently a book of their choice.","tlm":"Library books or storybooks","source":"M","ref":"p.7","n":11}],"procedures":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Handkerchief game","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","steps":[{"teacher":"Seat the learners in a circle and start clapping and singing the rhyme 'I caught a Fish Alive'.","learners":"Clap and sing together."},{"teacher":"One learner runs outside the circle holding a handkerchief and secretly places it behind another learner.","learners":"Everyone keeps clapping; the learner who finds the handkerchief behind them takes it and chases the runner."},{"teacher":"If the runner sits in the chaser's place before being caught, they stay in the game; if caught, they are out. Continue in this way.","learners":"Play fairly and take turns."}]},{"activity":"Oral conversation: listening and storytelling","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.9","steps":[{"teacher":"Say the starter: 'A small bird knocked on my door and asked for a story. Which story did I tell?'","learners":"Listen and imagine."},{"teacher":"Ask learners to continue the story one by one. Encourage those who speak less.","learners":"Add ideas to the story."},{"teacher":"Invite a learner to recite a poem or rhyme they know.","learners":"Recite and listen to others."}]},{"activity":"Story - Day 1 (a story about a forest and its animals)","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.10","steps":[{"teacher":"Discuss the title or picture of the story with the learners.","learners":"Talk about what they see and what the story may be about."},{"teacher":"Read the story aloud with expression and proper voice modulation. Learners should not simply repeat after you.","learners":"Listen carefully and enjoy the story."},{"teacher":"Discuss the story: factual, logical, vocabulary-based, judgment or opinion questions (today's focus: opinion: What did you like best? What would you have done in the story?). Begin in the home language if needed.","learners":"Think and respond thoughtfully; every learner takes part."},{"teacher":"Read the story again slowly, pointing to each word. Make sure each learner has a copy and follows with a finger.","learners":"Follow each word with their finger."},{"teacher":"Ask learners to read in small groups; select a group leader who helps the others. Learners read one sentence at a time while the others point with fingers.","learners":"Read with the help of one another."}]},{"activity":"Consonant clusters (sw) and the game 'Who is Whose Friend?'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.16-17","steps":[{"teacher":"Two-letter clusters: after same-letter clusters, familiarise learners with clusters of two different letters ('sw' as in swim, sweet, swing). Discuss the words, ask learners to pronounce them and to frame sentences using them.","learners":"Listen, pronounce and find words in the text."},{"teacher":"Write the words on the board: swim sweet swing sweep swan. Read them aloud with distinct pronunciation of the cluster.","learners":"Read the words aloud; point to the cluster in each word."},{"teacher":"Prepare cards: some with broken parts of conjunct consonants (b + l, c + r, s + t) and some with the full form (bl as in black, cr as in crab, st as in star). Take out all the cards.","learners":"Match each full form with its broken parts and discover 'who is whose friend'."}]},{"activity":"Mind mapping: 'summer'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Small group (level-wise) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.14","steps":[{"teacher":"Choose a word that can generate many related words: 'summer'. Ask: 'What words come to your mind when you hear the word summer?' Write the answers on the board or floor.","learners":"Say words they link with 'summer'."},{"teacher":"Discuss the words: what they mean and how they are connected.","learners":"Explain their words and listen to others."},{"teacher":"In small groups, let the learners classify the words (Foods: mango, ice cream, lemon water, watermelon; Clothes: cap, cotton, shorts, sandals; Things: fan, sun, shade, sweat).","learners":"Sort the words into groups."},{"teacher":"Give the individual tasks by level and help each learner.","learners":"Work individually; read the work aloud at the end if time allows."}]}],"levelTasks":[{"activity":"Story - Day 1: individual tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.10","tasks":{"Beginner":"Circle or search for a favourite word or letter in the story and say it aloud. If a learner cannot draw a circle, write words on the board and ask them to identify them.","Letter":"Find, read and write favourite words from the story.","Word":"Find the consonant clusters in the story, read them and write them in the notebook.","Para":"Silently read the story from the textbook; find unfamiliar words and try to understand them; find rhyming words, use them in sentences and write in the notebook; ask other groups for meanings; make questions in groups.","Story":"Silently read the story; find unfamiliar words and rhyming words; practise reading with emotion; one group reads sentences formed with consonant clusters to the other group; ask and answer group questions (information, thinking and opinion questions)."}},{"activity":"Consonant clusters (sw): level tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.16-17","tasks":{"Beginner":"Listen to the sound of the cluster and point to it in a word; continue with letter-sound work (interpretation: the manual describes clusters for learners lagging in reading words and sentences).","Letter":"Listen to the cluster sound and pick words with the cluster from a word card (interpretation).","Word":"Find the cluster in the story or textbook words, read the words and write them in the notebook.","Para":"Form words and sentences using the cluster; read the sentences aloud.","Story":"Form words and sentences using the cluster; read the sentences aloud; use them in the story writing."}},{"activity":"Mind mapping 'summer': level tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.14","tasks":{"Beginner":"Circle all the words that contain the letter 'A' on the board; make a list. See how many learners find the most words.","Letter":"Circle all the words that contain the letter 'A' and make a list of them.","Word":"Use 4-5 words (for example cap, fan, sun, mango, shade) to form sentences, starting with words of one or two syllables. Example: Dream - I had a dream last night.","Para":"Choose any five words from the map and create a story with them. Use consonant clusters correctly, read the story aloud, correct mistakes of sentence structure, spelling or grammar, then display it on the wall.","Story":"Choose any five words from the map and create a story with them. Use consonant clusters correctly, read the story aloud, correct mistakes of sentence structure, spelling or grammar, then display it on the wall."}}],"organisation":[{"grouping":"Whole class (big group)","how":"All learners of all levels sit in a 'U' shape arranged by level (Beginner, Letter, Word, Para, Story) so that the move to small groups is easy.","activities":["Warm-up: Handkerchief game","Oral conversation: listening and storytelling","Story (Day 1 of the story): reading aloud and discussion","Consonant clusters: introduction","Mind mapping (Day 1): the word 'summer'"]},{"grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","how":"Learners of similar levels work together; the teacher gives each group a task for its level and spends more time with learners who need support. Rotate responsibilities (for example group leader).","activities":["Story: reading in small groups","Consonant cluster game: Who is Whose Friend?","Mind mapping: classify the words"]},{"grouping":"Individual","how":"Each learner works on a task for their own level; the teacher moves around, observes difficulties and supports individuals.","activities":["Story: level-wise individual tasks","Mind mapping: level-wise individual tasks","Daily reading (10 minutes)"]}],"materials":["A handkerchief","A story from the school library (a story about a forest","its animals)","a copy for each learner","Story book copies","Story book","notebooks","board","Board","chalk","words list (swim sweet swing sweep swan)","Broken-part cards","full-form cards","chalk (or floor)","word cards (optional)","Notebooks","Library books or storybooks"],"outcomes":["Learners take part in the oral conversation and speak without fear.","Learners show understanding of the story in the discussion and complete the task for their level.","Learners respond to the sound-symbol task for today (Consonant clusters: sw (swim, sweet)) at their own level.","Learners add words to the mind map and use them in sentences or a story at their level.","Each learner reads a book for 10 minutes."],"observation":["Observe each learner's reading and writing during the individual tasks; note who needs individual support and how many learners share the same difficulty.","Note any learner whose level is improving; move the learner to the next level group when you see steady progress (manual p.5).","Record each learner's progress for the day in the notebook, according to the learner's level (manual p.4).","Use today's observations to adjust tomorrow's plan (manual p.5)."],"teacherNotes":["Story selection: the manual asks teachers to use picture story books or stories in the school library. Today's suggested theme (a story about a forest and its animals) is a planning suggestion; use any suitable story you have.","Consonant clusters: do these activities daily for learners who find reading complex words hard; the aim is to remove the fear of reading clusters. Teachers may carry out similar activities on their own.","Mind mapping topic for this day: 'summer'. The manual's example uses the word 'shop'; today's topic follows the same method.","Pace: the manual says not to assume all learners progress at the same speed. Repeat a day's activity with the groups that need it before moving on.","Special needs: give extra time and prepare materials for slower learners; seat learners with hearing or vision difficulty at the front; for learners who reverse or confuse letters, trace letters on the letter card with a finger and write with dots to trace with a pencil (manual p.6)."],"components":[{"no":1,"key":"warmup","name":"Warm-up activities","keywords":["Handkerchief game","two learners lead"],"rows":[1]},{"no":2,"key":"oral","name":"Oral Discussion","keywords":["listening and storytelling","every learner speaks"],"rows":[2]},{"no":3,"key":"story","name":"Story","keywords":["Day 1","title / picture talk","read aloud with expression","opinion questions","re-read pointing","group reading","level tasks"],"rows":[3,4,5]},{"no":4,"key":"sound","name":"Sound symbol games, Sound separation-pairing","keywords":["consonant cluster 'sw'","pronounce and find words","game: Who is Whose Friend?"],"rows":[6,7]},{"no":5,"key":"mindwrite","name":"Mind Mapping (Day 1)","keywords":["mind map: summer","classify the words","level task: circle letter A / sentences / story"],"rows":[8,9,10]},{"no":6,"key":"reading","name":"Daily reading","keywords":["library book","read alone","teacher listens"],"rows":[11]}],"preLesson":null},{"programme":"TARL Literacy","id":"lit-035","day":35,"phase":1,"phaseLabel":"Phase 1 (Days 1-45)","title":"Story: a story about a forest and its animals (Day 2)","dayType":"Story Day 2 + Self-writing","focus":"Identifying the first, second and last sound (dog, sun, pig) | Self-writing: my family","duration":70,"objectives":["Listen, speak and answer in the oral conversation (What did you see on your way?).","Retell the story, read it with expression, ask and answer questions about it and write answers.","Develop sound-symbol skills: Identifying the first, second and last sound (dog, sun, pig).","Write about a topic at their own level and review the writing (my family).","Read independently for 10 minutes every day."],"sequence":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Rhyme - 'I saw a Little Bird'","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Say the rhyme with actions, then say it together. Lines: I saw a little bird go hop, hop, hop / I told the little bird to stop, stop, stop. / I went to the window to say 'How do you do?' / He wagged his little tail and far away he flew! Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Listen, then say the rhyme with actions.","tlm":"Rhyme chart or board (optional)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","n":1},{"activity":"Oral conversation: What did you see on your way?","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Ask learners to describe what they saw on their way to school. If they are hesitant, begin yourself: 'When I arrived today, I saw two cats chasing each other, a farmer ploughing in the field, and goats grazing on the river bank. What did you see?'","learners":"Describe what they saw on the way to school and connect with what others share.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.9","n":2},{"activity":"Story (Day 2 of the story): retelling","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":6,"teacher":"Ask learners to retell yesterday's story in their own words. Prompt with questions on the beginning, middle and end.","learners":"Retell the story using their own words.","tlm":"The same story book as yesterday","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":3},{"activity":"Story: reading with actions and group questions","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":9,"teacher":"Learners practise reading with actions and expressions; one learner per group reads aloud to the class. Guide groups to make questions about the story (guide initially). Groups take turns to ask and answer each other's questions. Word-level learners also read aloud the consonants learned on the first day.","learners":"Read with actions; make questions (word-level learners help write them); ask and answer questions with another group.","tlm":"Story book, slate or paper for questions","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":4},{"activity":"Story: writing answers individually","grouping":"Individual","minutes":5,"teacher":"Para and Story level learners write answers to all questions individually; read and correct their responses after they finish.","learners":"Write the answers in their notebooks; Beginner/Letter/Word learners read or listen and answer orally.","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":5},{"activity":"Sound-symbol activity: oral sound awareness","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":4,"teacher":"Say words and ask learners to identify the first, second or last sound. Example: pan - first sound p, second sound a, third sound n; log: l, o, g; cup: c, u, p.","learners":"Say the first, second or last sound of the word.","tlm":"None (oral activity)","source":"M","ref":"p.12","n":6},{"activity":"Sound-symbol games by level","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":6,"teacher":"Give each level group its game (see level table). Move among the groups and help those who need support; say each word clearly.","learners":"Play the game for their level in small groups.","tlm":"Board, chalk, letter cards","source":"M","ref":"p.12","n":7},{"activity":"Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on my family","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Start a conversation about a situation: 'my family'. Involve all learners and ask open-ended questions.","learners":"Take part in the discussion and share thoughts freely.","tlm":"Picture card or topic on the board","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":8},{"activity":"Self-writing: individual writing","grouping":"Individual","minutes":7,"teacher":"Give each level its task (see level table). Let learners take ownership of what they draw and write; mistakes are fine.","learners":"Draw and write about the topic at their level.","tlm":"Notebooks, crayons or pencils","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":9},{"activity":"Self-writing: review and reading back","grouping":"Individual","minutes":3,"teacher":"Ask each learner 'What did you draw or write?' and have them read it aloud once. Word-level learners read to the group; discuss spelling, punctuation and sentence structure. Help beginners by writing their text in the notebook for them if needed.","learners":"Read what they wrote; correct mistakes after listening to their own reading.","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":10},{"activity":"Daily reading (10 minutes)","grouping":"Individual","minutes":10,"teacher":"Give each learner a library book or any storybook. Move around, listen to individual readers and note their level.","learners":"Read independently a book of their choice.","tlm":"Library books or storybooks","source":"M","ref":"p.7","n":11}],"procedures":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Rhyme - 'I saw a Little Bird'","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","steps":[{"teacher":"Say the rhyme 'I saw a Little Bird' slowly with actions: I saw a little bird go hop, hop, hop / I told the little bird to stop, stop, stop. / I went to the window to say 'How do you do?' / He wagged his little tail and far away he flew!","learners":"Listen and watch the actions."},{"teacher":"Say it again; invite learners to join with actions.","learners":"Say the rhyme together with actions."},{"teacher":"Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Choose a rhyme they like and lead."}]},{"activity":"Oral conversation: What did you see on your way?","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.9","steps":[{"teacher":"Ask: 'What did you see on your way to school today?'","learners":"Think about the way to school."},{"teacher":"If learners hesitate, start: 'When I arrived today, I saw two cats chasing each other, a farmer ploughing in the field, and goats grazing on the river bank. What did you see?'","learners":"Listen to the model and then share their own observations."},{"teacher":"Connect learners' answers with each other.","learners":"Listen and add what they noticed."}]},{"activity":"Story - Day 2 (a story about a forest and its animals)","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.11","steps":[{"teacher":"Ask learners to retell the story they read yesterday in their own words.","learners":"Retell, helping each other remember."},{"teacher":"In small groups learners practise reading the story using actions and expressions; one learner from each group then reads aloud to the class.","learners":"Read with actions and expression; a representative reads aloud."},{"teacher":"Guide the groups to come up with questions about the story (guide initially). Word-level learners can support by helping write them down.","learners":"Make questions together."},{"teacher":"Groups take turns to ask and answer each other's questions. Useful kinds: questions whose answer is not in the text; questions needing thinking beyond the text; questions asking for an opinion.","learners":"Ask, answer and discuss in the groups."},{"teacher":"Word-level learners also read aloud the consonants they learned on the first day.","learners":"Read the consonant clusters aloud."}]},{"activity":"Sound-symbol: oral and level games","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.12","steps":[{"teacher":"Say words and ask learners to identify the first, second or last sound. Example: pan - first sound p, second sound a, third sound n; log: l, o, g; cup: c, u, p.","learners":"Say the first, second or last sound of the word."},{"teacher":"Write the sounds or words for the day on the board and give each level group its task (see the level table).","learners":"Work in small groups and share their answers."},{"teacher":"Say each word clearly with distinct pronunciation. Give learners enough time to respond and think; use words learners commonly use at home (regional language and the medium of instruction).","learners":"Think, say and write the sounds."}]},{"activity":"Self-writing: 'Discussion, Writing, Self-review'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.15","steps":[{"teacher":"Start a conversation about a situation: 'my family'. Involve all learners and ask open-ended questions.","learners":"Discuss and answer questions."},{"teacher":"Give writing time at each level: draw then write (Beginner), write about what they liked (Letter), a sentence (Word), a paragraph or story on a topic of their choice (Para/Story).","learners":"Write at their level and take ownership of the work."},{"teacher":"Review: ask 'What did you draw or write?' Have each learner read the text aloud once. Support with writing if needed.","learners":"Read aloud, listen to their pronunciation and correct mistakes."}]}],"levelTasks":[{"activity":"Story - Day 2: level-wise tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.11","tasks":{"Beginner":"Retell with the group by pointing to pictures or words; read aloud with group support (interpretation of the manual's group reading task).","Letter":"Read with the group, pointing to words; say the letters and words they know (interpretation of the manual's group reading task).","Word":"Support the group in writing the questions; read aloud the consonant clusters learned on the first day.","Para":"Ask the group's questions to another group, discuss them, then write answers to all questions individually; the teacher reads and corrects.","Story":"Ask the group's questions to another group, discuss them, then write answers to all questions individually; the teacher reads and corrects."}},{"activity":"Sound-symbol games by level (small groups)","source":"M","ref":"p.12","tasks":{"Beginner":"'What is the first sound in the word apple?' 'Is there a letter that makes the sound /a/?' 'Can you name objects that start with the letter A?' Learners think and share names in the group.","Letter":"Write the rhyming ending -in on the board and ask learners to add new letters to form words: p + in = pin, b + in = bin, f + in = fin.","Word":"Say a word and tell its sounds, for example 'sun' = /s/ + /u/ + /n/. Then tell what word is formed if /r/ is put before 'at': r + at = rat. Do 8-10 such combinations; at first learners may form meaningless words, later only meaningful words.","Para":"Write two or three sounds on the board (for example Br, cl, st) and let the learners form words that start with those sounds; this builds a word list for the learner.","Story":"Write two or three sounds on the board (for example Br, cl, st) and let the learners form words that start with those sounds; this builds a word list for the learner."}},{"activity":"Self-writing: level tasks and review","source":"M","ref":"p.15","tasks":{"Beginner":"Draw a picture about the discussion and then write a few sentences about it, expressing thoughts freely. Review: say what they drew or wrote; read the text aloud once; the teacher may write the text in the notebook for them.","Letter":"Write about what they liked, using drawing and writing; write any words or sentences they can. Review: read the text aloud once; correct punctuation mistakes using the Barakhadi chart.","Word":"Write a sentence based on the conversation. Mistakes in spelling, punctuation and sentence structure are fine. Review: read it to the group; discuss and correct mistakes together.","Para":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation.","Story":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation."}}],"organisation":[{"grouping":"Whole class (big group)","how":"All learners of all levels sit in a 'U' shape arranged by level (Beginner, Letter, Word, Para, Story) so that the move to small groups is easy.","activities":["Warm-up: Rhyme - 'I saw a Little Bird'","Oral conversation: What did you see on your way?","Story (Day 2 of the story): retelling","Sound-symbol activity: oral sound awareness","Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on my family"]},{"grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","how":"Learners of similar levels work together; the teacher gives each group a task for its level and spends more time with learners who need support. Rotate responsibilities (for example group leader).","activities":["Story: reading with actions and group questions","Sound-symbol games by level"]},{"grouping":"Individual","how":"Each learner works on a task for their own level; the teacher moves around, observes difficulties and supports individuals.","activities":["Story: writing answers individually","Self-writing: individual writing","Self-writing: review and reading back","Daily reading (10 minutes)"]}],"materials":["Rhyme chart or board (optional)","The same story book as yesterday","Story book","slate or paper for questions","Notebooks","Board","chalk","letter cards","Picture card or topic on the board","crayons or pencils","Library books or storybooks"],"outcomes":["Learners take part in the oral conversation and speak without fear.","Learners retell the story, read with expression and ask or answer questions at their level.","Learners respond to the sound-symbol task for today (Identifying the first, second and last sound (dog, sun, pig)) at their own level.","Learners write about the topic at their level and read it aloud.","Each learner reads a book for 10 minutes."],"observation":["Observe each learner's reading and writing during the individual tasks; note who needs individual support and how many learners share the same difficulty.","Note any learner whose level is improving; move the learner to the next level group when you see steady progress (manual p.5).","Record each learner's progress for the day in the notebook, according to the learner's level (manual p.4).","Use today's observations to adjust tomorrow's plan (manual p.5)."],"teacherNotes":["Questions to elicit on Day 2: information questions (answer not in the text), thinking questions (needs knowledge beyond the text) and opinion questions (feedback on something in the text).","Sound-symbol: for the first 4-5 days, play sound-based games with the learners at word level. Include the sounds learners find difficult when you prepare the Class Transaction Plan.","Writing has two parts, content and sequence: encourage learners to read what they wrote, improve it and rewrite it for clarity and correctness (manual p.15).","Pace: the manual says not to assume all learners progress at the same speed. Repeat a day's activity with the groups that need it before moving on.","Special needs: give extra time and prepare materials for slower learners; seat learners with hearing or vision difficulty at the front; for learners who reverse or confuse letters, trace letters on the letter card with a finger and write with dots to trace with a pencil (manual p.6)."],"components":[{"no":1,"key":"warmup","name":"Warm-up activities","keywords":["Rhyme - 'I saw a Little Bird'","two learners lead"],"rows":[1]},{"no":2,"key":"oral","name":"Oral Discussion","keywords":["What did you see on your way?","every learner speaks"],"rows":[2]},{"no":3,"key":"story","name":"Story","keywords":["Day 2","retell","read with actions","group questions","ask and answer","write answers (Para/Story)"],"rows":[3,4,5]},{"no":4,"key":"sound","name":"Sound symbol games, Sound separation-pairing","keywords":["oral sound awareness","first / second / last sound","level games in small groups"],"rows":[6,7]},{"no":5,"key":"mindwrite","name":"Individual-Writing (Day 2)","keywords":["discussion","write at own level","self-review (read aloud)"],"rows":[8,9,10]},{"no":6,"key":"reading","name":"Daily reading","keywords":["library book","read alone","teacher listens"],"rows":[11]}],"preLesson":null},{"programme":"TARL Literacy","id":"lit-036","day":36,"phase":1,"phaseLabel":"Phase 1 (Days 1-45)","title":"Saturday: drama presentation","dayType":"Saturday drama + Self-writing","focus":"Language game: The Wind is Blowing | Self-writing: the story we acted out (a story about a forest and its animals)","duration":70,"objectives":["Listen, speak and answer in the oral conversation (familiar topic).","Express a story through role play, using voice, facial expressions and gestures.","Develop sound-symbol skills: Language game: The Wind is Blowing.","Write about the story and review the writing.","Read independently for 10 minutes every day."],"sequence":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Singing and Spinning","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Learners sit in a circle and pass a small object while you clap with your back turned; when the clapping stops, the learner holding it sings a song, recites a poem or tells a joke. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Pass the object round the circle; sing, recite or tell a joke when the clapping stops.","tlm":"A small object (chalk or pencil)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","n":1},{"activity":"Oral conversation: familiar topic","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Hold a conversation on the topic 'the place I like most in our village'. Give each learner a chance to speak; be patient with learners who need extra time.","learners":"Talk about the topic and listen to others.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.9","n":2},{"activity":"Dramatic presentation: introduction and reading","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Explain what a dramatic presentation is and how it is done. Provide stories discussed during the week and read one aloud once more. Para and Story level learners support Beginner and Letter level learners in reading.","learners":"Listen, read along, then each learner chooses a character.","tlm":"Stories discussed in the week (a story about honesty; a story about a forest and its animals)","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":3},{"activity":"Dramatic presentation: planning in small groups","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":8,"teacher":"Each group discusses and plans dialogues; Para or Story level learners write the dialogues. Groups prepare their dramatic presentation.","learners":"Choose characters, plan and rehearse dialogues with facial expressions and gestures.","tlm":"Story, paper for dialogues","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":4},{"activity":"Dramatic presentation: performances and feedback","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":7,"teacher":"Learners sit in a U shape. Each group presents; after each performance, watching learners say what they enjoyed and what could be improved.","learners":"Perform in turn; watch; give feedback.","tlm":"Open space (U-shape seating)","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":5},{"activity":"Language game: The Wind is Blowing","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Learners hold a secret letter card; the one whose letter the teacher names says words beginning with it. Observe each learner and give help where needed.","learners":"Play the game, take turns and read or say the words they make.","tlm":"Letter flashcards","source":"M","ref":"p.19","n":6},{"activity":"Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on the story we acted out (a story about a forest and its animals)","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Start a conversation about the story used for the drama: 'the story we acted out (a story about a forest and its animals)'. Involve all learners with open-ended questions.","learners":"Take part in the discussion and share thoughts freely.","tlm":"Picture card or topic on the board","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":7},{"activity":"Self-writing: individual writing","grouping":"Individual","minutes":7,"teacher":"Give each level its task (see level table). Let learners take ownership of what they draw and write; mistakes are fine.","learners":"Draw and write about the topic at their level.","tlm":"Notebooks, crayons or pencils","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":8},{"activity":"Self-writing: review and reading back","grouping":"Individual","minutes":3,"teacher":"Ask each learner 'What did you draw or write?' and have them read it aloud once. Word-level learners read to the group; discuss spelling, punctuation and sentence structure. Help beginners by writing their text in the notebook for them if needed.","learners":"Read what they wrote; correct mistakes after listening to their own reading.","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":9},{"activity":"Daily reading (10 minutes)","grouping":"Individual","minutes":10,"teacher":"Give each learner a library book or any storybook. Move around, listen to individual readers and note their level.","learners":"Read independently a book of their choice.","tlm":"Library books or storybooks","source":"M","ref":"p.7","n":10}],"procedures":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Singing and Spinning","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","steps":[{"teacher":"Seat the learners in a circle; give a small object to one learner.","learners":"Sit in a circle."},{"teacher":"Stand outside the circle with your back to them and clap steadily; they pass the object.","learners":"Pass the object while the clapping continues."},{"teacher":"Stop clapping; the learner holding the object sings, recites or tells a joke.","learners":"Perform, and everybody claps."}]},{"activity":"Oral conversation: familiar topic","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.9","steps":[{"teacher":"Introduce the topic: 'the place I like most in our village'.","learners":"Think about their own experience."},{"teacher":"Ask open questions; give every learner a chance. Involve learners who speak less.","learners":"Speak freely and without fear."},{"teacher":"Praise efforts and sum up.","learners":"Listen and respect each other's ideas."}]},{"activity":"Saturday special: dramatic presentation","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.11","steps":[{"teacher":"Explain what a dramatic presentation is and how it can be done. Give the groups the stories discussed during the week.","learners":"Listen to the explanation."},{"teacher":"Read a story aloud once more. Learners at story and paragraph level support those at beginner and letter level in reading.","learners":"Read along; helpers support their friends."},{"teacher":"After reading, each learner chooses a character from the story.","learners":"Choose a role (boys may play girl roles and girls may play boy roles)."},{"teacher":"In groups, learners discuss and plan the dialogues; paragraph or story level learners write the dialogues.","learners":"Plan and write dialogues together."},{"teacher":"Learners sit in a U shape. Each group presents its drama. After each performance, ask what the audience enjoyed and what could be improved.","learners":"Perform, watch and give kind feedback."}]},{"activity":"Language game: The Wind is Blowing","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.19","steps":[{"teacher":"Stand all learners in a circle and give each one a letter flashcard, which they must not show to anyone.","learners":"Hold the card against the chest; do not show it."},{"teacher":"Say: 'The wind is blowing.' Learners answer: 'Which way is it blowing?' Say: 'The wind is blowing towards T.'","learners":"Reply together; the learner with the letter T steps to the centre."},{"teacher":"Ask the learner in the centre to say a few words that start with T. Continue with other letters.","learners":"Say words such as tree, tiger, toy."}]},{"activity":"Self-writing: 'Discussion, Writing, Self-review'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.15","steps":[{"teacher":"Start a conversation about the story used for the drama: 'the story we acted out (a story about a forest and its animals)'. Involve all learners with open-ended questions.","learners":"Discuss and answer questions."},{"teacher":"Give writing time at each level: draw then write (Beginner), write about what they liked (Letter), a sentence (Word), a paragraph or story on a topic of their choice (Para/Story).","learners":"Write at their level and take ownership of the work."},{"teacher":"Review: ask 'What did you draw or write?' Have each learner read the text aloud once. Support with writing if needed.","learners":"Read aloud, listen to their pronunciation and correct mistakes."}]}],"levelTasks":[{"activity":"Drama: roles by level","source":"M","ref":"p.11","tasks":{"Beginner":"Take a character role and say or act short lines with help from Para and Story level learners.","Letter":"Take a character role and say or act short lines with help from Para and Story level learners.","Word":"Take a role and speak the dialogues; help rehearse.","Para":"Write the dialogues for the group and support Beginner, Letter and Word level learners throughout.","Story":"Write the dialogues for the group and support Beginner, Letter and Word level learners throughout."}},{"activity":"Language game: The Wind is Blowing - level support","source":"I","ref":"p.19","tasks":{"Beginner":"Take part by saying or pointing to the letters involved and by listening carefully; Para and Story level partners help.","Letter":"Say the letters/sounds and give simple words they know.","Word":"Say and write words and short sentences for the game.","Para":"Write sentences with the words; help groups to record answers.","Story":"Write sentences or short stories with the words; help groups to record answers."}},{"activity":"Self-writing: level tasks and review","source":"M","ref":"p.15","tasks":{"Beginner":"Draw a picture about the discussion and then write a few sentences about it, expressing thoughts freely. Review: say what they drew or wrote; read the text aloud once; the teacher may write the text in the notebook for them.","Letter":"Write about what they liked, using drawing and writing; write any words or sentences they can. Review: read the text aloud once; correct punctuation mistakes using the Barakhadi chart.","Word":"Write a sentence based on the conversation. Mistakes in spelling, punctuation and sentence structure are fine. Review: read it to the group; discuss and correct mistakes together.","Para":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation.","Story":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation."}}],"organisation":[{"grouping":"Whole class (big group)","how":"All learners of all levels sit in a 'U' shape arranged by level (Beginner, Letter, Word, Para, Story) so that the move to small groups is easy.","activities":["Warm-up: Singing and Spinning","Oral conversation: familiar topic","Dramatic presentation: introduction and reading","Dramatic presentation: performances and feedback","Language game: The Wind is Blowing","Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on the story we acted out (a story about a forest and its animals)"]},{"grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","how":"Learners of similar levels work together; the teacher gives each group a task for its level and spends more time with learners who need support. Rotate responsibilities (for example group leader).","activities":["Dramatic presentation: planning in small groups"]},{"grouping":"Individual","how":"Each learner works on a task for their own level; the teacher moves around, observes difficulties and supports individuals.","activities":["Self-writing: individual writing","Self-writing: review and reading back","Daily reading (10 minutes)"]}],"materials":["A small object (chalk or pencil)","Stories discussed in the week (a story about honesty; a story about a forest","its animals)","Story","paper for dialogues","Open space (U-shape seating)","Letter flashcards","Picture card or topic on the board","Notebooks","crayons or pencils","Library books or storybooks"],"outcomes":["Learners take part in the oral conversation and speak without fear.","Learners present a role in the group drama and give feedback to others.","Learners respond to the sound-symbol task for today (Language game: The Wind is Blowing) at their own level.","Learners write about the story at their level and read it aloud.","Each learner reads a book for 10 minutes."],"observation":["Observe each learner's reading and writing during the individual tasks; note who needs individual support and how many learners share the same difficulty.","Note any learner whose level is improving; move the learner to the next level group when you see steady progress (manual p.5).","Record each learner's progress for the day in the notebook, according to the learner's level (manual p.4).","Use today's observations to adjust tomorrow's plan (manual p.5)."],"teacherNotes":["Saturday: this plan assumes Day 1 is a Monday (six teaching days per week). If your school week is different, hold the drama presentation on your Saturday and keep the other days in sequence.","The manual lists the letter and word games but does not fix the slot in the daily timetable where they are used. This plan places them in the 10-minute sound-symbol / alphabet slot (interpretation).","Writing has two parts, content and sequence: encourage learners to read what they wrote, improve it and rewrite it for clarity and correctness (manual p.15).","Pace: the manual says not to assume all learners progress at the same speed. Repeat a day's activity with the groups that need it before moving on.","Special needs: give extra time and prepare materials for slower learners; seat learners with hearing or vision difficulty at the front; for learners who reverse or confuse letters, trace letters on the letter card with a finger and write with dots to trace with a pencil (manual p.6)."],"components":[{"no":1,"key":"warmup","name":"Warm-up activities","keywords":["Singing and Spinning","two learners lead"],"rows":[1]},{"no":2,"key":"oral","name":"Oral Discussion","keywords":["familiar topic","every learner speaks"],"rows":[2]},{"no":3,"key":"story","name":"Story (Saturday: dramatic presentation)","keywords":["Saturday drama","choose a character","plan dialogues","perform in U shape","feedback"],"rows":[3,4,5]},{"no":4,"key":"sound","name":"Sound symbol games, Sound separation-pairing","keywords":["The Wind is Blowing","play in turns","level support"],"rows":[6]},{"no":5,"key":"mindwrite","name":"Individual-Writing (Day 2)","keywords":["discussion","write at own level","self-review (read aloud)"],"rows":[7,8,9]},{"no":6,"key":"reading","name":"Daily reading","keywords":["library book","read alone","teacher listens"],"rows":[10]}],"preLesson":null},{"programme":"TARL Literacy","id":"lit-037","day":37,"phase":1,"phaseLabel":"Phase 1 (Days 1-45)","title":"Story: a story about a magic object (Day 1)","dayType":"Story Day 1 + Mind mapping","focus":"Language game: Find My Word | Mind map: winter","duration":70,"objectives":["Listen, speak and answer in the oral conversation (conversation on a picture).","Listen to and read a story with understanding; discuss it in big and small groups and respond at their own level.","Develop sound-symbol skills: Language game: Find My Word.","Build vocabulary through a mind map ('winter') and use the words at their own level.","Read independently for 10 minutes every day."],"sequence":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Rain clapping","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Everyone stands in a circle with eyes closed and keeps clapping: first one finger, then two, three, four and finally five fingers. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Stand in a circle, close the eyes and clap with 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 fingers.","tlm":"After the activity ask: What did the sound remind you of?","source":"M","ref":"p.8","n":1},{"activity":"Oral conversation: conversation on a picture","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Show a picture of women weaving cloth and ask what is happening, who is doing what and what is happening around them. Let learners think creatively and even make up a story.","learners":"Look at the picture, answer questions and make up their own story about it.","tlm":"Picture card of women weaving cloth","source":"M","ref":"p.9","n":2},{"activity":"Story (Day 1 of the story): reading aloud and discussion","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":8,"teacher":"Discuss the title or picture of the story with the learners. Read the story aloud with expression and voice modulation (learners do not repeat after you). Discuss it, with emphasis on factual questions. Read it again slowly, pointing to each word.","learners":"Talk about the title/picture; listen; answer questions; follow each word with a finger in their own copy.","tlm":"A story from the school library (a story about a magic object), a copy for each learner","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":3},{"activity":"Story: reading in small groups","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":7,"teacher":"Form level-wise groups with a group leader. Learners read the story one sentence at a time while the others follow with their fingers. Para and Story level learners practise reading with emotion and expression.","learners":"Read the story sentence by sentence, supporting each other; the group leader helps.","tlm":"Story book copies","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":4},{"activity":"Story: level-wise individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":5,"teacher":"Give each learner the task for their level (see level table) and support those who need it.","learners":"Beginner/Letter: find and write favourite words or letters. Word: find consonant clusters. Para/Story: silently read, find unfamiliar and rhyming words.","tlm":"Story book, notebooks, board","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":5},{"activity":"Language game: Find My Word","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Learners search their book pages for words beginning with a letter chosen by a classmate. Observe each learner and give help where needed.","learners":"Play the game, take turns and read or say the words they make.","tlm":"Textbooks or storybooks","source":"M","ref":"p.19","n":6},{"activity":"Mind mapping (Day 1): the word 'winter'","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Ask: 'What words come to your mind when you hear the word winter?' Write learners' answers on the board or floor (Para and Story level learners write the words themselves). Guide the map towards the learning objective. Example words: sweater, cap, shawl, socks, tea, orange, soup, jaggery, fog, fire, blanket, cold.","learners":"Say words connected with 'winter'; share the meaning and feeling of words.","tlm":"Board, chalk (or floor)","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":7},{"activity":"Mind mapping: classify the words","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":4,"teacher":"Ask learners to classify the words in groups, for example: Clothes: sweater, cap, shawl, socks; Foods: tea, orange, soup, jaggery; Things: fog, fire, blanket, cold.","learners":"Sort the words into groups and say why.","tlm":"Board, chalk, word cards (optional)","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":8},{"activity":"Mind mapping: level-wise individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":6,"teacher":"Give each learner the individual task for their level; observe closely and give individual support. Display corrected stories on the wall.","learners":"Complete the task for their level (see level table).","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":9},{"activity":"Daily reading (10 minutes)","grouping":"Individual","minutes":10,"teacher":"Give each learner a library book or any storybook. Move around, listen to individual readers and note their level.","learners":"Read independently a book of their choice.","tlm":"Library books or storybooks","source":"M","ref":"p.7","n":10}],"procedures":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Rain clapping","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","steps":[{"teacher":"Stand the learners in a circle and ask them to close their eyes. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Stand in a circle and close their eyes."},{"teacher":"Start clapping with one finger; then two fingers, three, four and finally five fingers.","learners":"Keep clapping, copying the change of fingers."},{"teacher":"After the activity ask: What did the sound remind you of?","learners":"Tell how they felt and what the sounds reminded them of."}]},{"activity":"Oral conversation: conversation on a picture","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.9","steps":[{"teacher":"Show the picture of women weaving cloth.","learners":"Look carefully."},{"teacher":"Ask: What is happening in the picture? Who is doing what? What is happening around them? Then: How do the people feel? How can you tell?","learners":"Answer in their own words; every learner gets a chance."},{"teacher":"Let learners imagine and make up a short story from the picture.","learners":"Tell their stories to the class."}]},{"activity":"Story - Day 1 (a story about a magic object)","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.10","steps":[{"teacher":"Discuss the title or picture of the story with the learners.","learners":"Talk about what they see and what the story may be about."},{"teacher":"Read the story aloud with expression and proper voice modulation. Learners should not simply repeat after you.","learners":"Listen carefully and enjoy the story."},{"teacher":"Discuss the story: factual, logical, vocabulary-based, judgment or opinion questions (today's focus: factual: Who was in the story? Where did it happen? What did the character do first?). Begin in the home language if needed.","learners":"Think and respond thoughtfully; every learner takes part."},{"teacher":"Read the story again slowly, pointing to each word. Make sure each learner has a copy and follows with a finger.","learners":"Follow each word with their finger."},{"teacher":"Ask learners to read in small groups; select a group leader who helps the others. Learners read one sentence at a time while the others point with fingers.","learners":"Read with the help of one another."}]},{"activity":"Language game: Find My Word","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.19","steps":[{"teacher":"Ask the learners to open any page of their books. Choose a learner to say a letter, for example 'b'.","learners":"Open a book page and listen for the letter."},{"teacher":"The others look through the page to find and say words that begin with that letter (book, ball, bat).","learners":"Find words and read them aloud."},{"teacher":"The learner who finds the most words wins the round. Another learner picks a new letter.","learners":"Choose a new letter and play again."}]},{"activity":"Mind mapping: 'winter'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Small group (level-wise) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.14","steps":[{"teacher":"Choose a word that can generate many related words: 'winter'. Ask: 'What words come to your mind when you hear the word winter?' Write the answers on the board or floor.","learners":"Say words they link with 'winter'."},{"teacher":"Discuss the words: what they mean and how they are connected.","learners":"Explain their words and listen to others."},{"teacher":"In small groups, let the learners classify the words (Clothes: sweater, cap, shawl, socks; Foods: tea, orange, soup, jaggery; Things: fog, fire, blanket, cold).","learners":"Sort the words into groups."},{"teacher":"Give the individual tasks by level and help each learner.","learners":"Work individually; read the work aloud at the end if time allows."}]}],"levelTasks":[{"activity":"Story - Day 1: individual tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.10","tasks":{"Beginner":"Circle or search for a favourite word or letter in the story and say it aloud. If a learner cannot draw a circle, write words on the board and ask them to identify them.","Letter":"Find, read and write favourite words from the story.","Word":"Find the consonant clusters in the story, read them and write them in the notebook.","Para":"Silently read the story from the textbook; find unfamiliar words and try to understand them; find rhyming words, use them in sentences and write in the notebook; ask other groups for meanings; make questions in groups.","Story":"Silently read the story; find unfamiliar words and rhyming words; practise reading with emotion; one group reads sentences formed with consonant clusters to the other group; ask and answer group questions (information, thinking and opinion questions)."}},{"activity":"Language game: Find My Word - level support","source":"I","ref":"p.19","tasks":{"Beginner":"Take part by saying or pointing to the letters involved and by listening carefully; Para and Story level partners help.","Letter":"Say the letters/sounds and give simple words they know.","Word":"Say and write words and short sentences for the game.","Para":"Write sentences with the words; help groups to record answers.","Story":"Write sentences or short stories with the words; help groups to record answers."}},{"activity":"Mind mapping 'winter': level tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.14","tasks":{"Beginner":"Circle all the words that contain the letter 'A' on the board; make a list. See how many learners find the most words.","Letter":"Circle all the words that contain the letter 'A' and make a list of them.","Word":"Use 4-5 words (for example cap, fog, tea, cold, fire) to form sentences, starting with words of one or two syllables. Example: Dream - I had a dream last night.","Para":"Choose any five words from the map and create a story with them. Use consonant clusters correctly, read the story aloud, correct mistakes of sentence structure, spelling or grammar, then display it on the wall.","Story":"Choose any five words from the map and create a story with them. Use consonant clusters correctly, read the story aloud, correct mistakes of sentence structure, spelling or grammar, then display it on the wall."}}],"organisation":[{"grouping":"Whole class (big group)","how":"All learners of all levels sit in a 'U' shape arranged by level (Beginner, Letter, Word, Para, Story) so that the move to small groups is easy.","activities":["Warm-up: Rain clapping","Oral conversation: conversation on a picture","Story (Day 1 of the story): reading aloud and discussion","Mind mapping (Day 1): the word 'winter'"]},{"grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","how":"Learners of similar levels work together; the teacher gives each group a task for its level and spends more time with learners who need support. Rotate responsibilities (for example group leader).","activities":["Story: reading in small groups","Language game: Find My Word","Mind mapping: classify the words"]},{"grouping":"Individual","how":"Each learner works on a task for their own level; the teacher moves around, observes difficulties and supports individuals.","activities":["Story: level-wise individual tasks","Mind mapping: level-wise individual tasks","Daily reading (10 minutes)"]}],"materials":["After the activity ask: What did the sound remind you of?","Picture card of women weaving cloth","A story from the school library (a story about a magic object)","a copy for each learner","Story book copies","Story book","notebooks","board","Textbooks or storybooks","Board","chalk (or floor)","chalk","word cards (optional)","Notebooks","Library books or storybooks"],"outcomes":["Learners take part in the oral conversation and speak without fear.","Learners show understanding of the story in the discussion and complete the task for their level.","Learners respond to the sound-symbol task for today (Language game: Find My Word) at their own level.","Learners add words to the mind map and use them in sentences or a story at their level.","Each learner reads a book for 10 minutes."],"observation":["Observe each learner's reading and writing during the individual tasks; note who needs individual support and how many learners share the same difficulty.","Note any learner whose level is improving; move the learner to the next level group when you see steady progress (manual p.5).","Record each learner's progress for the day in the notebook, according to the learner's level (manual p.4).","Use today's observations to adjust tomorrow's plan (manual p.5)."],"teacherNotes":["Story selection: the manual asks teachers to use picture story books or stories in the school library. Today's suggested theme (a story about a magic object) is a planning suggestion; use any suitable story you have.","The manual lists the letter and word games but does not fix the slot in the daily timetable where they are used. This plan places them in the 10-minute sound-symbol / alphabet slot (interpretation).","Mind mapping topic for this day: 'winter'. The manual's example uses the word 'shop'; today's topic follows the same method.","Pace: the manual says not to assume all learners progress at the same speed. Repeat a day's activity with the groups that need it before moving on.","Special needs: give extra time and prepare materials for slower learners; seat learners with hearing or vision difficulty at the front; for learners who reverse or confuse letters, trace letters on the letter card with a finger and write with dots to trace with a pencil (manual p.6)."],"components":[{"no":1,"key":"warmup","name":"Warm-up activities","keywords":["Rain clapping","two learners lead"],"rows":[1]},{"no":2,"key":"oral","name":"Oral Discussion","keywords":["conversation on a picture","every learner speaks"],"rows":[2]},{"no":3,"key":"story","name":"Story","keywords":["Day 1","title / picture talk","read aloud with expression","factual questions","re-read pointing","group reading","level tasks"],"rows":[3,4,5]},{"no":4,"key":"sound","name":"Sound symbol games, Sound separation-pairing","keywords":["Find My Word","play in turns","level support"],"rows":[6]},{"no":5,"key":"mindwrite","name":"Mind Mapping (Day 1)","keywords":["mind map: winter","classify the words","level task: circle letter A / sentences / story"],"rows":[7,8,9]},{"no":6,"key":"reading","name":"Daily reading","keywords":["library book","read alone","teacher listens"],"rows":[10]}],"preLesson":null},{"programme":"TARL Literacy","id":"lit-038","day":38,"phase":1,"phaseLabel":"Phase 1 (Days 1-45)","title":"Story: a story about a magic object (Day 2)","dayType":"Story Day 2 + Self-writing","focus":"Barakhadi / alphabet and phonics chart (line 3, letter 'g') | Self-writing: a story about a clever animal","duration":70,"objectives":["Listen, speak and answer in the oral conversation (listening and storytelling).","Retell the story, read it with expression, ask and answer questions about it and write answers.","Develop sound-symbol skills: Barakhadi / alphabet and phonics chart (line 3, letter 'g').","Write about a topic at their own level and review the writing (a story about a clever animal).","Read independently for 10 minutes every day."],"sequence":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Writing with body parts","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Learners stand in a circle. Demonstrate writing the word 'fish' in the air with a finger, then ask them to write it with different body parts. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Write the word 'fish' in the air with the finger, then with the head, shoulders, knees or elbows.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.8","n":1},{"activity":"Oral conversation: listening and storytelling","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Tell an interesting story starter and involve the learners: 'Our cow learned to read. What was her favourite book?' Let learners imagine and continue the story.","learners":"Listen to the teacher, then imagine and continue the story. Learners can also recite a rhyme or story they know.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.9","n":2},{"activity":"Story (Day 2 of the story): retelling","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":6,"teacher":"Ask learners to retell yesterday's story in their own words. Prompt with questions on the beginning, middle and end.","learners":"Retell the story using their own words.","tlm":"The same story book as yesterday","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":3},{"activity":"Story: reading with actions and group questions","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":9,"teacher":"Learners practise reading with actions and expressions; one learner per group reads aloud to the class. Guide groups to make questions about the story (guide initially). Groups take turns to ask and answer each other's questions. Word-level learners also read aloud the consonants learned on the first day.","learners":"Read with actions; make questions (word-level learners help write them); ask and answer questions with another group.","tlm":"Story book, slate or paper for questions","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":4},{"activity":"Story: writing answers individually","grouping":"Individual","minutes":5,"teacher":"Para and Story level learners write answers to all questions individually; read and correct their responses after they finish.","learners":"Write the answers in their notebooks; Beginner/Letter/Word learners read or listen and answer orally.","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":5},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart: big group reading","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":3,"teacher":"Show the Barakhadi chart and ask which letter they like. Read the letter 'g' on the chart; learners listen carefully and point to it on their own chart (they do not repeat after you).","learners":"Listen and point to the letter on their own chart.","tlm":"Barakhadi chart, alphabet or phonics chart","source":"M","ref":"p.13","n":6},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart: small-group practice","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Learners practise reading the alphabet or phonics chart in groups and help each other. One learner per group reads aloud. Occasionally ask learners to identify the sounds of letters. Give each level its group task.","learners":"Read the chart in groups; one learner reads aloud; do the level task.","tlm":"Alphabet or phonics chart, board or floor","source":"M","ref":"p.13","n":7},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart: individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":2,"teacher":"Give each learner an individual task for their level and observe closely; assist any learner who needs individual support.","learners":"Say and write a letter or word, a sentence or a short paragraph (by level).","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.13","n":8},{"activity":"Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on a story about a clever animal","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Start a conversation about a picture card: 'a story about a clever animal'. Involve all learners and ask open-ended questions.","learners":"Take part in the discussion and share thoughts freely.","tlm":"Picture card or topic on the board","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":9},{"activity":"Self-writing: individual writing","grouping":"Individual","minutes":7,"teacher":"Give each level its task (see level table). Let learners take ownership of what they draw and write; mistakes are fine.","learners":"Draw and write about the topic at their level.","tlm":"Notebooks, crayons or pencils","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":10},{"activity":"Self-writing: review and reading back","grouping":"Individual","minutes":3,"teacher":"Ask each learner 'What did you draw or write?' and have them read it aloud once. Word-level learners read to the group; discuss spelling, punctuation and sentence structure. Help beginners by writing their text in the notebook for them if needed.","learners":"Read what they wrote; correct mistakes after listening to their own reading.","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":11},{"activity":"Daily reading (10 minutes)","grouping":"Individual","minutes":10,"teacher":"Give each learner a library book or any storybook. Move around, listen to individual readers and note their level.","learners":"Read independently a book of their choice.","tlm":"Library books or storybooks","source":"M","ref":"p.7","n":12}],"procedures":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Writing with body parts","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","steps":[{"teacher":"Stand the learners in a circle. Demonstrate writing the word 'fish' in the air with your finger.","learners":"Watch and then copy with their own finger."},{"teacher":"Ask them to write it again using hips and other body parts (head, shoulders, knees, ...).","learners":"Write the letters in the air with the named body part."},{"teacher":"Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Take turns to lead."}]},{"activity":"Oral conversation: listening and storytelling","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.9","steps":[{"teacher":"Say the starter: 'Our cow learned to read. What was her favourite book?'","learners":"Listen and imagine."},{"teacher":"Ask learners to continue the story one by one. Encourage those who speak less.","learners":"Add ideas to the story."},{"teacher":"Invite a learner to recite a poem or rhyme they know.","learners":"Recite and listen to others."}]},{"activity":"Story - Day 2 (a story about a magic object)","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.11","steps":[{"teacher":"Ask learners to retell the story they read yesterday in their own words.","learners":"Retell, helping each other remember."},{"teacher":"In small groups learners practise reading the story using actions and expressions; one learner from each group then reads aloud to the class.","learners":"Read with actions and expression; a representative reads aloud."},{"teacher":"Guide the groups to come up with questions about the story (guide initially). Word-level learners can support by helping write them down.","learners":"Make questions together."},{"teacher":"Groups take turns to ask and answer each other's questions. Useful kinds: questions whose answer is not in the text; questions needing thinking beyond the text; questions asking for an opinion.","learners":"Ask, answer and discuss in the groups."},{"teacher":"Word-level learners also read aloud the consonants they learned on the first day.","learners":"Read the consonant clusters aloud."}]},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart activity (line 3)","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Small group (level-wise) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.13","steps":[{"teacher":"Show the Barakhadi chart and ask the learners which letter they like. Where is the letter 'g'?","learners":"Look for the letter on the chart."},{"teacher":"Read the letter 'g' on the chart. Learners listen and point to it on their own chart. Make sure they do not repeat after you.","learners":"Listen and point to the letter."},{"teacher":"Learners read the alphabet or phonics chart in their groups and help each other; one learner from each group comes forward to read aloud.","learners":"Read in groups; the representative reads aloud."},{"teacher":"Occasionally ask them to identify the sounds of letters from the chart.","learners":"Say the sound of the letter you point to."},{"teacher":"As an extra activity, write some letters on the floor, call out each letter one by one and let the learners jump onto the correct letter.","learners":"Jump onto the letter that is called."}]},{"activity":"Self-writing: 'Discussion, Writing, Self-review'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.15","steps":[{"teacher":"Start a conversation about a picture card: 'a story about a clever animal'. Involve all learners and ask open-ended questions.","learners":"Discuss and answer questions."},{"teacher":"Give writing time at each level: draw then write (Beginner), write about what they liked (Letter), a sentence (Word), a paragraph or story on a topic of their choice (Para/Story).","learners":"Write at their level and take ownership of the work."},{"teacher":"Review: ask 'What did you draw or write?' Have each learner read the text aloud once. Support with writing if needed.","learners":"Read aloud, listen to their pronunciation and correct mistakes."}]}],"levelTasks":[{"activity":"Story - Day 2: level-wise tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.11","tasks":{"Beginner":"Retell with the group by pointing to pictures or words; read aloud with group support (interpretation of the manual's group reading task).","Letter":"Read with the group, pointing to words; say the letters and words they know (interpretation of the manual's group reading task).","Word":"Support the group in writing the questions; read aloud the consonant clusters learned on the first day.","Para":"Ask the group's questions to another group, discuss them, then write answers to all questions individually; the teacher reads and corrects.","Story":"Ask the group's questions to another group, discuss them, then write answers to all questions individually; the teacher reads and corrects."}},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart: level tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.13","tasks":{"Beginner":"Small group: read the chart in the group; find and write favourite letters from the line. Individual: say and write a letter of their choice.","Letter":"Small group: read the chart; find and write favourite letters or words from any line. Individual: say a word on their own that begins with any letter.","Word":"Small group: write one or two lines of letters on the board or floor and use them to form words. Individual: speak and write sentences using words they know.","Para":"Small group: prepare word lists using the Barakhadi chart (for example items found in a shop or in the kitchen). Individual: write short paragraphs using the words formed with the Barakhadi chart.","Story":"Small group: prepare word lists using the Barakhadi chart. Individual: write short paragraphs using the words formed with the Barakhadi chart."}},{"activity":"Self-writing: level tasks and review","source":"M","ref":"p.15","tasks":{"Beginner":"Draw a picture about the discussion and then write a few sentences about it, expressing thoughts freely. Review: say what they drew or wrote; read the text aloud once; the teacher may write the text in the notebook for them.","Letter":"Write about what they liked, using drawing and writing; write any words or sentences they can. Review: read the text aloud once; correct punctuation mistakes using the Barakhadi chart.","Word":"Write a sentence based on the conversation. Mistakes in spelling, punctuation and sentence structure are fine. Review: read it to the group; discuss and correct mistakes together.","Para":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation.","Story":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation."}}],"organisation":[{"grouping":"Whole class (big group)","how":"All learners of all levels sit in a 'U' shape arranged by level (Beginner, Letter, Word, Para, Story) so that the move to small groups is easy.","activities":["Warm-up: Writing with body parts","Oral conversation: listening and storytelling","Story (Day 2 of the story): retelling","Barakhadi chart: big group reading","Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on a story about a clever animal"]},{"grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","how":"Learners of similar levels work together; the teacher gives each group a task for its level and spends more time with learners who need support. Rotate responsibilities (for example group leader).","activities":["Story: reading with actions and group questions","Barakhadi chart: small-group practice"]},{"grouping":"Individual","how":"Each learner works on a task for their own level; the teacher moves around, observes difficulties and supports individuals.","activities":["Story: writing answers individually","Barakhadi chart: individual tasks","Self-writing: individual writing","Self-writing: review and reading back","Daily reading (10 minutes)"]}],"materials":["The same story book as yesterday","Story book","slate or paper for questions","Notebooks","Barakhadi chart","alphabet or phonics chart","Alphabet or phonics chart","board or floor","Picture card or topic on the board","crayons or pencils","Library books or storybooks"],"outcomes":["Learners take part in the oral conversation and speak without fear.","Learners retell the story, read with expression and ask or answer questions at their level.","Learners respond to the sound-symbol task for today (Barakhadi / alphabet and phonics chart (line 3, letter 'g')) at their own level.","Learners write about the topic at their level and read it aloud.","Each learner reads a book for 10 minutes."],"observation":["Observe each learner's reading and writing during the individual tasks; note who needs individual support and how many learners share the same difficulty.","Note any learner whose level is improving; move the learner to the next level group when you see steady progress (manual p.5).","Record each learner's progress for the day in the notebook, according to the learner's level (manual p.4).","Use today's observations to adjust tomorrow's plan (manual p.5)."],"teacherNotes":["Questions to elicit on Day 2: information questions (answer not in the text), thinking questions (needs knowledge beyond the text) and opinion questions (feedback on something in the text).","Barakhadi: learners who need extra time should get repeated practice using one or two sound units at a time. Topic-based discussion helps oral expression, thinking and understanding.","Writing has two parts, content and sequence: encourage learners to read what they wrote, improve it and rewrite it for clarity and correctness (manual p.15).","Pace: the manual says not to assume all learners progress at the same speed. Repeat a day's activity with the groups that need it before moving on.","Special needs: give extra time and prepare materials for slower learners; seat learners with hearing or vision difficulty at the front; for learners who reverse or confuse letters, trace letters on the letter card with a finger and write with dots to trace with a pencil (manual p.6)."],"components":[{"no":1,"key":"warmup","name":"Warm-up activities","keywords":["Writing with body parts","two learners lead"],"rows":[1]},{"no":2,"key":"oral","name":"Oral Discussion","keywords":["listening and storytelling","every learner speaks"],"rows":[2]},{"no":3,"key":"story","name":"Story","keywords":["Day 2","retell","read with actions","group questions","ask and answer","write answers (Para/Story)"],"rows":[3,4,5]},{"no":4,"key":"sound","name":"Sound symbol games, Sound separation-pairing","keywords":["Barakhadi / alphabet chart","listen and point (no repeating)","group reading","level tasks"],"rows":[6,7,8]},{"no":5,"key":"mindwrite","name":"Individual-Writing (Day 2)","keywords":["discussion","write at own level","self-review (read aloud)"],"rows":[9,10,11]},{"no":6,"key":"reading","name":"Daily reading","keywords":["library book","read alone","teacher listens"],"rows":[12]}],"preLesson":null},{"programme":"TARL Literacy","id":"lit-039","day":39,"phase":1,"phaseLabel":"Phase 1 (Days 1-45)","title":"Story: a story about a grandmother's tale (Day 1)","dayType":"Story Day 1 + Mind mapping","focus":"Consonant clusters: mb (lamb, comb) | Mind map: birthday party","duration":70,"objectives":["Listen, speak and answer in the oral conversation (What did you see on your way?).","Listen to and read a story with understanding; discuss it in big and small groups and respond at their own level.","Develop sound-symbol skills: Consonant clusters: mb (lamb, comb).","Build vocabulary through a mind map ('birthday party') and use the words at their own level.","Read independently for 10 minutes every day."],"sequence":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Alphabet song (last-letter word chain)","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Say a word to the big group, for example 'road'. Learners say a word that starts with the last letter ('d'). A learner who cannot say a word is out. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Say a word that starts with the last letter of the previous word; step out if unable to.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.8","n":1},{"activity":"Oral conversation: What did you see on your way?","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Ask learners to describe what they saw on their way to school. If they are hesitant, begin yourself: 'On my way I saw a bus full of people, a boy on a bicycle and an old man selling guavas. What did you see?'","learners":"Describe what they saw on the way to school and connect with what others share.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.9","n":2},{"activity":"Story (Day 1 of the story): reading aloud and discussion","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":8,"teacher":"Discuss the title or picture of the story with the learners. Read the story aloud with expression and voice modulation (learners do not repeat after you). Discuss it, with emphasis on logical questions. Read it again slowly, pointing to each word.","learners":"Talk about the title/picture; listen; answer questions; follow each word with a finger in their own copy.","tlm":"A story from the school library (a story about a grandmother's tale), a copy for each learner","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":3},{"activity":"Story: reading in small groups","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":7,"teacher":"Form level-wise groups with a group leader. Learners read the story one sentence at a time while the others follow with their fingers. Para and Story level learners practise reading with emotion and expression.","learners":"Read the story sentence by sentence, supporting each other; the group leader helps.","tlm":"Story book copies","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":4},{"activity":"Story: level-wise individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":5,"teacher":"Give each learner the task for their level (see level table) and support those who need it.","learners":"Beginner/Letter: find and write favourite words or letters. Word: find consonant clusters. Para/Story: silently read, find unfamiliar and rhyming words.","tlm":"Story book, notebooks, board","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":5},{"activity":"Consonant clusters: introduction","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":4,"teacher":"Two-letter clusters: after same-letter clusters, familiarise learners with clusters of two different letters ('mb' as in lamb, comb, climb). Discuss the words, ask learners to pronounce them and to frame sentences using them.","learners":"Listen, pronounce the cluster and say words that contain it.","tlm":"Board and chalk, words list (lamb comb climb thumb crumb)","source":"M","ref":"p.16","n":6},{"activity":"Consonant cluster game: Looking for Similar Ones","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":6,"teacher":"Write some words with the same conjunct consonants on the board, for example bl, tr, st. Observe closely and help learners who need support.","learners":"Match words that have the same conjunct consonant (black, blue, blanket, blow, blink).","tlm":"Words on the board","source":"M","ref":"p.17","n":7},{"activity":"Mind mapping (Day 1): the word 'birthday party'","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Ask: 'What words come to your mind when you hear the word birthday party?' Write learners' answers on the board or floor (Para and Story level learners write the words themselves). Guide the map towards the learning objective. Example words: cake, sweets, juice, chips, balloon, candle, gift, card, song, dance, game, clap.","learners":"Say words connected with 'birthday party'; share the meaning and feeling of words.","tlm":"Board, chalk (or floor)","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":8},{"activity":"Mind mapping: classify the words","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":4,"teacher":"Ask learners to classify the words in groups, for example: Food: cake, sweets, juice, chips; Things: balloon, candle, gift, card; Fun: song, dance, game, clap.","learners":"Sort the words into groups and say why.","tlm":"Board, chalk, word cards (optional)","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":9},{"activity":"Mind mapping: level-wise individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":6,"teacher":"Give each learner the individual task for their level; observe closely and give individual support. Display corrected stories on the wall.","learners":"Complete the task for their level (see level table).","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":10},{"activity":"Daily reading (10 minutes)","grouping":"Individual","minutes":10,"teacher":"Give each learner a library book or any storybook. Move around, listen to individual readers and note their level.","learners":"Read independently a book of their choice.","tlm":"Library books or storybooks","source":"M","ref":"p.7","n":11}],"procedures":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Alphabet song (last-letter word chain)","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","steps":[{"teacher":"Say the word 'road' to the big group and show that its last letter is 'd'.","learners":"Listen and think of a word starting with 'd'."},{"teacher":"Ask learners in turn to say a word that starts with the last letter of the previous word. Example: rain -> nest.","learners":"Say a word in turn; anyone who cannot say a word is out of the game."},{"teacher":"Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Lead the game when it is their turn."}]},{"activity":"Oral conversation: What did you see on your way?","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.9","steps":[{"teacher":"Ask: 'What did you see on your way to school today?'","learners":"Think about the way to school."},{"teacher":"If learners hesitate, start: 'On my way I saw a bus full of people, a boy on a bicycle and an old man selling guavas. What did you see?'","learners":"Listen to the model and then share their own observations."},{"teacher":"Connect learners' answers with each other.","learners":"Listen and add what they noticed."}]},{"activity":"Story - Day 1 (a story about a grandmother's tale)","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.10","steps":[{"teacher":"Discuss the title or picture of the story with the learners.","learners":"Talk about what they see and what the story may be about."},{"teacher":"Read the story aloud with expression and proper voice modulation. Learners should not simply repeat after you.","learners":"Listen carefully and enjoy the story."},{"teacher":"Discuss the story: factual, logical, vocabulary-based, judgment or opinion questions (today's focus: logical: Why did the character do that? What would have happened if ...?). Begin in the home language if needed.","learners":"Think and respond thoughtfully; every learner takes part."},{"teacher":"Read the story again slowly, pointing to each word. Make sure each learner has a copy and follows with a finger.","learners":"Follow each word with their finger."},{"teacher":"Ask learners to read in small groups; select a group leader who helps the others. Learners read one sentence at a time while the others point with fingers.","learners":"Read with the help of one another."}]},{"activity":"Consonant clusters (mb) and the game 'Looking for Similar Ones'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.16-17","steps":[{"teacher":"Two-letter clusters: after same-letter clusters, familiarise learners with clusters of two different letters ('mb' as in lamb, comb, climb). Discuss the words, ask learners to pronounce them and to frame sentences using them.","learners":"Listen, pronounce and find words in the text."},{"teacher":"Write the words on the board: lamb comb climb thumb crumb. Read them aloud with distinct pronunciation of the cluster.","learners":"Read the words aloud; point to the cluster in each word."},{"teacher":"Write some words with the same conjunct consonants on the board, for example bl, tr, st.","learners":"Match words that have the same conjunct consonant (black, blue, blanket, blow, blink)."}]},{"activity":"Mind mapping: 'birthday party'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Small group (level-wise) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.14","steps":[{"teacher":"Choose a word that can generate many related words: 'birthday party'. Ask: 'What words come to your mind when you hear the word birthday party?' Write the answers on the board or floor.","learners":"Say words they link with 'birthday party'."},{"teacher":"Discuss the words: what they mean and how they are connected.","learners":"Explain their words and listen to others."},{"teacher":"In small groups, let the learners classify the words (Food: cake, sweets, juice, chips; Things: balloon, candle, gift, card; Fun: song, dance, game, clap).","learners":"Sort the words into groups."},{"teacher":"Give the individual tasks by level and help each learner.","learners":"Work individually; read the work aloud at the end if time allows."}]}],"levelTasks":[{"activity":"Story - Day 1: individual tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.10","tasks":{"Beginner":"Circle or search for a favourite word or letter in the story and say it aloud. If a learner cannot draw a circle, write words on the board and ask them to identify them.","Letter":"Find, read and write favourite words from the story.","Word":"Find the consonant clusters in the story, read them and write them in the notebook.","Para":"Silently read the story from the textbook; find unfamiliar words and try to understand them; find rhyming words, use them in sentences and write in the notebook; ask other groups for meanings; make questions in groups.","Story":"Silently read the story; find unfamiliar words and rhyming words; practise reading with emotion; one group reads sentences formed with consonant clusters to the other group; ask and answer group questions (information, thinking and opinion questions)."}},{"activity":"Consonant clusters (mb): level tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.16-17","tasks":{"Beginner":"Listen to the sound of the cluster and point to it in a word; continue with letter-sound work (interpretation: the manual describes clusters for learners lagging in reading words and sentences).","Letter":"Listen to the cluster sound and pick words with the cluster from a word card (interpretation).","Word":"Find the cluster in the story or textbook words, read the words and write them in the notebook.","Para":"Form words and sentences using the cluster; read the sentences aloud.","Story":"Form words and sentences using the cluster; read the sentences aloud; use them in the story writing."}},{"activity":"Mind mapping 'birthday party': level tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.14","tasks":{"Beginner":"Circle all the words that contain the letter 'A' on the board; make a list. See how many learners find the most words.","Letter":"Circle all the words that contain the letter 'A' and make a list of them.","Word":"Use 4-5 words (for example cake, card, clap, game, gift) to form sentences, starting with words of one or two syllables. Example: Dream - I had a dream last night.","Para":"Choose any five words from the map and create a story with them. Use consonant clusters correctly, read the story aloud, correct mistakes of sentence structure, spelling or grammar, then display it on the wall.","Story":"Choose any five words from the map and create a story with them. Use consonant clusters correctly, read the story aloud, correct mistakes of sentence structure, spelling or grammar, then display it on the wall."}}],"organisation":[{"grouping":"Whole class (big group)","how":"All learners of all levels sit in a 'U' shape arranged by level (Beginner, Letter, Word, Para, Story) so that the move to small groups is easy.","activities":["Warm-up: Alphabet song (last-letter word chain)","Oral conversation: What did you see on your way?","Story (Day 1 of the story): reading aloud and discussion","Consonant clusters: introduction","Mind mapping (Day 1): the word 'birthday party'"]},{"grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","how":"Learners of similar levels work together; the teacher gives each group a task for its level and spends more time with learners who need support. Rotate responsibilities (for example group leader).","activities":["Story: reading in small groups","Consonant cluster game: Looking for Similar Ones","Mind mapping: classify the words"]},{"grouping":"Individual","how":"Each learner works on a task for their own level; the teacher moves around, observes difficulties and supports individuals.","activities":["Story: level-wise individual tasks","Mind mapping: level-wise individual tasks","Daily reading (10 minutes)"]}],"materials":["A story from the school library (a story about a grandmother's tale)","a copy for each learner","Story book copies","Story book","notebooks","board","Board","chalk","words list (lamb comb climb thumb crumb)","Words on the board","chalk (or floor)","word cards (optional)","Notebooks","Library books or storybooks"],"outcomes":["Learners take part in the oral conversation and speak without fear.","Learners show understanding of the story in the discussion and complete the task for their level.","Learners respond to the sound-symbol task for today (Consonant clusters: mb (lamb, comb)) at their own level.","Learners add words to the mind map and use them in sentences or a story at their level.","Each learner reads a book for 10 minutes."],"observation":["Observe each learner's reading and writing during the individual tasks; note who needs individual support and how many learners share the same difficulty.","Note any learner whose level is improving; move the learner to the next level group when you see steady progress (manual p.5).","Record each learner's progress for the day in the notebook, according to the learner's level (manual p.4).","Use today's observations to adjust tomorrow's plan (manual p.5)."],"teacherNotes":["Story selection: the manual asks teachers to use picture story books or stories in the school library. Today's suggested theme (a story about a grandmother's tale) is a planning suggestion; use any suitable story you have.","Consonant clusters: do these activities daily for learners who find reading complex words hard; the aim is to remove the fear of reading clusters. Teachers may carry out similar activities on their own.","Mind mapping topic for this day: 'birthday party'. The manual's example uses the word 'shop'; today's topic follows the same method.","Pace: the manual says not to assume all learners progress at the same speed. Repeat a day's activity with the groups that need it before moving on.","Special needs: give extra time and prepare materials for slower learners; seat learners with hearing or vision difficulty at the front; for learners who reverse or confuse letters, trace letters on the letter card with a finger and write with dots to trace with a pencil (manual p.6)."],"components":[{"no":1,"key":"warmup","name":"Warm-up activities","keywords":["Alphabet song (last-letter word chain)","two learners lead"],"rows":[1]},{"no":2,"key":"oral","name":"Oral Discussion","keywords":["What did you see on your way?","every learner speaks"],"rows":[2]},{"no":3,"key":"story","name":"Story","keywords":["Day 1","title / picture talk","read aloud with expression","logical questions","re-read pointing","group reading","level tasks"],"rows":[3,4,5]},{"no":4,"key":"sound","name":"Sound symbol games, Sound separation-pairing","keywords":["consonant cluster 'mb'","pronounce and find words","game: Looking for Similar Ones"],"rows":[6,7]},{"no":5,"key":"mindwrite","name":"Mind Mapping (Day 1)","keywords":["mind map: birthday party","classify the words","level task: circle letter A / sentences / story"],"rows":[8,9,10]},{"no":6,"key":"reading","name":"Daily reading","keywords":["library book","read alone","teacher listens"],"rows":[11]}],"preLesson":null},{"programme":"TARL Literacy","id":"lit-040","day":40,"phase":1,"phaseLabel":"Phase 1 (Days 1-45)","title":"Story: a story about a grandmother's tale (Day 2)","dayType":"Story Day 2 + Self-writing","focus":"Language game: Making Stories out of Words | Self-writing: the season I like best","duration":70,"objectives":["Listen, speak and answer in the oral conversation (familiar topic).","Retell the story, read it with expression, ask and answer questions about it and write answers.","Develop sound-symbol skills: Language game: Making Stories out of Words.","Write about a topic at their own level and review the writing (the season I like best).","Read independently for 10 minutes every day."],"sequence":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Handkerchief game","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Learners sit in a circle and clap while singing a rhyme ('I saw a Little Bird'). One learner runs outside the circle with a handkerchief and secretly places it behind another learner, who must chase the runner. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Sit in a circle, clap and sing; run, place the handkerchief or chase as the game requires.","tlm":"A handkerchief","source":"M","ref":"p.8","n":1},{"activity":"Oral conversation: familiar topic","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Hold a conversation on the topic 'my favourite rhyme or song, which I will recite'. Give each learner a chance to speak; be patient with learners who need extra time.","learners":"Talk about the topic and listen to others.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.9","n":2},{"activity":"Story (Day 2 of the story): retelling","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":6,"teacher":"Ask learners to retell yesterday's story in their own words. Prompt with questions on the beginning, middle and end.","learners":"Retell the story using their own words.","tlm":"The same story book as yesterday","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":3},{"activity":"Story: reading with actions and group questions","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":9,"teacher":"Learners practise reading with actions and expressions; one learner per group reads aloud to the class. Guide groups to make questions about the story (guide initially). Groups take turns to ask and answer each other's questions. Word-level learners also read aloud the consonants learned on the first day.","learners":"Read with actions; make questions (word-level learners help write them); ask and answer questions with another group.","tlm":"Story book, slate or paper for questions","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":4},{"activity":"Story: writing answers individually","grouping":"Individual","minutes":5,"teacher":"Para and Story level learners write answers to all questions individually; read and correct their responses after they finish.","learners":"Write the answers in their notebooks; Beginner/Letter/Word learners read or listen and answer orally.","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":5},{"activity":"Language game: Making Stories out of Words","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Learners are given five words and make a short story using all of them. Observe each learner and give help where needed.","learners":"Play the game, take turns and read or say the words they make.","tlm":"Five words on the board","source":"M","ref":"p.21","n":6},{"activity":"Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on the season I like best","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Start a conversation about a topic: 'the season I like best'. Involve all learners and ask open-ended questions.","learners":"Take part in the discussion and share thoughts freely.","tlm":"Picture card or topic on the board","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":7},{"activity":"Self-writing: individual writing","grouping":"Individual","minutes":7,"teacher":"Give each level its task (see level table). Let learners take ownership of what they draw and write; mistakes are fine.","learners":"Draw and write about the topic at their level.","tlm":"Notebooks, crayons or pencils","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":8},{"activity":"Self-writing: review and reading back","grouping":"Individual","minutes":3,"teacher":"Ask each learner 'What did you draw or write?' and have them read it aloud once. Word-level learners read to the group; discuss spelling, punctuation and sentence structure. Help beginners by writing their text in the notebook for them if needed.","learners":"Read what they wrote; correct mistakes after listening to their own reading.","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":9},{"activity":"Daily reading (10 minutes)","grouping":"Individual","minutes":10,"teacher":"Give each learner a library book or any storybook. Move around, listen to individual readers and note their level.","learners":"Read independently a book of their choice.","tlm":"Library books or storybooks","source":"M","ref":"p.7","n":10}],"procedures":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Handkerchief game","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","steps":[{"teacher":"Seat the learners in a circle and start clapping and singing the rhyme 'I saw a Little Bird'.","learners":"Clap and sing together."},{"teacher":"One learner runs outside the circle holding a handkerchief and secretly places it behind another learner.","learners":"Everyone keeps clapping; the learner who finds the handkerchief behind them takes it and chases the runner."},{"teacher":"If the runner sits in the chaser's place before being caught, they stay in the game; if caught, they are out. Continue in this way.","learners":"Play fairly and take turns."}]},{"activity":"Oral conversation: familiar topic","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.9","steps":[{"teacher":"Introduce the topic: 'my favourite rhyme or song, which I will recite'.","learners":"Think about their own experience."},{"teacher":"Ask open questions; give every learner a chance. Involve learners who speak less.","learners":"Speak freely and without fear."},{"teacher":"Praise efforts and sum up.","learners":"Listen and respect each other's ideas."}]},{"activity":"Story - Day 2 (a story about a grandmother's tale)","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.11","steps":[{"teacher":"Ask learners to retell the story they read yesterday in their own words.","learners":"Retell, helping each other remember."},{"teacher":"In small groups learners practise reading the story using actions and expressions; one learner from each group then reads aloud to the class.","learners":"Read with actions and expression; a representative reads aloud."},{"teacher":"Guide the groups to come up with questions about the story (guide initially). Word-level learners can support by helping write them down.","learners":"Make questions together."},{"teacher":"Groups take turns to ask and answer each other's questions. Useful kinds: questions whose answer is not in the text; questions needing thinking beyond the text; questions asking for an opinion.","learners":"Ask, answer and discuss in the groups."},{"teacher":"Word-level learners also read aloud the consonants they learned on the first day.","learners":"Read the consonant clusters aloud."}]},{"activity":"Language game: Making Stories out of Words","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.21","steps":[{"teacher":"Give the learners five words, for example Lion, Sugarcane, Rope, Rabbit, Tree.","learners":"Read the five words."},{"teacher":"Ask them to create a short story that uses all the words.","learners":"Discuss, then tell or write a story with all five words."},{"teacher":"Let learners read or tell their stories to the group.","learners":"Share the story."}]},{"activity":"Self-writing: 'Discussion, Writing, Self-review'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.15","steps":[{"teacher":"Start a conversation about a topic: 'the season I like best'. Involve all learners and ask open-ended questions.","learners":"Discuss and answer questions."},{"teacher":"Give writing time at each level: draw then write (Beginner), write about what they liked (Letter), a sentence (Word), a paragraph or story on a topic of their choice (Para/Story).","learners":"Write at their level and take ownership of the work."},{"teacher":"Review: ask 'What did you draw or write?' Have each learner read the text aloud once. Support with writing if needed.","learners":"Read aloud, listen to their pronunciation and correct mistakes."}]}],"levelTasks":[{"activity":"Story - Day 2: level-wise tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.11","tasks":{"Beginner":"Retell with the group by pointing to pictures or words; read aloud with group support (interpretation of the manual's group reading task).","Letter":"Read with the group, pointing to words; say the letters and words they know (interpretation of the manual's group reading task).","Word":"Support the group in writing the questions; read aloud the consonant clusters learned on the first day.","Para":"Ask the group's questions to another group, discuss them, then write answers to all questions individually; the teacher reads and corrects.","Story":"Ask the group's questions to another group, discuss them, then write answers to all questions individually; the teacher reads and corrects."}},{"activity":"Language game: Making Stories out of Words - level support","source":"I","ref":"p.21","tasks":{"Beginner":"Take part by saying or pointing to the letters involved and by listening carefully; Para and Story level partners help.","Letter":"Say the letters/sounds and give simple words they know.","Word":"Say and write words and short sentences for the game.","Para":"Write sentences with the words; help groups to record answers.","Story":"Write sentences or short stories with the words; help groups to record answers."}},{"activity":"Self-writing: level tasks and review","source":"M","ref":"p.15","tasks":{"Beginner":"Draw a picture about the discussion and then write a few sentences about it, expressing thoughts freely. Review: say what they drew or wrote; read the text aloud once; the teacher may write the text in the notebook for them.","Letter":"Write about what they liked, using drawing and writing; write any words or sentences they can. Review: read the text aloud once; correct punctuation mistakes using the Barakhadi chart.","Word":"Write a sentence based on the conversation. Mistakes in spelling, punctuation and sentence structure are fine. Review: read it to the group; discuss and correct mistakes together.","Para":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation.","Story":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation."}}],"organisation":[{"grouping":"Whole class (big group)","how":"All learners of all levels sit in a 'U' shape arranged by level (Beginner, Letter, Word, Para, Story) so that the move to small groups is easy.","activities":["Warm-up: Handkerchief game","Oral conversation: familiar topic","Story (Day 2 of the story): retelling","Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on the season I like best"]},{"grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","how":"Learners of similar levels work together; the teacher gives each group a task for its level and spends more time with learners who need support. Rotate responsibilities (for example group leader).","activities":["Story: reading with actions and group questions","Language game: Making Stories out of Words"]},{"grouping":"Individual","how":"Each learner works on a task for their own level; the teacher moves around, observes difficulties and supports individuals.","activities":["Story: writing answers individually","Self-writing: individual writing","Self-writing: review and reading back","Daily reading (10 minutes)"]}],"materials":["A handkerchief","The same story book as yesterday","Story book","slate or paper for questions","Notebooks","Five words on the board","Picture card or topic on the board","crayons or pencils","Library books or storybooks"],"outcomes":["Learners take part in the oral conversation and speak without fear.","Learners retell the story, read with expression and ask or answer questions at their level.","Learners respond to the sound-symbol task for today (Language game: Making Stories out of Words) at their own level.","Learners write about the topic at their level and read it aloud.","Each learner reads a book for 10 minutes."],"observation":["Observe each learner's reading and writing during the individual tasks; note who needs individual support and how many learners share the same difficulty.","Note any learner whose level is improving; move the learner to the next level group when you see steady progress (manual p.5).","Record each learner's progress for the day in the notebook, according to the learner's level (manual p.4).","Use today's observations to adjust tomorrow's plan (manual p.5)."],"teacherNotes":["Questions to elicit on Day 2: information questions (answer not in the text), thinking questions (needs knowledge beyond the text) and opinion questions (feedback on something in the text).","The manual lists the letter and word games but does not fix the slot in the daily timetable where they are used. This plan places them in the 10-minute sound-symbol / alphabet slot (interpretation).","Writing has two parts, content and sequence: encourage learners to read what they wrote, improve it and rewrite it for clarity and correctness (manual p.15).","Level check: if learners have moved up to a new level, celebrate with an appreciation-oriented game (beginner level to letter level): 'Where Have You Seen Me?' or 'Jump on the Letters' (manual p.42-45). Teachers may use such activities on their own.","Pace: the manual says not to assume all learners progress at the same speed. Repeat a day's activity with the groups that need it before moving on.","Special needs: give extra time and prepare materials for slower learners; seat learners with hearing or vision difficulty at the front; for learners who reverse or confuse letters, trace letters on the letter card with a finger and write with dots to trace with a pencil (manual p.6)."],"components":[{"no":1,"key":"warmup","name":"Warm-up activities","keywords":["Handkerchief game","two learners lead"],"rows":[1]},{"no":2,"key":"oral","name":"Oral Discussion","keywords":["familiar topic","every learner speaks"],"rows":[2]},{"no":3,"key":"story","name":"Story","keywords":["Day 2","retell","read with actions","group questions","ask and answer","write answers (Para/Story)"],"rows":[3,4,5]},{"no":4,"key":"sound","name":"Sound symbol games, Sound separation-pairing","keywords":["Making Stories out of Words","play in turns","level support"],"rows":[6]},{"no":5,"key":"mindwrite","name":"Individual-Writing (Day 2)","keywords":["discussion","write at own level","self-review (read aloud)"],"rows":[7,8,9]},{"no":6,"key":"reading","name":"Daily reading","keywords":["library book","read alone","teacher listens"],"rows":[10]}],"preLesson":null},{"programme":"TARL Literacy","id":"lit-041","day":41,"phase":1,"phaseLabel":"Phase 1 (Days 1-45)","title":"Story: a story about a lost thing that is found (Day 1)","dayType":"Story Day 1 + Mind mapping","focus":"Identifying the first, second and last sound (bed, run, zip) | Mind map: wedding","duration":70,"objectives":["Listen, speak and answer in the oral conversation (conversation on a picture).","Listen to and read a story with understanding; discuss it in big and small groups and respond at their own level.","Develop sound-symbol skills: Identifying the first, second and last sound (bed, run, zip).","Build vocabulary through a mind map ('wedding') and use the words at their own level.","Read independently for 10 minutes every day."],"sequence":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Rhyme - 'I caught a Fish Alive'","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Say the rhyme with actions, then say it together. Lines: One, two, three, four, five, once I caught a fish alive. / Six, seven, eight, nine, ten, then I let it go again. / Why did you let it go? Because it bit my finger so. / Which finger did it bite? This little finger on my right. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Listen, then say the rhyme with actions.","tlm":"Rhyme chart or board (optional)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","n":1},{"activity":"Oral conversation: conversation on a picture","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Show a picture of a fisherman with his net and ask what is happening, who is doing what and what is happening around them. Let learners think creatively and even make up a story.","learners":"Look at the picture, answer questions and make up their own story about it.","tlm":"Picture card of a fisherman with his net","source":"M","ref":"p.9","n":2},{"activity":"Story (Day 1 of the story): reading aloud and discussion","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":8,"teacher":"Discuss the title or picture of the story with the learners. Read the story aloud with expression and voice modulation (learners do not repeat after you). Discuss it, with emphasis on vocabulary-based questions. Read it again slowly, pointing to each word.","learners":"Talk about the title/picture; listen; answer questions; follow each word with a finger in their own copy.","tlm":"A story from the school library (a story about a lost thing that is found), a copy for each learner","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":3},{"activity":"Story: reading in small groups","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":7,"teacher":"Form level-wise groups with a group leader. Learners read the story one sentence at a time while the others follow with their fingers. Para and Story level learners practise reading with emotion and expression.","learners":"Read the story sentence by sentence, supporting each other; the group leader helps.","tlm":"Story book copies","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":4},{"activity":"Story: level-wise individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":5,"teacher":"Give each learner the task for their level (see level table) and support those who need it.","learners":"Beginner/Letter: find and write favourite words or letters. Word: find consonant clusters. Para/Story: silently read, find unfamiliar and rhyming words.","tlm":"Story book, notebooks, board","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":5},{"activity":"Sound-symbol activity: oral sound awareness","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":4,"teacher":"Say words and ask learners to identify the first, second or last sound. Example: pan - first sound p, second sound a, third sound n; log: l, o, g; cup: c, u, p.","learners":"Say the first, second or last sound of the word.","tlm":"None (oral activity)","source":"M","ref":"p.12","n":6},{"activity":"Sound-symbol games by level","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":6,"teacher":"Give each level group its game (see level table). Move among the groups and help those who need support; say each word clearly.","learners":"Play the game for their level in small groups.","tlm":"Board, chalk, letter cards","source":"M","ref":"p.12","n":7},{"activity":"Mind mapping (Day 1): the word 'wedding'","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Ask: 'What words come to your mind when you hear the word wedding?' Write learners' answers on the board or floor (Para and Story level learners write the words themselves). Guide the map towards the learning objective. Example words: saree, dhoti, jewellery, flowers, rice, fish, sweets, curd, music, lights, gifts, mandap.","learners":"Say words connected with 'wedding'; share the meaning and feeling of words.","tlm":"Board, chalk (or floor)","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":8},{"activity":"Mind mapping: classify the words","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":4,"teacher":"Ask learners to classify the words in groups, for example: Clothes: saree, dhoti, jewellery, flowers; Food: rice, fish, sweets, curd; Things: music, lights, gifts, mandap.","learners":"Sort the words into groups and say why.","tlm":"Board, chalk, word cards (optional)","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":9},{"activity":"Mind mapping: level-wise individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":6,"teacher":"Give each learner the individual task for their level; observe closely and give individual support. Display corrected stories on the wall.","learners":"Complete the task for their level (see level table).","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":10},{"activity":"Daily reading (10 minutes)","grouping":"Individual","minutes":10,"teacher":"Give each learner a library book or any storybook. Move around, listen to individual readers and note their level.","learners":"Read independently a book of their choice.","tlm":"Library books or storybooks","source":"M","ref":"p.7","n":11}],"procedures":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Rhyme - 'I caught a Fish Alive'","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","steps":[{"teacher":"Say the rhyme 'I caught a Fish Alive' slowly with actions: One, two, three, four, five, once I caught a fish alive. / Six, seven, eight, nine, ten, then I let it go again. / Why did you let it go? Because it bit my finger so. / Which finger did it bite? This little finger on my right.","learners":"Listen and watch the actions."},{"teacher":"Say it again; invite learners to join with actions.","learners":"Say the rhyme together with actions."},{"teacher":"Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Choose a rhyme they like and lead."}]},{"activity":"Oral conversation: conversation on a picture","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.9","steps":[{"teacher":"Show the picture of a fisherman with his net.","learners":"Look carefully."},{"teacher":"Ask: What is happening in the picture? Who is doing what? What is happening around them? Then: What might happen next?","learners":"Answer in their own words; every learner gets a chance."},{"teacher":"Let learners imagine and make up a short story from the picture.","learners":"Tell their stories to the class."}]},{"activity":"Story - Day 1 (a story about a lost thing that is found)","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.10","steps":[{"teacher":"Discuss the title or picture of the story with the learners.","learners":"Talk about what they see and what the story may be about."},{"teacher":"Read the story aloud with expression and proper voice modulation. Learners should not simply repeat after you.","learners":"Listen carefully and enjoy the story."},{"teacher":"Discuss the story: factual, logical, vocabulary-based, judgment or opinion questions (today's focus: vocabulary-based: What does this word mean? Which word in the story means the same as ...?). Begin in the home language if needed.","learners":"Think and respond thoughtfully; every learner takes part."},{"teacher":"Read the story again slowly, pointing to each word. Make sure each learner has a copy and follows with a finger.","learners":"Follow each word with their finger."},{"teacher":"Ask learners to read in small groups; select a group leader who helps the others. Learners read one sentence at a time while the others point with fingers.","learners":"Read with the help of one another."}]},{"activity":"Sound-symbol: oral and level games","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.12","steps":[{"teacher":"Say words and ask learners to identify the first, second or last sound. Example: pan - first sound p, second sound a, third sound n; log: l, o, g; cup: c, u, p.","learners":"Say the first, second or last sound of the word."},{"teacher":"Write the sounds or words for the day on the board and give each level group its task (see the level table).","learners":"Work in small groups and share their answers."},{"teacher":"Say each word clearly with distinct pronunciation. Give learners enough time to respond and think; use words learners commonly use at home (regional language and the medium of instruction).","learners":"Think, say and write the sounds."}]},{"activity":"Mind mapping: 'wedding'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Small group (level-wise) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.14","steps":[{"teacher":"Choose a word that can generate many related words: 'wedding'. Ask: 'What words come to your mind when you hear the word wedding?' Write the answers on the board or floor.","learners":"Say words they link with 'wedding'."},{"teacher":"Discuss the words: what they mean and how they are connected.","learners":"Explain their words and listen to others."},{"teacher":"In small groups, let the learners classify the words (Clothes: saree, dhoti, jewellery, flowers; Food: rice, fish, sweets, curd; Things: music, lights, gifts, mandap).","learners":"Sort the words into groups."},{"teacher":"Give the individual tasks by level and help each learner.","learners":"Work individually; read the work aloud at the end if time allows."}]}],"levelTasks":[{"activity":"Story - Day 1: individual tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.10","tasks":{"Beginner":"Circle or search for a favourite word or letter in the story and say it aloud. If a learner cannot draw a circle, write words on the board and ask them to identify them.","Letter":"Find, read and write favourite words from the story.","Word":"Find the consonant clusters in the story, read them and write them in the notebook.","Para":"Silently read the story from the textbook; find unfamiliar words and try to understand them; find rhyming words, use them in sentences and write in the notebook; ask other groups for meanings; make questions in groups.","Story":"Silently read the story; find unfamiliar words and rhyming words; practise reading with emotion; one group reads sentences formed with consonant clusters to the other group; ask and answer group questions (information, thinking and opinion questions)."}},{"activity":"Sound-symbol games by level (small groups)","source":"M","ref":"p.12","tasks":{"Beginner":"'What is the first sound in the word rat?' 'Is there a letter that makes the sound /r/?' 'Can you name objects that start with the letter R?' Learners think and share names in the group.","Letter":"Write the rhyming ending -ap on the board and ask learners to add new letters to form words: c + ap = cap, m + ap = map, t + ap = tap.","Word":"Say a word and tell its sounds, for example 'sun' = /s/ + /u/ + /n/. Then tell what word is formed if /r/ is put before 'at': r + at = rat. Do 8-10 such combinations; at first learners may form meaningless words, later only meaningful words.","Para":"Write two or three sounds on the board (for example Br, cl, st) and let the learners form words that start with those sounds; this builds a word list for the learner.","Story":"Write two or three sounds on the board (for example Br, cl, st) and let the learners form words that start with those sounds; this builds a word list for the learner."}},{"activity":"Mind mapping 'wedding': level tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.14","tasks":{"Beginner":"Circle all the words that contain the letter 'S' on the board; make a list. See how many learners find the most words.","Letter":"Circle all the words that contain the letter 'S' and make a list of them.","Word":"Use 4-5 words (for example curd, fish, rice, dhoti, gifts) to form sentences, starting with words of one or two syllables. Example: Dream - I had a dream last night.","Para":"Choose any five words from the map and create a story with them. Use consonant clusters correctly, read the story aloud, correct mistakes of sentence structure, spelling or grammar, then display it on the wall.","Story":"Choose any five words from the map and create a story with them. Use consonant clusters correctly, read the story aloud, correct mistakes of sentence structure, spelling or grammar, then display it on the wall."}}],"organisation":[{"grouping":"Whole class (big group)","how":"All learners of all levels sit in a 'U' shape arranged by level (Beginner, Letter, Word, Para, Story) so that the move to small groups is easy.","activities":["Warm-up: Rhyme - 'I caught a Fish Alive'","Oral conversation: conversation on a picture","Story (Day 1 of the story): reading aloud and discussion","Sound-symbol activity: oral sound awareness","Mind mapping (Day 1): the word 'wedding'"]},{"grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","how":"Learners of similar levels work together; the teacher gives each group a task for its level and spends more time with learners who need support. Rotate responsibilities (for example group leader).","activities":["Story: reading in small groups","Sound-symbol games by level","Mind mapping: classify the words"]},{"grouping":"Individual","how":"Each learner works on a task for their own level; the teacher moves around, observes difficulties and supports individuals.","activities":["Story: level-wise individual tasks","Mind mapping: level-wise individual tasks","Daily reading (10 minutes)"]}],"materials":["Rhyme chart or board (optional)","Picture card of a fisherman with his net","A story from the school library (a story about a lost thing that is found)","a copy for each learner","Story book copies","Story book","notebooks","board","Board","chalk","letter cards","chalk (or floor)","word cards (optional)","Notebooks","Library books or storybooks"],"outcomes":["Learners take part in the oral conversation and speak without fear.","Learners show understanding of the story in the discussion and complete the task for their level.","Learners respond to the sound-symbol task for today (Identifying the first, second and last sound (bed, run, zip)) at their own level.","Learners add words to the mind map and use them in sentences or a story at their level.","Each learner reads a book for 10 minutes."],"observation":["Observe each learner's reading and writing during the individual tasks; note who needs individual support and how many learners share the same difficulty.","Note any learner whose level is improving; move the learner to the next level group when you see steady progress (manual p.5).","Record each learner's progress for the day in the notebook, according to the learner's level (manual p.4).","Use today's observations to adjust tomorrow's plan (manual p.5)."],"teacherNotes":["Story selection: the manual asks teachers to use picture story books or stories in the school library. Today's suggested theme (a story about a lost thing that is found) is a planning suggestion; use any suitable story you have.","Sound-symbol: for the first 4-5 days, play sound-based games with the learners at word level. Include the sounds learners find difficult when you prepare the Class Transaction Plan.","Mind mapping topic for this day: 'wedding'. The manual's example uses the word 'shop'; today's topic follows the same method.","Pace: the manual says not to assume all learners progress at the same speed. Repeat a day's activity with the groups that need it before moving on.","Special needs: give extra time and prepare materials for slower learners; seat learners with hearing or vision difficulty at the front; for learners who reverse or confuse letters, trace letters on the letter card with a finger and write with dots to trace with a pencil (manual p.6)."],"components":[{"no":1,"key":"warmup","name":"Warm-up activities","keywords":["Rhyme - 'I caught a Fish Alive'","two learners lead"],"rows":[1]},{"no":2,"key":"oral","name":"Oral Discussion","keywords":["conversation on a picture","every learner speaks"],"rows":[2]},{"no":3,"key":"story","name":"Story","keywords":["Day 1","title / picture talk","read aloud with expression","vocabulary-based questions","re-read pointing","group reading","level tasks"],"rows":[3,4,5]},{"no":4,"key":"sound","name":"Sound symbol games, Sound separation-pairing","keywords":["oral sound awareness","first / second / last sound","level games in small groups"],"rows":[6,7]},{"no":5,"key":"mindwrite","name":"Mind Mapping (Day 1)","keywords":["mind map: wedding","classify the words","level task: circle letter S / sentences / story"],"rows":[8,9,10]},{"no":6,"key":"reading","name":"Daily reading","keywords":["library book","read alone","teacher listens"],"rows":[11]}],"preLesson":null},{"programme":"TARL Literacy","id":"lit-042","day":42,"phase":1,"phaseLabel":"Phase 1 (Days 1-45)","title":"Saturday: drama presentation","dayType":"Saturday drama + Self-writing","focus":"Consonant clusters: nd (hand, sand) | Self-writing: the story we acted out (a story about a lost thing that is found)","duration":70,"objectives":["Listen, speak and answer in the oral conversation (listening and storytelling).","Express a story through role play, using voice, facial expressions and gestures.","Develop sound-symbol skills: Consonant clusters: nd (hand, sand).","Write about the story and review the writing.","Read independently for 10 minutes every day."],"sequence":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Singing and Spinning","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Learners sit in a circle and pass a small object while you clap with your back turned; when the clapping stops, the learner holding it sings a song, recites a poem or tells a joke. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Pass the object round the circle; sing, recite or tell a joke when the clapping stops.","tlm":"A small object (chalk or pencil)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","n":1},{"activity":"Oral conversation: listening and storytelling","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Tell an interesting story starter and involve the learners: 'I woke up and everything in my house was upside down. What did I do?' Let learners imagine and continue the story.","learners":"Listen to the teacher, then imagine and continue the story. Learners can also recite a rhyme or story they know.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.9","n":2},{"activity":"Dramatic presentation: introduction and reading","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Explain what a dramatic presentation is and how it is done. Provide stories discussed during the week and read one aloud once more. Para and Story level learners support Beginner and Letter level learners in reading.","learners":"Listen, read along, then each learner chooses a character.","tlm":"Stories discussed in the week (a story about a grandmother's tale; a story about a lost thing that is found)","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":3},{"activity":"Dramatic presentation: planning in small groups","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":8,"teacher":"Each group discusses and plans dialogues; Para or Story level learners write the dialogues. Groups prepare their dramatic presentation.","learners":"Choose characters, plan and rehearse dialogues with facial expressions and gestures.","tlm":"Story, paper for dialogues","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":4},{"activity":"Dramatic presentation: performances and feedback","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":7,"teacher":"Learners sit in a U shape. Each group presents; after each performance, watching learners say what they enjoyed and what could be improved.","learners":"Perform in turn; watch; give feedback.","tlm":"Open space (U-shape seating)","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":5},{"activity":"Consonant clusters: introduction","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":4,"teacher":"Two-letter clusters: after same-letter clusters, familiarise learners with clusters of two different letters ('nd' as in hand, sand, pond). Discuss the words, ask learners to pronounce them and to frame sentences using them.","learners":"Listen, pronounce the cluster and say words that contain it.","tlm":"Board and chalk, words list (hand sand pond wind band)","source":"M","ref":"p.16","n":6},{"activity":"Consonant cluster game: Who is Whose Friend?","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":6,"teacher":"Prepare cards: some with broken parts of conjunct consonants (b + l, c + r, s + t) and some with the full form (bl as in black, cr as in crab, st as in star). Take out all the cards. Observe closely and help learners who need support.","learners":"Match each full form with its broken parts and discover 'who is whose friend'.","tlm":"Broken-part cards and full-form cards","source":"M","ref":"p.17","n":7},{"activity":"Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on the story we acted out (a story about a lost thing that is found)","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Start a conversation about the story used for the drama: 'the story we acted out (a story about a lost thing that is found)'. Involve all learners with open-ended questions.","learners":"Take part in the discussion and share thoughts freely.","tlm":"Picture card or topic on the board","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":8},{"activity":"Self-writing: individual writing","grouping":"Individual","minutes":7,"teacher":"Give each level its task (see level table). Let learners take ownership of what they draw and write; mistakes are fine.","learners":"Draw and write about the topic at their level.","tlm":"Notebooks, crayons or pencils","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":9},{"activity":"Self-writing: review and reading back","grouping":"Individual","minutes":3,"teacher":"Ask each learner 'What did you draw or write?' and have them read it aloud once. Word-level learners read to the group; discuss spelling, punctuation and sentence structure. Help beginners by writing their text in the notebook for them if needed.","learners":"Read what they wrote; correct mistakes after listening to their own reading.","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":10},{"activity":"Daily reading (10 minutes)","grouping":"Individual","minutes":10,"teacher":"Give each learner a library book or any storybook. Move around, listen to individual readers and note their level.","learners":"Read independently a book of their choice.","tlm":"Library books or storybooks","source":"M","ref":"p.7","n":11}],"procedures":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Singing and Spinning","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","steps":[{"teacher":"Seat the learners in a circle; give a small object to one learner.","learners":"Sit in a circle."},{"teacher":"Stand outside the circle with your back to them and clap steadily; they pass the object.","learners":"Pass the object while the clapping continues."},{"teacher":"Stop clapping; the learner holding the object sings, recites or tells a joke.","learners":"Perform, and everybody claps."}]},{"activity":"Oral conversation: listening and storytelling","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.9","steps":[{"teacher":"Say the starter: 'I woke up and everything in my house was upside down. What did I do?'","learners":"Listen and imagine."},{"teacher":"Ask learners to continue the story one by one. Encourage those who speak less.","learners":"Add ideas to the story."},{"teacher":"Invite a learner to recite a poem or rhyme they know.","learners":"Recite and listen to others."}]},{"activity":"Saturday special: dramatic presentation","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.11","steps":[{"teacher":"Explain what a dramatic presentation is and how it can be done. Give the groups the stories discussed during the week.","learners":"Listen to the explanation."},{"teacher":"Read a story aloud once more. Learners at story and paragraph level support those at beginner and letter level in reading.","learners":"Read along; helpers support their friends."},{"teacher":"After reading, each learner chooses a character from the story.","learners":"Choose a role (boys may play girl roles and girls may play boy roles)."},{"teacher":"In groups, learners discuss and plan the dialogues; paragraph or story level learners write the dialogues.","learners":"Plan and write dialogues together."},{"teacher":"Learners sit in a U shape. Each group presents its drama. After each performance, ask what the audience enjoyed and what could be improved.","learners":"Perform, watch and give kind feedback."}]},{"activity":"Consonant clusters (nd) and the game 'Who is Whose Friend?'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.16-17","steps":[{"teacher":"Two-letter clusters: after same-letter clusters, familiarise learners with clusters of two different letters ('nd' as in hand, sand, pond). Discuss the words, ask learners to pronounce them and to frame sentences using them.","learners":"Listen, pronounce and find words in the text."},{"teacher":"Write the words on the board: hand sand pond wind band. Read them aloud with distinct pronunciation of the cluster.","learners":"Read the words aloud; point to the cluster in each word."},{"teacher":"Prepare cards: some with broken parts of conjunct consonants (b + l, c + r, s + t) and some with the full form (bl as in black, cr as in crab, st as in star). Take out all the cards.","learners":"Match each full form with its broken parts and discover 'who is whose friend'."}]},{"activity":"Self-writing: 'Discussion, Writing, Self-review'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.15","steps":[{"teacher":"Start a conversation about the story used for the drama: 'the story we acted out (a story about a lost thing that is found)'. Involve all learners with open-ended questions.","learners":"Discuss and answer questions."},{"teacher":"Give writing time at each level: draw then write (Beginner), write about what they liked (Letter), a sentence (Word), a paragraph or story on a topic of their choice (Para/Story).","learners":"Write at their level and take ownership of the work."},{"teacher":"Review: ask 'What did you draw or write?' Have each learner read the text aloud once. Support with writing if needed.","learners":"Read aloud, listen to their pronunciation and correct mistakes."}]}],"levelTasks":[{"activity":"Drama: roles by level","source":"M","ref":"p.11","tasks":{"Beginner":"Take a character role and say or act short lines with help from Para and Story level learners.","Letter":"Take a character role and say or act short lines with help from Para and Story level learners.","Word":"Take a role and speak the dialogues; help rehearse.","Para":"Write the dialogues for the group and support Beginner, Letter and Word level learners throughout.","Story":"Write the dialogues for the group and support Beginner, Letter and Word level learners throughout."}},{"activity":"Consonant clusters (nd): level tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.16-17","tasks":{"Beginner":"Listen to the sound of the cluster and point to it in a word; continue with letter-sound work (interpretation: the manual describes clusters for learners lagging in reading words and sentences).","Letter":"Listen to the cluster sound and pick words with the cluster from a word card (interpretation).","Word":"Find the cluster in the story or textbook words, read the words and write them in the notebook.","Para":"Form words and sentences using the cluster; read the sentences aloud.","Story":"Form words and sentences using the cluster; read the sentences aloud; use them in the story writing."}},{"activity":"Self-writing: level tasks and review","source":"M","ref":"p.15","tasks":{"Beginner":"Draw a picture about the discussion and then write a few sentences about it, expressing thoughts freely. Review: say what they drew or wrote; read the text aloud once; the teacher may write the text in the notebook for them.","Letter":"Write about what they liked, using drawing and writing; write any words or sentences they can. Review: read the text aloud once; correct punctuation mistakes using the Barakhadi chart.","Word":"Write a sentence based on the conversation. Mistakes in spelling, punctuation and sentence structure are fine. Review: read it to the group; discuss and correct mistakes together.","Para":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation.","Story":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation."}}],"organisation":[{"grouping":"Whole class (big group)","how":"All learners of all levels sit in a 'U' shape arranged by level (Beginner, Letter, Word, Para, Story) so that the move to small groups is easy.","activities":["Warm-up: Singing and Spinning","Oral conversation: listening and storytelling","Dramatic presentation: introduction and reading","Dramatic presentation: performances and feedback","Consonant clusters: introduction","Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on the story we acted out (a story about a lost thing that is found)"]},{"grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","how":"Learners of similar levels work together; the teacher gives each group a task for its level and spends more time with learners who need support. Rotate responsibilities (for example group leader).","activities":["Dramatic presentation: planning in small groups","Consonant cluster game: Who is Whose Friend?"]},{"grouping":"Individual","how":"Each learner works on a task for their own level; the teacher moves around, observes difficulties and supports individuals.","activities":["Self-writing: individual writing","Self-writing: review and reading back","Daily reading (10 minutes)"]}],"materials":["A small object (chalk or pencil)","Stories discussed in the week (a story about a grandmother's tale; a story about a lost thing that is found)","Story","paper for dialogues","Open space (U-shape seating)","Board","chalk","words list (hand sand pond wind band)","Broken-part cards","full-form cards","Picture card or topic on the board","Notebooks","crayons or pencils","Library books or storybooks"],"outcomes":["Learners take part in the oral conversation and speak without fear.","Learners present a role in the group drama and give feedback to others.","Learners respond to the sound-symbol task for today (Consonant clusters: nd (hand, sand)) at their own level.","Learners write about the story at their level and read it aloud.","Each learner reads a book for 10 minutes."],"observation":["Observe each learner's reading and writing during the individual tasks; note who needs individual support and how many learners share the same difficulty.","Note any learner whose level is improving; move the learner to the next level group when you see steady progress (manual p.5).","Record each learner's progress for the day in the notebook, according to the learner's level (manual p.4).","Use today's observations to adjust tomorrow's plan (manual p.5)."],"teacherNotes":["Saturday: this plan assumes Day 1 is a Monday (six teaching days per week). If your school week is different, hold the drama presentation on your Saturday and keep the other days in sequence.","Consonant clusters: do these activities daily for learners who find reading complex words hard; the aim is to remove the fear of reading clusters. Teachers may carry out similar activities on their own.","Writing has two parts, content and sequence: encourage learners to read what they wrote, improve it and rewrite it for clarity and correctness (manual p.15).","Pace: the manual says not to assume all learners progress at the same speed. Repeat a day's activity with the groups that need it before moving on.","Special needs: give extra time and prepare materials for slower learners; seat learners with hearing or vision difficulty at the front; for learners who reverse or confuse letters, trace letters on the letter card with a finger and write with dots to trace with a pencil (manual p.6)."],"components":[{"no":1,"key":"warmup","name":"Warm-up activities","keywords":["Singing and Spinning","two learners lead"],"rows":[1]},{"no":2,"key":"oral","name":"Oral Discussion","keywords":["listening and storytelling","every learner speaks"],"rows":[2]},{"no":3,"key":"story","name":"Story (Saturday: dramatic presentation)","keywords":["Saturday drama","choose a character","plan dialogues","perform in U shape","feedback"],"rows":[3,4,5]},{"no":4,"key":"sound","name":"Sound symbol games, Sound separation-pairing","keywords":["consonant cluster 'nd'","pronounce and find words","game: Who is Whose Friend?"],"rows":[6,7]},{"no":5,"key":"mindwrite","name":"Individual-Writing (Day 2)","keywords":["discussion","write at own level","self-review (read aloud)"],"rows":[8,9,10]},{"no":6,"key":"reading","name":"Daily reading","keywords":["library book","read alone","teacher listens"],"rows":[11]}],"preLesson":null},{"programme":"TARL Literacy","id":"lit-043","day":43,"phase":1,"phaseLabel":"Phase 1 (Days 1-45)","title":"Story: a story about a lost thing that is found (Day 2)","dayType":"Story Day 2 + Self-writing","focus":"Barakhadi / alphabet and phonics chart (line 8, letter 'j') | Self-writing: a picture of a railway station","duration":70,"objectives":["Listen, speak and answer in the oral conversation (What did you see on your way?).","Retell the story, read it with expression, ask and answer questions about it and write answers.","Develop sound-symbol skills: Barakhadi / alphabet and phonics chart (line 8, letter 'j').","Write about a topic at their own level and review the writing (a picture of a railway station).","Read independently for 10 minutes every day."],"sequence":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Rain clapping","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Everyone stands in a circle with eyes closed and keeps clapping: first one finger, then two, three, four and finally five fingers. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Stand in a circle, close the eyes and clap with 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 fingers.","tlm":"After the activity ask: Was it a gentle rain or a storm? How did you feel?","source":"M","ref":"p.8","n":1},{"activity":"Oral conversation: What did you see on your way?","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Ask learners to describe what they saw on their way to school. If they are hesitant, begin yourself: 'This morning I saw a flock of ducks crossing the road and a girl carrying water. What did you see?'","learners":"Describe what they saw on the way to school and connect with what others share.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.9","n":2},{"activity":"Story (Day 2 of the story): retelling","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":6,"teacher":"Ask learners to retell yesterday's story in their own words. Prompt with questions on the beginning, middle and end.","learners":"Retell the story using their own words.","tlm":"The same story book as yesterday","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":3},{"activity":"Story: reading with actions and group questions","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":9,"teacher":"Learners practise reading with actions and expressions; one learner per group reads aloud to the class. Guide groups to make questions about the story (guide initially). Groups take turns to ask and answer each other's questions. Word-level learners also read aloud the consonants learned on the first day.","learners":"Read with actions; make questions (word-level learners help write them); ask and answer questions with another group.","tlm":"Story book, slate or paper for questions","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":4},{"activity":"Story: writing answers individually","grouping":"Individual","minutes":5,"teacher":"Para and Story level learners write answers to all questions individually; read and correct their responses after they finish.","learners":"Write the answers in their notebooks; Beginner/Letter/Word learners read or listen and answer orally.","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":5},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart: big group reading","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":3,"teacher":"Show the Barakhadi chart and ask which letter they like. Read the letter 'j' on the chart; learners listen carefully and point to it on their own chart (they do not repeat after you).","learners":"Listen and point to the letter on their own chart.","tlm":"Barakhadi chart, alphabet or phonics chart","source":"M","ref":"p.13","n":6},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart: small-group practice","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Learners practise reading the alphabet or phonics chart in groups and help each other. One learner per group reads aloud. Occasionally ask learners to identify the sounds of letters. Give each level its group task.","learners":"Read the chart in groups; one learner reads aloud; do the level task.","tlm":"Alphabet or phonics chart, board or floor","source":"M","ref":"p.13","n":7},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart: individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":2,"teacher":"Give each learner an individual task for their level and observe closely; assist any learner who needs individual support.","learners":"Say and write a letter or word, a sentence or a short paragraph (by level).","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.13","n":8},{"activity":"Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on a picture of a railway station","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Start a conversation about a situation: 'a picture of a railway station'. Involve all learners and ask open-ended questions.","learners":"Take part in the discussion and share thoughts freely.","tlm":"Picture card or topic on the board","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":9},{"activity":"Self-writing: individual writing","grouping":"Individual","minutes":7,"teacher":"Give each level its task (see level table). Let learners take ownership of what they draw and write; mistakes are fine.","learners":"Draw and write about the topic at their level.","tlm":"Notebooks, crayons or pencils","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":10},{"activity":"Self-writing: review and reading back","grouping":"Individual","minutes":3,"teacher":"Ask each learner 'What did you draw or write?' and have them read it aloud once. Word-level learners read to the group; discuss spelling, punctuation and sentence structure. Help beginners by writing their text in the notebook for them if needed.","learners":"Read what they wrote; correct mistakes after listening to their own reading.","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":11},{"activity":"Daily reading (10 minutes)","grouping":"Individual","minutes":10,"teacher":"Give each learner a library book or any storybook. Move around, listen to individual readers and note their level.","learners":"Read independently a book of their choice.","tlm":"Library books or storybooks","source":"M","ref":"p.7","n":12}],"procedures":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Rain clapping","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","steps":[{"teacher":"Stand the learners in a circle and ask them to close their eyes. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Stand in a circle and close their eyes."},{"teacher":"Start clapping with one finger; then two fingers, three, four and finally five fingers.","learners":"Keep clapping, copying the change of fingers."},{"teacher":"After the activity ask: Was it a gentle rain or a storm? How did you feel?","learners":"Tell how they felt and what the sounds reminded them of."}]},{"activity":"Oral conversation: What did you see on your way?","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.9","steps":[{"teacher":"Ask: 'What did you see on your way to school today?'","learners":"Think about the way to school."},{"teacher":"If learners hesitate, start: 'This morning I saw a flock of ducks crossing the road and a girl carrying water. What did you see?'","learners":"Listen to the model and then share their own observations."},{"teacher":"Connect learners' answers with each other.","learners":"Listen and add what they noticed."}]},{"activity":"Story - Day 2 (a story about a lost thing that is found)","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.11","steps":[{"teacher":"Ask learners to retell the story they read yesterday in their own words.","learners":"Retell, helping each other remember."},{"teacher":"In small groups learners practise reading the story using actions and expressions; one learner from each group then reads aloud to the class.","learners":"Read with actions and expression; a representative reads aloud."},{"teacher":"Guide the groups to come up with questions about the story (guide initially). Word-level learners can support by helping write them down.","learners":"Make questions together."},{"teacher":"Groups take turns to ask and answer each other's questions. Useful kinds: questions whose answer is not in the text; questions needing thinking beyond the text; questions asking for an opinion.","learners":"Ask, answer and discuss in the groups."},{"teacher":"Word-level learners also read aloud the consonants they learned on the first day.","learners":"Read the consonant clusters aloud."}]},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart activity (line 8)","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Small group (level-wise) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.13","steps":[{"teacher":"Show the Barakhadi chart and ask the learners which letter they like. Where is the letter 'j'?","learners":"Look for the letter on the chart."},{"teacher":"Read the letter 'j' on the chart. Learners listen and point to it on their own chart. Make sure they do not repeat after you.","learners":"Listen and point to the letter."},{"teacher":"Learners read the alphabet or phonics chart in their groups and help each other; one learner from each group comes forward to read aloud.","learners":"Read in groups; the representative reads aloud."},{"teacher":"Occasionally ask them to identify the sounds of letters from the chart.","learners":"Say the sound of the letter you point to."},{"teacher":"As an extra activity, write some letters on the floor, call out each letter one by one and let the learners jump onto the correct letter.","learners":"Jump onto the letter that is called."}]},{"activity":"Self-writing: 'Discussion, Writing, Self-review'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.15","steps":[{"teacher":"Start a conversation about a situation: 'a picture of a railway station'. Involve all learners and ask open-ended questions.","learners":"Discuss and answer questions."},{"teacher":"Give writing time at each level: draw then write (Beginner), write about what they liked (Letter), a sentence (Word), a paragraph or story on a topic of their choice (Para/Story).","learners":"Write at their level and take ownership of the work."},{"teacher":"Review: ask 'What did you draw or write?' Have each learner read the text aloud once. Support with writing if needed.","learners":"Read aloud, listen to their pronunciation and correct mistakes."}]}],"levelTasks":[{"activity":"Story - Day 2: level-wise tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.11","tasks":{"Beginner":"Retell with the group by pointing to pictures or words; read aloud with group support (interpretation of the manual's group reading task).","Letter":"Read with the group, pointing to words; say the letters and words they know (interpretation of the manual's group reading task).","Word":"Support the group in writing the questions; read aloud the consonant clusters learned on the first day.","Para":"Ask the group's questions to another group, discuss them, then write answers to all questions individually; the teacher reads and corrects.","Story":"Ask the group's questions to another group, discuss them, then write answers to all questions individually; the teacher reads and corrects."}},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart: level tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.13","tasks":{"Beginner":"Small group: read the chart in the group; find and write favourite letters from the line. Individual: say and write a letter of their choice.","Letter":"Small group: read the chart; find and write favourite letters or words from any line. Individual: say a word on their own that begins with any letter.","Word":"Small group: write one or two lines of letters on the board or floor and use them to form words. Individual: speak and write sentences using words they know.","Para":"Small group: prepare word lists using the Barakhadi chart (for example items found in a shop or in the kitchen). Individual: write short paragraphs using the words formed with the Barakhadi chart.","Story":"Small group: prepare word lists using the Barakhadi chart. Individual: write short paragraphs using the words formed with the Barakhadi chart."}},{"activity":"Self-writing: level tasks and review","source":"M","ref":"p.15","tasks":{"Beginner":"Draw a picture about the discussion and then write a few sentences about it, expressing thoughts freely. Review: say what they drew or wrote; read the text aloud once; the teacher may write the text in the notebook for them.","Letter":"Write about what they liked, using drawing and writing; write any words or sentences they can. Review: read the text aloud once; correct punctuation mistakes using the Barakhadi chart.","Word":"Write a sentence based on the conversation. Mistakes in spelling, punctuation and sentence structure are fine. Review: read it to the group; discuss and correct mistakes together.","Para":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation.","Story":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation."}}],"organisation":[{"grouping":"Whole class (big group)","how":"All learners of all levels sit in a 'U' shape arranged by level (Beginner, Letter, Word, Para, Story) so that the move to small groups is easy.","activities":["Warm-up: Rain clapping","Oral conversation: What did you see on your way?","Story (Day 2 of the story): retelling","Barakhadi chart: big group reading","Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on a picture of a railway station"]},{"grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","how":"Learners of similar levels work together; the teacher gives each group a task for its level and spends more time with learners who need support. Rotate responsibilities (for example group leader).","activities":["Story: reading with actions and group questions","Barakhadi chart: small-group practice"]},{"grouping":"Individual","how":"Each learner works on a task for their own level; the teacher moves around, observes difficulties and supports individuals.","activities":["Story: writing answers individually","Barakhadi chart: individual tasks","Self-writing: individual writing","Self-writing: review and reading back","Daily reading (10 minutes)"]}],"materials":["After the activity ask: Was it a gentle rain or a storm? How did you feel?","The same story book as yesterday","Story book","slate or paper for questions","Notebooks","Barakhadi chart","alphabet or phonics chart","Alphabet or phonics chart","board or floor","Picture card or topic on the board","crayons or pencils","Library books or storybooks"],"outcomes":["Learners take part in the oral conversation and speak without fear.","Learners retell the story, read with expression and ask or answer questions at their level.","Learners respond to the sound-symbol task for today (Barakhadi / alphabet and phonics chart (line 8, letter 'j')) at their own level.","Learners write about the topic at their level and read it aloud.","Each learner reads a book for 10 minutes."],"observation":["Observe each learner's reading and writing during the individual tasks; note who needs individual support and how many learners share the same difficulty.","Note any learner whose level is improving; move the learner to the next level group when you see steady progress (manual p.5).","Record each learner's progress for the day in the notebook, according to the learner's level (manual p.4).","Use today's observations to adjust tomorrow's plan (manual p.5)."],"teacherNotes":["Questions to elicit on Day 2: information questions (answer not in the text), thinking questions (needs knowledge beyond the text) and opinion questions (feedback on something in the text).","Barakhadi: learners who need extra time should get repeated practice using one or two sound units at a time. Topic-based discussion helps oral expression, thinking and understanding.","Writing has two parts, content and sequence: encourage learners to read what they wrote, improve it and rewrite it for clarity and correctness (manual p.15).","Pace: the manual says not to assume all learners progress at the same speed. Repeat a day's activity with the groups that need it before moving on.","Special needs: give extra time and prepare materials for slower learners; seat learners with hearing or vision difficulty at the front; for learners who reverse or confuse letters, trace letters on the letter card with a finger and write with dots to trace with a pencil (manual p.6)."],"components":[{"no":1,"key":"warmup","name":"Warm-up activities","keywords":["Rain clapping","two learners lead"],"rows":[1]},{"no":2,"key":"oral","name":"Oral Discussion","keywords":["What did you see on your way?","every learner speaks"],"rows":[2]},{"no":3,"key":"story","name":"Story","keywords":["Day 2","retell","read with actions","group questions","ask and answer","write answers (Para/Story)"],"rows":[3,4,5]},{"no":4,"key":"sound","name":"Sound symbol games, Sound separation-pairing","keywords":["Barakhadi / alphabet chart","listen and point (no repeating)","group reading","level tasks"],"rows":[6,7,8]},{"no":5,"key":"mindwrite","name":"Individual-Writing (Day 2)","keywords":["discussion","write at own level","self-review (read aloud)"],"rows":[9,10,11]},{"no":6,"key":"reading","name":"Daily reading","keywords":["library book","read alone","teacher listens"],"rows":[12]}],"preLesson":null},{"programme":"TARL Literacy","id":"lit-044","day":44,"phase":1,"phaseLabel":"Phase 1 (Days 1-45)","title":"Story: a story about a sports day (Day 1)","dayType":"Story Day 1 + Mind mapping","focus":"Language game: The Story Continued Slowly | Mind map: playground","duration":70,"objectives":["Listen, speak and answer in the oral conversation (familiar topic).","Listen to and read a story with understanding; discuss it in big and small groups and respond at their own level.","Develop sound-symbol skills: Language game: The Story Continued Slowly.","Build vocabulary through a mind map ('playground') and use the words at their own level.","Read independently for 10 minutes every day."],"sequence":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Writing with body parts","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Learners stand in a circle. Demonstrate writing the word 'tree' in the air with a finger, then ask them to write it with different body parts. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Write the word 'tree' in the air with the finger, then with the head, shoulders, knees or elbows.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.8","n":1},{"activity":"Oral conversation: familiar topic","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Hold a conversation on the topic 'something I am good at'. Give each learner a chance to speak; be patient with learners who need extra time.","learners":"Talk about the topic and listen to others.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.9","n":2},{"activity":"Story (Day 1 of the story): reading aloud and discussion","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":8,"teacher":"Discuss the title or picture of the story with the learners. Read the story aloud with expression and voice modulation (learners do not repeat after you). Discuss it, with emphasis on judgment questions. Read it again slowly, pointing to each word.","learners":"Talk about the title/picture; listen; answer questions; follow each word with a finger in their own copy.","tlm":"A story from the school library (a story about a sports day), a copy for each learner","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":3},{"activity":"Story: reading in small groups","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":7,"teacher":"Form level-wise groups with a group leader. Learners read the story one sentence at a time while the others follow with their fingers. Para and Story level learners practise reading with emotion and expression.","learners":"Read the story sentence by sentence, supporting each other; the group leader helps.","tlm":"Story book copies","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":4},{"activity":"Story: level-wise individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":5,"teacher":"Give each learner the task for their level (see level table) and support those who need it.","learners":"Beginner/Letter: find and write favourite words or letters. Word: find consonant clusters. Para/Story: silently read, find unfamiliar and rhyming words.","tlm":"Story book, notebooks, board","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":5},{"activity":"Language game: The Story Continued Slowly","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Learners add one sentence each to a story, first orally, then in writing; some draw a picture and think of a title. Observe each learner and give help where needed.","learners":"Play the game, take turns and read or say the words they make.","tlm":"Board, notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.21","n":6},{"activity":"Mind mapping (Day 1): the word 'playground'","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Ask: 'What words come to your mind when you hear the word playground?' Write learners' answers on the board or floor (Para and Story level learners write the words themselves). Guide the map towards the learning objective. Example words: cricket, kabaddi, football, hide-and-seek, ball, bat, rope, swing, fun, run, laugh, jump.","learners":"Say words connected with 'playground'; share the meaning and feeling of words.","tlm":"Board, chalk (or floor)","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":7},{"activity":"Mind mapping: classify the words","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":4,"teacher":"Ask learners to classify the words in groups, for example: Games: cricket, kabaddi, football, hide-and-seek; Things: ball, bat, rope, swing; Feelings: fun, run, laugh, jump.","learners":"Sort the words into groups and say why.","tlm":"Board, chalk, word cards (optional)","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":8},{"activity":"Mind mapping: level-wise individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":6,"teacher":"Give each learner the individual task for their level; observe closely and give individual support. Display corrected stories on the wall.","learners":"Complete the task for their level (see level table).","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":9},{"activity":"Daily reading (10 minutes)","grouping":"Individual","minutes":10,"teacher":"Give each learner a library book or any storybook. Move around, listen to individual readers and note their level.","learners":"Read independently a book of their choice.","tlm":"Library books or storybooks","source":"M","ref":"p.7","n":10}],"procedures":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Writing with body parts","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","steps":[{"teacher":"Stand the learners in a circle. Demonstrate writing the word 'tree' in the air with your finger.","learners":"Watch and then copy with their own finger."},{"teacher":"Ask them to write it again using head and other body parts (head, shoulders, knees, ...).","learners":"Write the letters in the air with the named body part."},{"teacher":"Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Take turns to lead."}]},{"activity":"Oral conversation: familiar topic","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.9","steps":[{"teacher":"Introduce the topic: 'something I am good at'.","learners":"Think about their own experience."},{"teacher":"Ask open questions; give every learner a chance. Involve learners who speak less.","learners":"Speak freely and without fear."},{"teacher":"Praise efforts and sum up.","learners":"Listen and respect each other's ideas."}]},{"activity":"Story - Day 1 (a story about a sports day)","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.10","steps":[{"teacher":"Discuss the title or picture of the story with the learners.","learners":"Talk about what they see and what the story may be about."},{"teacher":"Read the story aloud with expression and proper voice modulation. Learners should not simply repeat after you.","learners":"Listen carefully and enjoy the story."},{"teacher":"Discuss the story: factual, logical, vocabulary-based, judgment or opinion questions (today's focus: judgment: Was the character right or wrong? Was that a good thing to do? Why?). Begin in the home language if needed.","learners":"Think and respond thoughtfully; every learner takes part."},{"teacher":"Read the story again slowly, pointing to each word. Make sure each learner has a copy and follows with a finger.","learners":"Follow each word with their finger."},{"teacher":"Ask learners to read in small groups; select a group leader who helps the others. Learners read one sentence at a time while the others point with fingers.","learners":"Read with the help of one another."}]},{"activity":"Language game: The Story Continued Slowly","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.21","steps":[{"teacher":"Say: 'Let us write a beautiful story together.' Each sentence must follow from the previous sentence. Start speaking orally first.","learners":"Listen and add one sentence each."},{"teacher":"Move to writing the story sentence by sentence; a few learners draw a picture and think of a title.","learners":"Write sentences; draw and think of a title."},{"teacher":"As learners get used to writing stories, discuss what the story will be like before writing.","learners":"Plan the story orally before writing."}]},{"activity":"Mind mapping: 'playground'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Small group (level-wise) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.14","steps":[{"teacher":"Choose a word that can generate many related words: 'playground'. Ask: 'What words come to your mind when you hear the word playground?' Write the answers on the board or floor.","learners":"Say words they link with 'playground'."},{"teacher":"Discuss the words: what they mean and how they are connected.","learners":"Explain their words and listen to others."},{"teacher":"In small groups, let the learners classify the words (Games: cricket, kabaddi, football, hide-and-seek; Things: ball, bat, rope, swing; Feelings: fun, run, laugh, jump).","learners":"Sort the words into groups."},{"teacher":"Give the individual tasks by level and help each learner.","learners":"Work individually; read the work aloud at the end if time allows."}]}],"levelTasks":[{"activity":"Story - Day 1: individual tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.10","tasks":{"Beginner":"Circle or search for a favourite word or letter in the story and say it aloud. If a learner cannot draw a circle, write words on the board and ask them to identify them.","Letter":"Find, read and write favourite words from the story.","Word":"Find the consonant clusters in the story, read them and write them in the notebook.","Para":"Silently read the story from the textbook; find unfamiliar words and try to understand them; find rhyming words, use them in sentences and write in the notebook; ask other groups for meanings; make questions in groups.","Story":"Silently read the story; find unfamiliar words and rhyming words; practise reading with emotion; one group reads sentences formed with consonant clusters to the other group; ask and answer group questions (information, thinking and opinion questions)."}},{"activity":"Language game: The Story Continued Slowly - level support","source":"I","ref":"p.21","tasks":{"Beginner":"Take part by saying or pointing to the letters involved and by listening carefully; Para and Story level partners help.","Letter":"Say the letters/sounds and give simple words they know.","Word":"Say and write words and short sentences for the game.","Para":"Write sentences with the words; help groups to record answers.","Story":"Write sentences or short stories with the words; help groups to record answers."}},{"activity":"Mind mapping 'playground': level tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.14","tasks":{"Beginner":"Circle all the words that contain the letter 'A' on the board; make a list. See how many learners find the most words.","Letter":"Circle all the words that contain the letter 'A' and make a list of them.","Word":"Use 4-5 words (for example bat, fun, run, ball, jump) to form sentences, starting with words of one or two syllables. Example: Dream - I had a dream last night.","Para":"Choose any five words from the map and create a story with them. Use consonant clusters correctly, read the story aloud, correct mistakes of sentence structure, spelling or grammar, then display it on the wall.","Story":"Choose any five words from the map and create a story with them. Use consonant clusters correctly, read the story aloud, correct mistakes of sentence structure, spelling or grammar, then display it on the wall."}}],"organisation":[{"grouping":"Whole class (big group)","how":"All learners of all levels sit in a 'U' shape arranged by level (Beginner, Letter, Word, Para, Story) so that the move to small groups is easy.","activities":["Warm-up: Writing with body parts","Oral conversation: familiar topic","Story (Day 1 of the story): reading aloud and discussion","Language game: The Story Continued Slowly","Mind mapping (Day 1): the word 'playground'"]},{"grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","how":"Learners of similar levels work together; the teacher gives each group a task for its level and spends more time with learners who need support. Rotate responsibilities (for example group leader).","activities":["Story: reading in small groups","Mind mapping: classify the words"]},{"grouping":"Individual","how":"Each learner works on a task for their own level; the teacher moves around, observes difficulties and supports individuals.","activities":["Story: level-wise individual tasks","Mind mapping: level-wise individual tasks","Daily reading (10 minutes)"]}],"materials":["A story from the school library (a story about a sports day)","a copy for each learner","Story book copies","Story book","notebooks","board","Board","chalk (or floor)","chalk","word cards (optional)","Notebooks","Library books or storybooks"],"outcomes":["Learners take part in the oral conversation and speak without fear.","Learners show understanding of the story in the discussion and complete the task for their level.","Learners respond to the sound-symbol task for today (Language game: The Story Continued Slowly) at their own level.","Learners add words to the mind map and use them in sentences or a story at their level.","Each learner reads a book for 10 minutes."],"observation":["Observe each learner's reading and writing during the individual tasks; note who needs individual support and how many learners share the same difficulty.","Note any learner whose level is improving; move the learner to the next level group when you see steady progress (manual p.5).","Record each learner's progress for the day in the notebook, according to the learner's level (manual p.4).","Use today's observations to adjust tomorrow's plan (manual p.5)."],"teacherNotes":["Story selection: the manual asks teachers to use picture story books or stories in the school library. Today's suggested theme (a story about a sports day) is a planning suggestion; use any suitable story you have.","The manual lists the letter and word games but does not fix the slot in the daily timetable where they are used. This plan places them in the 10-minute sound-symbol / alphabet slot (interpretation).","Mind mapping topic for this day: 'playground'. The manual's example uses the word 'shop'; today's topic follows the same method.","Pace: the manual says not to assume all learners progress at the same speed. Repeat a day's activity with the groups that need it before moving on.","Special needs: give extra time and prepare materials for slower learners; seat learners with hearing or vision difficulty at the front; for learners who reverse or confuse letters, trace letters on the letter card with a finger and write with dots to trace with a pencil (manual p.6)."],"components":[{"no":1,"key":"warmup","name":"Warm-up activities","keywords":["Writing with body parts","two learners lead"],"rows":[1]},{"no":2,"key":"oral","name":"Oral Discussion","keywords":["familiar topic","every learner speaks"],"rows":[2]},{"no":3,"key":"story","name":"Story","keywords":["Day 1","title / picture talk","read aloud with expression","judgment questions","re-read pointing","group reading","level tasks"],"rows":[3,4,5]},{"no":4,"key":"sound","name":"Sound symbol games, Sound separation-pairing","keywords":["The Story Continued Slowly","play in turns","level support"],"rows":[6]},{"no":5,"key":"mindwrite","name":"Mind Mapping (Day 1)","keywords":["mind map: playground","classify the words","level task: circle letter A / sentences / story"],"rows":[7,8,9]},{"no":6,"key":"reading","name":"Daily reading","keywords":["library book","read alone","teacher listens"],"rows":[10]}],"preLesson":null},{"programme":"TARL Literacy","id":"lit-045","day":45,"phase":1,"phaseLabel":"Phase 1 (Days 1-45)","title":"Story: a story about a sports day (Day 2)","dayType":"Story Day 2 + Self-writing","focus":"Language game: Singing and Spinning | Self-writing: helping at home","duration":70,"objectives":["Listen, speak and answer in the oral conversation (conversation on a picture).","Retell the story, read it with expression, ask and answer questions about it and write answers.","Develop sound-symbol skills: Language game: Singing and Spinning.","Write about a topic at their own level and review the writing (helping at home).","Read independently for 10 minutes every day."],"sequence":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Alphabet song (last-letter word chain)","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Say a word to the big group, for example 'tea'. Learners say a word that starts with the last letter ('a'). A learner who cannot say a word is out. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Say a word that starts with the last letter of the previous word; step out if unable to.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.8","n":1},{"activity":"Oral conversation: conversation on a picture","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Show a picture of a hospital waiting room and ask what is happening, who is doing what and what is happening around them. Let learners think creatively and even make up a story.","learners":"Look at the picture, answer questions and make up their own story about it.","tlm":"Picture card of a hospital waiting room","source":"M","ref":"p.9","n":2},{"activity":"Story (Day 2 of the story): retelling","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":6,"teacher":"Ask learners to retell yesterday's story in their own words. Prompt with questions on the beginning, middle and end.","learners":"Retell the story using their own words.","tlm":"The same story book as yesterday","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":3},{"activity":"Story: reading with actions and group questions","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":9,"teacher":"Learners practise reading with actions and expressions; one learner per group reads aloud to the class. Guide groups to make questions about the story (guide initially). Groups take turns to ask and answer each other's questions. Word-level learners also read aloud the consonants learned on the first day.","learners":"Read with actions; make questions (word-level learners help write them); ask and answer questions with another group.","tlm":"Story book, slate or paper for questions","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":4},{"activity":"Story: writing answers individually","grouping":"Individual","minutes":5,"teacher":"Para and Story level learners write answers to all questions individually; read and correct their responses after they finish.","learners":"Write the answers in their notebooks; Beginner/Letter/Word learners read or listen and answer orally.","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":5},{"activity":"Language game: Singing and Spinning","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Learners sit in a circle; a small object (chalk, pencil) is passed around while the teacher, back turned, claps steadily. Observe each learner and give help where needed.","learners":"Play the game, take turns and read or say the words they make.","tlm":"A small object (chalk or pencil)","source":"M","ref":"p.18","n":6},{"activity":"Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on helping at home","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Start a conversation about a picture card: 'helping at home'. Involve all learners and ask open-ended questions.","learners":"Take part in the discussion and share thoughts freely.","tlm":"Picture card or topic on the board","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":7},{"activity":"Self-writing: individual writing","grouping":"Individual","minutes":7,"teacher":"Give each level its task (see level table). Let learners take ownership of what they draw and write; mistakes are fine.","learners":"Draw and write about the topic at their level.","tlm":"Notebooks, crayons or pencils","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":8},{"activity":"Self-writing: review and reading back","grouping":"Individual","minutes":3,"teacher":"Ask each learner 'What did you draw or write?' and have them read it aloud once. Word-level learners read to the group; discuss spelling, punctuation and sentence structure. Help beginners by writing their text in the notebook for them if needed.","learners":"Read what they wrote; correct mistakes after listening to their own reading.","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":9},{"activity":"Daily reading (10 minutes)","grouping":"Individual","minutes":10,"teacher":"Give each learner a library book or any storybook. Move around, listen to individual readers and note their level.","learners":"Read independently a book of their choice.","tlm":"Library books or storybooks","source":"M","ref":"p.7","n":10}],"procedures":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Alphabet song (last-letter word chain)","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","steps":[{"teacher":"Say the word 'tea' to the big group and show that its last letter is 'a'.","learners":"Listen and think of a word starting with 'a'."},{"teacher":"Ask learners in turn to say a word that starts with the last letter of the previous word. Example: rain -> nest.","learners":"Say a word in turn; anyone who cannot say a word is out of the game."},{"teacher":"Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Lead the game when it is their turn."}]},{"activity":"Oral conversation: conversation on a picture","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.9","steps":[{"teacher":"Show the picture of a hospital waiting room.","learners":"Look carefully."},{"teacher":"Ask: What is happening in the picture? Who is doing what? What is happening around them? Then: How do the people feel? How can you tell?","learners":"Answer in their own words; every learner gets a chance."},{"teacher":"Let learners imagine and make up a short story from the picture.","learners":"Tell their stories to the class."}]},{"activity":"Story - Day 2 (a story about a sports day)","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.11","steps":[{"teacher":"Ask learners to retell the story they read yesterday in their own words.","learners":"Retell, helping each other remember."},{"teacher":"In small groups learners practise reading the story using actions and expressions; one learner from each group then reads aloud to the class.","learners":"Read with actions and expression; a representative reads aloud."},{"teacher":"Guide the groups to come up with questions about the story (guide initially). Word-level learners can support by helping write them down.","learners":"Make questions together."},{"teacher":"Groups take turns to ask and answer each other's questions. Useful kinds: questions whose answer is not in the text; questions needing thinking beyond the text; questions asking for an opinion.","learners":"Ask, answer and discuss in the groups."},{"teacher":"Word-level learners also read aloud the consonants they learned on the first day.","learners":"Read the consonant clusters aloud."}]},{"activity":"Language game: Singing and Spinning","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.18","steps":[{"teacher":"Seat the learners in a circle. Give one learner a small object such as a piece of chalk.","learners":"Sit in a circle and listen for the clapping."},{"teacher":"Stand outside the circle with your back to the learners and clap steadily. Stop clapping without warning.","learners":"Pass the object round while the clapping continues."},{"teacher":"Ask the learner holding the object when you stop to sing a song, recite a poem or tell a joke.","learners":"Sing, recite or tell a joke; the others listen and clap."}]},{"activity":"Self-writing: 'Discussion, Writing, Self-review'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.15","steps":[{"teacher":"Start a conversation about a picture card: 'helping at home'. Involve all learners and ask open-ended questions.","learners":"Discuss and answer questions."},{"teacher":"Give writing time at each level: draw then write (Beginner), write about what they liked (Letter), a sentence (Word), a paragraph or story on a topic of their choice (Para/Story).","learners":"Write at their level and take ownership of the work."},{"teacher":"Review: ask 'What did you draw or write?' Have each learner read the text aloud once. Support with writing if needed.","learners":"Read aloud, listen to their pronunciation and correct mistakes."}]}],"levelTasks":[{"activity":"Story - Day 2: level-wise tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.11","tasks":{"Beginner":"Retell with the group by pointing to pictures or words; read aloud with group support (interpretation of the manual's group reading task).","Letter":"Read with the group, pointing to words; say the letters and words they know (interpretation of the manual's group reading task).","Word":"Support the group in writing the questions; read aloud the consonant clusters learned on the first day.","Para":"Ask the group's questions to another group, discuss them, then write answers to all questions individually; the teacher reads and corrects.","Story":"Ask the group's questions to another group, discuss them, then write answers to all questions individually; the teacher reads and corrects."}},{"activity":"Language game: Singing and Spinning - level support","source":"I","ref":"p.18","tasks":{"Beginner":"Take part by saying or pointing to the letters involved and by listening carefully; Para and Story level partners help.","Letter":"Say the letters/sounds and give simple words they know.","Word":"Say and write words and short sentences for the game.","Para":"Write sentences with the words; help groups to record answers.","Story":"Write sentences or short stories with the words; help groups to record answers."}},{"activity":"Self-writing: level tasks and review","source":"M","ref":"p.15","tasks":{"Beginner":"Draw a picture about the discussion and then write a few sentences about it, expressing thoughts freely. Review: say what they drew or wrote; read the text aloud once; the teacher may write the text in the notebook for them.","Letter":"Write about what they liked, using drawing and writing; write any words or sentences they can. Review: read the text aloud once; correct punctuation mistakes using the Barakhadi chart.","Word":"Write a sentence based on the conversation. Mistakes in spelling, punctuation and sentence structure are fine. Review: read it to the group; discuss and correct mistakes together.","Para":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation.","Story":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation."}}],"organisation":[{"grouping":"Whole class (big group)","how":"All learners of all levels sit in a 'U' shape arranged by level (Beginner, Letter, Word, Para, Story) so that the move to small groups is easy.","activities":["Warm-up: Alphabet song (last-letter word chain)","Oral conversation: conversation on a picture","Story (Day 2 of the story): retelling","Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on helping at home"]},{"grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","how":"Learners of similar levels work together; the teacher gives each group a task for its level and spends more time with learners who need support. Rotate responsibilities (for example group leader).","activities":["Story: reading with actions and group questions","Language game: Singing and Spinning"]},{"grouping":"Individual","how":"Each learner works on a task for their own level; the teacher moves around, observes difficulties and supports individuals.","activities":["Story: writing answers individually","Self-writing: individual writing","Self-writing: review and reading back","Daily reading (10 minutes)"]}],"materials":["Picture card of a hospital waiting room","The same story book as yesterday","Story book","slate or paper for questions","Notebooks","A small object (chalk or pencil)","Picture card or topic on the board","crayons or pencils","Library books or storybooks"],"outcomes":["Learners take part in the oral conversation and speak without fear.","Learners retell the story, read with expression and ask or answer questions at their level.","Learners respond to the sound-symbol task for today (Language game: Singing and Spinning) at their own level.","Learners write about the topic at their level and read it aloud.","Each learner reads a book for 10 minutes."],"observation":["Observe each learner's reading and writing during the individual tasks; note who needs individual support and how many learners share the same difficulty.","Note any learner whose level is improving; move the learner to the next level group when you see steady progress (manual p.5).","Record each learner's progress for the day in the notebook, according to the learner's level (manual p.4).","Use today's observations to adjust tomorrow's plan (manual p.5)."],"teacherNotes":["Questions to elicit on Day 2: information questions (answer not in the text), thinking questions (needs knowledge beyond the text) and opinion questions (feedback on something in the text).","The manual lists the letter and word games but does not fix the slot in the daily timetable where they are used. This plan places them in the 10-minute sound-symbol / alphabet slot (interpretation).","Writing has two parts, content and sequence: encourage learners to read what they wrote, improve it and rewrite it for clarity and correctness (manual p.15).","Day 45 is the last lesson of Phase 1. Conduct the midline assessment next (it is not a lesson day), then start Day 46 with regrouping.","Pace: the manual says not to assume all learners progress at the same speed. Repeat a day's activity with the groups that need it before moving on.","Special needs: give extra time and prepare materials for slower learners; seat learners with hearing or vision difficulty at the front; for learners who reverse or confuse letters, trace letters on the letter card with a finger and write with dots to trace with a pencil (manual p.6)."],"components":[{"no":1,"key":"warmup","name":"Warm-up activities","keywords":["Alphabet song (last-letter word chain)","two learners lead"],"rows":[1]},{"no":2,"key":"oral","name":"Oral Discussion","keywords":["conversation on a picture","every learner speaks"],"rows":[2]},{"no":3,"key":"story","name":"Story","keywords":["Day 2","retell","read with actions","group questions","ask and answer","write answers (Para/Story)"],"rows":[3,4,5]},{"no":4,"key":"sound","name":"Sound symbol games, Sound separation-pairing","keywords":["Singing and Spinning","play in turns","level support"],"rows":[6]},{"no":5,"key":"mindwrite","name":"Individual-Writing (Day 2)","keywords":["discussion","write at own level","self-review (read aloud)"],"rows":[7,8,9]},{"no":6,"key":"reading","name":"Daily reading","keywords":["library book","read alone","teacher listens"],"rows":[10]}],"preLesson":null},{"programme":"TARL Literacy","id":"lit-046","day":46,"phase":2,"phaseLabel":"Phase 2 (Days 46-90)","title":"Story: a story about a king and a wise helper (Day 1)","dayType":"Story Day 1 + Mind mapping","focus":"Consonant clusters: nk (bank, pink) | Mind map: library","duration":70,"objectives":["Listen, speak and answer in the oral conversation (listening and storytelling).","Listen to and read a story with understanding; discuss it in big and small groups and respond at their own level.","Develop sound-symbol skills: Consonant clusters: nk (bank, pink).","Build vocabulary through a mind map ('library') and use the words at their own level.","Read independently for 10 minutes every day."],"sequence":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Handkerchief game","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Learners sit in a circle and clap while singing a rhyme ('I caught a Fish Alive'). One learner runs outside the circle with a handkerchief and secretly places it behind another learner, who must chase the runner. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Sit in a circle, clap and sing; run, place the handkerchief or chase as the game requires.","tlm":"A handkerchief","source":"M","ref":"p.8","n":1},{"activity":"Oral conversation: listening and storytelling","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Tell an interesting story starter and involve the learners: 'A magician came to our village market. What trick did he show?' Let learners imagine and continue the story.","learners":"Listen to the teacher, then imagine and continue the story. Learners can also recite a rhyme or story they know.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.9","n":2},{"activity":"Story (Day 1 of the story): reading aloud and discussion","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":8,"teacher":"Discuss the title or picture of the story with the learners. Read the story aloud with expression and voice modulation (learners do not repeat after you). Discuss it, with emphasis on opinion questions. Read it again slowly, pointing to each word.","learners":"Talk about the title/picture; listen; answer questions; follow each word with a finger in their own copy.","tlm":"A story from the school library (a story about a king and a wise helper), a copy for each learner","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":3},{"activity":"Story: reading in small groups","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":7,"teacher":"Form level-wise groups with a group leader. Learners read the story one sentence at a time while the others follow with their fingers. Para and Story level learners practise reading with emotion and expression.","learners":"Read the story sentence by sentence, supporting each other; the group leader helps.","tlm":"Story book copies","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":4},{"activity":"Story: level-wise individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":5,"teacher":"Give each learner the task for their level (see level table) and support those who need it.","learners":"Beginner/Letter: find and write favourite words or letters. Word: find consonant clusters. Para/Story: silently read, find unfamiliar and rhyming words.","tlm":"Story book, notebooks, board","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":5},{"activity":"Consonant clusters: introduction","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":4,"teacher":"Two-letter clusters: after same-letter clusters, familiarise learners with clusters of two different letters ('nk' as in bank, pink, drink). Discuss the words, ask learners to pronounce them and to frame sentences using them.","learners":"Listen, pronounce the cluster and say words that contain it.","tlm":"Board and chalk, words list (bank pink drink trunk ink)","source":"M","ref":"p.16","n":6},{"activity":"Consonant cluster game: Who is Whose Friend?","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":6,"teacher":"Prepare cards: some with broken parts of conjunct consonants (b + l, c + r, s + t) and some with the full form (bl as in black, cr as in crab, st as in star). Take out all the cards. Observe closely and help learners who need support.","learners":"Match each full form with its broken parts and discover 'who is whose friend'.","tlm":"Broken-part cards and full-form cards","source":"M","ref":"p.17","n":7},{"activity":"Mind mapping (Day 1): the word 'library'","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Ask: 'What words come to your mind when you hear the word library?' Write learners' answers on the board or floor (Para and Story level learners write the words themselves). Guide the map towards the learning objective. Example words: book, shelf, table, card, reader, writer, librarian, child, story, poem, map, picture.","learners":"Say words connected with 'library'; share the meaning and feeling of words.","tlm":"Board, chalk (or floor)","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":8},{"activity":"Mind mapping: classify the words","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":4,"teacher":"Ask learners to classify the words in groups, for example: Things: book, shelf, table, card; People: reader, writer, librarian, child; Books: story, poem, map, picture.","learners":"Sort the words into groups and say why.","tlm":"Board, chalk, word cards (optional)","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":9},{"activity":"Mind mapping: level-wise individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":6,"teacher":"Give each learner the individual task for their level; observe closely and give individual support. Display corrected stories on the wall.","learners":"Complete the task for their level (see level table).","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":10},{"activity":"Daily reading (10 minutes)","grouping":"Individual","minutes":10,"teacher":"Give each learner a library book or any storybook. Move around, listen to individual readers and note their level.","learners":"Read independently a book of their choice.","tlm":"Library books or storybooks","source":"M","ref":"p.7","n":11}],"procedures":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Handkerchief game","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","steps":[{"teacher":"Seat the learners in a circle and start clapping and singing the rhyme 'I caught a Fish Alive'.","learners":"Clap and sing together."},{"teacher":"One learner runs outside the circle holding a handkerchief and secretly places it behind another learner.","learners":"Everyone keeps clapping; the learner who finds the handkerchief behind them takes it and chases the runner."},{"teacher":"If the runner sits in the chaser's place before being caught, they stay in the game; if caught, they are out. Continue in this way.","learners":"Play fairly and take turns."}]},{"activity":"Oral conversation: listening and storytelling","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.9","steps":[{"teacher":"Say the starter: 'A magician came to our village market. What trick did he show?'","learners":"Listen and imagine."},{"teacher":"Ask learners to continue the story one by one. Encourage those who speak less.","learners":"Add ideas to the story."},{"teacher":"Invite a learner to recite a poem or rhyme they know.","learners":"Recite and listen to others."}]},{"activity":"Story - Day 1 (a story about a king and a wise helper)","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.10","steps":[{"teacher":"Discuss the title or picture of the story with the learners.","learners":"Talk about what they see and what the story may be about."},{"teacher":"Read the story aloud with expression and proper voice modulation. Learners should not simply repeat after you.","learners":"Listen carefully and enjoy the story."},{"teacher":"Discuss the story: factual, logical, vocabulary-based, judgment or opinion questions (today's focus: opinion: What did you like best? What would you have done in the story?). Begin in the home language if needed.","learners":"Think and respond thoughtfully; every learner takes part."},{"teacher":"Read the story again slowly, pointing to each word. Make sure each learner has a copy and follows with a finger.","learners":"Follow each word with their finger."},{"teacher":"Ask learners to read in small groups; select a group leader who helps the others. Learners read one sentence at a time while the others point with fingers.","learners":"Read with the help of one another."}]},{"activity":"Consonant clusters (nk) and the game 'Who is Whose Friend?'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.16-17","steps":[{"teacher":"Two-letter clusters: after same-letter clusters, familiarise learners with clusters of two different letters ('nk' as in bank, pink, drink). Discuss the words, ask learners to pronounce them and to frame sentences using them.","learners":"Listen, pronounce and find words in the text."},{"teacher":"Write the words on the board: bank pink drink trunk ink. Read them aloud with distinct pronunciation of the cluster.","learners":"Read the words aloud; point to the cluster in each word."},{"teacher":"Prepare cards: some with broken parts of conjunct consonants (b + l, c + r, s + t) and some with the full form (bl as in black, cr as in crab, st as in star). Take out all the cards.","learners":"Match each full form with its broken parts and discover 'who is whose friend'."}]},{"activity":"Mind mapping: 'library'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Small group (level-wise) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.14","steps":[{"teacher":"Choose a word that can generate many related words: 'library'. Ask: 'What words come to your mind when you hear the word library?' Write the answers on the board or floor.","learners":"Say words they link with 'library'."},{"teacher":"Discuss the words: what they mean and how they are connected.","learners":"Explain their words and listen to others."},{"teacher":"In small groups, let the learners classify the words (Things: book, shelf, table, card; People: reader, writer, librarian, child; Books: story, poem, map, picture).","learners":"Sort the words into groups."},{"teacher":"Give the individual tasks by level and help each learner.","learners":"Work individually; read the work aloud at the end if time allows."}]}],"levelTasks":[{"activity":"Story - Day 1: individual tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.10","tasks":{"Beginner":"Circle or search for a favourite word or letter in the story and say it aloud. If a learner cannot draw a circle, write words on the board and ask them to identify them.","Letter":"Find, read and write favourite words from the story.","Word":"Find the consonant clusters in the story, read them and write them in the notebook.","Para":"Silently read the story from the textbook; find unfamiliar words and try to understand them; find rhyming words, use them in sentences and write in the notebook; ask other groups for meanings; make questions in groups.","Story":"Silently read the story; find unfamiliar words and rhyming words; practise reading with emotion; one group reads sentences formed with consonant clusters to the other group; ask and answer group questions (information, thinking and opinion questions)."}},{"activity":"Consonant clusters (nk): level tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.16-17","tasks":{"Beginner":"Listen to the sound of the cluster and point to it in a word; continue with letter-sound work (interpretation: the manual describes clusters for learners lagging in reading words and sentences).","Letter":"Listen to the cluster sound and pick words with the cluster from a word card (interpretation).","Word":"Find the cluster in the story or textbook words, read the words and write them in the notebook.","Para":"Form words and sentences using the cluster; read the sentences aloud.","Story":"Form words and sentences using the cluster; read the sentences aloud; use them in the story writing."}},{"activity":"Mind mapping 'library': level tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.14","tasks":{"Beginner":"Circle all the words that contain the letter 'E' on the board; make a list. See how many learners find the most words.","Letter":"Circle all the words that contain the letter 'E' and make a list of them.","Word":"Use 4-5 words (for example map, book, card, poem, child) to form sentences, starting with words of one or two syllables. Example: Dream - I had a dream last night.","Para":"Choose any five words from the map and create a story with them. Use consonant clusters correctly, read the story aloud, correct mistakes of sentence structure, spelling or grammar, then display it on the wall.","Story":"Choose any five words from the map and create a story with them. Use consonant clusters correctly, read the story aloud, correct mistakes of sentence structure, spelling or grammar, then display it on the wall."}}],"organisation":[{"grouping":"Whole class (big group)","how":"All learners of all levels sit in a 'U' shape arranged by level (Beginner, Letter, Word, Para, Story) so that the move to small groups is easy.","activities":["Warm-up: Handkerchief game","Oral conversation: listening and storytelling","Story (Day 1 of the story): reading aloud and discussion","Consonant clusters: introduction","Mind mapping (Day 1): the word 'library'"]},{"grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","how":"Learners of similar levels work together; the teacher gives each group a task for its level and spends more time with learners who need support. Rotate responsibilities (for example group leader).","activities":["Story: reading in small groups","Consonant cluster game: Who is Whose Friend?","Mind mapping: classify the words"]},{"grouping":"Individual","how":"Each learner works on a task for their own level; the teacher moves around, observes difficulties and supports individuals.","activities":["Story: level-wise individual tasks","Mind mapping: level-wise individual tasks","Daily reading (10 minutes)"]}],"materials":["A handkerchief","A story from the school library (a story about a king","a wise helper)","a copy for each learner","Story book copies","Story book","notebooks","board","Board","chalk","words list (bank pink drink trunk ink)","Broken-part cards","full-form cards","chalk (or floor)","word cards (optional)","Notebooks","Library books or storybooks"],"outcomes":["Learners take part in the oral conversation and speak without fear.","Learners show understanding of the story in the discussion and complete the task for their level.","Learners respond to the sound-symbol task for today (Consonant clusters: nk (bank, pink)) at their own level.","Learners add words to the mind map and use them in sentences or a story at their level.","Each learner reads a book for 10 minutes."],"observation":["Observe each learner's reading and writing during the individual tasks; note who needs individual support and how many learners share the same difficulty.","Note any learner whose level is improving; move the learner to the next level group when you see steady progress (manual p.5).","Record each learner's progress for the day in the notebook, according to the learner's level (manual p.4).","Use today's observations to adjust tomorrow's plan (manual p.5)."],"teacherNotes":["Story selection: the manual asks teachers to use picture story books or stories in the school library. Today's suggested theme (a story about a king and a wise helper) is a planning suggestion; use any suitable story you have.","Consonant clusters: do these activities daily for learners who find reading complex words hard; the aim is to remove the fear of reading clusters. Teachers may carry out similar activities on their own.","Mind mapping topic for this day: 'library'. The manual's example uses the word 'shop'; today's topic follows the same method.","Pace: the manual says not to assume all learners progress at the same speed. Repeat a day's activity with the groups that need it before moving on.","Special needs: give extra time and prepare materials for slower learners; seat learners with hearing or vision difficulty at the front; for learners who reverse or confuse letters, trace letters on the letter card with a finger and write with dots to trace with a pencil (manual p.6)."],"components":[{"no":1,"key":"warmup","name":"Warm-up activities","keywords":["Handkerchief game","two learners lead"],"rows":[1]},{"no":2,"key":"oral","name":"Oral Discussion","keywords":["listening and storytelling","every learner speaks"],"rows":[2]},{"no":3,"key":"story","name":"Story","keywords":["Day 1","title / picture talk","read aloud with expression","opinion questions","re-read pointing","group reading","level tasks"],"rows":[3,4,5]},{"no":4,"key":"sound","name":"Sound symbol games, Sound separation-pairing","keywords":["consonant cluster 'nk'","pronounce and find words","game: Who is Whose Friend?"],"rows":[6,7]},{"no":5,"key":"mindwrite","name":"Mind Mapping (Day 1)","keywords":["mind map: library","classify the words","level task: circle letter E / sentences / story"],"rows":[8,9,10]},{"no":6,"key":"reading","name":"Daily reading","keywords":["library book","read alone","teacher listens"],"rows":[11]}],"preLesson":"Before the timed lesson (not part of the lesson time): use the midline results to re-group learners, move learners whose level has improved to the next level group and re-arrange the 'U' shape seating by level. Manual p.5-6."},{"programme":"TARL Literacy","id":"lit-047","day":47,"phase":2,"phaseLabel":"Phase 2 (Days 46-90)","title":"Story: a story about a king and a wise helper (Day 2)","dayType":"Story Day 2 + Self-writing","focus":"Language game: Words from Letters | Self-writing: a visit to a fair","duration":70,"objectives":["Listen, speak and answer in the oral conversation (What did you see on your way?).","Retell the story, read it with expression, ask and answer questions about it and write answers.","Develop sound-symbol skills: Language game: Words from Letters.","Write about a topic at their own level and review the writing (a visit to a fair).","Read independently for 10 minutes every day."],"sequence":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Rhyme - 'I saw a Little Bird'","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Say the rhyme with actions, then say it together. Lines: I saw a little bird go hop, hop, hop / I told the little bird to stop, stop, stop. / I went to the window to say 'How do you do?' / He wagged his little tail and far away he flew! Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Listen, then say the rhyme with actions.","tlm":"Rhyme chart or board (optional)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","n":1},{"activity":"Oral conversation: What did you see on your way?","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Ask learners to describe what they saw on their way to school. If they are hesitant, begin yourself: 'I saw smoke rising from a kitchen, a dog sleeping under a tree and children walking to school together. What did you see?'","learners":"Describe what they saw on the way to school and connect with what others share.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.9","n":2},{"activity":"Story (Day 2 of the story): retelling","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":6,"teacher":"Ask learners to retell yesterday's story in their own words. Prompt with questions on the beginning, middle and end.","learners":"Retell the story using their own words.","tlm":"The same story book as yesterday","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":3},{"activity":"Story: reading with actions and group questions","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":9,"teacher":"Learners practise reading with actions and expressions; one learner per group reads aloud to the class. Guide groups to make questions about the story (guide initially). Groups take turns to ask and answer each other's questions. Word-level learners also read aloud the consonants learned on the first day.","learners":"Read with actions; make questions (word-level learners help write them); ask and answer questions with another group.","tlm":"Story book, slate or paper for questions","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":4},{"activity":"Story: writing answers individually","grouping":"Individual","minutes":5,"teacher":"Para and Story level learners write answers to all questions individually; read and correct their responses after they finish.","learners":"Write the answers in their notebooks; Beginner/Letter/Word learners read or listen and answer orally.","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":5},{"activity":"Language game: Words from Letters","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Four or five letters are written on the board; learners form simple words and read them. Observe each learner and give help where needed.","learners":"Play the game, take turns and read or say the words they make.","tlm":"Board, chalk, notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.20","n":6},{"activity":"Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on a visit to a fair","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Start a conversation about a topic: 'a visit to a fair'. Involve all learners and ask open-ended questions.","learners":"Take part in the discussion and share thoughts freely.","tlm":"Picture card or topic on the board","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":7},{"activity":"Self-writing: individual writing","grouping":"Individual","minutes":7,"teacher":"Give each level its task (see level table). Let learners take ownership of what they draw and write; mistakes are fine.","learners":"Draw and write about the topic at their level.","tlm":"Notebooks, crayons or pencils","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":8},{"activity":"Self-writing: review and reading back","grouping":"Individual","minutes":3,"teacher":"Ask each learner 'What did you draw or write?' and have them read it aloud once. Word-level learners read to the group; discuss spelling, punctuation and sentence structure. Help beginners by writing their text in the notebook for them if needed.","learners":"Read what they wrote; correct mistakes after listening to their own reading.","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":9},{"activity":"Daily reading (10 minutes)","grouping":"Individual","minutes":10,"teacher":"Give each learner a library book or any storybook. Move around, listen to individual readers and note their level.","learners":"Read independently a book of their choice.","tlm":"Library books or storybooks","source":"M","ref":"p.7","n":10}],"procedures":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Rhyme - 'I saw a Little Bird'","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","steps":[{"teacher":"Say the rhyme 'I saw a Little Bird' slowly with actions: I saw a little bird go hop, hop, hop / I told the little bird to stop, stop, stop. / I went to the window to say 'How do you do?' / He wagged his little tail and far away he flew!","learners":"Listen and watch the actions."},{"teacher":"Say it again; invite learners to join with actions.","learners":"Say the rhyme together with actions."},{"teacher":"Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Choose a rhyme they like and lead."}]},{"activity":"Oral conversation: What did you see on your way?","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.9","steps":[{"teacher":"Ask: 'What did you see on your way to school today?'","learners":"Think about the way to school."},{"teacher":"If learners hesitate, start: 'I saw smoke rising from a kitchen, a dog sleeping under a tree and children walking to school together. What did you see?'","learners":"Listen to the model and then share their own observations."},{"teacher":"Connect learners' answers with each other.","learners":"Listen and add what they noticed."}]},{"activity":"Story - Day 2 (a story about a king and a wise helper)","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.11","steps":[{"teacher":"Ask learners to retell the story they read yesterday in their own words.","learners":"Retell, helping each other remember."},{"teacher":"In small groups learners practise reading the story using actions and expressions; one learner from each group then reads aloud to the class.","learners":"Read with actions and expression; a representative reads aloud."},{"teacher":"Guide the groups to come up with questions about the story (guide initially). Word-level learners can support by helping write them down.","learners":"Make questions together."},{"teacher":"Groups take turns to ask and answer each other's questions. Useful kinds: questions whose answer is not in the text; questions needing thinking beyond the text; questions asking for an opinion.","learners":"Ask, answer and discuss in the groups."},{"teacher":"Word-level learners also read aloud the consonants they learned on the first day.","learners":"Read the consonant clusters aloud."}]},{"activity":"Language game: Words from Letters","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.20","steps":[{"teacher":"Write 4-5 letters, for example m, t, a, l, b. Show how to combine them: bat, mat, lab (2-3 examples).","learners":"Watch the examples."},{"teacher":"Ask each learner to try forming a word with the given letters and write it.","learners":"Form and write a word."},{"teacher":"Move around and ask each learner to read the word aloud.","learners":"Read the word aloud."}]},{"activity":"Self-writing: 'Discussion, Writing, Self-review'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.15","steps":[{"teacher":"Start a conversation about a topic: 'a visit to a fair'. Involve all learners and ask open-ended questions.","learners":"Discuss and answer questions."},{"teacher":"Give writing time at each level: draw then write (Beginner), write about what they liked (Letter), a sentence (Word), a paragraph or story on a topic of their choice (Para/Story).","learners":"Write at their level and take ownership of the work."},{"teacher":"Review: ask 'What did you draw or write?' Have each learner read the text aloud once. Support with writing if needed.","learners":"Read aloud, listen to their pronunciation and correct mistakes."}]}],"levelTasks":[{"activity":"Story - Day 2: level-wise tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.11","tasks":{"Beginner":"Retell with the group by pointing to pictures or words; read aloud with group support (interpretation of the manual's group reading task).","Letter":"Read with the group, pointing to words; say the letters and words they know (interpretation of the manual's group reading task).","Word":"Support the group in writing the questions; read aloud the consonant clusters learned on the first day.","Para":"Ask the group's questions to another group, discuss them, then write answers to all questions individually; the teacher reads and corrects.","Story":"Ask the group's questions to another group, discuss them, then write answers to all questions individually; the teacher reads and corrects."}},{"activity":"Language game: Words from Letters - level support","source":"I","ref":"p.20","tasks":{"Beginner":"Take part by saying or pointing to the letters involved and by listening carefully; Para and Story level partners help.","Letter":"Say the letters/sounds and give simple words they know.","Word":"Say and write words and short sentences for the game.","Para":"Write sentences with the words; help groups to record answers.","Story":"Write sentences or short stories with the words; help groups to record answers."}},{"activity":"Self-writing: level tasks and review","source":"M","ref":"p.15","tasks":{"Beginner":"Draw a picture about the discussion and then write a few sentences about it, expressing thoughts freely. Review: say what they drew or wrote; read the text aloud once; the teacher may write the text in the notebook for them.","Letter":"Write about what they liked, using drawing and writing; write any words or sentences they can. Review: read the text aloud once; correct punctuation mistakes using the Barakhadi chart.","Word":"Write a sentence based on the conversation. Mistakes in spelling, punctuation and sentence structure are fine. Review: read it to the group; discuss and correct mistakes together.","Para":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation.","Story":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation."}}],"organisation":[{"grouping":"Whole class (big group)","how":"All learners of all levels sit in a 'U' shape arranged by level (Beginner, Letter, Word, Para, Story) so that the move to small groups is easy.","activities":["Warm-up: Rhyme - 'I saw a Little Bird'","Oral conversation: What did you see on your way?","Story (Day 2 of the story): retelling","Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on a visit to a fair"]},{"grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","how":"Learners of similar levels work together; the teacher gives each group a task for its level and spends more time with learners who need support. Rotate responsibilities (for example group leader).","activities":["Story: reading with actions and group questions","Language game: Words from Letters"]},{"grouping":"Individual","how":"Each learner works on a task for their own level; the teacher moves around, observes difficulties and supports individuals.","activities":["Story: writing answers individually","Self-writing: individual writing","Self-writing: review and reading back","Daily reading (10 minutes)"]}],"materials":["Rhyme chart or board (optional)","The same story book as yesterday","Story book","slate or paper for questions","Notebooks","Board","chalk","notebooks","Picture card or topic on the board","crayons or pencils","Library books or storybooks"],"outcomes":["Learners take part in the oral conversation and speak without fear.","Learners retell the story, read with expression and ask or answer questions at their level.","Learners respond to the sound-symbol task for today (Language game: Words from Letters) at their own level.","Learners write about the topic at their level and read it aloud.","Each learner reads a book for 10 minutes."],"observation":["Observe each learner's reading and writing during the individual tasks; note who needs individual support and how many learners share the same difficulty.","Note any learner whose level is improving; move the learner to the next level group when you see steady progress (manual p.5).","Record each learner's progress for the day in the notebook, according to the learner's level (manual p.4).","Use today's observations to adjust tomorrow's plan (manual p.5)."],"teacherNotes":["Questions to elicit on Day 2: information questions (answer not in the text), thinking questions (needs knowledge beyond the text) and opinion questions (feedback on something in the text).","The manual lists the letter and word games but does not fix the slot in the daily timetable where they are used. This plan places them in the 10-minute sound-symbol / alphabet slot (interpretation).","Writing has two parts, content and sequence: encourage learners to read what they wrote, improve it and rewrite it for clarity and correctness (manual p.15).","Pace: the manual says not to assume all learners progress at the same speed. Repeat a day's activity with the groups that need it before moving on.","Special needs: give extra time and prepare materials for slower learners; seat learners with hearing or vision difficulty at the front; for learners who reverse or confuse letters, trace letters on the letter card with a finger and write with dots to trace with a pencil (manual p.6)."],"components":[{"no":1,"key":"warmup","name":"Warm-up activities","keywords":["Rhyme - 'I saw a Little Bird'","two learners lead"],"rows":[1]},{"no":2,"key":"oral","name":"Oral Discussion","keywords":["What did you see on your way?","every learner speaks"],"rows":[2]},{"no":3,"key":"story","name":"Story","keywords":["Day 2","retell","read with actions","group questions","ask and answer","write answers (Para/Story)"],"rows":[3,4,5]},{"no":4,"key":"sound","name":"Sound symbol games, Sound separation-pairing","keywords":["Words from Letters","play in turns","level support"],"rows":[6]},{"no":5,"key":"mindwrite","name":"Individual-Writing (Day 2)","keywords":["discussion","write at own level","self-review (read aloud)"],"rows":[7,8,9]},{"no":6,"key":"reading","name":"Daily reading","keywords":["library book","read alone","teacher listens"],"rows":[10]}],"preLesson":null},{"programme":"TARL Literacy","id":"lit-048","day":48,"phase":2,"phaseLabel":"Phase 2 (Days 46-90)","title":"Saturday: drama presentation","dayType":"Saturday drama + Self-writing","focus":"Barakhadi / alphabet and phonics chart (line 4, letter 'u') | Self-writing: the story we acted out (a story about a king and a wise helper)","duration":70,"objectives":["Listen, speak and answer in the oral conversation (familiar topic).","Express a story through role play, using voice, facial expressions and gestures.","Develop sound-symbol skills: Barakhadi / alphabet and phonics chart (line 4, letter 'u').","Write about the story and review the writing.","Read independently for 10 minutes every day."],"sequence":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Singing and Spinning","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Learners sit in a circle and pass a small object while you clap with your back turned; when the clapping stops, the learner holding it sings a song, recites a poem or tells a joke. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Pass the object round the circle; sing, recite or tell a joke when the clapping stops.","tlm":"A small object (chalk or pencil)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","n":1},{"activity":"Oral conversation: familiar topic","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Hold a conversation on the topic 'a helpful person in our village'. Give each learner a chance to speak; be patient with learners who need extra time.","learners":"Talk about the topic and listen to others.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.9","n":2},{"activity":"Dramatic presentation: introduction and reading","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Explain what a dramatic presentation is and how it is done. Provide stories discussed during the week and read one aloud once more. Para and Story level learners support Beginner and Letter level learners in reading.","learners":"Listen, read along, then each learner chooses a character.","tlm":"Stories discussed in the week (a story about a sports day; a story about a king and a wise helper)","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":3},{"activity":"Dramatic presentation: planning in small groups","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":8,"teacher":"Each group discusses and plans dialogues; Para or Story level learners write the dialogues. Groups prepare their dramatic presentation.","learners":"Choose characters, plan and rehearse dialogues with facial expressions and gestures.","tlm":"Story, paper for dialogues","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":4},{"activity":"Dramatic presentation: performances and feedback","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":7,"teacher":"Learners sit in a U shape. Each group presents; after each performance, watching learners say what they enjoyed and what could be improved.","learners":"Perform in turn; watch; give feedback.","tlm":"Open space (U-shape seating)","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":5},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart: big group reading","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":3,"teacher":"Show the Barakhadi chart and ask which letter they like. Read the letter 'u' on the chart; learners listen carefully and point to it on their own chart (they do not repeat after you).","learners":"Listen and point to the letter on their own chart.","tlm":"Barakhadi chart, alphabet or phonics chart","source":"M","ref":"p.13","n":6},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart: small-group practice","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Learners practise reading the alphabet or phonics chart in groups and help each other. One learner per group reads aloud. Occasionally ask learners to identify the sounds of letters. Give each level its group task.","learners":"Read the chart in groups; one learner reads aloud; do the level task.","tlm":"Alphabet or phonics chart, board or floor","source":"M","ref":"p.13","n":7},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart: individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":2,"teacher":"Give each learner an individual task for their level and observe closely; assist any learner who needs individual support.","learners":"Say and write a letter or word, a sentence or a short paragraph (by level).","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.13","n":8},{"activity":"Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on the story we acted out (a story about a king and a wise helper)","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Start a conversation about the story used for the drama: 'the story we acted out (a story about a king and a wise helper)'. Involve all learners with open-ended questions.","learners":"Take part in the discussion and share thoughts freely.","tlm":"Picture card or topic on the board","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":9},{"activity":"Self-writing: individual writing","grouping":"Individual","minutes":7,"teacher":"Give each level its task (see level table). Let learners take ownership of what they draw and write; mistakes are fine.","learners":"Draw and write about the topic at their level.","tlm":"Notebooks, crayons or pencils","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":10},{"activity":"Self-writing: review and reading back","grouping":"Individual","minutes":3,"teacher":"Ask each learner 'What did you draw or write?' and have them read it aloud once. Word-level learners read to the group; discuss spelling, punctuation and sentence structure. Help beginners by writing their text in the notebook for them if needed.","learners":"Read what they wrote; correct mistakes after listening to their own reading.","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":11},{"activity":"Daily reading (10 minutes)","grouping":"Individual","minutes":10,"teacher":"Give each learner a library book or any storybook. Move around, listen to individual readers and note their level.","learners":"Read independently a book of their choice.","tlm":"Library books or storybooks","source":"M","ref":"p.7","n":12}],"procedures":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Singing and Spinning","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","steps":[{"teacher":"Seat the learners in a circle; give a small object to one learner.","learners":"Sit in a circle."},{"teacher":"Stand outside the circle with your back to them and clap steadily; they pass the object.","learners":"Pass the object while the clapping continues."},{"teacher":"Stop clapping; the learner holding the object sings, recites or tells a joke.","learners":"Perform, and everybody claps."}]},{"activity":"Oral conversation: familiar topic","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.9","steps":[{"teacher":"Introduce the topic: 'a helpful person in our village'.","learners":"Think about their own experience."},{"teacher":"Ask open questions; give every learner a chance. Involve learners who speak less.","learners":"Speak freely and without fear."},{"teacher":"Praise efforts and sum up.","learners":"Listen and respect each other's ideas."}]},{"activity":"Saturday special: dramatic presentation","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.11","steps":[{"teacher":"Explain what a dramatic presentation is and how it can be done. Give the groups the stories discussed during the week.","learners":"Listen to the explanation."},{"teacher":"Read a story aloud once more. Learners at story and paragraph level support those at beginner and letter level in reading.","learners":"Read along; helpers support their friends."},{"teacher":"After reading, each learner chooses a character from the story.","learners":"Choose a role (boys may play girl roles and girls may play boy roles)."},{"teacher":"In groups, learners discuss and plan the dialogues; paragraph or story level learners write the dialogues.","learners":"Plan and write dialogues together."},{"teacher":"Learners sit in a U shape. Each group presents its drama. After each performance, ask what the audience enjoyed and what could be improved.","learners":"Perform, watch and give kind feedback."}]},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart activity (line 4)","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Small group (level-wise) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.13","steps":[{"teacher":"Show the Barakhadi chart and ask the learners which letter they like. Where is the letter 'u'?","learners":"Look for the letter on the chart."},{"teacher":"Read the letter 'u' on the chart. Learners listen and point to it on their own chart. Make sure they do not repeat after you.","learners":"Listen and point to the letter."},{"teacher":"Learners read the alphabet or phonics chart in their groups and help each other; one learner from each group comes forward to read aloud.","learners":"Read in groups; the representative reads aloud."},{"teacher":"Occasionally ask them to identify the sounds of letters from the chart.","learners":"Say the sound of the letter you point to."},{"teacher":"As an extra activity, write some letters on the floor, call out each letter one by one and let the learners jump onto the correct letter.","learners":"Jump onto the letter that is called."}]},{"activity":"Self-writing: 'Discussion, Writing, Self-review'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.15","steps":[{"teacher":"Start a conversation about the story used for the drama: 'the story we acted out (a story about a king and a wise helper)'. Involve all learners with open-ended questions.","learners":"Discuss and answer questions."},{"teacher":"Give writing time at each level: draw then write (Beginner), write about what they liked (Letter), a sentence (Word), a paragraph or story on a topic of their choice (Para/Story).","learners":"Write at their level and take ownership of the work."},{"teacher":"Review: ask 'What did you draw or write?' Have each learner read the text aloud once. Support with writing if needed.","learners":"Read aloud, listen to their pronunciation and correct mistakes."}]}],"levelTasks":[{"activity":"Drama: roles by level","source":"M","ref":"p.11","tasks":{"Beginner":"Take a character role and say or act short lines with help from Para and Story level learners.","Letter":"Take a character role and say or act short lines with help from Para and Story level learners.","Word":"Take a role and speak the dialogues; help rehearse.","Para":"Write the dialogues for the group and support Beginner, Letter and Word level learners throughout.","Story":"Write the dialogues for the group and support Beginner, Letter and Word level learners throughout."}},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart: level tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.13","tasks":{"Beginner":"Small group: read the chart in the group; find and write favourite letters from the line. Individual: say and write a letter of their choice.","Letter":"Small group: read the chart; find and write favourite letters or words from any line. Individual: say a word on their own that begins with any letter.","Word":"Small group: write one or two lines of letters on the board or floor and use them to form words. Individual: speak and write sentences using words they know.","Para":"Small group: prepare word lists using the Barakhadi chart (for example items found in a shop or in the kitchen). Individual: write short paragraphs using the words formed with the Barakhadi chart.","Story":"Small group: prepare word lists using the Barakhadi chart. Individual: write short paragraphs using the words formed with the Barakhadi chart."}},{"activity":"Self-writing: level tasks and review","source":"M","ref":"p.15","tasks":{"Beginner":"Draw a picture about the discussion and then write a few sentences about it, expressing thoughts freely. Review: say what they drew or wrote; read the text aloud once; the teacher may write the text in the notebook for them.","Letter":"Write about what they liked, using drawing and writing; write any words or sentences they can. Review: read the text aloud once; correct punctuation mistakes using the Barakhadi chart.","Word":"Write a sentence based on the conversation. Mistakes in spelling, punctuation and sentence structure are fine. Review: read it to the group; discuss and correct mistakes together.","Para":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation.","Story":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation."}}],"organisation":[{"grouping":"Whole class (big group)","how":"All learners of all levels sit in a 'U' shape arranged by level (Beginner, Letter, Word, Para, Story) so that the move to small groups is easy.","activities":["Warm-up: Singing and Spinning","Oral conversation: familiar topic","Dramatic presentation: introduction and reading","Dramatic presentation: performances and feedback","Barakhadi chart: big group reading","Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on the story we acted out (a story about a king and a wise helper)"]},{"grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","how":"Learners of similar levels work together; the teacher gives each group a task for its level and spends more time with learners who need support. Rotate responsibilities (for example group leader).","activities":["Dramatic presentation: planning in small groups","Barakhadi chart: small-group practice"]},{"grouping":"Individual","how":"Each learner works on a task for their own level; the teacher moves around, observes difficulties and supports individuals.","activities":["Barakhadi chart: individual tasks","Self-writing: individual writing","Self-writing: review and reading back","Daily reading (10 minutes)"]}],"materials":["A small object (chalk or pencil)","Stories discussed in the week (a story about a sports day; a story about a king","a wise helper)","Story","paper for dialogues","Open space (U-shape seating)","Barakhadi chart","alphabet or phonics chart","Alphabet or phonics chart","board or floor","Notebooks","Picture card or topic on the board","crayons or pencils","Library books or storybooks"],"outcomes":["Learners take part in the oral conversation and speak without fear.","Learners present a role in the group drama and give feedback to others.","Learners respond to the sound-symbol task for today (Barakhadi / alphabet and phonics chart (line 4, letter 'u')) at their own level.","Learners write about the story at their level and read it aloud.","Each learner reads a book for 10 minutes."],"observation":["Observe each learner's reading and writing during the individual tasks; note who needs individual support and how many learners share the same difficulty.","Note any learner whose level is improving; move the learner to the next level group when you see steady progress (manual p.5).","Record each learner's progress for the day in the notebook, according to the learner's level (manual p.4).","Use today's observations to adjust tomorrow's plan (manual p.5)."],"teacherNotes":["Saturday: this plan assumes Day 1 is a Monday (six teaching days per week). If your school week is different, hold the drama presentation on your Saturday and keep the other days in sequence.","Barakhadi: learners who need extra time should get repeated practice using one or two sound units at a time. Topic-based discussion helps oral expression, thinking and understanding.","Writing has two parts, content and sequence: encourage learners to read what they wrote, improve it and rewrite it for clarity and correctness (manual p.15).","Pace: the manual says not to assume all learners progress at the same speed. Repeat a day's activity with the groups that need it before moving on.","Special needs: give extra time and prepare materials for slower learners; seat learners with hearing or vision difficulty at the front; for learners who reverse or confuse letters, trace letters on the letter card with a finger and write with dots to trace with a pencil (manual p.6)."],"components":[{"no":1,"key":"warmup","name":"Warm-up activities","keywords":["Singing and Spinning","two learners lead"],"rows":[1]},{"no":2,"key":"oral","name":"Oral Discussion","keywords":["familiar topic","every learner speaks"],"rows":[2]},{"no":3,"key":"story","name":"Story (Saturday: dramatic presentation)","keywords":["Saturday drama","choose a character","plan dialogues","perform in U shape","feedback"],"rows":[3,4,5]},{"no":4,"key":"sound","name":"Sound symbol games, Sound separation-pairing","keywords":["Barakhadi / alphabet chart","listen and point (no repeating)","group reading","level tasks"],"rows":[6,7,8]},{"no":5,"key":"mindwrite","name":"Individual-Writing (Day 2)","keywords":["discussion","write at own level","self-review (read aloud)"],"rows":[9,10,11]},{"no":6,"key":"reading","name":"Daily reading","keywords":["library book","read alone","teacher listens"],"rows":[12]}],"preLesson":null},{"programme":"TARL Literacy","id":"lit-049","day":49,"phase":2,"phaseLabel":"Phase 2 (Days 46-90)","title":"Story: a story about a kind teacher (Day 1)","dayType":"Story Day 1 + Mind mapping","focus":"Consonant clusters: sk (desk, skate) | Mind map: post office","duration":70,"objectives":["Listen, speak and answer in the oral conversation (conversation on a picture).","Listen to and read a story with understanding; discuss it in big and small groups and respond at their own level.","Develop sound-symbol skills: Consonant clusters: sk (desk, skate).","Build vocabulary through a mind map ('post office') and use the words at their own level.","Read independently for 10 minutes every day."],"sequence":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Rain clapping","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Everyone stands in a circle with eyes closed and keeps clapping: first one finger, then two, three, four and finally five fingers. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Stand in a circle, close the eyes and clap with 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 fingers.","tlm":"After the activity ask: Where were you when you last heard real rain?","source":"M","ref":"p.8","n":1},{"activity":"Oral conversation: conversation on a picture","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Show a picture of a playground full of children and ask what is happening, who is doing what and what is happening around them. Let learners think creatively and even make up a story.","learners":"Look at the picture, answer questions and make up their own story about it.","tlm":"Picture card of a playground full of children","source":"M","ref":"p.9","n":2},{"activity":"Story (Day 1 of the story): reading aloud and discussion","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":8,"teacher":"Discuss the title or picture of the story with the learners. Read the story aloud with expression and voice modulation (learners do not repeat after you). Discuss it, with emphasis on factual questions. Read it again slowly, pointing to each word.","learners":"Talk about the title/picture; listen; answer questions; follow each word with a finger in their own copy.","tlm":"A story from the school library (a story about a kind teacher), a copy for each learner","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":3},{"activity":"Story: reading in small groups","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":7,"teacher":"Form level-wise groups with a group leader. Learners read the story one sentence at a time while the others follow with their fingers. Para and Story level learners practise reading with emotion and expression.","learners":"Read the story sentence by sentence, supporting each other; the group leader helps.","tlm":"Story book copies","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":4},{"activity":"Story: level-wise individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":5,"teacher":"Give each learner the task for their level (see level table) and support those who need it.","learners":"Beginner/Letter: find and write favourite words or letters. Word: find consonant clusters. Para/Story: silently read, find unfamiliar and rhyming words.","tlm":"Story book, notebooks, board","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":5},{"activity":"Consonant clusters: introduction","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":4,"teacher":"Two-letter clusters: after same-letter clusters, familiarise learners with clusters of two different letters ('sk' as in desk, skate, mask). Discuss the words, ask learners to pronounce them and to frame sentences using them.","learners":"Listen, pronounce the cluster and say words that contain it.","tlm":"Board and chalk, words list (desk skate mask risk skirt)","source":"M","ref":"p.16","n":6},{"activity":"Consonant cluster game: Conjunct Consonant Game","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":6,"teacher":"Give each child a set of conjunct consonant cards. Observe closely and help learners who need support.","learners":"Choose one conjunct consonant and form five words with it. Learners at paragraph or story level can make sentences with the words they formed.","tlm":"Conjunct consonant cards","source":"M","ref":"p.17","n":7},{"activity":"Mind mapping (Day 1): the word 'post office'","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Ask: 'What words come to your mind when you hear the word post office?' Write learners' answers on the board or floor (Para and Story level learners write the words themselves). Guide the map towards the learning objective. Example words: postman, clerk, sender, reader, letter, stamp, parcel, envelope, write, post, send, receive.","learners":"Say words connected with 'post office'; share the meaning and feeling of words.","tlm":"Board, chalk (or floor)","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":8},{"activity":"Mind mapping: classify the words","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":4,"teacher":"Ask learners to classify the words in groups, for example: People: postman, clerk, sender, reader; Things: letter, stamp, parcel, envelope; Actions: write, post, send, receive.","learners":"Sort the words into groups and say why.","tlm":"Board, chalk, word cards (optional)","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":9},{"activity":"Mind mapping: level-wise individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":6,"teacher":"Give each learner the individual task for their level; observe closely and give individual support. Display corrected stories on the wall.","learners":"Complete the task for their level (see level table).","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":10},{"activity":"Daily reading (10 minutes)","grouping":"Individual","minutes":10,"teacher":"Give each learner a library book or any storybook. Move around, listen to individual readers and note their level.","learners":"Read independently a book of their choice.","tlm":"Library books or storybooks","source":"M","ref":"p.7","n":11}],"procedures":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Rain clapping","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","steps":[{"teacher":"Stand the learners in a circle and ask them to close their eyes. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Stand in a circle and close their eyes."},{"teacher":"Start clapping with one finger; then two fingers, three, four and finally five fingers.","learners":"Keep clapping, copying the change of fingers."},{"teacher":"After the activity ask: Where were you when you last heard real rain?","learners":"Tell how they felt and what the sounds reminded them of."}]},{"activity":"Oral conversation: conversation on a picture","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.9","steps":[{"teacher":"Show the picture of a playground full of children.","learners":"Look carefully."},{"teacher":"Ask: What is happening in the picture? Who is doing what? What is happening around them? Then: What might happen next?","learners":"Answer in their own words; every learner gets a chance."},{"teacher":"Let learners imagine and make up a short story from the picture.","learners":"Tell their stories to the class."}]},{"activity":"Story - Day 1 (a story about a kind teacher)","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.10","steps":[{"teacher":"Discuss the title or picture of the story with the learners.","learners":"Talk about what they see and what the story may be about."},{"teacher":"Read the story aloud with expression and proper voice modulation. Learners should not simply repeat after you.","learners":"Listen carefully and enjoy the story."},{"teacher":"Discuss the story: factual, logical, vocabulary-based, judgment or opinion questions (today's focus: factual: Who was in the story? Where did it happen? What did the character do first?). Begin in the home language if needed.","learners":"Think and respond thoughtfully; every learner takes part."},{"teacher":"Read the story again slowly, pointing to each word. Make sure each learner has a copy and follows with a finger.","learners":"Follow each word with their finger."},{"teacher":"Ask learners to read in small groups; select a group leader who helps the others. Learners read one sentence at a time while the others point with fingers.","learners":"Read with the help of one another."}]},{"activity":"Consonant clusters (sk) and the game 'Conjunct Consonant Game'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.16-17","steps":[{"teacher":"Two-letter clusters: after same-letter clusters, familiarise learners with clusters of two different letters ('sk' as in desk, skate, mask). Discuss the words, ask learners to pronounce them and to frame sentences using them.","learners":"Listen, pronounce and find words in the text."},{"teacher":"Write the words on the board: desk skate mask risk skirt. Read them aloud with distinct pronunciation of the cluster.","learners":"Read the words aloud; point to the cluster in each word."},{"teacher":"Give each child a set of conjunct consonant cards.","learners":"Choose one conjunct consonant and form five words with it. Learners at paragraph or story level can make sentences with the words they formed."}]},{"activity":"Mind mapping: 'post office'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Small group (level-wise) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.14","steps":[{"teacher":"Choose a word that can generate many related words: 'post office'. Ask: 'What words come to your mind when you hear the word post office?' Write the answers on the board or floor.","learners":"Say words they link with 'post office'."},{"teacher":"Discuss the words: what they mean and how they are connected.","learners":"Explain their words and listen to others."},{"teacher":"In small groups, let the learners classify the words (People: postman, clerk, sender, reader; Things: letter, stamp, parcel, envelope; Actions: write, post, send, receive).","learners":"Sort the words into groups."},{"teacher":"Give the individual tasks by level and help each learner.","learners":"Work individually; read the work aloud at the end if time allows."}]}],"levelTasks":[{"activity":"Story - Day 1: individual tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.10","tasks":{"Beginner":"Circle or search for a favourite word or letter in the story and say it aloud. If a learner cannot draw a circle, write words on the board and ask them to identify them.","Letter":"Find, read and write favourite words from the story.","Word":"Find the consonant clusters in the story, read them and write them in the notebook.","Para":"Silently read the story from the textbook; find unfamiliar words and try to understand them; find rhyming words, use them in sentences and write in the notebook; ask other groups for meanings; make questions in groups.","Story":"Silently read the story; find unfamiliar words and rhyming words; practise reading with emotion; one group reads sentences formed with consonant clusters to the other group; ask and answer group questions (information, thinking and opinion questions)."}},{"activity":"Consonant clusters (sk): level tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.16-17","tasks":{"Beginner":"Listen to the sound of the cluster and point to it in a word; continue with letter-sound work (interpretation: the manual describes clusters for learners lagging in reading words and sentences).","Letter":"Listen to the cluster sound and pick words with the cluster from a word card (interpretation).","Word":"Find the cluster in the story or textbook words, read the words and write them in the notebook.","Para":"Form words and sentences using the cluster; read the sentences aloud.","Story":"Form words and sentences using the cluster; read the sentences aloud; use them in the story writing."}},{"activity":"Mind mapping 'post office': level tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.14","tasks":{"Beginner":"Circle all the words that contain the letter 'E' on the board; make a list. See how many learners find the most words.","Letter":"Circle all the words that contain the letter 'E' and make a list of them.","Word":"Use 4-5 words (for example post, send, clerk, stamp, write) to form sentences, starting with words of one or two syllables. Example: Dream - I had a dream last night.","Para":"Choose any five words from the map and create a story with them. Use consonant clusters correctly, read the story aloud, correct mistakes of sentence structure, spelling or grammar, then display it on the wall.","Story":"Choose any five words from the map and create a story with them. Use consonant clusters correctly, read the story aloud, correct mistakes of sentence structure, spelling or grammar, then display it on the wall."}}],"organisation":[{"grouping":"Whole class (big group)","how":"All learners of all levels sit in a 'U' shape arranged by level (Beginner, Letter, Word, Para, Story) so that the move to small groups is easy.","activities":["Warm-up: Rain clapping","Oral conversation: conversation on a picture","Story (Day 1 of the story): reading aloud and discussion","Consonant clusters: introduction","Mind mapping (Day 1): the word 'post office'"]},{"grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","how":"Learners of similar levels work together; the teacher gives each group a task for its level and spends more time with learners who need support. Rotate responsibilities (for example group leader).","activities":["Story: reading in small groups","Consonant cluster game: Conjunct Consonant Game","Mind mapping: classify the words"]},{"grouping":"Individual","how":"Each learner works on a task for their own level; the teacher moves around, observes difficulties and supports individuals.","activities":["Story: level-wise individual tasks","Mind mapping: level-wise individual tasks","Daily reading (10 minutes)"]}],"materials":["After the activity ask: Where were you when you last heard real rain?","Picture card of a playground full of children","A story from the school library (a story about a kind teacher)","a copy for each learner","Story book copies","Story book","notebooks","board","Board","chalk","words list (desk skate mask risk skirt)","Conjunct consonant cards","chalk (or floor)","word cards (optional)","Notebooks","Library books or storybooks"],"outcomes":["Learners take part in the oral conversation and speak without fear.","Learners show understanding of the story in the discussion and complete the task for their level.","Learners respond to the sound-symbol task for today (Consonant clusters: sk (desk, skate)) at their own level.","Learners add words to the mind map and use them in sentences or a story at their level.","Each learner reads a book for 10 minutes."],"observation":["Observe each learner's reading and writing during the individual tasks; note who needs individual support and how many learners share the same difficulty.","Note any learner whose level is improving; move the learner to the next level group when you see steady progress (manual p.5).","Record each learner's progress for the day in the notebook, according to the learner's level (manual p.4).","Use today's observations to adjust tomorrow's plan (manual p.5)."],"teacherNotes":["Story selection: the manual asks teachers to use picture story books or stories in the school library. Today's suggested theme (a story about a kind teacher) is a planning suggestion; use any suitable story you have.","Consonant clusters: do these activities daily for learners who find reading complex words hard; the aim is to remove the fear of reading clusters. Teachers may carry out similar activities on their own.","Mind mapping topic for this day: 'post office'. The manual's example uses the word 'shop'; today's topic follows the same method.","Pace: the manual says not to assume all learners progress at the same speed. Repeat a day's activity with the groups that need it before moving on.","Special needs: give extra time and prepare materials for slower learners; seat learners with hearing or vision difficulty at the front; for learners who reverse or confuse letters, trace letters on the letter card with a finger and write with dots to trace with a pencil (manual p.6)."],"components":[{"no":1,"key":"warmup","name":"Warm-up activities","keywords":["Rain clapping","two learners lead"],"rows":[1]},{"no":2,"key":"oral","name":"Oral Discussion","keywords":["conversation on a picture","every learner speaks"],"rows":[2]},{"no":3,"key":"story","name":"Story","keywords":["Day 1","title / picture talk","read aloud with expression","factual questions","re-read pointing","group reading","level tasks"],"rows":[3,4,5]},{"no":4,"key":"sound","name":"Sound symbol games, Sound separation-pairing","keywords":["consonant cluster 'sk'","pronounce and find words","game: Conjunct Consonant Game"],"rows":[6,7]},{"no":5,"key":"mindwrite","name":"Mind Mapping (Day 1)","keywords":["mind map: post office","classify the words","level task: circle letter E / sentences / story"],"rows":[8,9,10]},{"no":6,"key":"reading","name":"Daily reading","keywords":["library book","read alone","teacher listens"],"rows":[11]}],"preLesson":null},{"programme":"TARL Literacy","id":"lit-050","day":50,"phase":2,"phaseLabel":"Phase 2 (Days 46-90)","title":"Story: a story about a kind teacher (Day 2)","dayType":"Story Day 2 + Self-writing","focus":"Language game: Singing and Spinning | Self-writing: my favourite game","duration":70,"objectives":["Listen, speak and answer in the oral conversation (listening and storytelling).","Retell the story, read it with expression, ask and answer questions about it and write answers.","Develop sound-symbol skills: Language game: Singing and Spinning.","Write about a topic at their own level and review the writing (my favourite game).","Read independently for 10 minutes every day."],"sequence":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Writing with body parts","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Learners stand in a circle. Demonstrate writing the word 'ball' in the air with a finger, then ask them to write it with different body parts. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Write the word 'ball' in the air with the finger, then with the head, shoulders, knees or elbows.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.8","n":1},{"activity":"Oral conversation: listening and storytelling","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Tell an interesting story starter and involve the learners: 'A rainbow touched the ground near our school. What did we find there?' Let learners imagine and continue the story.","learners":"Listen to the teacher, then imagine and continue the story. Learners can also recite a rhyme or story they know.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.9","n":2},{"activity":"Story (Day 2 of the story): retelling","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":6,"teacher":"Ask learners to retell yesterday's story in their own words. Prompt with questions on the beginning, middle and end.","learners":"Retell the story using their own words.","tlm":"The same story book as yesterday","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":3},{"activity":"Story: reading with actions and group questions","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":9,"teacher":"Learners practise reading with actions and expressions; one learner per group reads aloud to the class. Guide groups to make questions about the story (guide initially). Groups take turns to ask and answer each other's questions. Word-level learners also read aloud the consonants learned on the first day.","learners":"Read with actions; make questions (word-level learners help write them); ask and answer questions with another group.","tlm":"Story book, slate or paper for questions","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":4},{"activity":"Story: writing answers individually","grouping":"Individual","minutes":5,"teacher":"Para and Story level learners write answers to all questions individually; read and correct their responses after they finish.","learners":"Write the answers in their notebooks; Beginner/Letter/Word learners read or listen and answer orally.","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":5},{"activity":"Language game: Singing and Spinning","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Learners sit in a circle; a small object (chalk, pencil) is passed around while the teacher, back turned, claps steadily. Observe each learner and give help where needed.","learners":"Play the game, take turns and read or say the words they make.","tlm":"A small object (chalk or pencil)","source":"M","ref":"p.18","n":6},{"activity":"Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on my favourite game","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Start a conversation about a situation: 'my favourite game'. Involve all learners and ask open-ended questions.","learners":"Take part in the discussion and share thoughts freely.","tlm":"Picture card or topic on the board","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":7},{"activity":"Self-writing: individual writing","grouping":"Individual","minutes":7,"teacher":"Give each level its task (see level table). Let learners take ownership of what they draw and write; mistakes are fine.","learners":"Draw and write about the topic at their level.","tlm":"Notebooks, crayons or pencils","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":8},{"activity":"Self-writing: review and reading back","grouping":"Individual","minutes":3,"teacher":"Ask each learner 'What did you draw or write?' and have them read it aloud once. Word-level learners read to the group; discuss spelling, punctuation and sentence structure. Help beginners by writing their text in the notebook for them if needed.","learners":"Read what they wrote; correct mistakes after listening to their own reading.","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":9},{"activity":"Daily reading (10 minutes)","grouping":"Individual","minutes":10,"teacher":"Give each learner a library book or any storybook. Move around, listen to individual readers and note their level.","learners":"Read independently a book of their choice.","tlm":"Library books or storybooks","source":"M","ref":"p.7","n":10}],"procedures":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Writing with body parts","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","steps":[{"teacher":"Stand the learners in a circle. Demonstrate writing the word 'ball' in the air with your finger.","learners":"Watch and then copy with their own finger."},{"teacher":"Ask them to write it again using shoulders and other body parts (head, shoulders, knees, ...).","learners":"Write the letters in the air with the named body part."},{"teacher":"Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Take turns to lead."}]},{"activity":"Oral conversation: listening and storytelling","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.9","steps":[{"teacher":"Say the starter: 'A rainbow touched the ground near our school. What did we find there?'","learners":"Listen and imagine."},{"teacher":"Ask learners to continue the story one by one. Encourage those who speak less.","learners":"Add ideas to the story."},{"teacher":"Invite a learner to recite a poem or rhyme they know.","learners":"Recite and listen to others."}]},{"activity":"Story - Day 2 (a story about a kind teacher)","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.11","steps":[{"teacher":"Ask learners to retell the story they read yesterday in their own words.","learners":"Retell, helping each other remember."},{"teacher":"In small groups learners practise reading the story using actions and expressions; one learner from each group then reads aloud to the class.","learners":"Read with actions and expression; a representative reads aloud."},{"teacher":"Guide the groups to come up with questions about the story (guide initially). Word-level learners can support by helping write them down.","learners":"Make questions together."},{"teacher":"Groups take turns to ask and answer each other's questions. Useful kinds: questions whose answer is not in the text; questions needing thinking beyond the text; questions asking for an opinion.","learners":"Ask, answer and discuss in the groups."},{"teacher":"Word-level learners also read aloud the consonants they learned on the first day.","learners":"Read the consonant clusters aloud."}]},{"activity":"Language game: Singing and Spinning","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.18","steps":[{"teacher":"Seat the learners in a circle. Give one learner a small object such as a piece of chalk.","learners":"Sit in a circle and listen for the clapping."},{"teacher":"Stand outside the circle with your back to the learners and clap steadily. Stop clapping without warning.","learners":"Pass the object round while the clapping continues."},{"teacher":"Ask the learner holding the object when you stop to sing a song, recite a poem or tell a joke.","learners":"Sing, recite or tell a joke; the others listen and clap."}]},{"activity":"Self-writing: 'Discussion, Writing, Self-review'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.15","steps":[{"teacher":"Start a conversation about a situation: 'my favourite game'. Involve all learners and ask open-ended questions.","learners":"Discuss and answer questions."},{"teacher":"Give writing time at each level: draw then write (Beginner), write about what they liked (Letter), a sentence (Word), a paragraph or story on a topic of their choice (Para/Story).","learners":"Write at their level and take ownership of the work."},{"teacher":"Review: ask 'What did you draw or write?' Have each learner read the text aloud once. Support with writing if needed.","learners":"Read aloud, listen to their pronunciation and correct mistakes."}]}],"levelTasks":[{"activity":"Story - Day 2: level-wise tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.11","tasks":{"Beginner":"Retell with the group by pointing to pictures or words; read aloud with group support (interpretation of the manual's group reading task).","Letter":"Read with the group, pointing to words; say the letters and words they know (interpretation of the manual's group reading task).","Word":"Support the group in writing the questions; read aloud the consonant clusters learned on the first day.","Para":"Ask the group's questions to another group, discuss them, then write answers to all questions individually; the teacher reads and corrects.","Story":"Ask the group's questions to another group, discuss them, then write answers to all questions individually; the teacher reads and corrects."}},{"activity":"Language game: Singing and Spinning - level support","source":"I","ref":"p.18","tasks":{"Beginner":"Take part by saying or pointing to the letters involved and by listening carefully; Para and Story level partners help.","Letter":"Say the letters/sounds and give simple words they know.","Word":"Say and write words and short sentences for the game.","Para":"Write sentences with the words; help groups to record answers.","Story":"Write sentences or short stories with the words; help groups to record answers."}},{"activity":"Self-writing: level tasks and review","source":"M","ref":"p.15","tasks":{"Beginner":"Draw a picture about the discussion and then write a few sentences about it, expressing thoughts freely. Review: say what they drew or wrote; read the text aloud once; the teacher may write the text in the notebook for them.","Letter":"Write about what they liked, using drawing and writing; write any words or sentences they can. Review: read the text aloud once; correct punctuation mistakes using the Barakhadi chart.","Word":"Write a sentence based on the conversation. Mistakes in spelling, punctuation and sentence structure are fine. Review: read it to the group; discuss and correct mistakes together.","Para":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation.","Story":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation."}}],"organisation":[{"grouping":"Whole class (big group)","how":"All learners of all levels sit in a 'U' shape arranged by level (Beginner, Letter, Word, Para, Story) so that the move to small groups is easy.","activities":["Warm-up: Writing with body parts","Oral conversation: listening and storytelling","Story (Day 2 of the story): retelling","Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on my favourite game"]},{"grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","how":"Learners of similar levels work together; the teacher gives each group a task for its level and spends more time with learners who need support. Rotate responsibilities (for example group leader).","activities":["Story: reading with actions and group questions","Language game: Singing and Spinning"]},{"grouping":"Individual","how":"Each learner works on a task for their own level; the teacher moves around, observes difficulties and supports individuals.","activities":["Story: writing answers individually","Self-writing: individual writing","Self-writing: review and reading back","Daily reading (10 minutes)"]}],"materials":["The same story book as yesterday","Story book","slate or paper for questions","Notebooks","A small object (chalk or pencil)","Picture card or topic on the board","crayons or pencils","Library books or storybooks"],"outcomes":["Learners take part in the oral conversation and speak without fear.","Learners retell the story, read with expression and ask or answer questions at their level.","Learners respond to the sound-symbol task for today (Language game: Singing and Spinning) at their own level.","Learners write about the topic at their level and read it aloud.","Each learner reads a book for 10 minutes."],"observation":["Observe each learner's reading and writing during the individual tasks; note who needs individual support and how many learners share the same difficulty.","Note any learner whose level is improving; move the learner to the next level group when you see steady progress (manual p.5).","Record each learner's progress for the day in the notebook, according to the learner's level (manual p.4).","Use today's observations to adjust tomorrow's plan (manual p.5)."],"teacherNotes":["Questions to elicit on Day 2: information questions (answer not in the text), thinking questions (needs knowledge beyond the text) and opinion questions (feedback on something in the text).","The manual lists the letter and word games but does not fix the slot in the daily timetable where they are used. This plan places them in the 10-minute sound-symbol / alphabet slot (interpretation).","Writing has two parts, content and sequence: encourage learners to read what they wrote, improve it and rewrite it for clarity and correctness (manual p.15).","Pace: the manual says not to assume all learners progress at the same speed. Repeat a day's activity with the groups that need it before moving on.","Special needs: give extra time and prepare materials for slower learners; seat learners with hearing or vision difficulty at the front; for learners who reverse or confuse letters, trace letters on the letter card with a finger and write with dots to trace with a pencil (manual p.6)."],"components":[{"no":1,"key":"warmup","name":"Warm-up activities","keywords":["Writing with body parts","two learners lead"],"rows":[1]},{"no":2,"key":"oral","name":"Oral Discussion","keywords":["listening and storytelling","every learner speaks"],"rows":[2]},{"no":3,"key":"story","name":"Story","keywords":["Day 2","retell","read with actions","group questions","ask and answer","write answers (Para/Story)"],"rows":[3,4,5]},{"no":4,"key":"sound","name":"Sound symbol games, Sound separation-pairing","keywords":["Singing and Spinning","play in turns","level support"],"rows":[6]},{"no":5,"key":"mindwrite","name":"Individual-Writing (Day 2)","keywords":["discussion","write at own level","self-review (read aloud)"],"rows":[7,8,9]},{"no":6,"key":"reading","name":"Daily reading","keywords":["library book","read alone","teacher listens"],"rows":[10]}],"preLesson":null},{"programme":"TARL Literacy","id":"lit-051","day":51,"phase":2,"phaseLabel":"Phase 2 (Days 46-90)","title":"Story: a story about two brothers or sisters (Day 1)","dayType":"Story Day 1 + Mind mapping","focus":"Language game: Think and Make a List | Mind map: tea garden","duration":70,"objectives":["Listen, speak and answer in the oral conversation (What did you see on your way?).","Listen to and read a story with understanding; discuss it in big and small groups and respond at their own level.","Develop sound-symbol skills: Language game: Think and Make a List.","Build vocabulary through a mind map ('tea garden') and use the words at their own level.","Read independently for 10 minutes every day."],"sequence":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Alphabet song (last-letter word chain)","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Say a word to the big group, for example 'yak'. Learners say a word that starts with the last letter ('k'). A learner who cannot say a word is out. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Say a word that starts with the last letter of the previous word; step out if unable to.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.8","n":1},{"activity":"Oral conversation: What did you see on your way?","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Ask learners to describe what they saw on their way to school. If they are hesitant, begin yourself: 'On the road I saw a bullock cart, a tea stall and a boy flying a kite. What did you see?'","learners":"Describe what they saw on the way to school and connect with what others share.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.9","n":2},{"activity":"Story (Day 1 of the story): reading aloud and discussion","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":8,"teacher":"Discuss the title or picture of the story with the learners. Read the story aloud with expression and voice modulation (learners do not repeat after you). Discuss it, with emphasis on logical questions. Read it again slowly, pointing to each word.","learners":"Talk about the title/picture; listen; answer questions; follow each word with a finger in their own copy.","tlm":"A story from the school library (a story about two brothers or sisters), a copy for each learner","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":3},{"activity":"Story: reading in small groups","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":7,"teacher":"Form level-wise groups with a group leader. Learners read the story one sentence at a time while the others follow with their fingers. Para and Story level learners practise reading with emotion and expression.","learners":"Read the story sentence by sentence, supporting each other; the group leader helps.","tlm":"Story book copies","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":4},{"activity":"Story: level-wise individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":5,"teacher":"Give each learner the task for their level (see level table) and support those who need it.","learners":"Beginner/Letter: find and write favourite words or letters. Word: find consonant clusters. Para/Story: silently read, find unfamiliar and rhyming words.","tlm":"Story book, notebooks, board","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":5},{"activity":"Language game: Think and Make a List","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Each group gets a topic and writes a list together; the lists are displayed on the classroom wall. Observe each learner and give help where needed.","learners":"Play the game, take turns and read or say the words they make.","tlm":"Paper or notebooks, chalk","source":"M","ref":"p.20","n":6},{"activity":"Mind mapping (Day 1): the word 'tea garden'","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Ask: 'What words come to your mind when you hear the word tea garden?' Write learners' answers on the board or floor (Para and Story level learners write the words themselves). Guide the map towards the learning objective. Example words: tea, shade tree, leaf, bud, worker, manager, picker, driver, basket, factory, cup, kettle.","learners":"Say words connected with 'tea garden'; share the meaning and feeling of words.","tlm":"Board, chalk (or floor)","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":7},{"activity":"Mind mapping: classify the words","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":4,"teacher":"Ask learners to classify the words in groups, for example: Plants: tea, shade tree, leaf, bud; People: worker, manager, picker, driver; Things: basket, factory, cup, kettle.","learners":"Sort the words into groups and say why.","tlm":"Board, chalk, word cards (optional)","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":8},{"activity":"Mind mapping: level-wise individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":6,"teacher":"Give each learner the individual task for their level; observe closely and give individual support. Display corrected stories on the wall.","learners":"Complete the task for their level (see level table).","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":9},{"activity":"Daily reading (10 minutes)","grouping":"Individual","minutes":10,"teacher":"Give each learner a library book or any storybook. Move around, listen to individual readers and note their level.","learners":"Read independently a book of their choice.","tlm":"Library books or storybooks","source":"M","ref":"p.7","n":10}],"procedures":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Alphabet song (last-letter word chain)","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","steps":[{"teacher":"Say the word 'yak' to the big group and show that its last letter is 'k'.","learners":"Listen and think of a word starting with 'k'."},{"teacher":"Ask learners in turn to say a word that starts with the last letter of the previous word. Example: rain -> nest.","learners":"Say a word in turn; anyone who cannot say a word is out of the game."},{"teacher":"Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Lead the game when it is their turn."}]},{"activity":"Oral conversation: What did you see on your way?","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.9","steps":[{"teacher":"Ask: 'What did you see on your way to school today?'","learners":"Think about the way to school."},{"teacher":"If learners hesitate, start: 'On the road I saw a bullock cart, a tea stall and a boy flying a kite. What did you see?'","learners":"Listen to the model and then share their own observations."},{"teacher":"Connect learners' answers with each other.","learners":"Listen and add what they noticed."}]},{"activity":"Story - Day 1 (a story about two brothers or sisters)","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.10","steps":[{"teacher":"Discuss the title or picture of the story with the learners.","learners":"Talk about what they see and what the story may be about."},{"teacher":"Read the story aloud with expression and proper voice modulation. Learners should not simply repeat after you.","learners":"Listen carefully and enjoy the story."},{"teacher":"Discuss the story: factual, logical, vocabulary-based, judgment or opinion questions (today's focus: logical: Why did the character do that? What would have happened if ...?). Begin in the home language if needed.","learners":"Think and respond thoughtfully; every learner takes part."},{"teacher":"Read the story again slowly, pointing to each word. Make sure each learner has a copy and follows with a finger.","learners":"Follow each word with their finger."},{"teacher":"Ask learners to read in small groups; select a group leader who helps the others. Learners read one sentence at a time while the others point with fingers.","learners":"Read with the help of one another."}]},{"activity":"Language game: Think and Make a List","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.20","steps":[{"teacher":"Divide learners into small groups, each with at least one learner who can write. Give each group a different topic: names of animals, birds, wooden objects, favourite foods, wedding-related items.","learners":"Sit in groups."},{"teacher":"Ask the groups to discuss and say the names aloud, then write the list together.","learners":"Discuss, say and write the list."},{"teacher":"Display the lists on the classroom wall. Make different lists every day.","learners":"Read the displayed lists with pride."}]},{"activity":"Mind mapping: 'tea garden'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Small group (level-wise) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.14","steps":[{"teacher":"Choose a word that can generate many related words: 'tea garden'. Ask: 'What words come to your mind when you hear the word tea garden?' Write the answers on the board or floor.","learners":"Say words they link with 'tea garden'."},{"teacher":"Discuss the words: what they mean and how they are connected.","learners":"Explain their words and listen to others."},{"teacher":"In small groups, let the learners classify the words (Plants: tea, shade tree, leaf, bud; People: worker, manager, picker, driver; Things: basket, factory, cup, kettle).","learners":"Sort the words into groups."},{"teacher":"Give the individual tasks by level and help each learner.","learners":"Work individually; read the work aloud at the end if time allows."}]}],"levelTasks":[{"activity":"Story - Day 1: individual tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.10","tasks":{"Beginner":"Circle or search for a favourite word or letter in the story and say it aloud. If a learner cannot draw a circle, write words on the board and ask them to identify them.","Letter":"Find, read and write favourite words from the story.","Word":"Find the consonant clusters in the story, read them and write them in the notebook.","Para":"Silently read the story from the textbook; find unfamiliar words and try to understand them; find rhyming words, use them in sentences and write in the notebook; ask other groups for meanings; make questions in groups.","Story":"Silently read the story; find unfamiliar words and rhyming words; practise reading with emotion; one group reads sentences formed with consonant clusters to the other group; ask and answer group questions (information, thinking and opinion questions)."}},{"activity":"Language game: Think and Make a List - level support","source":"I","ref":"p.20","tasks":{"Beginner":"Take part by saying or pointing to the letters involved and by listening carefully; Para and Story level partners help.","Letter":"Say the letters/sounds and give simple words they know.","Word":"Say and write words and short sentences for the game.","Para":"Write sentences with the words; help groups to record answers.","Story":"Write sentences or short stories with the words; help groups to record answers."}},{"activity":"Mind mapping 'tea garden': level tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.14","tasks":{"Beginner":"Circle all the words that contain the letter 'E' on the board; make a list. See how many learners find the most words.","Letter":"Circle all the words that contain the letter 'E' and make a list of them.","Word":"Use 4-5 words (for example bud, cup, tea, leaf, basket) to form sentences, starting with words of one or two syllables. Example: Dream - I had a dream last night.","Para":"Choose any five words from the map and create a story with them. Use consonant clusters correctly, read the story aloud, correct mistakes of sentence structure, spelling or grammar, then display it on the wall.","Story":"Choose any five words from the map and create a story with them. Use consonant clusters correctly, read the story aloud, correct mistakes of sentence structure, spelling or grammar, then display it on the wall."}}],"organisation":[{"grouping":"Whole class (big group)","how":"All learners of all levels sit in a 'U' shape arranged by level (Beginner, Letter, Word, Para, Story) so that the move to small groups is easy.","activities":["Warm-up: Alphabet song (last-letter word chain)","Oral conversation: What did you see on your way?","Story (Day 1 of the story): reading aloud and discussion","Mind mapping (Day 1): the word 'tea garden'"]},{"grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","how":"Learners of similar levels work together; the teacher gives each group a task for its level and spends more time with learners who need support. Rotate responsibilities (for example group leader).","activities":["Story: reading in small groups","Language game: Think and Make a List","Mind mapping: classify the words"]},{"grouping":"Individual","how":"Each learner works on a task for their own level; the teacher moves around, observes difficulties and supports individuals.","activities":["Story: level-wise individual tasks","Mind mapping: level-wise individual tasks","Daily reading (10 minutes)"]}],"materials":["A story from the school library (a story about two brothers or sisters)","a copy for each learner","Story book copies","Story book","notebooks","board","Paper or notebooks","chalk","Board","chalk (or floor)","word cards (optional)","Notebooks","Library books or storybooks"],"outcomes":["Learners take part in the oral conversation and speak without fear.","Learners show understanding of the story in the discussion and complete the task for their level.","Learners respond to the sound-symbol task for today (Language game: Think and Make a List) at their own level.","Learners add words to the mind map and use them in sentences or a story at their level.","Each learner reads a book for 10 minutes."],"observation":["Observe each learner's reading and writing during the individual tasks; note who needs individual support and how many learners share the same difficulty.","Note any learner whose level is improving; move the learner to the next level group when you see steady progress (manual p.5).","Record each learner's progress for the day in the notebook, according to the learner's level (manual p.4).","Use today's observations to adjust tomorrow's plan (manual p.5)."],"teacherNotes":["Story selection: the manual asks teachers to use picture story books or stories in the school library. Today's suggested theme (a story about two brothers or sisters) is a planning suggestion; use any suitable story you have.","The manual lists the letter and word games but does not fix the slot in the daily timetable where they are used. This plan places them in the 10-minute sound-symbol / alphabet slot (interpretation).","Mind mapping topic for this day: 'tea garden'. The manual's example uses the word 'shop'; today's topic follows the same method.","Pace: the manual says not to assume all learners progress at the same speed. Repeat a day's activity with the groups that need it before moving on.","Special needs: give extra time and prepare materials for slower learners; seat learners with hearing or vision difficulty at the front; for learners who reverse or confuse letters, trace letters on the letter card with a finger and write with dots to trace with a pencil (manual p.6)."],"components":[{"no":1,"key":"warmup","name":"Warm-up activities","keywords":["Alphabet song (last-letter word chain)","two learners lead"],"rows":[1]},{"no":2,"key":"oral","name":"Oral Discussion","keywords":["What did you see on your way?","every learner speaks"],"rows":[2]},{"no":3,"key":"story","name":"Story","keywords":["Day 1","title / picture talk","read aloud with expression","logical questions","re-read pointing","group reading","level tasks"],"rows":[3,4,5]},{"no":4,"key":"sound","name":"Sound symbol games, Sound separation-pairing","keywords":["Think and Make a List","play in turns","level support"],"rows":[6]},{"no":5,"key":"mindwrite","name":"Mind Mapping (Day 1)","keywords":["mind map: tea garden","classify the words","level task: circle letter E / sentences / story"],"rows":[7,8,9]},{"no":6,"key":"reading","name":"Daily reading","keywords":["library book","read alone","teacher listens"],"rows":[10]}],"preLesson":null},{"programme":"TARL Literacy","id":"lit-052","day":52,"phase":2,"phaseLabel":"Phase 2 (Days 46-90)","title":"Story: a story about two brothers or sisters (Day 2)","dayType":"Story Day 2 + Self-writing","focus":"Consonant clusters: lk (milk, silk) | Self-writing: a picture of a flood","duration":70,"objectives":["Listen, speak and answer in the oral conversation (familiar topic).","Retell the story, read it with expression, ask and answer questions about it and write answers.","Develop sound-symbol skills: Consonant clusters: lk (milk, silk).","Write about a topic at their own level and review the writing (a picture of a flood).","Read independently for 10 minutes every day."],"sequence":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Handkerchief game","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Learners sit in a circle and clap while singing a rhyme ('I saw a Little Bird'). One learner runs outside the circle with a handkerchief and secretly places it behind another learner, who must chase the runner. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Sit in a circle, clap and sing; run, place the handkerchief or chase as the game requires.","tlm":"A handkerchief","source":"M","ref":"p.8","n":1},{"activity":"Oral conversation: familiar topic","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Hold a conversation on the topic 'what I do after school'. Give each learner a chance to speak; be patient with learners who need extra time.","learners":"Talk about the topic and listen to others.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.9","n":2},{"activity":"Story (Day 2 of the story): retelling","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":6,"teacher":"Ask learners to retell yesterday's story in their own words. Prompt with questions on the beginning, middle and end.","learners":"Retell the story using their own words.","tlm":"The same story book as yesterday","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":3},{"activity":"Story: reading with actions and group questions","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":9,"teacher":"Learners practise reading with actions and expressions; one learner per group reads aloud to the class. Guide groups to make questions about the story (guide initially). Groups take turns to ask and answer each other's questions. Word-level learners also read aloud the consonants learned on the first day.","learners":"Read with actions; make questions (word-level learners help write them); ask and answer questions with another group.","tlm":"Story book, slate or paper for questions","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":4},{"activity":"Story: writing answers individually","grouping":"Individual","minutes":5,"teacher":"Para and Story level learners write answers to all questions individually; read and correct their responses after they finish.","learners":"Write the answers in their notebooks; Beginner/Letter/Word learners read or listen and answer orally.","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":5},{"activity":"Consonant clusters: introduction","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":4,"teacher":"Two-letter clusters: after same-letter clusters, familiarise learners with clusters of two different letters ('lk' as in milk, silk, bulk). Discuss the words, ask learners to pronounce them and to frame sentences using them.","learners":"Listen, pronounce the cluster and say words that contain it.","tlm":"Board and chalk, words list (milk silk bulk elk sulk)","source":"M","ref":"p.16","n":6},{"activity":"Consonant cluster game: List of Conjunct Consonants","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":6,"teacher":"Write the names of the children in the class on the board and list those that contain conjunct consonants. If no names contain them, say words or sentences with conjunct consonants and write them on the board. Observe closely and help learners who need support.","learners":"Try to form new words using those conjunct consonants.","tlm":"Names, words or sentences on the board","source":"M","ref":"p.17","n":7},{"activity":"Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on a picture of a flood","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Start a conversation about a picture card: 'a picture of a flood'. Involve all learners and ask open-ended questions.","learners":"Take part in the discussion and share thoughts freely.","tlm":"Picture card or topic on the board","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":8},{"activity":"Self-writing: individual writing","grouping":"Individual","minutes":7,"teacher":"Give each level its task (see level table). Let learners take ownership of what they draw and write; mistakes are fine.","learners":"Draw and write about the topic at their level.","tlm":"Notebooks, crayons or pencils","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":9},{"activity":"Self-writing: review and reading back","grouping":"Individual","minutes":3,"teacher":"Ask each learner 'What did you draw or write?' and have them read it aloud once. Word-level learners read to the group; discuss spelling, punctuation and sentence structure. Help beginners by writing their text in the notebook for them if needed.","learners":"Read what they wrote; correct mistakes after listening to their own reading.","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":10},{"activity":"Daily reading (10 minutes)","grouping":"Individual","minutes":10,"teacher":"Give each learner a library book or any storybook. Move around, listen to individual readers and note their level.","learners":"Read independently a book of their choice.","tlm":"Library books or storybooks","source":"M","ref":"p.7","n":11}],"procedures":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Handkerchief game","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","steps":[{"teacher":"Seat the learners in a circle and start clapping and singing the rhyme 'I saw a Little Bird'.","learners":"Clap and sing together."},{"teacher":"One learner runs outside the circle holding a handkerchief and secretly places it behind another learner.","learners":"Everyone keeps clapping; the learner who finds the handkerchief behind them takes it and chases the runner."},{"teacher":"If the runner sits in the chaser's place before being caught, they stay in the game; if caught, they are out. Continue in this way.","learners":"Play fairly and take turns."}]},{"activity":"Oral conversation: familiar topic","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.9","steps":[{"teacher":"Introduce the topic: 'what I do after school'.","learners":"Think about their own experience."},{"teacher":"Ask open questions; give every learner a chance. Involve learners who speak less.","learners":"Speak freely and without fear."},{"teacher":"Praise efforts and sum up.","learners":"Listen and respect each other's ideas."}]},{"activity":"Story - Day 2 (a story about two brothers or sisters)","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.11","steps":[{"teacher":"Ask learners to retell the story they read yesterday in their own words.","learners":"Retell, helping each other remember."},{"teacher":"In small groups learners practise reading the story using actions and expressions; one learner from each group then reads aloud to the class.","learners":"Read with actions and expression; a representative reads aloud."},{"teacher":"Guide the groups to come up with questions about the story (guide initially). Word-level learners can support by helping write them down.","learners":"Make questions together."},{"teacher":"Groups take turns to ask and answer each other's questions. Useful kinds: questions whose answer is not in the text; questions needing thinking beyond the text; questions asking for an opinion.","learners":"Ask, answer and discuss in the groups."},{"teacher":"Word-level learners also read aloud the consonants they learned on the first day.","learners":"Read the consonant clusters aloud."}]},{"activity":"Consonant clusters (lk) and the game 'List of Conjunct Consonants'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.16-17","steps":[{"teacher":"Two-letter clusters: after same-letter clusters, familiarise learners with clusters of two different letters ('lk' as in milk, silk, bulk). Discuss the words, ask learners to pronounce them and to frame sentences using them.","learners":"Listen, pronounce and find words in the text."},{"teacher":"Write the words on the board: milk silk bulk elk sulk. Read them aloud with distinct pronunciation of the cluster.","learners":"Read the words aloud; point to the cluster in each word."},{"teacher":"Write the names of the children in the class on the board and list those that contain conjunct consonants. If no names contain them, say words or sentences with conjunct consonants and write them on the board.","learners":"Try to form new words using those conjunct consonants."}]},{"activity":"Self-writing: 'Discussion, Writing, Self-review'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.15","steps":[{"teacher":"Start a conversation about a picture card: 'a picture of a flood'. Involve all learners and ask open-ended questions.","learners":"Discuss and answer questions."},{"teacher":"Give writing time at each level: draw then write (Beginner), write about what they liked (Letter), a sentence (Word), a paragraph or story on a topic of their choice (Para/Story).","learners":"Write at their level and take ownership of the work."},{"teacher":"Review: ask 'What did you draw or write?' Have each learner read the text aloud once. Support with writing if needed.","learners":"Read aloud, listen to their pronunciation and correct mistakes."}]}],"levelTasks":[{"activity":"Story - Day 2: level-wise tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.11","tasks":{"Beginner":"Retell with the group by pointing to pictures or words; read aloud with group support (interpretation of the manual's group reading task).","Letter":"Read with the group, pointing to words; say the letters and words they know (interpretation of the manual's group reading task).","Word":"Support the group in writing the questions; read aloud the consonant clusters learned on the first day.","Para":"Ask the group's questions to another group, discuss them, then write answers to all questions individually; the teacher reads and corrects.","Story":"Ask the group's questions to another group, discuss them, then write answers to all questions individually; the teacher reads and corrects."}},{"activity":"Consonant clusters (lk): level tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.16-17","tasks":{"Beginner":"Listen to the sound of the cluster and point to it in a word; continue with letter-sound work (interpretation: the manual describes clusters for learners lagging in reading words and sentences).","Letter":"Listen to the cluster sound and pick words with the cluster from a word card (interpretation).","Word":"Find the cluster in the story or textbook words, read the words and write them in the notebook.","Para":"Form words and sentences using the cluster; read the sentences aloud.","Story":"Form words and sentences using the cluster; read the sentences aloud; use them in the story writing."}},{"activity":"Self-writing: level tasks and review","source":"M","ref":"p.15","tasks":{"Beginner":"Draw a picture about the discussion and then write a few sentences about it, expressing thoughts freely. Review: say what they drew or wrote; read the text aloud once; the teacher may write the text in the notebook for them.","Letter":"Write about what they liked, using drawing and writing; write any words or sentences they can. Review: read the text aloud once; correct punctuation mistakes using the Barakhadi chart.","Word":"Write a sentence based on the conversation. Mistakes in spelling, punctuation and sentence structure are fine. Review: read it to the group; discuss and correct mistakes together.","Para":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation.","Story":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation."}}],"organisation":[{"grouping":"Whole class (big group)","how":"All learners of all levels sit in a 'U' shape arranged by level (Beginner, Letter, Word, Para, Story) so that the move to small groups is easy.","activities":["Warm-up: Handkerchief game","Oral conversation: familiar topic","Story (Day 2 of the story): retelling","Consonant clusters: introduction","Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on a picture of a flood"]},{"grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","how":"Learners of similar levels work together; the teacher gives each group a task for its level and spends more time with learners who need support. Rotate responsibilities (for example group leader).","activities":["Story: reading with actions and group questions","Consonant cluster game: List of Conjunct Consonants"]},{"grouping":"Individual","how":"Each learner works on a task for their own level; the teacher moves around, observes difficulties and supports individuals.","activities":["Story: writing answers individually","Self-writing: individual writing","Self-writing: review and reading back","Daily reading (10 minutes)"]}],"materials":["A handkerchief","The same story book as yesterday","Story book","slate or paper for questions","Notebooks","Board","chalk","words list (milk silk bulk elk sulk)","Names","words or sentences on the board","Picture card or topic on the board","crayons or pencils","Library books or storybooks"],"outcomes":["Learners take part in the oral conversation and speak without fear.","Learners retell the story, read with expression and ask or answer questions at their level.","Learners respond to the sound-symbol task for today (Consonant clusters: lk (milk, silk)) at their own level.","Learners write about the topic at their level and read it aloud.","Each learner reads a book for 10 minutes."],"observation":["Observe each learner's reading and writing during the individual tasks; note who needs individual support and how many learners share the same difficulty.","Note any learner whose level is improving; move the learner to the next level group when you see steady progress (manual p.5).","Record each learner's progress for the day in the notebook, according to the learner's level (manual p.4).","Use today's observations to adjust tomorrow's plan (manual p.5)."],"teacherNotes":["Questions to elicit on Day 2: information questions (answer not in the text), thinking questions (needs knowledge beyond the text) and opinion questions (feedback on something in the text).","Consonant clusters: do these activities daily for learners who find reading complex words hard; the aim is to remove the fear of reading clusters. Teachers may carry out similar activities on their own.","Writing has two parts, content and sequence: encourage learners to read what they wrote, improve it and rewrite it for clarity and correctness (manual p.15).","Pace: the manual says not to assume all learners progress at the same speed. Repeat a day's activity with the groups that need it before moving on.","Special needs: give extra time and prepare materials for slower learners; seat learners with hearing or vision difficulty at the front; for learners who reverse or confuse letters, trace letters on the letter card with a finger and write with dots to trace with a pencil (manual p.6)."],"components":[{"no":1,"key":"warmup","name":"Warm-up activities","keywords":["Handkerchief game","two learners lead"],"rows":[1]},{"no":2,"key":"oral","name":"Oral Discussion","keywords":["familiar topic","every learner speaks"],"rows":[2]},{"no":3,"key":"story","name":"Story","keywords":["Day 2","retell","read with actions","group questions","ask and answer","write answers (Para/Story)"],"rows":[3,4,5]},{"no":4,"key":"sound","name":"Sound symbol games, Sound separation-pairing","keywords":["consonant cluster 'lk'","pronounce and find words","game: List of Conjunct Consonants"],"rows":[6,7]},{"no":5,"key":"mindwrite","name":"Individual-Writing (Day 2)","keywords":["discussion","write at own level","self-review (read aloud)"],"rows":[8,9,10]},{"no":6,"key":"reading","name":"Daily reading","keywords":["library book","read alone","teacher listens"],"rows":[11]}],"preLesson":null},{"programme":"TARL Literacy","id":"lit-053","day":53,"phase":2,"phaseLabel":"Phase 2 (Days 46-90)","title":"Story: a story about a tiny creature with a big heart (Day 1)","dayType":"Story Day 1 + Mind mapping","focus":"Barakhadi / alphabet and phonics chart (line 9, letter 'b') | Mind map: fishing","duration":70,"objectives":["Listen, speak and answer in the oral conversation (conversation on a picture).","Listen to and read a story with understanding; discuss it in big and small groups and respond at their own level.","Develop sound-symbol skills: Barakhadi / alphabet and phonics chart (line 9, letter 'b').","Build vocabulary through a mind map ('fishing') and use the words at their own level.","Read independently for 10 minutes every day."],"sequence":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Rhyme - 'I caught a Fish Alive'","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Say the rhyme with actions, then say it together. Lines: One, two, three, four, five, once I caught a fish alive. / Six, seven, eight, nine, ten, then I let it go again. / Why did you let it go? Because it bit my finger so. / Which finger did it bite? This little finger on my right. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Listen, then say the rhyme with actions.","tlm":"Rhyme chart or board (optional)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","n":1},{"activity":"Oral conversation: conversation on a picture","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Show a picture of a kitchen where food is being cooked and ask what is happening, who is doing what and what is happening around them. Let learners think creatively and even make up a story.","learners":"Look at the picture, answer questions and make up their own story about it.","tlm":"Picture card of a kitchen where food is being cooked","source":"M","ref":"p.9","n":2},{"activity":"Story (Day 1 of the story): reading aloud and discussion","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":8,"teacher":"Discuss the title or picture of the story with the learners. Read the story aloud with expression and voice modulation (learners do not repeat after you). Discuss it, with emphasis on vocabulary-based questions. Read it again slowly, pointing to each word.","learners":"Talk about the title/picture; listen; answer questions; follow each word with a finger in their own copy.","tlm":"A story from the school library (a story about a tiny creature with a big heart), a copy for each learner","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":3},{"activity":"Story: reading in small groups","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":7,"teacher":"Form level-wise groups with a group leader. Learners read the story one sentence at a time while the others follow with their fingers. Para and Story level learners practise reading with emotion and expression.","learners":"Read the story sentence by sentence, supporting each other; the group leader helps.","tlm":"Story book copies","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":4},{"activity":"Story: level-wise individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":5,"teacher":"Give each learner the task for their level (see level table) and support those who need it.","learners":"Beginner/Letter: find and write favourite words or letters. Word: find consonant clusters. Para/Story: silently read, find unfamiliar and rhyming words.","tlm":"Story book, notebooks, board","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":5},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart: big group reading","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":3,"teacher":"Show the Barakhadi chart and ask which letter they like. Read the letter 'b' on the chart; learners listen carefully and point to it on their own chart (they do not repeat after you).","learners":"Listen and point to the letter on their own chart.","tlm":"Barakhadi chart, alphabet or phonics chart","source":"M","ref":"p.13","n":6},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart: small-group practice","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Learners practise reading the alphabet or phonics chart in groups and help each other. One learner per group reads aloud. Occasionally ask learners to identify the sounds of letters. Give each level its group task.","learners":"Read the chart in groups; one learner reads aloud; do the level task.","tlm":"Alphabet or phonics chart, board or floor","source":"M","ref":"p.13","n":7},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart: individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":2,"teacher":"Give each learner an individual task for their level and observe closely; assist any learner who needs individual support.","learners":"Say and write a letter or word, a sentence or a short paragraph (by level).","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.13","n":8},{"activity":"Mind mapping (Day 1): the word 'fishing'","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Ask: 'What words come to your mind when you hear the word fishing?' Write learners' answers on the board or floor (Para and Story level learners write the words themselves). Guide the map towards the learning objective. Example words: rohu, catla, magur, puti, net, hook, line, basket, pond, river, lake, market.","learners":"Say words connected with 'fishing'; share the meaning and feeling of words.","tlm":"Board, chalk (or floor)","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":9},{"activity":"Mind mapping: classify the words","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":4,"teacher":"Ask learners to classify the words in groups, for example: Fish: rohu, catla, magur, puti; Things: net, hook, line, basket; Places: pond, river, lake, market.","learners":"Sort the words into groups and say why.","tlm":"Board, chalk, word cards (optional)","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":10},{"activity":"Mind mapping: level-wise individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":6,"teacher":"Give each learner the individual task for their level; observe closely and give individual support. Display corrected stories on the wall.","learners":"Complete the task for their level (see level table).","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":11},{"activity":"Daily reading (10 minutes)","grouping":"Individual","minutes":10,"teacher":"Give each learner a library book or any storybook. Move around, listen to individual readers and note their level.","learners":"Read independently a book of their choice.","tlm":"Library books or storybooks","source":"M","ref":"p.7","n":12}],"procedures":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Rhyme - 'I caught a Fish Alive'","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","steps":[{"teacher":"Say the rhyme 'I caught a Fish Alive' slowly with actions: One, two, three, four, five, once I caught a fish alive. / Six, seven, eight, nine, ten, then I let it go again. / Why did you let it go? Because it bit my finger so. / Which finger did it bite? This little finger on my right.","learners":"Listen and watch the actions."},{"teacher":"Say it again; invite learners to join with actions.","learners":"Say the rhyme together with actions."},{"teacher":"Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Choose a rhyme they like and lead."}]},{"activity":"Oral conversation: conversation on a picture","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.9","steps":[{"teacher":"Show the picture of a kitchen where food is being cooked.","learners":"Look carefully."},{"teacher":"Ask: What is happening in the picture? Who is doing what? What is happening around them? Then: How do the people feel? How can you tell?","learners":"Answer in their own words; every learner gets a chance."},{"teacher":"Let learners imagine and make up a short story from the picture.","learners":"Tell their stories to the class."}]},{"activity":"Story - Day 1 (a story about a tiny creature with a big heart)","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.10","steps":[{"teacher":"Discuss the title or picture of the story with the learners.","learners":"Talk about what they see and what the story may be about."},{"teacher":"Read the story aloud with expression and proper voice modulation. Learners should not simply repeat after you.","learners":"Listen carefully and enjoy the story."},{"teacher":"Discuss the story: factual, logical, vocabulary-based, judgment or opinion questions (today's focus: vocabulary-based: What does this word mean? Which word in the story means the same as ...?). Begin in the home language if needed.","learners":"Think and respond thoughtfully; every learner takes part."},{"teacher":"Read the story again slowly, pointing to each word. Make sure each learner has a copy and follows with a finger.","learners":"Follow each word with their finger."},{"teacher":"Ask learners to read in small groups; select a group leader who helps the others. Learners read one sentence at a time while the others point with fingers.","learners":"Read with the help of one another."}]},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart activity (line 9)","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Small group (level-wise) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.13","steps":[{"teacher":"Show the Barakhadi chart and ask the learners which letter they like. Where is the letter 'b'?","learners":"Look for the letter on the chart."},{"teacher":"Read the letter 'b' on the chart. Learners listen and point to it on their own chart. Make sure they do not repeat after you.","learners":"Listen and point to the letter."},{"teacher":"Learners read the alphabet or phonics chart in their groups and help each other; one learner from each group comes forward to read aloud.","learners":"Read in groups; the representative reads aloud."},{"teacher":"Occasionally ask them to identify the sounds of letters from the chart.","learners":"Say the sound of the letter you point to."},{"teacher":"As an extra activity, write some letters on the floor, call out each letter one by one and let the learners jump onto the correct letter.","learners":"Jump onto the letter that is called."}]},{"activity":"Mind mapping: 'fishing'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Small group (level-wise) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.14","steps":[{"teacher":"Choose a word that can generate many related words: 'fishing'. Ask: 'What words come to your mind when you hear the word fishing?' Write the answers on the board or floor.","learners":"Say words they link with 'fishing'."},{"teacher":"Discuss the words: what they mean and how they are connected.","learners":"Explain their words and listen to others."},{"teacher":"In small groups, let the learners classify the words (Fish: rohu, catla, magur, puti; Things: net, hook, line, basket; Places: pond, river, lake, market).","learners":"Sort the words into groups."},{"teacher":"Give the individual tasks by level and help each learner.","learners":"Work individually; read the work aloud at the end if time allows."}]}],"levelTasks":[{"activity":"Story - Day 1: individual tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.10","tasks":{"Beginner":"Circle or search for a favourite word or letter in the story and say it aloud. If a learner cannot draw a circle, write words on the board and ask them to identify them.","Letter":"Find, read and write favourite words from the story.","Word":"Find the consonant clusters in the story, read them and write them in the notebook.","Para":"Silently read the story from the textbook; find unfamiliar words and try to understand them; find rhyming words, use them in sentences and write in the notebook; ask other groups for meanings; make questions in groups.","Story":"Silently read the story; find unfamiliar words and rhyming words; practise reading with emotion; one group reads sentences formed with consonant clusters to the other group; ask and answer group questions (information, thinking and opinion questions)."}},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart: level tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.13","tasks":{"Beginner":"Small group: read the chart in the group; find and write favourite letters from the line. Individual: say and write a letter of their choice.","Letter":"Small group: read the chart; find and write favourite letters or words from any line. Individual: say a word on their own that begins with any letter.","Word":"Small group: write one or two lines of letters on the board or floor and use them to form words. Individual: speak and write sentences using words they know.","Para":"Small group: prepare word lists using the Barakhadi chart (for example items found in a shop or in the kitchen). Individual: write short paragraphs using the words formed with the Barakhadi chart.","Story":"Small group: prepare word lists using the Barakhadi chart. Individual: write short paragraphs using the words formed with the Barakhadi chart."}},{"activity":"Mind mapping 'fishing': level tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.14","tasks":{"Beginner":"Circle all the words that contain the letter 'E' on the board; make a list. See how many learners find the most words.","Letter":"Circle all the words that contain the letter 'E' and make a list of them.","Word":"Use 4-5 words (for example net, hook, lake, line, pond) to form sentences, starting with words of one or two syllables. Example: Dream - I had a dream last night.","Para":"Choose any five words from the map and create a story with them. Use consonant clusters correctly, read the story aloud, correct mistakes of sentence structure, spelling or grammar, then display it on the wall.","Story":"Choose any five words from the map and create a story with them. Use consonant clusters correctly, read the story aloud, correct mistakes of sentence structure, spelling or grammar, then display it on the wall."}}],"organisation":[{"grouping":"Whole class (big group)","how":"All learners of all levels sit in a 'U' shape arranged by level (Beginner, Letter, Word, Para, Story) so that the move to small groups is easy.","activities":["Warm-up: Rhyme - 'I caught a Fish Alive'","Oral conversation: conversation on a picture","Story (Day 1 of the story): reading aloud and discussion","Barakhadi chart: big group reading","Mind mapping (Day 1): the word 'fishing'"]},{"grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","how":"Learners of similar levels work together; the teacher gives each group a task for its level and spends more time with learners who need support. Rotate responsibilities (for example group leader).","activities":["Story: reading in small groups","Barakhadi chart: small-group practice","Mind mapping: classify the words"]},{"grouping":"Individual","how":"Each learner works on a task for their own level; the teacher moves around, observes difficulties and supports individuals.","activities":["Story: level-wise individual tasks","Barakhadi chart: individual tasks","Mind mapping: level-wise individual tasks","Daily reading (10 minutes)"]}],"materials":["Rhyme chart or board (optional)","Picture card of a kitchen where food is being cooked","A story from the school library (a story about a tiny creature with a big heart)","a copy for each learner","Story book copies","Story book","notebooks","board","Barakhadi chart","alphabet or phonics chart","Alphabet or phonics chart","board or floor","Notebooks","Board","chalk (or floor)","chalk","word cards (optional)","Library books or storybooks"],"outcomes":["Learners take part in the oral conversation and speak without fear.","Learners show understanding of the story in the discussion and complete the task for their level.","Learners respond to the sound-symbol task for today (Barakhadi / alphabet and phonics chart (line 9, letter 'b')) at their own level.","Learners add words to the mind map and use them in sentences or a story at their level.","Each learner reads a book for 10 minutes."],"observation":["Observe each learner's reading and writing during the individual tasks; note who needs individual support and how many learners share the same difficulty.","Note any learner whose level is improving; move the learner to the next level group when you see steady progress (manual p.5).","Record each learner's progress for the day in the notebook, according to the learner's level (manual p.4).","Use today's observations to adjust tomorrow's plan (manual p.5)."],"teacherNotes":["Story selection: the manual asks teachers to use picture story books or stories in the school library. Today's suggested theme (a story about a tiny creature with a big heart) is a planning suggestion; use any suitable story you have.","Barakhadi: learners who need extra time should get repeated practice using one or two sound units at a time. Topic-based discussion helps oral expression, thinking and understanding.","Mind mapping topic for this day: 'fishing'. The manual's example uses the word 'shop'; today's topic follows the same method.","Pace: the manual says not to assume all learners progress at the same speed. Repeat a day's activity with the groups that need it before moving on.","Special needs: give extra time and prepare materials for slower learners; seat learners with hearing or vision difficulty at the front; for learners who reverse or confuse letters, trace letters on the letter card with a finger and write with dots to trace with a pencil (manual p.6)."],"components":[{"no":1,"key":"warmup","name":"Warm-up activities","keywords":["Rhyme - 'I caught a Fish Alive'","two learners lead"],"rows":[1]},{"no":2,"key":"oral","name":"Oral Discussion","keywords":["conversation on a picture","every learner speaks"],"rows":[2]},{"no":3,"key":"story","name":"Story","keywords":["Day 1","title / picture talk","read aloud with expression","vocabulary-based questions","re-read pointing","group reading","level tasks"],"rows":[3,4,5]},{"no":4,"key":"sound","name":"Sound symbol games, Sound separation-pairing","keywords":["Barakhadi / alphabet chart","listen and point (no repeating)","group reading","level tasks"],"rows":[6,7,8]},{"no":5,"key":"mindwrite","name":"Mind Mapping (Day 1)","keywords":["mind map: fishing","classify the words","level task: circle letter E / sentences / story"],"rows":[9,10,11]},{"no":6,"key":"reading","name":"Daily reading","keywords":["library book","read alone","teacher listens"],"rows":[12]}],"preLesson":null},{"programme":"TARL Literacy","id":"lit-054","day":54,"phase":2,"phaseLabel":"Phase 2 (Days 46-90)","title":"Saturday: drama presentation","dayType":"Saturday drama + Self-writing","focus":"Language game: Think and Make a List | Self-writing: the story we acted out (a story about a tiny creature with a big heart)","duration":70,"objectives":["Listen, speak and answer in the oral conversation (listening and storytelling).","Express a story through role play, using voice, facial expressions and gestures.","Develop sound-symbol skills: Language game: Think and Make a List.","Write about the story and review the writing.","Read independently for 10 minutes every day."],"sequence":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Singing and Spinning","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Learners sit in a circle and pass a small object while you clap with your back turned; when the clapping stops, the learner holding it sings a song, recites a poem or tells a joke. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Pass the object round the circle; sing, recite or tell a joke when the clapping stops.","tlm":"A small object (chalk or pencil)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","n":1},{"activity":"Oral conversation: listening and storytelling","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Tell an interesting story starter and involve the learners: 'A tiny elephant lived in my pocket. Where did we go together?' Let learners imagine and continue the story.","learners":"Listen to the teacher, then imagine and continue the story. Learners can also recite a rhyme or story they know.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.9","n":2},{"activity":"Dramatic presentation: introduction and reading","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Explain what a dramatic presentation is and how it is done. Provide stories discussed during the week and read one aloud once more. Para and Story level learners support Beginner and Letter level learners in reading.","learners":"Listen, read along, then each learner chooses a character.","tlm":"Stories discussed in the week (a story about two brothers or sisters; a story about a tiny creature with a big heart)","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":3},{"activity":"Dramatic presentation: planning in small groups","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":8,"teacher":"Each group discusses and plans dialogues; Para or Story level learners write the dialogues. Groups prepare their dramatic presentation.","learners":"Choose characters, plan and rehearse dialogues with facial expressions and gestures.","tlm":"Story, paper for dialogues","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":4},{"activity":"Dramatic presentation: performances and feedback","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":7,"teacher":"Learners sit in a U shape. Each group presents; after each performance, watching learners say what they enjoyed and what could be improved.","learners":"Perform in turn; watch; give feedback.","tlm":"Open space (U-shape seating)","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":5},{"activity":"Language game: Think and Make a List","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Each group gets a topic and writes a list together; the lists are displayed on the classroom wall. Observe each learner and give help where needed.","learners":"Play the game, take turns and read or say the words they make.","tlm":"Paper or notebooks, chalk","source":"M","ref":"p.20","n":6},{"activity":"Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on the story we acted out (a story about a tiny creature with a big heart)","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Start a conversation about the story used for the drama: 'the story we acted out (a story about a tiny creature with a big heart)'. Involve all learners with open-ended questions.","learners":"Take part in the discussion and share thoughts freely.","tlm":"Picture card or topic on the board","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":7},{"activity":"Self-writing: individual writing","grouping":"Individual","minutes":7,"teacher":"Give each level its task (see level table). Let learners take ownership of what they draw and write; mistakes are fine.","learners":"Draw and write about the topic at their level.","tlm":"Notebooks, crayons or pencils","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":8},{"activity":"Self-writing: review and reading back","grouping":"Individual","minutes":3,"teacher":"Ask each learner 'What did you draw or write?' and have them read it aloud once. Word-level learners read to the group; discuss spelling, punctuation and sentence structure. Help beginners by writing their text in the notebook for them if needed.","learners":"Read what they wrote; correct mistakes after listening to their own reading.","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":9},{"activity":"Daily reading (10 minutes)","grouping":"Individual","minutes":10,"teacher":"Give each learner a library book or any storybook. Move around, listen to individual readers and note their level.","learners":"Read independently a book of their choice.","tlm":"Library books or storybooks","source":"M","ref":"p.7","n":10}],"procedures":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Singing and Spinning","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","steps":[{"teacher":"Seat the learners in a circle; give a small object to one learner.","learners":"Sit in a circle."},{"teacher":"Stand outside the circle with your back to them and clap steadily; they pass the object.","learners":"Pass the object while the clapping continues."},{"teacher":"Stop clapping; the learner holding the object sings, recites or tells a joke.","learners":"Perform, and everybody claps."}]},{"activity":"Oral conversation: listening and storytelling","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.9","steps":[{"teacher":"Say the starter: 'A tiny elephant lived in my pocket. Where did we go together?'","learners":"Listen and imagine."},{"teacher":"Ask learners to continue the story one by one. Encourage those who speak less.","learners":"Add ideas to the story."},{"teacher":"Invite a learner to recite a poem or rhyme they know.","learners":"Recite and listen to others."}]},{"activity":"Saturday special: dramatic presentation","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.11","steps":[{"teacher":"Explain what a dramatic presentation is and how it can be done. Give the groups the stories discussed during the week.","learners":"Listen to the explanation."},{"teacher":"Read a story aloud once more. Learners at story and paragraph level support those at beginner and letter level in reading.","learners":"Read along; helpers support their friends."},{"teacher":"After reading, each learner chooses a character from the story.","learners":"Choose a role (boys may play girl roles and girls may play boy roles)."},{"teacher":"In groups, learners discuss and plan the dialogues; paragraph or story level learners write the dialogues.","learners":"Plan and write dialogues together."},{"teacher":"Learners sit in a U shape. Each group presents its drama. After each performance, ask what the audience enjoyed and what could be improved.","learners":"Perform, watch and give kind feedback."}]},{"activity":"Language game: Think and Make a List","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.20","steps":[{"teacher":"Divide learners into small groups, each with at least one learner who can write. Give each group a different topic: names of animals, birds, wooden objects, favourite foods, wedding-related items.","learners":"Sit in groups."},{"teacher":"Ask the groups to discuss and say the names aloud, then write the list together.","learners":"Discuss, say and write the list."},{"teacher":"Display the lists on the classroom wall. Make different lists every day.","learners":"Read the displayed lists with pride."}]},{"activity":"Self-writing: 'Discussion, Writing, Self-review'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.15","steps":[{"teacher":"Start a conversation about the story used for the drama: 'the story we acted out (a story about a tiny creature with a big heart)'. Involve all learners with open-ended questions.","learners":"Discuss and answer questions."},{"teacher":"Give writing time at each level: draw then write (Beginner), write about what they liked (Letter), a sentence (Word), a paragraph or story on a topic of their choice (Para/Story).","learners":"Write at their level and take ownership of the work."},{"teacher":"Review: ask 'What did you draw or write?' Have each learner read the text aloud once. Support with writing if needed.","learners":"Read aloud, listen to their pronunciation and correct mistakes."}]}],"levelTasks":[{"activity":"Drama: roles by level","source":"M","ref":"p.11","tasks":{"Beginner":"Take a character role and say or act short lines with help from Para and Story level learners.","Letter":"Take a character role and say or act short lines with help from Para and Story level learners.","Word":"Take a role and speak the dialogues; help rehearse.","Para":"Write the dialogues for the group and support Beginner, Letter and Word level learners throughout.","Story":"Write the dialogues for the group and support Beginner, Letter and Word level learners throughout."}},{"activity":"Language game: Think and Make a List - level support","source":"I","ref":"p.20","tasks":{"Beginner":"Take part by saying or pointing to the letters involved and by listening carefully; Para and Story level partners help.","Letter":"Say the letters/sounds and give simple words they know.","Word":"Say and write words and short sentences for the game.","Para":"Write sentences with the words; help groups to record answers.","Story":"Write sentences or short stories with the words; help groups to record answers."}},{"activity":"Self-writing: level tasks and review","source":"M","ref":"p.15","tasks":{"Beginner":"Draw a picture about the discussion and then write a few sentences about it, expressing thoughts freely. Review: say what they drew or wrote; read the text aloud once; the teacher may write the text in the notebook for them.","Letter":"Write about what they liked, using drawing and writing; write any words or sentences they can. Review: read the text aloud once; correct punctuation mistakes using the Barakhadi chart.","Word":"Write a sentence based on the conversation. Mistakes in spelling, punctuation and sentence structure are fine. Review: read it to the group; discuss and correct mistakes together.","Para":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation.","Story":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation."}}],"organisation":[{"grouping":"Whole class (big group)","how":"All learners of all levels sit in a 'U' shape arranged by level (Beginner, Letter, Word, Para, Story) so that the move to small groups is easy.","activities":["Warm-up: Singing and Spinning","Oral conversation: listening and storytelling","Dramatic presentation: introduction and reading","Dramatic presentation: performances and feedback","Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on the story we acted out (a story about a tiny creature with a big heart)"]},{"grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","how":"Learners of similar levels work together; the teacher gives each group a task for its level and spends more time with learners who need support. Rotate responsibilities (for example group leader).","activities":["Dramatic presentation: planning in small groups","Language game: Think and Make a List"]},{"grouping":"Individual","how":"Each learner works on a task for their own level; the teacher moves around, observes difficulties and supports individuals.","activities":["Self-writing: individual writing","Self-writing: review and reading back","Daily reading (10 minutes)"]}],"materials":["A small object (chalk or pencil)","Stories discussed in the week (a story about two brothers or sisters; a story about a tiny creature with a big heart)","Story","paper for dialogues","Open space (U-shape seating)","Paper or notebooks","chalk","Picture card or topic on the board","Notebooks","crayons or pencils","Library books or storybooks"],"outcomes":["Learners take part in the oral conversation and speak without fear.","Learners present a role in the group drama and give feedback to others.","Learners respond to the sound-symbol task for today (Language game: Think and Make a List) at their own level.","Learners write about the story at their level and read it aloud.","Each learner reads a book for 10 minutes."],"observation":["Observe each learner's reading and writing during the individual tasks; note who needs individual support and how many learners share the same difficulty.","Note any learner whose level is improving; move the learner to the next level group when you see steady progress (manual p.5).","Record each learner's progress for the day in the notebook, according to the learner's level (manual p.4).","Use today's observations to adjust tomorrow's plan (manual p.5)."],"teacherNotes":["Saturday: this plan assumes Day 1 is a Monday (six teaching days per week). If your school week is different, hold the drama presentation on your Saturday and keep the other days in sequence.","The manual lists the letter and word games but does not fix the slot in the daily timetable where they are used. This plan places them in the 10-minute sound-symbol / alphabet slot (interpretation).","Writing has two parts, content and sequence: encourage learners to read what they wrote, improve it and rewrite it for clarity and correctness (manual p.15).","Pace: the manual says not to assume all learners progress at the same speed. Repeat a day's activity with the groups that need it before moving on.","Special needs: give extra time and prepare materials for slower learners; seat learners with hearing or vision difficulty at the front; for learners who reverse or confuse letters, trace letters on the letter card with a finger and write with dots to trace with a pencil (manual p.6)."],"components":[{"no":1,"key":"warmup","name":"Warm-up activities","keywords":["Singing and Spinning","two learners lead"],"rows":[1]},{"no":2,"key":"oral","name":"Oral Discussion","keywords":["listening and storytelling","every learner speaks"],"rows":[2]},{"no":3,"key":"story","name":"Story (Saturday: dramatic presentation)","keywords":["Saturday drama","choose a character","plan dialogues","perform in U shape","feedback"],"rows":[3,4,5]},{"no":4,"key":"sound","name":"Sound symbol games, Sound separation-pairing","keywords":["Think and Make a List","play in turns","level support"],"rows":[6]},{"no":5,"key":"mindwrite","name":"Individual-Writing (Day 2)","keywords":["discussion","write at own level","self-review (read aloud)"],"rows":[7,8,9]},{"no":6,"key":"reading","name":"Daily reading","keywords":["library book","read alone","teacher listens"],"rows":[10]}],"preLesson":null},{"programme":"TARL Literacy","id":"lit-055","day":55,"phase":2,"phaseLabel":"Phase 2 (Days 46-90)","title":"Story: a story about a tiny creature with a big heart (Day 2)","dayType":"Story Day 2 + Self-writing","focus":"Consonant clusters: str (string, street) | Self-writing: a kind person I know","duration":70,"objectives":["Listen, speak and answer in the oral conversation (What did you see on your way?).","Retell the story, read it with expression, ask and answer questions about it and write answers.","Develop sound-symbol skills: Consonant clusters: str (string, street).","Write about a topic at their own level and review the writing (a kind person I know).","Read independently for 10 minutes every day."],"sequence":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Rain clapping","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Everyone stands in a circle with eyes closed and keeps clapping: first one finger, then two, three, four and finally five fingers. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Stand in a circle, close the eyes and clap with 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 fingers.","tlm":"After the activity ask: What sound came after the last clap?","source":"M","ref":"p.8","n":1},{"activity":"Oral conversation: What did you see on your way?","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Ask learners to describe what they saw on their way to school. If they are hesitant, begin yourself: 'I saw the river shining, a boat leaving the bank and two birds on a bamboo pole. What did you see on your way?'","learners":"Describe what they saw on the way to school and connect with what others share.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.9","n":2},{"activity":"Story (Day 2 of the story): retelling","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":6,"teacher":"Ask learners to retell yesterday's story in their own words. Prompt with questions on the beginning, middle and end.","learners":"Retell the story using their own words.","tlm":"The same story book as yesterday","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":3},{"activity":"Story: reading with actions and group questions","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":9,"teacher":"Learners practise reading with actions and expressions; one learner per group reads aloud to the class. Guide groups to make questions about the story (guide initially). Groups take turns to ask and answer each other's questions. Word-level learners also read aloud the consonants learned on the first day.","learners":"Read with actions; make questions (word-level learners help write them); ask and answer questions with another group.","tlm":"Story book, slate or paper for questions","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":4},{"activity":"Story: writing answers individually","grouping":"Individual","minutes":5,"teacher":"Para and Story level learners write answers to all questions individually; read and correct their responses after they finish.","learners":"Write the answers in their notebooks; Beginner/Letter/Word learners read or listen and answer orally.","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":5},{"activity":"Consonant clusters: introduction","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":4,"teacher":"Three-letter clusters: after two-letter clusters, familiarise learners with clusters of three letters ('str' as in string, street, straw). Discuss the words, then ask learners to tell and write sentences using them.","learners":"Listen, pronounce the cluster and say words that contain it.","tlm":"Board and chalk, words list (string street straw strong stream)","source":"M","ref":"p.16","n":6},{"activity":"Consonant cluster game: Looking for Similar Ones","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":6,"teacher":"Write some words with the same conjunct consonants on the board, for example bl, tr, st. Observe closely and help learners who need support.","learners":"Match words that have the same conjunct consonant (black, blue, blanket, blow, blink).","tlm":"Words on the board","source":"M","ref":"p.17","n":7},{"activity":"Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on a kind person I know","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Start a conversation about a topic: 'a kind person I know'. Involve all learners and ask open-ended questions.","learners":"Take part in the discussion and share thoughts freely.","tlm":"Picture card or topic on the board","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":8},{"activity":"Self-writing: individual writing","grouping":"Individual","minutes":7,"teacher":"Give each level its task (see level table). Let learners take ownership of what they draw and write; mistakes are fine.","learners":"Draw and write about the topic at their level.","tlm":"Notebooks, crayons or pencils","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":9},{"activity":"Self-writing: review and reading back","grouping":"Individual","minutes":3,"teacher":"Ask each learner 'What did you draw or write?' and have them read it aloud once. Word-level learners read to the group; discuss spelling, punctuation and sentence structure. Help beginners by writing their text in the notebook for them if needed.","learners":"Read what they wrote; correct mistakes after listening to their own reading.","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":10},{"activity":"Daily reading (10 minutes)","grouping":"Individual","minutes":10,"teacher":"Give each learner a library book or any storybook. Move around, listen to individual readers and note their level.","learners":"Read independently a book of their choice.","tlm":"Library books or storybooks","source":"M","ref":"p.7","n":11}],"procedures":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Rain clapping","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","steps":[{"teacher":"Stand the learners in a circle and ask them to close their eyes. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Stand in a circle and close their eyes."},{"teacher":"Start clapping with one finger; then two fingers, three, four and finally five fingers.","learners":"Keep clapping, copying the change of fingers."},{"teacher":"After the activity ask: What sound came after the last clap?","learners":"Tell how they felt and what the sounds reminded them of."}]},{"activity":"Oral conversation: What did you see on your way?","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.9","steps":[{"teacher":"Ask: 'What did you see on your way to school today?'","learners":"Think about the way to school."},{"teacher":"If learners hesitate, start: 'I saw the river shining, a boat leaving the bank and two birds on a bamboo pole. What did you see on your way?'","learners":"Listen to the model and then share their own observations."},{"teacher":"Connect learners' answers with each other.","learners":"Listen and add what they noticed."}]},{"activity":"Story - Day 2 (a story about a tiny creature with a big heart)","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.11","steps":[{"teacher":"Ask learners to retell the story they read yesterday in their own words.","learners":"Retell, helping each other remember."},{"teacher":"In small groups learners practise reading the story using actions and expressions; one learner from each group then reads aloud to the class.","learners":"Read with actions and expression; a representative reads aloud."},{"teacher":"Guide the groups to come up with questions about the story (guide initially). Word-level learners can support by helping write them down.","learners":"Make questions together."},{"teacher":"Groups take turns to ask and answer each other's questions. Useful kinds: questions whose answer is not in the text; questions needing thinking beyond the text; questions asking for an opinion.","learners":"Ask, answer and discuss in the groups."},{"teacher":"Word-level learners also read aloud the consonants they learned on the first day.","learners":"Read the consonant clusters aloud."}]},{"activity":"Consonant clusters (str) and the game 'Looking for Similar Ones'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.16-17","steps":[{"teacher":"Three-letter clusters: after two-letter clusters, familiarise learners with clusters of three letters ('str' as in string, street, straw). Discuss the words, then ask learners to tell and write sentences using them.","learners":"Listen, pronounce and find words in the text."},{"teacher":"Write the words on the board: string street straw strong stream. Read them aloud with distinct pronunciation of the cluster.","learners":"Read the words aloud; point to the cluster in each word."},{"teacher":"Write some words with the same conjunct consonants on the board, for example bl, tr, st.","learners":"Match words that have the same conjunct consonant (black, blue, blanket, blow, blink)."}]},{"activity":"Self-writing: 'Discussion, Writing, Self-review'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.15","steps":[{"teacher":"Start a conversation about a topic: 'a kind person I know'. Involve all learners and ask open-ended questions.","learners":"Discuss and answer questions."},{"teacher":"Give writing time at each level: draw then write (Beginner), write about what they liked (Letter), a sentence (Word), a paragraph or story on a topic of their choice (Para/Story).","learners":"Write at their level and take ownership of the work."},{"teacher":"Review: ask 'What did you draw or write?' Have each learner read the text aloud once. Support with writing if needed.","learners":"Read aloud, listen to their pronunciation and correct mistakes."}]}],"levelTasks":[{"activity":"Story - Day 2: level-wise tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.11","tasks":{"Beginner":"Retell with the group by pointing to pictures or words; read aloud with group support (interpretation of the manual's group reading task).","Letter":"Read with the group, pointing to words; say the letters and words they know (interpretation of the manual's group reading task).","Word":"Support the group in writing the questions; read aloud the consonant clusters learned on the first day.","Para":"Ask the group's questions to another group, discuss them, then write answers to all questions individually; the teacher reads and corrects.","Story":"Ask the group's questions to another group, discuss them, then write answers to all questions individually; the teacher reads and corrects."}},{"activity":"Consonant clusters (str): level tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.16-17","tasks":{"Beginner":"Listen to the sound of the cluster and point to it in a word; continue with letter-sound work (interpretation: the manual describes clusters for learners lagging in reading words and sentences).","Letter":"Listen to the cluster sound and pick words with the cluster from a word card (interpretation).","Word":"Find the cluster in the story or textbook words, read the words and write them in the notebook.","Para":"Form words and sentences using the cluster; read the sentences aloud.","Story":"Form words and sentences using the cluster; read the sentences aloud; use them in the story writing."}},{"activity":"Self-writing: level tasks and review","source":"M","ref":"p.15","tasks":{"Beginner":"Draw a picture about the discussion and then write a few sentences about it, expressing thoughts freely. Review: say what they drew or wrote; read the text aloud once; the teacher may write the text in the notebook for them.","Letter":"Write about what they liked, using drawing and writing; write any words or sentences they can. Review: read the text aloud once; correct punctuation mistakes using the Barakhadi chart.","Word":"Write a sentence based on the conversation. Mistakes in spelling, punctuation and sentence structure are fine. Review: read it to the group; discuss and correct mistakes together.","Para":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation.","Story":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation."}}],"organisation":[{"grouping":"Whole class (big group)","how":"All learners of all levels sit in a 'U' shape arranged by level (Beginner, Letter, Word, Para, Story) so that the move to small groups is easy.","activities":["Warm-up: Rain clapping","Oral conversation: What did you see on your way?","Story (Day 2 of the story): retelling","Consonant clusters: introduction","Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on a kind person I know"]},{"grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","how":"Learners of similar levels work together; the teacher gives each group a task for its level and spends more time with learners who need support. Rotate responsibilities (for example group leader).","activities":["Story: reading with actions and group questions","Consonant cluster game: Looking for Similar Ones"]},{"grouping":"Individual","how":"Each learner works on a task for their own level; the teacher moves around, observes difficulties and supports individuals.","activities":["Story: writing answers individually","Self-writing: individual writing","Self-writing: review and reading back","Daily reading (10 minutes)"]}],"materials":["After the activity ask: What sound came after the last clap?","The same story book as yesterday","Story book","slate or paper for questions","Notebooks","Board","chalk","words list (string street straw strong stream)","Words on the board","Picture card or topic on the board","crayons or pencils","Library books or storybooks"],"outcomes":["Learners take part in the oral conversation and speak without fear.","Learners retell the story, read with expression and ask or answer questions at their level.","Learners respond to the sound-symbol task for today (Consonant clusters: str (string, street)) at their own level.","Learners write about the topic at their level and read it aloud.","Each learner reads a book for 10 minutes."],"observation":["Observe each learner's reading and writing during the individual tasks; note who needs individual support and how many learners share the same difficulty.","Note any learner whose level is improving; move the learner to the next level group when you see steady progress (manual p.5).","Record each learner's progress for the day in the notebook, according to the learner's level (manual p.4).","Use today's observations to adjust tomorrow's plan (manual p.5)."],"teacherNotes":["Questions to elicit on Day 2: information questions (answer not in the text), thinking questions (needs knowledge beyond the text) and opinion questions (feedback on something in the text).","Consonant clusters: do these activities daily for learners who find reading complex words hard; the aim is to remove the fear of reading clusters. Teachers may carry out similar activities on their own.","Writing has two parts, content and sequence: encourage learners to read what they wrote, improve it and rewrite it for clarity and correctness (manual p.15).","Level check: if learners have moved up to a new level, celebrate with an appreciation-oriented game (para level to story level): 'Prepare a Paragraph with the Help of Picture Cards' or 'Read and Speak' (manual p.42-45). Teachers may use such activities on their own.","Pace: the manual says not to assume all learners progress at the same speed. Repeat a day's activity with the groups that need it before moving on.","Special needs: give extra time and prepare materials for slower learners; seat learners with hearing or vision difficulty at the front; for learners who reverse or confuse letters, trace letters on the letter card with a finger and write with dots to trace with a pencil (manual p.6)."],"components":[{"no":1,"key":"warmup","name":"Warm-up activities","keywords":["Rain clapping","two learners lead"],"rows":[1]},{"no":2,"key":"oral","name":"Oral Discussion","keywords":["What did you see on your way?","every learner speaks"],"rows":[2]},{"no":3,"key":"story","name":"Story","keywords":["Day 2","retell","read with actions","group questions","ask and answer","write answers (Para/Story)"],"rows":[3,4,5]},{"no":4,"key":"sound","name":"Sound symbol games, Sound separation-pairing","keywords":["consonant cluster 'str'","pronounce and find words","game: Looking for Similar Ones"],"rows":[6,7]},{"no":5,"key":"mindwrite","name":"Individual-Writing (Day 2)","keywords":["discussion","write at own level","self-review (read aloud)"],"rows":[8,9,10]},{"no":6,"key":"reading","name":"Daily reading","keywords":["library book","read alone","teacher listens"],"rows":[11]}],"preLesson":null},{"programme":"TARL Literacy","id":"lit-056","day":56,"phase":2,"phaseLabel":"Phase 2 (Days 46-90)","title":"Story: a story about a village fair (Day 1)","dayType":"Story Day 1 + Mind mapping","focus":"Language game: Think and Make a List | Mind map: weaving","duration":70,"objectives":["Listen, speak and answer in the oral conversation (familiar topic).","Listen to and read a story with understanding; discuss it in big and small groups and respond at their own level.","Develop sound-symbol skills: Language game: Think and Make a List.","Build vocabulary through a mind map ('weaving') and use the words at their own level.","Read independently for 10 minutes every day."],"sequence":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Writing with body parts","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Learners stand in a circle. Demonstrate writing the word 'star' in the air with a finger, then ask them to write it with different body parts. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Write the word 'star' in the air with the finger, then with the head, shoulders, knees or elbows.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.8","n":1},{"activity":"Oral conversation: familiar topic","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Hold a conversation on the topic 'the season I like best'. Give each learner a chance to speak; be patient with learners who need extra time.","learners":"Talk about the topic and listen to others.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.9","n":2},{"activity":"Story (Day 1 of the story): reading aloud and discussion","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":8,"teacher":"Discuss the title or picture of the story with the learners. Read the story aloud with expression and voice modulation (learners do not repeat after you). Discuss it, with emphasis on judgment questions. Read it again slowly, pointing to each word.","learners":"Talk about the title/picture; listen; answer questions; follow each word with a finger in their own copy.","tlm":"A story from the school library (a story about a village fair), a copy for each learner","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":3},{"activity":"Story: reading in small groups","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":7,"teacher":"Form level-wise groups with a group leader. Learners read the story one sentence at a time while the others follow with their fingers. Para and Story level learners practise reading with emotion and expression.","learners":"Read the story sentence by sentence, supporting each other; the group leader helps.","tlm":"Story book copies","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":4},{"activity":"Story: level-wise individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":5,"teacher":"Give each learner the task for their level (see level table) and support those who need it.","learners":"Beginner/Letter: find and write favourite words or letters. Word: find consonant clusters. Para/Story: silently read, find unfamiliar and rhyming words.","tlm":"Story book, notebooks, board","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":5},{"activity":"Language game: Think and Make a List","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Each group gets a topic and writes a list together; the lists are displayed on the classroom wall. Observe each learner and give help where needed.","learners":"Play the game, take turns and read or say the words they make.","tlm":"Paper or notebooks, chalk","source":"M","ref":"p.20","n":6},{"activity":"Mind mapping (Day 1): the word 'weaving'","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Ask: 'What words come to your mind when you hear the word weaving?' Write learners' answers on the board or floor (Para and Story level learners write the words themselves). Guide the map towards the learning objective. Example words: loom, yarn, shuttle, thread, gamosa, mekhela, scarf, shawl, red, white, blue, green.","learners":"Say words connected with 'weaving'; share the meaning and feeling of words.","tlm":"Board, chalk (or floor)","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":7},{"activity":"Mind mapping: classify the words","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":4,"teacher":"Ask learners to classify the words in groups, for example: Things: loom, yarn, shuttle, thread; Cloth: gamosa, mekhela, scarf, shawl; Colours: red, white, blue, green.","learners":"Sort the words into groups and say why.","tlm":"Board, chalk, word cards (optional)","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":8},{"activity":"Mind mapping: level-wise individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":6,"teacher":"Give each learner the individual task for their level; observe closely and give individual support. Display corrected stories on the wall.","learners":"Complete the task for their level (see level table).","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":9},{"activity":"Daily reading (10 minutes)","grouping":"Individual","minutes":10,"teacher":"Give each learner a library book or any storybook. Move around, listen to individual readers and note their level.","learners":"Read independently a book of their choice.","tlm":"Library books or storybooks","source":"M","ref":"p.7","n":10}],"procedures":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Writing with body parts","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","steps":[{"teacher":"Stand the learners in a circle. Demonstrate writing the word 'star' in the air with your finger.","learners":"Watch and then copy with their own finger."},{"teacher":"Ask them to write it again using knees and other body parts (head, shoulders, knees, ...).","learners":"Write the letters in the air with the named body part."},{"teacher":"Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Take turns to lead."}]},{"activity":"Oral conversation: familiar topic","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.9","steps":[{"teacher":"Introduce the topic: 'the season I like best'.","learners":"Think about their own experience."},{"teacher":"Ask open questions; give every learner a chance. Involve learners who speak less.","learners":"Speak freely and without fear."},{"teacher":"Praise efforts and sum up.","learners":"Listen and respect each other's ideas."}]},{"activity":"Story - Day 1 (a story about a village fair)","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.10","steps":[{"teacher":"Discuss the title or picture of the story with the learners.","learners":"Talk about what they see and what the story may be about."},{"teacher":"Read the story aloud with expression and proper voice modulation. Learners should not simply repeat after you.","learners":"Listen carefully and enjoy the story."},{"teacher":"Discuss the story: factual, logical, vocabulary-based, judgment or opinion questions (today's focus: judgment: Was the character right or wrong? Was that a good thing to do? Why?). Begin in the home language if needed.","learners":"Think and respond thoughtfully; every learner takes part."},{"teacher":"Read the story again slowly, pointing to each word. Make sure each learner has a copy and follows with a finger.","learners":"Follow each word with their finger."},{"teacher":"Ask learners to read in small groups; select a group leader who helps the others. Learners read one sentence at a time while the others point with fingers.","learners":"Read with the help of one another."}]},{"activity":"Language game: Think and Make a List","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.20","steps":[{"teacher":"Divide learners into small groups, each with at least one learner who can write. Give each group a different topic: names of animals, birds, wooden objects, favourite foods, wedding-related items.","learners":"Sit in groups."},{"teacher":"Ask the groups to discuss and say the names aloud, then write the list together.","learners":"Discuss, say and write the list."},{"teacher":"Display the lists on the classroom wall. Make different lists every day.","learners":"Read the displayed lists with pride."}]},{"activity":"Mind mapping: 'weaving'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Small group (level-wise) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.14","steps":[{"teacher":"Choose a word that can generate many related words: 'weaving'. Ask: 'What words come to your mind when you hear the word weaving?' Write the answers on the board or floor.","learners":"Say words they link with 'weaving'."},{"teacher":"Discuss the words: what they mean and how they are connected.","learners":"Explain their words and listen to others."},{"teacher":"In small groups, let the learners classify the words (Things: loom, yarn, shuttle, thread; Cloth: gamosa, mekhela, scarf, shawl; Colours: red, white, blue, green).","learners":"Sort the words into groups."},{"teacher":"Give the individual tasks by level and help each learner.","learners":"Work individually; read the work aloud at the end if time allows."}]}],"levelTasks":[{"activity":"Story - Day 1: individual tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.10","tasks":{"Beginner":"Circle or search for a favourite word or letter in the story and say it aloud. If a learner cannot draw a circle, write words on the board and ask them to identify them.","Letter":"Find, read and write favourite words from the story.","Word":"Find the consonant clusters in the story, read them and write them in the notebook.","Para":"Silently read the story from the textbook; find unfamiliar words and try to understand them; find rhyming words, use them in sentences and write in the notebook; ask other groups for meanings; make questions in groups.","Story":"Silently read the story; find unfamiliar words and rhyming words; practise reading with emotion; one group reads sentences formed with consonant clusters to the other group; ask and answer group questions (information, thinking and opinion questions)."}},{"activity":"Language game: Think and Make a List - level support","source":"I","ref":"p.20","tasks":{"Beginner":"Take part by saying or pointing to the letters involved and by listening carefully; Para and Story level partners help.","Letter":"Say the letters/sounds and give simple words they know.","Word":"Say and write words and short sentences for the game.","Para":"Write sentences with the words; help groups to record answers.","Story":"Write sentences or short stories with the words; help groups to record answers."}},{"activity":"Mind mapping 'weaving': level tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.14","tasks":{"Beginner":"Circle all the words that contain the letter 'E' on the board; make a list. See how many learners find the most words.","Letter":"Circle all the words that contain the letter 'E' and make a list of them.","Word":"Use 4-5 words (for example red, blue, loom, yarn, green) to form sentences, starting with words of one or two syllables. Example: Dream - I had a dream last night.","Para":"Choose any five words from the map and create a story with them. Use consonant clusters correctly, read the story aloud, correct mistakes of sentence structure, spelling or grammar, then display it on the wall.","Story":"Choose any five words from the map and create a story with them. Use consonant clusters correctly, read the story aloud, correct mistakes of sentence structure, spelling or grammar, then display it on the wall."}}],"organisation":[{"grouping":"Whole class (big group)","how":"All learners of all levels sit in a 'U' shape arranged by level (Beginner, Letter, Word, Para, Story) so that the move to small groups is easy.","activities":["Warm-up: Writing with body parts","Oral conversation: familiar topic","Story (Day 1 of the story): reading aloud and discussion","Mind mapping (Day 1): the word 'weaving'"]},{"grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","how":"Learners of similar levels work together; the teacher gives each group a task for its level and spends more time with learners who need support. Rotate responsibilities (for example group leader).","activities":["Story: reading in small groups","Language game: Think and Make a List","Mind mapping: classify the words"]},{"grouping":"Individual","how":"Each learner works on a task for their own level; the teacher moves around, observes difficulties and supports individuals.","activities":["Story: level-wise individual tasks","Mind mapping: level-wise individual tasks","Daily reading (10 minutes)"]}],"materials":["A story from the school library (a story about a village fair)","a copy for each learner","Story book copies","Story book","notebooks","board","Paper or notebooks","chalk","Board","chalk (or floor)","word cards (optional)","Notebooks","Library books or storybooks"],"outcomes":["Learners take part in the oral conversation and speak without fear.","Learners show understanding of the story in the discussion and complete the task for their level.","Learners respond to the sound-symbol task for today (Language game: Think and Make a List) at their own level.","Learners add words to the mind map and use them in sentences or a story at their level.","Each learner reads a book for 10 minutes."],"observation":["Observe each learner's reading and writing during the individual tasks; note who needs individual support and how many learners share the same difficulty.","Note any learner whose level is improving; move the learner to the next level group when you see steady progress (manual p.5).","Record each learner's progress for the day in the notebook, according to the learner's level (manual p.4).","Use today's observations to adjust tomorrow's plan (manual p.5)."],"teacherNotes":["Story selection: the manual asks teachers to use picture story books or stories in the school library. Today's suggested theme (a story about a village fair) is a planning suggestion; use any suitable story you have.","The manual lists the letter and word games but does not fix the slot in the daily timetable where they are used. This plan places them in the 10-minute sound-symbol / alphabet slot (interpretation).","Mind mapping topic for this day: 'weaving'. The manual's example uses the word 'shop'; today's topic follows the same method.","Pace: the manual says not to assume all learners progress at the same speed. Repeat a day's activity with the groups that need it before moving on.","Special needs: give extra time and prepare materials for slower learners; seat learners with hearing or vision difficulty at the front; for learners who reverse or confuse letters, trace letters on the letter card with a finger and write with dots to trace with a pencil (manual p.6)."],"components":[{"no":1,"key":"warmup","name":"Warm-up activities","keywords":["Writing with body parts","two learners lead"],"rows":[1]},{"no":2,"key":"oral","name":"Oral Discussion","keywords":["familiar topic","every learner speaks"],"rows":[2]},{"no":3,"key":"story","name":"Story","keywords":["Day 1","title / picture talk","read aloud with expression","judgment questions","re-read pointing","group reading","level tasks"],"rows":[3,4,5]},{"no":4,"key":"sound","name":"Sound symbol games, Sound separation-pairing","keywords":["Think and Make a List","play in turns","level support"],"rows":[6]},{"no":5,"key":"mindwrite","name":"Mind Mapping (Day 1)","keywords":["mind map: weaving","classify the words","level task: circle letter E / sentences / story"],"rows":[7,8,9]},{"no":6,"key":"reading","name":"Daily reading","keywords":["library book","read alone","teacher listens"],"rows":[10]}],"preLesson":null},{"programme":"TARL Literacy","id":"lit-057","day":57,"phase":2,"phaseLabel":"Phase 2 (Days 46-90)","title":"Story: a story about a village fair (Day 2)","dayType":"Story Day 2 + Self-writing","focus":"Blending sounds to form words (map, jam, fox) | Self-writing: my favourite book or story","duration":70,"objectives":["Listen, speak and answer in the oral conversation (conversation on a picture).","Retell the story, read it with expression, ask and answer questions about it and write answers.","Develop sound-symbol skills: Blending sounds to form words (map, jam, fox).","Write about a topic at their own level and review the writing (my favourite book or story).","Read independently for 10 minutes every day."],"sequence":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Alphabet song (last-letter word chain)","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Say a word to the big group, for example 'earth'. Learners say a word that starts with the last letter ('h'). A learner who cannot say a word is out. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Say a word that starts with the last letter of the previous word; step out if unable to.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.8","n":1},{"activity":"Oral conversation: conversation on a picture","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Show a picture of a road with buses, bicycles and cattle and ask what is happening, who is doing what and what is happening around them. Let learners think creatively and even make up a story.","learners":"Look at the picture, answer questions and make up their own story about it.","tlm":"Picture card of a road with buses, bicycles and cattle","source":"M","ref":"p.9","n":2},{"activity":"Story (Day 2 of the story): retelling","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":6,"teacher":"Ask learners to retell yesterday's story in their own words. Prompt with questions on the beginning, middle and end.","learners":"Retell the story using their own words.","tlm":"The same story book as yesterday","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":3},{"activity":"Story: reading with actions and group questions","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":9,"teacher":"Learners practise reading with actions and expressions; one learner per group reads aloud to the class. Guide groups to make questions about the story (guide initially). Groups take turns to ask and answer each other's questions. Word-level learners also read aloud the consonants learned on the first day.","learners":"Read with actions; make questions (word-level learners help write them); ask and answer questions with another group.","tlm":"Story book, slate or paper for questions","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":4},{"activity":"Story: writing answers individually","grouping":"Individual","minutes":5,"teacher":"Para and Story level learners write answers to all questions individually; read and correct their responses after they finish.","learners":"Write the answers in their notebooks; Beginner/Letter/Word learners read or listen and answer orally.","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":5},{"activity":"Sound-symbol activity: oral sound awareness","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":4,"teacher":"Say separate sounds from 10-12 words (map: m - a - p; jam: j - a - m; fox: f - o - x; bed: b - e - d) and ask learners to blend the sounds into the complete word.","learners":"Listen to the separate sounds and blend them to say the whole word.","tlm":"None (oral activity)","source":"M","ref":"p.12","n":6},{"activity":"Sound-symbol games by level","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":6,"teacher":"Give each level group its game (see level table). Move among the groups and help those who need support; say each word clearly.","learners":"Play the game for their level in small groups.","tlm":"Board, chalk, letter cards","source":"M","ref":"p.12","n":7},{"activity":"Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on my favourite book or story","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Start a conversation about a situation: 'my favourite book or story'. Involve all learners and ask open-ended questions.","learners":"Take part in the discussion and share thoughts freely.","tlm":"Picture card or topic on the board","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":8},{"activity":"Self-writing: individual writing","grouping":"Individual","minutes":7,"teacher":"Give each level its task (see level table). Let learners take ownership of what they draw and write; mistakes are fine.","learners":"Draw and write about the topic at their level.","tlm":"Notebooks, crayons or pencils","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":9},{"activity":"Self-writing: review and reading back","grouping":"Individual","minutes":3,"teacher":"Ask each learner 'What did you draw or write?' and have them read it aloud once. Word-level learners read to the group; discuss spelling, punctuation and sentence structure. Help beginners by writing their text in the notebook for them if needed.","learners":"Read what they wrote; correct mistakes after listening to their own reading.","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":10},{"activity":"Daily reading (10 minutes)","grouping":"Individual","minutes":10,"teacher":"Give each learner a library book or any storybook. Move around, listen to individual readers and note their level.","learners":"Read independently a book of their choice.","tlm":"Library books or storybooks","source":"M","ref":"p.7","n":11}],"procedures":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Alphabet song (last-letter word chain)","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","steps":[{"teacher":"Say the word 'earth' to the big group and show that its last letter is 'h'.","learners":"Listen and think of a word starting with 'h'."},{"teacher":"Ask learners in turn to say a word that starts with the last letter of the previous word. Example: rain -> nest.","learners":"Say a word in turn; anyone who cannot say a word is out of the game."},{"teacher":"Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Lead the game when it is their turn."}]},{"activity":"Oral conversation: conversation on a picture","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.9","steps":[{"teacher":"Show the picture of a road with buses, bicycles and cattle.","learners":"Look carefully."},{"teacher":"Ask: What is happening in the picture? Who is doing what? What is happening around them? Then: What might happen next?","learners":"Answer in their own words; every learner gets a chance."},{"teacher":"Let learners imagine and make up a short story from the picture.","learners":"Tell their stories to the class."}]},{"activity":"Story - Day 2 (a story about a village fair)","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.11","steps":[{"teacher":"Ask learners to retell the story they read yesterday in their own words.","learners":"Retell, helping each other remember."},{"teacher":"In small groups learners practise reading the story using actions and expressions; one learner from each group then reads aloud to the class.","learners":"Read with actions and expression; a representative reads aloud."},{"teacher":"Guide the groups to come up with questions about the story (guide initially). Word-level learners can support by helping write them down.","learners":"Make questions together."},{"teacher":"Groups take turns to ask and answer each other's questions. Useful kinds: questions whose answer is not in the text; questions needing thinking beyond the text; questions asking for an opinion.","learners":"Ask, answer and discuss in the groups."},{"teacher":"Word-level learners also read aloud the consonants they learned on the first day.","learners":"Read the consonant clusters aloud."}]},{"activity":"Sound-symbol: oral and level games","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.12","steps":[{"teacher":"Say separate sounds from 10-12 words (map: m - a - p; jam: j - a - m; fox: f - o - x; bed: b - e - d) and ask learners to blend the sounds into the complete word.","learners":"Listen to the separate sounds and blend them to say the whole word."},{"teacher":"Write the sounds or words for the day on the board and give each level group its task (see the level table).","learners":"Work in small groups and share their answers."},{"teacher":"Say each word clearly with distinct pronunciation. Give learners enough time to respond and think; use words learners commonly use at home (regional language and the medium of instruction).","learners":"Think, say and write the sounds."}]},{"activity":"Self-writing: 'Discussion, Writing, Self-review'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.15","steps":[{"teacher":"Start a conversation about a situation: 'my favourite book or story'. Involve all learners and ask open-ended questions.","learners":"Discuss and answer questions."},{"teacher":"Give writing time at each level: draw then write (Beginner), write about what they liked (Letter), a sentence (Word), a paragraph or story on a topic of their choice (Para/Story).","learners":"Write at their level and take ownership of the work."},{"teacher":"Review: ask 'What did you draw or write?' Have each learner read the text aloud once. Support with writing if needed.","learners":"Read aloud, listen to their pronunciation and correct mistakes."}]}],"levelTasks":[{"activity":"Story - Day 2: level-wise tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.11","tasks":{"Beginner":"Retell with the group by pointing to pictures or words; read aloud with group support (interpretation of the manual's group reading task).","Letter":"Read with the group, pointing to words; say the letters and words they know (interpretation of the manual's group reading task).","Word":"Support the group in writing the questions; read aloud the consonant clusters learned on the first day.","Para":"Ask the group's questions to another group, discuss them, then write answers to all questions individually; the teacher reads and corrects.","Story":"Ask the group's questions to another group, discuss them, then write answers to all questions individually; the teacher reads and corrects."}},{"activity":"Sound-symbol games by level (small groups)","source":"M","ref":"p.12","tasks":{"Beginner":"'What is the first sound in the word pen?' 'Is there a letter that makes the sound /p/?' 'Can you name objects that start with the letter P?' Learners think and share names in the group.","Letter":"Write the rhyming ending -og on the board and ask learners to add new letters to form words: d + og = dog, l + og = log, f + og = fog.","Word":"Say a word and tell its sounds, for example 'sun' = /s/ + /u/ + /n/. Then tell what word is formed if /r/ is put before 'at': r + at = rat. Do 8-10 such combinations; at first learners may form meaningless words, later only meaningful words.","Para":"Write two or three sounds on the board (for example Br, cl, st) and let the learners form words that start with those sounds; this builds a word list for the learner.","Story":"Write two or three sounds on the board (for example Br, cl, st) and let the learners form words that start with those sounds; this builds a word list for the learner."}},{"activity":"Self-writing: level tasks and review","source":"M","ref":"p.15","tasks":{"Beginner":"Draw a picture about the discussion and then write a few sentences about it, expressing thoughts freely. Review: say what they drew or wrote; read the text aloud once; the teacher may write the text in the notebook for them.","Letter":"Write about what they liked, using drawing and writing; write any words or sentences they can. Review: read the text aloud once; correct punctuation mistakes using the Barakhadi chart.","Word":"Write a sentence based on the conversation. Mistakes in spelling, punctuation and sentence structure are fine. Review: read it to the group; discuss and correct mistakes together.","Para":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation.","Story":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation."}}],"organisation":[{"grouping":"Whole class (big group)","how":"All learners of all levels sit in a 'U' shape arranged by level (Beginner, Letter, Word, Para, Story) so that the move to small groups is easy.","activities":["Warm-up: Alphabet song (last-letter word chain)","Oral conversation: conversation on a picture","Story (Day 2 of the story): retelling","Sound-symbol activity: oral sound awareness","Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on my favourite book or story"]},{"grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","how":"Learners of similar levels work together; the teacher gives each group a task for its level and spends more time with learners who need support. Rotate responsibilities (for example group leader).","activities":["Story: reading with actions and group questions","Sound-symbol games by level"]},{"grouping":"Individual","how":"Each learner works on a task for their own level; the teacher moves around, observes difficulties and supports individuals.","activities":["Story: writing answers individually","Self-writing: individual writing","Self-writing: review and reading back","Daily reading (10 minutes)"]}],"materials":["Picture card of a road with buses","bicycles","cattle","The same story book as yesterday","Story book","slate or paper for questions","Notebooks","Board","chalk","letter cards","Picture card or topic on the board","crayons or pencils","Library books or storybooks"],"outcomes":["Learners take part in the oral conversation and speak without fear.","Learners retell the story, read with expression and ask or answer questions at their level.","Learners respond to the sound-symbol task for today (Blending sounds to form words (map, jam, fox)) at their own level.","Learners write about the topic at their level and read it aloud.","Each learner reads a book for 10 minutes."],"observation":["Observe each learner's reading and writing during the individual tasks; note who needs individual support and how many learners share the same difficulty.","Note any learner whose level is improving; move the learner to the next level group when you see steady progress (manual p.5).","Record each learner's progress for the day in the notebook, according to the learner's level (manual p.4).","Use today's observations to adjust tomorrow's plan (manual p.5)."],"teacherNotes":["Questions to elicit on Day 2: information questions (answer not in the text), thinking questions (needs knowledge beyond the text) and opinion questions (feedback on something in the text).","Sound-symbol: for the first 4-5 days, play sound-based games with the learners at word level. Include the sounds learners find difficult when you prepare the Class Transaction Plan.","Writing has two parts, content and sequence: encourage learners to read what they wrote, improve it and rewrite it for clarity and correctness (manual p.15).","Pace: the manual says not to assume all learners progress at the same speed. Repeat a day's activity with the groups that need it before moving on.","Special needs: give extra time and prepare materials for slower learners; seat learners with hearing or vision difficulty at the front; for learners who reverse or confuse letters, trace letters on the letter card with a finger and write with dots to trace with a pencil (manual p.6)."],"components":[{"no":1,"key":"warmup","name":"Warm-up activities","keywords":["Alphabet song (last-letter word chain)","two learners lead"],"rows":[1]},{"no":2,"key":"oral","name":"Oral Discussion","keywords":["conversation on a picture","every learner speaks"],"rows":[2]},{"no":3,"key":"story","name":"Story","keywords":["Day 2","retell","read with actions","group questions","ask and answer","write answers (Para/Story)"],"rows":[3,4,5]},{"no":4,"key":"sound","name":"Sound symbol games, Sound separation-pairing","keywords":["oral sound awareness","blend sounds to a word","level games in small groups"],"rows":[6,7]},{"no":5,"key":"mindwrite","name":"Individual-Writing (Day 2)","keywords":["discussion","write at own level","self-review (read aloud)"],"rows":[8,9,10]},{"no":6,"key":"reading","name":"Daily reading","keywords":["library book","read alone","teacher listens"],"rows":[11]}],"preLesson":null},{"programme":"TARL Literacy","id":"lit-058","day":58,"phase":2,"phaseLabel":"Phase 2 (Days 46-90)","title":"Story: a story about growing a plant (Day 1)","dayType":"Story Day 1 + Mind mapping","focus":"Consonant clusters: spl (split, splash) | Mind map: house","duration":70,"objectives":["Listen, speak and answer in the oral conversation (listening and storytelling).","Listen to and read a story with understanding; discuss it in big and small groups and respond at their own level.","Develop sound-symbol skills: Consonant clusters: spl (split, splash).","Build vocabulary through a mind map ('house') and use the words at their own level.","Read independently for 10 minutes every day."],"sequence":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Handkerchief game","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Learners sit in a circle and clap while singing a rhyme ('I caught a Fish Alive'). One learner runs outside the circle with a handkerchief and secretly places it behind another learner, who must chase the runner. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Sit in a circle, clap and sing; run, place the handkerchief or chase as the game requires.","tlm":"A handkerchief","source":"M","ref":"p.8","n":1},{"activity":"Oral conversation: listening and storytelling","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Tell an interesting story starter and involve the learners: 'The river said 'good morning' to me today. What did I answer?' Let learners imagine and continue the story.","learners":"Listen to the teacher, then imagine and continue the story. Learners can also recite a rhyme or story they know.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.9","n":2},{"activity":"Story (Day 1 of the story): reading aloud and discussion","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":8,"teacher":"Discuss the title or picture of the story with the learners. Read the story aloud with expression and voice modulation (learners do not repeat after you). Discuss it, with emphasis on opinion questions. Read it again slowly, pointing to each word.","learners":"Talk about the title/picture; listen; answer questions; follow each word with a finger in their own copy.","tlm":"A story from the school library (a story about growing a plant), a copy for each learner","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":3},{"activity":"Story: reading in small groups","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":7,"teacher":"Form level-wise groups with a group leader. Learners read the story one sentence at a time while the others follow with their fingers. Para and Story level learners practise reading with emotion and expression.","learners":"Read the story sentence by sentence, supporting each other; the group leader helps.","tlm":"Story book copies","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":4},{"activity":"Story: level-wise individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":5,"teacher":"Give each learner the task for their level (see level table) and support those who need it.","learners":"Beginner/Letter: find and write favourite words or letters. Word: find consonant clusters. Para/Story: silently read, find unfamiliar and rhyming words.","tlm":"Story book, notebooks, board","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":5},{"activity":"Consonant clusters: introduction","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":4,"teacher":"Three-letter clusters: after two-letter clusters, familiarise learners with clusters of three letters ('spl' as in split, splash, splendid). Discuss the words, then ask learners to tell and write sentences using them.","learners":"Listen, pronounce the cluster and say words that contain it.","tlm":"Board and chalk, words list (split splash splendid splinter splatter)","source":"M","ref":"p.16","n":6},{"activity":"Consonant cluster game: Who is Whose Friend?","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":6,"teacher":"Prepare cards: some with broken parts of conjunct consonants (b + l, c + r, s + t) and some with the full form (bl as in black, cr as in crab, st as in star). Take out all the cards. Observe closely and help learners who need support.","learners":"Match each full form with its broken parts and discover 'who is whose friend'.","tlm":"Broken-part cards and full-form cards","source":"M","ref":"p.17","n":7},{"activity":"Mind mapping (Day 1): the word 'house'","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Ask: 'What words come to your mind when you hear the word house?' Write learners' answers on the board or floor (Para and Story level learners write the words themselves). Guide the map towards the learning objective. Example words: kitchen, bedroom, bathroom, verandah, bed, table, chair, lamp, roof, wall, window, door.","learners":"Say words connected with 'house'; share the meaning and feeling of words.","tlm":"Board, chalk (or floor)","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":8},{"activity":"Mind mapping: classify the words","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":4,"teacher":"Ask learners to classify the words in groups, for example: Rooms: kitchen, bedroom, bathroom, verandah; Things: bed, table, chair, lamp; Parts: roof, wall, window, door.","learners":"Sort the words into groups and say why.","tlm":"Board, chalk, word cards (optional)","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":9},{"activity":"Mind mapping: level-wise individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":6,"teacher":"Give each learner the individual task for their level; observe closely and give individual support. Display corrected stories on the wall.","learners":"Complete the task for their level (see level table).","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":10},{"activity":"Daily reading (10 minutes)","grouping":"Individual","minutes":10,"teacher":"Give each learner a library book or any storybook. Move around, listen to individual readers and note their level.","learners":"Read independently a book of their choice.","tlm":"Library books or storybooks","source":"M","ref":"p.7","n":11}],"procedures":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Handkerchief game","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","steps":[{"teacher":"Seat the learners in a circle and start clapping and singing the rhyme 'I caught a Fish Alive'.","learners":"Clap and sing together."},{"teacher":"One learner runs outside the circle holding a handkerchief and secretly places it behind another learner.","learners":"Everyone keeps clapping; the learner who finds the handkerchief behind them takes it and chases the runner."},{"teacher":"If the runner sits in the chaser's place before being caught, they stay in the game; if caught, they are out. Continue in this way.","learners":"Play fairly and take turns."}]},{"activity":"Oral conversation: listening and storytelling","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.9","steps":[{"teacher":"Say the starter: 'The river said 'good morning' to me today. What did I answer?'","learners":"Listen and imagine."},{"teacher":"Ask learners to continue the story one by one. Encourage those who speak less.","learners":"Add ideas to the story."},{"teacher":"Invite a learner to recite a poem or rhyme they know.","learners":"Recite and listen to others."}]},{"activity":"Story - Day 1 (a story about growing a plant)","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.10","steps":[{"teacher":"Discuss the title or picture of the story with the learners.","learners":"Talk about what they see and what the story may be about."},{"teacher":"Read the story aloud with expression and proper voice modulation. Learners should not simply repeat after you.","learners":"Listen carefully and enjoy the story."},{"teacher":"Discuss the story: factual, logical, vocabulary-based, judgment or opinion questions (today's focus: opinion: What did you like best? What would you have done in the story?). Begin in the home language if needed.","learners":"Think and respond thoughtfully; every learner takes part."},{"teacher":"Read the story again slowly, pointing to each word. Make sure each learner has a copy and follows with a finger.","learners":"Follow each word with their finger."},{"teacher":"Ask learners to read in small groups; select a group leader who helps the others. Learners read one sentence at a time while the others point with fingers.","learners":"Read with the help of one another."}]},{"activity":"Consonant clusters (spl) and the game 'Who is Whose Friend?'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.16-17","steps":[{"teacher":"Three-letter clusters: after two-letter clusters, familiarise learners with clusters of three letters ('spl' as in split, splash, splendid). Discuss the words, then ask learners to tell and write sentences using them.","learners":"Listen, pronounce and find words in the text."},{"teacher":"Write the words on the board: split splash splendid splinter splatter. Read them aloud with distinct pronunciation of the cluster.","learners":"Read the words aloud; point to the cluster in each word."},{"teacher":"Prepare cards: some with broken parts of conjunct consonants (b + l, c + r, s + t) and some with the full form (bl as in black, cr as in crab, st as in star). Take out all the cards.","learners":"Match each full form with its broken parts and discover 'who is whose friend'."}]},{"activity":"Mind mapping: 'house'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Small group (level-wise) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.14","steps":[{"teacher":"Choose a word that can generate many related words: 'house'. Ask: 'What words come to your mind when you hear the word house?' Write the answers on the board or floor.","learners":"Say words they link with 'house'."},{"teacher":"Discuss the words: what they mean and how they are connected.","learners":"Explain their words and listen to others."},{"teacher":"In small groups, let the learners classify the words (Rooms: kitchen, bedroom, bathroom, verandah; Things: bed, table, chair, lamp; Parts: roof, wall, window, door).","learners":"Sort the words into groups."},{"teacher":"Give the individual tasks by level and help each learner.","learners":"Work individually; read the work aloud at the end if time allows."}]}],"levelTasks":[{"activity":"Story - Day 1: individual tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.10","tasks":{"Beginner":"Circle or search for a favourite word or letter in the story and say it aloud. If a learner cannot draw a circle, write words on the board and ask them to identify them.","Letter":"Find, read and write favourite words from the story.","Word":"Find the consonant clusters in the story, read them and write them in the notebook.","Para":"Silently read the story from the textbook; find unfamiliar words and try to understand them; find rhyming words, use them in sentences and write in the notebook; ask other groups for meanings; make questions in groups.","Story":"Silently read the story; find unfamiliar words and rhyming words; practise reading with emotion; one group reads sentences formed with consonant clusters to the other group; ask and answer group questions (information, thinking and opinion questions)."}},{"activity":"Consonant clusters (spl): level tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.16-17","tasks":{"Beginner":"Listen to the sound of the cluster and point to it in a word; continue with letter-sound work (interpretation: the manual describes clusters for learners lagging in reading words and sentences).","Letter":"Listen to the cluster sound and pick words with the cluster from a word card (interpretation).","Word":"Find the cluster in the story or textbook words, read the words and write them in the notebook.","Para":"Form words and sentences using the cluster; read the sentences aloud.","Story":"Form words and sentences using the cluster; read the sentences aloud; use them in the story writing."}},{"activity":"Mind mapping 'house': level tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.14","tasks":{"Beginner":"Circle all the words that contain the letter 'A' on the board; make a list. See how many learners find the most words.","Letter":"Circle all the words that contain the letter 'A' and make a list of them.","Word":"Use 4-5 words (for example bed, door, lamp, roof, wall) to form sentences, starting with words of one or two syllables. Example: Dream - I had a dream last night.","Para":"Choose any five words from the map and create a story with them. Use consonant clusters correctly, read the story aloud, correct mistakes of sentence structure, spelling or grammar, then display it on the wall.","Story":"Choose any five words from the map and create a story with them. Use consonant clusters correctly, read the story aloud, correct mistakes of sentence structure, spelling or grammar, then display it on the wall."}}],"organisation":[{"grouping":"Whole class (big group)","how":"All learners of all levels sit in a 'U' shape arranged by level (Beginner, Letter, Word, Para, Story) so that the move to small groups is easy.","activities":["Warm-up: Handkerchief game","Oral conversation: listening and storytelling","Story (Day 1 of the story): reading aloud and discussion","Consonant clusters: introduction","Mind mapping (Day 1): the word 'house'"]},{"grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","how":"Learners of similar levels work together; the teacher gives each group a task for its level and spends more time with learners who need support. Rotate responsibilities (for example group leader).","activities":["Story: reading in small groups","Consonant cluster game: Who is Whose Friend?","Mind mapping: classify the words"]},{"grouping":"Individual","how":"Each learner works on a task for their own level; the teacher moves around, observes difficulties and supports individuals.","activities":["Story: level-wise individual tasks","Mind mapping: level-wise individual tasks","Daily reading (10 minutes)"]}],"materials":["A handkerchief","A story from the school library (a story about growing a plant)","a copy for each learner","Story book copies","Story book","notebooks","board","Board","chalk","words list (split splash splendid splinter splatter)","Broken-part cards","full-form cards","chalk (or floor)","word cards (optional)","Notebooks","Library books or storybooks"],"outcomes":["Learners take part in the oral conversation and speak without fear.","Learners show understanding of the story in the discussion and complete the task for their level.","Learners respond to the sound-symbol task for today (Consonant clusters: spl (split, splash)) at their own level.","Learners add words to the mind map and use them in sentences or a story at their level.","Each learner reads a book for 10 minutes."],"observation":["Observe each learner's reading and writing during the individual tasks; note who needs individual support and how many learners share the same difficulty.","Note any learner whose level is improving; move the learner to the next level group when you see steady progress (manual p.5).","Record each learner's progress for the day in the notebook, according to the learner's level (manual p.4).","Use today's observations to adjust tomorrow's plan (manual p.5)."],"teacherNotes":["Story selection: the manual asks teachers to use picture story books or stories in the school library. Today's suggested theme (a story about growing a plant) is a planning suggestion; use any suitable story you have.","Consonant clusters: do these activities daily for learners who find reading complex words hard; the aim is to remove the fear of reading clusters. Teachers may carry out similar activities on their own.","Mind mapping topic for this day: 'house'. The manual's example uses the word 'shop'; today's topic follows the same method.","Pace: the manual says not to assume all learners progress at the same speed. Repeat a day's activity with the groups that need it before moving on.","Special needs: give extra time and prepare materials for slower learners; seat learners with hearing or vision difficulty at the front; for learners who reverse or confuse letters, trace letters on the letter card with a finger and write with dots to trace with a pencil (manual p.6)."],"components":[{"no":1,"key":"warmup","name":"Warm-up activities","keywords":["Handkerchief game","two learners lead"],"rows":[1]},{"no":2,"key":"oral","name":"Oral Discussion","keywords":["listening and storytelling","every learner speaks"],"rows":[2]},{"no":3,"key":"story","name":"Story","keywords":["Day 1","title / picture talk","read aloud with expression","opinion questions","re-read pointing","group reading","level tasks"],"rows":[3,4,5]},{"no":4,"key":"sound","name":"Sound symbol games, Sound separation-pairing","keywords":["consonant cluster 'spl'","pronounce and find words","game: Who is Whose Friend?"],"rows":[6,7]},{"no":5,"key":"mindwrite","name":"Mind Mapping (Day 1)","keywords":["mind map: house","classify the words","level task: circle letter A / sentences / story"],"rows":[8,9,10]},{"no":6,"key":"reading","name":"Daily reading","keywords":["library book","read alone","teacher listens"],"rows":[11]}],"preLesson":null},{"programme":"TARL Literacy","id":"lit-059","day":59,"phase":2,"phaseLabel":"Phase 2 (Days 46-90)","title":"Story: a story about growing a plant (Day 2)","dayType":"Story Day 2 + Self-writing","focus":"Barakhadi / alphabet and phonics chart (line 6, letter 'c') | Self-writing: a day in winter","duration":70,"objectives":["Listen, speak and answer in the oral conversation (What did you see on your way?).","Retell the story, read it with expression, ask and answer questions about it and write answers.","Develop sound-symbol skills: Barakhadi / alphabet and phonics chart (line 6, letter 'c').","Write about a topic at their own level and review the writing (a day in winter).","Read independently for 10 minutes every day."],"sequence":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Rhyme - 'I saw a Little Bird'","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Say the rhyme with actions, then say it together. Lines: I saw a little bird go hop, hop, hop / I told the little bird to stop, stop, stop. / I went to the window to say 'How do you do?' / He wagged his little tail and far away he flew! Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Listen, then say the rhyme with actions.","tlm":"Rhyme chart or board (optional)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","n":1},{"activity":"Oral conversation: What did you see on your way?","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Ask learners to describe what they saw on their way to school. If they are hesitant, begin yourself: 'Today I saw a rainbow over the school, wet leaves on the path and a frog near the drain. What did you see?'","learners":"Describe what they saw on the way to school and connect with what others share.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.9","n":2},{"activity":"Story (Day 2 of the story): retelling","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":6,"teacher":"Ask learners to retell yesterday's story in their own words. Prompt with questions on the beginning, middle and end.","learners":"Retell the story using their own words.","tlm":"The same story book as yesterday","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":3},{"activity":"Story: reading with actions and group questions","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":9,"teacher":"Learners practise reading with actions and expressions; one learner per group reads aloud to the class. Guide groups to make questions about the story (guide initially). Groups take turns to ask and answer each other's questions. Word-level learners also read aloud the consonants learned on the first day.","learners":"Read with actions; make questions (word-level learners help write them); ask and answer questions with another group.","tlm":"Story book, slate or paper for questions","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":4},{"activity":"Story: writing answers individually","grouping":"Individual","minutes":5,"teacher":"Para and Story level learners write answers to all questions individually; read and correct their responses after they finish.","learners":"Write the answers in their notebooks; Beginner/Letter/Word learners read or listen and answer orally.","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":5},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart: big group reading","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":3,"teacher":"Show the Barakhadi chart and ask which letter they like. Read the letter 'c' on the chart; learners listen carefully and point to it on their own chart (they do not repeat after you).","learners":"Listen and point to the letter on their own chart.","tlm":"Barakhadi chart, alphabet or phonics chart","source":"M","ref":"p.13","n":6},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart: small-group practice","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Learners practise reading the alphabet or phonics chart in groups and help each other. One learner per group reads aloud. Occasionally ask learners to identify the sounds of letters. Give each level its group task.","learners":"Read the chart in groups; one learner reads aloud; do the level task.","tlm":"Alphabet or phonics chart, board or floor","source":"M","ref":"p.13","n":7},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart: individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":2,"teacher":"Give each learner an individual task for their level and observe closely; assist any learner who needs individual support.","learners":"Say and write a letter or word, a sentence or a short paragraph (by level).","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.13","n":8},{"activity":"Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on a day in winter","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Start a conversation about a picture card: 'a day in winter'. Involve all learners and ask open-ended questions.","learners":"Take part in the discussion and share thoughts freely.","tlm":"Picture card or topic on the board","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":9},{"activity":"Self-writing: individual writing","grouping":"Individual","minutes":7,"teacher":"Give each level its task (see level table). Let learners take ownership of what they draw and write; mistakes are fine.","learners":"Draw and write about the topic at their level.","tlm":"Notebooks, crayons or pencils","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":10},{"activity":"Self-writing: review and reading back","grouping":"Individual","minutes":3,"teacher":"Ask each learner 'What did you draw or write?' and have them read it aloud once. Word-level learners read to the group; discuss spelling, punctuation and sentence structure. Help beginners by writing their text in the notebook for them if needed.","learners":"Read what they wrote; correct mistakes after listening to their own reading.","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":11},{"activity":"Daily reading (10 minutes)","grouping":"Individual","minutes":10,"teacher":"Give each learner a library book or any storybook. Move around, listen to individual readers and note their level.","learners":"Read independently a book of their choice.","tlm":"Library books or storybooks","source":"M","ref":"p.7","n":12}],"procedures":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Rhyme - 'I saw a Little Bird'","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","steps":[{"teacher":"Say the rhyme 'I saw a Little Bird' slowly with actions: I saw a little bird go hop, hop, hop / I told the little bird to stop, stop, stop. / I went to the window to say 'How do you do?' / He wagged his little tail and far away he flew!","learners":"Listen and watch the actions."},{"teacher":"Say it again; invite learners to join with actions.","learners":"Say the rhyme together with actions."},{"teacher":"Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Choose a rhyme they like and lead."}]},{"activity":"Oral conversation: What did you see on your way?","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.9","steps":[{"teacher":"Ask: 'What did you see on your way to school today?'","learners":"Think about the way to school."},{"teacher":"If learners hesitate, start: 'Today I saw a rainbow over the school, wet leaves on the path and a frog near the drain. What did you see?'","learners":"Listen to the model and then share their own observations."},{"teacher":"Connect learners' answers with each other.","learners":"Listen and add what they noticed."}]},{"activity":"Story - Day 2 (a story about growing a plant)","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.11","steps":[{"teacher":"Ask learners to retell the story they read yesterday in their own words.","learners":"Retell, helping each other remember."},{"teacher":"In small groups learners practise reading the story using actions and expressions; one learner from each group then reads aloud to the class.","learners":"Read with actions and expression; a representative reads aloud."},{"teacher":"Guide the groups to come up with questions about the story (guide initially). Word-level learners can support by helping write them down.","learners":"Make questions together."},{"teacher":"Groups take turns to ask and answer each other's questions. Useful kinds: questions whose answer is not in the text; questions needing thinking beyond the text; questions asking for an opinion.","learners":"Ask, answer and discuss in the groups."},{"teacher":"Word-level learners also read aloud the consonants they learned on the first day.","learners":"Read the consonant clusters aloud."}]},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart activity (line 6)","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Small group (level-wise) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.13","steps":[{"teacher":"Show the Barakhadi chart and ask the learners which letter they like. Where is the letter 'c'?","learners":"Look for the letter on the chart."},{"teacher":"Read the letter 'c' on the chart. Learners listen and point to it on their own chart. Make sure they do not repeat after you.","learners":"Listen and point to the letter."},{"teacher":"Learners read the alphabet or phonics chart in their groups and help each other; one learner from each group comes forward to read aloud.","learners":"Read in groups; the representative reads aloud."},{"teacher":"Occasionally ask them to identify the sounds of letters from the chart.","learners":"Say the sound of the letter you point to."},{"teacher":"As an extra activity, write some letters on the floor, call out each letter one by one and let the learners jump onto the correct letter.","learners":"Jump onto the letter that is called."}]},{"activity":"Self-writing: 'Discussion, Writing, Self-review'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.15","steps":[{"teacher":"Start a conversation about a picture card: 'a day in winter'. Involve all learners and ask open-ended questions.","learners":"Discuss and answer questions."},{"teacher":"Give writing time at each level: draw then write (Beginner), write about what they liked (Letter), a sentence (Word), a paragraph or story on a topic of their choice (Para/Story).","learners":"Write at their level and take ownership of the work."},{"teacher":"Review: ask 'What did you draw or write?' Have each learner read the text aloud once. Support with writing if needed.","learners":"Read aloud, listen to their pronunciation and correct mistakes."}]}],"levelTasks":[{"activity":"Story - Day 2: level-wise tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.11","tasks":{"Beginner":"Retell with the group by pointing to pictures or words; read aloud with group support (interpretation of the manual's group reading task).","Letter":"Read with the group, pointing to words; say the letters and words they know (interpretation of the manual's group reading task).","Word":"Support the group in writing the questions; read aloud the consonant clusters learned on the first day.","Para":"Ask the group's questions to another group, discuss them, then write answers to all questions individually; the teacher reads and corrects.","Story":"Ask the group's questions to another group, discuss them, then write answers to all questions individually; the teacher reads and corrects."}},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart: level tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.13","tasks":{"Beginner":"Small group: read the chart in the group; find and write favourite letters from the line. Individual: say and write a letter of their choice.","Letter":"Small group: read the chart; find and write favourite letters or words from any line. Individual: say a word on their own that begins with any letter.","Word":"Small group: write one or two lines of letters on the board or floor and use them to form words. Individual: speak and write sentences using words they know.","Para":"Small group: prepare word lists using the Barakhadi chart (for example items found in a shop or in the kitchen). Individual: write short paragraphs using the words formed with the Barakhadi chart.","Story":"Small group: prepare word lists using the Barakhadi chart. Individual: write short paragraphs using the words formed with the Barakhadi chart."}},{"activity":"Self-writing: level tasks and review","source":"M","ref":"p.15","tasks":{"Beginner":"Draw a picture about the discussion and then write a few sentences about it, expressing thoughts freely. Review: say what they drew or wrote; read the text aloud once; the teacher may write the text in the notebook for them.","Letter":"Write about what they liked, using drawing and writing; write any words or sentences they can. Review: read the text aloud once; correct punctuation mistakes using the Barakhadi chart.","Word":"Write a sentence based on the conversation. Mistakes in spelling, punctuation and sentence structure are fine. Review: read it to the group; discuss and correct mistakes together.","Para":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation.","Story":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation."}}],"organisation":[{"grouping":"Whole class (big group)","how":"All learners of all levels sit in a 'U' shape arranged by level (Beginner, Letter, Word, Para, Story) so that the move to small groups is easy.","activities":["Warm-up: Rhyme - 'I saw a Little Bird'","Oral conversation: What did you see on your way?","Story (Day 2 of the story): retelling","Barakhadi chart: big group reading","Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on a day in winter"]},{"grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","how":"Learners of similar levels work together; the teacher gives each group a task for its level and spends more time with learners who need support. Rotate responsibilities (for example group leader).","activities":["Story: reading with actions and group questions","Barakhadi chart: small-group practice"]},{"grouping":"Individual","how":"Each learner works on a task for their own level; the teacher moves around, observes difficulties and supports individuals.","activities":["Story: writing answers individually","Barakhadi chart: individual tasks","Self-writing: individual writing","Self-writing: review and reading back","Daily reading (10 minutes)"]}],"materials":["Rhyme chart or board (optional)","The same story book as yesterday","Story book","slate or paper for questions","Notebooks","Barakhadi chart","alphabet or phonics chart","Alphabet or phonics chart","board or floor","Picture card or topic on the board","crayons or pencils","Library books or storybooks"],"outcomes":["Learners take part in the oral conversation and speak without fear.","Learners retell the story, read with expression and ask or answer questions at their level.","Learners respond to the sound-symbol task for today (Barakhadi / alphabet and phonics chart (line 6, letter 'c')) at their own level.","Learners write about the topic at their level and read it aloud.","Each learner reads a book for 10 minutes."],"observation":["Observe each learner's reading and writing during the individual tasks; note who needs individual support and how many learners share the same difficulty.","Note any learner whose level is improving; move the learner to the next level group when you see steady progress (manual p.5).","Record each learner's progress for the day in the notebook, according to the learner's level (manual p.4).","Use today's observations to adjust tomorrow's plan (manual p.5)."],"teacherNotes":["Questions to elicit on Day 2: information questions (answer not in the text), thinking questions (needs knowledge beyond the text) and opinion questions (feedback on something in the text).","Barakhadi: learners who need extra time should get repeated practice using one or two sound units at a time. Topic-based discussion helps oral expression, thinking and understanding.","Writing has two parts, content and sequence: encourage learners to read what they wrote, improve it and rewrite it for clarity and correctness (manual p.15).","Pace: the manual says not to assume all learners progress at the same speed. Repeat a day's activity with the groups that need it before moving on.","Special needs: give extra time and prepare materials for slower learners; seat learners with hearing or vision difficulty at the front; for learners who reverse or confuse letters, trace letters on the letter card with a finger and write with dots to trace with a pencil (manual p.6)."],"components":[{"no":1,"key":"warmup","name":"Warm-up activities","keywords":["Rhyme - 'I saw a Little Bird'","two learners lead"],"rows":[1]},{"no":2,"key":"oral","name":"Oral Discussion","keywords":["What did you see on your way?","every learner speaks"],"rows":[2]},{"no":3,"key":"story","name":"Story","keywords":["Day 2","retell","read with actions","group questions","ask and answer","write answers (Para/Story)"],"rows":[3,4,5]},{"no":4,"key":"sound","name":"Sound symbol games, Sound separation-pairing","keywords":["Barakhadi / alphabet chart","listen and point (no repeating)","group reading","level tasks"],"rows":[6,7,8]},{"no":5,"key":"mindwrite","name":"Individual-Writing (Day 2)","keywords":["discussion","write at own level","self-review (read aloud)"],"rows":[9,10,11]},{"no":6,"key":"reading","name":"Daily reading","keywords":["library book","read alone","teacher listens"],"rows":[12]}],"preLesson":null},{"programme":"TARL Literacy","id":"lit-060","day":60,"phase":2,"phaseLabel":"Phase 2 (Days 46-90)","title":"Saturday: drama presentation","dayType":"Saturday drama + Self-writing","focus":"Language game: Build the Sentence! | Self-writing: the story we acted out (a story about growing a plant)","duration":70,"objectives":["Listen, speak and answer in the oral conversation (familiar topic).","Express a story through role play, using voice, facial expressions and gestures.","Develop sound-symbol skills: Language game: Build the Sentence!.","Write about the story and review the writing.","Read independently for 10 minutes every day."],"sequence":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Singing and Spinning","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Learners sit in a circle and pass a small object while you clap with your back turned; when the clapping stops, the learner holding it sings a song, recites a poem or tells a joke. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Pass the object round the circle; sing, recite or tell a joke when the clapping stops.","tlm":"A small object (chalk or pencil)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","n":1},{"activity":"Oral conversation: familiar topic","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Hold a conversation on the topic 'a story my grandmother told me'. Give each learner a chance to speak; be patient with learners who need extra time.","learners":"Talk about the topic and listen to others.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.9","n":2},{"activity":"Dramatic presentation: introduction and reading","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Explain what a dramatic presentation is and how it is done. Provide stories discussed during the week and read one aloud once more. Para and Story level learners support Beginner and Letter level learners in reading.","learners":"Listen, read along, then each learner chooses a character.","tlm":"Stories discussed in the week (a story about a village fair; a story about growing a plant)","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":3},{"activity":"Dramatic presentation: planning in small groups","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":8,"teacher":"Each group discusses and plans dialogues; Para or Story level learners write the dialogues. Groups prepare their dramatic presentation.","learners":"Choose characters, plan and rehearse dialogues with facial expressions and gestures.","tlm":"Story, paper for dialogues","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":4},{"activity":"Dramatic presentation: performances and feedback","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":7,"teacher":"Learners sit in a U shape. Each group presents; after each performance, watching learners say what they enjoyed and what could be improved.","learners":"Perform in turn; watch; give feedback.","tlm":"Open space (U-shape seating)","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":5},{"activity":"Language game: Build the Sentence!","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"A simple sentence is made longer by each learner in turn: 'This is a boy' -> 'This is a good boy'. Observe each learner and give help where needed.","learners":"Play the game, take turns and read or say the words they make.","tlm":"Board, chalk","source":"M","ref":"p.21","n":6},{"activity":"Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on the story we acted out (a story about growing a plant)","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Start a conversation about the story used for the drama: 'the story we acted out (a story about growing a plant)'. Involve all learners with open-ended questions.","learners":"Take part in the discussion and share thoughts freely.","tlm":"Picture card or topic on the board","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":7},{"activity":"Self-writing: individual writing","grouping":"Individual","minutes":7,"teacher":"Give each level its task (see level table). Let learners take ownership of what they draw and write; mistakes are fine.","learners":"Draw and write about the topic at their level.","tlm":"Notebooks, crayons or pencils","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":8},{"activity":"Self-writing: review and reading back","grouping":"Individual","minutes":3,"teacher":"Ask each learner 'What did you draw or write?' and have them read it aloud once. Word-level learners read to the group; discuss spelling, punctuation and sentence structure. Help beginners by writing their text in the notebook for them if needed.","learners":"Read what they wrote; correct mistakes after listening to their own reading.","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":9},{"activity":"Daily reading (10 minutes)","grouping":"Individual","minutes":10,"teacher":"Give each learner a library book or any storybook. Move around, listen to individual readers and note their level.","learners":"Read independently a book of their choice.","tlm":"Library books or storybooks","source":"M","ref":"p.7","n":10}],"procedures":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Singing and Spinning","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","steps":[{"teacher":"Seat the learners in a circle; give a small object to one learner.","learners":"Sit in a circle."},{"teacher":"Stand outside the circle with your back to them and clap steadily; they pass the object.","learners":"Pass the object while the clapping continues."},{"teacher":"Stop clapping; the learner holding the object sings, recites or tells a joke.","learners":"Perform, and everybody claps."}]},{"activity":"Oral conversation: familiar topic","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.9","steps":[{"teacher":"Introduce the topic: 'a story my grandmother told me'.","learners":"Think about their own experience."},{"teacher":"Ask open questions; give every learner a chance. Involve learners who speak less.","learners":"Speak freely and without fear."},{"teacher":"Praise efforts and sum up.","learners":"Listen and respect each other's ideas."}]},{"activity":"Saturday special: dramatic presentation","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.11","steps":[{"teacher":"Explain what a dramatic presentation is and how it can be done. Give the groups the stories discussed during the week.","learners":"Listen to the explanation."},{"teacher":"Read a story aloud once more. Learners at story and paragraph level support those at beginner and letter level in reading.","learners":"Read along; helpers support their friends."},{"teacher":"After reading, each learner chooses a character from the story.","learners":"Choose a role (boys may play girl roles and girls may play boy roles)."},{"teacher":"In groups, learners discuss and plan the dialogues; paragraph or story level learners write the dialogues.","learners":"Plan and write dialogues together."},{"teacher":"Learners sit in a U shape. Each group presents its drama. After each performance, ask what the audience enjoyed and what could be improved.","learners":"Perform, watch and give kind feedback."}]},{"activity":"Language game: Build the Sentence!","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.21","steps":[{"teacher":"Start with a simple sentence such as 'This is a boy.'","learners":"Listen to the sentence."},{"teacher":"The next learner makes it a little longer and better: 'This is a good boy.' Then another: 'This is a good boy and he is smiling.'","learners":"Add a few words to the sentence."},{"teacher":"Continue until the sentence cannot be made longer, then start again with a new sentence. The game can be adapted to write creative stories.","learners":"Say the longer sentence and, later, write it."}]},{"activity":"Self-writing: 'Discussion, Writing, Self-review'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.15","steps":[{"teacher":"Start a conversation about the story used for the drama: 'the story we acted out (a story about growing a plant)'. Involve all learners with open-ended questions.","learners":"Discuss and answer questions."},{"teacher":"Give writing time at each level: draw then write (Beginner), write about what they liked (Letter), a sentence (Word), a paragraph or story on a topic of their choice (Para/Story).","learners":"Write at their level and take ownership of the work."},{"teacher":"Review: ask 'What did you draw or write?' Have each learner read the text aloud once. Support with writing if needed.","learners":"Read aloud, listen to their pronunciation and correct mistakes."}]}],"levelTasks":[{"activity":"Drama: roles by level","source":"M","ref":"p.11","tasks":{"Beginner":"Take a character role and say or act short lines with help from Para and Story level learners.","Letter":"Take a character role and say or act short lines with help from Para and Story level learners.","Word":"Take a role and speak the dialogues; help rehearse.","Para":"Write the dialogues for the group and support Beginner, Letter and Word level learners throughout.","Story":"Write the dialogues for the group and support Beginner, Letter and Word level learners throughout."}},{"activity":"Language game: Build the Sentence! - level support","source":"I","ref":"p.21","tasks":{"Beginner":"Take part by saying or pointing to the letters involved and by listening carefully; Para and Story level partners help.","Letter":"Say the letters/sounds and give simple words they know.","Word":"Say and write words and short sentences for the game.","Para":"Write sentences with the words; help groups to record answers.","Story":"Write sentences or short stories with the words; help groups to record answers."}},{"activity":"Self-writing: level tasks and review","source":"M","ref":"p.15","tasks":{"Beginner":"Draw a picture about the discussion and then write a few sentences about it, expressing thoughts freely. Review: say what they drew or wrote; read the text aloud once; the teacher may write the text in the notebook for them.","Letter":"Write about what they liked, using drawing and writing; write any words or sentences they can. Review: read the text aloud once; correct punctuation mistakes using the Barakhadi chart.","Word":"Write a sentence based on the conversation. Mistakes in spelling, punctuation and sentence structure are fine. Review: read it to the group; discuss and correct mistakes together.","Para":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation.","Story":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation."}}],"organisation":[{"grouping":"Whole class (big group)","how":"All learners of all levels sit in a 'U' shape arranged by level (Beginner, Letter, Word, Para, Story) so that the move to small groups is easy.","activities":["Warm-up: Singing and Spinning","Oral conversation: familiar topic","Dramatic presentation: introduction and reading","Dramatic presentation: performances and feedback","Language game: Build the Sentence!","Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on the story we acted out (a story about growing a plant)"]},{"grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","how":"Learners of similar levels work together; the teacher gives each group a task for its level and spends more time with learners who need support. Rotate responsibilities (for example group leader).","activities":["Dramatic presentation: planning in small groups"]},{"grouping":"Individual","how":"Each learner works on a task for their own level; the teacher moves around, observes difficulties and supports individuals.","activities":["Self-writing: individual writing","Self-writing: review and reading back","Daily reading (10 minutes)"]}],"materials":["A small object (chalk or pencil)","Stories discussed in the week (a story about a village fair; a story about growing a plant)","Story","paper for dialogues","Open space (U-shape seating)","Board","chalk","Picture card or topic on the board","Notebooks","crayons or pencils","Library books or storybooks"],"outcomes":["Learners take part in the oral conversation and speak without fear.","Learners present a role in the group drama and give feedback to others.","Learners respond to the sound-symbol task for today (Language game: Build the Sentence!) at their own level.","Learners write about the story at their level and read it aloud.","Each learner reads a book for 10 minutes."],"observation":["Observe each learner's reading and writing during the individual tasks; note who needs individual support and how many learners share the same difficulty.","Note any learner whose level is improving; move the learner to the next level group when you see steady progress (manual p.5).","Record each learner's progress for the day in the notebook, according to the learner's level (manual p.4).","Use today's observations to adjust tomorrow's plan (manual p.5)."],"teacherNotes":["Saturday: this plan assumes Day 1 is a Monday (six teaching days per week). If your school week is different, hold the drama presentation on your Saturday and keep the other days in sequence.","The manual lists the letter and word games but does not fix the slot in the daily timetable where they are used. This plan places them in the 10-minute sound-symbol / alphabet slot (interpretation).","Writing has two parts, content and sequence: encourage learners to read what they wrote, improve it and rewrite it for clarity and correctness (manual p.15).","Pace: the manual says not to assume all learners progress at the same speed. Repeat a day's activity with the groups that need it before moving on.","Special needs: give extra time and prepare materials for slower learners; seat learners with hearing or vision difficulty at the front; for learners who reverse or confuse letters, trace letters on the letter card with a finger and write with dots to trace with a pencil (manual p.6)."],"components":[{"no":1,"key":"warmup","name":"Warm-up activities","keywords":["Singing and Spinning","two learners lead"],"rows":[1]},{"no":2,"key":"oral","name":"Oral Discussion","keywords":["familiar topic","every learner speaks"],"rows":[2]},{"no":3,"key":"story","name":"Story (Saturday: dramatic presentation)","keywords":["Saturday drama","choose a character","plan dialogues","perform in U shape","feedback"],"rows":[3,4,5]},{"no":4,"key":"sound","name":"Sound symbol games, Sound separation-pairing","keywords":["Build the Sentence!","play in turns","level support"],"rows":[6]},{"no":5,"key":"mindwrite","name":"Individual-Writing (Day 2)","keywords":["discussion","write at own level","self-review (read aloud)"],"rows":[7,8,9]},{"no":6,"key":"reading","name":"Daily reading","keywords":["library book","read alone","teacher listens"],"rows":[10]}],"preLesson":null},{"programme":"TARL Literacy","id":"lit-061","day":61,"phase":2,"phaseLabel":"Phase 2 (Days 46-90)","title":"Story: a story about a boat journey (Day 1)","dayType":"Story Day 1 + Mind mapping","focus":"Consonant clusters: thr (three, throw) | Mind map: my body","duration":70,"objectives":["Listen, speak and answer in the oral conversation (conversation on a picture).","Listen to and read a story with understanding; discuss it in big and small groups and respond at their own level.","Develop sound-symbol skills: Consonant clusters: thr (three, throw).","Build vocabulary through a mind map ('my body') and use the words at their own level.","Read independently for 10 minutes every day."],"sequence":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Rain clapping","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Everyone stands in a circle with eyes closed and keeps clapping: first one finger, then two, three, four and finally five fingers. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Stand in a circle, close the eyes and clap with 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 fingers.","tlm":"After the activity ask: Which finger sound was your favourite?","source":"M","ref":"p.8","n":1},{"activity":"Oral conversation: conversation on a picture","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Show a picture of a fair with swings and toy sellers and ask what is happening, who is doing what and what is happening around them. Let learners think creatively and even make up a story.","learners":"Look at the picture, answer questions and make up their own story about it.","tlm":"Picture card of a fair with swings and toy sellers","source":"M","ref":"p.9","n":2},{"activity":"Story (Day 1 of the story): reading aloud and discussion","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":8,"teacher":"Discuss the title or picture of the story with the learners. Read the story aloud with expression and voice modulation (learners do not repeat after you). Discuss it, with emphasis on factual questions. Read it again slowly, pointing to each word.","learners":"Talk about the title/picture; listen; answer questions; follow each word with a finger in their own copy.","tlm":"A story from the school library (a story about a boat journey), a copy for each learner","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":3},{"activity":"Story: reading in small groups","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":7,"teacher":"Form level-wise groups with a group leader. Learners read the story one sentence at a time while the others follow with their fingers. Para and Story level learners practise reading with emotion and expression.","learners":"Read the story sentence by sentence, supporting each other; the group leader helps.","tlm":"Story book copies","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":4},{"activity":"Story: level-wise individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":5,"teacher":"Give each learner the task for their level (see level table) and support those who need it.","learners":"Beginner/Letter: find and write favourite words or letters. Word: find consonant clusters. Para/Story: silently read, find unfamiliar and rhyming words.","tlm":"Story book, notebooks, board","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":5},{"activity":"Consonant clusters: introduction","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":4,"teacher":"Three-letter clusters: after two-letter clusters, familiarise learners with clusters of three letters ('thr' as in three, throw, throat). Discuss the words, then ask learners to tell and write sentences using them.","learners":"Listen, pronounce the cluster and say words that contain it.","tlm":"Board and chalk, words list (three throw throat thread thrill)","source":"M","ref":"p.16","n":6},{"activity":"Consonant cluster game: Conjunct Consonant Game","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":6,"teacher":"Give each child a set of conjunct consonant cards. Observe closely and help learners who need support.","learners":"Choose one conjunct consonant and form five words with it. Learners at paragraph or story level can make sentences with the words they formed.","tlm":"Conjunct consonant cards","source":"M","ref":"p.17","n":7},{"activity":"Mind mapping (Day 1): the word 'my body'","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Ask: 'What words come to your mind when you hear the word my body?' Write learners' answers on the board or floor (Para and Story level learners write the words themselves). Guide the map towards the learning objective. Example words: eye, ear, nose, mouth, elbow, wrist, finger, thumb, knee, ankle, foot, toe.","learners":"Say words connected with 'my body'; share the meaning and feeling of words.","tlm":"Board, chalk (or floor)","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":8},{"activity":"Mind mapping: classify the words","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":4,"teacher":"Ask learners to classify the words in groups, for example: Head: eye, ear, nose, mouth; Arms and hands: elbow, wrist, finger, thumb; Legs: knee, ankle, foot, toe.","learners":"Sort the words into groups and say why.","tlm":"Board, chalk, word cards (optional)","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":9},{"activity":"Mind mapping: level-wise individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":6,"teacher":"Give each learner the individual task for their level; observe closely and give individual support. Display corrected stories on the wall.","learners":"Complete the task for their level (see level table).","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":10},{"activity":"Daily reading (10 minutes)","grouping":"Individual","minutes":10,"teacher":"Give each learner a library book or any storybook. Move around, listen to individual readers and note their level.","learners":"Read independently a book of their choice.","tlm":"Library books or storybooks","source":"M","ref":"p.7","n":11}],"procedures":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Rain clapping","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","steps":[{"teacher":"Stand the learners in a circle and ask them to close their eyes. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Stand in a circle and close their eyes."},{"teacher":"Start clapping with one finger; then two fingers, three, four and finally five fingers.","learners":"Keep clapping, copying the change of fingers."},{"teacher":"After the activity ask: Which finger sound was your favourite?","learners":"Tell how they felt and what the sounds reminded them of."}]},{"activity":"Oral conversation: conversation on a picture","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.9","steps":[{"teacher":"Show the picture of a fair with swings and toy sellers.","learners":"Look carefully."},{"teacher":"Ask: What is happening in the picture? Who is doing what? What is happening around them? Then: How do the people feel? How can you tell?","learners":"Answer in their own words; every learner gets a chance."},{"teacher":"Let learners imagine and make up a short story from the picture.","learners":"Tell their stories to the class."}]},{"activity":"Story - Day 1 (a story about a boat journey)","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.10","steps":[{"teacher":"Discuss the title or picture of the story with the learners.","learners":"Talk about what they see and what the story may be about."},{"teacher":"Read the story aloud with expression and proper voice modulation. Learners should not simply repeat after you.","learners":"Listen carefully and enjoy the story."},{"teacher":"Discuss the story: factual, logical, vocabulary-based, judgment or opinion questions (today's focus: factual: Who was in the story? Where did it happen? What did the character do first?). Begin in the home language if needed.","learners":"Think and respond thoughtfully; every learner takes part."},{"teacher":"Read the story again slowly, pointing to each word. Make sure each learner has a copy and follows with a finger.","learners":"Follow each word with their finger."},{"teacher":"Ask learners to read in small groups; select a group leader who helps the others. Learners read one sentence at a time while the others point with fingers.","learners":"Read with the help of one another."}]},{"activity":"Consonant clusters (thr) and the game 'Conjunct Consonant Game'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.16-17","steps":[{"teacher":"Three-letter clusters: after two-letter clusters, familiarise learners with clusters of three letters ('thr' as in three, throw, throat). Discuss the words, then ask learners to tell and write sentences using them.","learners":"Listen, pronounce and find words in the text."},{"teacher":"Write the words on the board: three throw throat thread thrill. Read them aloud with distinct pronunciation of the cluster.","learners":"Read the words aloud; point to the cluster in each word."},{"teacher":"Give each child a set of conjunct consonant cards.","learners":"Choose one conjunct consonant and form five words with it. Learners at paragraph or story level can make sentences with the words they formed."}]},{"activity":"Mind mapping: 'my body'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Small group (level-wise) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.14","steps":[{"teacher":"Choose a word that can generate many related words: 'my body'. Ask: 'What words come to your mind when you hear the word my body?' Write the answers on the board or floor.","learners":"Say words they link with 'my body'."},{"teacher":"Discuss the words: what they mean and how they are connected.","learners":"Explain their words and listen to others."},{"teacher":"In small groups, let the learners classify the words (Head: eye, ear, nose, mouth; Arms and hands: elbow, wrist, finger, thumb; Legs: knee, ankle, foot, toe).","learners":"Sort the words into groups."},{"teacher":"Give the individual tasks by level and help each learner.","learners":"Work individually; read the work aloud at the end if time allows."}]}],"levelTasks":[{"activity":"Story - Day 1: individual tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.10","tasks":{"Beginner":"Circle or search for a favourite word or letter in the story and say it aloud. If a learner cannot draw a circle, write words on the board and ask them to identify them.","Letter":"Find, read and write favourite words from the story.","Word":"Find the consonant clusters in the story, read them and write them in the notebook.","Para":"Silently read the story from the textbook; find unfamiliar words and try to understand them; find rhyming words, use them in sentences and write in the notebook; ask other groups for meanings; make questions in groups.","Story":"Silently read the story; find unfamiliar words and rhyming words; practise reading with emotion; one group reads sentences formed with consonant clusters to the other group; ask and answer group questions (information, thinking and opinion questions)."}},{"activity":"Consonant clusters (thr): level tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.16-17","tasks":{"Beginner":"Listen to the sound of the cluster and point to it in a word; continue with letter-sound work (interpretation: the manual describes clusters for learners lagging in reading words and sentences).","Letter":"Listen to the cluster sound and pick words with the cluster from a word card (interpretation).","Word":"Find the cluster in the story or textbook words, read the words and write them in the notebook.","Para":"Form words and sentences using the cluster; read the sentences aloud.","Story":"Form words and sentences using the cluster; read the sentences aloud; use them in the story writing."}},{"activity":"Mind mapping 'my body': level tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.14","tasks":{"Beginner":"Circle all the words that contain the letter 'E' on the board; make a list. See how many learners find the most words.","Letter":"Circle all the words that contain the letter 'E' and make a list of them.","Word":"Use 4-5 words (for example ear, eye, toe, foot, knee) to form sentences, starting with words of one or two syllables. Example: Dream - I had a dream last night.","Para":"Choose any five words from the map and create a story with them. Use consonant clusters correctly, read the story aloud, correct mistakes of sentence structure, spelling or grammar, then display it on the wall.","Story":"Choose any five words from the map and create a story with them. Use consonant clusters correctly, read the story aloud, correct mistakes of sentence structure, spelling or grammar, then display it on the wall."}}],"organisation":[{"grouping":"Whole class (big group)","how":"All learners of all levels sit in a 'U' shape arranged by level (Beginner, Letter, Word, Para, Story) so that the move to small groups is easy.","activities":["Warm-up: Rain clapping","Oral conversation: conversation on a picture","Story (Day 1 of the story): reading aloud and discussion","Consonant clusters: introduction","Mind mapping (Day 1): the word 'my body'"]},{"grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","how":"Learners of similar levels work together; the teacher gives each group a task for its level and spends more time with learners who need support. Rotate responsibilities (for example group leader).","activities":["Story: reading in small groups","Consonant cluster game: Conjunct Consonant Game","Mind mapping: classify the words"]},{"grouping":"Individual","how":"Each learner works on a task for their own level; the teacher moves around, observes difficulties and supports individuals.","activities":["Story: level-wise individual tasks","Mind mapping: level-wise individual tasks","Daily reading (10 minutes)"]}],"materials":["After the activity ask: Which finger sound was your favourite?","Picture card of a fair with swings","toy sellers","A story from the school library (a story about a boat journey)","a copy for each learner","Story book copies","Story book","notebooks","board","Board","chalk","words list (three throw throat thread thrill)","Conjunct consonant cards","chalk (or floor)","word cards (optional)","Notebooks","Library books or storybooks"],"outcomes":["Learners take part in the oral conversation and speak without fear.","Learners show understanding of the story in the discussion and complete the task for their level.","Learners respond to the sound-symbol task for today (Consonant clusters: thr (three, throw)) at their own level.","Learners add words to the mind map and use them in sentences or a story at their level.","Each learner reads a book for 10 minutes."],"observation":["Observe each learner's reading and writing during the individual tasks; note who needs individual support and how many learners share the same difficulty.","Note any learner whose level is improving; move the learner to the next level group when you see steady progress (manual p.5).","Record each learner's progress for the day in the notebook, according to the learner's level (manual p.4).","Use today's observations to adjust tomorrow's plan (manual p.5)."],"teacherNotes":["Story selection: the manual asks teachers to use picture story books or stories in the school library. Today's suggested theme (a story about a boat journey) is a planning suggestion; use any suitable story you have.","Consonant clusters: do these activities daily for learners who find reading complex words hard; the aim is to remove the fear of reading clusters. Teachers may carry out similar activities on their own.","Mind mapping topic for this day: 'my body'. The manual's example uses the word 'shop'; today's topic follows the same method.","Pace: the manual says not to assume all learners progress at the same speed. Repeat a day's activity with the groups that need it before moving on.","Special needs: give extra time and prepare materials for slower learners; seat learners with hearing or vision difficulty at the front; for learners who reverse or confuse letters, trace letters on the letter card with a finger and write with dots to trace with a pencil (manual p.6)."],"components":[{"no":1,"key":"warmup","name":"Warm-up activities","keywords":["Rain clapping","two learners lead"],"rows":[1]},{"no":2,"key":"oral","name":"Oral Discussion","keywords":["conversation on a picture","every learner speaks"],"rows":[2]},{"no":3,"key":"story","name":"Story","keywords":["Day 1","title / picture talk","read aloud with expression","factual questions","re-read pointing","group reading","level tasks"],"rows":[3,4,5]},{"no":4,"key":"sound","name":"Sound symbol games, Sound separation-pairing","keywords":["consonant cluster 'thr'","pronounce and find words","game: Conjunct Consonant Game"],"rows":[6,7]},{"no":5,"key":"mindwrite","name":"Mind Mapping (Day 1)","keywords":["mind map: my body","classify the words","level task: circle letter E / sentences / story"],"rows":[8,9,10]},{"no":6,"key":"reading","name":"Daily reading","keywords":["library book","read alone","teacher listens"],"rows":[11]}],"preLesson":null},{"programme":"TARL Literacy","id":"lit-062","day":62,"phase":2,"phaseLabel":"Phase 2 (Days 46-90)","title":"Story: a story about a boat journey (Day 2)","dayType":"Story Day 2 + Self-writing","focus":"Language game: The Wind is Blowing | Self-writing: a picture of a tea garden","duration":70,"objectives":["Listen, speak and answer in the oral conversation (listening and storytelling).","Retell the story, read it with expression, ask and answer questions about it and write answers.","Develop sound-symbol skills: Language game: The Wind is Blowing.","Write about a topic at their own level and review the writing (a picture of a tea garden).","Read independently for 10 minutes every day."],"sequence":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Writing with body parts","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Learners stand in a circle. Demonstrate writing the word 'rain' in the air with a finger, then ask them to write it with different body parts. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Write the word 'rain' in the air with the finger, then with the head, shoulders, knees or elbows.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.8","n":1},{"activity":"Oral conversation: listening and storytelling","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Tell an interesting story starter and involve the learners: 'A little boy found a lamp under a tree. What did he wish for?' Let learners imagine and continue the story.","learners":"Listen to the teacher, then imagine and continue the story. Learners can also recite a rhyme or story they know.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.9","n":2},{"activity":"Story (Day 2 of the story): retelling","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":6,"teacher":"Ask learners to retell yesterday's story in their own words. Prompt with questions on the beginning, middle and end.","learners":"Retell the story using their own words.","tlm":"The same story book as yesterday","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":3},{"activity":"Story: reading with actions and group questions","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":9,"teacher":"Learners practise reading with actions and expressions; one learner per group reads aloud to the class. Guide groups to make questions about the story (guide initially). Groups take turns to ask and answer each other's questions. Word-level learners also read aloud the consonants learned on the first day.","learners":"Read with actions; make questions (word-level learners help write them); ask and answer questions with another group.","tlm":"Story book, slate or paper for questions","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":4},{"activity":"Story: writing answers individually","grouping":"Individual","minutes":5,"teacher":"Para and Story level learners write answers to all questions individually; read and correct their responses after they finish.","learners":"Write the answers in their notebooks; Beginner/Letter/Word learners read or listen and answer orally.","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":5},{"activity":"Language game: The Wind is Blowing","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Learners hold a secret letter card; the one whose letter the teacher names says words beginning with it. Observe each learner and give help where needed.","learners":"Play the game, take turns and read or say the words they make.","tlm":"Letter flashcards","source":"M","ref":"p.19","n":6},{"activity":"Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on a picture of a tea garden","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Start a conversation about a topic: 'a picture of a tea garden'. Involve all learners and ask open-ended questions.","learners":"Take part in the discussion and share thoughts freely.","tlm":"Picture card or topic on the board","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":7},{"activity":"Self-writing: individual writing","grouping":"Individual","minutes":7,"teacher":"Give each level its task (see level table). Let learners take ownership of what they draw and write; mistakes are fine.","learners":"Draw and write about the topic at their level.","tlm":"Notebooks, crayons or pencils","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":8},{"activity":"Self-writing: review and reading back","grouping":"Individual","minutes":3,"teacher":"Ask each learner 'What did you draw or write?' and have them read it aloud once. Word-level learners read to the group; discuss spelling, punctuation and sentence structure. Help beginners by writing their text in the notebook for them if needed.","learners":"Read what they wrote; correct mistakes after listening to their own reading.","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":9},{"activity":"Daily reading (10 minutes)","grouping":"Individual","minutes":10,"teacher":"Give each learner a library book or any storybook. Move around, listen to individual readers and note their level.","learners":"Read independently a book of their choice.","tlm":"Library books or storybooks","source":"M","ref":"p.7","n":10}],"procedures":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Writing with body parts","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","steps":[{"teacher":"Stand the learners in a circle. Demonstrate writing the word 'rain' in the air with your finger.","learners":"Watch and then copy with their own finger."},{"teacher":"Ask them to write it again using elbows and other body parts (head, shoulders, knees, ...).","learners":"Write the letters in the air with the named body part."},{"teacher":"Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Take turns to lead."}]},{"activity":"Oral conversation: listening and storytelling","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.9","steps":[{"teacher":"Say the starter: 'A little boy found a lamp under a tree. What did he wish for?'","learners":"Listen and imagine."},{"teacher":"Ask learners to continue the story one by one. Encourage those who speak less.","learners":"Add ideas to the story."},{"teacher":"Invite a learner to recite a poem or rhyme they know.","learners":"Recite and listen to others."}]},{"activity":"Story - Day 2 (a story about a boat journey)","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.11","steps":[{"teacher":"Ask learners to retell the story they read yesterday in their own words.","learners":"Retell, helping each other remember."},{"teacher":"In small groups learners practise reading the story using actions and expressions; one learner from each group then reads aloud to the class.","learners":"Read with actions and expression; a representative reads aloud."},{"teacher":"Guide the groups to come up with questions about the story (guide initially). Word-level learners can support by helping write them down.","learners":"Make questions together."},{"teacher":"Groups take turns to ask and answer each other's questions. Useful kinds: questions whose answer is not in the text; questions needing thinking beyond the text; questions asking for an opinion.","learners":"Ask, answer and discuss in the groups."},{"teacher":"Word-level learners also read aloud the consonants they learned on the first day.","learners":"Read the consonant clusters aloud."}]},{"activity":"Language game: The Wind is Blowing","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.19","steps":[{"teacher":"Stand all learners in a circle and give each one a letter flashcard, which they must not show to anyone.","learners":"Hold the card against the chest; do not show it."},{"teacher":"Say: 'The wind is blowing.' Learners answer: 'Which way is it blowing?' Say: 'The wind is blowing towards T.'","learners":"Reply together; the learner with the letter T steps to the centre."},{"teacher":"Ask the learner in the centre to say a few words that start with T. Continue with other letters.","learners":"Say words such as tree, tiger, toy."}]},{"activity":"Self-writing: 'Discussion, Writing, Self-review'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.15","steps":[{"teacher":"Start a conversation about a topic: 'a picture of a tea garden'. Involve all learners and ask open-ended questions.","learners":"Discuss and answer questions."},{"teacher":"Give writing time at each level: draw then write (Beginner), write about what they liked (Letter), a sentence (Word), a paragraph or story on a topic of their choice (Para/Story).","learners":"Write at their level and take ownership of the work."},{"teacher":"Review: ask 'What did you draw or write?' Have each learner read the text aloud once. Support with writing if needed.","learners":"Read aloud, listen to their pronunciation and correct mistakes."}]}],"levelTasks":[{"activity":"Story - Day 2: level-wise tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.11","tasks":{"Beginner":"Retell with the group by pointing to pictures or words; read aloud with group support (interpretation of the manual's group reading task).","Letter":"Read with the group, pointing to words; say the letters and words they know (interpretation of the manual's group reading task).","Word":"Support the group in writing the questions; read aloud the consonant clusters learned on the first day.","Para":"Ask the group's questions to another group, discuss them, then write answers to all questions individually; the teacher reads and corrects.","Story":"Ask the group's questions to another group, discuss them, then write answers to all questions individually; the teacher reads and corrects."}},{"activity":"Language game: The Wind is Blowing - level support","source":"I","ref":"p.19","tasks":{"Beginner":"Take part by saying or pointing to the letters involved and by listening carefully; Para and Story level partners help.","Letter":"Say the letters/sounds and give simple words they know.","Word":"Say and write words and short sentences for the game.","Para":"Write sentences with the words; help groups to record answers.","Story":"Write sentences or short stories with the words; help groups to record answers."}},{"activity":"Self-writing: level tasks and review","source":"M","ref":"p.15","tasks":{"Beginner":"Draw a picture about the discussion and then write a few sentences about it, expressing thoughts freely. Review: say what they drew or wrote; read the text aloud once; the teacher may write the text in the notebook for them.","Letter":"Write about what they liked, using drawing and writing; write any words or sentences they can. Review: read the text aloud once; correct punctuation mistakes using the Barakhadi chart.","Word":"Write a sentence based on the conversation. Mistakes in spelling, punctuation and sentence structure are fine. Review: read it to the group; discuss and correct mistakes together.","Para":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation.","Story":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation."}}],"organisation":[{"grouping":"Whole class (big group)","how":"All learners of all levels sit in a 'U' shape arranged by level (Beginner, Letter, Word, Para, Story) so that the move to small groups is easy.","activities":["Warm-up: Writing with body parts","Oral conversation: listening and storytelling","Story (Day 2 of the story): retelling","Language game: The Wind is Blowing","Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on a picture of a tea garden"]},{"grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","how":"Learners of similar levels work together; the teacher gives each group a task for its level and spends more time with learners who need support. Rotate responsibilities (for example group leader).","activities":["Story: reading with actions and group questions"]},{"grouping":"Individual","how":"Each learner works on a task for their own level; the teacher moves around, observes difficulties and supports individuals.","activities":["Story: writing answers individually","Self-writing: individual writing","Self-writing: review and reading back","Daily reading (10 minutes)"]}],"materials":["The same story book as yesterday","Story book","slate or paper for questions","Notebooks","Letter flashcards","Picture card or topic on the board","crayons or pencils","Library books or storybooks"],"outcomes":["Learners take part in the oral conversation and speak without fear.","Learners retell the story, read with expression and ask or answer questions at their level.","Learners respond to the sound-symbol task for today (Language game: The Wind is Blowing) at their own level.","Learners write about the topic at their level and read it aloud.","Each learner reads a book for 10 minutes."],"observation":["Observe each learner's reading and writing during the individual tasks; note who needs individual support and how many learners share the same difficulty.","Note any learner whose level is improving; move the learner to the next level group when you see steady progress (manual p.5).","Record each learner's progress for the day in the notebook, according to the learner's level (manual p.4).","Use today's observations to adjust tomorrow's plan (manual p.5)."],"teacherNotes":["Questions to elicit on Day 2: information questions (answer not in the text), thinking questions (needs knowledge beyond the text) and opinion questions (feedback on something in the text).","The manual lists the letter and word games but does not fix the slot in the daily timetable where they are used. This plan places them in the 10-minute sound-symbol / alphabet slot (interpretation).","Writing has two parts, content and sequence: encourage learners to read what they wrote, improve it and rewrite it for clarity and correctness (manual p.15).","Pace: the manual says not to assume all learners progress at the same speed. Repeat a day's activity with the groups that need it before moving on.","Special needs: give extra time and prepare materials for slower learners; seat learners with hearing or vision difficulty at the front; for learners who reverse or confuse letters, trace letters on the letter card with a finger and write with dots to trace with a pencil (manual p.6)."],"components":[{"no":1,"key":"warmup","name":"Warm-up activities","keywords":["Writing with body parts","two learners lead"],"rows":[1]},{"no":2,"key":"oral","name":"Oral Discussion","keywords":["listening and storytelling","every learner speaks"],"rows":[2]},{"no":3,"key":"story","name":"Story","keywords":["Day 2","retell","read with actions","group questions","ask and answer","write answers (Para/Story)"],"rows":[3,4,5]},{"no":4,"key":"sound","name":"Sound symbol games, Sound separation-pairing","keywords":["The Wind is Blowing","play in turns","level support"],"rows":[6]},{"no":5,"key":"mindwrite","name":"Individual-Writing (Day 2)","keywords":["discussion","write at own level","self-review (read aloud)"],"rows":[7,8,9]},{"no":6,"key":"reading","name":"Daily reading","keywords":["library book","read alone","teacher listens"],"rows":[10]}],"preLesson":null},{"programme":"TARL Literacy","id":"lit-063","day":63,"phase":2,"phaseLabel":"Phase 2 (Days 46-90)","title":"Story: a story about a festival of lights (Day 1)","dayType":"Story Day 1 + Mind mapping","focus":"Language game: The Story Continued Slowly | Mind map: clothes","duration":70,"objectives":["Listen, speak and answer in the oral conversation (What did you see on your way?).","Listen to and read a story with understanding; discuss it in big and small groups and respond at their own level.","Develop sound-symbol skills: Language game: The Story Continued Slowly.","Build vocabulary through a mind map ('clothes') and use the words at their own level.","Read independently for 10 minutes every day."],"sequence":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Alphabet song (last-letter word chain)","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Say a word to the big group, for example 'tree'. Learners say a word that starts with the last letter ('e'). A learner who cannot say a word is out. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Say a word that starts with the last letter of the previous word; step out if unable to.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.8","n":1},{"activity":"Oral conversation: What did you see on your way?","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Ask learners to describe what they saw on their way to school. If they are hesitant, begin yourself: 'I saw a shop opening, a bus stopping and a mother holding her child's hand. What did you see?'","learners":"Describe what they saw on the way to school and connect with what others share.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.9","n":2},{"activity":"Story (Day 1 of the story): reading aloud and discussion","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":8,"teacher":"Discuss the title or picture of the story with the learners. Read the story aloud with expression and voice modulation (learners do not repeat after you). Discuss it, with emphasis on logical questions. Read it again slowly, pointing to each word.","learners":"Talk about the title/picture; listen; answer questions; follow each word with a finger in their own copy.","tlm":"A story from the school library (a story about a festival of lights), a copy for each learner","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":3},{"activity":"Story: reading in small groups","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":7,"teacher":"Form level-wise groups with a group leader. Learners read the story one sentence at a time while the others follow with their fingers. Para and Story level learners practise reading with emotion and expression.","learners":"Read the story sentence by sentence, supporting each other; the group leader helps.","tlm":"Story book copies","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":4},{"activity":"Story: level-wise individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":5,"teacher":"Give each learner the task for their level (see level table) and support those who need it.","learners":"Beginner/Letter: find and write favourite words or letters. Word: find consonant clusters. Para/Story: silently read, find unfamiliar and rhyming words.","tlm":"Story book, notebooks, board","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":5},{"activity":"Language game: The Story Continued Slowly","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Learners add one sentence each to a story, first orally, then in writing; some draw a picture and think of a title. Observe each learner and give help where needed.","learners":"Play the game, take turns and read or say the words they make.","tlm":"Board, notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.21","n":6},{"activity":"Mind mapping (Day 1): the word 'clothes'","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Ask: 'What words come to your mind when you hear the word clothes?' Write learners' answers on the board or floor (Para and Story level learners write the words themselves). Guide the map towards the learning objective. Example words: shirt, frock, cap, shorts, sweater, shawl, jacket, socks, dhoti, saree, kurta, gamosa.","learners":"Say words connected with 'clothes'; share the meaning and feeling of words.","tlm":"Board, chalk (or floor)","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":7},{"activity":"Mind mapping: classify the words","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":4,"teacher":"Ask learners to classify the words in groups, for example: Wear in summer: shirt, frock, cap, shorts; Wear in winter: sweater, shawl, jacket, socks; Wear on festivals: dhoti, saree, kurta, gamosa.","learners":"Sort the words into groups and say why.","tlm":"Board, chalk, word cards (optional)","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":8},{"activity":"Mind mapping: level-wise individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":6,"teacher":"Give each learner the individual task for their level; observe closely and give individual support. Display corrected stories on the wall.","learners":"Complete the task for their level (see level table).","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":9},{"activity":"Daily reading (10 minutes)","grouping":"Individual","minutes":10,"teacher":"Give each learner a library book or any storybook. Move around, listen to individual readers and note their level.","learners":"Read independently a book of their choice.","tlm":"Library books or storybooks","source":"M","ref":"p.7","n":10}],"procedures":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Alphabet song (last-letter word chain)","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","steps":[{"teacher":"Say the word 'tree' to the big group and show that its last letter is 'e'.","learners":"Listen and think of a word starting with 'e'."},{"teacher":"Ask learners in turn to say a word that starts with the last letter of the previous word. Example: rain -> nest.","learners":"Say a word in turn; anyone who cannot say a word is out of the game."},{"teacher":"Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Lead the game when it is their turn."}]},{"activity":"Oral conversation: What did you see on your way?","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.9","steps":[{"teacher":"Ask: 'What did you see on your way to school today?'","learners":"Think about the way to school."},{"teacher":"If learners hesitate, start: 'I saw a shop opening, a bus stopping and a mother holding her child's hand. What did you see?'","learners":"Listen to the model and then share their own observations."},{"teacher":"Connect learners' answers with each other.","learners":"Listen and add what they noticed."}]},{"activity":"Story - Day 1 (a story about a festival of lights)","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.10","steps":[{"teacher":"Discuss the title or picture of the story with the learners.","learners":"Talk about what they see and what the story may be about."},{"teacher":"Read the story aloud with expression and proper voice modulation. Learners should not simply repeat after you.","learners":"Listen carefully and enjoy the story."},{"teacher":"Discuss the story: factual, logical, vocabulary-based, judgment or opinion questions (today's focus: logical: Why did the character do that? What would have happened if ...?). Begin in the home language if needed.","learners":"Think and respond thoughtfully; every learner takes part."},{"teacher":"Read the story again slowly, pointing to each word. Make sure each learner has a copy and follows with a finger.","learners":"Follow each word with their finger."},{"teacher":"Ask learners to read in small groups; select a group leader who helps the others. Learners read one sentence at a time while the others point with fingers.","learners":"Read with the help of one another."}]},{"activity":"Language game: The Story Continued Slowly","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.21","steps":[{"teacher":"Say: 'Let us write a beautiful story together.' Each sentence must follow from the previous sentence. Start speaking orally first.","learners":"Listen and add one sentence each."},{"teacher":"Move to writing the story sentence by sentence; a few learners draw a picture and think of a title.","learners":"Write sentences; draw and think of a title."},{"teacher":"As learners get used to writing stories, discuss what the story will be like before writing.","learners":"Plan the story orally before writing."}]},{"activity":"Mind mapping: 'clothes'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Small group (level-wise) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.14","steps":[{"teacher":"Choose a word that can generate many related words: 'clothes'. Ask: 'What words come to your mind when you hear the word clothes?' Write the answers on the board or floor.","learners":"Say words they link with 'clothes'."},{"teacher":"Discuss the words: what they mean and how they are connected.","learners":"Explain their words and listen to others."},{"teacher":"In small groups, let the learners classify the words (Wear in summer: shirt, frock, cap, shorts; Wear in winter: sweater, shawl, jacket, socks; Wear on festivals: dhoti, saree, kurta, gamosa).","learners":"Sort the words into groups."},{"teacher":"Give the individual tasks by level and help each learner.","learners":"Work individually; read the work aloud at the end if time allows."}]}],"levelTasks":[{"activity":"Story - Day 1: individual tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.10","tasks":{"Beginner":"Circle or search for a favourite word or letter in the story and say it aloud. If a learner cannot draw a circle, write words on the board and ask them to identify them.","Letter":"Find, read and write favourite words from the story.","Word":"Find the consonant clusters in the story, read them and write them in the notebook.","Para":"Silently read the story from the textbook; find unfamiliar words and try to understand them; find rhyming words, use them in sentences and write in the notebook; ask other groups for meanings; make questions in groups.","Story":"Silently read the story; find unfamiliar words and rhyming words; practise reading with emotion; one group reads sentences formed with consonant clusters to the other group; ask and answer group questions (information, thinking and opinion questions)."}},{"activity":"Language game: The Story Continued Slowly - level support","source":"I","ref":"p.21","tasks":{"Beginner":"Take part by saying or pointing to the letters involved and by listening carefully; Para and Story level partners help.","Letter":"Say the letters/sounds and give simple words they know.","Word":"Say and write words and short sentences for the game.","Para":"Write sentences with the words; help groups to record answers.","Story":"Write sentences or short stories with the words; help groups to record answers."}},{"activity":"Mind mapping 'clothes': level tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.14","tasks":{"Beginner":"Circle all the words that contain the letter 'A' on the board; make a list. See how many learners find the most words.","Letter":"Circle all the words that contain the letter 'A' and make a list of them.","Word":"Use 4-5 words (for example cap, dhoti, frock, kurta, saree) to form sentences, starting with words of one or two syllables. Example: Dream - I had a dream last night.","Para":"Choose any five words from the map and create a story with them. Use consonant clusters correctly, read the story aloud, correct mistakes of sentence structure, spelling or grammar, then display it on the wall.","Story":"Choose any five words from the map and create a story with them. Use consonant clusters correctly, read the story aloud, correct mistakes of sentence structure, spelling or grammar, then display it on the wall."}}],"organisation":[{"grouping":"Whole class (big group)","how":"All learners of all levels sit in a 'U' shape arranged by level (Beginner, Letter, Word, Para, Story) so that the move to small groups is easy.","activities":["Warm-up: Alphabet song (last-letter word chain)","Oral conversation: What did you see on your way?","Story (Day 1 of the story): reading aloud and discussion","Language game: The Story Continued Slowly","Mind mapping (Day 1): the word 'clothes'"]},{"grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","how":"Learners of similar levels work together; the teacher gives each group a task for its level and spends more time with learners who need support. Rotate responsibilities (for example group leader).","activities":["Story: reading in small groups","Mind mapping: classify the words"]},{"grouping":"Individual","how":"Each learner works on a task for their own level; the teacher moves around, observes difficulties and supports individuals.","activities":["Story: level-wise individual tasks","Mind mapping: level-wise individual tasks","Daily reading (10 minutes)"]}],"materials":["A story from the school library (a story about a festival of lights)","a copy for each learner","Story book copies","Story book","notebooks","board","Board","chalk (or floor)","chalk","word cards (optional)","Notebooks","Library books or storybooks"],"outcomes":["Learners take part in the oral conversation and speak without fear.","Learners show understanding of the story in the discussion and complete the task for their level.","Learners respond to the sound-symbol task for today (Language game: The Story Continued Slowly) at their own level.","Learners add words to the mind map and use them in sentences or a story at their level.","Each learner reads a book for 10 minutes."],"observation":["Observe each learner's reading and writing during the individual tasks; note who needs individual support and how many learners share the same difficulty.","Note any learner whose level is improving; move the learner to the next level group when you see steady progress (manual p.5).","Record each learner's progress for the day in the notebook, according to the learner's level (manual p.4).","Use today's observations to adjust tomorrow's plan (manual p.5)."],"teacherNotes":["Story selection: the manual asks teachers to use picture story books or stories in the school library. Today's suggested theme (a story about a festival of lights) is a planning suggestion; use any suitable story you have.","The manual lists the letter and word games but does not fix the slot in the daily timetable where they are used. This plan places them in the 10-minute sound-symbol / alphabet slot (interpretation).","Mind mapping topic for this day: 'clothes'. The manual's example uses the word 'shop'; today's topic follows the same method.","Pace: the manual says not to assume all learners progress at the same speed. Repeat a day's activity with the groups that need it before moving on.","Special needs: give extra time and prepare materials for slower learners; seat learners with hearing or vision difficulty at the front; for learners who reverse or confuse letters, trace letters on the letter card with a finger and write with dots to trace with a pencil (manual p.6)."],"components":[{"no":1,"key":"warmup","name":"Warm-up activities","keywords":["Alphabet song (last-letter word chain)","two learners lead"],"rows":[1]},{"no":2,"key":"oral","name":"Oral Discussion","keywords":["What did you see on your way?","every learner speaks"],"rows":[2]},{"no":3,"key":"story","name":"Story","keywords":["Day 1","title / picture talk","read aloud with expression","logical questions","re-read pointing","group reading","level tasks"],"rows":[3,4,5]},{"no":4,"key":"sound","name":"Sound symbol games, Sound separation-pairing","keywords":["The Story Continued Slowly","play in turns","level support"],"rows":[6]},{"no":5,"key":"mindwrite","name":"Mind Mapping (Day 1)","keywords":["mind map: clothes","classify the words","level task: circle letter A / sentences / story"],"rows":[7,8,9]},{"no":6,"key":"reading","name":"Daily reading","keywords":["library book","read alone","teacher listens"],"rows":[10]}],"preLesson":null},{"programme":"TARL Literacy","id":"lit-064","day":64,"phase":2,"phaseLabel":"Phase 2 (Days 46-90)","title":"Story: a story about a festival of lights (Day 2)","dayType":"Story Day 2 + Self-writing","focus":"Language game: Making Stories out of Words | Self-writing: a visit to the doctor","duration":70,"objectives":["Listen, speak and answer in the oral conversation (familiar topic).","Retell the story, read it with expression, ask and answer questions about it and write answers.","Develop sound-symbol skills: Language game: Making Stories out of Words.","Write about a topic at their own level and review the writing (a visit to the doctor).","Read independently for 10 minutes every day."],"sequence":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Handkerchief game","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Learners sit in a circle and clap while singing a rhyme ('I saw a Little Bird'). One learner runs outside the circle with a handkerchief and secretly places it behind another learner, who must chase the runner. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Sit in a circle, clap and sing; run, place the handkerchief or chase as the game requires.","tlm":"A handkerchief","source":"M","ref":"p.8","n":1},{"activity":"Oral conversation: familiar topic","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Hold a conversation on the topic 'my favourite colour and things that have that colour'. Give each learner a chance to speak; be patient with learners who need extra time.","learners":"Talk about the topic and listen to others.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.9","n":2},{"activity":"Story (Day 2 of the story): retelling","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":6,"teacher":"Ask learners to retell yesterday's story in their own words. Prompt with questions on the beginning, middle and end.","learners":"Retell the story using their own words.","tlm":"The same story book as yesterday","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":3},{"activity":"Story: reading with actions and group questions","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":9,"teacher":"Learners practise reading with actions and expressions; one learner per group reads aloud to the class. Guide groups to make questions about the story (guide initially). Groups take turns to ask and answer each other's questions. Word-level learners also read aloud the consonants learned on the first day.","learners":"Read with actions; make questions (word-level learners help write them); ask and answer questions with another group.","tlm":"Story book, slate or paper for questions","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":4},{"activity":"Story: writing answers individually","grouping":"Individual","minutes":5,"teacher":"Para and Story level learners write answers to all questions individually; read and correct their responses after they finish.","learners":"Write the answers in their notebooks; Beginner/Letter/Word learners read or listen and answer orally.","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":5},{"activity":"Language game: Making Stories out of Words","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Learners are given five words and make a short story using all of them. Observe each learner and give help where needed.","learners":"Play the game, take turns and read or say the words they make.","tlm":"Five words on the board","source":"M","ref":"p.21","n":6},{"activity":"Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on a visit to the doctor","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Start a conversation about a situation: 'a visit to the doctor'. Involve all learners and ask open-ended questions.","learners":"Take part in the discussion and share thoughts freely.","tlm":"Picture card or topic on the board","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":7},{"activity":"Self-writing: individual writing","grouping":"Individual","minutes":7,"teacher":"Give each level its task (see level table). Let learners take ownership of what they draw and write; mistakes are fine.","learners":"Draw and write about the topic at their level.","tlm":"Notebooks, crayons or pencils","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":8},{"activity":"Self-writing: review and reading back","grouping":"Individual","minutes":3,"teacher":"Ask each learner 'What did you draw or write?' and have them read it aloud once. Word-level learners read to the group; discuss spelling, punctuation and sentence structure. Help beginners by writing their text in the notebook for them if needed.","learners":"Read what they wrote; correct mistakes after listening to their own reading.","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":9},{"activity":"Daily reading (10 minutes)","grouping":"Individual","minutes":10,"teacher":"Give each learner a library book or any storybook. Move around, listen to individual readers and note their level.","learners":"Read independently a book of their choice.","tlm":"Library books or storybooks","source":"M","ref":"p.7","n":10}],"procedures":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Handkerchief game","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","steps":[{"teacher":"Seat the learners in a circle and start clapping and singing the rhyme 'I saw a Little Bird'.","learners":"Clap and sing together."},{"teacher":"One learner runs outside the circle holding a handkerchief and secretly places it behind another learner.","learners":"Everyone keeps clapping; the learner who finds the handkerchief behind them takes it and chases the runner."},{"teacher":"If the runner sits in the chaser's place before being caught, they stay in the game; if caught, they are out. Continue in this way.","learners":"Play fairly and take turns."}]},{"activity":"Oral conversation: familiar topic","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.9","steps":[{"teacher":"Introduce the topic: 'my favourite colour and things that have that colour'.","learners":"Think about their own experience."},{"teacher":"Ask open questions; give every learner a chance. Involve learners who speak less.","learners":"Speak freely and without fear."},{"teacher":"Praise efforts and sum up.","learners":"Listen and respect each other's ideas."}]},{"activity":"Story - Day 2 (a story about a festival of lights)","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.11","steps":[{"teacher":"Ask learners to retell the story they read yesterday in their own words.","learners":"Retell, helping each other remember."},{"teacher":"In small groups learners practise reading the story using actions and expressions; one learner from each group then reads aloud to the class.","learners":"Read with actions and expression; a representative reads aloud."},{"teacher":"Guide the groups to come up with questions about the story (guide initially). Word-level learners can support by helping write them down.","learners":"Make questions together."},{"teacher":"Groups take turns to ask and answer each other's questions. Useful kinds: questions whose answer is not in the text; questions needing thinking beyond the text; questions asking for an opinion.","learners":"Ask, answer and discuss in the groups."},{"teacher":"Word-level learners also read aloud the consonants they learned on the first day.","learners":"Read the consonant clusters aloud."}]},{"activity":"Language game: Making Stories out of Words","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.21","steps":[{"teacher":"Give the learners five words, for example Lion, Sugarcane, Rope, Rabbit, Tree.","learners":"Read the five words."},{"teacher":"Ask them to create a short story that uses all the words.","learners":"Discuss, then tell or write a story with all five words."},{"teacher":"Let learners read or tell their stories to the group.","learners":"Share the story."}]},{"activity":"Self-writing: 'Discussion, Writing, Self-review'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.15","steps":[{"teacher":"Start a conversation about a situation: 'a visit to the doctor'. Involve all learners and ask open-ended questions.","learners":"Discuss and answer questions."},{"teacher":"Give writing time at each level: draw then write (Beginner), write about what they liked (Letter), a sentence (Word), a paragraph or story on a topic of their choice (Para/Story).","learners":"Write at their level and take ownership of the work."},{"teacher":"Review: ask 'What did you draw or write?' Have each learner read the text aloud once. Support with writing if needed.","learners":"Read aloud, listen to their pronunciation and correct mistakes."}]}],"levelTasks":[{"activity":"Story - Day 2: level-wise tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.11","tasks":{"Beginner":"Retell with the group by pointing to pictures or words; read aloud with group support (interpretation of the manual's group reading task).","Letter":"Read with the group, pointing to words; say the letters and words they know (interpretation of the manual's group reading task).","Word":"Support the group in writing the questions; read aloud the consonant clusters learned on the first day.","Para":"Ask the group's questions to another group, discuss them, then write answers to all questions individually; the teacher reads and corrects.","Story":"Ask the group's questions to another group, discuss them, then write answers to all questions individually; the teacher reads and corrects."}},{"activity":"Language game: Making Stories out of Words - level support","source":"I","ref":"p.21","tasks":{"Beginner":"Take part by saying or pointing to the letters involved and by listening carefully; Para and Story level partners help.","Letter":"Say the letters/sounds and give simple words they know.","Word":"Say and write words and short sentences for the game.","Para":"Write sentences with the words; help groups to record answers.","Story":"Write sentences or short stories with the words; help groups to record answers."}},{"activity":"Self-writing: level tasks and review","source":"M","ref":"p.15","tasks":{"Beginner":"Draw a picture about the discussion and then write a few sentences about it, expressing thoughts freely. Review: say what they drew or wrote; read the text aloud once; the teacher may write the text in the notebook for them.","Letter":"Write about what they liked, using drawing and writing; write any words or sentences they can. Review: read the text aloud once; correct punctuation mistakes using the Barakhadi chart.","Word":"Write a sentence based on the conversation. Mistakes in spelling, punctuation and sentence structure are fine. Review: read it to the group; discuss and correct mistakes together.","Para":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation.","Story":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation."}}],"organisation":[{"grouping":"Whole class (big group)","how":"All learners of all levels sit in a 'U' shape arranged by level (Beginner, Letter, Word, Para, Story) so that the move to small groups is easy.","activities":["Warm-up: Handkerchief game","Oral conversation: familiar topic","Story (Day 2 of the story): retelling","Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on a visit to the doctor"]},{"grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","how":"Learners of similar levels work together; the teacher gives each group a task for its level and spends more time with learners who need support. Rotate responsibilities (for example group leader).","activities":["Story: reading with actions and group questions","Language game: Making Stories out of Words"]},{"grouping":"Individual","how":"Each learner works on a task for their own level; the teacher moves around, observes difficulties and supports individuals.","activities":["Story: writing answers individually","Self-writing: individual writing","Self-writing: review and reading back","Daily reading (10 minutes)"]}],"materials":["A handkerchief","The same story book as yesterday","Story book","slate or paper for questions","Notebooks","Five words on the board","Picture card or topic on the board","crayons or pencils","Library books or storybooks"],"outcomes":["Learners take part in the oral conversation and speak without fear.","Learners retell the story, read with expression and ask or answer questions at their level.","Learners respond to the sound-symbol task for today (Language game: Making Stories out of Words) at their own level.","Learners write about the topic at their level and read it aloud.","Each learner reads a book for 10 minutes."],"observation":["Observe each learner's reading and writing during the individual tasks; note who needs individual support and how many learners share the same difficulty.","Note any learner whose level is improving; move the learner to the next level group when you see steady progress (manual p.5).","Record each learner's progress for the day in the notebook, according to the learner's level (manual p.4).","Use today's observations to adjust tomorrow's plan (manual p.5)."],"teacherNotes":["Questions to elicit on Day 2: information questions (answer not in the text), thinking questions (needs knowledge beyond the text) and opinion questions (feedback on something in the text).","The manual lists the letter and word games but does not fix the slot in the daily timetable where they are used. This plan places them in the 10-minute sound-symbol / alphabet slot (interpretation).","Writing has two parts, content and sequence: encourage learners to read what they wrote, improve it and rewrite it for clarity and correctness (manual p.15).","Pace: the manual says not to assume all learners progress at the same speed. Repeat a day's activity with the groups that need it before moving on.","Special needs: give extra time and prepare materials for slower learners; seat learners with hearing or vision difficulty at the front; for learners who reverse or confuse letters, trace letters on the letter card with a finger and write with dots to trace with a pencil (manual p.6)."],"components":[{"no":1,"key":"warmup","name":"Warm-up activities","keywords":["Handkerchief game","two learners lead"],"rows":[1]},{"no":2,"key":"oral","name":"Oral Discussion","keywords":["familiar topic","every learner speaks"],"rows":[2]},{"no":3,"key":"story","name":"Story","keywords":["Day 2","retell","read with actions","group questions","ask and answer","write answers (Para/Story)"],"rows":[3,4,5]},{"no":4,"key":"sound","name":"Sound symbol games, Sound separation-pairing","keywords":["Making Stories out of Words","play in turns","level support"],"rows":[6]},{"no":5,"key":"mindwrite","name":"Individual-Writing (Day 2)","keywords":["discussion","write at own level","self-review (read aloud)"],"rows":[7,8,9]},{"no":6,"key":"reading","name":"Daily reading","keywords":["library book","read alone","teacher listens"],"rows":[10]}],"preLesson":null},{"programme":"TARL Literacy","id":"lit-065","day":65,"phase":2,"phaseLabel":"Phase 2 (Days 46-90)","title":"Story: a story about a talking animal (Day 1)","dayType":"Story Day 1 + Mind mapping","focus":"Barakhadi / alphabet and phonics chart (line 3, letter 'h') | Mind map: vegetables","duration":70,"objectives":["Listen, speak and answer in the oral conversation (conversation on a picture).","Listen to and read a story with understanding; discuss it in big and small groups and respond at their own level.","Develop sound-symbol skills: Barakhadi / alphabet and phonics chart (line 3, letter 'h').","Build vocabulary through a mind map ('vegetables') and use the words at their own level.","Read independently for 10 minutes every day."],"sequence":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Rhyme - 'I caught a Fish Alive'","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Say the rhyme with actions, then say it together. Lines: One, two, three, four, five, once I caught a fish alive. / Six, seven, eight, nine, ten, then I let it go again. / Why did you let it go? Because it bit my finger so. / Which finger did it bite? This little finger on my right. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Listen, then say the rhyme with actions.","tlm":"Rhyme chart or board (optional)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","n":1},{"activity":"Oral conversation: conversation on a picture","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Show a picture of a flood-hit village and ask what is happening, who is doing what and what is happening around them. Let learners think creatively and even make up a story.","learners":"Look at the picture, answer questions and make up their own story about it.","tlm":"Picture card of a flood-hit village","source":"M","ref":"p.9","n":2},{"activity":"Story (Day 1 of the story): reading aloud and discussion","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":8,"teacher":"Discuss the title or picture of the story with the learners. Read the story aloud with expression and voice modulation (learners do not repeat after you). Discuss it, with emphasis on vocabulary-based questions. Read it again slowly, pointing to each word.","learners":"Talk about the title/picture; listen; answer questions; follow each word with a finger in their own copy.","tlm":"A story from the school library (a story about a talking animal), a copy for each learner","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":3},{"activity":"Story: reading in small groups","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":7,"teacher":"Form level-wise groups with a group leader. Learners read the story one sentence at a time while the others follow with their fingers. Para and Story level learners practise reading with emotion and expression.","learners":"Read the story sentence by sentence, supporting each other; the group leader helps.","tlm":"Story book copies","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":4},{"activity":"Story: level-wise individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":5,"teacher":"Give each learner the task for their level (see level table) and support those who need it.","learners":"Beginner/Letter: find and write favourite words or letters. Word: find consonant clusters. Para/Story: silently read, find unfamiliar and rhyming words.","tlm":"Story book, notebooks, board","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":5},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart: big group reading","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":3,"teacher":"Show the Barakhadi chart and ask which letter they like. Read the letter 'h' on the chart; learners listen carefully and point to it on their own chart (they do not repeat after you).","learners":"Listen and point to the letter on their own chart.","tlm":"Barakhadi chart, alphabet or phonics chart","source":"M","ref":"p.13","n":6},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart: small-group practice","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Learners practise reading the alphabet or phonics chart in groups and help each other. One learner per group reads aloud. Occasionally ask learners to identify the sounds of letters. Give each level its group task.","learners":"Read the chart in groups; one learner reads aloud; do the level task.","tlm":"Alphabet or phonics chart, board or floor","source":"M","ref":"p.13","n":7},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart: individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":2,"teacher":"Give each learner an individual task for their level and observe closely; assist any learner who needs individual support.","learners":"Say and write a letter or word, a sentence or a short paragraph (by level).","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.13","n":8},{"activity":"Mind mapping (Day 1): the word 'vegetables'","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Ask: 'What words come to your mind when you hear the word vegetables?' Write learners' answers on the board or floor (Para and Story level learners write the words themselves). Guide the map towards the learning objective. Example words: potato, carrot, radish, onion, brinjal, tomato, beans, pumpkin, spinach, cabbage, coriander, mint.","learners":"Say words connected with 'vegetables'; share the meaning and feeling of words.","tlm":"Board, chalk (or floor)","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":9},{"activity":"Mind mapping: classify the words","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":4,"teacher":"Ask learners to classify the words in groups, for example: Under the ground: potato, carrot, radish, onion; On plants: brinjal, tomato, beans, pumpkin; Leafy: spinach, cabbage, coriander, mint.","learners":"Sort the words into groups and say why.","tlm":"Board, chalk, word cards (optional)","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":10},{"activity":"Mind mapping: level-wise individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":6,"teacher":"Give each learner the individual task for their level; observe closely and give individual support. Display corrected stories on the wall.","learners":"Complete the task for their level (see level table).","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":11},{"activity":"Daily reading (10 minutes)","grouping":"Individual","minutes":10,"teacher":"Give each learner a library book or any storybook. Move around, listen to individual readers and note their level.","learners":"Read independently a book of their choice.","tlm":"Library books or storybooks","source":"M","ref":"p.7","n":12}],"procedures":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Rhyme - 'I caught a Fish Alive'","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","steps":[{"teacher":"Say the rhyme 'I caught a Fish Alive' slowly with actions: One, two, three, four, five, once I caught a fish alive. / Six, seven, eight, nine, ten, then I let it go again. / Why did you let it go? Because it bit my finger so. / Which finger did it bite? This little finger on my right.","learners":"Listen and watch the actions."},{"teacher":"Say it again; invite learners to join with actions.","learners":"Say the rhyme together with actions."},{"teacher":"Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Choose a rhyme they like and lead."}]},{"activity":"Oral conversation: conversation on a picture","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.9","steps":[{"teacher":"Show the picture of a flood-hit village.","learners":"Look carefully."},{"teacher":"Ask: What is happening in the picture? Who is doing what? What is happening around them? Then: What might happen next?","learners":"Answer in their own words; every learner gets a chance."},{"teacher":"Let learners imagine and make up a short story from the picture.","learners":"Tell their stories to the class."}]},{"activity":"Story - Day 1 (a story about a talking animal)","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.10","steps":[{"teacher":"Discuss the title or picture of the story with the learners.","learners":"Talk about what they see and what the story may be about."},{"teacher":"Read the story aloud with expression and proper voice modulation. Learners should not simply repeat after you.","learners":"Listen carefully and enjoy the story."},{"teacher":"Discuss the story: factual, logical, vocabulary-based, judgment or opinion questions (today's focus: vocabulary-based: What does this word mean? Which word in the story means the same as ...?). Begin in the home language if needed.","learners":"Think and respond thoughtfully; every learner takes part."},{"teacher":"Read the story again slowly, pointing to each word. Make sure each learner has a copy and follows with a finger.","learners":"Follow each word with their finger."},{"teacher":"Ask learners to read in small groups; select a group leader who helps the others. Learners read one sentence at a time while the others point with fingers.","learners":"Read with the help of one another."}]},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart activity (line 3)","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Small group (level-wise) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.13","steps":[{"teacher":"Show the Barakhadi chart and ask the learners which letter they like. Where is the letter 'h'?","learners":"Look for the letter on the chart."},{"teacher":"Read the letter 'h' on the chart. Learners listen and point to it on their own chart. Make sure they do not repeat after you.","learners":"Listen and point to the letter."},{"teacher":"Learners read the alphabet or phonics chart in their groups and help each other; one learner from each group comes forward to read aloud.","learners":"Read in groups; the representative reads aloud."},{"teacher":"Occasionally ask them to identify the sounds of letters from the chart.","learners":"Say the sound of the letter you point to."},{"teacher":"As an extra activity, write some letters on the floor, call out each letter one by one and let the learners jump onto the correct letter.","learners":"Jump onto the letter that is called."}]},{"activity":"Mind mapping: 'vegetables'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Small group (level-wise) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.14","steps":[{"teacher":"Choose a word that can generate many related words: 'vegetables'. Ask: 'What words come to your mind when you hear the word vegetables?' Write the answers on the board or floor.","learners":"Say words they link with 'vegetables'."},{"teacher":"Discuss the words: what they mean and how they are connected.","learners":"Explain their words and listen to others."},{"teacher":"In small groups, let the learners classify the words (Under the ground: potato, carrot, radish, onion; On plants: brinjal, tomato, beans, pumpkin; Leafy: spinach, cabbage, coriander, mint).","learners":"Sort the words into groups."},{"teacher":"Give the individual tasks by level and help each learner.","learners":"Work individually; read the work aloud at the end if time allows."}]}],"levelTasks":[{"activity":"Story - Day 1: individual tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.10","tasks":{"Beginner":"Circle or search for a favourite word or letter in the story and say it aloud. If a learner cannot draw a circle, write words on the board and ask them to identify them.","Letter":"Find, read and write favourite words from the story.","Word":"Find the consonant clusters in the story, read them and write them in the notebook.","Para":"Silently read the story from the textbook; find unfamiliar words and try to understand them; find rhyming words, use them in sentences and write in the notebook; ask other groups for meanings; make questions in groups.","Story":"Silently read the story; find unfamiliar words and rhyming words; practise reading with emotion; one group reads sentences formed with consonant clusters to the other group; ask and answer group questions (information, thinking and opinion questions)."}},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart: level tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.13","tasks":{"Beginner":"Small group: read the chart in the group; find and write favourite letters from the line. Individual: say and write a letter of their choice.","Letter":"Small group: read the chart; find and write favourite letters or words from any line. Individual: say a word on their own that begins with any letter.","Word":"Small group: write one or two lines of letters on the board or floor and use them to form words. Individual: speak and write sentences using words they know.","Para":"Small group: prepare word lists using the Barakhadi chart (for example items found in a shop or in the kitchen). Individual: write short paragraphs using the words formed with the Barakhadi chart.","Story":"Small group: prepare word lists using the Barakhadi chart. Individual: write short paragraphs using the words formed with the Barakhadi chart."}},{"activity":"Mind mapping 'vegetables': level tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.14","tasks":{"Beginner":"Circle all the words that contain the letter 'A' on the board; make a list. See how many learners find the most words.","Letter":"Circle all the words that contain the letter 'A' and make a list of them.","Word":"Use 4-5 words (for example mint, beans, onion, carrot, potato) to form sentences, starting with words of one or two syllables. Example: Dream - I had a dream last night.","Para":"Choose any five words from the map and create a story with them. Use consonant clusters correctly, read the story aloud, correct mistakes of sentence structure, spelling or grammar, then display it on the wall.","Story":"Choose any five words from the map and create a story with them. Use consonant clusters correctly, read the story aloud, correct mistakes of sentence structure, spelling or grammar, then display it on the wall."}}],"organisation":[{"grouping":"Whole class (big group)","how":"All learners of all levels sit in a 'U' shape arranged by level (Beginner, Letter, Word, Para, Story) so that the move to small groups is easy.","activities":["Warm-up: Rhyme - 'I caught a Fish Alive'","Oral conversation: conversation on a picture","Story (Day 1 of the story): reading aloud and discussion","Barakhadi chart: big group reading","Mind mapping (Day 1): the word 'vegetables'"]},{"grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","how":"Learners of similar levels work together; the teacher gives each group a task for its level and spends more time with learners who need support. Rotate responsibilities (for example group leader).","activities":["Story: reading in small groups","Barakhadi chart: small-group practice","Mind mapping: classify the words"]},{"grouping":"Individual","how":"Each learner works on a task for their own level; the teacher moves around, observes difficulties and supports individuals.","activities":["Story: level-wise individual tasks","Barakhadi chart: individual tasks","Mind mapping: level-wise individual tasks","Daily reading (10 minutes)"]}],"materials":["Rhyme chart or board (optional)","Picture card of a flood-hit village","A story from the school library (a story about a talking animal)","a copy for each learner","Story book copies","Story book","notebooks","board","Barakhadi chart","alphabet or phonics chart","Alphabet or phonics chart","board or floor","Notebooks","Board","chalk (or floor)","chalk","word cards (optional)","Library books or storybooks"],"outcomes":["Learners take part in the oral conversation and speak without fear.","Learners show understanding of the story in the discussion and complete the task for their level.","Learners respond to the sound-symbol task for today (Barakhadi / alphabet and phonics chart (line 3, letter 'h')) at their own level.","Learners add words to the mind map and use them in sentences or a story at their level.","Each learner reads a book for 10 minutes."],"observation":["Observe each learner's reading and writing during the individual tasks; note who needs individual support and how many learners share the same difficulty.","Note any learner whose level is improving; move the learner to the next level group when you see steady progress (manual p.5).","Record each learner's progress for the day in the notebook, according to the learner's level (manual p.4).","Use today's observations to adjust tomorrow's plan (manual p.5)."],"teacherNotes":["Story selection: the manual asks teachers to use picture story books or stories in the school library. Today's suggested theme (a story about a talking animal) is a planning suggestion; use any suitable story you have.","Barakhadi: learners who need extra time should get repeated practice using one or two sound units at a time. Topic-based discussion helps oral expression, thinking and understanding.","Mind mapping topic for this day: 'vegetables'. The manual's example uses the word 'shop'; today's topic follows the same method.","Level check: if learners have moved up to a new level, celebrate with an appreciation-oriented game (letter level to word level): 'Which one are you?' or 'Matching words with pictures' (manual p.42-45). Teachers may use such activities on their own.","Pace: the manual says not to assume all learners progress at the same speed. Repeat a day's activity with the groups that need it before moving on.","Special needs: give extra time and prepare materials for slower learners; seat learners with hearing or vision difficulty at the front; for learners who reverse or confuse letters, trace letters on the letter card with a finger and write with dots to trace with a pencil (manual p.6)."],"components":[{"no":1,"key":"warmup","name":"Warm-up activities","keywords":["Rhyme - 'I caught a Fish Alive'","two learners lead"],"rows":[1]},{"no":2,"key":"oral","name":"Oral Discussion","keywords":["conversation on a picture","every learner speaks"],"rows":[2]},{"no":3,"key":"story","name":"Story","keywords":["Day 1","title / picture talk","read aloud with expression","vocabulary-based questions","re-read pointing","group reading","level tasks"],"rows":[3,4,5]},{"no":4,"key":"sound","name":"Sound symbol games, Sound separation-pairing","keywords":["Barakhadi / alphabet chart","listen and point (no repeating)","group reading","level tasks"],"rows":[6,7,8]},{"no":5,"key":"mindwrite","name":"Mind Mapping (Day 1)","keywords":["mind map: vegetables","classify the words","level task: circle letter A / sentences / story"],"rows":[9,10,11]},{"no":6,"key":"reading","name":"Daily reading","keywords":["library book","read alone","teacher listens"],"rows":[12]}],"preLesson":null},{"programme":"TARL Literacy","id":"lit-066","day":66,"phase":2,"phaseLabel":"Phase 2 (Days 46-90)","title":"Saturday: drama presentation","dayType":"Saturday drama + Self-writing","focus":"Consonant clusters: shr (shrimp, shrink) | Self-writing: the story we acted out (a story about a talking animal)","duration":70,"objectives":["Listen, speak and answer in the oral conversation (listening and storytelling).","Express a story through role play, using voice, facial expressions and gestures.","Develop sound-symbol skills: Consonant clusters: shr (shrimp, shrink).","Write about the story and review the writing.","Read independently for 10 minutes every day."],"sequence":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Singing and Spinning","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Learners sit in a circle and pass a small object while you clap with your back turned; when the clapping stops, the learner holding it sings a song, recites a poem or tells a joke. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Pass the object round the circle; sing, recite or tell a joke when the clapping stops.","tlm":"A small object (chalk or pencil)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","n":1},{"activity":"Oral conversation: listening and storytelling","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Tell an interesting story starter and involve the learners: 'The wind took my hat and carried it over the hills. Who found it?' Let learners imagine and continue the story.","learners":"Listen to the teacher, then imagine and continue the story. Learners can also recite a rhyme or story they know.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.9","n":2},{"activity":"Dramatic presentation: introduction and reading","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Explain what a dramatic presentation is and how it is done. Provide stories discussed during the week and read one aloud once more. Para and Story level learners support Beginner and Letter level learners in reading.","learners":"Listen, read along, then each learner chooses a character.","tlm":"Stories discussed in the week (a story about a festival of lights; a story about a talking animal)","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":3},{"activity":"Dramatic presentation: planning in small groups","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":8,"teacher":"Each group discusses and plans dialogues; Para or Story level learners write the dialogues. Groups prepare their dramatic presentation.","learners":"Choose characters, plan and rehearse dialogues with facial expressions and gestures.","tlm":"Story, paper for dialogues","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":4},{"activity":"Dramatic presentation: performances and feedback","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":7,"teacher":"Learners sit in a U shape. Each group presents; after each performance, watching learners say what they enjoyed and what could be improved.","learners":"Perform in turn; watch; give feedback.","tlm":"Open space (U-shape seating)","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":5},{"activity":"Consonant clusters: introduction","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":4,"teacher":"Three-letter clusters: after two-letter clusters, familiarise learners with clusters of three letters ('shr' as in shrimp, shrink, shrub). Discuss the words, then ask learners to tell and write sentences using them.","learners":"Listen, pronounce the cluster and say words that contain it.","tlm":"Board and chalk, words list (shrimp shrink shrub shrug shred)","source":"M","ref":"p.16","n":6},{"activity":"Consonant cluster game: Who is Whose Friend?","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":6,"teacher":"Prepare cards: some with broken parts of conjunct consonants (b + l, c + r, s + t) and some with the full form (bl as in black, cr as in crab, st as in star). Take out all the cards. Observe closely and help learners who need support.","learners":"Match each full form with its broken parts and discover 'who is whose friend'.","tlm":"Broken-part cards and full-form cards","source":"M","ref":"p.17","n":7},{"activity":"Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on the story we acted out (a story about a talking animal)","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Start a conversation about the story used for the drama: 'the story we acted out (a story about a talking animal)'. Involve all learners with open-ended questions.","learners":"Take part in the discussion and share thoughts freely.","tlm":"Picture card or topic on the board","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":8},{"activity":"Self-writing: individual writing","grouping":"Individual","minutes":7,"teacher":"Give each level its task (see level table). Let learners take ownership of what they draw and write; mistakes are fine.","learners":"Draw and write about the topic at their level.","tlm":"Notebooks, crayons or pencils","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":9},{"activity":"Self-writing: review and reading back","grouping":"Individual","minutes":3,"teacher":"Ask each learner 'What did you draw or write?' and have them read it aloud once. Word-level learners read to the group; discuss spelling, punctuation and sentence structure. Help beginners by writing their text in the notebook for them if needed.","learners":"Read what they wrote; correct mistakes after listening to their own reading.","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":10},{"activity":"Daily reading (10 minutes)","grouping":"Individual","minutes":10,"teacher":"Give each learner a library book or any storybook. Move around, listen to individual readers and note their level.","learners":"Read independently a book of their choice.","tlm":"Library books or storybooks","source":"M","ref":"p.7","n":11}],"procedures":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Singing and Spinning","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","steps":[{"teacher":"Seat the learners in a circle; give a small object to one learner.","learners":"Sit in a circle."},{"teacher":"Stand outside the circle with your back to them and clap steadily; they pass the object.","learners":"Pass the object while the clapping continues."},{"teacher":"Stop clapping; the learner holding the object sings, recites or tells a joke.","learners":"Perform, and everybody claps."}]},{"activity":"Oral conversation: listening and storytelling","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.9","steps":[{"teacher":"Say the starter: 'The wind took my hat and carried it over the hills. Who found it?'","learners":"Listen and imagine."},{"teacher":"Ask learners to continue the story one by one. Encourage those who speak less.","learners":"Add ideas to the story."},{"teacher":"Invite a learner to recite a poem or rhyme they know.","learners":"Recite and listen to others."}]},{"activity":"Saturday special: dramatic presentation","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.11","steps":[{"teacher":"Explain what a dramatic presentation is and how it can be done. Give the groups the stories discussed during the week.","learners":"Listen to the explanation."},{"teacher":"Read a story aloud once more. Learners at story and paragraph level support those at beginner and letter level in reading.","learners":"Read along; helpers support their friends."},{"teacher":"After reading, each learner chooses a character from the story.","learners":"Choose a role (boys may play girl roles and girls may play boy roles)."},{"teacher":"In groups, learners discuss and plan the dialogues; paragraph or story level learners write the dialogues.","learners":"Plan and write dialogues together."},{"teacher":"Learners sit in a U shape. Each group presents its drama. After each performance, ask what the audience enjoyed and what could be improved.","learners":"Perform, watch and give kind feedback."}]},{"activity":"Consonant clusters (shr) and the game 'Who is Whose Friend?'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.16-17","steps":[{"teacher":"Three-letter clusters: after two-letter clusters, familiarise learners with clusters of three letters ('shr' as in shrimp, shrink, shrub). Discuss the words, then ask learners to tell and write sentences using them.","learners":"Listen, pronounce and find words in the text."},{"teacher":"Write the words on the board: shrimp shrink shrub shrug shred. Read them aloud with distinct pronunciation of the cluster.","learners":"Read the words aloud; point to the cluster in each word."},{"teacher":"Prepare cards: some with broken parts of conjunct consonants (b + l, c + r, s + t) and some with the full form (bl as in black, cr as in crab, st as in star). Take out all the cards.","learners":"Match each full form with its broken parts and discover 'who is whose friend'."}]},{"activity":"Self-writing: 'Discussion, Writing, Self-review'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.15","steps":[{"teacher":"Start a conversation about the story used for the drama: 'the story we acted out (a story about a talking animal)'. Involve all learners with open-ended questions.","learners":"Discuss and answer questions."},{"teacher":"Give writing time at each level: draw then write (Beginner), write about what they liked (Letter), a sentence (Word), a paragraph or story on a topic of their choice (Para/Story).","learners":"Write at their level and take ownership of the work."},{"teacher":"Review: ask 'What did you draw or write?' Have each learner read the text aloud once. Support with writing if needed.","learners":"Read aloud, listen to their pronunciation and correct mistakes."}]}],"levelTasks":[{"activity":"Drama: roles by level","source":"M","ref":"p.11","tasks":{"Beginner":"Take a character role and say or act short lines with help from Para and Story level learners.","Letter":"Take a character role and say or act short lines with help from Para and Story level learners.","Word":"Take a role and speak the dialogues; help rehearse.","Para":"Write the dialogues for the group and support Beginner, Letter and Word level learners throughout.","Story":"Write the dialogues for the group and support Beginner, Letter and Word level learners throughout."}},{"activity":"Consonant clusters (shr): level tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.16-17","tasks":{"Beginner":"Listen to the sound of the cluster and point to it in a word; continue with letter-sound work (interpretation: the manual describes clusters for learners lagging in reading words and sentences).","Letter":"Listen to the cluster sound and pick words with the cluster from a word card (interpretation).","Word":"Find the cluster in the story or textbook words, read the words and write them in the notebook.","Para":"Form words and sentences using the cluster; read the sentences aloud.","Story":"Form words and sentences using the cluster; read the sentences aloud; use them in the story writing."}},{"activity":"Self-writing: level tasks and review","source":"M","ref":"p.15","tasks":{"Beginner":"Draw a picture about the discussion and then write a few sentences about it, expressing thoughts freely. Review: say what they drew or wrote; read the text aloud once; the teacher may write the text in the notebook for them.","Letter":"Write about what they liked, using drawing and writing; write any words or sentences they can. Review: read the text aloud once; correct punctuation mistakes using the Barakhadi chart.","Word":"Write a sentence based on the conversation. Mistakes in spelling, punctuation and sentence structure are fine. Review: read it to the group; discuss and correct mistakes together.","Para":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation.","Story":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation."}}],"organisation":[{"grouping":"Whole class (big group)","how":"All learners of all levels sit in a 'U' shape arranged by level (Beginner, Letter, Word, Para, Story) so that the move to small groups is easy.","activities":["Warm-up: Singing and Spinning","Oral conversation: listening and storytelling","Dramatic presentation: introduction and reading","Dramatic presentation: performances and feedback","Consonant clusters: introduction","Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on the story we acted out (a story about a talking animal)"]},{"grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","how":"Learners of similar levels work together; the teacher gives each group a task for its level and spends more time with learners who need support. Rotate responsibilities (for example group leader).","activities":["Dramatic presentation: planning in small groups","Consonant cluster game: Who is Whose Friend?"]},{"grouping":"Individual","how":"Each learner works on a task for their own level; the teacher moves around, observes difficulties and supports individuals.","activities":["Self-writing: individual writing","Self-writing: review and reading back","Daily reading (10 minutes)"]}],"materials":["A small object (chalk or pencil)","Stories discussed in the week (a story about a festival of lights; a story about a talking animal)","Story","paper for dialogues","Open space (U-shape seating)","Board","chalk","words list (shrimp shrink shrub shrug shred)","Broken-part cards","full-form cards","Picture card or topic on the board","Notebooks","crayons or pencils","Library books or storybooks"],"outcomes":["Learners take part in the oral conversation and speak without fear.","Learners present a role in the group drama and give feedback to others.","Learners respond to the sound-symbol task for today (Consonant clusters: shr (shrimp, shrink)) at their own level.","Learners write about the story at their level and read it aloud.","Each learner reads a book for 10 minutes."],"observation":["Observe each learner's reading and writing during the individual tasks; note who needs individual support and how many learners share the same difficulty.","Note any learner whose level is improving; move the learner to the next level group when you see steady progress (manual p.5).","Record each learner's progress for the day in the notebook, according to the learner's level (manual p.4).","Use today's observations to adjust tomorrow's plan (manual p.5)."],"teacherNotes":["Saturday: this plan assumes Day 1 is a Monday (six teaching days per week). If your school week is different, hold the drama presentation on your Saturday and keep the other days in sequence.","Consonant clusters: do these activities daily for learners who find reading complex words hard; the aim is to remove the fear of reading clusters. Teachers may carry out similar activities on their own.","Writing has two parts, content and sequence: encourage learners to read what they wrote, improve it and rewrite it for clarity and correctness (manual p.15).","Pace: the manual says not to assume all learners progress at the same speed. Repeat a day's activity with the groups that need it before moving on.","Special needs: give extra time and prepare materials for slower learners; seat learners with hearing or vision difficulty at the front; for learners who reverse or confuse letters, trace letters on the letter card with a finger and write with dots to trace with a pencil (manual p.6)."],"components":[{"no":1,"key":"warmup","name":"Warm-up activities","keywords":["Singing and Spinning","two learners lead"],"rows":[1]},{"no":2,"key":"oral","name":"Oral Discussion","keywords":["listening and storytelling","every learner speaks"],"rows":[2]},{"no":3,"key":"story","name":"Story (Saturday: dramatic presentation)","keywords":["Saturday drama","choose a character","plan dialogues","perform in U shape","feedback"],"rows":[3,4,5]},{"no":4,"key":"sound","name":"Sound symbol games, Sound separation-pairing","keywords":["consonant cluster 'shr'","pronounce and find words","game: Who is Whose Friend?"],"rows":[6,7]},{"no":5,"key":"mindwrite","name":"Individual-Writing (Day 2)","keywords":["discussion","write at own level","self-review (read aloud)"],"rows":[8,9,10]},{"no":6,"key":"reading","name":"Daily reading","keywords":["library book","read alone","teacher listens"],"rows":[11]}],"preLesson":null},{"programme":"TARL Literacy","id":"lit-067","day":67,"phase":2,"phaseLabel":"Phase 2 (Days 46-90)","title":"Story: a story about a talking animal (Day 2)","dayType":"Story Day 2 + Self-writing","focus":"Language game: Tell Me in a Minute | Self-writing: what I saw on my way to school","duration":70,"objectives":["Listen, speak and answer in the oral conversation (What did you see on your way?).","Retell the story, read it with expression, ask and answer questions about it and write answers.","Develop sound-symbol skills: Language game: Tell Me in a Minute.","Write about a topic at their own level and review the writing (what I saw on my way to school).","Read independently for 10 minutes every day."],"sequence":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Rain clapping","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Everyone stands in a circle with eyes closed and keeps clapping: first one finger, then two, three, four and finally five fingers. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Stand in a circle, close the eyes and clap with 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 fingers.","tlm":"After the activity ask: What does the rain do to the fields?","source":"M","ref":"p.8","n":1},{"activity":"Oral conversation: What did you see on your way?","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Ask learners to describe what they saw on their way to school. If they are hesitant, begin yourself: 'When I arrived today, I saw two cats chasing each other, a farmer ploughing in the field, and goats grazing on the river bank. What did you see?'","learners":"Describe what they saw on the way to school and connect with what others share.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.9","n":2},{"activity":"Story (Day 2 of the story): retelling","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":6,"teacher":"Ask learners to retell yesterday's story in their own words. Prompt with questions on the beginning, middle and end.","learners":"Retell the story using their own words.","tlm":"The same story book as yesterday","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":3},{"activity":"Story: reading with actions and group questions","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":9,"teacher":"Learners practise reading with actions and expressions; one learner per group reads aloud to the class. Guide groups to make questions about the story (guide initially). Groups take turns to ask and answer each other's questions. Word-level learners also read aloud the consonants learned on the first day.","learners":"Read with actions; make questions (word-level learners help write them); ask and answer questions with another group.","tlm":"Story book, slate or paper for questions","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":4},{"activity":"Story: writing answers individually","grouping":"Individual","minutes":5,"teacher":"Para and Story level learners write answers to all questions individually; read and correct their responses after they finish.","learners":"Write the answers in their notebooks; Beginner/Letter/Word learners read or listen and answer orally.","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":5},{"activity":"Language game: Tell Me in a Minute","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Each learner gets a familiar topic, thinks for 2-3 minutes and speaks about it for one minute. Observe each learner and give help where needed.","learners":"Play the game, take turns and read or say the words they make.","tlm":"Topic slips (optional)","source":"M","ref":"p.21","n":6},{"activity":"Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on what I saw on my way to school","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Start a conversation about a picture card: 'what I saw on my way to school'. Involve all learners and ask open-ended questions.","learners":"Take part in the discussion and share thoughts freely.","tlm":"Picture card or topic on the board","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":7},{"activity":"Self-writing: individual writing","grouping":"Individual","minutes":7,"teacher":"Give each level its task (see level table). Let learners take ownership of what they draw and write; mistakes are fine.","learners":"Draw and write about the topic at their level.","tlm":"Notebooks, crayons or pencils","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":8},{"activity":"Self-writing: review and reading back","grouping":"Individual","minutes":3,"teacher":"Ask each learner 'What did you draw or write?' and have them read it aloud once. Word-level learners read to the group; discuss spelling, punctuation and sentence structure. Help beginners by writing their text in the notebook for them if needed.","learners":"Read what they wrote; correct mistakes after listening to their own reading.","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":9},{"activity":"Daily reading (10 minutes)","grouping":"Individual","minutes":10,"teacher":"Give each learner a library book or any storybook. Move around, listen to individual readers and note their level.","learners":"Read independently a book of their choice.","tlm":"Library books or storybooks","source":"M","ref":"p.7","n":10}],"procedures":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Rain clapping","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","steps":[{"teacher":"Stand the learners in a circle and ask them to close their eyes. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Stand in a circle and close their eyes."},{"teacher":"Start clapping with one finger; then two fingers, three, four and finally five fingers.","learners":"Keep clapping, copying the change of fingers."},{"teacher":"After the activity ask: What does the rain do to the fields?","learners":"Tell how they felt and what the sounds reminded them of."}]},{"activity":"Oral conversation: What did you see on your way?","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.9","steps":[{"teacher":"Ask: 'What did you see on your way to school today?'","learners":"Think about the way to school."},{"teacher":"If learners hesitate, start: 'When I arrived today, I saw two cats chasing each other, a farmer ploughing in the field, and goats grazing on the river bank. What did you see?'","learners":"Listen to the model and then share their own observations."},{"teacher":"Connect learners' answers with each other.","learners":"Listen and add what they noticed."}]},{"activity":"Story - Day 2 (a story about a talking animal)","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.11","steps":[{"teacher":"Ask learners to retell the story they read yesterday in their own words.","learners":"Retell, helping each other remember."},{"teacher":"In small groups learners practise reading the story using actions and expressions; one learner from each group then reads aloud to the class.","learners":"Read with actions and expression; a representative reads aloud."},{"teacher":"Guide the groups to come up with questions about the story (guide initially). Word-level learners can support by helping write them down.","learners":"Make questions together."},{"teacher":"Groups take turns to ask and answer each other's questions. Useful kinds: questions whose answer is not in the text; questions needing thinking beyond the text; questions asking for an opinion.","learners":"Ask, answer and discuss in the groups."},{"teacher":"Word-level learners also read aloud the consonants they learned on the first day.","learners":"Read the consonant clusters aloud."}]},{"activity":"Language game: Tell Me in a Minute","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.21","steps":[{"teacher":"Give each learner a different familiar topic. Learners can also choose their own topic.","learners":"Choose or receive a topic."},{"teacher":"Give them 2-3 minutes to think about the topic.","learners":"Think about what to say."},{"teacher":"Encourage each learner to speak about it for one minute.","learners":"Speak for one minute; others listen."}]},{"activity":"Self-writing: 'Discussion, Writing, Self-review'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.15","steps":[{"teacher":"Start a conversation about a picture card: 'what I saw on my way to school'. Involve all learners and ask open-ended questions.","learners":"Discuss and answer questions."},{"teacher":"Give writing time at each level: draw then write (Beginner), write about what they liked (Letter), a sentence (Word), a paragraph or story on a topic of their choice (Para/Story).","learners":"Write at their level and take ownership of the work."},{"teacher":"Review: ask 'What did you draw or write?' Have each learner read the text aloud once. Support with writing if needed.","learners":"Read aloud, listen to their pronunciation and correct mistakes."}]}],"levelTasks":[{"activity":"Story - Day 2: level-wise tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.11","tasks":{"Beginner":"Retell with the group by pointing to pictures or words; read aloud with group support (interpretation of the manual's group reading task).","Letter":"Read with the group, pointing to words; say the letters and words they know (interpretation of the manual's group reading task).","Word":"Support the group in writing the questions; read aloud the consonant clusters learned on the first day.","Para":"Ask the group's questions to another group, discuss them, then write answers to all questions individually; the teacher reads and corrects.","Story":"Ask the group's questions to another group, discuss them, then write answers to all questions individually; the teacher reads and corrects."}},{"activity":"Language game: Tell Me in a Minute - level support","source":"I","ref":"p.21","tasks":{"Beginner":"Take part by saying or pointing to the letters involved and by listening carefully; Para and Story level partners help.","Letter":"Say the letters/sounds and give simple words they know.","Word":"Say and write words and short sentences for the game.","Para":"Write sentences with the words; help groups to record answers.","Story":"Write sentences or short stories with the words; help groups to record answers."}},{"activity":"Self-writing: level tasks and review","source":"M","ref":"p.15","tasks":{"Beginner":"Draw a picture about the discussion and then write a few sentences about it, expressing thoughts freely. Review: say what they drew or wrote; read the text aloud once; the teacher may write the text in the notebook for them.","Letter":"Write about what they liked, using drawing and writing; write any words or sentences they can. Review: read the text aloud once; correct punctuation mistakes using the Barakhadi chart.","Word":"Write a sentence based on the conversation. Mistakes in spelling, punctuation and sentence structure are fine. Review: read it to the group; discuss and correct mistakes together.","Para":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation.","Story":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation."}}],"organisation":[{"grouping":"Whole class (big group)","how":"All learners of all levels sit in a 'U' shape arranged by level (Beginner, Letter, Word, Para, Story) so that the move to small groups is easy.","activities":["Warm-up: Rain clapping","Oral conversation: What did you see on your way?","Story (Day 2 of the story): retelling","Language game: Tell Me in a Minute","Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on what I saw on my way to school"]},{"grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","how":"Learners of similar levels work together; the teacher gives each group a task for its level and spends more time with learners who need support. Rotate responsibilities (for example group leader).","activities":["Story: reading with actions and group questions"]},{"grouping":"Individual","how":"Each learner works on a task for their own level; the teacher moves around, observes difficulties and supports individuals.","activities":["Story: writing answers individually","Self-writing: individual writing","Self-writing: review and reading back","Daily reading (10 minutes)"]}],"materials":["After the activity ask: What does the rain do to the fields?","The same story book as yesterday","Story book","slate or paper for questions","Notebooks","Topic slips (optional)","Picture card or topic on the board","crayons or pencils","Library books or storybooks"],"outcomes":["Learners take part in the oral conversation and speak without fear.","Learners retell the story, read with expression and ask or answer questions at their level.","Learners respond to the sound-symbol task for today (Language game: Tell Me in a Minute) at their own level.","Learners write about the topic at their level and read it aloud.","Each learner reads a book for 10 minutes."],"observation":["Observe each learner's reading and writing during the individual tasks; note who needs individual support and how many learners share the same difficulty.","Note any learner whose level is improving; move the learner to the next level group when you see steady progress (manual p.5).","Record each learner's progress for the day in the notebook, according to the learner's level (manual p.4).","Use today's observations to adjust tomorrow's plan (manual p.5)."],"teacherNotes":["Questions to elicit on Day 2: information questions (answer not in the text), thinking questions (needs knowledge beyond the text) and opinion questions (feedback on something in the text).","The manual lists the letter and word games but does not fix the slot in the daily timetable where they are used. This plan places them in the 10-minute sound-symbol / alphabet slot (interpretation).","Writing has two parts, content and sequence: encourage learners to read what they wrote, improve it and rewrite it for clarity and correctness (manual p.15).","Pace: the manual says not to assume all learners progress at the same speed. Repeat a day's activity with the groups that need it before moving on.","Special needs: give extra time and prepare materials for slower learners; seat learners with hearing or vision difficulty at the front; for learners who reverse or confuse letters, trace letters on the letter card with a finger and write with dots to trace with a pencil (manual p.6)."],"components":[{"no":1,"key":"warmup","name":"Warm-up activities","keywords":["Rain clapping","two learners lead"],"rows":[1]},{"no":2,"key":"oral","name":"Oral Discussion","keywords":["What did you see on your way?","every learner speaks"],"rows":[2]},{"no":3,"key":"story","name":"Story","keywords":["Day 2","retell","read with actions","group questions","ask and answer","write answers (Para/Story)"],"rows":[3,4,5]},{"no":4,"key":"sound","name":"Sound symbol games, Sound separation-pairing","keywords":["Tell Me in a Minute","play in turns","level support"],"rows":[6]},{"no":5,"key":"mindwrite","name":"Individual-Writing (Day 2)","keywords":["discussion","write at own level","self-review (read aloud)"],"rows":[7,8,9]},{"no":6,"key":"reading","name":"Daily reading","keywords":["library book","read alone","teacher listens"],"rows":[10]}],"preLesson":null},{"programme":"TARL Literacy","id":"lit-068","day":68,"phase":2,"phaseLabel":"Phase 2 (Days 46-90)","title":"Story: a story about a hungry traveller (Day 1)","dayType":"Story Day 1 + Mind mapping","focus":"Blending sounds to form words (cup, map, jam) | Mind map: fruits","duration":70,"objectives":["Listen, speak and answer in the oral conversation (familiar topic).","Listen to and read a story with understanding; discuss it in big and small groups and respond at their own level.","Develop sound-symbol skills: Blending sounds to form words (cup, map, jam).","Build vocabulary through a mind map ('fruits') and use the words at their own level.","Read independently for 10 minutes every day."],"sequence":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Writing with body parts","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Learners stand in a circle. Demonstrate writing the word 'bird' in the air with a finger, then ask them to write it with different body parts. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Write the word 'bird' in the air with the finger, then with the head, shoulders, knees or elbows.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.8","n":1},{"activity":"Oral conversation: familiar topic","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Hold a conversation on the topic 'something that made me laugh'. Give each learner a chance to speak; be patient with learners who need extra time.","learners":"Talk about the topic and listen to others.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.9","n":2},{"activity":"Story (Day 1 of the story): reading aloud and discussion","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":8,"teacher":"Discuss the title or picture of the story with the learners. Read the story aloud with expression and voice modulation (learners do not repeat after you). Discuss it, with emphasis on judgment questions. Read it again slowly, pointing to each word.","learners":"Talk about the title/picture; listen; answer questions; follow each word with a finger in their own copy.","tlm":"A story from the school library (a story about a hungry traveller), a copy for each learner","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":3},{"activity":"Story: reading in small groups","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":7,"teacher":"Form level-wise groups with a group leader. Learners read the story one sentence at a time while the others follow with their fingers. Para and Story level learners practise reading with emotion and expression.","learners":"Read the story sentence by sentence, supporting each other; the group leader helps.","tlm":"Story book copies","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":4},{"activity":"Story: level-wise individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":5,"teacher":"Give each learner the task for their level (see level table) and support those who need it.","learners":"Beginner/Letter: find and write favourite words or letters. Word: find consonant clusters. Para/Story: silently read, find unfamiliar and rhyming words.","tlm":"Story book, notebooks, board","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":5},{"activity":"Sound-symbol activity: oral sound awareness","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":4,"teacher":"Say separate sounds from 10-12 words (cup: c - u - p; map: m - a - p; jam: j - a - m; fox: f - o - x) and ask learners to blend the sounds into the complete word.","learners":"Listen to the separate sounds and blend them to say the whole word.","tlm":"None (oral activity)","source":"M","ref":"p.12","n":6},{"activity":"Sound-symbol games by level","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":6,"teacher":"Give each level group its game (see level table). Move among the groups and help those who need support; say each word clearly.","learners":"Play the game for their level in small groups.","tlm":"Board, chalk, letter cards","source":"M","ref":"p.12","n":7},{"activity":"Mind mapping (Day 1): the word 'fruits'","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Ask: 'What words come to your mind when you hear the word fruits?' Write learners' answers on the board or floor (Para and Story level learners write the words themselves). Guide the map towards the learning objective. Example words: mango, banana, orange, grapes, lemon, tamarind, gooseberry, olive, seed, peel, juice, pulp.","learners":"Say words connected with 'fruits'; share the meaning and feeling of words.","tlm":"Board, chalk (or floor)","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":8},{"activity":"Mind mapping: classify the words","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":4,"teacher":"Ask learners to classify the words in groups, for example: Sweet: mango, banana, orange, grapes; Sour: lemon, tamarind, gooseberry, olive; Seeds and skins: seed, peel, juice, pulp.","learners":"Sort the words into groups and say why.","tlm":"Board, chalk, word cards (optional)","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":9},{"activity":"Mind mapping: level-wise individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":6,"teacher":"Give each learner the individual task for their level; observe closely and give individual support. Display corrected stories on the wall.","learners":"Complete the task for their level (see level table).","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":10},{"activity":"Daily reading (10 minutes)","grouping":"Individual","minutes":10,"teacher":"Give each learner a library book or any storybook. Move around, listen to individual readers and note their level.","learners":"Read independently a book of their choice.","tlm":"Library books or storybooks","source":"M","ref":"p.7","n":11}],"procedures":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Writing with body parts","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","steps":[{"teacher":"Stand the learners in a circle. Demonstrate writing the word 'bird' in the air with your finger.","learners":"Watch and then copy with their own finger."},{"teacher":"Ask them to write it again using toes and other body parts (head, shoulders, knees, ...).","learners":"Write the letters in the air with the named body part."},{"teacher":"Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Take turns to lead."}]},{"activity":"Oral conversation: familiar topic","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.9","steps":[{"teacher":"Introduce the topic: 'something that made me laugh'.","learners":"Think about their own experience."},{"teacher":"Ask open questions; give every learner a chance. Involve learners who speak less.","learners":"Speak freely and without fear."},{"teacher":"Praise efforts and sum up.","learners":"Listen and respect each other's ideas."}]},{"activity":"Story - Day 1 (a story about a hungry traveller)","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.10","steps":[{"teacher":"Discuss the title or picture of the story with the learners.","learners":"Talk about what they see and what the story may be about."},{"teacher":"Read the story aloud with expression and proper voice modulation. Learners should not simply repeat after you.","learners":"Listen carefully and enjoy the story."},{"teacher":"Discuss the story: factual, logical, vocabulary-based, judgment or opinion questions (today's focus: judgment: Was the character right or wrong? Was that a good thing to do? Why?). Begin in the home language if needed.","learners":"Think and respond thoughtfully; every learner takes part."},{"teacher":"Read the story again slowly, pointing to each word. Make sure each learner has a copy and follows with a finger.","learners":"Follow each word with their finger."},{"teacher":"Ask learners to read in small groups; select a group leader who helps the others. Learners read one sentence at a time while the others point with fingers.","learners":"Read with the help of one another."}]},{"activity":"Sound-symbol: oral and level games","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.12","steps":[{"teacher":"Say separate sounds from 10-12 words (cup: c - u - p; map: m - a - p; jam: j - a - m; fox: f - o - x) and ask learners to blend the sounds into the complete word.","learners":"Listen to the separate sounds and blend them to say the whole word."},{"teacher":"Write the sounds or words for the day on the board and give each level group its task (see the level table).","learners":"Work in small groups and share their answers."},{"teacher":"Say each word clearly with distinct pronunciation. Give learners enough time to respond and think; use words learners commonly use at home (regional language and the medium of instruction).","learners":"Think, say and write the sounds."}]},{"activity":"Mind mapping: 'fruits'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Small group (level-wise) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.14","steps":[{"teacher":"Choose a word that can generate many related words: 'fruits'. Ask: 'What words come to your mind when you hear the word fruits?' Write the answers on the board or floor.","learners":"Say words they link with 'fruits'."},{"teacher":"Discuss the words: what they mean and how they are connected.","learners":"Explain their words and listen to others."},{"teacher":"In small groups, let the learners classify the words (Sweet: mango, banana, orange, grapes; Sour: lemon, tamarind, gooseberry, olive; Seeds and skins: seed, peel, juice, pulp).","learners":"Sort the words into groups."},{"teacher":"Give the individual tasks by level and help each learner.","learners":"Work individually; read the work aloud at the end if time allows."}]}],"levelTasks":[{"activity":"Story - Day 1: individual tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.10","tasks":{"Beginner":"Circle or search for a favourite word or letter in the story and say it aloud. If a learner cannot draw a circle, write words on the board and ask them to identify them.","Letter":"Find, read and write favourite words from the story.","Word":"Find the consonant clusters in the story, read them and write them in the notebook.","Para":"Silently read the story from the textbook; find unfamiliar words and try to understand them; find rhyming words, use them in sentences and write in the notebook; ask other groups for meanings; make questions in groups.","Story":"Silently read the story; find unfamiliar words and rhyming words; practise reading with emotion; one group reads sentences formed with consonant clusters to the other group; ask and answer group questions (information, thinking and opinion questions)."}},{"activity":"Sound-symbol games by level (small groups)","source":"M","ref":"p.12","tasks":{"Beginner":"'What is the first sound in the word kite?' 'Is there a letter that makes the sound /k/?' 'Can you name objects that start with the letter K?' Learners think and share names in the group.","Letter":"Write the rhyming ending -ub on the board and ask learners to add new letters to form words: t + ub = tub, r + ub = rub, c + ub = cub.","Word":"Say a word and tell its sounds, for example 'sun' = /s/ + /u/ + /n/. Then tell what word is formed if /r/ is put before 'at': r + at = rat. Do 8-10 such combinations; at first learners may form meaningless words, later only meaningful words.","Para":"Write two or three sounds on the board (for example Br, cl, st) and let the learners form words that start with those sounds; this builds a word list for the learner.","Story":"Write two or three sounds on the board (for example Br, cl, st) and let the learners form words that start with those sounds; this builds a word list for the learner."}},{"activity":"Mind mapping 'fruits': level tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.14","tasks":{"Beginner":"Circle all the words that contain the letter 'E' on the board; make a list. See how many learners find the most words.","Letter":"Circle all the words that contain the letter 'E' and make a list of them.","Word":"Use 4-5 words (for example peel, pulp, seed, juice, lemon) to form sentences, starting with words of one or two syllables. Example: Dream - I had a dream last night.","Para":"Choose any five words from the map and create a story with them. Use consonant clusters correctly, read the story aloud, correct mistakes of sentence structure, spelling or grammar, then display it on the wall.","Story":"Choose any five words from the map and create a story with them. Use consonant clusters correctly, read the story aloud, correct mistakes of sentence structure, spelling or grammar, then display it on the wall."}}],"organisation":[{"grouping":"Whole class (big group)","how":"All learners of all levels sit in a 'U' shape arranged by level (Beginner, Letter, Word, Para, Story) so that the move to small groups is easy.","activities":["Warm-up: Writing with body parts","Oral conversation: familiar topic","Story (Day 1 of the story): reading aloud and discussion","Sound-symbol activity: oral sound awareness","Mind mapping (Day 1): the word 'fruits'"]},{"grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","how":"Learners of similar levels work together; the teacher gives each group a task for its level and spends more time with learners who need support. Rotate responsibilities (for example group leader).","activities":["Story: reading in small groups","Sound-symbol games by level","Mind mapping: classify the words"]},{"grouping":"Individual","how":"Each learner works on a task for their own level; the teacher moves around, observes difficulties and supports individuals.","activities":["Story: level-wise individual tasks","Mind mapping: level-wise individual tasks","Daily reading (10 minutes)"]}],"materials":["A story from the school library (a story about a hungry traveller)","a copy for each learner","Story book copies","Story book","notebooks","board","Board","chalk","letter cards","chalk (or floor)","word cards (optional)","Notebooks","Library books or storybooks"],"outcomes":["Learners take part in the oral conversation and speak without fear.","Learners show understanding of the story in the discussion and complete the task for their level.","Learners respond to the sound-symbol task for today (Blending sounds to form words (cup, map, jam)) at their own level.","Learners add words to the mind map and use them in sentences or a story at their level.","Each learner reads a book for 10 minutes."],"observation":["Observe each learner's reading and writing during the individual tasks; note who needs individual support and how many learners share the same difficulty.","Note any learner whose level is improving; move the learner to the next level group when you see steady progress (manual p.5).","Record each learner's progress for the day in the notebook, according to the learner's level (manual p.4).","Use today's observations to adjust tomorrow's plan (manual p.5)."],"teacherNotes":["Story selection: the manual asks teachers to use picture story books or stories in the school library. Today's suggested theme (a story about a hungry traveller) is a planning suggestion; use any suitable story you have.","Sound-symbol: for the first 4-5 days, play sound-based games with the learners at word level. Include the sounds learners find difficult when you prepare the Class Transaction Plan.","Mind mapping topic for this day: 'fruits'. The manual's example uses the word 'shop'; today's topic follows the same method.","Pace: the manual says not to assume all learners progress at the same speed. Repeat a day's activity with the groups that need it before moving on.","Special needs: give extra time and prepare materials for slower learners; seat learners with hearing or vision difficulty at the front; for learners who reverse or confuse letters, trace letters on the letter card with a finger and write with dots to trace with a pencil (manual p.6)."],"components":[{"no":1,"key":"warmup","name":"Warm-up activities","keywords":["Writing with body parts","two learners lead"],"rows":[1]},{"no":2,"key":"oral","name":"Oral Discussion","keywords":["familiar topic","every learner speaks"],"rows":[2]},{"no":3,"key":"story","name":"Story","keywords":["Day 1","title / picture talk","read aloud with expression","judgment questions","re-read pointing","group reading","level tasks"],"rows":[3,4,5]},{"no":4,"key":"sound","name":"Sound symbol games, Sound separation-pairing","keywords":["oral sound awareness","blend sounds to a word","level games in small groups"],"rows":[6,7]},{"no":5,"key":"mindwrite","name":"Mind Mapping (Day 1)","keywords":["mind map: fruits","classify the words","level task: circle letter E / sentences / story"],"rows":[8,9,10]},{"no":6,"key":"reading","name":"Daily reading","keywords":["library book","read alone","teacher listens"],"rows":[11]}],"preLesson":null},{"programme":"TARL Literacy","id":"lit-069","day":69,"phase":2,"phaseLabel":"Phase 2 (Days 46-90)","title":"Story: a story about a hungry traveller (Day 2)","dayType":"Story Day 2 + Self-writing","focus":"Language game: Singing and Spinning | Self-writing: my favourite place","duration":70,"objectives":["Listen, speak and answer in the oral conversation (conversation on a picture).","Retell the story, read it with expression, ask and answer questions about it and write answers.","Develop sound-symbol skills: Language game: Singing and Spinning.","Write about a topic at their own level and review the writing (my favourite place).","Read independently for 10 minutes every day."],"sequence":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Alphabet song (last-letter word chain)","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Say a word to the big group, for example 'road'. Learners say a word that starts with the last letter ('d'). A learner who cannot say a word is out. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Say a word that starts with the last letter of the previous word; step out if unable to.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.8","n":1},{"activity":"Oral conversation: conversation on a picture","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Show a picture of a classroom with a blackboard and ask what is happening, who is doing what and what is happening around them. Let learners think creatively and even make up a story.","learners":"Look at the picture, answer questions and make up their own story about it.","tlm":"Picture card of a classroom with a blackboard","source":"M","ref":"p.9","n":2},{"activity":"Story (Day 2 of the story): retelling","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":6,"teacher":"Ask learners to retell yesterday's story in their own words. Prompt with questions on the beginning, middle and end.","learners":"Retell the story using their own words.","tlm":"The same story book as yesterday","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":3},{"activity":"Story: reading with actions and group questions","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":9,"teacher":"Learners practise reading with actions and expressions; one learner per group reads aloud to the class. Guide groups to make questions about the story (guide initially). Groups take turns to ask and answer each other's questions. Word-level learners also read aloud the consonants learned on the first day.","learners":"Read with actions; make questions (word-level learners help write them); ask and answer questions with another group.","tlm":"Story book, slate or paper for questions","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":4},{"activity":"Story: writing answers individually","grouping":"Individual","minutes":5,"teacher":"Para and Story level learners write answers to all questions individually; read and correct their responses after they finish.","learners":"Write the answers in their notebooks; Beginner/Letter/Word learners read or listen and answer orally.","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":5},{"activity":"Language game: Singing and Spinning","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Learners sit in a circle; a small object (chalk, pencil) is passed around while the teacher, back turned, claps steadily. Observe each learner and give help where needed.","learners":"Play the game, take turns and read or say the words they make.","tlm":"A small object (chalk or pencil)","source":"M","ref":"p.18","n":6},{"activity":"Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on my favourite place","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Start a conversation about a topic: 'my favourite place'. Involve all learners and ask open-ended questions.","learners":"Take part in the discussion and share thoughts freely.","tlm":"Picture card or topic on the board","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":7},{"activity":"Self-writing: individual writing","grouping":"Individual","minutes":7,"teacher":"Give each level its task (see level table). Let learners take ownership of what they draw and write; mistakes are fine.","learners":"Draw and write about the topic at their level.","tlm":"Notebooks, crayons or pencils","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":8},{"activity":"Self-writing: review and reading back","grouping":"Individual","minutes":3,"teacher":"Ask each learner 'What did you draw or write?' and have them read it aloud once. Word-level learners read to the group; discuss spelling, punctuation and sentence structure. Help beginners by writing their text in the notebook for them if needed.","learners":"Read what they wrote; correct mistakes after listening to their own reading.","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":9},{"activity":"Daily reading (10 minutes)","grouping":"Individual","minutes":10,"teacher":"Give each learner a library book or any storybook. Move around, listen to individual readers and note their level.","learners":"Read independently a book of their choice.","tlm":"Library books or storybooks","source":"M","ref":"p.7","n":10}],"procedures":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Alphabet song (last-letter word chain)","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","steps":[{"teacher":"Say the word 'road' to the big group and show that its last letter is 'd'.","learners":"Listen and think of a word starting with 'd'."},{"teacher":"Ask learners in turn to say a word that starts with the last letter of the previous word. Example: rain -> nest.","learners":"Say a word in turn; anyone who cannot say a word is out of the game."},{"teacher":"Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Lead the game when it is their turn."}]},{"activity":"Oral conversation: conversation on a picture","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.9","steps":[{"teacher":"Show the picture of a classroom with a blackboard.","learners":"Look carefully."},{"teacher":"Ask: What is happening in the picture? Who is doing what? What is happening around them? Then: How do the people feel? How can you tell?","learners":"Answer in their own words; every learner gets a chance."},{"teacher":"Let learners imagine and make up a short story from the picture.","learners":"Tell their stories to the class."}]},{"activity":"Story - Day 2 (a story about a hungry traveller)","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.11","steps":[{"teacher":"Ask learners to retell the story they read yesterday in their own words.","learners":"Retell, helping each other remember."},{"teacher":"In small groups learners practise reading the story using actions and expressions; one learner from each group then reads aloud to the class.","learners":"Read with actions and expression; a representative reads aloud."},{"teacher":"Guide the groups to come up with questions about the story (guide initially). Word-level learners can support by helping write them down.","learners":"Make questions together."},{"teacher":"Groups take turns to ask and answer each other's questions. Useful kinds: questions whose answer is not in the text; questions needing thinking beyond the text; questions asking for an opinion.","learners":"Ask, answer and discuss in the groups."},{"teacher":"Word-level learners also read aloud the consonants they learned on the first day.","learners":"Read the consonant clusters aloud."}]},{"activity":"Language game: Singing and Spinning","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.18","steps":[{"teacher":"Seat the learners in a circle. Give one learner a small object such as a piece of chalk.","learners":"Sit in a circle and listen for the clapping."},{"teacher":"Stand outside the circle with your back to the learners and clap steadily. Stop clapping without warning.","learners":"Pass the object round while the clapping continues."},{"teacher":"Ask the learner holding the object when you stop to sing a song, recite a poem or tell a joke.","learners":"Sing, recite or tell a joke; the others listen and clap."}]},{"activity":"Self-writing: 'Discussion, Writing, Self-review'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.15","steps":[{"teacher":"Start a conversation about a topic: 'my favourite place'. Involve all learners and ask open-ended questions.","learners":"Discuss and answer questions."},{"teacher":"Give writing time at each level: draw then write (Beginner), write about what they liked (Letter), a sentence (Word), a paragraph or story on a topic of their choice (Para/Story).","learners":"Write at their level and take ownership of the work."},{"teacher":"Review: ask 'What did you draw or write?' Have each learner read the text aloud once. Support with writing if needed.","learners":"Read aloud, listen to their pronunciation and correct mistakes."}]}],"levelTasks":[{"activity":"Story - Day 2: level-wise tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.11","tasks":{"Beginner":"Retell with the group by pointing to pictures or words; read aloud with group support (interpretation of the manual's group reading task).","Letter":"Read with the group, pointing to words; say the letters and words they know (interpretation of the manual's group reading task).","Word":"Support the group in writing the questions; read aloud the consonant clusters learned on the first day.","Para":"Ask the group's questions to another group, discuss them, then write answers to all questions individually; the teacher reads and corrects.","Story":"Ask the group's questions to another group, discuss them, then write answers to all questions individually; the teacher reads and corrects."}},{"activity":"Language game: Singing and Spinning - level support","source":"I","ref":"p.18","tasks":{"Beginner":"Take part by saying or pointing to the letters involved and by listening carefully; Para and Story level partners help.","Letter":"Say the letters/sounds and give simple words they know.","Word":"Say and write words and short sentences for the game.","Para":"Write sentences with the words; help groups to record answers.","Story":"Write sentences or short stories with the words; help groups to record answers."}},{"activity":"Self-writing: level tasks and review","source":"M","ref":"p.15","tasks":{"Beginner":"Draw a picture about the discussion and then write a few sentences about it, expressing thoughts freely. Review: say what they drew or wrote; read the text aloud once; the teacher may write the text in the notebook for them.","Letter":"Write about what they liked, using drawing and writing; write any words or sentences they can. Review: read the text aloud once; correct punctuation mistakes using the Barakhadi chart.","Word":"Write a sentence based on the conversation. Mistakes in spelling, punctuation and sentence structure are fine. Review: read it to the group; discuss and correct mistakes together.","Para":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation.","Story":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation."}}],"organisation":[{"grouping":"Whole class (big group)","how":"All learners of all levels sit in a 'U' shape arranged by level (Beginner, Letter, Word, Para, Story) so that the move to small groups is easy.","activities":["Warm-up: Alphabet song (last-letter word chain)","Oral conversation: conversation on a picture","Story (Day 2 of the story): retelling","Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on my favourite place"]},{"grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","how":"Learners of similar levels work together; the teacher gives each group a task for its level and spends more time with learners who need support. Rotate responsibilities (for example group leader).","activities":["Story: reading with actions and group questions","Language game: Singing and Spinning"]},{"grouping":"Individual","how":"Each learner works on a task for their own level; the teacher moves around, observes difficulties and supports individuals.","activities":["Story: writing answers individually","Self-writing: individual writing","Self-writing: review and reading back","Daily reading (10 minutes)"]}],"materials":["Picture card of a classroom with a blackboard","The same story book as yesterday","Story book","slate or paper for questions","Notebooks","A small object (chalk or pencil)","Picture card or topic on the board","crayons or pencils","Library books or storybooks"],"outcomes":["Learners take part in the oral conversation and speak without fear.","Learners retell the story, read with expression and ask or answer questions at their level.","Learners respond to the sound-symbol task for today (Language game: Singing and Spinning) at their own level.","Learners write about the topic at their level and read it aloud.","Each learner reads a book for 10 minutes."],"observation":["Observe each learner's reading and writing during the individual tasks; note who needs individual support and how many learners share the same difficulty.","Note any learner whose level is improving; move the learner to the next level group when you see steady progress (manual p.5).","Record each learner's progress for the day in the notebook, according to the learner's level (manual p.4).","Use today's observations to adjust tomorrow's plan (manual p.5)."],"teacherNotes":["Questions to elicit on Day 2: information questions (answer not in the text), thinking questions (needs knowledge beyond the text) and opinion questions (feedback on something in the text).","The manual lists the letter and word games but does not fix the slot in the daily timetable where they are used. This plan places them in the 10-minute sound-symbol / alphabet slot (interpretation).","Writing has two parts, content and sequence: encourage learners to read what they wrote, improve it and rewrite it for clarity and correctness (manual p.15).","Pace: the manual says not to assume all learners progress at the same speed. Repeat a day's activity with the groups that need it before moving on.","Special needs: give extra time and prepare materials for slower learners; seat learners with hearing or vision difficulty at the front; for learners who reverse or confuse letters, trace letters on the letter card with a finger and write with dots to trace with a pencil (manual p.6)."],"components":[{"no":1,"key":"warmup","name":"Warm-up activities","keywords":["Alphabet song (last-letter word chain)","two learners lead"],"rows":[1]},{"no":2,"key":"oral","name":"Oral Discussion","keywords":["conversation on a picture","every learner speaks"],"rows":[2]},{"no":3,"key":"story","name":"Story","keywords":["Day 2","retell","read with actions","group questions","ask and answer","write answers (Para/Story)"],"rows":[3,4,5]},{"no":4,"key":"sound","name":"Sound symbol games, Sound separation-pairing","keywords":["Singing and Spinning","play in turns","level support"],"rows":[6]},{"no":5,"key":"mindwrite","name":"Individual-Writing (Day 2)","keywords":["discussion","write at own level","self-review (read aloud)"],"rows":[7,8,9]},{"no":6,"key":"reading","name":"Daily reading","keywords":["library book","read alone","teacher listens"],"rows":[10]}],"preLesson":null},{"programme":"TARL Literacy","id":"lit-070","day":70,"phase":2,"phaseLabel":"Phase 2 (Days 46-90)","title":"Story: a story about working together (Day 1)","dayType":"Story Day 1 + Mind mapping","focus":"Language game: Tell Me in a Minute | Mind map: birds","duration":70,"objectives":["Listen, speak and answer in the oral conversation (listening and storytelling).","Listen to and read a story with understanding; discuss it in big and small groups and respond at their own level.","Develop sound-symbol skills: Language game: Tell Me in a Minute.","Build vocabulary through a mind map ('birds') and use the words at their own level.","Read independently for 10 minutes every day."],"sequence":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Handkerchief game","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Learners sit in a circle and clap while singing a rhyme ('I caught a Fish Alive'). One learner runs outside the circle with a handkerchief and secretly places it behind another learner, who must chase the runner. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Sit in a circle, clap and sing; run, place the handkerchief or chase as the game requires.","tlm":"A handkerchief","source":"M","ref":"p.8","n":1},{"activity":"Oral conversation: listening and storytelling","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Tell an interesting story starter and involve the learners: 'A parrot came to class and sat on the teacher's chair. What lesson did it teach?' Let learners imagine and continue the story.","learners":"Listen to the teacher, then imagine and continue the story. Learners can also recite a rhyme or story they know.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.9","n":2},{"activity":"Story (Day 1 of the story): reading aloud and discussion","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":8,"teacher":"Discuss the title or picture of the story with the learners. Read the story aloud with expression and voice modulation (learners do not repeat after you). Discuss it, with emphasis on opinion questions. Read it again slowly, pointing to each word.","learners":"Talk about the title/picture; listen; answer questions; follow each word with a finger in their own copy.","tlm":"A story from the school library (a story about working together), a copy for each learner","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":3},{"activity":"Story: reading in small groups","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":7,"teacher":"Form level-wise groups with a group leader. Learners read the story one sentence at a time while the others follow with their fingers. Para and Story level learners practise reading with emotion and expression.","learners":"Read the story sentence by sentence, supporting each other; the group leader helps.","tlm":"Story book copies","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":4},{"activity":"Story: level-wise individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":5,"teacher":"Give each learner the task for their level (see level table) and support those who need it.","learners":"Beginner/Letter: find and write favourite words or letters. Word: find consonant clusters. Para/Story: silently read, find unfamiliar and rhyming words.","tlm":"Story book, notebooks, board","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":5},{"activity":"Language game: Tell Me in a Minute","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Each learner gets a familiar topic, thinks for 2-3 minutes and speaks about it for one minute. Observe each learner and give help where needed.","learners":"Play the game, take turns and read or say the words they make.","tlm":"Topic slips (optional)","source":"M","ref":"p.21","n":6},{"activity":"Mind mapping (Day 1): the word 'birds'","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Ask: 'What words come to your mind when you hear the word birds?' Write learners' answers on the board or floor (Para and Story level learners write the words themselves). Guide the map towards the learning objective. Example words: duck, crane, heron, swan, sparrow, crow, parrot, dove, eagle, owl, kite, hawk.","learners":"Say words connected with 'birds'; share the meaning and feeling of words.","tlm":"Board, chalk (or floor)","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":7},{"activity":"Mind mapping: classify the words","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":4,"teacher":"Ask learners to classify the words in groups, for example: Water birds: duck, crane, heron, swan; Garden birds: sparrow, crow, parrot, dove; Birds of prey: eagle, owl, kite, hawk.","learners":"Sort the words into groups and say why.","tlm":"Board, chalk, word cards (optional)","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":8},{"activity":"Mind mapping: level-wise individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":6,"teacher":"Give each learner the individual task for their level; observe closely and give individual support. Display corrected stories on the wall.","learners":"Complete the task for their level (see level table).","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":9},{"activity":"Daily reading (10 minutes)","grouping":"Individual","minutes":10,"teacher":"Give each learner a library book or any storybook. Move around, listen to individual readers and note their level.","learners":"Read independently a book of their choice.","tlm":"Library books or storybooks","source":"M","ref":"p.7","n":10}],"procedures":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Handkerchief game","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","steps":[{"teacher":"Seat the learners in a circle and start clapping and singing the rhyme 'I caught a Fish Alive'.","learners":"Clap and sing together."},{"teacher":"One learner runs outside the circle holding a handkerchief and secretly places it behind another learner.","learners":"Everyone keeps clapping; the learner who finds the handkerchief behind them takes it and chases the runner."},{"teacher":"If the runner sits in the chaser's place before being caught, they stay in the game; if caught, they are out. Continue in this way.","learners":"Play fairly and take turns."}]},{"activity":"Oral conversation: listening and storytelling","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.9","steps":[{"teacher":"Say the starter: 'A parrot came to class and sat on the teacher's chair. What lesson did it teach?'","learners":"Listen and imagine."},{"teacher":"Ask learners to continue the story one by one. Encourage those who speak less.","learners":"Add ideas to the story."},{"teacher":"Invite a learner to recite a poem or rhyme they know.","learners":"Recite and listen to others."}]},{"activity":"Story - Day 1 (a story about working together)","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.10","steps":[{"teacher":"Discuss the title or picture of the story with the learners.","learners":"Talk about what they see and what the story may be about."},{"teacher":"Read the story aloud with expression and proper voice modulation. Learners should not simply repeat after you.","learners":"Listen carefully and enjoy the story."},{"teacher":"Discuss the story: factual, logical, vocabulary-based, judgment or opinion questions (today's focus: opinion: What did you like best? What would you have done in the story?). Begin in the home language if needed.","learners":"Think and respond thoughtfully; every learner takes part."},{"teacher":"Read the story again slowly, pointing to each word. Make sure each learner has a copy and follows with a finger.","learners":"Follow each word with their finger."},{"teacher":"Ask learners to read in small groups; select a group leader who helps the others. Learners read one sentence at a time while the others point with fingers.","learners":"Read with the help of one another."}]},{"activity":"Language game: Tell Me in a Minute","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.21","steps":[{"teacher":"Give each learner a different familiar topic. Learners can also choose their own topic.","learners":"Choose or receive a topic."},{"teacher":"Give them 2-3 minutes to think about the topic.","learners":"Think about what to say."},{"teacher":"Encourage each learner to speak about it for one minute.","learners":"Speak for one minute; others listen."}]},{"activity":"Mind mapping: 'birds'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Small group (level-wise) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.14","steps":[{"teacher":"Choose a word that can generate many related words: 'birds'. Ask: 'What words come to your mind when you hear the word birds?' Write the answers on the board or floor.","learners":"Say words they link with 'birds'."},{"teacher":"Discuss the words: what they mean and how they are connected.","learners":"Explain their words and listen to others."},{"teacher":"In small groups, let the learners classify the words (Water birds: duck, crane, heron, swan; Garden birds: sparrow, crow, parrot, dove; Birds of prey: eagle, owl, kite, hawk).","learners":"Sort the words into groups."},{"teacher":"Give the individual tasks by level and help each learner.","learners":"Work individually; read the work aloud at the end if time allows."}]}],"levelTasks":[{"activity":"Story - Day 1: individual tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.10","tasks":{"Beginner":"Circle or search for a favourite word or letter in the story and say it aloud. If a learner cannot draw a circle, write words on the board and ask them to identify them.","Letter":"Find, read and write favourite words from the story.","Word":"Find the consonant clusters in the story, read them and write them in the notebook.","Para":"Silently read the story from the textbook; find unfamiliar words and try to understand them; find rhyming words, use them in sentences and write in the notebook; ask other groups for meanings; make questions in groups.","Story":"Silently read the story; find unfamiliar words and rhyming words; practise reading with emotion; one group reads sentences formed with consonant clusters to the other group; ask and answer group questions (information, thinking and opinion questions)."}},{"activity":"Language game: Tell Me in a Minute - level support","source":"I","ref":"p.21","tasks":{"Beginner":"Take part by saying or pointing to the letters involved and by listening carefully; Para and Story level partners help.","Letter":"Say the letters/sounds and give simple words they know.","Word":"Say and write words and short sentences for the game.","Para":"Write sentences with the words; help groups to record answers.","Story":"Write sentences or short stories with the words; help groups to record answers."}},{"activity":"Mind mapping 'birds': level tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.14","tasks":{"Beginner":"Circle all the words that contain the letter 'A' on the board; make a list. See how many learners find the most words.","Letter":"Circle all the words that contain the letter 'A' and make a list of them.","Word":"Use 4-5 words (for example owl, crow, dove, duck, hawk) to form sentences, starting with words of one or two syllables. Example: Dream - I had a dream last night.","Para":"Choose any five words from the map and create a story with them. Use consonant clusters correctly, read the story aloud, correct mistakes of sentence structure, spelling or grammar, then display it on the wall.","Story":"Choose any five words from the map and create a story with them. Use consonant clusters correctly, read the story aloud, correct mistakes of sentence structure, spelling or grammar, then display it on the wall."}}],"organisation":[{"grouping":"Whole class (big group)","how":"All learners of all levels sit in a 'U' shape arranged by level (Beginner, Letter, Word, Para, Story) so that the move to small groups is easy.","activities":["Warm-up: Handkerchief game","Oral conversation: listening and storytelling","Story (Day 1 of the story): reading aloud and discussion","Language game: Tell Me in a Minute","Mind mapping (Day 1): the word 'birds'"]},{"grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","how":"Learners of similar levels work together; the teacher gives each group a task for its level and spends more time with learners who need support. Rotate responsibilities (for example group leader).","activities":["Story: reading in small groups","Mind mapping: classify the words"]},{"grouping":"Individual","how":"Each learner works on a task for their own level; the teacher moves around, observes difficulties and supports individuals.","activities":["Story: level-wise individual tasks","Mind mapping: level-wise individual tasks","Daily reading (10 minutes)"]}],"materials":["A handkerchief","A story from the school library (a story about working together)","a copy for each learner","Story book copies","Story book","notebooks","board","Topic slips (optional)","Board","chalk (or floor)","chalk","word cards (optional)","Notebooks","Library books or storybooks"],"outcomes":["Learners take part in the oral conversation and speak without fear.","Learners show understanding of the story in the discussion and complete the task for their level.","Learners respond to the sound-symbol task for today (Language game: Tell Me in a Minute) at their own level.","Learners add words to the mind map and use them in sentences or a story at their level.","Each learner reads a book for 10 minutes."],"observation":["Observe each learner's reading and writing during the individual tasks; note who needs individual support and how many learners share the same difficulty.","Note any learner whose level is improving; move the learner to the next level group when you see steady progress (manual p.5).","Record each learner's progress for the day in the notebook, according to the learner's level (manual p.4).","Use today's observations to adjust tomorrow's plan (manual p.5)."],"teacherNotes":["Story selection: the manual asks teachers to use picture story books or stories in the school library. Today's suggested theme (a story about working together) is a planning suggestion; use any suitable story you have.","The manual lists the letter and word games but does not fix the slot in the daily timetable where they are used. This plan places them in the 10-minute sound-symbol / alphabet slot (interpretation).","Mind mapping topic for this day: 'birds'. The manual's example uses the word 'shop'; today's topic follows the same method.","Pace: the manual says not to assume all learners progress at the same speed. Repeat a day's activity with the groups that need it before moving on.","Special needs: give extra time and prepare materials for slower learners; seat learners with hearing or vision difficulty at the front; for learners who reverse or confuse letters, trace letters on the letter card with a finger and write with dots to trace with a pencil (manual p.6)."],"components":[{"no":1,"key":"warmup","name":"Warm-up activities","keywords":["Handkerchief game","two learners lead"],"rows":[1]},{"no":2,"key":"oral","name":"Oral Discussion","keywords":["listening and storytelling","every learner speaks"],"rows":[2]},{"no":3,"key":"story","name":"Story","keywords":["Day 1","title / picture talk","read aloud with expression","opinion questions","re-read pointing","group reading","level tasks"],"rows":[3,4,5]},{"no":4,"key":"sound","name":"Sound symbol games, Sound separation-pairing","keywords":["Tell Me in a Minute","play in turns","level support"],"rows":[6]},{"no":5,"key":"mindwrite","name":"Mind Mapping (Day 1)","keywords":["mind map: birds","classify the words","level task: circle letter A / sentences / story"],"rows":[7,8,9]},{"no":6,"key":"reading","name":"Daily reading","keywords":["library book","read alone","teacher listens"],"rows":[10]}],"preLesson":null},{"programme":"TARL Literacy","id":"lit-071","day":71,"phase":2,"phaseLabel":"Phase 2 (Days 46-90)","title":"Story: a story about working together (Day 2)","dayType":"Story Day 2 + Self-writing","focus":"Consonant clusters: str (strap, stripe) | Self-writing: a picture of a wedding","duration":70,"objectives":["Listen, speak and answer in the oral conversation (What did you see on your way?).","Retell the story, read it with expression, ask and answer questions about it and write answers.","Develop sound-symbol skills: Consonant clusters: str (strap, stripe).","Write about a topic at their own level and review the writing (a picture of a wedding).","Read independently for 10 minutes every day."],"sequence":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Rhyme - 'I saw a Little Bird'","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Say the rhyme with actions, then say it together. Lines: I saw a little bird go hop, hop, hop / I told the little bird to stop, stop, stop. / I went to the window to say 'How do you do?' / He wagged his little tail and far away he flew! Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Listen, then say the rhyme with actions.","tlm":"Rhyme chart or board (optional)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","n":1},{"activity":"Oral conversation: What did you see on your way?","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Ask learners to describe what they saw on their way to school. If they are hesitant, begin yourself: 'On my way I saw a bus full of people, a boy on a bicycle and an old man selling guavas. What did you see?'","learners":"Describe what they saw on the way to school and connect with what others share.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.9","n":2},{"activity":"Story (Day 2 of the story): retelling","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":6,"teacher":"Ask learners to retell yesterday's story in their own words. Prompt with questions on the beginning, middle and end.","learners":"Retell the story using their own words.","tlm":"The same story book as yesterday","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":3},{"activity":"Story: reading with actions and group questions","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":9,"teacher":"Learners practise reading with actions and expressions; one learner per group reads aloud to the class. Guide groups to make questions about the story (guide initially). Groups take turns to ask and answer each other's questions. Word-level learners also read aloud the consonants learned on the first day.","learners":"Read with actions; make questions (word-level learners help write them); ask and answer questions with another group.","tlm":"Story book, slate or paper for questions","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":4},{"activity":"Story: writing answers individually","grouping":"Individual","minutes":5,"teacher":"Para and Story level learners write answers to all questions individually; read and correct their responses after they finish.","learners":"Write the answers in their notebooks; Beginner/Letter/Word learners read or listen and answer orally.","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":5},{"activity":"Consonant clusters: introduction","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":4,"teacher":"Three-letter clusters: after two-letter clusters, familiarise learners with clusters of three letters ('str' as in strap, stripe, stroke). Discuss the words, then ask learners to tell and write sentences using them.","learners":"Listen, pronounce the cluster and say words that contain it.","tlm":"Board and chalk, words list (strap stripe stroke strike stretch)","source":"M","ref":"p.16","n":6},{"activity":"Consonant cluster game: Looking for Similar Ones","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":6,"teacher":"Write some words with the same conjunct consonants on the board, for example bl, tr, st. Observe closely and help learners who need support.","learners":"Match words that have the same conjunct consonant (black, blue, blanket, blow, blink).","tlm":"Words on the board","source":"M","ref":"p.17","n":7},{"activity":"Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on a picture of a wedding","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Start a conversation about a situation: 'a picture of a wedding'. Involve all learners and ask open-ended questions.","learners":"Take part in the discussion and share thoughts freely.","tlm":"Picture card or topic on the board","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":8},{"activity":"Self-writing: individual writing","grouping":"Individual","minutes":7,"teacher":"Give each level its task (see level table). Let learners take ownership of what they draw and write; mistakes are fine.","learners":"Draw and write about the topic at their level.","tlm":"Notebooks, crayons or pencils","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":9},{"activity":"Self-writing: review and reading back","grouping":"Individual","minutes":3,"teacher":"Ask each learner 'What did you draw or write?' and have them read it aloud once. Word-level learners read to the group; discuss spelling, punctuation and sentence structure. Help beginners by writing their text in the notebook for them if needed.","learners":"Read what they wrote; correct mistakes after listening to their own reading.","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":10},{"activity":"Daily reading (10 minutes)","grouping":"Individual","minutes":10,"teacher":"Give each learner a library book or any storybook. Move around, listen to individual readers and note their level.","learners":"Read independently a book of their choice.","tlm":"Library books or storybooks","source":"M","ref":"p.7","n":11}],"procedures":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Rhyme - 'I saw a Little Bird'","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","steps":[{"teacher":"Say the rhyme 'I saw a Little Bird' slowly with actions: I saw a little bird go hop, hop, hop / I told the little bird to stop, stop, stop. / I went to the window to say 'How do you do?' / He wagged his little tail and far away he flew!","learners":"Listen and watch the actions."},{"teacher":"Say it again; invite learners to join with actions.","learners":"Say the rhyme together with actions."},{"teacher":"Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Choose a rhyme they like and lead."}]},{"activity":"Oral conversation: What did you see on your way?","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.9","steps":[{"teacher":"Ask: 'What did you see on your way to school today?'","learners":"Think about the way to school."},{"teacher":"If learners hesitate, start: 'On my way I saw a bus full of people, a boy on a bicycle and an old man selling guavas. What did you see?'","learners":"Listen to the model and then share their own observations."},{"teacher":"Connect learners' answers with each other.","learners":"Listen and add what they noticed."}]},{"activity":"Story - Day 2 (a story about working together)","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.11","steps":[{"teacher":"Ask learners to retell the story they read yesterday in their own words.","learners":"Retell, helping each other remember."},{"teacher":"In small groups learners practise reading the story using actions and expressions; one learner from each group then reads aloud to the class.","learners":"Read with actions and expression; a representative reads aloud."},{"teacher":"Guide the groups to come up with questions about the story (guide initially). Word-level learners can support by helping write them down.","learners":"Make questions together."},{"teacher":"Groups take turns to ask and answer each other's questions. Useful kinds: questions whose answer is not in the text; questions needing thinking beyond the text; questions asking for an opinion.","learners":"Ask, answer and discuss in the groups."},{"teacher":"Word-level learners also read aloud the consonants they learned on the first day.","learners":"Read the consonant clusters aloud."}]},{"activity":"Consonant clusters (str) and the game 'Looking for Similar Ones'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.16-17","steps":[{"teacher":"Three-letter clusters: after two-letter clusters, familiarise learners with clusters of three letters ('str' as in strap, stripe, stroke). Discuss the words, then ask learners to tell and write sentences using them.","learners":"Listen, pronounce and find words in the text."},{"teacher":"Write the words on the board: strap stripe stroke strike stretch. Read them aloud with distinct pronunciation of the cluster.","learners":"Read the words aloud; point to the cluster in each word."},{"teacher":"Write some words with the same conjunct consonants on the board, for example bl, tr, st.","learners":"Match words that have the same conjunct consonant (black, blue, blanket, blow, blink)."}]},{"activity":"Self-writing: 'Discussion, Writing, Self-review'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.15","steps":[{"teacher":"Start a conversation about a situation: 'a picture of a wedding'. Involve all learners and ask open-ended questions.","learners":"Discuss and answer questions."},{"teacher":"Give writing time at each level: draw then write (Beginner), write about what they liked (Letter), a sentence (Word), a paragraph or story on a topic of their choice (Para/Story).","learners":"Write at their level and take ownership of the work."},{"teacher":"Review: ask 'What did you draw or write?' Have each learner read the text aloud once. Support with writing if needed.","learners":"Read aloud, listen to their pronunciation and correct mistakes."}]}],"levelTasks":[{"activity":"Story - Day 2: level-wise tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.11","tasks":{"Beginner":"Retell with the group by pointing to pictures or words; read aloud with group support (interpretation of the manual's group reading task).","Letter":"Read with the group, pointing to words; say the letters and words they know (interpretation of the manual's group reading task).","Word":"Support the group in writing the questions; read aloud the consonant clusters learned on the first day.","Para":"Ask the group's questions to another group, discuss them, then write answers to all questions individually; the teacher reads and corrects.","Story":"Ask the group's questions to another group, discuss them, then write answers to all questions individually; the teacher reads and corrects."}},{"activity":"Consonant clusters (str): level tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.16-17","tasks":{"Beginner":"Listen to the sound of the cluster and point to it in a word; continue with letter-sound work (interpretation: the manual describes clusters for learners lagging in reading words and sentences).","Letter":"Listen to the cluster sound and pick words with the cluster from a word card (interpretation).","Word":"Find the cluster in the story or textbook words, read the words and write them in the notebook.","Para":"Form words and sentences using the cluster; read the sentences aloud.","Story":"Form words and sentences using the cluster; read the sentences aloud; use them in the story writing."}},{"activity":"Self-writing: level tasks and review","source":"M","ref":"p.15","tasks":{"Beginner":"Draw a picture about the discussion and then write a few sentences about it, expressing thoughts freely. Review: say what they drew or wrote; read the text aloud once; the teacher may write the text in the notebook for them.","Letter":"Write about what they liked, using drawing and writing; write any words or sentences they can. Review: read the text aloud once; correct punctuation mistakes using the Barakhadi chart.","Word":"Write a sentence based on the conversation. Mistakes in spelling, punctuation and sentence structure are fine. Review: read it to the group; discuss and correct mistakes together.","Para":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation.","Story":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation."}}],"organisation":[{"grouping":"Whole class (big group)","how":"All learners of all levels sit in a 'U' shape arranged by level (Beginner, Letter, Word, Para, Story) so that the move to small groups is easy.","activities":["Warm-up: Rhyme - 'I saw a Little Bird'","Oral conversation: What did you see on your way?","Story (Day 2 of the story): retelling","Consonant clusters: introduction","Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on a picture of a wedding"]},{"grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","how":"Learners of similar levels work together; the teacher gives each group a task for its level and spends more time with learners who need support. Rotate responsibilities (for example group leader).","activities":["Story: reading with actions and group questions","Consonant cluster game: Looking for Similar Ones"]},{"grouping":"Individual","how":"Each learner works on a task for their own level; the teacher moves around, observes difficulties and supports individuals.","activities":["Story: writing answers individually","Self-writing: individual writing","Self-writing: review and reading back","Daily reading (10 minutes)"]}],"materials":["Rhyme chart or board (optional)","The same story book as yesterday","Story book","slate or paper for questions","Notebooks","Board","chalk","words list (strap stripe stroke strike stretch)","Words on the board","Picture card or topic on the board","crayons or pencils","Library books or storybooks"],"outcomes":["Learners take part in the oral conversation and speak without fear.","Learners retell the story, read with expression and ask or answer questions at their level.","Learners respond to the sound-symbol task for today (Consonant clusters: str (strap, stripe)) at their own level.","Learners write about the topic at their level and read it aloud.","Each learner reads a book for 10 minutes."],"observation":["Observe each learner's reading and writing during the individual tasks; note who needs individual support and how many learners share the same difficulty.","Note any learner whose level is improving; move the learner to the next level group when you see steady progress (manual p.5).","Record each learner's progress for the day in the notebook, according to the learner's level (manual p.4).","Use today's observations to adjust tomorrow's plan (manual p.5)."],"teacherNotes":["Questions to elicit on Day 2: information questions (answer not in the text), thinking questions (needs knowledge beyond the text) and opinion questions (feedback on something in the text).","Consonant clusters: do these activities daily for learners who find reading complex words hard; the aim is to remove the fear of reading clusters. Teachers may carry out similar activities on their own.","Writing has two parts, content and sequence: encourage learners to read what they wrote, improve it and rewrite it for clarity and correctness (manual p.15).","Pace: the manual says not to assume all learners progress at the same speed. Repeat a day's activity with the groups that need it before moving on.","Special needs: give extra time and prepare materials for slower learners; seat learners with hearing or vision difficulty at the front; for learners who reverse or confuse letters, trace letters on the letter card with a finger and write with dots to trace with a pencil (manual p.6)."],"components":[{"no":1,"key":"warmup","name":"Warm-up activities","keywords":["Rhyme - 'I saw a Little Bird'","two learners lead"],"rows":[1]},{"no":2,"key":"oral","name":"Oral Discussion","keywords":["What did you see on your way?","every learner speaks"],"rows":[2]},{"no":3,"key":"story","name":"Story","keywords":["Day 2","retell","read with actions","group questions","ask and answer","write answers (Para/Story)"],"rows":[3,4,5]},{"no":4,"key":"sound","name":"Sound symbol games, Sound separation-pairing","keywords":["consonant cluster 'str'","pronounce and find words","game: Looking for Similar Ones"],"rows":[6,7]},{"no":5,"key":"mindwrite","name":"Individual-Writing (Day 2)","keywords":["discussion","write at own level","self-review (read aloud)"],"rows":[8,9,10]},{"no":6,"key":"reading","name":"Daily reading","keywords":["library book","read alone","teacher listens"],"rows":[11]}],"preLesson":null},{"programme":"TARL Literacy","id":"lit-072","day":72,"phase":2,"phaseLabel":"Phase 2 (Days 46-90)","title":"Saturday: drama presentation","dayType":"Saturday drama + Self-writing","focus":"Barakhadi / alphabet and phonics chart (line 1, letter 'y') | Self-writing: the story we acted out (a story about working together)","duration":70,"objectives":["Listen, speak and answer in the oral conversation (familiar topic).","Express a story through role play, using voice, facial expressions and gestures.","Develop sound-symbol skills: Barakhadi / alphabet and phonics chart (line 1, letter 'y').","Write about the story and review the writing.","Read independently for 10 minutes every day."],"sequence":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Singing and Spinning","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Learners sit in a circle and pass a small object while you clap with your back turned; when the clapping stops, the learner holding it sings a song, recites a poem or tells a joke. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Pass the object round the circle; sing, recite or tell a joke when the clapping stops.","tlm":"A small object (chalk or pencil)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","n":1},{"activity":"Oral conversation: familiar topic","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Hold a conversation on the topic 'a place I would like to visit'. Give each learner a chance to speak; be patient with learners who need extra time.","learners":"Talk about the topic and listen to others.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.9","n":2},{"activity":"Dramatic presentation: introduction and reading","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Explain what a dramatic presentation is and how it is done. Provide stories discussed during the week and read one aloud once more. Para and Story level learners support Beginner and Letter level learners in reading.","learners":"Listen, read along, then each learner chooses a character.","tlm":"Stories discussed in the week (a story about a hungry traveller; a story about working together)","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":3},{"activity":"Dramatic presentation: planning in small groups","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":8,"teacher":"Each group discusses and plans dialogues; Para or Story level learners write the dialogues. Groups prepare their dramatic presentation.","learners":"Choose characters, plan and rehearse dialogues with facial expressions and gestures.","tlm":"Story, paper for dialogues","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":4},{"activity":"Dramatic presentation: performances and feedback","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":7,"teacher":"Learners sit in a U shape. Each group presents; after each performance, watching learners say what they enjoyed and what could be improved.","learners":"Perform in turn; watch; give feedback.","tlm":"Open space (U-shape seating)","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":5},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart: big group reading","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":3,"teacher":"Show the Barakhadi chart and ask which letter they like. Read the letter 'y' on the chart; learners listen carefully and point to it on their own chart (they do not repeat after you).","learners":"Listen and point to the letter on their own chart.","tlm":"Barakhadi chart, alphabet or phonics chart","source":"M","ref":"p.13","n":6},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart: small-group practice","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Learners practise reading the alphabet or phonics chart in groups and help each other. One learner per group reads aloud. Occasionally ask learners to identify the sounds of letters. Give each level its group task.","learners":"Read the chart in groups; one learner reads aloud; do the level task.","tlm":"Alphabet or phonics chart, board or floor","source":"M","ref":"p.13","n":7},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart: individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":2,"teacher":"Give each learner an individual task for their level and observe closely; assist any learner who needs individual support.","learners":"Say and write a letter or word, a sentence or a short paragraph (by level).","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.13","n":8},{"activity":"Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on the story we acted out (a story about working together)","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Start a conversation about the story used for the drama: 'the story we acted out (a story about working together)'. Involve all learners with open-ended questions.","learners":"Take part in the discussion and share thoughts freely.","tlm":"Picture card or topic on the board","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":9},{"activity":"Self-writing: individual writing","grouping":"Individual","minutes":7,"teacher":"Give each level its task (see level table). Let learners take ownership of what they draw and write; mistakes are fine.","learners":"Draw and write about the topic at their level.","tlm":"Notebooks, crayons or pencils","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":10},{"activity":"Self-writing: review and reading back","grouping":"Individual","minutes":3,"teacher":"Ask each learner 'What did you draw or write?' and have them read it aloud once. Word-level learners read to the group; discuss spelling, punctuation and sentence structure. Help beginners by writing their text in the notebook for them if needed.","learners":"Read what they wrote; correct mistakes after listening to their own reading.","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":11},{"activity":"Daily reading (10 minutes)","grouping":"Individual","minutes":10,"teacher":"Give each learner a library book or any storybook. Move around, listen to individual readers and note their level.","learners":"Read independently a book of their choice.","tlm":"Library books or storybooks","source":"M","ref":"p.7","n":12}],"procedures":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Singing and Spinning","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","steps":[{"teacher":"Seat the learners in a circle; give a small object to one learner.","learners":"Sit in a circle."},{"teacher":"Stand outside the circle with your back to them and clap steadily; they pass the object.","learners":"Pass the object while the clapping continues."},{"teacher":"Stop clapping; the learner holding the object sings, recites or tells a joke.","learners":"Perform, and everybody claps."}]},{"activity":"Oral conversation: familiar topic","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.9","steps":[{"teacher":"Introduce the topic: 'a place I would like to visit'.","learners":"Think about their own experience."},{"teacher":"Ask open questions; give every learner a chance. Involve learners who speak less.","learners":"Speak freely and without fear."},{"teacher":"Praise efforts and sum up.","learners":"Listen and respect each other's ideas."}]},{"activity":"Saturday special: dramatic presentation","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.11","steps":[{"teacher":"Explain what a dramatic presentation is and how it can be done. Give the groups the stories discussed during the week.","learners":"Listen to the explanation."},{"teacher":"Read a story aloud once more. Learners at story and paragraph level support those at beginner and letter level in reading.","learners":"Read along; helpers support their friends."},{"teacher":"After reading, each learner chooses a character from the story.","learners":"Choose a role (boys may play girl roles and girls may play boy roles)."},{"teacher":"In groups, learners discuss and plan the dialogues; paragraph or story level learners write the dialogues.","learners":"Plan and write dialogues together."},{"teacher":"Learners sit in a U shape. Each group presents its drama. After each performance, ask what the audience enjoyed and what could be improved.","learners":"Perform, watch and give kind feedback."}]},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart activity (line 1)","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Small group (level-wise) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.13","steps":[{"teacher":"Show the Barakhadi chart and ask the learners which letter they like. Where is the letter 'y'?","learners":"Look for the letter on the chart."},{"teacher":"Read the letter 'y' on the chart. Learners listen and point to it on their own chart. Make sure they do not repeat after you.","learners":"Listen and point to the letter."},{"teacher":"Learners read the alphabet or phonics chart in their groups and help each other; one learner from each group comes forward to read aloud.","learners":"Read in groups; the representative reads aloud."},{"teacher":"Occasionally ask them to identify the sounds of letters from the chart.","learners":"Say the sound of the letter you point to."},{"teacher":"As an extra activity, write some letters on the floor, call out each letter one by one and let the learners jump onto the correct letter.","learners":"Jump onto the letter that is called."}]},{"activity":"Self-writing: 'Discussion, Writing, Self-review'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.15","steps":[{"teacher":"Start a conversation about the story used for the drama: 'the story we acted out (a story about working together)'. Involve all learners with open-ended questions.","learners":"Discuss and answer questions."},{"teacher":"Give writing time at each level: draw then write (Beginner), write about what they liked (Letter), a sentence (Word), a paragraph or story on a topic of their choice (Para/Story).","learners":"Write at their level and take ownership of the work."},{"teacher":"Review: ask 'What did you draw or write?' Have each learner read the text aloud once. Support with writing if needed.","learners":"Read aloud, listen to their pronunciation and correct mistakes."}]}],"levelTasks":[{"activity":"Drama: roles by level","source":"M","ref":"p.11","tasks":{"Beginner":"Take a character role and say or act short lines with help from Para and Story level learners.","Letter":"Take a character role and say or act short lines with help from Para and Story level learners.","Word":"Take a role and speak the dialogues; help rehearse.","Para":"Write the dialogues for the group and support Beginner, Letter and Word level learners throughout.","Story":"Write the dialogues for the group and support Beginner, Letter and Word level learners throughout."}},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart: level tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.13","tasks":{"Beginner":"Small group: read the chart in the group; find and write favourite letters from the line. Individual: say and write a letter of their choice.","Letter":"Small group: read the chart; find and write favourite letters or words from any line. Individual: say a word on their own that begins with any letter.","Word":"Small group: write one or two lines of letters on the board or floor and use them to form words. Individual: speak and write sentences using words they know.","Para":"Small group: prepare word lists using the Barakhadi chart (for example items found in a shop or in the kitchen). Individual: write short paragraphs using the words formed with the Barakhadi chart.","Story":"Small group: prepare word lists using the Barakhadi chart. Individual: write short paragraphs using the words formed with the Barakhadi chart."}},{"activity":"Self-writing: level tasks and review","source":"M","ref":"p.15","tasks":{"Beginner":"Draw a picture about the discussion and then write a few sentences about it, expressing thoughts freely. Review: say what they drew or wrote; read the text aloud once; the teacher may write the text in the notebook for them.","Letter":"Write about what they liked, using drawing and writing; write any words or sentences they can. Review: read the text aloud once; correct punctuation mistakes using the Barakhadi chart.","Word":"Write a sentence based on the conversation. Mistakes in spelling, punctuation and sentence structure are fine. Review: read it to the group; discuss and correct mistakes together.","Para":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation.","Story":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation."}}],"organisation":[{"grouping":"Whole class (big group)","how":"All learners of all levels sit in a 'U' shape arranged by level (Beginner, Letter, Word, Para, Story) so that the move to small groups is easy.","activities":["Warm-up: Singing and Spinning","Oral conversation: familiar topic","Dramatic presentation: introduction and reading","Dramatic presentation: performances and feedback","Barakhadi chart: big group reading","Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on the story we acted out (a story about working together)"]},{"grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","how":"Learners of similar levels work together; the teacher gives each group a task for its level and spends more time with learners who need support. Rotate responsibilities (for example group leader).","activities":["Dramatic presentation: planning in small groups","Barakhadi chart: small-group practice"]},{"grouping":"Individual","how":"Each learner works on a task for their own level; the teacher moves around, observes difficulties and supports individuals.","activities":["Barakhadi chart: individual tasks","Self-writing: individual writing","Self-writing: review and reading back","Daily reading (10 minutes)"]}],"materials":["A small object (chalk or pencil)","Stories discussed in the week (a story about a hungry traveller; a story about working together)","Story","paper for dialogues","Open space (U-shape seating)","Barakhadi chart","alphabet or phonics chart","Alphabet or phonics chart","board or floor","Notebooks","Picture card or topic on the board","crayons or pencils","Library books or storybooks"],"outcomes":["Learners take part in the oral conversation and speak without fear.","Learners present a role in the group drama and give feedback to others.","Learners respond to the sound-symbol task for today (Barakhadi / alphabet and phonics chart (line 1, letter 'y')) at their own level.","Learners write about the story at their level and read it aloud.","Each learner reads a book for 10 minutes."],"observation":["Observe each learner's reading and writing during the individual tasks; note who needs individual support and how many learners share the same difficulty.","Note any learner whose level is improving; move the learner to the next level group when you see steady progress (manual p.5).","Record each learner's progress for the day in the notebook, according to the learner's level (manual p.4).","Use today's observations to adjust tomorrow's plan (manual p.5)."],"teacherNotes":["Saturday: this plan assumes Day 1 is a Monday (six teaching days per week). If your school week is different, hold the drama presentation on your Saturday and keep the other days in sequence.","Barakhadi: learners who need extra time should get repeated practice using one or two sound units at a time. Topic-based discussion helps oral expression, thinking and understanding.","Writing has two parts, content and sequence: encourage learners to read what they wrote, improve it and rewrite it for clarity and correctness (manual p.15).","Pace: the manual says not to assume all learners progress at the same speed. Repeat a day's activity with the groups that need it before moving on.","Special needs: give extra time and prepare materials for slower learners; seat learners with hearing or vision difficulty at the front; for learners who reverse or confuse letters, trace letters on the letter card with a finger and write with dots to trace with a pencil (manual p.6)."],"components":[{"no":1,"key":"warmup","name":"Warm-up activities","keywords":["Singing and Spinning","two learners lead"],"rows":[1]},{"no":2,"key":"oral","name":"Oral Discussion","keywords":["familiar topic","every learner speaks"],"rows":[2]},{"no":3,"key":"story","name":"Story (Saturday: dramatic presentation)","keywords":["Saturday drama","choose a character","plan dialogues","perform in U shape","feedback"],"rows":[3,4,5]},{"no":4,"key":"sound","name":"Sound symbol games, Sound separation-pairing","keywords":["Barakhadi / alphabet chart","listen and point (no repeating)","group reading","level tasks"],"rows":[6,7,8]},{"no":5,"key":"mindwrite","name":"Individual-Writing (Day 2)","keywords":["discussion","write at own level","self-review (read aloud)"],"rows":[9,10,11]},{"no":6,"key":"reading","name":"Daily reading","keywords":["library book","read alone","teacher listens"],"rows":[12]}],"preLesson":null},{"programme":"TARL Literacy","id":"lit-073","day":73,"phase":2,"phaseLabel":"Phase 2 (Days 46-90)","title":"Story: a story about a tea garden or a hill village (Day 1)","dayType":"Story Day 1 + Mind mapping","focus":"Language game: Last Letter Chain (Antakshari of words) | Mind map: vehicles","duration":70,"objectives":["Listen, speak and answer in the oral conversation (conversation on a picture).","Listen to and read a story with understanding; discuss it in big and small groups and respond at their own level.","Develop sound-symbol skills: Language game: Last Letter Chain (Antakshari of words).","Build vocabulary through a mind map ('vehicles') and use the words at their own level.","Read independently for 10 minutes every day."],"sequence":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Rain clapping","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Everyone stands in a circle with eyes closed and keeps clapping: first one finger, then two, three, four and finally five fingers. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Stand in a circle, close the eyes and clap with 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 fingers.","tlm":"After the activity ask: What did the sound remind you of?","source":"M","ref":"p.8","n":1},{"activity":"Oral conversation: conversation on a picture","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Show a picture of a mango tree with birds and children and ask what is happening, who is doing what and what is happening around them. Let learners think creatively and even make up a story.","learners":"Look at the picture, answer questions and make up their own story about it.","tlm":"Picture card of a mango tree with birds and children","source":"M","ref":"p.9","n":2},{"activity":"Story (Day 1 of the story): reading aloud and discussion","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":8,"teacher":"Discuss the title or picture of the story with the learners. Read the story aloud with expression and voice modulation (learners do not repeat after you). Discuss it, with emphasis on factual questions. Read it again slowly, pointing to each word.","learners":"Talk about the title/picture; listen; answer questions; follow each word with a finger in their own copy.","tlm":"A story from the school library (a story about a tea garden or a hill village), a copy for each learner","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":3},{"activity":"Story: reading in small groups","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":7,"teacher":"Form level-wise groups with a group leader. Learners read the story one sentence at a time while the others follow with their fingers. Para and Story level learners practise reading with emotion and expression.","learners":"Read the story sentence by sentence, supporting each other; the group leader helps.","tlm":"Story book copies","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":4},{"activity":"Story: level-wise individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":5,"teacher":"Give each learner the task for their level (see level table) and support those who need it.","learners":"Beginner/Letter: find and write favourite words or letters. Word: find consonant clusters. Para/Story: silently read, find unfamiliar and rhyming words.","tlm":"Story book, notebooks, board","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":5},{"activity":"Language game: Last Letter Chain (Antakshari of words)","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Two groups take turns; each word must begin with the last letter of the previous word. Observe each learner and give help where needed.","learners":"Play the game, take turns and read or say the words they make.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.20","n":6},{"activity":"Mind mapping (Day 1): the word 'vehicles'","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Ask: 'What words come to your mind when you hear the word vehicles?' Write learners' answers on the board or floor (Para and Story level learners write the words themselves). Guide the map towards the learning objective. Example words: bus, truck, bicycle, scooter, boat, steamer, ship, raft, plane, train, helicopter, balloon.","learners":"Say words connected with 'vehicles'; share the meaning and feeling of words.","tlm":"Board, chalk (or floor)","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":7},{"activity":"Mind mapping: classify the words","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":4,"teacher":"Ask learners to classify the words in groups, for example: On road: bus, truck, bicycle, scooter; On water: boat, steamer, ship, raft; In the air and on rails: plane, train, helicopter, balloon.","learners":"Sort the words into groups and say why.","tlm":"Board, chalk, word cards (optional)","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":8},{"activity":"Mind mapping: level-wise individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":6,"teacher":"Give each learner the individual task for their level; observe closely and give individual support. Display corrected stories on the wall.","learners":"Complete the task for their level (see level table).","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":9},{"activity":"Daily reading (10 minutes)","grouping":"Individual","minutes":10,"teacher":"Give each learner a library book or any storybook. Move around, listen to individual readers and note their level.","learners":"Read independently a book of their choice.","tlm":"Library books or storybooks","source":"M","ref":"p.7","n":10}],"procedures":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Rain clapping","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","steps":[{"teacher":"Stand the learners in a circle and ask them to close their eyes. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Stand in a circle and close their eyes."},{"teacher":"Start clapping with one finger; then two fingers, three, four and finally five fingers.","learners":"Keep clapping, copying the change of fingers."},{"teacher":"After the activity ask: What did the sound remind you of?","learners":"Tell how they felt and what the sounds reminded them of."}]},{"activity":"Oral conversation: conversation on a picture","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.9","steps":[{"teacher":"Show the picture of a mango tree with birds and children.","learners":"Look carefully."},{"teacher":"Ask: What is happening in the picture? Who is doing what? What is happening around them? Then: What might happen next?","learners":"Answer in their own words; every learner gets a chance."},{"teacher":"Let learners imagine and make up a short story from the picture.","learners":"Tell their stories to the class."}]},{"activity":"Story - Day 1 (a story about a tea garden or a hill village)","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.10","steps":[{"teacher":"Discuss the title or picture of the story with the learners.","learners":"Talk about what they see and what the story may be about."},{"teacher":"Read the story aloud with expression and proper voice modulation. Learners should not simply repeat after you.","learners":"Listen carefully and enjoy the story."},{"teacher":"Discuss the story: factual, logical, vocabulary-based, judgment or opinion questions (today's focus: factual: Who was in the story? Where did it happen? What did the character do first?). Begin in the home language if needed.","learners":"Think and respond thoughtfully; every learner takes part."},{"teacher":"Read the story again slowly, pointing to each word. Make sure each learner has a copy and follows with a finger.","learners":"Follow each word with their finger."},{"teacher":"Ask learners to read in small groups; select a group leader who helps the others. Learners read one sentence at a time while the others point with fingers.","learners":"Read with the help of one another."}]},{"activity":"Language game: Last Letter Chain (Antakshari of words)","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.20","steps":[{"teacher":"Divide the learners into two groups. A learner from the first group says a word, for example 'peas'.","learners":"Listen to the word and its last letter."},{"teacher":"A learner from the second group must say a new word starting with the last letter of 'peas', for example 'sun'.","learners":"Think quickly and say a word that starts with the last letter."},{"teacher":"Continue, with each group taking turns.","learners":"Cheer your group and listen carefully."}]},{"activity":"Mind mapping: 'vehicles'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Small group (level-wise) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.14","steps":[{"teacher":"Choose a word that can generate many related words: 'vehicles'. Ask: 'What words come to your mind when you hear the word vehicles?' Write the answers on the board or floor.","learners":"Say words they link with 'vehicles'."},{"teacher":"Discuss the words: what they mean and how they are connected.","learners":"Explain their words and listen to others."},{"teacher":"In small groups, let the learners classify the words (On road: bus, truck, bicycle, scooter; On water: boat, steamer, ship, raft; In the air and on rails: plane, train, helicopter, balloon).","learners":"Sort the words into groups."},{"teacher":"Give the individual tasks by level and help each learner.","learners":"Work individually; read the work aloud at the end if time allows."}]}],"levelTasks":[{"activity":"Story - Day 1: individual tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.10","tasks":{"Beginner":"Circle or search for a favourite word or letter in the story and say it aloud. If a learner cannot draw a circle, write words on the board and ask them to identify them.","Letter":"Find, read and write favourite words from the story.","Word":"Find the consonant clusters in the story, read them and write them in the notebook.","Para":"Silently read the story from the textbook; find unfamiliar words and try to understand them; find rhyming words, use them in sentences and write in the notebook; ask other groups for meanings; make questions in groups.","Story":"Silently read the story; find unfamiliar words and rhyming words; practise reading with emotion; one group reads sentences formed with consonant clusters to the other group; ask and answer group questions (information, thinking and opinion questions)."}},{"activity":"Language game: Last Letter Chain (Antakshari of words) - level support","source":"I","ref":"p.20","tasks":{"Beginner":"Take part by saying or pointing to the letters involved and by listening carefully; Para and Story level partners help.","Letter":"Say the letters/sounds and give simple words they know.","Word":"Say and write words and short sentences for the game.","Para":"Write sentences with the words; help groups to record answers.","Story":"Write sentences or short stories with the words; help groups to record answers."}},{"activity":"Mind mapping 'vehicles': level tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.14","tasks":{"Beginner":"Circle all the words that contain the letter 'T' on the board; make a list. See how many learners find the most words.","Letter":"Circle all the words that contain the letter 'T' and make a list of them.","Word":"Use 4-5 words (for example bus, boat, raft, ship, plane) to form sentences, starting with words of one or two syllables. Example: Dream - I had a dream last night.","Para":"Choose any five words from the map and create a story with them. Use consonant clusters correctly, read the story aloud, correct mistakes of sentence structure, spelling or grammar, then display it on the wall.","Story":"Choose any five words from the map and create a story with them. Use consonant clusters correctly, read the story aloud, correct mistakes of sentence structure, spelling or grammar, then display it on the wall."}}],"organisation":[{"grouping":"Whole class (big group)","how":"All learners of all levels sit in a 'U' shape arranged by level (Beginner, Letter, Word, Para, Story) so that the move to small groups is easy.","activities":["Warm-up: Rain clapping","Oral conversation: conversation on a picture","Story (Day 1 of the story): reading aloud and discussion","Language game: Last Letter Chain (Antakshari of words)","Mind mapping (Day 1): the word 'vehicles'"]},{"grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","how":"Learners of similar levels work together; the teacher gives each group a task for its level and spends more time with learners who need support. Rotate responsibilities (for example group leader).","activities":["Story: reading in small groups","Mind mapping: classify the words"]},{"grouping":"Individual","how":"Each learner works on a task for their own level; the teacher moves around, observes difficulties and supports individuals.","activities":["Story: level-wise individual tasks","Mind mapping: level-wise individual tasks","Daily reading (10 minutes)"]}],"materials":["After the activity ask: What did the sound remind you of?","Picture card of a mango tree with birds","children","A story from the school library (a story about a tea garden or a hill village)","a copy for each learner","Story book copies","Story book","notebooks","board","Board","chalk (or floor)","chalk","word cards (optional)","Notebooks","Library books or storybooks"],"outcomes":["Learners take part in the oral conversation and speak without fear.","Learners show understanding of the story in the discussion and complete the task for their level.","Learners respond to the sound-symbol task for today (Language game: Last Letter Chain (Antakshari of words)) at their own level.","Learners add words to the mind map and use them in sentences or a story at their level.","Each learner reads a book for 10 minutes."],"observation":["Observe each learner's reading and writing during the individual tasks; note who needs individual support and how many learners share the same difficulty.","Note any learner whose level is improving; move the learner to the next level group when you see steady progress (manual p.5).","Record each learner's progress for the day in the notebook, according to the learner's level (manual p.4).","Use today's observations to adjust tomorrow's plan (manual p.5)."],"teacherNotes":["Story selection: the manual asks teachers to use picture story books or stories in the school library. Today's suggested theme (a story about a tea garden or a hill village) is a planning suggestion; use any suitable story you have.","The manual lists the letter and word games but does not fix the slot in the daily timetable where they are used. This plan places them in the 10-minute sound-symbol / alphabet slot (interpretation).","Mind mapping topic for this day: 'vehicles'. The manual's example uses the word 'shop'; today's topic follows the same method.","Pace: the manual says not to assume all learners progress at the same speed. Repeat a day's activity with the groups that need it before moving on.","Special needs: give extra time and prepare materials for slower learners; seat learners with hearing or vision difficulty at the front; for learners who reverse or confuse letters, trace letters on the letter card with a finger and write with dots to trace with a pencil (manual p.6)."],"components":[{"no":1,"key":"warmup","name":"Warm-up activities","keywords":["Rain clapping","two learners lead"],"rows":[1]},{"no":2,"key":"oral","name":"Oral Discussion","keywords":["conversation on a picture","every learner speaks"],"rows":[2]},{"no":3,"key":"story","name":"Story","keywords":["Day 1","title / picture talk","read aloud with expression","factual questions","re-read pointing","group reading","level tasks"],"rows":[3,4,5]},{"no":4,"key":"sound","name":"Sound symbol games, Sound separation-pairing","keywords":["Last Letter Chain (Antakshari of words)","play in turns","level support"],"rows":[6]},{"no":5,"key":"mindwrite","name":"Mind Mapping (Day 1)","keywords":["mind map: vehicles","classify the words","level task: circle letter T / sentences / story"],"rows":[7,8,9]},{"no":6,"key":"reading","name":"Daily reading","keywords":["library book","read alone","teacher listens"],"rows":[10]}],"preLesson":null},{"programme":"TARL Literacy","id":"lit-074","day":74,"phase":2,"phaseLabel":"Phase 2 (Days 46-90)","title":"Story: a story about a tea garden or a hill village (Day 2)","dayType":"Story Day 2 + Self-writing","focus":"Consonant clusters: spr (spring, spray) | Self-writing: a day when I was very happy","duration":70,"objectives":["Listen, speak and answer in the oral conversation (listening and storytelling).","Retell the story, read it with expression, ask and answer questions about it and write answers.","Develop sound-symbol skills: Consonant clusters: spr (spring, spray).","Write about a topic at their own level and review the writing (a day when I was very happy).","Read independently for 10 minutes every day."],"sequence":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Writing with body parts","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Learners stand in a circle. Demonstrate writing the word 'boat' in the air with a finger, then ask them to write it with different body parts. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Write the word 'boat' in the air with the finger, then with the head, shoulders, knees or elbows.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.8","n":1},{"activity":"Oral conversation: listening and storytelling","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Tell an interesting story starter and involve the learners: 'A train stopped in front of our school. Who got out?' Let learners imagine and continue the story.","learners":"Listen to the teacher, then imagine and continue the story. Learners can also recite a rhyme or story they know.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.9","n":2},{"activity":"Story (Day 2 of the story): retelling","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":6,"teacher":"Ask learners to retell yesterday's story in their own words. Prompt with questions on the beginning, middle and end.","learners":"Retell the story using their own words.","tlm":"The same story book as yesterday","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":3},{"activity":"Story: reading with actions and group questions","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":9,"teacher":"Learners practise reading with actions and expressions; one learner per group reads aloud to the class. Guide groups to make questions about the story (guide initially). Groups take turns to ask and answer each other's questions. Word-level learners also read aloud the consonants learned on the first day.","learners":"Read with actions; make questions (word-level learners help write them); ask and answer questions with another group.","tlm":"Story book, slate or paper for questions","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":4},{"activity":"Story: writing answers individually","grouping":"Individual","minutes":5,"teacher":"Para and Story level learners write answers to all questions individually; read and correct their responses after they finish.","learners":"Write the answers in their notebooks; Beginner/Letter/Word learners read or listen and answer orally.","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":5},{"activity":"Consonant clusters: introduction","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":4,"teacher":"Three-letter clusters: after two-letter clusters, familiarise learners with clusters of three letters ('spr' as in spring, spray, spread). Discuss the words, then ask learners to tell and write sentences using them.","learners":"Listen, pronounce the cluster and say words that contain it.","tlm":"Board and chalk, words list (spring spray spread sprout spring)","source":"M","ref":"p.16","n":6},{"activity":"Consonant cluster game: Who is Whose Friend?","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":6,"teacher":"Prepare cards: some with broken parts of conjunct consonants (b + l, c + r, s + t) and some with the full form (bl as in black, cr as in crab, st as in star). Take out all the cards. Observe closely and help learners who need support.","learners":"Match each full form with its broken parts and discover 'who is whose friend'.","tlm":"Broken-part cards and full-form cards","source":"M","ref":"p.17","n":7},{"activity":"Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on a day when I was very happy","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Start a conversation about a picture card: 'a day when I was very happy'. Involve all learners and ask open-ended questions.","learners":"Take part in the discussion and share thoughts freely.","tlm":"Picture card or topic on the board","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":8},{"activity":"Self-writing: individual writing","grouping":"Individual","minutes":7,"teacher":"Give each level its task (see level table). Let learners take ownership of what they draw and write; mistakes are fine.","learners":"Draw and write about the topic at their level.","tlm":"Notebooks, crayons or pencils","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":9},{"activity":"Self-writing: review and reading back","grouping":"Individual","minutes":3,"teacher":"Ask each learner 'What did you draw or write?' and have them read it aloud once. Word-level learners read to the group; discuss spelling, punctuation and sentence structure. Help beginners by writing their text in the notebook for them if needed.","learners":"Read what they wrote; correct mistakes after listening to their own reading.","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":10},{"activity":"Daily reading (10 minutes)","grouping":"Individual","minutes":10,"teacher":"Give each learner a library book or any storybook. Move around, listen to individual readers and note their level.","learners":"Read independently a book of their choice.","tlm":"Library books or storybooks","source":"M","ref":"p.7","n":11}],"procedures":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Writing with body parts","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","steps":[{"teacher":"Stand the learners in a circle. Demonstrate writing the word 'boat' in the air with your finger.","learners":"Watch and then copy with their own finger."},{"teacher":"Ask them to write it again using nose and other body parts (head, shoulders, knees, ...).","learners":"Write the letters in the air with the named body part."},{"teacher":"Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Take turns to lead."}]},{"activity":"Oral conversation: listening and storytelling","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.9","steps":[{"teacher":"Say the starter: 'A train stopped in front of our school. Who got out?'","learners":"Listen and imagine."},{"teacher":"Ask learners to continue the story one by one. Encourage those who speak less.","learners":"Add ideas to the story."},{"teacher":"Invite a learner to recite a poem or rhyme they know.","learners":"Recite and listen to others."}]},{"activity":"Story - Day 2 (a story about a tea garden or a hill village)","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.11","steps":[{"teacher":"Ask learners to retell the story they read yesterday in their own words.","learners":"Retell, helping each other remember."},{"teacher":"In small groups learners practise reading the story using actions and expressions; one learner from each group then reads aloud to the class.","learners":"Read with actions and expression; a representative reads aloud."},{"teacher":"Guide the groups to come up with questions about the story (guide initially). Word-level learners can support by helping write them down.","learners":"Make questions together."},{"teacher":"Groups take turns to ask and answer each other's questions. Useful kinds: questions whose answer is not in the text; questions needing thinking beyond the text; questions asking for an opinion.","learners":"Ask, answer and discuss in the groups."},{"teacher":"Word-level learners also read aloud the consonants they learned on the first day.","learners":"Read the consonant clusters aloud."}]},{"activity":"Consonant clusters (spr) and the game 'Who is Whose Friend?'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.16-17","steps":[{"teacher":"Three-letter clusters: after two-letter clusters, familiarise learners with clusters of three letters ('spr' as in spring, spray, spread). Discuss the words, then ask learners to tell and write sentences using them.","learners":"Listen, pronounce and find words in the text."},{"teacher":"Write the words on the board: spring spray spread sprout spring. Read them aloud with distinct pronunciation of the cluster.","learners":"Read the words aloud; point to the cluster in each word."},{"teacher":"Prepare cards: some with broken parts of conjunct consonants (b + l, c + r, s + t) and some with the full form (bl as in black, cr as in crab, st as in star). Take out all the cards.","learners":"Match each full form with its broken parts and discover 'who is whose friend'."}]},{"activity":"Self-writing: 'Discussion, Writing, Self-review'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.15","steps":[{"teacher":"Start a conversation about a picture card: 'a day when I was very happy'. Involve all learners and ask open-ended questions.","learners":"Discuss and answer questions."},{"teacher":"Give writing time at each level: draw then write (Beginner), write about what they liked (Letter), a sentence (Word), a paragraph or story on a topic of their choice (Para/Story).","learners":"Write at their level and take ownership of the work."},{"teacher":"Review: ask 'What did you draw or write?' Have each learner read the text aloud once. Support with writing if needed.","learners":"Read aloud, listen to their pronunciation and correct mistakes."}]}],"levelTasks":[{"activity":"Story - Day 2: level-wise tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.11","tasks":{"Beginner":"Retell with the group by pointing to pictures or words; read aloud with group support (interpretation of the manual's group reading task).","Letter":"Read with the group, pointing to words; say the letters and words they know (interpretation of the manual's group reading task).","Word":"Support the group in writing the questions; read aloud the consonant clusters learned on the first day.","Para":"Ask the group's questions to another group, discuss them, then write answers to all questions individually; the teacher reads and corrects.","Story":"Ask the group's questions to another group, discuss them, then write answers to all questions individually; the teacher reads and corrects."}},{"activity":"Consonant clusters (spr): level tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.16-17","tasks":{"Beginner":"Listen to the sound of the cluster and point to it in a word; continue with letter-sound work (interpretation: the manual describes clusters for learners lagging in reading words and sentences).","Letter":"Listen to the cluster sound and pick words with the cluster from a word card (interpretation).","Word":"Find the cluster in the story or textbook words, read the words and write them in the notebook.","Para":"Form words and sentences using the cluster; read the sentences aloud.","Story":"Form words and sentences using the cluster; read the sentences aloud; use them in the story writing."}},{"activity":"Self-writing: level tasks and review","source":"M","ref":"p.15","tasks":{"Beginner":"Draw a picture about the discussion and then write a few sentences about it, expressing thoughts freely. Review: say what they drew or wrote; read the text aloud once; the teacher may write the text in the notebook for them.","Letter":"Write about what they liked, using drawing and writing; write any words or sentences they can. Review: read the text aloud once; correct punctuation mistakes using the Barakhadi chart.","Word":"Write a sentence based on the conversation. Mistakes in spelling, punctuation and sentence structure are fine. Review: read it to the group; discuss and correct mistakes together.","Para":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation.","Story":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation."}}],"organisation":[{"grouping":"Whole class (big group)","how":"All learners of all levels sit in a 'U' shape arranged by level (Beginner, Letter, Word, Para, Story) so that the move to small groups is easy.","activities":["Warm-up: Writing with body parts","Oral conversation: listening and storytelling","Story (Day 2 of the story): retelling","Consonant clusters: introduction","Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on a day when I was very happy"]},{"grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","how":"Learners of similar levels work together; the teacher gives each group a task for its level and spends more time with learners who need support. Rotate responsibilities (for example group leader).","activities":["Story: reading with actions and group questions","Consonant cluster game: Who is Whose Friend?"]},{"grouping":"Individual","how":"Each learner works on a task for their own level; the teacher moves around, observes difficulties and supports individuals.","activities":["Story: writing answers individually","Self-writing: individual writing","Self-writing: review and reading back","Daily reading (10 minutes)"]}],"materials":["The same story book as yesterday","Story book","slate or paper for questions","Notebooks","Board","chalk","words list (spring spray spread sprout spring)","Broken-part cards","full-form cards","Picture card or topic on the board","crayons or pencils","Library books or storybooks"],"outcomes":["Learners take part in the oral conversation and speak without fear.","Learners retell the story, read with expression and ask or answer questions at their level.","Learners respond to the sound-symbol task for today (Consonant clusters: spr (spring, spray)) at their own level.","Learners write about the topic at their level and read it aloud.","Each learner reads a book for 10 minutes."],"observation":["Observe each learner's reading and writing during the individual tasks; note who needs individual support and how many learners share the same difficulty.","Note any learner whose level is improving; move the learner to the next level group when you see steady progress (manual p.5).","Record each learner's progress for the day in the notebook, according to the learner's level (manual p.4).","Use today's observations to adjust tomorrow's plan (manual p.5)."],"teacherNotes":["Questions to elicit on Day 2: information questions (answer not in the text), thinking questions (needs knowledge beyond the text) and opinion questions (feedback on something in the text).","Consonant clusters: do these activities daily for learners who find reading complex words hard; the aim is to remove the fear of reading clusters. Teachers may carry out similar activities on their own.","Writing has two parts, content and sequence: encourage learners to read what they wrote, improve it and rewrite it for clarity and correctness (manual p.15).","Pace: the manual says not to assume all learners progress at the same speed. Repeat a day's activity with the groups that need it before moving on.","Special needs: give extra time and prepare materials for slower learners; seat learners with hearing or vision difficulty at the front; for learners who reverse or confuse letters, trace letters on the letter card with a finger and write with dots to trace with a pencil (manual p.6)."],"components":[{"no":1,"key":"warmup","name":"Warm-up activities","keywords":["Writing with body parts","two learners lead"],"rows":[1]},{"no":2,"key":"oral","name":"Oral Discussion","keywords":["listening and storytelling","every learner speaks"],"rows":[2]},{"no":3,"key":"story","name":"Story","keywords":["Day 2","retell","read with actions","group questions","ask and answer","write answers (Para/Story)"],"rows":[3,4,5]},{"no":4,"key":"sound","name":"Sound symbol games, Sound separation-pairing","keywords":["consonant cluster 'spr'","pronounce and find words","game: Who is Whose Friend?"],"rows":[6,7]},{"no":5,"key":"mindwrite","name":"Individual-Writing (Day 2)","keywords":["discussion","write at own level","self-review (read aloud)"],"rows":[8,9,10]},{"no":6,"key":"reading","name":"Daily reading","keywords":["library book","read alone","teacher listens"],"rows":[11]}],"preLesson":null},{"programme":"TARL Literacy","id":"lit-075","day":75,"phase":2,"phaseLabel":"Phase 2 (Days 46-90)","title":"Story: a story about a fisherman (Day 1)","dayType":"Story Day 1 + Mind mapping","focus":"Barakhadi / alphabet and phonics chart (line 4, letter 'e') | Mind map: sports","duration":70,"objectives":["Listen, speak and answer in the oral conversation (What did you see on your way?).","Listen to and read a story with understanding; discuss it in big and small groups and respond at their own level.","Develop sound-symbol skills: Barakhadi / alphabet and phonics chart (line 4, letter 'e').","Build vocabulary through a mind map ('sports') and use the words at their own level.","Read independently for 10 minutes every day."],"sequence":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Alphabet song (last-letter word chain)","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Say a word to the big group, for example 'tea'. Learners say a word that starts with the last letter ('a'). A learner who cannot say a word is out. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Say a word that starts with the last letter of the previous word; step out if unable to.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.8","n":1},{"activity":"Oral conversation: What did you see on your way?","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Ask learners to describe what they saw on their way to school. If they are hesitant, begin yourself: 'This morning I saw a flock of ducks crossing the road and a girl carrying water. What did you see?'","learners":"Describe what they saw on the way to school and connect with what others share.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.9","n":2},{"activity":"Story (Day 1 of the story): reading aloud and discussion","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":8,"teacher":"Discuss the title or picture of the story with the learners. Read the story aloud with expression and voice modulation (learners do not repeat after you). Discuss it, with emphasis on logical questions. Read it again slowly, pointing to each word.","learners":"Talk about the title/picture; listen; answer questions; follow each word with a finger in their own copy.","tlm":"A story from the school library (a story about a fisherman), a copy for each learner","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":3},{"activity":"Story: reading in small groups","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":7,"teacher":"Form level-wise groups with a group leader. Learners read the story one sentence at a time while the others follow with their fingers. Para and Story level learners practise reading with emotion and expression.","learners":"Read the story sentence by sentence, supporting each other; the group leader helps.","tlm":"Story book copies","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":4},{"activity":"Story: level-wise individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":5,"teacher":"Give each learner the task for their level (see level table) and support those who need it.","learners":"Beginner/Letter: find and write favourite words or letters. Word: find consonant clusters. Para/Story: silently read, find unfamiliar and rhyming words.","tlm":"Story book, notebooks, board","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":5},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart: big group reading","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":3,"teacher":"Show the Barakhadi chart and ask which letter they like. Read the letter 'e' on the chart; learners listen carefully and point to it on their own chart (they do not repeat after you).","learners":"Listen and point to the letter on their own chart.","tlm":"Barakhadi chart, alphabet or phonics chart","source":"M","ref":"p.13","n":6},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart: small-group practice","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Learners practise reading the alphabet or phonics chart in groups and help each other. One learner per group reads aloud. Occasionally ask learners to identify the sounds of letters. Give each level its group task.","learners":"Read the chart in groups; one learner reads aloud; do the level task.","tlm":"Alphabet or phonics chart, board or floor","source":"M","ref":"p.13","n":7},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart: individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":2,"teacher":"Give each learner an individual task for their level and observe closely; assist any learner who needs individual support.","learners":"Say and write a letter or word, a sentence or a short paragraph (by level).","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.13","n":8},{"activity":"Mind mapping (Day 1): the word 'sports'","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Ask: 'What words come to your mind when you hear the word sports?' Write learners' answers on the board or floor (Para and Story level learners write the words themselves). Guide the map towards the learning objective. Example words: cricket, football, kabaddi, kho-kho, carrom, chess, ludo, cards, ball, bat, net, whistle.","learners":"Say words connected with 'sports'; share the meaning and feeling of words.","tlm":"Board, chalk (or floor)","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":9},{"activity":"Mind mapping: classify the words","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":4,"teacher":"Ask learners to classify the words in groups, for example: Outdoor: cricket, football, kabaddi, kho-kho; Indoor: carrom, chess, ludo, cards; Things: ball, bat, net, whistle.","learners":"Sort the words into groups and say why.","tlm":"Board, chalk, word cards (optional)","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":10},{"activity":"Mind mapping: level-wise individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":6,"teacher":"Give each learner the individual task for their level; observe closely and give individual support. Display corrected stories on the wall.","learners":"Complete the task for their level (see level table).","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":11},{"activity":"Daily reading (10 minutes)","grouping":"Individual","minutes":10,"teacher":"Give each learner a library book or any storybook. Move around, listen to individual readers and note their level.","learners":"Read independently a book of their choice.","tlm":"Library books or storybooks","source":"M","ref":"p.7","n":12}],"procedures":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Alphabet song (last-letter word chain)","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","steps":[{"teacher":"Say the word 'tea' to the big group and show that its last letter is 'a'.","learners":"Listen and think of a word starting with 'a'."},{"teacher":"Ask learners in turn to say a word that starts with the last letter of the previous word. Example: rain -> nest.","learners":"Say a word in turn; anyone who cannot say a word is out of the game."},{"teacher":"Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Lead the game when it is their turn."}]},{"activity":"Oral conversation: What did you see on your way?","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.9","steps":[{"teacher":"Ask: 'What did you see on your way to school today?'","learners":"Think about the way to school."},{"teacher":"If learners hesitate, start: 'This morning I saw a flock of ducks crossing the road and a girl carrying water. What did you see?'","learners":"Listen to the model and then share their own observations."},{"teacher":"Connect learners' answers with each other.","learners":"Listen and add what they noticed."}]},{"activity":"Story - Day 1 (a story about a fisherman)","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.10","steps":[{"teacher":"Discuss the title or picture of the story with the learners.","learners":"Talk about what they see and what the story may be about."},{"teacher":"Read the story aloud with expression and proper voice modulation. Learners should not simply repeat after you.","learners":"Listen carefully and enjoy the story."},{"teacher":"Discuss the story: factual, logical, vocabulary-based, judgment or opinion questions (today's focus: logical: Why did the character do that? What would have happened if ...?). Begin in the home language if needed.","learners":"Think and respond thoughtfully; every learner takes part."},{"teacher":"Read the story again slowly, pointing to each word. Make sure each learner has a copy and follows with a finger.","learners":"Follow each word with their finger."},{"teacher":"Ask learners to read in small groups; select a group leader who helps the others. Learners read one sentence at a time while the others point with fingers.","learners":"Read with the help of one another."}]},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart activity (line 4)","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Small group (level-wise) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.13","steps":[{"teacher":"Show the Barakhadi chart and ask the learners which letter they like. Where is the letter 'e'?","learners":"Look for the letter on the chart."},{"teacher":"Read the letter 'e' on the chart. Learners listen and point to it on their own chart. Make sure they do not repeat after you.","learners":"Listen and point to the letter."},{"teacher":"Learners read the alphabet or phonics chart in their groups and help each other; one learner from each group comes forward to read aloud.","learners":"Read in groups; the representative reads aloud."},{"teacher":"Occasionally ask them to identify the sounds of letters from the chart.","learners":"Say the sound of the letter you point to."},{"teacher":"As an extra activity, write some letters on the floor, call out each letter one by one and let the learners jump onto the correct letter.","learners":"Jump onto the letter that is called."}]},{"activity":"Mind mapping: 'sports'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Small group (level-wise) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.14","steps":[{"teacher":"Choose a word that can generate many related words: 'sports'. Ask: 'What words come to your mind when you hear the word sports?' Write the answers on the board or floor.","learners":"Say words they link with 'sports'."},{"teacher":"Discuss the words: what they mean and how they are connected.","learners":"Explain their words and listen to others."},{"teacher":"In small groups, let the learners classify the words (Outdoor: cricket, football, kabaddi, kho-kho; Indoor: carrom, chess, ludo, cards; Things: ball, bat, net, whistle).","learners":"Sort the words into groups."},{"teacher":"Give the individual tasks by level and help each learner.","learners":"Work individually; read the work aloud at the end if time allows."}]}],"levelTasks":[{"activity":"Story - Day 1: individual tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.10","tasks":{"Beginner":"Circle or search for a favourite word or letter in the story and say it aloud. If a learner cannot draw a circle, write words on the board and ask them to identify them.","Letter":"Find, read and write favourite words from the story.","Word":"Find the consonant clusters in the story, read them and write them in the notebook.","Para":"Silently read the story from the textbook; find unfamiliar words and try to understand them; find rhyming words, use them in sentences and write in the notebook; ask other groups for meanings; make questions in groups.","Story":"Silently read the story; find unfamiliar words and rhyming words; practise reading with emotion; one group reads sentences formed with consonant clusters to the other group; ask and answer group questions (information, thinking and opinion questions)."}},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart: level tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.13","tasks":{"Beginner":"Small group: read the chart in the group; find and write favourite letters from the line. Individual: say and write a letter of their choice.","Letter":"Small group: read the chart; find and write favourite letters or words from any line. Individual: say a word on their own that begins with any letter.","Word":"Small group: write one or two lines of letters on the board or floor and use them to form words. Individual: speak and write sentences using words they know.","Para":"Small group: prepare word lists using the Barakhadi chart (for example items found in a shop or in the kitchen). Individual: write short paragraphs using the words formed with the Barakhadi chart.","Story":"Small group: prepare word lists using the Barakhadi chart. Individual: write short paragraphs using the words formed with the Barakhadi chart."}},{"activity":"Mind mapping 'sports': level tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.14","tasks":{"Beginner":"Circle all the words that contain the letter 'A' on the board; make a list. See how many learners find the most words.","Letter":"Circle all the words that contain the letter 'A' and make a list of them.","Word":"Use 4-5 words (for example bat, net, ball, ludo, cards) to form sentences, starting with words of one or two syllables. Example: Dream - I had a dream last night.","Para":"Choose any five words from the map and create a story with them. Use consonant clusters correctly, read the story aloud, correct mistakes of sentence structure, spelling or grammar, then display it on the wall.","Story":"Choose any five words from the map and create a story with them. Use consonant clusters correctly, read the story aloud, correct mistakes of sentence structure, spelling or grammar, then display it on the wall."}}],"organisation":[{"grouping":"Whole class (big group)","how":"All learners of all levels sit in a 'U' shape arranged by level (Beginner, Letter, Word, Para, Story) so that the move to small groups is easy.","activities":["Warm-up: Alphabet song (last-letter word chain)","Oral conversation: What did you see on your way?","Story (Day 1 of the story): reading aloud and discussion","Barakhadi chart: big group reading","Mind mapping (Day 1): the word 'sports'"]},{"grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","how":"Learners of similar levels work together; the teacher gives each group a task for its level and spends more time with learners who need support. Rotate responsibilities (for example group leader).","activities":["Story: reading in small groups","Barakhadi chart: small-group practice","Mind mapping: classify the words"]},{"grouping":"Individual","how":"Each learner works on a task for their own level; the teacher moves around, observes difficulties and supports individuals.","activities":["Story: level-wise individual tasks","Barakhadi chart: individual tasks","Mind mapping: level-wise individual tasks","Daily reading (10 minutes)"]}],"materials":["A story from the school library (a story about a fisherman)","a copy for each learner","Story book copies","Story book","notebooks","board","Barakhadi chart","alphabet or phonics chart","Alphabet or phonics chart","board or floor","Notebooks","Board","chalk (or floor)","chalk","word cards (optional)","Library books or storybooks"],"outcomes":["Learners take part in the oral conversation and speak without fear.","Learners show understanding of the story in the discussion and complete the task for their level.","Learners respond to the sound-symbol task for today (Barakhadi / alphabet and phonics chart (line 4, letter 'e')) at their own level.","Learners add words to the mind map and use them in sentences or a story at their level.","Each learner reads a book for 10 minutes."],"observation":["Observe each learner's reading and writing during the individual tasks; note who needs individual support and how many learners share the same difficulty.","Note any learner whose level is improving; move the learner to the next level group when you see steady progress (manual p.5).","Record each learner's progress for the day in the notebook, according to the learner's level (manual p.4).","Use today's observations to adjust tomorrow's plan (manual p.5)."],"teacherNotes":["Story selection: the manual asks teachers to use picture story books or stories in the school library. Today's suggested theme (a story about a fisherman) is a planning suggestion; use any suitable story you have.","Barakhadi: learners who need extra time should get repeated practice using one or two sound units at a time. Topic-based discussion helps oral expression, thinking and understanding.","Mind mapping topic for this day: 'sports'. The manual's example uses the word 'shop'; today's topic follows the same method.","Level check: if learners have moved up to a new level, celebrate with an appreciation-oriented game (para level to story level): 'Mix and Match' or 'With the Help of Paragraph Cards' (manual p.42-45). Teachers may use such activities on their own.","Pace: the manual says not to assume all learners progress at the same speed. Repeat a day's activity with the groups that need it before moving on.","Special needs: give extra time and prepare materials for slower learners; seat learners with hearing or vision difficulty at the front; for learners who reverse or confuse letters, trace letters on the letter card with a finger and write with dots to trace with a pencil (manual p.6)."],"components":[{"no":1,"key":"warmup","name":"Warm-up activities","keywords":["Alphabet song (last-letter word chain)","two learners lead"],"rows":[1]},{"no":2,"key":"oral","name":"Oral Discussion","keywords":["What did you see on your way?","every learner speaks"],"rows":[2]},{"no":3,"key":"story","name":"Story","keywords":["Day 1","title / picture talk","read aloud with expression","logical questions","re-read pointing","group reading","level tasks"],"rows":[3,4,5]},{"no":4,"key":"sound","name":"Sound symbol games, Sound separation-pairing","keywords":["Barakhadi / alphabet chart","listen and point (no repeating)","group reading","level tasks"],"rows":[6,7,8]},{"no":5,"key":"mindwrite","name":"Mind Mapping (Day 1)","keywords":["mind map: sports","classify the words","level task: circle letter A / sentences / story"],"rows":[9,10,11]},{"no":6,"key":"reading","name":"Daily reading","keywords":["library book","read alone","teacher listens"],"rows":[12]}],"preLesson":null},{"programme":"TARL Literacy","id":"lit-076","day":76,"phase":2,"phaseLabel":"Phase 2 (Days 46-90)","title":"Story: a story about a fisherman (Day 2)","dayType":"Story Day 2 + Self-writing","focus":"Language game: Last Letter Chain (Antakshari of words) | Self-writing: a surprise","duration":70,"objectives":["Listen, speak and answer in the oral conversation (familiar topic).","Retell the story, read it with expression, ask and answer questions about it and write answers.","Develop sound-symbol skills: Language game: Last Letter Chain (Antakshari of words).","Write about a topic at their own level and review the writing (a surprise).","Read independently for 10 minutes every day."],"sequence":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Handkerchief game","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Learners sit in a circle and clap while singing a rhyme ('I saw a Little Bird'). One learner runs outside the circle with a handkerchief and secretly places it behind another learner, who must chase the runner. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Sit in a circle, clap and sing; run, place the handkerchief or chase as the game requires.","tlm":"A handkerchief","source":"M","ref":"p.8","n":1},{"activity":"Oral conversation: familiar topic","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Hold a conversation on the topic 'what I learnt in school this week'. Give each learner a chance to speak; be patient with learners who need extra time.","learners":"Talk about the topic and listen to others.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.9","n":2},{"activity":"Story (Day 2 of the story): retelling","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":6,"teacher":"Ask learners to retell yesterday's story in their own words. Prompt with questions on the beginning, middle and end.","learners":"Retell the story using their own words.","tlm":"The same story book as yesterday","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":3},{"activity":"Story: reading with actions and group questions","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":9,"teacher":"Learners practise reading with actions and expressions; one learner per group reads aloud to the class. Guide groups to make questions about the story (guide initially). Groups take turns to ask and answer each other's questions. Word-level learners also read aloud the consonants learned on the first day.","learners":"Read with actions; make questions (word-level learners help write them); ask and answer questions with another group.","tlm":"Story book, slate or paper for questions","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":4},{"activity":"Story: writing answers individually","grouping":"Individual","minutes":5,"teacher":"Para and Story level learners write answers to all questions individually; read and correct their responses after they finish.","learners":"Write the answers in their notebooks; Beginner/Letter/Word learners read or listen and answer orally.","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":5},{"activity":"Language game: Last Letter Chain (Antakshari of words)","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Two groups take turns; each word must begin with the last letter of the previous word. Observe each learner and give help where needed.","learners":"Play the game, take turns and read or say the words they make.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.20","n":6},{"activity":"Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on a surprise","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Start a conversation about a topic: 'a surprise'. Involve all learners and ask open-ended questions.","learners":"Take part in the discussion and share thoughts freely.","tlm":"Picture card or topic on the board","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":7},{"activity":"Self-writing: individual writing","grouping":"Individual","minutes":7,"teacher":"Give each level its task (see level table). Let learners take ownership of what they draw and write; mistakes are fine.","learners":"Draw and write about the topic at their level.","tlm":"Notebooks, crayons or pencils","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":8},{"activity":"Self-writing: review and reading back","grouping":"Individual","minutes":3,"teacher":"Ask each learner 'What did you draw or write?' and have them read it aloud once. Word-level learners read to the group; discuss spelling, punctuation and sentence structure. Help beginners by writing their text in the notebook for them if needed.","learners":"Read what they wrote; correct mistakes after listening to their own reading.","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":9},{"activity":"Daily reading (10 minutes)","grouping":"Individual","minutes":10,"teacher":"Give each learner a library book or any storybook. Move around, listen to individual readers and note their level.","learners":"Read independently a book of their choice.","tlm":"Library books or storybooks","source":"M","ref":"p.7","n":10}],"procedures":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Handkerchief game","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","steps":[{"teacher":"Seat the learners in a circle and start clapping and singing the rhyme 'I saw a Little Bird'.","learners":"Clap and sing together."},{"teacher":"One learner runs outside the circle holding a handkerchief and secretly places it behind another learner.","learners":"Everyone keeps clapping; the learner who finds the handkerchief behind them takes it and chases the runner."},{"teacher":"If the runner sits in the chaser's place before being caught, they stay in the game; if caught, they are out. Continue in this way.","learners":"Play fairly and take turns."}]},{"activity":"Oral conversation: familiar topic","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.9","steps":[{"teacher":"Introduce the topic: 'what I learnt in school this week'.","learners":"Think about their own experience."},{"teacher":"Ask open questions; give every learner a chance. Involve learners who speak less.","learners":"Speak freely and without fear."},{"teacher":"Praise efforts and sum up.","learners":"Listen and respect each other's ideas."}]},{"activity":"Story - Day 2 (a story about a fisherman)","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.11","steps":[{"teacher":"Ask learners to retell the story they read yesterday in their own words.","learners":"Retell, helping each other remember."},{"teacher":"In small groups learners practise reading the story using actions and expressions; one learner from each group then reads aloud to the class.","learners":"Read with actions and expression; a representative reads aloud."},{"teacher":"Guide the groups to come up with questions about the story (guide initially). Word-level learners can support by helping write them down.","learners":"Make questions together."},{"teacher":"Groups take turns to ask and answer each other's questions. Useful kinds: questions whose answer is not in the text; questions needing thinking beyond the text; questions asking for an opinion.","learners":"Ask, answer and discuss in the groups."},{"teacher":"Word-level learners also read aloud the consonants they learned on the first day.","learners":"Read the consonant clusters aloud."}]},{"activity":"Language game: Last Letter Chain (Antakshari of words)","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.20","steps":[{"teacher":"Divide the learners into two groups. A learner from the first group says a word, for example 'peas'.","learners":"Listen to the word and its last letter."},{"teacher":"A learner from the second group must say a new word starting with the last letter of 'peas', for example 'sun'.","learners":"Think quickly and say a word that starts with the last letter."},{"teacher":"Continue, with each group taking turns.","learners":"Cheer your group and listen carefully."}]},{"activity":"Self-writing: 'Discussion, Writing, Self-review'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.15","steps":[{"teacher":"Start a conversation about a topic: 'a surprise'. Involve all learners and ask open-ended questions.","learners":"Discuss and answer questions."},{"teacher":"Give writing time at each level: draw then write (Beginner), write about what they liked (Letter), a sentence (Word), a paragraph or story on a topic of their choice (Para/Story).","learners":"Write at their level and take ownership of the work."},{"teacher":"Review: ask 'What did you draw or write?' Have each learner read the text aloud once. Support with writing if needed.","learners":"Read aloud, listen to their pronunciation and correct mistakes."}]}],"levelTasks":[{"activity":"Story - Day 2: level-wise tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.11","tasks":{"Beginner":"Retell with the group by pointing to pictures or words; read aloud with group support (interpretation of the manual's group reading task).","Letter":"Read with the group, pointing to words; say the letters and words they know (interpretation of the manual's group reading task).","Word":"Support the group in writing the questions; read aloud the consonant clusters learned on the first day.","Para":"Ask the group's questions to another group, discuss them, then write answers to all questions individually; the teacher reads and corrects.","Story":"Ask the group's questions to another group, discuss them, then write answers to all questions individually; the teacher reads and corrects."}},{"activity":"Language game: Last Letter Chain (Antakshari of words) - level support","source":"I","ref":"p.20","tasks":{"Beginner":"Take part by saying or pointing to the letters involved and by listening carefully; Para and Story level partners help.","Letter":"Say the letters/sounds and give simple words they know.","Word":"Say and write words and short sentences for the game.","Para":"Write sentences with the words; help groups to record answers.","Story":"Write sentences or short stories with the words; help groups to record answers."}},{"activity":"Self-writing: level tasks and review","source":"M","ref":"p.15","tasks":{"Beginner":"Draw a picture about the discussion and then write a few sentences about it, expressing thoughts freely. Review: say what they drew or wrote; read the text aloud once; the teacher may write the text in the notebook for them.","Letter":"Write about what they liked, using drawing and writing; write any words or sentences they can. Review: read the text aloud once; correct punctuation mistakes using the Barakhadi chart.","Word":"Write a sentence based on the conversation. Mistakes in spelling, punctuation and sentence structure are fine. Review: read it to the group; discuss and correct mistakes together.","Para":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation.","Story":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation."}}],"organisation":[{"grouping":"Whole class (big group)","how":"All learners of all levels sit in a 'U' shape arranged by level (Beginner, Letter, Word, Para, Story) so that the move to small groups is easy.","activities":["Warm-up: Handkerchief game","Oral conversation: familiar topic","Story (Day 2 of the story): retelling","Language game: Last Letter Chain (Antakshari of words)","Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on a surprise"]},{"grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","how":"Learners of similar levels work together; the teacher gives each group a task for its level and spends more time with learners who need support. Rotate responsibilities (for example group leader).","activities":["Story: reading with actions and group questions"]},{"grouping":"Individual","how":"Each learner works on a task for their own level; the teacher moves around, observes difficulties and supports individuals.","activities":["Story: writing answers individually","Self-writing: individual writing","Self-writing: review and reading back","Daily reading (10 minutes)"]}],"materials":["A handkerchief","The same story book as yesterday","Story book","slate or paper for questions","Notebooks","Picture card or topic on the board","crayons or pencils","Library books or storybooks"],"outcomes":["Learners take part in the oral conversation and speak without fear.","Learners retell the story, read with expression and ask or answer questions at their level.","Learners respond to the sound-symbol task for today (Language game: Last Letter Chain (Antakshari of words)) at their own level.","Learners write about the topic at their level and read it aloud.","Each learner reads a book for 10 minutes."],"observation":["Observe each learner's reading and writing during the individual tasks; note who needs individual support and how many learners share the same difficulty.","Note any learner whose level is improving; move the learner to the next level group when you see steady progress (manual p.5).","Record each learner's progress for the day in the notebook, according to the learner's level (manual p.4).","Use today's observations to adjust tomorrow's plan (manual p.5)."],"teacherNotes":["Questions to elicit on Day 2: information questions (answer not in the text), thinking questions (needs knowledge beyond the text) and opinion questions (feedback on something in the text).","The manual lists the letter and word games but does not fix the slot in the daily timetable where they are used. This plan places them in the 10-minute sound-symbol / alphabet slot (interpretation).","Writing has two parts, content and sequence: encourage learners to read what they wrote, improve it and rewrite it for clarity and correctness (manual p.15).","Pace: the manual says not to assume all learners progress at the same speed. Repeat a day's activity with the groups that need it before moving on.","Special needs: give extra time and prepare materials for slower learners; seat learners with hearing or vision difficulty at the front; for learners who reverse or confuse letters, trace letters on the letter card with a finger and write with dots to trace with a pencil (manual p.6)."],"components":[{"no":1,"key":"warmup","name":"Warm-up activities","keywords":["Handkerchief game","two learners lead"],"rows":[1]},{"no":2,"key":"oral","name":"Oral Discussion","keywords":["familiar topic","every learner speaks"],"rows":[2]},{"no":3,"key":"story","name":"Story","keywords":["Day 2","retell","read with actions","group questions","ask and answer","write answers (Para/Story)"],"rows":[3,4,5]},{"no":4,"key":"sound","name":"Sound symbol games, Sound separation-pairing","keywords":["Last Letter Chain (Antakshari of words)","play in turns","level support"],"rows":[6]},{"no":5,"key":"mindwrite","name":"Individual-Writing (Day 2)","keywords":["discussion","write at own level","self-review (read aloud)"],"rows":[7,8,9]},{"no":6,"key":"reading","name":"Daily reading","keywords":["library book","read alone","teacher listens"],"rows":[10]}],"preLesson":null},{"programme":"TARL Literacy","id":"lit-077","day":77,"phase":2,"phaseLabel":"Phase 2 (Days 46-90)","title":"Story: a story about a naughty monkey (Day 1)","dayType":"Story Day 1 + Mind mapping","focus":"Language game: Jumping on Letters | Mind map: cooking","duration":70,"objectives":["Listen, speak and answer in the oral conversation (conversation on a picture).","Listen to and read a story with understanding; discuss it in big and small groups and respond at their own level.","Develop sound-symbol skills: Language game: Jumping on Letters.","Build vocabulary through a mind map ('cooking') and use the words at their own level.","Read independently for 10 minutes every day."],"sequence":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Rhyme - 'I caught a Fish Alive'","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Say the rhyme with actions, then say it together. Lines: One, two, three, four, five, once I caught a fish alive. / Six, seven, eight, nine, ten, then I let it go again. / Why did you let it go? Because it bit my finger so. / Which finger did it bite? This little finger on my right. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Listen, then say the rhyme with actions.","tlm":"Rhyme chart or board (optional)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","n":1},{"activity":"Oral conversation: conversation on a picture","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Show a picture of a wedding house with decorations and ask what is happening, who is doing what and what is happening around them. Let learners think creatively and even make up a story.","learners":"Look at the picture, answer questions and make up their own story about it.","tlm":"Picture card of a wedding house with decorations","source":"M","ref":"p.9","n":2},{"activity":"Story (Day 1 of the story): reading aloud and discussion","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":8,"teacher":"Discuss the title or picture of the story with the learners. Read the story aloud with expression and voice modulation (learners do not repeat after you). Discuss it, with emphasis on vocabulary-based questions. Read it again slowly, pointing to each word.","learners":"Talk about the title/picture; listen; answer questions; follow each word with a finger in their own copy.","tlm":"A story from the school library (a story about a naughty monkey), a copy for each learner","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":3},{"activity":"Story: reading in small groups","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":7,"teacher":"Form level-wise groups with a group leader. Learners read the story one sentence at a time while the others follow with their fingers. Para and Story level learners practise reading with emotion and expression.","learners":"Read the story sentence by sentence, supporting each other; the group leader helps.","tlm":"Story book copies","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":4},{"activity":"Story: level-wise individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":5,"teacher":"Give each learner the task for their level (see level table) and support those who need it.","learners":"Beginner/Letter: find and write favourite words or letters. Word: find consonant clusters. Para/Story: silently read, find unfamiliar and rhyming words.","tlm":"Story book, notebooks, board","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":5},{"activity":"Language game: Jumping on Letters","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Big boxes with one letter each are drawn on the ground; learners jump onto the letter the teacher calls. Observe each learner and give help where needed.","learners":"Play the game, take turns and read or say the words they make.","tlm":"Chalk, ground or floor","source":"M","ref":"p.18","n":6},{"activity":"Mind mapping (Day 1): the word 'cooking'","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Ask: 'What words come to your mind when you hear the word cooking?' Write learners' answers on the board or floor (Para and Story level learners write the words themselves). Guide the map towards the learning objective. Example words: wash, cut, boil, fry, pot, pan, spoon, knife, salty, sweet, sour, spicy.","learners":"Say words connected with 'cooking'; share the meaning and feeling of words.","tlm":"Board, chalk (or floor)","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":7},{"activity":"Mind mapping: classify the words","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":4,"teacher":"Ask learners to classify the words in groups, for example: Steps: wash, cut, boil, fry; Things: pot, pan, spoon, knife; Tastes: salty, sweet, sour, spicy.","learners":"Sort the words into groups and say why.","tlm":"Board, chalk, word cards (optional)","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":8},{"activity":"Mind mapping: level-wise individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":6,"teacher":"Give each learner the individual task for their level; observe closely and give individual support. Display corrected stories on the wall.","learners":"Complete the task for their level (see level table).","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":9},{"activity":"Daily reading (10 minutes)","grouping":"Individual","minutes":10,"teacher":"Give each learner a library book or any storybook. Move around, listen to individual readers and note their level.","learners":"Read independently a book of their choice.","tlm":"Library books or storybooks","source":"M","ref":"p.7","n":10}],"procedures":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Rhyme - 'I caught a Fish Alive'","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","steps":[{"teacher":"Say the rhyme 'I caught a Fish Alive' slowly with actions: One, two, three, four, five, once I caught a fish alive. / Six, seven, eight, nine, ten, then I let it go again. / Why did you let it go? Because it bit my finger so. / Which finger did it bite? This little finger on my right.","learners":"Listen and watch the actions."},{"teacher":"Say it again; invite learners to join with actions.","learners":"Say the rhyme together with actions."},{"teacher":"Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Choose a rhyme they like and lead."}]},{"activity":"Oral conversation: conversation on a picture","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.9","steps":[{"teacher":"Show the picture of a wedding house with decorations.","learners":"Look carefully."},{"teacher":"Ask: What is happening in the picture? Who is doing what? What is happening around them? Then: How do the people feel? How can you tell?","learners":"Answer in their own words; every learner gets a chance."},{"teacher":"Let learners imagine and make up a short story from the picture.","learners":"Tell their stories to the class."}]},{"activity":"Story - Day 1 (a story about a naughty monkey)","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.10","steps":[{"teacher":"Discuss the title or picture of the story with the learners.","learners":"Talk about what they see and what the story may be about."},{"teacher":"Read the story aloud with expression and proper voice modulation. Learners should not simply repeat after you.","learners":"Listen carefully and enjoy the story."},{"teacher":"Discuss the story: factual, logical, vocabulary-based, judgment or opinion questions (today's focus: vocabulary-based: What does this word mean? Which word in the story means the same as ...?). Begin in the home language if needed.","learners":"Think and respond thoughtfully; every learner takes part."},{"teacher":"Read the story again slowly, pointing to each word. Make sure each learner has a copy and follows with a finger.","learners":"Follow each word with their finger."},{"teacher":"Ask learners to read in small groups; select a group leader who helps the others. Learners read one sentence at a time while the others point with fingers.","learners":"Read with the help of one another."}]},{"activity":"Language game: Jumping on Letters","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.18","steps":[{"teacher":"Draw large boxes on the ground with chalk and write one letter inside each box.","learners":"Look at the letters in the boxes."},{"teacher":"Call learners one by one and say a letter aloud, for example p, m, t, n.","learners":"Listen to the sound and jump onto the correct letter."},{"teacher":"Repeat with new letters and let learners take turns to be the caller.","learners":"Take turns to jump and to call out letters."}]},{"activity":"Mind mapping: 'cooking'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Small group (level-wise) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.14","steps":[{"teacher":"Choose a word that can generate many related words: 'cooking'. Ask: 'What words come to your mind when you hear the word cooking?' Write the answers on the board or floor.","learners":"Say words they link with 'cooking'."},{"teacher":"Discuss the words: what they mean and how they are connected.","learners":"Explain their words and listen to others."},{"teacher":"In small groups, let the learners classify the words (Steps: wash, cut, boil, fry; Things: pot, pan, spoon, knife; Tastes: salty, sweet, sour, spicy).","learners":"Sort the words into groups."},{"teacher":"Give the individual tasks by level and help each learner.","learners":"Work individually; read the work aloud at the end if time allows."}]}],"levelTasks":[{"activity":"Story - Day 1: individual tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.10","tasks":{"Beginner":"Circle or search for a favourite word or letter in the story and say it aloud. If a learner cannot draw a circle, write words on the board and ask them to identify them.","Letter":"Find, read and write favourite words from the story.","Word":"Find the consonant clusters in the story, read them and write them in the notebook.","Para":"Silently read the story from the textbook; find unfamiliar words and try to understand them; find rhyming words, use them in sentences and write in the notebook; ask other groups for meanings; make questions in groups.","Story":"Silently read the story; find unfamiliar words and rhyming words; practise reading with emotion; one group reads sentences formed with consonant clusters to the other group; ask and answer group questions (information, thinking and opinion questions)."}},{"activity":"Language game: Jumping on Letters - level support","source":"I","ref":"p.18","tasks":{"Beginner":"Take part by saying or pointing to the letters involved and by listening carefully; Para and Story level partners help.","Letter":"Say the letters/sounds and give simple words they know.","Word":"Say and write words and short sentences for the game.","Para":"Write sentences with the words; help groups to record answers.","Story":"Write sentences or short stories with the words; help groups to record answers."}},{"activity":"Mind mapping 'cooking': level tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.14","tasks":{"Beginner":"Circle all the words that contain the letter 'S' on the board; make a list. See how many learners find the most words.","Letter":"Circle all the words that contain the letter 'S' and make a list of them.","Word":"Use 4-5 words (for example cut, fry, pan, pot, boil) to form sentences, starting with words of one or two syllables. Example: Dream - I had a dream last night.","Para":"Choose any five words from the map and create a story with them. Use consonant clusters correctly, read the story aloud, correct mistakes of sentence structure, spelling or grammar, then display it on the wall.","Story":"Choose any five words from the map and create a story with them. Use consonant clusters correctly, read the story aloud, correct mistakes of sentence structure, spelling or grammar, then display it on the wall."}}],"organisation":[{"grouping":"Whole class (big group)","how":"All learners of all levels sit in a 'U' shape arranged by level (Beginner, Letter, Word, Para, Story) so that the move to small groups is easy.","activities":["Warm-up: Rhyme - 'I caught a Fish Alive'","Oral conversation: conversation on a picture","Story (Day 1 of the story): reading aloud and discussion","Language game: Jumping on Letters","Mind mapping (Day 1): the word 'cooking'"]},{"grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","how":"Learners of similar levels work together; the teacher gives each group a task for its level and spends more time with learners who need support. Rotate responsibilities (for example group leader).","activities":["Story: reading in small groups","Mind mapping: classify the words"]},{"grouping":"Individual","how":"Each learner works on a task for their own level; the teacher moves around, observes difficulties and supports individuals.","activities":["Story: level-wise individual tasks","Mind mapping: level-wise individual tasks","Daily reading (10 minutes)"]}],"materials":["Rhyme chart or board (optional)","Picture card of a wedding house with decorations","A story from the school library (a story about a naughty monkey)","a copy for each learner","Story book copies","Story book","notebooks","board","Chalk","ground or floor","Board","chalk (or floor)","chalk","word cards (optional)","Notebooks","Library books or storybooks"],"outcomes":["Learners take part in the oral conversation and speak without fear.","Learners show understanding of the story in the discussion and complete the task for their level.","Learners respond to the sound-symbol task for today (Language game: Jumping on Letters) at their own level.","Learners add words to the mind map and use them in sentences or a story at their level.","Each learner reads a book for 10 minutes."],"observation":["Observe each learner's reading and writing during the individual tasks; note who needs individual support and how many learners share the same difficulty.","Note any learner whose level is improving; move the learner to the next level group when you see steady progress (manual p.5).","Record each learner's progress for the day in the notebook, according to the learner's level (manual p.4).","Use today's observations to adjust tomorrow's plan (manual p.5)."],"teacherNotes":["Story selection: the manual asks teachers to use picture story books or stories in the school library. Today's suggested theme (a story about a naughty monkey) is a planning suggestion; use any suitable story you have.","The manual lists the letter and word games but does not fix the slot in the daily timetable where they are used. This plan places them in the 10-minute sound-symbol / alphabet slot (interpretation).","Mind mapping topic for this day: 'cooking'. The manual's example uses the word 'shop'; today's topic follows the same method.","Pace: the manual says not to assume all learners progress at the same speed. Repeat a day's activity with the groups that need it before moving on.","Special needs: give extra time and prepare materials for slower learners; seat learners with hearing or vision difficulty at the front; for learners who reverse or confuse letters, trace letters on the letter card with a finger and write with dots to trace with a pencil (manual p.6)."],"components":[{"no":1,"key":"warmup","name":"Warm-up activities","keywords":["Rhyme - 'I caught a Fish Alive'","two learners lead"],"rows":[1]},{"no":2,"key":"oral","name":"Oral Discussion","keywords":["conversation on a picture","every learner speaks"],"rows":[2]},{"no":3,"key":"story","name":"Story","keywords":["Day 1","title / picture talk","read aloud with expression","vocabulary-based questions","re-read pointing","group reading","level tasks"],"rows":[3,4,5]},{"no":4,"key":"sound","name":"Sound symbol games, Sound separation-pairing","keywords":["Jumping on Letters","play in turns","level support"],"rows":[6]},{"no":5,"key":"mindwrite","name":"Mind Mapping (Day 1)","keywords":["mind map: cooking","classify the words","level task: circle letter S / sentences / story"],"rows":[7,8,9]},{"no":6,"key":"reading","name":"Daily reading","keywords":["library book","read alone","teacher listens"],"rows":[10]}],"preLesson":null},{"programme":"TARL Literacy","id":"lit-078","day":78,"phase":2,"phaseLabel":"Phase 2 (Days 46-90)","title":"Saturday: drama presentation","dayType":"Saturday drama + Self-writing","focus":"Consonant clusters: ss (kiss, grass) | Self-writing: the story we acted out (a story about a naughty monkey)","duration":70,"objectives":["Listen, speak and answer in the oral conversation (listening and storytelling).","Express a story through role play, using voice, facial expressions and gestures.","Develop sound-symbol skills: Consonant clusters: ss (kiss, grass).","Write about the story and review the writing.","Read independently for 10 minutes every day."],"sequence":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Singing and Spinning","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Learners sit in a circle and pass a small object while you clap with your back turned; when the clapping stops, the learner holding it sings a song, recites a poem or tells a joke. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Pass the object round the circle; sing, recite or tell a joke when the clapping stops.","tlm":"A small object (chalk or pencil)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","n":1},{"activity":"Oral conversation: listening and storytelling","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Tell an interesting story starter and involve the learners: 'I planted a seed in the morning and by evening it was a giant tree. What grew on it?' Let learners imagine and continue the story.","learners":"Listen to the teacher, then imagine and continue the story. Learners can also recite a rhyme or story they know.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.9","n":2},{"activity":"Dramatic presentation: introduction and reading","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Explain what a dramatic presentation is and how it is done. Provide stories discussed during the week and read one aloud once more. Para and Story level learners support Beginner and Letter level learners in reading.","learners":"Listen, read along, then each learner chooses a character.","tlm":"Stories discussed in the week (a story about a fisherman; a story about a naughty monkey)","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":3},{"activity":"Dramatic presentation: planning in small groups","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":8,"teacher":"Each group discusses and plans dialogues; Para or Story level learners write the dialogues. Groups prepare their dramatic presentation.","learners":"Choose characters, plan and rehearse dialogues with facial expressions and gestures.","tlm":"Story, paper for dialogues","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":4},{"activity":"Dramatic presentation: performances and feedback","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":7,"teacher":"Learners sit in a U shape. Each group presents; after each performance, watching learners say what they enjoyed and what could be improved.","learners":"Perform in turn; watch; give feedback.","tlm":"Open space (U-shape seating)","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":5},{"activity":"Consonant clusters: introduction","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":4,"teacher":"Same-letter clusters: familiarise learners with clusters made of the same letter ('ss' as in kiss, grass, glass). Ask them to pronounce them and find such words in the text and write them down.","learners":"Listen, pronounce the cluster and say words that contain it.","tlm":"Board and chalk, words list (kiss grass glass class dress)","source":"M","ref":"p.16","n":6},{"activity":"Consonant cluster game: Who is Whose Friend?","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":6,"teacher":"Prepare cards: some with broken parts of conjunct consonants (b + l, c + r, s + t) and some with the full form (bl as in black, cr as in crab, st as in star). Take out all the cards. Observe closely and help learners who need support.","learners":"Match each full form with its broken parts and discover 'who is whose friend'.","tlm":"Broken-part cards and full-form cards","source":"M","ref":"p.17","n":7},{"activity":"Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on the story we acted out (a story about a naughty monkey)","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Start a conversation about the story used for the drama: 'the story we acted out (a story about a naughty monkey)'. Involve all learners with open-ended questions.","learners":"Take part in the discussion and share thoughts freely.","tlm":"Picture card or topic on the board","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":8},{"activity":"Self-writing: individual writing","grouping":"Individual","minutes":7,"teacher":"Give each level its task (see level table). Let learners take ownership of what they draw and write; mistakes are fine.","learners":"Draw and write about the topic at their level.","tlm":"Notebooks, crayons or pencils","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":9},{"activity":"Self-writing: review and reading back","grouping":"Individual","minutes":3,"teacher":"Ask each learner 'What did you draw or write?' and have them read it aloud once. Word-level learners read to the group; discuss spelling, punctuation and sentence structure. Help beginners by writing their text in the notebook for them if needed.","learners":"Read what they wrote; correct mistakes after listening to their own reading.","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":10},{"activity":"Daily reading (10 minutes)","grouping":"Individual","minutes":10,"teacher":"Give each learner a library book or any storybook. Move around, listen to individual readers and note their level.","learners":"Read independently a book of their choice.","tlm":"Library books or storybooks","source":"M","ref":"p.7","n":11}],"procedures":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Singing and Spinning","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","steps":[{"teacher":"Seat the learners in a circle; give a small object to one learner.","learners":"Sit in a circle."},{"teacher":"Stand outside the circle with your back to them and clap steadily; they pass the object.","learners":"Pass the object while the clapping continues."},{"teacher":"Stop clapping; the learner holding the object sings, recites or tells a joke.","learners":"Perform, and everybody claps."}]},{"activity":"Oral conversation: listening and storytelling","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.9","steps":[{"teacher":"Say the starter: 'I planted a seed in the morning and by evening it was a giant tree. What grew on it?'","learners":"Listen and imagine."},{"teacher":"Ask learners to continue the story one by one. Encourage those who speak less.","learners":"Add ideas to the story."},{"teacher":"Invite a learner to recite a poem or rhyme they know.","learners":"Recite and listen to others."}]},{"activity":"Saturday special: dramatic presentation","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.11","steps":[{"teacher":"Explain what a dramatic presentation is and how it can be done. Give the groups the stories discussed during the week.","learners":"Listen to the explanation."},{"teacher":"Read a story aloud once more. Learners at story and paragraph level support those at beginner and letter level in reading.","learners":"Read along; helpers support their friends."},{"teacher":"After reading, each learner chooses a character from the story.","learners":"Choose a role (boys may play girl roles and girls may play boy roles)."},{"teacher":"In groups, learners discuss and plan the dialogues; paragraph or story level learners write the dialogues.","learners":"Plan and write dialogues together."},{"teacher":"Learners sit in a U shape. Each group presents its drama. After each performance, ask what the audience enjoyed and what could be improved.","learners":"Perform, watch and give kind feedback."}]},{"activity":"Consonant clusters (ss) and the game 'Who is Whose Friend?'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.16-17","steps":[{"teacher":"Same-letter clusters: familiarise learners with clusters made of the same letter ('ss' as in kiss, grass, glass). Ask them to pronounce them and find such words in the text and write them down.","learners":"Listen, pronounce and find words in the text."},{"teacher":"Write the words on the board: kiss grass glass class dress. Read them aloud with distinct pronunciation of the cluster.","learners":"Read the words aloud; point to the cluster in each word."},{"teacher":"Prepare cards: some with broken parts of conjunct consonants (b + l, c + r, s + t) and some with the full form (bl as in black, cr as in crab, st as in star). Take out all the cards.","learners":"Match each full form with its broken parts and discover 'who is whose friend'."}]},{"activity":"Self-writing: 'Discussion, Writing, Self-review'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.15","steps":[{"teacher":"Start a conversation about the story used for the drama: 'the story we acted out (a story about a naughty monkey)'. Involve all learners with open-ended questions.","learners":"Discuss and answer questions."},{"teacher":"Give writing time at each level: draw then write (Beginner), write about what they liked (Letter), a sentence (Word), a paragraph or story on a topic of their choice (Para/Story).","learners":"Write at their level and take ownership of the work."},{"teacher":"Review: ask 'What did you draw or write?' Have each learner read the text aloud once. Support with writing if needed.","learners":"Read aloud, listen to their pronunciation and correct mistakes."}]}],"levelTasks":[{"activity":"Drama: roles by level","source":"M","ref":"p.11","tasks":{"Beginner":"Take a character role and say or act short lines with help from Para and Story level learners.","Letter":"Take a character role and say or act short lines with help from Para and Story level learners.","Word":"Take a role and speak the dialogues; help rehearse.","Para":"Write the dialogues for the group and support Beginner, Letter and Word level learners throughout.","Story":"Write the dialogues for the group and support Beginner, Letter and Word level learners throughout."}},{"activity":"Consonant clusters (ss): level tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.16-17","tasks":{"Beginner":"Listen to the sound of the cluster and point to it in a word; continue with letter-sound work (interpretation: the manual describes clusters for learners lagging in reading words and sentences).","Letter":"Listen to the cluster sound and pick words with the cluster from a word card (interpretation).","Word":"Find the cluster in the story or textbook words, read the words and write them in the notebook.","Para":"Form words and sentences using the cluster; read the sentences aloud.","Story":"Form words and sentences using the cluster; read the sentences aloud; use them in the story writing."}},{"activity":"Self-writing: level tasks and review","source":"M","ref":"p.15","tasks":{"Beginner":"Draw a picture about the discussion and then write a few sentences about it, expressing thoughts freely. Review: say what they drew or wrote; read the text aloud once; the teacher may write the text in the notebook for them.","Letter":"Write about what they liked, using drawing and writing; write any words or sentences they can. Review: read the text aloud once; correct punctuation mistakes using the Barakhadi chart.","Word":"Write a sentence based on the conversation. Mistakes in spelling, punctuation and sentence structure are fine. Review: read it to the group; discuss and correct mistakes together.","Para":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation.","Story":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation."}}],"organisation":[{"grouping":"Whole class (big group)","how":"All learners of all levels sit in a 'U' shape arranged by level (Beginner, Letter, Word, Para, Story) so that the move to small groups is easy.","activities":["Warm-up: Singing and Spinning","Oral conversation: listening and storytelling","Dramatic presentation: introduction and reading","Dramatic presentation: performances and feedback","Consonant clusters: introduction","Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on the story we acted out (a story about a naughty monkey)"]},{"grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","how":"Learners of similar levels work together; the teacher gives each group a task for its level and spends more time with learners who need support. Rotate responsibilities (for example group leader).","activities":["Dramatic presentation: planning in small groups","Consonant cluster game: Who is Whose Friend?"]},{"grouping":"Individual","how":"Each learner works on a task for their own level; the teacher moves around, observes difficulties and supports individuals.","activities":["Self-writing: individual writing","Self-writing: review and reading back","Daily reading (10 minutes)"]}],"materials":["A small object (chalk or pencil)","Stories discussed in the week (a story about a fisherman; a story about a naughty monkey)","Story","paper for dialogues","Open space (U-shape seating)","Board","chalk","words list (kiss grass glass class dress)","Broken-part cards","full-form cards","Picture card or topic on the board","Notebooks","crayons or pencils","Library books or storybooks"],"outcomes":["Learners take part in the oral conversation and speak without fear.","Learners present a role in the group drama and give feedback to others.","Learners respond to the sound-symbol task for today (Consonant clusters: ss (kiss, grass)) at their own level.","Learners write about the story at their level and read it aloud.","Each learner reads a book for 10 minutes."],"observation":["Observe each learner's reading and writing during the individual tasks; note who needs individual support and how many learners share the same difficulty.","Note any learner whose level is improving; move the learner to the next level group when you see steady progress (manual p.5).","Record each learner's progress for the day in the notebook, according to the learner's level (manual p.4).","Use today's observations to adjust tomorrow's plan (manual p.5)."],"teacherNotes":["Saturday: this plan assumes Day 1 is a Monday (six teaching days per week). If your school week is different, hold the drama presentation on your Saturday and keep the other days in sequence.","Consonant clusters: do these activities daily for learners who find reading complex words hard; the aim is to remove the fear of reading clusters. Teachers may carry out similar activities on their own.","Writing has two parts, content and sequence: encourage learners to read what they wrote, improve it and rewrite it for clarity and correctness (manual p.15).","Pace: the manual says not to assume all learners progress at the same speed. Repeat a day's activity with the groups that need it before moving on.","Special needs: give extra time and prepare materials for slower learners; seat learners with hearing or vision difficulty at the front; for learners who reverse or confuse letters, trace letters on the letter card with a finger and write with dots to trace with a pencil (manual p.6)."],"components":[{"no":1,"key":"warmup","name":"Warm-up activities","keywords":["Singing and Spinning","two learners lead"],"rows":[1]},{"no":2,"key":"oral","name":"Oral Discussion","keywords":["listening and storytelling","every learner speaks"],"rows":[2]},{"no":3,"key":"story","name":"Story (Saturday: dramatic presentation)","keywords":["Saturday drama","choose a character","plan dialogues","perform in U shape","feedback"],"rows":[3,4,5]},{"no":4,"key":"sound","name":"Sound symbol games, Sound separation-pairing","keywords":["consonant cluster 'ss'","pronounce and find words","game: Who is Whose Friend?"],"rows":[6,7]},{"no":5,"key":"mindwrite","name":"Individual-Writing (Day 2)","keywords":["discussion","write at own level","self-review (read aloud)"],"rows":[8,9,10]},{"no":6,"key":"reading","name":"Daily reading","keywords":["library book","read alone","teacher listens"],"rows":[11]}],"preLesson":null},{"programme":"TARL Literacy","id":"lit-079","day":79,"phase":2,"phaseLabel":"Phase 2 (Days 46-90)","title":"Story: a story about a naughty monkey (Day 2)","dayType":"Story Day 2 + Self-writing","focus":"Language game: Pick a Word, Build a Sentence | Self-writing: a picture of the sky at night","duration":70,"objectives":["Listen, speak and answer in the oral conversation (What did you see on your way?).","Retell the story, read it with expression, ask and answer questions about it and write answers.","Develop sound-symbol skills: Language game: Pick a Word, Build a Sentence.","Write about a topic at their own level and review the writing (a picture of the sky at night).","Read independently for 10 minutes every day."],"sequence":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Rain clapping","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Everyone stands in a circle with eyes closed and keeps clapping: first one finger, then two, three, four and finally five fingers. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Stand in a circle, close the eyes and clap with 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 fingers.","tlm":"After the activity ask: Was it a gentle rain or a storm? How did you feel?","source":"M","ref":"p.8","n":1},{"activity":"Oral conversation: What did you see on your way?","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Ask learners to describe what they saw on their way to school. If they are hesitant, begin yourself: 'I saw smoke rising from a kitchen, a dog sleeping under a tree and children walking to school together. What did you see?'","learners":"Describe what they saw on the way to school and connect with what others share.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.9","n":2},{"activity":"Story (Day 2 of the story): retelling","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":6,"teacher":"Ask learners to retell yesterday's story in their own words. Prompt with questions on the beginning, middle and end.","learners":"Retell the story using their own words.","tlm":"The same story book as yesterday","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":3},{"activity":"Story: reading with actions and group questions","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":9,"teacher":"Learners practise reading with actions and expressions; one learner per group reads aloud to the class. Guide groups to make questions about the story (guide initially). Groups take turns to ask and answer each other's questions. Word-level learners also read aloud the consonants learned on the first day.","learners":"Read with actions; make questions (word-level learners help write them); ask and answer questions with another group.","tlm":"Story book, slate or paper for questions","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":4},{"activity":"Story: writing answers individually","grouping":"Individual","minutes":5,"teacher":"Para and Story level learners write answers to all questions individually; read and correct their responses after they finish.","learners":"Write the answers in their notebooks; Beginner/Letter/Word learners read or listen and answer orally.","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":5},{"activity":"Language game: Pick a Word, Build a Sentence","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Words on slips are kept in a basket; each learner picks one, reads it and says a sentence, linking to the previous sentence. Observe each learner and give help where needed.","learners":"Play the game, take turns and read or say the words they make.","tlm":"Word slips, basket or pan","source":"M","ref":"p.20","n":6},{"activity":"Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on a picture of the sky at night","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Start a conversation about a situation: 'a picture of the sky at night'. Involve all learners and ask open-ended questions.","learners":"Take part in the discussion and share thoughts freely.","tlm":"Picture card or topic on the board","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":7},{"activity":"Self-writing: individual writing","grouping":"Individual","minutes":7,"teacher":"Give each level its task (see level table). Let learners take ownership of what they draw and write; mistakes are fine.","learners":"Draw and write about the topic at their level.","tlm":"Notebooks, crayons or pencils","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":8},{"activity":"Self-writing: review and reading back","grouping":"Individual","minutes":3,"teacher":"Ask each learner 'What did you draw or write?' and have them read it aloud once. Word-level learners read to the group; discuss spelling, punctuation and sentence structure. Help beginners by writing their text in the notebook for them if needed.","learners":"Read what they wrote; correct mistakes after listening to their own reading.","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":9},{"activity":"Daily reading (10 minutes)","grouping":"Individual","minutes":10,"teacher":"Give each learner a library book or any storybook. Move around, listen to individual readers and note their level.","learners":"Read independently a book of their choice.","tlm":"Library books or storybooks","source":"M","ref":"p.7","n":10}],"procedures":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Rain clapping","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","steps":[{"teacher":"Stand the learners in a circle and ask them to close their eyes. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Stand in a circle and close their eyes."},{"teacher":"Start clapping with one finger; then two fingers, three, four and finally five fingers.","learners":"Keep clapping, copying the change of fingers."},{"teacher":"After the activity ask: Was it a gentle rain or a storm? How did you feel?","learners":"Tell how they felt and what the sounds reminded them of."}]},{"activity":"Oral conversation: What did you see on your way?","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.9","steps":[{"teacher":"Ask: 'What did you see on your way to school today?'","learners":"Think about the way to school."},{"teacher":"If learners hesitate, start: 'I saw smoke rising from a kitchen, a dog sleeping under a tree and children walking to school together. What did you see?'","learners":"Listen to the model and then share their own observations."},{"teacher":"Connect learners' answers with each other.","learners":"Listen and add what they noticed."}]},{"activity":"Story - Day 2 (a story about a naughty monkey)","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.11","steps":[{"teacher":"Ask learners to retell the story they read yesterday in their own words.","learners":"Retell, helping each other remember."},{"teacher":"In small groups learners practise reading the story using actions and expressions; one learner from each group then reads aloud to the class.","learners":"Read with actions and expression; a representative reads aloud."},{"teacher":"Guide the groups to come up with questions about the story (guide initially). Word-level learners can support by helping write them down.","learners":"Make questions together."},{"teacher":"Groups take turns to ask and answer each other's questions. Useful kinds: questions whose answer is not in the text; questions needing thinking beyond the text; questions asking for an opinion.","learners":"Ask, answer and discuss in the groups."},{"teacher":"Word-level learners also read aloud the consonants they learned on the first day.","learners":"Read the consonant clusters aloud."}]},{"activity":"Language game: Pick a Word, Build a Sentence","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.20","steps":[{"teacher":"Write different words on small slips and put them in an earthen basket or pan.","learners":"Sit in a circle."},{"teacher":"Call one learner at a time to pick a slip, read the word aloud and say a sentence using it.","learners":"Read the word, say a sentence."},{"teacher":"The next learner picks a new word and says a sentence that connects with the previous one, using their own word.","learners":"Build a chain of sentences together."}]},{"activity":"Self-writing: 'Discussion, Writing, Self-review'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.15","steps":[{"teacher":"Start a conversation about a situation: 'a picture of the sky at night'. Involve all learners and ask open-ended questions.","learners":"Discuss and answer questions."},{"teacher":"Give writing time at each level: draw then write (Beginner), write about what they liked (Letter), a sentence (Word), a paragraph or story on a topic of their choice (Para/Story).","learners":"Write at their level and take ownership of the work."},{"teacher":"Review: ask 'What did you draw or write?' Have each learner read the text aloud once. Support with writing if needed.","learners":"Read aloud, listen to their pronunciation and correct mistakes."}]}],"levelTasks":[{"activity":"Story - Day 2: level-wise tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.11","tasks":{"Beginner":"Retell with the group by pointing to pictures or words; read aloud with group support (interpretation of the manual's group reading task).","Letter":"Read with the group, pointing to words; say the letters and words they know (interpretation of the manual's group reading task).","Word":"Support the group in writing the questions; read aloud the consonant clusters learned on the first day.","Para":"Ask the group's questions to another group, discuss them, then write answers to all questions individually; the teacher reads and corrects.","Story":"Ask the group's questions to another group, discuss them, then write answers to all questions individually; the teacher reads and corrects."}},{"activity":"Language game: Pick a Word, Build a Sentence - level support","source":"I","ref":"p.20","tasks":{"Beginner":"Take part by saying or pointing to the letters involved and by listening carefully; Para and Story level partners help.","Letter":"Say the letters/sounds and give simple words they know.","Word":"Say and write words and short sentences for the game.","Para":"Write sentences with the words; help groups to record answers.","Story":"Write sentences or short stories with the words; help groups to record answers."}},{"activity":"Self-writing: level tasks and review","source":"M","ref":"p.15","tasks":{"Beginner":"Draw a picture about the discussion and then write a few sentences about it, expressing thoughts freely. Review: say what they drew or wrote; read the text aloud once; the teacher may write the text in the notebook for them.","Letter":"Write about what they liked, using drawing and writing; write any words or sentences they can. Review: read the text aloud once; correct punctuation mistakes using the Barakhadi chart.","Word":"Write a sentence based on the conversation. Mistakes in spelling, punctuation and sentence structure are fine. Review: read it to the group; discuss and correct mistakes together.","Para":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation.","Story":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation."}}],"organisation":[{"grouping":"Whole class (big group)","how":"All learners of all levels sit in a 'U' shape arranged by level (Beginner, Letter, Word, Para, Story) so that the move to small groups is easy.","activities":["Warm-up: Rain clapping","Oral conversation: What did you see on your way?","Story (Day 2 of the story): retelling","Language game: Pick a Word, Build a Sentence","Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on a picture of the sky at night"]},{"grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","how":"Learners of similar levels work together; the teacher gives each group a task for its level and spends more time with learners who need support. Rotate responsibilities (for example group leader).","activities":["Story: reading with actions and group questions"]},{"grouping":"Individual","how":"Each learner works on a task for their own level; the teacher moves around, observes difficulties and supports individuals.","activities":["Story: writing answers individually","Self-writing: individual writing","Self-writing: review and reading back","Daily reading (10 minutes)"]}],"materials":["After the activity ask: Was it a gentle rain or a storm? How did you feel?","The same story book as yesterday","Story book","slate or paper for questions","Notebooks","Word slips","basket or pan","Picture card or topic on the board","crayons or pencils","Library books or storybooks"],"outcomes":["Learners take part in the oral conversation and speak without fear.","Learners retell the story, read with expression and ask or answer questions at their level.","Learners respond to the sound-symbol task for today (Language game: Pick a Word, Build a Sentence) at their own level.","Learners write about the topic at their level and read it aloud.","Each learner reads a book for 10 minutes."],"observation":["Observe each learner's reading and writing during the individual tasks; note who needs individual support and how many learners share the same difficulty.","Note any learner whose level is improving; move the learner to the next level group when you see steady progress (manual p.5).","Record each learner's progress for the day in the notebook, according to the learner's level (manual p.4).","Use today's observations to adjust tomorrow's plan (manual p.5)."],"teacherNotes":["Questions to elicit on Day 2: information questions (answer not in the text), thinking questions (needs knowledge beyond the text) and opinion questions (feedback on something in the text).","The manual lists the letter and word games but does not fix the slot in the daily timetable where they are used. This plan places them in the 10-minute sound-symbol / alphabet slot (interpretation).","Writing has two parts, content and sequence: encourage learners to read what they wrote, improve it and rewrite it for clarity and correctness (manual p.15).","Pace: the manual says not to assume all learners progress at the same speed. Repeat a day's activity with the groups that need it before moving on.","Special needs: give extra time and prepare materials for slower learners; seat learners with hearing or vision difficulty at the front; for learners who reverse or confuse letters, trace letters on the letter card with a finger and write with dots to trace with a pencil (manual p.6)."],"components":[{"no":1,"key":"warmup","name":"Warm-up activities","keywords":["Rain clapping","two learners lead"],"rows":[1]},{"no":2,"key":"oral","name":"Oral Discussion","keywords":["What did you see on your way?","every learner speaks"],"rows":[2]},{"no":3,"key":"story","name":"Story","keywords":["Day 2","retell","read with actions","group questions","ask and answer","write answers (Para/Story)"],"rows":[3,4,5]},{"no":4,"key":"sound","name":"Sound symbol games, Sound separation-pairing","keywords":["Pick a Word, Build a Sentence","play in turns","level support"],"rows":[6]},{"no":5,"key":"mindwrite","name":"Individual-Writing (Day 2)","keywords":["discussion","write at own level","self-review (read aloud)"],"rows":[7,8,9]},{"no":6,"key":"reading","name":"Daily reading","keywords":["library book","read alone","teacher listens"],"rows":[10]}],"preLesson":null},{"programme":"TARL Literacy","id":"lit-080","day":80,"phase":2,"phaseLabel":"Phase 2 (Days 46-90)","title":"Story: a story about a rainy-day adventure (Day 1)","dayType":"Story Day 1 + Mind mapping","focus":"Blending sounds to form words (cup, map, jam) | Mind map: tools","duration":70,"objectives":["Listen, speak and answer in the oral conversation (familiar topic).","Listen to and read a story with understanding; discuss it in big and small groups and respond at their own level.","Develop sound-symbol skills: Blending sounds to form words (cup, map, jam).","Build vocabulary through a mind map ('tools') and use the words at their own level.","Read independently for 10 minutes every day."],"sequence":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Writing with body parts","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Learners stand in a circle. Demonstrate writing the word 'home' in the air with a finger, then ask them to write it with different body parts. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Write the word 'home' in the air with the finger, then with the head, shoulders, knees or elbows.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.8","n":1},{"activity":"Oral conversation: familiar topic","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Hold a conversation on the topic 'a time I helped someone'. Give each learner a chance to speak; be patient with learners who need extra time.","learners":"Talk about the topic and listen to others.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.9","n":2},{"activity":"Story (Day 1 of the story): reading aloud and discussion","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":8,"teacher":"Discuss the title or picture of the story with the learners. Read the story aloud with expression and voice modulation (learners do not repeat after you). Discuss it, with emphasis on judgment questions. Read it again slowly, pointing to each word.","learners":"Talk about the title/picture; listen; answer questions; follow each word with a finger in their own copy.","tlm":"A story from the school library (a story about a rainy-day adventure), a copy for each learner","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":3},{"activity":"Story: reading in small groups","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":7,"teacher":"Form level-wise groups with a group leader. Learners read the story one sentence at a time while the others follow with their fingers. Para and Story level learners practise reading with emotion and expression.","learners":"Read the story sentence by sentence, supporting each other; the group leader helps.","tlm":"Story book copies","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":4},{"activity":"Story: level-wise individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":5,"teacher":"Give each learner the task for their level (see level table) and support those who need it.","learners":"Beginner/Letter: find and write favourite words or letters. Word: find consonant clusters. Para/Story: silently read, find unfamiliar and rhyming words.","tlm":"Story book, notebooks, board","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":5},{"activity":"Sound-symbol activity: oral sound awareness","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":4,"teacher":"Say separate sounds from 10-12 words (cup: c - u - p; map: m - a - p; jam: j - a - m; fox: f - o - x) and ask learners to blend the sounds into the complete word.","learners":"Listen to the separate sounds and blend them to say the whole word.","tlm":"None (oral activity)","source":"M","ref":"p.12","n":6},{"activity":"Sound-symbol games by level","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":6,"teacher":"Give each level group its game (see level table). Move among the groups and help those who need support; say each word clearly.","learners":"Play the game for their level in small groups.","tlm":"Board, chalk, letter cards","source":"M","ref":"p.12","n":7},{"activity":"Mind mapping (Day 1): the word 'tools'","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Ask: 'What words come to your mind when you hear the word tools?' Write learners' answers on the board or floor (Para and Story level learners write the words themselves). Guide the map towards the learning objective. Example words: plough, sickle, spade, axe, hammer, saw, brush, trowel, net, hook, loom, needle.","learners":"Say words connected with 'tools'; share the meaning and feeling of words.","tlm":"Board, chalk (or floor)","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":8},{"activity":"Mind mapping: classify the words","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":4,"teacher":"Ask learners to classify the words in groups, for example: Farming: plough, sickle, spade, axe; House building: hammer, saw, brush, trowel; Fishing and weaving: net, hook, loom, needle.","learners":"Sort the words into groups and say why.","tlm":"Board, chalk, word cards (optional)","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":9},{"activity":"Mind mapping: level-wise individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":6,"teacher":"Give each learner the individual task for their level; observe closely and give individual support. Display corrected stories on the wall.","learners":"Complete the task for their level (see level table).","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":10},{"activity":"Daily reading (10 minutes)","grouping":"Individual","minutes":10,"teacher":"Give each learner a library book or any storybook. Move around, listen to individual readers and note their level.","learners":"Read independently a book of their choice.","tlm":"Library books or storybooks","source":"M","ref":"p.7","n":11}],"procedures":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Writing with body parts","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","steps":[{"teacher":"Stand the learners in a circle. Demonstrate writing the word 'home' in the air with your finger.","learners":"Watch and then copy with their own finger."},{"teacher":"Ask them to write it again using hips and other body parts (head, shoulders, knees, ...).","learners":"Write the letters in the air with the named body part."},{"teacher":"Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Take turns to lead."}]},{"activity":"Oral conversation: familiar topic","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.9","steps":[{"teacher":"Introduce the topic: 'a time I helped someone'.","learners":"Think about their own experience."},{"teacher":"Ask open questions; give every learner a chance. Involve learners who speak less.","learners":"Speak freely and without fear."},{"teacher":"Praise efforts and sum up.","learners":"Listen and respect each other's ideas."}]},{"activity":"Story - Day 1 (a story about a rainy-day adventure)","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.10","steps":[{"teacher":"Discuss the title or picture of the story with the learners.","learners":"Talk about what they see and what the story may be about."},{"teacher":"Read the story aloud with expression and proper voice modulation. Learners should not simply repeat after you.","learners":"Listen carefully and enjoy the story."},{"teacher":"Discuss the story: factual, logical, vocabulary-based, judgment or opinion questions (today's focus: judgment: Was the character right or wrong? Was that a good thing to do? Why?). Begin in the home language if needed.","learners":"Think and respond thoughtfully; every learner takes part."},{"teacher":"Read the story again slowly, pointing to each word. Make sure each learner has a copy and follows with a finger.","learners":"Follow each word with their finger."},{"teacher":"Ask learners to read in small groups; select a group leader who helps the others. Learners read one sentence at a time while the others point with fingers.","learners":"Read with the help of one another."}]},{"activity":"Sound-symbol: oral and level games","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.12","steps":[{"teacher":"Say separate sounds from 10-12 words (cup: c - u - p; map: m - a - p; jam: j - a - m; fox: f - o - x) and ask learners to blend the sounds into the complete word.","learners":"Listen to the separate sounds and blend them to say the whole word."},{"teacher":"Write the sounds or words for the day on the board and give each level group its task (see the level table).","learners":"Work in small groups and share their answers."},{"teacher":"Say each word clearly with distinct pronunciation. Give learners enough time to respond and think; use words learners commonly use at home (regional language and the medium of instruction).","learners":"Think, say and write the sounds."}]},{"activity":"Mind mapping: 'tools'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Small group (level-wise) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.14","steps":[{"teacher":"Choose a word that can generate many related words: 'tools'. Ask: 'What words come to your mind when you hear the word tools?' Write the answers on the board or floor.","learners":"Say words they link with 'tools'."},{"teacher":"Discuss the words: what they mean and how they are connected.","learners":"Explain their words and listen to others."},{"teacher":"In small groups, let the learners classify the words (Farming: plough, sickle, spade, axe; House building: hammer, saw, brush, trowel; Fishing and weaving: net, hook, loom, needle).","learners":"Sort the words into groups."},{"teacher":"Give the individual tasks by level and help each learner.","learners":"Work individually; read the work aloud at the end if time allows."}]}],"levelTasks":[{"activity":"Story - Day 1: individual tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.10","tasks":{"Beginner":"Circle or search for a favourite word or letter in the story and say it aloud. If a learner cannot draw a circle, write words on the board and ask them to identify them.","Letter":"Find, read and write favourite words from the story.","Word":"Find the consonant clusters in the story, read them and write them in the notebook.","Para":"Silently read the story from the textbook; find unfamiliar words and try to understand them; find rhyming words, use them in sentences and write in the notebook; ask other groups for meanings; make questions in groups.","Story":"Silently read the story; find unfamiliar words and rhyming words; practise reading with emotion; one group reads sentences formed with consonant clusters to the other group; ask and answer group questions (information, thinking and opinion questions)."}},{"activity":"Sound-symbol games by level (small groups)","source":"M","ref":"p.12","tasks":{"Beginner":"'What is the first sound in the word mango?' 'Is there a letter that makes the sound /m/?' 'Can you name objects that start with the letter M?' Learners think and share names in the group.","Letter":"Write the rhyming ending -op on the board and ask learners to add new letters to form words: h + op = hop, m + op = mop, t + op = top.","Word":"Say a word and tell its sounds, for example 'sun' = /s/ + /u/ + /n/. Then tell what word is formed if /r/ is put before 'at': r + at = rat. Do 8-10 such combinations; at first learners may form meaningless words, later only meaningful words.","Para":"Write two or three sounds on the board (for example Br, cl, st) and let the learners form words that start with those sounds; this builds a word list for the learner.","Story":"Write two or three sounds on the board (for example Br, cl, st) and let the learners form words that start with those sounds; this builds a word list for the learner."}},{"activity":"Mind mapping 'tools': level tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.14","tasks":{"Beginner":"Circle all the words that contain the letter 'E' on the board; make a list. See how many learners find the most words.","Letter":"Circle all the words that contain the letter 'E' and make a list of them.","Word":"Use 4-5 words (for example axe, net, saw, hook, loom) to form sentences, starting with words of one or two syllables. Example: Dream - I had a dream last night.","Para":"Choose any five words from the map and create a story with them. Use consonant clusters correctly, read the story aloud, correct mistakes of sentence structure, spelling or grammar, then display it on the wall.","Story":"Choose any five words from the map and create a story with them. Use consonant clusters correctly, read the story aloud, correct mistakes of sentence structure, spelling or grammar, then display it on the wall."}}],"organisation":[{"grouping":"Whole class (big group)","how":"All learners of all levels sit in a 'U' shape arranged by level (Beginner, Letter, Word, Para, Story) so that the move to small groups is easy.","activities":["Warm-up: Writing with body parts","Oral conversation: familiar topic","Story (Day 1 of the story): reading aloud and discussion","Sound-symbol activity: oral sound awareness","Mind mapping (Day 1): the word 'tools'"]},{"grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","how":"Learners of similar levels work together; the teacher gives each group a task for its level and spends more time with learners who need support. Rotate responsibilities (for example group leader).","activities":["Story: reading in small groups","Sound-symbol games by level","Mind mapping: classify the words"]},{"grouping":"Individual","how":"Each learner works on a task for their own level; the teacher moves around, observes difficulties and supports individuals.","activities":["Story: level-wise individual tasks","Mind mapping: level-wise individual tasks","Daily reading (10 minutes)"]}],"materials":["A story from the school library (a story about a rainy-day adventure)","a copy for each learner","Story book copies","Story book","notebooks","board","Board","chalk","letter cards","chalk (or floor)","word cards (optional)","Notebooks","Library books or storybooks"],"outcomes":["Learners take part in the oral conversation and speak without fear.","Learners show understanding of the story in the discussion and complete the task for their level.","Learners respond to the sound-symbol task for today (Blending sounds to form words (cup, map, jam)) at their own level.","Learners add words to the mind map and use them in sentences or a story at their level.","Each learner reads a book for 10 minutes."],"observation":["Observe each learner's reading and writing during the individual tasks; note who needs individual support and how many learners share the same difficulty.","Note any learner whose level is improving; move the learner to the next level group when you see steady progress (manual p.5).","Record each learner's progress for the day in the notebook, according to the learner's level (manual p.4).","Use today's observations to adjust tomorrow's plan (manual p.5)."],"teacherNotes":["Story selection: the manual asks teachers to use picture story books or stories in the school library. Today's suggested theme (a story about a rainy-day adventure) is a planning suggestion; use any suitable story you have.","Sound-symbol: for the first 4-5 days, play sound-based games with the learners at word level. Include the sounds learners find difficult when you prepare the Class Transaction Plan.","Mind mapping topic for this day: 'tools'. The manual's example uses the word 'shop'; today's topic follows the same method.","Pace: the manual says not to assume all learners progress at the same speed. Repeat a day's activity with the groups that need it before moving on.","Special needs: give extra time and prepare materials for slower learners; seat learners with hearing or vision difficulty at the front; for learners who reverse or confuse letters, trace letters on the letter card with a finger and write with dots to trace with a pencil (manual p.6)."],"components":[{"no":1,"key":"warmup","name":"Warm-up activities","keywords":["Writing with body parts","two learners lead"],"rows":[1]},{"no":2,"key":"oral","name":"Oral Discussion","keywords":["familiar topic","every learner speaks"],"rows":[2]},{"no":3,"key":"story","name":"Story","keywords":["Day 1","title / picture talk","read aloud with expression","judgment questions","re-read pointing","group reading","level tasks"],"rows":[3,4,5]},{"no":4,"key":"sound","name":"Sound symbol games, Sound separation-pairing","keywords":["oral sound awareness","blend sounds to a word","level games in small groups"],"rows":[6,7]},{"no":5,"key":"mindwrite","name":"Mind Mapping (Day 1)","keywords":["mind map: tools","classify the words","level task: circle letter E / sentences / story"],"rows":[8,9,10]},{"no":6,"key":"reading","name":"Daily reading","keywords":["library book","read alone","teacher listens"],"rows":[11]}],"preLesson":null},{"programme":"TARL Literacy","id":"lit-081","day":81,"phase":2,"phaseLabel":"Phase 2 (Days 46-90)","title":"Story: a story about a rainy-day adventure (Day 2)","dayType":"Story Day 2 + Self-writing","focus":"Barakhadi / alphabet and phonics chart (line 1, letter 's') | Self-writing: a lost and found thing","duration":70,"objectives":["Listen, speak and answer in the oral conversation (conversation on a picture).","Retell the story, read it with expression, ask and answer questions about it and write answers.","Develop sound-symbol skills: Barakhadi / alphabet and phonics chart (line 1, letter 's').","Write about a topic at their own level and review the writing (a lost and found thing).","Read independently for 10 minutes every day."],"sequence":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Alphabet song (last-letter word chain)","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Say a word to the big group, for example 'yak'. Learners say a word that starts with the last letter ('k'). A learner who cannot say a word is out. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Say a word that starts with the last letter of the previous word; step out if unable to.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.8","n":1},{"activity":"Oral conversation: conversation on a picture","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Show a picture of a library with children reading and ask what is happening, who is doing what and what is happening around them. Let learners think creatively and even make up a story.","learners":"Look at the picture, answer questions and make up their own story about it.","tlm":"Picture card of a library with children reading","source":"M","ref":"p.9","n":2},{"activity":"Story (Day 2 of the story): retelling","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":6,"teacher":"Ask learners to retell yesterday's story in their own words. Prompt with questions on the beginning, middle and end.","learners":"Retell the story using their own words.","tlm":"The same story book as yesterday","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":3},{"activity":"Story: reading with actions and group questions","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":9,"teacher":"Learners practise reading with actions and expressions; one learner per group reads aloud to the class. Guide groups to make questions about the story (guide initially). Groups take turns to ask and answer each other's questions. Word-level learners also read aloud the consonants learned on the first day.","learners":"Read with actions; make questions (word-level learners help write them); ask and answer questions with another group.","tlm":"Story book, slate or paper for questions","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":4},{"activity":"Story: writing answers individually","grouping":"Individual","minutes":5,"teacher":"Para and Story level learners write answers to all questions individually; read and correct their responses after they finish.","learners":"Write the answers in their notebooks; Beginner/Letter/Word learners read or listen and answer orally.","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":5},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart: big group reading","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":3,"teacher":"Show the Barakhadi chart and ask which letter they like. Read the letter 's' on the chart; learners listen carefully and point to it on their own chart (they do not repeat after you).","learners":"Listen and point to the letter on their own chart.","tlm":"Barakhadi chart, alphabet or phonics chart","source":"M","ref":"p.13","n":6},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart: small-group practice","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Learners practise reading the alphabet or phonics chart in groups and help each other. One learner per group reads aloud. Occasionally ask learners to identify the sounds of letters. Give each level its group task.","learners":"Read the chart in groups; one learner reads aloud; do the level task.","tlm":"Alphabet or phonics chart, board or floor","source":"M","ref":"p.13","n":7},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart: individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":2,"teacher":"Give each learner an individual task for their level and observe closely; assist any learner who needs individual support.","learners":"Say and write a letter or word, a sentence or a short paragraph (by level).","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.13","n":8},{"activity":"Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on a lost and found thing","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Start a conversation about a picture card: 'a lost and found thing'. Involve all learners and ask open-ended questions.","learners":"Take part in the discussion and share thoughts freely.","tlm":"Picture card or topic on the board","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":9},{"activity":"Self-writing: individual writing","grouping":"Individual","minutes":7,"teacher":"Give each level its task (see level table). Let learners take ownership of what they draw and write; mistakes are fine.","learners":"Draw and write about the topic at their level.","tlm":"Notebooks, crayons or pencils","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":10},{"activity":"Self-writing: review and reading back","grouping":"Individual","minutes":3,"teacher":"Ask each learner 'What did you draw or write?' and have them read it aloud once. Word-level learners read to the group; discuss spelling, punctuation and sentence structure. Help beginners by writing their text in the notebook for them if needed.","learners":"Read what they wrote; correct mistakes after listening to their own reading.","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":11},{"activity":"Daily reading (10 minutes)","grouping":"Individual","minutes":10,"teacher":"Give each learner a library book or any storybook. Move around, listen to individual readers and note their level.","learners":"Read independently a book of their choice.","tlm":"Library books or storybooks","source":"M","ref":"p.7","n":12}],"procedures":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Alphabet song (last-letter word chain)","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","steps":[{"teacher":"Say the word 'yak' to the big group and show that its last letter is 'k'.","learners":"Listen and think of a word starting with 'k'."},{"teacher":"Ask learners in turn to say a word that starts with the last letter of the previous word. Example: rain -> nest.","learners":"Say a word in turn; anyone who cannot say a word is out of the game."},{"teacher":"Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Lead the game when it is their turn."}]},{"activity":"Oral conversation: conversation on a picture","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.9","steps":[{"teacher":"Show the picture of a library with children reading.","learners":"Look carefully."},{"teacher":"Ask: What is happening in the picture? Who is doing what? What is happening around them? Then: What might happen next?","learners":"Answer in their own words; every learner gets a chance."},{"teacher":"Let learners imagine and make up a short story from the picture.","learners":"Tell their stories to the class."}]},{"activity":"Story - Day 2 (a story about a rainy-day adventure)","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.11","steps":[{"teacher":"Ask learners to retell the story they read yesterday in their own words.","learners":"Retell, helping each other remember."},{"teacher":"In small groups learners practise reading the story using actions and expressions; one learner from each group then reads aloud to the class.","learners":"Read with actions and expression; a representative reads aloud."},{"teacher":"Guide the groups to come up with questions about the story (guide initially). Word-level learners can support by helping write them down.","learners":"Make questions together."},{"teacher":"Groups take turns to ask and answer each other's questions. Useful kinds: questions whose answer is not in the text; questions needing thinking beyond the text; questions asking for an opinion.","learners":"Ask, answer and discuss in the groups."},{"teacher":"Word-level learners also read aloud the consonants they learned on the first day.","learners":"Read the consonant clusters aloud."}]},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart activity (line 1)","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Small group (level-wise) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.13","steps":[{"teacher":"Show the Barakhadi chart and ask the learners which letter they like. Where is the letter 's'?","learners":"Look for the letter on the chart."},{"teacher":"Read the letter 's' on the chart. Learners listen and point to it on their own chart. Make sure they do not repeat after you.","learners":"Listen and point to the letter."},{"teacher":"Learners read the alphabet or phonics chart in their groups and help each other; one learner from each group comes forward to read aloud.","learners":"Read in groups; the representative reads aloud."},{"teacher":"Occasionally ask them to identify the sounds of letters from the chart.","learners":"Say the sound of the letter you point to."},{"teacher":"As an extra activity, write some letters on the floor, call out each letter one by one and let the learners jump onto the correct letter.","learners":"Jump onto the letter that is called."}]},{"activity":"Self-writing: 'Discussion, Writing, Self-review'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.15","steps":[{"teacher":"Start a conversation about a picture card: 'a lost and found thing'. Involve all learners and ask open-ended questions.","learners":"Discuss and answer questions."},{"teacher":"Give writing time at each level: draw then write (Beginner), write about what they liked (Letter), a sentence (Word), a paragraph or story on a topic of their choice (Para/Story).","learners":"Write at their level and take ownership of the work."},{"teacher":"Review: ask 'What did you draw or write?' Have each learner read the text aloud once. Support with writing if needed.","learners":"Read aloud, listen to their pronunciation and correct mistakes."}]}],"levelTasks":[{"activity":"Story - Day 2: level-wise tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.11","tasks":{"Beginner":"Retell with the group by pointing to pictures or words; read aloud with group support (interpretation of the manual's group reading task).","Letter":"Read with the group, pointing to words; say the letters and words they know (interpretation of the manual's group reading task).","Word":"Support the group in writing the questions; read aloud the consonant clusters learned on the first day.","Para":"Ask the group's questions to another group, discuss them, then write answers to all questions individually; the teacher reads and corrects.","Story":"Ask the group's questions to another group, discuss them, then write answers to all questions individually; the teacher reads and corrects."}},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart: level tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.13","tasks":{"Beginner":"Small group: read the chart in the group; find and write favourite letters from the line. Individual: say and write a letter of their choice.","Letter":"Small group: read the chart; find and write favourite letters or words from any line. Individual: say a word on their own that begins with any letter.","Word":"Small group: write one or two lines of letters on the board or floor and use them to form words. Individual: speak and write sentences using words they know.","Para":"Small group: prepare word lists using the Barakhadi chart (for example items found in a shop or in the kitchen). Individual: write short paragraphs using the words formed with the Barakhadi chart.","Story":"Small group: prepare word lists using the Barakhadi chart. Individual: write short paragraphs using the words formed with the Barakhadi chart."}},{"activity":"Self-writing: level tasks and review","source":"M","ref":"p.15","tasks":{"Beginner":"Draw a picture about the discussion and then write a few sentences about it, expressing thoughts freely. Review: say what they drew or wrote; read the text aloud once; the teacher may write the text in the notebook for them.","Letter":"Write about what they liked, using drawing and writing; write any words or sentences they can. Review: read the text aloud once; correct punctuation mistakes using the Barakhadi chart.","Word":"Write a sentence based on the conversation. Mistakes in spelling, punctuation and sentence structure are fine. Review: read it to the group; discuss and correct mistakes together.","Para":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation.","Story":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation."}}],"organisation":[{"grouping":"Whole class (big group)","how":"All learners of all levels sit in a 'U' shape arranged by level (Beginner, Letter, Word, Para, Story) so that the move to small groups is easy.","activities":["Warm-up: Alphabet song (last-letter word chain)","Oral conversation: conversation on a picture","Story (Day 2 of the story): retelling","Barakhadi chart: big group reading","Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on a lost and found thing"]},{"grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","how":"Learners of similar levels work together; the teacher gives each group a task for its level and spends more time with learners who need support. Rotate responsibilities (for example group leader).","activities":["Story: reading with actions and group questions","Barakhadi chart: small-group practice"]},{"grouping":"Individual","how":"Each learner works on a task for their own level; the teacher moves around, observes difficulties and supports individuals.","activities":["Story: writing answers individually","Barakhadi chart: individual tasks","Self-writing: individual writing","Self-writing: review and reading back","Daily reading (10 minutes)"]}],"materials":["Picture card of a library with children reading","The same story book as yesterday","Story book","slate or paper for questions","Notebooks","Barakhadi chart","alphabet or phonics chart","Alphabet or phonics chart","board or floor","Picture card or topic on the board","crayons or pencils","Library books or storybooks"],"outcomes":["Learners take part in the oral conversation and speak without fear.","Learners retell the story, read with expression and ask or answer questions at their level.","Learners respond to the sound-symbol task for today (Barakhadi / alphabet and phonics chart (line 1, letter 's')) at their own level.","Learners write about the topic at their level and read it aloud.","Each learner reads a book for 10 minutes."],"observation":["Observe each learner's reading and writing during the individual tasks; note who needs individual support and how many learners share the same difficulty.","Note any learner whose level is improving; move the learner to the next level group when you see steady progress (manual p.5).","Record each learner's progress for the day in the notebook, according to the learner's level (manual p.4).","Use today's observations to adjust tomorrow's plan (manual p.5)."],"teacherNotes":["Questions to elicit on Day 2: information questions (answer not in the text), thinking questions (needs knowledge beyond the text) and opinion questions (feedback on something in the text).","Barakhadi: learners who need extra time should get repeated practice using one or two sound units at a time. Topic-based discussion helps oral expression, thinking and understanding.","Writing has two parts, content and sequence: encourage learners to read what they wrote, improve it and rewrite it for clarity and correctness (manual p.15).","Pace: the manual says not to assume all learners progress at the same speed. Repeat a day's activity with the groups that need it before moving on.","Special needs: give extra time and prepare materials for slower learners; seat learners with hearing or vision difficulty at the front; for learners who reverse or confuse letters, trace letters on the letter card with a finger and write with dots to trace with a pencil (manual p.6)."],"components":[{"no":1,"key":"warmup","name":"Warm-up activities","keywords":["Alphabet song (last-letter word chain)","two learners lead"],"rows":[1]},{"no":2,"key":"oral","name":"Oral Discussion","keywords":["conversation on a picture","every learner speaks"],"rows":[2]},{"no":3,"key":"story","name":"Story","keywords":["Day 2","retell","read with actions","group questions","ask and answer","write answers (Para/Story)"],"rows":[3,4,5]},{"no":4,"key":"sound","name":"Sound symbol games, Sound separation-pairing","keywords":["Barakhadi / alphabet chart","listen and point (no repeating)","group reading","level tasks"],"rows":[6,7,8]},{"no":5,"key":"mindwrite","name":"Individual-Writing (Day 2)","keywords":["discussion","write at own level","self-review (read aloud)"],"rows":[9,10,11]},{"no":6,"key":"reading","name":"Daily reading","keywords":["library book","read alone","teacher listens"],"rows":[12]}],"preLesson":null},{"programme":"TARL Literacy","id":"lit-082","day":82,"phase":2,"phaseLabel":"Phase 2 (Days 46-90)","title":"Story: a story about courage in a storm (Day 1)","dayType":"Story Day 1 + Mind mapping","focus":"Language game: Pick a Word, Build a Sentence | Mind map: mountains","duration":70,"objectives":["Listen, speak and answer in the oral conversation (listening and storytelling).","Listen to and read a story with understanding; discuss it in big and small groups and respond at their own level.","Develop sound-symbol skills: Language game: Pick a Word, Build a Sentence.","Build vocabulary through a mind map ('mountains') and use the words at their own level.","Read independently for 10 minutes every day."],"sequence":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Handkerchief game","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Learners sit in a circle and clap while singing a rhyme ('I caught a Fish Alive'). One learner runs outside the circle with a handkerchief and secretly places it behind another learner, who must chase the runner. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Sit in a circle, clap and sing; run, place the handkerchief or chase as the game requires.","tlm":"A handkerchief","source":"M","ref":"p.8","n":1},{"activity":"Oral conversation: listening and storytelling","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Tell an interesting story starter and involve the learners: 'Yesterday I grabbed an elephant's tail and flew into the sky. What do you think happened next?' Let learners imagine and continue the story.","learners":"Listen to the teacher, then imagine and continue the story. Learners can also recite a rhyme or story they know.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.9","n":2},{"activity":"Story (Day 1 of the story): reading aloud and discussion","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":8,"teacher":"Discuss the title or picture of the story with the learners. Read the story aloud with expression and voice modulation (learners do not repeat after you). Discuss it, with emphasis on opinion questions. Read it again slowly, pointing to each word.","learners":"Talk about the title/picture; listen; answer questions; follow each word with a finger in their own copy.","tlm":"A story from the school library (a story about courage in a storm), a copy for each learner","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":3},{"activity":"Story: reading in small groups","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":7,"teacher":"Form level-wise groups with a group leader. Learners read the story one sentence at a time while the others follow with their fingers. Para and Story level learners practise reading with emotion and expression.","learners":"Read the story sentence by sentence, supporting each other; the group leader helps.","tlm":"Story book copies","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":4},{"activity":"Story: level-wise individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":5,"teacher":"Give each learner the task for their level (see level table) and support those who need it.","learners":"Beginner/Letter: find and write favourite words or letters. Word: find consonant clusters. Para/Story: silently read, find unfamiliar and rhyming words.","tlm":"Story book, notebooks, board","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":5},{"activity":"Language game: Pick a Word, Build a Sentence","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Words on slips are kept in a basket; each learner picks one, reads it and says a sentence, linking to the previous sentence. Observe each learner and give help where needed.","learners":"Play the game, take turns and read or say the words they make.","tlm":"Word slips, basket or pan","source":"M","ref":"p.20","n":6},{"activity":"Mind mapping (Day 1): the word 'mountains'","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Ask: 'What words come to your mind when you hear the word mountains?' Write learners' answers on the board or floor (Para and Story level learners write the words themselves). Guide the map towards the learning objective. Example words: peak, valley, stream, cave, yak, goat, eagle, snow leopard, snow, wind, fog, cold.","learners":"Say words connected with 'mountains'; share the meaning and feeling of words.","tlm":"Board, chalk (or floor)","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":7},{"activity":"Mind mapping: classify the words","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":4,"teacher":"Ask learners to classify the words in groups, for example: Things: peak, valley, stream, cave; Animals: yak, goat, eagle, snow leopard; Weather: snow, wind, fog, cold.","learners":"Sort the words into groups and say why.","tlm":"Board, chalk, word cards (optional)","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":8},{"activity":"Mind mapping: level-wise individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":6,"teacher":"Give each learner the individual task for their level; observe closely and give individual support. Display corrected stories on the wall.","learners":"Complete the task for their level (see level table).","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":9},{"activity":"Daily reading (10 minutes)","grouping":"Individual","minutes":10,"teacher":"Give each learner a library book or any storybook. Move around, listen to individual readers and note their level.","learners":"Read independently a book of their choice.","tlm":"Library books or storybooks","source":"M","ref":"p.7","n":10}],"procedures":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Handkerchief game","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","steps":[{"teacher":"Seat the learners in a circle and start clapping and singing the rhyme 'I caught a Fish Alive'.","learners":"Clap and sing together."},{"teacher":"One learner runs outside the circle holding a handkerchief and secretly places it behind another learner.","learners":"Everyone keeps clapping; the learner who finds the handkerchief behind them takes it and chases the runner."},{"teacher":"If the runner sits in the chaser's place before being caught, they stay in the game; if caught, they are out. Continue in this way.","learners":"Play fairly and take turns."}]},{"activity":"Oral conversation: listening and storytelling","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.9","steps":[{"teacher":"Say the starter: 'Yesterday I grabbed an elephant's tail and flew into the sky. What do you think happened next?'","learners":"Listen and imagine."},{"teacher":"Ask learners to continue the story one by one. Encourage those who speak less.","learners":"Add ideas to the story."},{"teacher":"Invite a learner to recite a poem or rhyme they know.","learners":"Recite and listen to others."}]},{"activity":"Story - Day 1 (a story about courage in a storm)","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.10","steps":[{"teacher":"Discuss the title or picture of the story with the learners.","learners":"Talk about what they see and what the story may be about."},{"teacher":"Read the story aloud with expression and proper voice modulation. Learners should not simply repeat after you.","learners":"Listen carefully and enjoy the story."},{"teacher":"Discuss the story: factual, logical, vocabulary-based, judgment or opinion questions (today's focus: opinion: What did you like best? What would you have done in the story?). Begin in the home language if needed.","learners":"Think and respond thoughtfully; every learner takes part."},{"teacher":"Read the story again slowly, pointing to each word. Make sure each learner has a copy and follows with a finger.","learners":"Follow each word with their finger."},{"teacher":"Ask learners to read in small groups; select a group leader who helps the others. Learners read one sentence at a time while the others point with fingers.","learners":"Read with the help of one another."}]},{"activity":"Language game: Pick a Word, Build a Sentence","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.20","steps":[{"teacher":"Write different words on small slips and put them in an earthen basket or pan.","learners":"Sit in a circle."},{"teacher":"Call one learner at a time to pick a slip, read the word aloud and say a sentence using it.","learners":"Read the word, say a sentence."},{"teacher":"The next learner picks a new word and says a sentence that connects with the previous one, using their own word.","learners":"Build a chain of sentences together."}]},{"activity":"Mind mapping: 'mountains'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Small group (level-wise) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.14","steps":[{"teacher":"Choose a word that can generate many related words: 'mountains'. Ask: 'What words come to your mind when you hear the word mountains?' Write the answers on the board or floor.","learners":"Say words they link with 'mountains'."},{"teacher":"Discuss the words: what they mean and how they are connected.","learners":"Explain their words and listen to others."},{"teacher":"In small groups, let the learners classify the words (Things: peak, valley, stream, cave; Animals: yak, goat, eagle, snow leopard; Weather: snow, wind, fog, cold).","learners":"Sort the words into groups."},{"teacher":"Give the individual tasks by level and help each learner.","learners":"Work individually; read the work aloud at the end if time allows."}]}],"levelTasks":[{"activity":"Story - Day 1: individual tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.10","tasks":{"Beginner":"Circle or search for a favourite word or letter in the story and say it aloud. If a learner cannot draw a circle, write words on the board and ask them to identify them.","Letter":"Find, read and write favourite words from the story.","Word":"Find the consonant clusters in the story, read them and write them in the notebook.","Para":"Silently read the story from the textbook; find unfamiliar words and try to understand them; find rhyming words, use them in sentences and write in the notebook; ask other groups for meanings; make questions in groups.","Story":"Silently read the story; find unfamiliar words and rhyming words; practise reading with emotion; one group reads sentences formed with consonant clusters to the other group; ask and answer group questions (information, thinking and opinion questions)."}},{"activity":"Language game: Pick a Word, Build a Sentence - level support","source":"I","ref":"p.20","tasks":{"Beginner":"Take part by saying or pointing to the letters involved and by listening carefully; Para and Story level partners help.","Letter":"Say the letters/sounds and give simple words they know.","Word":"Say and write words and short sentences for the game.","Para":"Write sentences with the words; help groups to record answers.","Story":"Write sentences or short stories with the words; help groups to record answers."}},{"activity":"Mind mapping 'mountains': level tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.14","tasks":{"Beginner":"Circle all the words that contain the letter 'A' on the board; make a list. See how many learners find the most words.","Letter":"Circle all the words that contain the letter 'A' and make a list of them.","Word":"Use 4-5 words (for example fog, yak, cave, cold, goat) to form sentences, starting with words of one or two syllables. Example: Dream - I had a dream last night.","Para":"Choose any five words from the map and create a story with them. Use consonant clusters correctly, read the story aloud, correct mistakes of sentence structure, spelling or grammar, then display it on the wall.","Story":"Choose any five words from the map and create a story with them. Use consonant clusters correctly, read the story aloud, correct mistakes of sentence structure, spelling or grammar, then display it on the wall."}}],"organisation":[{"grouping":"Whole class (big group)","how":"All learners of all levels sit in a 'U' shape arranged by level (Beginner, Letter, Word, Para, Story) so that the move to small groups is easy.","activities":["Warm-up: Handkerchief game","Oral conversation: listening and storytelling","Story (Day 1 of the story): reading aloud and discussion","Language game: Pick a Word, Build a Sentence","Mind mapping (Day 1): the word 'mountains'"]},{"grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","how":"Learners of similar levels work together; the teacher gives each group a task for its level and spends more time with learners who need support. Rotate responsibilities (for example group leader).","activities":["Story: reading in small groups","Mind mapping: classify the words"]},{"grouping":"Individual","how":"Each learner works on a task for their own level; the teacher moves around, observes difficulties and supports individuals.","activities":["Story: level-wise individual tasks","Mind mapping: level-wise individual tasks","Daily reading (10 minutes)"]}],"materials":["A handkerchief","A story from the school library (a story about courage in a storm)","a copy for each learner","Story book copies","Story book","notebooks","board","Word slips","basket or pan","Board","chalk (or floor)","chalk","word cards (optional)","Notebooks","Library books or storybooks"],"outcomes":["Learners take part in the oral conversation and speak without fear.","Learners show understanding of the story in the discussion and complete the task for their level.","Learners respond to the sound-symbol task for today (Language game: Pick a Word, Build a Sentence) at their own level.","Learners add words to the mind map and use them in sentences or a story at their level.","Each learner reads a book for 10 minutes."],"observation":["Observe each learner's reading and writing during the individual tasks; note who needs individual support and how many learners share the same difficulty.","Note any learner whose level is improving; move the learner to the next level group when you see steady progress (manual p.5).","Record each learner's progress for the day in the notebook, according to the learner's level (manual p.4).","Use today's observations to adjust tomorrow's plan (manual p.5)."],"teacherNotes":["Story selection: the manual asks teachers to use picture story books or stories in the school library. Today's suggested theme (a story about courage in a storm) is a planning suggestion; use any suitable story you have.","The manual lists the letter and word games but does not fix the slot in the daily timetable where they are used. This plan places them in the 10-minute sound-symbol / alphabet slot (interpretation).","Mind mapping topic for this day: 'mountains'. The manual's example uses the word 'shop'; today's topic follows the same method.","Pace: the manual says not to assume all learners progress at the same speed. Repeat a day's activity with the groups that need it before moving on.","Special needs: give extra time and prepare materials for slower learners; seat learners with hearing or vision difficulty at the front; for learners who reverse or confuse letters, trace letters on the letter card with a finger and write with dots to trace with a pencil (manual p.6)."],"components":[{"no":1,"key":"warmup","name":"Warm-up activities","keywords":["Handkerchief game","two learners lead"],"rows":[1]},{"no":2,"key":"oral","name":"Oral Discussion","keywords":["listening and storytelling","every learner speaks"],"rows":[2]},{"no":3,"key":"story","name":"Story","keywords":["Day 1","title / picture talk","read aloud with expression","opinion questions","re-read pointing","group reading","level tasks"],"rows":[3,4,5]},{"no":4,"key":"sound","name":"Sound symbol games, Sound separation-pairing","keywords":["Pick a Word, Build a Sentence","play in turns","level support"],"rows":[6]},{"no":5,"key":"mindwrite","name":"Mind Mapping (Day 1)","keywords":["mind map: mountains","classify the words","level task: circle letter A / sentences / story"],"rows":[7,8,9]},{"no":6,"key":"reading","name":"Daily reading","keywords":["library book","read alone","teacher listens"],"rows":[10]}],"preLesson":null},{"programme":"TARL Literacy","id":"lit-083","day":83,"phase":2,"phaseLabel":"Phase 2 (Days 46-90)","title":"Story: a story about courage in a storm (Day 2)","dayType":"Story Day 2 + Self-writing","focus":"Consonant clusters: spl (split, splash) | Self-writing: something I made myself","duration":70,"objectives":["Listen, speak and answer in the oral conversation (What did you see on your way?).","Retell the story, read it with expression, ask and answer questions about it and write answers.","Develop sound-symbol skills: Consonant clusters: spl (split, splash).","Write about a topic at their own level and review the writing (something I made myself).","Read independently for 10 minutes every day."],"sequence":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Rhyme - 'I saw a Little Bird'","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Say the rhyme with actions, then say it together. Lines: I saw a little bird go hop, hop, hop / I told the little bird to stop, stop, stop. / I went to the window to say 'How do you do?' / He wagged his little tail and far away he flew! Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Listen, then say the rhyme with actions.","tlm":"Rhyme chart or board (optional)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","n":1},{"activity":"Oral conversation: What did you see on your way?","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Ask learners to describe what they saw on their way to school. If they are hesitant, begin yourself: 'On the road I saw a bullock cart, a tea stall and a boy flying a kite. What did you see?'","learners":"Describe what they saw on the way to school and connect with what others share.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.9","n":2},{"activity":"Story (Day 2 of the story): retelling","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":6,"teacher":"Ask learners to retell yesterday's story in their own words. Prompt with questions on the beginning, middle and end.","learners":"Retell the story using their own words.","tlm":"The same story book as yesterday","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":3},{"activity":"Story: reading with actions and group questions","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":9,"teacher":"Learners practise reading with actions and expressions; one learner per group reads aloud to the class. Guide groups to make questions about the story (guide initially). Groups take turns to ask and answer each other's questions. Word-level learners also read aloud the consonants learned on the first day.","learners":"Read with actions; make questions (word-level learners help write them); ask and answer questions with another group.","tlm":"Story book, slate or paper for questions","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":4},{"activity":"Story: writing answers individually","grouping":"Individual","minutes":5,"teacher":"Para and Story level learners write answers to all questions individually; read and correct their responses after they finish.","learners":"Write the answers in their notebooks; Beginner/Letter/Word learners read or listen and answer orally.","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":5},{"activity":"Consonant clusters: introduction","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":4,"teacher":"Three-letter clusters: after two-letter clusters, familiarise learners with clusters of three letters ('spl' as in split, splash, splendid). Discuss the words, then ask learners to tell and write sentences using them.","learners":"Listen, pronounce the cluster and say words that contain it.","tlm":"Board and chalk, words list (split splash splendid splinter splatter)","source":"M","ref":"p.16","n":6},{"activity":"Consonant cluster game: Looking for Similar Ones","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":6,"teacher":"Write some words with the same conjunct consonants on the board, for example bl, tr, st. Observe closely and help learners who need support.","learners":"Match words that have the same conjunct consonant (black, blue, blanket, blow, blink).","tlm":"Words on the board","source":"M","ref":"p.17","n":7},{"activity":"Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on something I made myself","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Start a conversation about a topic: 'something I made myself'. Involve all learners and ask open-ended questions.","learners":"Take part in the discussion and share thoughts freely.","tlm":"Picture card or topic on the board","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":8},{"activity":"Self-writing: individual writing","grouping":"Individual","minutes":7,"teacher":"Give each level its task (see level table). Let learners take ownership of what they draw and write; mistakes are fine.","learners":"Draw and write about the topic at their level.","tlm":"Notebooks, crayons or pencils","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":9},{"activity":"Self-writing: review and reading back","grouping":"Individual","minutes":3,"teacher":"Ask each learner 'What did you draw or write?' and have them read it aloud once. Word-level learners read to the group; discuss spelling, punctuation and sentence structure. Help beginners by writing their text in the notebook for them if needed.","learners":"Read what they wrote; correct mistakes after listening to their own reading.","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":10},{"activity":"Daily reading (10 minutes)","grouping":"Individual","minutes":10,"teacher":"Give each learner a library book or any storybook. Move around, listen to individual readers and note their level.","learners":"Read independently a book of their choice.","tlm":"Library books or storybooks","source":"M","ref":"p.7","n":11}],"procedures":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Rhyme - 'I saw a Little Bird'","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","steps":[{"teacher":"Say the rhyme 'I saw a Little Bird' slowly with actions: I saw a little bird go hop, hop, hop / I told the little bird to stop, stop, stop. / I went to the window to say 'How do you do?' / He wagged his little tail and far away he flew!","learners":"Listen and watch the actions."},{"teacher":"Say it again; invite learners to join with actions.","learners":"Say the rhyme together with actions."},{"teacher":"Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Choose a rhyme they like and lead."}]},{"activity":"Oral conversation: What did you see on your way?","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.9","steps":[{"teacher":"Ask: 'What did you see on your way to school today?'","learners":"Think about the way to school."},{"teacher":"If learners hesitate, start: 'On the road I saw a bullock cart, a tea stall and a boy flying a kite. What did you see?'","learners":"Listen to the model and then share their own observations."},{"teacher":"Connect learners' answers with each other.","learners":"Listen and add what they noticed."}]},{"activity":"Story - Day 2 (a story about courage in a storm)","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.11","steps":[{"teacher":"Ask learners to retell the story they read yesterday in their own words.","learners":"Retell, helping each other remember."},{"teacher":"In small groups learners practise reading the story using actions and expressions; one learner from each group then reads aloud to the class.","learners":"Read with actions and expression; a representative reads aloud."},{"teacher":"Guide the groups to come up with questions about the story (guide initially). Word-level learners can support by helping write them down.","learners":"Make questions together."},{"teacher":"Groups take turns to ask and answer each other's questions. Useful kinds: questions whose answer is not in the text; questions needing thinking beyond the text; questions asking for an opinion.","learners":"Ask, answer and discuss in the groups."},{"teacher":"Word-level learners also read aloud the consonants they learned on the first day.","learners":"Read the consonant clusters aloud."}]},{"activity":"Consonant clusters (spl) and the game 'Looking for Similar Ones'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.16-17","steps":[{"teacher":"Three-letter clusters: after two-letter clusters, familiarise learners with clusters of three letters ('spl' as in split, splash, splendid). Discuss the words, then ask learners to tell and write sentences using them.","learners":"Listen, pronounce and find words in the text."},{"teacher":"Write the words on the board: split splash splendid splinter splatter. Read them aloud with distinct pronunciation of the cluster.","learners":"Read the words aloud; point to the cluster in each word."},{"teacher":"Write some words with the same conjunct consonants on the board, for example bl, tr, st.","learners":"Match words that have the same conjunct consonant (black, blue, blanket, blow, blink)."}]},{"activity":"Self-writing: 'Discussion, Writing, Self-review'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.15","steps":[{"teacher":"Start a conversation about a topic: 'something I made myself'. Involve all learners and ask open-ended questions.","learners":"Discuss and answer questions."},{"teacher":"Give writing time at each level: draw then write (Beginner), write about what they liked (Letter), a sentence (Word), a paragraph or story on a topic of their choice (Para/Story).","learners":"Write at their level and take ownership of the work."},{"teacher":"Review: ask 'What did you draw or write?' Have each learner read the text aloud once. Support with writing if needed.","learners":"Read aloud, listen to their pronunciation and correct mistakes."}]}],"levelTasks":[{"activity":"Story - Day 2: level-wise tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.11","tasks":{"Beginner":"Retell with the group by pointing to pictures or words; read aloud with group support (interpretation of the manual's group reading task).","Letter":"Read with the group, pointing to words; say the letters and words they know (interpretation of the manual's group reading task).","Word":"Support the group in writing the questions; read aloud the consonant clusters learned on the first day.","Para":"Ask the group's questions to another group, discuss them, then write answers to all questions individually; the teacher reads and corrects.","Story":"Ask the group's questions to another group, discuss them, then write answers to all questions individually; the teacher reads and corrects."}},{"activity":"Consonant clusters (spl): level tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.16-17","tasks":{"Beginner":"Listen to the sound of the cluster and point to it in a word; continue with letter-sound work (interpretation: the manual describes clusters for learners lagging in reading words and sentences).","Letter":"Listen to the cluster sound and pick words with the cluster from a word card (interpretation).","Word":"Find the cluster in the story or textbook words, read the words and write them in the notebook.","Para":"Form words and sentences using the cluster; read the sentences aloud.","Story":"Form words and sentences using the cluster; read the sentences aloud; use them in the story writing."}},{"activity":"Self-writing: level tasks and review","source":"M","ref":"p.15","tasks":{"Beginner":"Draw a picture about the discussion and then write a few sentences about it, expressing thoughts freely. Review: say what they drew or wrote; read the text aloud once; the teacher may write the text in the notebook for them.","Letter":"Write about what they liked, using drawing and writing; write any words or sentences they can. Review: read the text aloud once; correct punctuation mistakes using the Barakhadi chart.","Word":"Write a sentence based on the conversation. Mistakes in spelling, punctuation and sentence structure are fine. Review: read it to the group; discuss and correct mistakes together.","Para":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation.","Story":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation."}}],"organisation":[{"grouping":"Whole class (big group)","how":"All learners of all levels sit in a 'U' shape arranged by level (Beginner, Letter, Word, Para, Story) so that the move to small groups is easy.","activities":["Warm-up: Rhyme - 'I saw a Little Bird'","Oral conversation: What did you see on your way?","Story (Day 2 of the story): retelling","Consonant clusters: introduction","Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on something I made myself"]},{"grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","how":"Learners of similar levels work together; the teacher gives each group a task for its level and spends more time with learners who need support. Rotate responsibilities (for example group leader).","activities":["Story: reading with actions and group questions","Consonant cluster game: Looking for Similar Ones"]},{"grouping":"Individual","how":"Each learner works on a task for their own level; the teacher moves around, observes difficulties and supports individuals.","activities":["Story: writing answers individually","Self-writing: individual writing","Self-writing: review and reading back","Daily reading (10 minutes)"]}],"materials":["Rhyme chart or board (optional)","The same story book as yesterday","Story book","slate or paper for questions","Notebooks","Board","chalk","words list (split splash splendid splinter splatter)","Words on the board","Picture card or topic on the board","crayons or pencils","Library books or storybooks"],"outcomes":["Learners take part in the oral conversation and speak without fear.","Learners retell the story, read with expression and ask or answer questions at their level.","Learners respond to the sound-symbol task for today (Consonant clusters: spl (split, splash)) at their own level.","Learners write about the topic at their level and read it aloud.","Each learner reads a book for 10 minutes."],"observation":["Observe each learner's reading and writing during the individual tasks; note who needs individual support and how many learners share the same difficulty.","Note any learner whose level is improving; move the learner to the next level group when you see steady progress (manual p.5).","Record each learner's progress for the day in the notebook, according to the learner's level (manual p.4).","Use today's observations to adjust tomorrow's plan (manual p.5)."],"teacherNotes":["Questions to elicit on Day 2: information questions (answer not in the text), thinking questions (needs knowledge beyond the text) and opinion questions (feedback on something in the text).","Consonant clusters: do these activities daily for learners who find reading complex words hard; the aim is to remove the fear of reading clusters. Teachers may carry out similar activities on their own.","Writing has two parts, content and sequence: encourage learners to read what they wrote, improve it and rewrite it for clarity and correctness (manual p.15).","Pace: the manual says not to assume all learners progress at the same speed. Repeat a day's activity with the groups that need it before moving on.","Special needs: give extra time and prepare materials for slower learners; seat learners with hearing or vision difficulty at the front; for learners who reverse or confuse letters, trace letters on the letter card with a finger and write with dots to trace with a pencil (manual p.6)."],"components":[{"no":1,"key":"warmup","name":"Warm-up activities","keywords":["Rhyme - 'I saw a Little Bird'","two learners lead"],"rows":[1]},{"no":2,"key":"oral","name":"Oral Discussion","keywords":["What did you see on your way?","every learner speaks"],"rows":[2]},{"no":3,"key":"story","name":"Story","keywords":["Day 2","retell","read with actions","group questions","ask and answer","write answers (Para/Story)"],"rows":[3,4,5]},{"no":4,"key":"sound","name":"Sound symbol games, Sound separation-pairing","keywords":["consonant cluster 'spl'","pronounce and find words","game: Looking for Similar Ones"],"rows":[6,7]},{"no":5,"key":"mindwrite","name":"Individual-Writing (Day 2)","keywords":["discussion","write at own level","self-review (read aloud)"],"rows":[8,9,10]},{"no":6,"key":"reading","name":"Daily reading","keywords":["library book","read alone","teacher listens"],"rows":[11]}],"preLesson":null},{"programme":"TARL Literacy","id":"lit-084","day":84,"phase":2,"phaseLabel":"Phase 2 (Days 46-90)","title":"Saturday: drama presentation","dayType":"Saturday drama + Self-writing","focus":"Barakhadi / alphabet and phonics chart (line 4, letter 'n') | Self-writing: the story we acted out (a story about courage in a storm)","duration":70,"objectives":["Listen, speak and answer in the oral conversation (familiar topic).","Express a story through role play, using voice, facial expressions and gestures.","Develop sound-symbol skills: Barakhadi / alphabet and phonics chart (line 4, letter 'n').","Write about the story and review the writing.","Read independently for 10 minutes every day."],"sequence":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Singing and Spinning","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Learners sit in a circle and pass a small object while you clap with your back turned; when the clapping stops, the learner holding it sings a song, recites a poem or tells a joke. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Pass the object round the circle; sing, recite or tell a joke when the clapping stops.","tlm":"A small object (chalk or pencil)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","n":1},{"activity":"Oral conversation: familiar topic","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Hold a conversation on the topic 'my favourite food and who cooks it'. Give each learner a chance to speak; be patient with learners who need extra time.","learners":"Talk about the topic and listen to others.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.9","n":2},{"activity":"Dramatic presentation: introduction and reading","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Explain what a dramatic presentation is and how it is done. Provide stories discussed during the week and read one aloud once more. Para and Story level learners support Beginner and Letter level learners in reading.","learners":"Listen, read along, then each learner chooses a character.","tlm":"Stories discussed in the week (a story about a rainy-day adventure; a story about courage in a storm)","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":3},{"activity":"Dramatic presentation: planning in small groups","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":8,"teacher":"Each group discusses and plans dialogues; Para or Story level learners write the dialogues. Groups prepare their dramatic presentation.","learners":"Choose characters, plan and rehearse dialogues with facial expressions and gestures.","tlm":"Story, paper for dialogues","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":4},{"activity":"Dramatic presentation: performances and feedback","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":7,"teacher":"Learners sit in a U shape. Each group presents; after each performance, watching learners say what they enjoyed and what could be improved.","learners":"Perform in turn; watch; give feedback.","tlm":"Open space (U-shape seating)","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":5},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart: big group reading","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":3,"teacher":"Show the Barakhadi chart and ask which letter they like. Read the letter 'n' on the chart; learners listen carefully and point to it on their own chart (they do not repeat after you).","learners":"Listen and point to the letter on their own chart.","tlm":"Barakhadi chart, alphabet or phonics chart","source":"M","ref":"p.13","n":6},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart: small-group practice","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Learners practise reading the alphabet or phonics chart in groups and help each other. One learner per group reads aloud. Occasionally ask learners to identify the sounds of letters. Give each level its group task.","learners":"Read the chart in groups; one learner reads aloud; do the level task.","tlm":"Alphabet or phonics chart, board or floor","source":"M","ref":"p.13","n":7},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart: individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":2,"teacher":"Give each learner an individual task for their level and observe closely; assist any learner who needs individual support.","learners":"Say and write a letter or word, a sentence or a short paragraph (by level).","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.13","n":8},{"activity":"Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on the story we acted out (a story about courage in a storm)","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Start a conversation about the story used for the drama: 'the story we acted out (a story about courage in a storm)'. Involve all learners with open-ended questions.","learners":"Take part in the discussion and share thoughts freely.","tlm":"Picture card or topic on the board","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":9},{"activity":"Self-writing: individual writing","grouping":"Individual","minutes":7,"teacher":"Give each level its task (see level table). Let learners take ownership of what they draw and write; mistakes are fine.","learners":"Draw and write about the topic at their level.","tlm":"Notebooks, crayons or pencils","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":10},{"activity":"Self-writing: review and reading back","grouping":"Individual","minutes":3,"teacher":"Ask each learner 'What did you draw or write?' and have them read it aloud once. Word-level learners read to the group; discuss spelling, punctuation and sentence structure. Help beginners by writing their text in the notebook for them if needed.","learners":"Read what they wrote; correct mistakes after listening to their own reading.","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":11},{"activity":"Daily reading (10 minutes)","grouping":"Individual","minutes":10,"teacher":"Give each learner a library book or any storybook. Move around, listen to individual readers and note their level.","learners":"Read independently a book of their choice.","tlm":"Library books or storybooks","source":"M","ref":"p.7","n":12}],"procedures":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Singing and Spinning","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","steps":[{"teacher":"Seat the learners in a circle; give a small object to one learner.","learners":"Sit in a circle."},{"teacher":"Stand outside the circle with your back to them and clap steadily; they pass the object.","learners":"Pass the object while the clapping continues."},{"teacher":"Stop clapping; the learner holding the object sings, recites or tells a joke.","learners":"Perform, and everybody claps."}]},{"activity":"Oral conversation: familiar topic","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.9","steps":[{"teacher":"Introduce the topic: 'my favourite food and who cooks it'.","learners":"Think about their own experience."},{"teacher":"Ask open questions; give every learner a chance. Involve learners who speak less.","learners":"Speak freely and without fear."},{"teacher":"Praise efforts and sum up.","learners":"Listen and respect each other's ideas."}]},{"activity":"Saturday special: dramatic presentation","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.11","steps":[{"teacher":"Explain what a dramatic presentation is and how it can be done. Give the groups the stories discussed during the week.","learners":"Listen to the explanation."},{"teacher":"Read a story aloud once more. Learners at story and paragraph level support those at beginner and letter level in reading.","learners":"Read along; helpers support their friends."},{"teacher":"After reading, each learner chooses a character from the story.","learners":"Choose a role (boys may play girl roles and girls may play boy roles)."},{"teacher":"In groups, learners discuss and plan the dialogues; paragraph or story level learners write the dialogues.","learners":"Plan and write dialogues together."},{"teacher":"Learners sit in a U shape. Each group presents its drama. After each performance, ask what the audience enjoyed and what could be improved.","learners":"Perform, watch and give kind feedback."}]},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart activity (line 4)","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Small group (level-wise) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.13","steps":[{"teacher":"Show the Barakhadi chart and ask the learners which letter they like. Where is the letter 'n'?","learners":"Look for the letter on the chart."},{"teacher":"Read the letter 'n' on the chart. Learners listen and point to it on their own chart. Make sure they do not repeat after you.","learners":"Listen and point to the letter."},{"teacher":"Learners read the alphabet or phonics chart in their groups and help each other; one learner from each group comes forward to read aloud.","learners":"Read in groups; the representative reads aloud."},{"teacher":"Occasionally ask them to identify the sounds of letters from the chart.","learners":"Say the sound of the letter you point to."},{"teacher":"As an extra activity, write some letters on the floor, call out each letter one by one and let the learners jump onto the correct letter.","learners":"Jump onto the letter that is called."}]},{"activity":"Self-writing: 'Discussion, Writing, Self-review'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.15","steps":[{"teacher":"Start a conversation about the story used for the drama: 'the story we acted out (a story about courage in a storm)'. Involve all learners with open-ended questions.","learners":"Discuss and answer questions."},{"teacher":"Give writing time at each level: draw then write (Beginner), write about what they liked (Letter), a sentence (Word), a paragraph or story on a topic of their choice (Para/Story).","learners":"Write at their level and take ownership of the work."},{"teacher":"Review: ask 'What did you draw or write?' Have each learner read the text aloud once. Support with writing if needed.","learners":"Read aloud, listen to their pronunciation and correct mistakes."}]}],"levelTasks":[{"activity":"Drama: roles by level","source":"M","ref":"p.11","tasks":{"Beginner":"Take a character role and say or act short lines with help from Para and Story level learners.","Letter":"Take a character role and say or act short lines with help from Para and Story level learners.","Word":"Take a role and speak the dialogues; help rehearse.","Para":"Write the dialogues for the group and support Beginner, Letter and Word level learners throughout.","Story":"Write the dialogues for the group and support Beginner, Letter and Word level learners throughout."}},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart: level tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.13","tasks":{"Beginner":"Small group: read the chart in the group; find and write favourite letters from the line. Individual: say and write a letter of their choice.","Letter":"Small group: read the chart; find and write favourite letters or words from any line. Individual: say a word on their own that begins with any letter.","Word":"Small group: write one or two lines of letters on the board or floor and use them to form words. Individual: speak and write sentences using words they know.","Para":"Small group: prepare word lists using the Barakhadi chart (for example items found in a shop or in the kitchen). Individual: write short paragraphs using the words formed with the Barakhadi chart.","Story":"Small group: prepare word lists using the Barakhadi chart. Individual: write short paragraphs using the words formed with the Barakhadi chart."}},{"activity":"Self-writing: level tasks and review","source":"M","ref":"p.15","tasks":{"Beginner":"Draw a picture about the discussion and then write a few sentences about it, expressing thoughts freely. Review: say what they drew or wrote; read the text aloud once; the teacher may write the text in the notebook for them.","Letter":"Write about what they liked, using drawing and writing; write any words or sentences they can. Review: read the text aloud once; correct punctuation mistakes using the Barakhadi chart.","Word":"Write a sentence based on the conversation. Mistakes in spelling, punctuation and sentence structure are fine. Review: read it to the group; discuss and correct mistakes together.","Para":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation.","Story":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation."}}],"organisation":[{"grouping":"Whole class (big group)","how":"All learners of all levels sit in a 'U' shape arranged by level (Beginner, Letter, Word, Para, Story) so that the move to small groups is easy.","activities":["Warm-up: Singing and Spinning","Oral conversation: familiar topic","Dramatic presentation: introduction and reading","Dramatic presentation: performances and feedback","Barakhadi chart: big group reading","Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on the story we acted out (a story about courage in a storm)"]},{"grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","how":"Learners of similar levels work together; the teacher gives each group a task for its level and spends more time with learners who need support. Rotate responsibilities (for example group leader).","activities":["Dramatic presentation: planning in small groups","Barakhadi chart: small-group practice"]},{"grouping":"Individual","how":"Each learner works on a task for their own level; the teacher moves around, observes difficulties and supports individuals.","activities":["Barakhadi chart: individual tasks","Self-writing: individual writing","Self-writing: review and reading back","Daily reading (10 minutes)"]}],"materials":["A small object (chalk or pencil)","Stories discussed in the week (a story about a rainy-day adventure; a story about courage in a storm)","Story","paper for dialogues","Open space (U-shape seating)","Barakhadi chart","alphabet or phonics chart","Alphabet or phonics chart","board or floor","Notebooks","Picture card or topic on the board","crayons or pencils","Library books or storybooks"],"outcomes":["Learners take part in the oral conversation and speak without fear.","Learners present a role in the group drama and give feedback to others.","Learners respond to the sound-symbol task for today (Barakhadi / alphabet and phonics chart (line 4, letter 'n')) at their own level.","Learners write about the story at their level and read it aloud.","Each learner reads a book for 10 minutes."],"observation":["Observe each learner's reading and writing during the individual tasks; note who needs individual support and how many learners share the same difficulty.","Note any learner whose level is improving; move the learner to the next level group when you see steady progress (manual p.5).","Record each learner's progress for the day in the notebook, according to the learner's level (manual p.4).","Use today's observations to adjust tomorrow's plan (manual p.5)."],"teacherNotes":["Saturday: this plan assumes Day 1 is a Monday (six teaching days per week). If your school week is different, hold the drama presentation on your Saturday and keep the other days in sequence.","Barakhadi: learners who need extra time should get repeated practice using one or two sound units at a time. Topic-based discussion helps oral expression, thinking and understanding.","Writing has two parts, content and sequence: encourage learners to read what they wrote, improve it and rewrite it for clarity and correctness (manual p.15).","Pace: the manual says not to assume all learners progress at the same speed. Repeat a day's activity with the groups that need it before moving on.","Special needs: give extra time and prepare materials for slower learners; seat learners with hearing or vision difficulty at the front; for learners who reverse or confuse letters, trace letters on the letter card with a finger and write with dots to trace with a pencil (manual p.6)."],"components":[{"no":1,"key":"warmup","name":"Warm-up activities","keywords":["Singing and Spinning","two learners lead"],"rows":[1]},{"no":2,"key":"oral","name":"Oral Discussion","keywords":["familiar topic","every learner speaks"],"rows":[2]},{"no":3,"key":"story","name":"Story (Saturday: dramatic presentation)","keywords":["Saturday drama","choose a character","plan dialogues","perform in U shape","feedback"],"rows":[3,4,5]},{"no":4,"key":"sound","name":"Sound symbol games, Sound separation-pairing","keywords":["Barakhadi / alphabet chart","listen and point (no repeating)","group reading","level tasks"],"rows":[6,7,8]},{"no":5,"key":"mindwrite","name":"Individual-Writing (Day 2)","keywords":["discussion","write at own level","self-review (read aloud)"],"rows":[9,10,11]},{"no":6,"key":"reading","name":"Daily reading","keywords":["library book","read alone","teacher listens"],"rows":[12]}],"preLesson":null},{"programme":"TARL Literacy","id":"lit-085","day":85,"phase":2,"phaseLabel":"Phase 2 (Days 46-90)","title":"Story: a story about learning to read (Day 1)","dayType":"Story Day 1 + Mind mapping","focus":"Language game: Find My Word | Mind map: sky","duration":70,"objectives":["Listen, speak and answer in the oral conversation (conversation on a picture).","Listen to and read a story with understanding; discuss it in big and small groups and respond at their own level.","Develop sound-symbol skills: Language game: Find My Word.","Build vocabulary through a mind map ('sky') and use the words at their own level.","Read independently for 10 minutes every day."],"sequence":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Rain clapping","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Everyone stands in a circle with eyes closed and keeps clapping: first one finger, then two, three, four and finally five fingers. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Stand in a circle, close the eyes and clap with 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 fingers.","tlm":"After the activity ask: Where were you when you last heard real rain?","source":"M","ref":"p.8","n":1},{"activity":"Oral conversation: conversation on a picture","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Show a picture of a shop selling sweets and ask what is happening, who is doing what and what is happening around them. Let learners think creatively and even make up a story.","learners":"Look at the picture, answer questions and make up their own story about it.","tlm":"Picture card of a shop selling sweets","source":"M","ref":"p.9","n":2},{"activity":"Story (Day 1 of the story): reading aloud and discussion","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":8,"teacher":"Discuss the title or picture of the story with the learners. Read the story aloud with expression and voice modulation (learners do not repeat after you). Discuss it, with emphasis on factual questions. Read it again slowly, pointing to each word.","learners":"Talk about the title/picture; listen; answer questions; follow each word with a finger in their own copy.","tlm":"A story from the school library (a story about learning to read), a copy for each learner","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":3},{"activity":"Story: reading in small groups","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":7,"teacher":"Form level-wise groups with a group leader. Learners read the story one sentence at a time while the others follow with their fingers. Para and Story level learners practise reading with emotion and expression.","learners":"Read the story sentence by sentence, supporting each other; the group leader helps.","tlm":"Story book copies","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":4},{"activity":"Story: level-wise individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":5,"teacher":"Give each learner the task for their level (see level table) and support those who need it.","learners":"Beginner/Letter: find and write favourite words or letters. Word: find consonant clusters. Para/Story: silently read, find unfamiliar and rhyming words.","tlm":"Story book, notebooks, board","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":5},{"activity":"Language game: Find My Word","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Learners search their book pages for words beginning with a letter chosen by a classmate. Observe each learner and give help where needed.","learners":"Play the game, take turns and read or say the words they make.","tlm":"Textbooks or storybooks","source":"M","ref":"p.19","n":6},{"activity":"Mind mapping (Day 1): the word 'sky'","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Ask: 'What words come to your mind when you hear the word sky?' Write learners' answers on the board or floor (Para and Story level learners write the words themselves). Guide the map towards the learning objective. Example words: sun, cloud, bird, kite, moon, star, owl, bat, rain, thunder, rainbow, wind.","learners":"Say words connected with 'sky'; share the meaning and feeling of words.","tlm":"Board, chalk (or floor)","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":7},{"activity":"Mind mapping: classify the words","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":4,"teacher":"Ask learners to classify the words in groups, for example: Day: sun, cloud, bird, kite; Night: moon, star, owl, bat; Weather: rain, thunder, rainbow, wind.","learners":"Sort the words into groups and say why.","tlm":"Board, chalk, word cards (optional)","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":8},{"activity":"Mind mapping: level-wise individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":6,"teacher":"Give each learner the individual task for their level; observe closely and give individual support. Display corrected stories on the wall.","learners":"Complete the task for their level (see level table).","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":9},{"activity":"Daily reading (10 minutes)","grouping":"Individual","minutes":10,"teacher":"Give each learner a library book or any storybook. Move around, listen to individual readers and note their level.","learners":"Read independently a book of their choice.","tlm":"Library books or storybooks","source":"M","ref":"p.7","n":10}],"procedures":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Rain clapping","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","steps":[{"teacher":"Stand the learners in a circle and ask them to close their eyes. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Stand in a circle and close their eyes."},{"teacher":"Start clapping with one finger; then two fingers, three, four and finally five fingers.","learners":"Keep clapping, copying the change of fingers."},{"teacher":"After the activity ask: Where were you when you last heard real rain?","learners":"Tell how they felt and what the sounds reminded them of."}]},{"activity":"Oral conversation: conversation on a picture","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.9","steps":[{"teacher":"Show the picture of a shop selling sweets.","learners":"Look carefully."},{"teacher":"Ask: What is happening in the picture? Who is doing what? What is happening around them? Then: How do the people feel? How can you tell?","learners":"Answer in their own words; every learner gets a chance."},{"teacher":"Let learners imagine and make up a short story from the picture.","learners":"Tell their stories to the class."}]},{"activity":"Story - Day 1 (a story about learning to read)","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.10","steps":[{"teacher":"Discuss the title or picture of the story with the learners.","learners":"Talk about what they see and what the story may be about."},{"teacher":"Read the story aloud with expression and proper voice modulation. Learners should not simply repeat after you.","learners":"Listen carefully and enjoy the story."},{"teacher":"Discuss the story: factual, logical, vocabulary-based, judgment or opinion questions (today's focus: factual: Who was in the story? Where did it happen? What did the character do first?). Begin in the home language if needed.","learners":"Think and respond thoughtfully; every learner takes part."},{"teacher":"Read the story again slowly, pointing to each word. Make sure each learner has a copy and follows with a finger.","learners":"Follow each word with their finger."},{"teacher":"Ask learners to read in small groups; select a group leader who helps the others. Learners read one sentence at a time while the others point with fingers.","learners":"Read with the help of one another."}]},{"activity":"Language game: Find My Word","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.19","steps":[{"teacher":"Ask the learners to open any page of their books. Choose a learner to say a letter, for example 'b'.","learners":"Open a book page and listen for the letter."},{"teacher":"The others look through the page to find and say words that begin with that letter (book, ball, bat).","learners":"Find words and read them aloud."},{"teacher":"The learner who finds the most words wins the round. Another learner picks a new letter.","learners":"Choose a new letter and play again."}]},{"activity":"Mind mapping: 'sky'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Small group (level-wise) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.14","steps":[{"teacher":"Choose a word that can generate many related words: 'sky'. Ask: 'What words come to your mind when you hear the word sky?' Write the answers on the board or floor.","learners":"Say words they link with 'sky'."},{"teacher":"Discuss the words: what they mean and how they are connected.","learners":"Explain their words and listen to others."},{"teacher":"In small groups, let the learners classify the words (Day: sun, cloud, bird, kite; Night: moon, star, owl, bat; Weather: rain, thunder, rainbow, wind).","learners":"Sort the words into groups."},{"teacher":"Give the individual tasks by level and help each learner.","learners":"Work individually; read the work aloud at the end if time allows."}]}],"levelTasks":[{"activity":"Story - Day 1: individual tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.10","tasks":{"Beginner":"Circle or search for a favourite word or letter in the story and say it aloud. If a learner cannot draw a circle, write words on the board and ask them to identify them.","Letter":"Find, read and write favourite words from the story.","Word":"Find the consonant clusters in the story, read them and write them in the notebook.","Para":"Silently read the story from the textbook; find unfamiliar words and try to understand them; find rhyming words, use them in sentences and write in the notebook; ask other groups for meanings; make questions in groups.","Story":"Silently read the story; find unfamiliar words and rhyming words; practise reading with emotion; one group reads sentences formed with consonant clusters to the other group; ask and answer group questions (information, thinking and opinion questions)."}},{"activity":"Language game: Find My Word - level support","source":"I","ref":"p.19","tasks":{"Beginner":"Take part by saying or pointing to the letters involved and by listening carefully; Para and Story level partners help.","Letter":"Say the letters/sounds and give simple words they know.","Word":"Say and write words and short sentences for the game.","Para":"Write sentences with the words; help groups to record answers.","Story":"Write sentences or short stories with the words; help groups to record answers."}},{"activity":"Mind mapping 'sky': level tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.14","tasks":{"Beginner":"Circle all the words that contain the letter 'N' on the board; make a list. See how many learners find the most words.","Letter":"Circle all the words that contain the letter 'N' and make a list of them.","Word":"Use 4-5 words (for example bat, owl, sun, bird, kite) to form sentences, starting with words of one or two syllables. Example: Dream - I had a dream last night.","Para":"Choose any five words from the map and create a story with them. Use consonant clusters correctly, read the story aloud, correct mistakes of sentence structure, spelling or grammar, then display it on the wall.","Story":"Choose any five words from the map and create a story with them. Use consonant clusters correctly, read the story aloud, correct mistakes of sentence structure, spelling or grammar, then display it on the wall."}}],"organisation":[{"grouping":"Whole class (big group)","how":"All learners of all levels sit in a 'U' shape arranged by level (Beginner, Letter, Word, Para, Story) so that the move to small groups is easy.","activities":["Warm-up: Rain clapping","Oral conversation: conversation on a picture","Story (Day 1 of the story): reading aloud and discussion","Mind mapping (Day 1): the word 'sky'"]},{"grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","how":"Learners of similar levels work together; the teacher gives each group a task for its level and spends more time with learners who need support. Rotate responsibilities (for example group leader).","activities":["Story: reading in small groups","Language game: Find My Word","Mind mapping: classify the words"]},{"grouping":"Individual","how":"Each learner works on a task for their own level; the teacher moves around, observes difficulties and supports individuals.","activities":["Story: level-wise individual tasks","Mind mapping: level-wise individual tasks","Daily reading (10 minutes)"]}],"materials":["After the activity ask: Where were you when you last heard real rain?","Picture card of a shop selling sweets","A story from the school library (a story about learning to read)","a copy for each learner","Story book copies","Story book","notebooks","board","Textbooks or storybooks","Board","chalk (or floor)","chalk","word cards (optional)","Notebooks","Library books or storybooks"],"outcomes":["Learners take part in the oral conversation and speak without fear.","Learners show understanding of the story in the discussion and complete the task for their level.","Learners respond to the sound-symbol task for today (Language game: Find My Word) at their own level.","Learners add words to the mind map and use them in sentences or a story at their level.","Each learner reads a book for 10 minutes."],"observation":["Observe each learner's reading and writing during the individual tasks; note who needs individual support and how many learners share the same difficulty.","Note any learner whose level is improving; move the learner to the next level group when you see steady progress (manual p.5).","Record each learner's progress for the day in the notebook, according to the learner's level (manual p.4).","Use today's observations to adjust tomorrow's plan (manual p.5)."],"teacherNotes":["Story selection: the manual asks teachers to use picture story books or stories in the school library. Today's suggested theme (a story about learning to read) is a planning suggestion; use any suitable story you have.","The manual lists the letter and word games but does not fix the slot in the daily timetable where they are used. This plan places them in the 10-minute sound-symbol / alphabet slot (interpretation).","Mind mapping topic for this day: 'sky'. The manual's example uses the word 'shop'; today's topic follows the same method.","Level check: if learners have moved up to a new level, celebrate with an appreciation-oriented game (letter level to word level): 'Let us make words' or 'Say the word' (manual p.42-45). Teachers may use such activities on their own.","Pace: the manual says not to assume all learners progress at the same speed. Repeat a day's activity with the groups that need it before moving on.","Special needs: give extra time and prepare materials for slower learners; seat learners with hearing or vision difficulty at the front; for learners who reverse or confuse letters, trace letters on the letter card with a finger and write with dots to trace with a pencil (manual p.6)."],"components":[{"no":1,"key":"warmup","name":"Warm-up activities","keywords":["Rain clapping","two learners lead"],"rows":[1]},{"no":2,"key":"oral","name":"Oral Discussion","keywords":["conversation on a picture","every learner speaks"],"rows":[2]},{"no":3,"key":"story","name":"Story","keywords":["Day 1","title / picture talk","read aloud with expression","factual questions","re-read pointing","group reading","level tasks"],"rows":[3,4,5]},{"no":4,"key":"sound","name":"Sound symbol games, Sound separation-pairing","keywords":["Find My Word","play in turns","level support"],"rows":[6]},{"no":5,"key":"mindwrite","name":"Mind Mapping (Day 1)","keywords":["mind map: sky","classify the words","level task: circle letter N / sentences / story"],"rows":[7,8,9]},{"no":6,"key":"reading","name":"Daily reading","keywords":["library book","read alone","teacher listens"],"rows":[10]}],"preLesson":null},{"programme":"TARL Literacy","id":"lit-086","day":86,"phase":2,"phaseLabel":"Phase 2 (Days 46-90)","title":"Story: a story about learning to read (Day 2)","dayType":"Story Day 2 + Self-writing","focus":"Language game: Build the Sentence! | Self-writing: a picture of birds on a tree","duration":70,"objectives":["Listen, speak and answer in the oral conversation (listening and storytelling).","Retell the story, read it with expression, ask and answer questions about it and write answers.","Develop sound-symbol skills: Language game: Build the Sentence!.","Write about a topic at their own level and review the writing (a picture of birds on a tree).","Read independently for 10 minutes every day."],"sequence":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Writing with body parts","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Learners stand in a circle. Demonstrate writing the word 'milk' in the air with a finger, then ask them to write it with different body parts. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Write the word 'milk' in the air with the finger, then with the head, shoulders, knees or elbows.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.8","n":1},{"activity":"Oral conversation: listening and storytelling","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Tell an interesting story starter and involve the learners: 'One morning a tiny door appeared in the school wall. What was behind it?' Let learners imagine and continue the story.","learners":"Listen to the teacher, then imagine and continue the story. Learners can also recite a rhyme or story they know.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.9","n":2},{"activity":"Story (Day 2 of the story): retelling","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":6,"teacher":"Ask learners to retell yesterday's story in their own words. Prompt with questions on the beginning, middle and end.","learners":"Retell the story using their own words.","tlm":"The same story book as yesterday","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":3},{"activity":"Story: reading with actions and group questions","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":9,"teacher":"Learners practise reading with actions and expressions; one learner per group reads aloud to the class. Guide groups to make questions about the story (guide initially). Groups take turns to ask and answer each other's questions. Word-level learners also read aloud the consonants learned on the first day.","learners":"Read with actions; make questions (word-level learners help write them); ask and answer questions with another group.","tlm":"Story book, slate or paper for questions","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":4},{"activity":"Story: writing answers individually","grouping":"Individual","minutes":5,"teacher":"Para and Story level learners write answers to all questions individually; read and correct their responses after they finish.","learners":"Write the answers in their notebooks; Beginner/Letter/Word learners read or listen and answer orally.","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":5},{"activity":"Language game: Build the Sentence!","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"A simple sentence is made longer by each learner in turn: 'This is a boy' -> 'This is a good boy'. Observe each learner and give help where needed.","learners":"Play the game, take turns and read or say the words they make.","tlm":"Board, chalk","source":"M","ref":"p.21","n":6},{"activity":"Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on a picture of birds on a tree","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Start a conversation about a situation: 'a picture of birds on a tree'. Involve all learners and ask open-ended questions.","learners":"Take part in the discussion and share thoughts freely.","tlm":"Picture card or topic on the board","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":7},{"activity":"Self-writing: individual writing","grouping":"Individual","minutes":7,"teacher":"Give each level its task (see level table). Let learners take ownership of what they draw and write; mistakes are fine.","learners":"Draw and write about the topic at their level.","tlm":"Notebooks, crayons or pencils","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":8},{"activity":"Self-writing: review and reading back","grouping":"Individual","minutes":3,"teacher":"Ask each learner 'What did you draw or write?' and have them read it aloud once. Word-level learners read to the group; discuss spelling, punctuation and sentence structure. Help beginners by writing their text in the notebook for them if needed.","learners":"Read what they wrote; correct mistakes after listening to their own reading.","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":9},{"activity":"Daily reading (10 minutes)","grouping":"Individual","minutes":10,"teacher":"Give each learner a library book or any storybook. Move around, listen to individual readers and note their level.","learners":"Read independently a book of their choice.","tlm":"Library books or storybooks","source":"M","ref":"p.7","n":10}],"procedures":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Writing with body parts","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","steps":[{"teacher":"Stand the learners in a circle. Demonstrate writing the word 'milk' in the air with your finger.","learners":"Watch and then copy with their own finger."},{"teacher":"Ask them to write it again using head and other body parts (head, shoulders, knees, ...).","learners":"Write the letters in the air with the named body part."},{"teacher":"Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Take turns to lead."}]},{"activity":"Oral conversation: listening and storytelling","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.9","steps":[{"teacher":"Say the starter: 'One morning a tiny door appeared in the school wall. What was behind it?'","learners":"Listen and imagine."},{"teacher":"Ask learners to continue the story one by one. Encourage those who speak less.","learners":"Add ideas to the story."},{"teacher":"Invite a learner to recite a poem or rhyme they know.","learners":"Recite and listen to others."}]},{"activity":"Story - Day 2 (a story about learning to read)","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.11","steps":[{"teacher":"Ask learners to retell the story they read yesterday in their own words.","learners":"Retell, helping each other remember."},{"teacher":"In small groups learners practise reading the story using actions and expressions; one learner from each group then reads aloud to the class.","learners":"Read with actions and expression; a representative reads aloud."},{"teacher":"Guide the groups to come up with questions about the story (guide initially). Word-level learners can support by helping write them down.","learners":"Make questions together."},{"teacher":"Groups take turns to ask and answer each other's questions. Useful kinds: questions whose answer is not in the text; questions needing thinking beyond the text; questions asking for an opinion.","learners":"Ask, answer and discuss in the groups."},{"teacher":"Word-level learners also read aloud the consonants they learned on the first day.","learners":"Read the consonant clusters aloud."}]},{"activity":"Language game: Build the Sentence!","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.21","steps":[{"teacher":"Start with a simple sentence such as 'This is a boy.'","learners":"Listen to the sentence."},{"teacher":"The next learner makes it a little longer and better: 'This is a good boy.' Then another: 'This is a good boy and he is smiling.'","learners":"Add a few words to the sentence."},{"teacher":"Continue until the sentence cannot be made longer, then start again with a new sentence. The game can be adapted to write creative stories.","learners":"Say the longer sentence and, later, write it."}]},{"activity":"Self-writing: 'Discussion, Writing, Self-review'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.15","steps":[{"teacher":"Start a conversation about a situation: 'a picture of birds on a tree'. Involve all learners and ask open-ended questions.","learners":"Discuss and answer questions."},{"teacher":"Give writing time at each level: draw then write (Beginner), write about what they liked (Letter), a sentence (Word), a paragraph or story on a topic of their choice (Para/Story).","learners":"Write at their level and take ownership of the work."},{"teacher":"Review: ask 'What did you draw or write?' Have each learner read the text aloud once. Support with writing if needed.","learners":"Read aloud, listen to their pronunciation and correct mistakes."}]}],"levelTasks":[{"activity":"Story - Day 2: level-wise tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.11","tasks":{"Beginner":"Retell with the group by pointing to pictures or words; read aloud with group support (interpretation of the manual's group reading task).","Letter":"Read with the group, pointing to words; say the letters and words they know (interpretation of the manual's group reading task).","Word":"Support the group in writing the questions; read aloud the consonant clusters learned on the first day.","Para":"Ask the group's questions to another group, discuss them, then write answers to all questions individually; the teacher reads and corrects.","Story":"Ask the group's questions to another group, discuss them, then write answers to all questions individually; the teacher reads and corrects."}},{"activity":"Language game: Build the Sentence! - level support","source":"I","ref":"p.21","tasks":{"Beginner":"Take part by saying or pointing to the letters involved and by listening carefully; Para and Story level partners help.","Letter":"Say the letters/sounds and give simple words they know.","Word":"Say and write words and short sentences for the game.","Para":"Write sentences with the words; help groups to record answers.","Story":"Write sentences or short stories with the words; help groups to record answers."}},{"activity":"Self-writing: level tasks and review","source":"M","ref":"p.15","tasks":{"Beginner":"Draw a picture about the discussion and then write a few sentences about it, expressing thoughts freely. Review: say what they drew or wrote; read the text aloud once; the teacher may write the text in the notebook for them.","Letter":"Write about what they liked, using drawing and writing; write any words or sentences they can. Review: read the text aloud once; correct punctuation mistakes using the Barakhadi chart.","Word":"Write a sentence based on the conversation. Mistakes in spelling, punctuation and sentence structure are fine. Review: read it to the group; discuss and correct mistakes together.","Para":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation.","Story":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation."}}],"organisation":[{"grouping":"Whole class (big group)","how":"All learners of all levels sit in a 'U' shape arranged by level (Beginner, Letter, Word, Para, Story) so that the move to small groups is easy.","activities":["Warm-up: Writing with body parts","Oral conversation: listening and storytelling","Story (Day 2 of the story): retelling","Language game: Build the Sentence!","Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on a picture of birds on a tree"]},{"grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","how":"Learners of similar levels work together; the teacher gives each group a task for its level and spends more time with learners who need support. Rotate responsibilities (for example group leader).","activities":["Story: reading with actions and group questions"]},{"grouping":"Individual","how":"Each learner works on a task for their own level; the teacher moves around, observes difficulties and supports individuals.","activities":["Story: writing answers individually","Self-writing: individual writing","Self-writing: review and reading back","Daily reading (10 minutes)"]}],"materials":["The same story book as yesterday","Story book","slate or paper for questions","Notebooks","Board","chalk","Picture card or topic on the board","crayons or pencils","Library books or storybooks"],"outcomes":["Learners take part in the oral conversation and speak without fear.","Learners retell the story, read with expression and ask or answer questions at their level.","Learners respond to the sound-symbol task for today (Language game: Build the Sentence!) at their own level.","Learners write about the topic at their level and read it aloud.","Each learner reads a book for 10 minutes."],"observation":["Observe each learner's reading and writing during the individual tasks; note who needs individual support and how many learners share the same difficulty.","Note any learner whose level is improving; move the learner to the next level group when you see steady progress (manual p.5).","Record each learner's progress for the day in the notebook, according to the learner's level (manual p.4).","Use today's observations to adjust tomorrow's plan (manual p.5)."],"teacherNotes":["Questions to elicit on Day 2: information questions (answer not in the text), thinking questions (needs knowledge beyond the text) and opinion questions (feedback on something in the text).","The manual lists the letter and word games but does not fix the slot in the daily timetable where they are used. This plan places them in the 10-minute sound-symbol / alphabet slot (interpretation).","Writing has two parts, content and sequence: encourage learners to read what they wrote, improve it and rewrite it for clarity and correctness (manual p.15).","Pace: the manual says not to assume all learners progress at the same speed. Repeat a day's activity with the groups that need it before moving on.","Special needs: give extra time and prepare materials for slower learners; seat learners with hearing or vision difficulty at the front; for learners who reverse or confuse letters, trace letters on the letter card with a finger and write with dots to trace with a pencil (manual p.6)."],"components":[{"no":1,"key":"warmup","name":"Warm-up activities","keywords":["Writing with body parts","two learners lead"],"rows":[1]},{"no":2,"key":"oral","name":"Oral Discussion","keywords":["listening and storytelling","every learner speaks"],"rows":[2]},{"no":3,"key":"story","name":"Story","keywords":["Day 2","retell","read with actions","group questions","ask and answer","write answers (Para/Story)"],"rows":[3,4,5]},{"no":4,"key":"sound","name":"Sound symbol games, Sound separation-pairing","keywords":["Build the Sentence!","play in turns","level support"],"rows":[6]},{"no":5,"key":"mindwrite","name":"Individual-Writing (Day 2)","keywords":["discussion","write at own level","self-review (read aloud)"],"rows":[7,8,9]},{"no":6,"key":"reading","name":"Daily reading","keywords":["library book","read alone","teacher listens"],"rows":[10]}],"preLesson":null},{"programme":"TARL Literacy","id":"lit-087","day":87,"phase":2,"phaseLabel":"Phase 2 (Days 46-90)","title":"Story: a story about a promise kept (Day 1)","dayType":"Story Day 1 + Mind mapping","focus":"Consonant clusters: pp (apple, happy) | Mind map: water","duration":70,"objectives":["Listen, speak and answer in the oral conversation (What did you see on your way?).","Listen to and read a story with understanding; discuss it in big and small groups and respond at their own level.","Develop sound-symbol skills: Consonant clusters: pp (apple, happy).","Build vocabulary through a mind map ('water') and use the words at their own level.","Read independently for 10 minutes every day."],"sequence":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Alphabet song (last-letter word chain)","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Say a word to the big group, for example 'earth'. Learners say a word that starts with the last letter ('h'). A learner who cannot say a word is out. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Say a word that starts with the last letter of the previous word; step out if unable to.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.8","n":1},{"activity":"Oral conversation: What did you see on your way?","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Ask learners to describe what they saw on their way to school. If they are hesitant, begin yourself: 'I saw the river shining, a boat leaving the bank and two birds on a bamboo pole. What did you see on your way?'","learners":"Describe what they saw on the way to school and connect with what others share.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.9","n":2},{"activity":"Story (Day 1 of the story): reading aloud and discussion","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":8,"teacher":"Discuss the title or picture of the story with the learners. Read the story aloud with expression and voice modulation (learners do not repeat after you). Discuss it, with emphasis on logical questions. Read it again slowly, pointing to each word.","learners":"Talk about the title/picture; listen; answer questions; follow each word with a finger in their own copy.","tlm":"A story from the school library (a story about a promise kept), a copy for each learner","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":3},{"activity":"Story: reading in small groups","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":7,"teacher":"Form level-wise groups with a group leader. Learners read the story one sentence at a time while the others follow with their fingers. Para and Story level learners practise reading with emotion and expression.","learners":"Read the story sentence by sentence, supporting each other; the group leader helps.","tlm":"Story book copies","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":4},{"activity":"Story: level-wise individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":5,"teacher":"Give each learner the task for their level (see level table) and support those who need it.","learners":"Beginner/Letter: find and write favourite words or letters. Word: find consonant clusters. Para/Story: silently read, find unfamiliar and rhyming words.","tlm":"Story book, notebooks, board","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":5},{"activity":"Consonant clusters: introduction","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":4,"teacher":"Same-letter clusters: familiarise learners with clusters made of the same letter ('pp' as in apple, happy, puppy). Ask them to pronounce them and find such words in the text and write them down.","learners":"Listen, pronounce the cluster and say words that contain it.","tlm":"Board and chalk, words list (apple happy puppy supper hopping)","source":"M","ref":"p.16","n":6},{"activity":"Consonant cluster game: Looking for Similar Ones","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":6,"teacher":"Write some words with the same conjunct consonants on the board, for example bl, tr, st. Observe closely and help learners who need support.","learners":"Match words that have the same conjunct consonant (black, blue, blanket, blow, blink).","tlm":"Words on the board","source":"M","ref":"p.17","n":7},{"activity":"Mind mapping (Day 1): the word 'water'","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Ask: 'What words come to your mind when you hear the word water?' Write learners' answers on the board or floor (Para and Story level learners write the words themselves). Guide the map towards the learning objective. Example words: drink, wash, cook, farm, river, well, pond, tap, bucket, pot, pump, glass.","learners":"Say words connected with 'water'; share the meaning and feeling of words.","tlm":"Board, chalk (or floor)","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":8},{"activity":"Mind mapping: classify the words","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":4,"teacher":"Ask learners to classify the words in groups, for example: Uses: drink, wash, cook, farm; Places: river, well, pond, tap; Things: bucket, pot, pump, glass.","learners":"Sort the words into groups and say why.","tlm":"Board, chalk, word cards (optional)","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":9},{"activity":"Mind mapping: level-wise individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":6,"teacher":"Give each learner the individual task for their level; observe closely and give individual support. Display corrected stories on the wall.","learners":"Complete the task for their level (see level table).","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":10},{"activity":"Daily reading (10 minutes)","grouping":"Individual","minutes":10,"teacher":"Give each learner a library book or any storybook. Move around, listen to individual readers and note their level.","learners":"Read independently a book of their choice.","tlm":"Library books or storybooks","source":"M","ref":"p.7","n":11}],"procedures":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Alphabet song (last-letter word chain)","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","steps":[{"teacher":"Say the word 'earth' to the big group and show that its last letter is 'h'.","learners":"Listen and think of a word starting with 'h'."},{"teacher":"Ask learners in turn to say a word that starts with the last letter of the previous word. Example: rain -> nest.","learners":"Say a word in turn; anyone who cannot say a word is out of the game."},{"teacher":"Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Lead the game when it is their turn."}]},{"activity":"Oral conversation: What did you see on your way?","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.9","steps":[{"teacher":"Ask: 'What did you see on your way to school today?'","learners":"Think about the way to school."},{"teacher":"If learners hesitate, start: 'I saw the river shining, a boat leaving the bank and two birds on a bamboo pole. What did you see on your way?'","learners":"Listen to the model and then share their own observations."},{"teacher":"Connect learners' answers with each other.","learners":"Listen and add what they noticed."}]},{"activity":"Story - Day 1 (a story about a promise kept)","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.10","steps":[{"teacher":"Discuss the title or picture of the story with the learners.","learners":"Talk about what they see and what the story may be about."},{"teacher":"Read the story aloud with expression and proper voice modulation. Learners should not simply repeat after you.","learners":"Listen carefully and enjoy the story."},{"teacher":"Discuss the story: factual, logical, vocabulary-based, judgment or opinion questions (today's focus: logical: Why did the character do that? What would have happened if ...?). Begin in the home language if needed.","learners":"Think and respond thoughtfully; every learner takes part."},{"teacher":"Read the story again slowly, pointing to each word. Make sure each learner has a copy and follows with a finger.","learners":"Follow each word with their finger."},{"teacher":"Ask learners to read in small groups; select a group leader who helps the others. Learners read one sentence at a time while the others point with fingers.","learners":"Read with the help of one another."}]},{"activity":"Consonant clusters (pp) and the game 'Looking for Similar Ones'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.16-17","steps":[{"teacher":"Same-letter clusters: familiarise learners with clusters made of the same letter ('pp' as in apple, happy, puppy). Ask them to pronounce them and find such words in the text and write them down.","learners":"Listen, pronounce and find words in the text."},{"teacher":"Write the words on the board: apple happy puppy supper hopping. Read them aloud with distinct pronunciation of the cluster.","learners":"Read the words aloud; point to the cluster in each word."},{"teacher":"Write some words with the same conjunct consonants on the board, for example bl, tr, st.","learners":"Match words that have the same conjunct consonant (black, blue, blanket, blow, blink)."}]},{"activity":"Mind mapping: 'water'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Small group (level-wise) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.14","steps":[{"teacher":"Choose a word that can generate many related words: 'water'. Ask: 'What words come to your mind when you hear the word water?' Write the answers on the board or floor.","learners":"Say words they link with 'water'."},{"teacher":"Discuss the words: what they mean and how they are connected.","learners":"Explain their words and listen to others."},{"teacher":"In small groups, let the learners classify the words (Uses: drink, wash, cook, farm; Places: river, well, pond, tap; Things: bucket, pot, pump, glass).","learners":"Sort the words into groups."},{"teacher":"Give the individual tasks by level and help each learner.","learners":"Work individually; read the work aloud at the end if time allows."}]}],"levelTasks":[{"activity":"Story - Day 1: individual tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.10","tasks":{"Beginner":"Circle or search for a favourite word or letter in the story and say it aloud. If a learner cannot draw a circle, write words on the board and ask them to identify them.","Letter":"Find, read and write favourite words from the story.","Word":"Find the consonant clusters in the story, read them and write them in the notebook.","Para":"Silently read the story from the textbook; find unfamiliar words and try to understand them; find rhyming words, use them in sentences and write in the notebook; ask other groups for meanings; make questions in groups.","Story":"Silently read the story; find unfamiliar words and rhyming words; practise reading with emotion; one group reads sentences formed with consonant clusters to the other group; ask and answer group questions (information, thinking and opinion questions)."}},{"activity":"Consonant clusters (pp): level tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.16-17","tasks":{"Beginner":"Listen to the sound of the cluster and point to it in a word; continue with letter-sound work (interpretation: the manual describes clusters for learners lagging in reading words and sentences).","Letter":"Listen to the cluster sound and pick words with the cluster from a word card (interpretation).","Word":"Find the cluster in the story or textbook words, read the words and write them in the notebook.","Para":"Form words and sentences using the cluster; read the sentences aloud.","Story":"Form words and sentences using the cluster; read the sentences aloud; use them in the story writing."}},{"activity":"Mind mapping 'water': level tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.14","tasks":{"Beginner":"Circle all the words that contain the letter 'A' on the board; make a list. See how many learners find the most words.","Letter":"Circle all the words that contain the letter 'A' and make a list of them.","Word":"Use 4-5 words (for example pot, tap, cook, farm, pond) to form sentences, starting with words of one or two syllables. Example: Dream - I had a dream last night.","Para":"Choose any five words from the map and create a story with them. Use consonant clusters correctly, read the story aloud, correct mistakes of sentence structure, spelling or grammar, then display it on the wall.","Story":"Choose any five words from the map and create a story with them. Use consonant clusters correctly, read the story aloud, correct mistakes of sentence structure, spelling or grammar, then display it on the wall."}}],"organisation":[{"grouping":"Whole class (big group)","how":"All learners of all levels sit in a 'U' shape arranged by level (Beginner, Letter, Word, Para, Story) so that the move to small groups is easy.","activities":["Warm-up: Alphabet song (last-letter word chain)","Oral conversation: What did you see on your way?","Story (Day 1 of the story): reading aloud and discussion","Consonant clusters: introduction","Mind mapping (Day 1): the word 'water'"]},{"grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","how":"Learners of similar levels work together; the teacher gives each group a task for its level and spends more time with learners who need support. Rotate responsibilities (for example group leader).","activities":["Story: reading in small groups","Consonant cluster game: Looking for Similar Ones","Mind mapping: classify the words"]},{"grouping":"Individual","how":"Each learner works on a task for their own level; the teacher moves around, observes difficulties and supports individuals.","activities":["Story: level-wise individual tasks","Mind mapping: level-wise individual tasks","Daily reading (10 minutes)"]}],"materials":["A story from the school library (a story about a promise kept)","a copy for each learner","Story book copies","Story book","notebooks","board","Board","chalk","words list (apple happy puppy supper hopping)","Words on the board","chalk (or floor)","word cards (optional)","Notebooks","Library books or storybooks"],"outcomes":["Learners take part in the oral conversation and speak without fear.","Learners show understanding of the story in the discussion and complete the task for their level.","Learners respond to the sound-symbol task for today (Consonant clusters: pp (apple, happy)) at their own level.","Learners add words to the mind map and use them in sentences or a story at their level.","Each learner reads a book for 10 minutes."],"observation":["Observe each learner's reading and writing during the individual tasks; note who needs individual support and how many learners share the same difficulty.","Note any learner whose level is improving; move the learner to the next level group when you see steady progress (manual p.5).","Record each learner's progress for the day in the notebook, according to the learner's level (manual p.4).","Use today's observations to adjust tomorrow's plan (manual p.5)."],"teacherNotes":["Story selection: the manual asks teachers to use picture story books or stories in the school library. Today's suggested theme (a story about a promise kept) is a planning suggestion; use any suitable story you have.","Consonant clusters: do these activities daily for learners who find reading complex words hard; the aim is to remove the fear of reading clusters. Teachers may carry out similar activities on their own.","Mind mapping topic for this day: 'water'. The manual's example uses the word 'shop'; today's topic follows the same method.","Pace: the manual says not to assume all learners progress at the same speed. Repeat a day's activity with the groups that need it before moving on.","Special needs: give extra time and prepare materials for slower learners; seat learners with hearing or vision difficulty at the front; for learners who reverse or confuse letters, trace letters on the letter card with a finger and write with dots to trace with a pencil (manual p.6)."],"components":[{"no":1,"key":"warmup","name":"Warm-up activities","keywords":["Alphabet song (last-letter word chain)","two learners lead"],"rows":[1]},{"no":2,"key":"oral","name":"Oral Discussion","keywords":["What did you see on your way?","every learner speaks"],"rows":[2]},{"no":3,"key":"story","name":"Story","keywords":["Day 1","title / picture talk","read aloud with expression","logical questions","re-read pointing","group reading","level tasks"],"rows":[3,4,5]},{"no":4,"key":"sound","name":"Sound symbol games, Sound separation-pairing","keywords":["consonant cluster 'pp'","pronounce and find words","game: Looking for Similar Ones"],"rows":[6,7]},{"no":5,"key":"mindwrite","name":"Mind Mapping (Day 1)","keywords":["mind map: water","classify the words","level task: circle letter A / sentences / story"],"rows":[8,9,10]},{"no":6,"key":"reading","name":"Daily reading","keywords":["library book","read alone","teacher listens"],"rows":[11]}],"preLesson":null},{"programme":"TARL Literacy","id":"lit-088","day":88,"phase":2,"phaseLabel":"Phase 2 (Days 46-90)","title":"Story: a story about a promise kept (Day 2)","dayType":"Story Day 2 + Self-writing","focus":"Identifying the first, second and last sound (pan, log, cup) | Self-writing: what I will do tomorrow","duration":70,"objectives":["Listen, speak and answer in the oral conversation (familiar topic).","Retell the story, read it with expression, ask and answer questions about it and write answers.","Develop sound-symbol skills: Identifying the first, second and last sound (pan, log, cup).","Write about a topic at their own level and review the writing (what I will do tomorrow).","Read independently for 10 minutes every day."],"sequence":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Handkerchief game","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Learners sit in a circle and clap while singing a rhyme ('I saw a Little Bird'). One learner runs outside the circle with a handkerchief and secretly places it behind another learner, who must chase the runner. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Sit in a circle, clap and sing; run, place the handkerchief or chase as the game requires.","tlm":"A handkerchief","source":"M","ref":"p.8","n":1},{"activity":"Oral conversation: familiar topic","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Hold a conversation on the topic 'my best friend and what we play'. Give each learner a chance to speak; be patient with learners who need extra time.","learners":"Talk about the topic and listen to others.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.9","n":2},{"activity":"Story (Day 2 of the story): retelling","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":6,"teacher":"Ask learners to retell yesterday's story in their own words. Prompt with questions on the beginning, middle and end.","learners":"Retell the story using their own words.","tlm":"The same story book as yesterday","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":3},{"activity":"Story: reading with actions and group questions","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":9,"teacher":"Learners practise reading with actions and expressions; one learner per group reads aloud to the class. Guide groups to make questions about the story (guide initially). Groups take turns to ask and answer each other's questions. Word-level learners also read aloud the consonants learned on the first day.","learners":"Read with actions; make questions (word-level learners help write them); ask and answer questions with another group.","tlm":"Story book, slate or paper for questions","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":4},{"activity":"Story: writing answers individually","grouping":"Individual","minutes":5,"teacher":"Para and Story level learners write answers to all questions individually; read and correct their responses after they finish.","learners":"Write the answers in their notebooks; Beginner/Letter/Word learners read or listen and answer orally.","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":5},{"activity":"Sound-symbol activity: oral sound awareness","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":4,"teacher":"Say words and ask learners to identify the first, second or last sound. Example: pan - first sound p, second sound a, third sound n; log: l, o, g; cup: c, u, p.","learners":"Say the first, second or last sound of the word.","tlm":"None (oral activity)","source":"M","ref":"p.12","n":6},{"activity":"Sound-symbol games by level","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":6,"teacher":"Give each level group its game (see level table). Move among the groups and help those who need support; say each word clearly.","learners":"Play the game for their level in small groups.","tlm":"Board, chalk, letter cards","source":"M","ref":"p.12","n":7},{"activity":"Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on what I will do tomorrow","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Start a conversation about a picture card: 'what I will do tomorrow'. Involve all learners and ask open-ended questions.","learners":"Take part in the discussion and share thoughts freely.","tlm":"Picture card or topic on the board","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":8},{"activity":"Self-writing: individual writing","grouping":"Individual","minutes":7,"teacher":"Give each level its task (see level table). Let learners take ownership of what they draw and write; mistakes are fine.","learners":"Draw and write about the topic at their level.","tlm":"Notebooks, crayons or pencils","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":9},{"activity":"Self-writing: review and reading back","grouping":"Individual","minutes":3,"teacher":"Ask each learner 'What did you draw or write?' and have them read it aloud once. Word-level learners read to the group; discuss spelling, punctuation and sentence structure. Help beginners by writing their text in the notebook for them if needed.","learners":"Read what they wrote; correct mistakes after listening to their own reading.","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":10},{"activity":"Daily reading (10 minutes)","grouping":"Individual","minutes":10,"teacher":"Give each learner a library book or any storybook. Move around, listen to individual readers and note their level.","learners":"Read independently a book of their choice.","tlm":"Library books or storybooks","source":"M","ref":"p.7","n":11}],"procedures":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Handkerchief game","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","steps":[{"teacher":"Seat the learners in a circle and start clapping and singing the rhyme 'I saw a Little Bird'.","learners":"Clap and sing together."},{"teacher":"One learner runs outside the circle holding a handkerchief and secretly places it behind another learner.","learners":"Everyone keeps clapping; the learner who finds the handkerchief behind them takes it and chases the runner."},{"teacher":"If the runner sits in the chaser's place before being caught, they stay in the game; if caught, they are out. Continue in this way.","learners":"Play fairly and take turns."}]},{"activity":"Oral conversation: familiar topic","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.9","steps":[{"teacher":"Introduce the topic: 'my best friend and what we play'.","learners":"Think about their own experience."},{"teacher":"Ask open questions; give every learner a chance. Involve learners who speak less.","learners":"Speak freely and without fear."},{"teacher":"Praise efforts and sum up.","learners":"Listen and respect each other's ideas."}]},{"activity":"Story - Day 2 (a story about a promise kept)","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.11","steps":[{"teacher":"Ask learners to retell the story they read yesterday in their own words.","learners":"Retell, helping each other remember."},{"teacher":"In small groups learners practise reading the story using actions and expressions; one learner from each group then reads aloud to the class.","learners":"Read with actions and expression; a representative reads aloud."},{"teacher":"Guide the groups to come up with questions about the story (guide initially). Word-level learners can support by helping write them down.","learners":"Make questions together."},{"teacher":"Groups take turns to ask and answer each other's questions. Useful kinds: questions whose answer is not in the text; questions needing thinking beyond the text; questions asking for an opinion.","learners":"Ask, answer and discuss in the groups."},{"teacher":"Word-level learners also read aloud the consonants they learned on the first day.","learners":"Read the consonant clusters aloud."}]},{"activity":"Sound-symbol: oral and level games","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.12","steps":[{"teacher":"Say words and ask learners to identify the first, second or last sound. Example: pan - first sound p, second sound a, third sound n; log: l, o, g; cup: c, u, p.","learners":"Say the first, second or last sound of the word."},{"teacher":"Write the sounds or words for the day on the board and give each level group its task (see the level table).","learners":"Work in small groups and share their answers."},{"teacher":"Say each word clearly with distinct pronunciation. Give learners enough time to respond and think; use words learners commonly use at home (regional language and the medium of instruction).","learners":"Think, say and write the sounds."}]},{"activity":"Self-writing: 'Discussion, Writing, Self-review'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.15","steps":[{"teacher":"Start a conversation about a picture card: 'what I will do tomorrow'. Involve all learners and ask open-ended questions.","learners":"Discuss and answer questions."},{"teacher":"Give writing time at each level: draw then write (Beginner), write about what they liked (Letter), a sentence (Word), a paragraph or story on a topic of their choice (Para/Story).","learners":"Write at their level and take ownership of the work."},{"teacher":"Review: ask 'What did you draw or write?' Have each learner read the text aloud once. Support with writing if needed.","learners":"Read aloud, listen to their pronunciation and correct mistakes."}]}],"levelTasks":[{"activity":"Story - Day 2: level-wise tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.11","tasks":{"Beginner":"Retell with the group by pointing to pictures or words; read aloud with group support (interpretation of the manual's group reading task).","Letter":"Read with the group, pointing to words; say the letters and words they know (interpretation of the manual's group reading task).","Word":"Support the group in writing the questions; read aloud the consonant clusters learned on the first day.","Para":"Ask the group's questions to another group, discuss them, then write answers to all questions individually; the teacher reads and corrects.","Story":"Ask the group's questions to another group, discuss them, then write answers to all questions individually; the teacher reads and corrects."}},{"activity":"Sound-symbol games by level (small groups)","source":"M","ref":"p.12","tasks":{"Beginner":"'What is the first sound in the word orange?' 'Is there a letter that makes the sound /o/?' 'Can you name objects that start with the letter O?' Learners think and share names in the group.","Letter":"Write the rhyming ending -ip on the board and ask learners to add new letters to form words: s + ip = sip, h + ip = hip, l + ip = lip.","Word":"Say a word and tell its sounds, for example 'sun' = /s/ + /u/ + /n/. Then tell what word is formed if /r/ is put before 'at': r + at = rat. Do 8-10 such combinations; at first learners may form meaningless words, later only meaningful words.","Para":"Write two or three sounds on the board (for example Br, cl, st) and let the learners form words that start with those sounds; this builds a word list for the learner.","Story":"Write two or three sounds on the board (for example Br, cl, st) and let the learners form words that start with those sounds; this builds a word list for the learner."}},{"activity":"Self-writing: level tasks and review","source":"M","ref":"p.15","tasks":{"Beginner":"Draw a picture about the discussion and then write a few sentences about it, expressing thoughts freely. Review: say what they drew or wrote; read the text aloud once; the teacher may write the text in the notebook for them.","Letter":"Write about what they liked, using drawing and writing; write any words or sentences they can. Review: read the text aloud once; correct punctuation mistakes using the Barakhadi chart.","Word":"Write a sentence based on the conversation. Mistakes in spelling, punctuation and sentence structure are fine. Review: read it to the group; discuss and correct mistakes together.","Para":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation.","Story":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation."}}],"organisation":[{"grouping":"Whole class (big group)","how":"All learners of all levels sit in a 'U' shape arranged by level (Beginner, Letter, Word, Para, Story) so that the move to small groups is easy.","activities":["Warm-up: Handkerchief game","Oral conversation: familiar topic","Story (Day 2 of the story): retelling","Sound-symbol activity: oral sound awareness","Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on what I will do tomorrow"]},{"grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","how":"Learners of similar levels work together; the teacher gives each group a task for its level and spends more time with learners who need support. Rotate responsibilities (for example group leader).","activities":["Story: reading with actions and group questions","Sound-symbol games by level"]},{"grouping":"Individual","how":"Each learner works on a task for their own level; the teacher moves around, observes difficulties and supports individuals.","activities":["Story: writing answers individually","Self-writing: individual writing","Self-writing: review and reading back","Daily reading (10 minutes)"]}],"materials":["A handkerchief","The same story book as yesterday","Story book","slate or paper for questions","Notebooks","Board","chalk","letter cards","Picture card or topic on the board","crayons or pencils","Library books or storybooks"],"outcomes":["Learners take part in the oral conversation and speak without fear.","Learners retell the story, read with expression and ask or answer questions at their level.","Learners respond to the sound-symbol task for today (Identifying the first, second and last sound (pan, log, cup)) at their own level.","Learners write about the topic at their level and read it aloud.","Each learner reads a book for 10 minutes."],"observation":["Observe each learner's reading and writing during the individual tasks; note who needs individual support and how many learners share the same difficulty.","Note any learner whose level is improving; move the learner to the next level group when you see steady progress (manual p.5).","Record each learner's progress for the day in the notebook, according to the learner's level (manual p.4).","Use today's observations to adjust tomorrow's plan (manual p.5)."],"teacherNotes":["Questions to elicit on Day 2: information questions (answer not in the text), thinking questions (needs knowledge beyond the text) and opinion questions (feedback on something in the text).","Sound-symbol: for the first 4-5 days, play sound-based games with the learners at word level. Include the sounds learners find difficult when you prepare the Class Transaction Plan.","Writing has two parts, content and sequence: encourage learners to read what they wrote, improve it and rewrite it for clarity and correctness (manual p.15).","Pace: the manual says not to assume all learners progress at the same speed. Repeat a day's activity with the groups that need it before moving on.","Special needs: give extra time and prepare materials for slower learners; seat learners with hearing or vision difficulty at the front; for learners who reverse or confuse letters, trace letters on the letter card with a finger and write with dots to trace with a pencil (manual p.6)."],"components":[{"no":1,"key":"warmup","name":"Warm-up activities","keywords":["Handkerchief game","two learners lead"],"rows":[1]},{"no":2,"key":"oral","name":"Oral Discussion","keywords":["familiar topic","every learner speaks"],"rows":[2]},{"no":3,"key":"story","name":"Story","keywords":["Day 2","retell","read with actions","group questions","ask and answer","write answers (Para/Story)"],"rows":[3,4,5]},{"no":4,"key":"sound","name":"Sound symbol games, Sound separation-pairing","keywords":["oral sound awareness","first / second / last sound","level games in small groups"],"rows":[6,7]},{"no":5,"key":"mindwrite","name":"Individual-Writing (Day 2)","keywords":["discussion","write at own level","self-review (read aloud)"],"rows":[8,9,10]},{"no":6,"key":"reading","name":"Daily reading","keywords":["library book","read alone","teacher listens"],"rows":[11]}],"preLesson":null},{"programme":"TARL Literacy","id":"lit-089","day":89,"phase":2,"phaseLabel":"Phase 2 (Days 46-90)","title":"Story: a story about a happy ending after a problem (Day 1)","dayType":"Story Day 1 + Mind mapping","focus":"Language game: The Story Continued Slowly | Mind map: sweets","duration":70,"objectives":["Listen, speak and answer in the oral conversation (conversation on a picture).","Listen to and read a story with understanding; discuss it in big and small groups and respond at their own level.","Develop sound-symbol skills: Language game: The Story Continued Slowly.","Build vocabulary through a mind map ('sweets') and use the words at their own level.","Read independently for 10 minutes every day."],"sequence":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Rhyme - 'I caught a Fish Alive'","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Say the rhyme with actions, then say it together. Lines: One, two, three, four, five, once I caught a fish alive. / Six, seven, eight, nine, ten, then I let it go again. / Why did you let it go? Because it bit my finger so. / Which finger did it bite? This little finger on my right. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Listen, then say the rhyme with actions.","tlm":"Rhyme chart or board (optional)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","n":1},{"activity":"Oral conversation: conversation on a picture","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Show a picture of a cricket match in the field and ask what is happening, who is doing what and what is happening around them. Let learners think creatively and even make up a story.","learners":"Look at the picture, answer questions and make up their own story about it.","tlm":"Picture card of a cricket match in the field","source":"M","ref":"p.9","n":2},{"activity":"Story (Day 1 of the story): reading aloud and discussion","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":8,"teacher":"Discuss the title or picture of the story with the learners. Read the story aloud with expression and voice modulation (learners do not repeat after you). Discuss it, with emphasis on vocabulary-based questions. Read it again slowly, pointing to each word.","learners":"Talk about the title/picture; listen; answer questions; follow each word with a finger in their own copy.","tlm":"A story from the school library (a story about a happy ending after a problem), a copy for each learner","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":3},{"activity":"Story: reading in small groups","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":7,"teacher":"Form level-wise groups with a group leader. Learners read the story one sentence at a time while the others follow with their fingers. Para and Story level learners practise reading with emotion and expression.","learners":"Read the story sentence by sentence, supporting each other; the group leader helps.","tlm":"Story book copies","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":4},{"activity":"Story: level-wise individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":5,"teacher":"Give each learner the task for their level (see level table) and support those who need it.","learners":"Beginner/Letter: find and write favourite words or letters. Word: find consonant clusters. Para/Story: silently read, find unfamiliar and rhyming words.","tlm":"Story book, notebooks, board","source":"M","ref":"p.10","n":5},{"activity":"Language game: The Story Continued Slowly","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Learners add one sentence each to a story, first orally, then in writing; some draw a picture and think of a title. Observe each learner and give help where needed.","learners":"Play the game, take turns and read or say the words they make.","tlm":"Board, notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.21","n":6},{"activity":"Mind mapping (Day 1): the word 'sweets'","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Ask: 'What words come to your mind when you hear the word sweets?' Write learners' answers on the board or floor (Para and Story level learners write the words themselves). Guide the map towards the learning objective. Example words: laddu, jalebi, rasgulla, pitha, milk, sugar, rice, jaggery, festival, wedding, birthday, guests.","learners":"Say words connected with 'sweets'; share the meaning and feeling of words.","tlm":"Board, chalk (or floor)","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":7},{"activity":"Mind mapping: classify the words","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":4,"teacher":"Ask learners to classify the words in groups, for example: Kinds: laddu, jalebi, rasgulla, pitha; Made from: milk, sugar, rice, jaggery; When we eat: festival, wedding, birthday, guests.","learners":"Sort the words into groups and say why.","tlm":"Board, chalk, word cards (optional)","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":8},{"activity":"Mind mapping: level-wise individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":6,"teacher":"Give each learner the individual task for their level; observe closely and give individual support. Display corrected stories on the wall.","learners":"Complete the task for their level (see level table).","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.14","n":9},{"activity":"Daily reading (10 minutes)","grouping":"Individual","minutes":10,"teacher":"Give each learner a library book or any storybook. Move around, listen to individual readers and note their level.","learners":"Read independently a book of their choice.","tlm":"Library books or storybooks","source":"M","ref":"p.7","n":10}],"procedures":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Rhyme - 'I caught a Fish Alive'","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","steps":[{"teacher":"Say the rhyme 'I caught a Fish Alive' slowly with actions: One, two, three, four, five, once I caught a fish alive. / Six, seven, eight, nine, ten, then I let it go again. / Why did you let it go? Because it bit my finger so. / Which finger did it bite? This little finger on my right.","learners":"Listen and watch the actions."},{"teacher":"Say it again; invite learners to join with actions.","learners":"Say the rhyme together with actions."},{"teacher":"Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Choose a rhyme they like and lead."}]},{"activity":"Oral conversation: conversation on a picture","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.9","steps":[{"teacher":"Show the picture of a cricket match in the field.","learners":"Look carefully."},{"teacher":"Ask: What is happening in the picture? Who is doing what? What is happening around them? Then: What might happen next?","learners":"Answer in their own words; every learner gets a chance."},{"teacher":"Let learners imagine and make up a short story from the picture.","learners":"Tell their stories to the class."}]},{"activity":"Story - Day 1 (a story about a happy ending after a problem)","grouping":"Whole class (big group) then Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.10","steps":[{"teacher":"Discuss the title or picture of the story with the learners.","learners":"Talk about what they see and what the story may be about."},{"teacher":"Read the story aloud with expression and proper voice modulation. Learners should not simply repeat after you.","learners":"Listen carefully and enjoy the story."},{"teacher":"Discuss the story: factual, logical, vocabulary-based, judgment or opinion questions (today's focus: vocabulary-based: What does this word mean? Which word in the story means the same as ...?). Begin in the home language if needed.","learners":"Think and respond thoughtfully; every learner takes part."},{"teacher":"Read the story again slowly, pointing to each word. Make sure each learner has a copy and follows with a finger.","learners":"Follow each word with their finger."},{"teacher":"Ask learners to read in small groups; select a group leader who helps the others. Learners read one sentence at a time while the others point with fingers.","learners":"Read with the help of one another."}]},{"activity":"Language game: The Story Continued Slowly","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.21","steps":[{"teacher":"Say: 'Let us write a beautiful story together.' Each sentence must follow from the previous sentence. Start speaking orally first.","learners":"Listen and add one sentence each."},{"teacher":"Move to writing the story sentence by sentence; a few learners draw a picture and think of a title.","learners":"Write sentences; draw and think of a title."},{"teacher":"As learners get used to writing stories, discuss what the story will be like before writing.","learners":"Plan the story orally before writing."}]},{"activity":"Mind mapping: 'sweets'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Small group (level-wise) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.14","steps":[{"teacher":"Choose a word that can generate many related words: 'sweets'. Ask: 'What words come to your mind when you hear the word sweets?' Write the answers on the board or floor.","learners":"Say words they link with 'sweets'."},{"teacher":"Discuss the words: what they mean and how they are connected.","learners":"Explain their words and listen to others."},{"teacher":"In small groups, let the learners classify the words (Kinds: laddu, jalebi, rasgulla, pitha; Made from: milk, sugar, rice, jaggery; When we eat: festival, wedding, birthday, guests).","learners":"Sort the words into groups."},{"teacher":"Give the individual tasks by level and help each learner.","learners":"Work individually; read the work aloud at the end if time allows."}]}],"levelTasks":[{"activity":"Story - Day 1: individual tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.10","tasks":{"Beginner":"Circle or search for a favourite word or letter in the story and say it aloud. If a learner cannot draw a circle, write words on the board and ask them to identify them.","Letter":"Find, read and write favourite words from the story.","Word":"Find the consonant clusters in the story, read them and write them in the notebook.","Para":"Silently read the story from the textbook; find unfamiliar words and try to understand them; find rhyming words, use them in sentences and write in the notebook; ask other groups for meanings; make questions in groups.","Story":"Silently read the story; find unfamiliar words and rhyming words; practise reading with emotion; one group reads sentences formed with consonant clusters to the other group; ask and answer group questions (information, thinking and opinion questions)."}},{"activity":"Language game: The Story Continued Slowly - level support","source":"I","ref":"p.21","tasks":{"Beginner":"Take part by saying or pointing to the letters involved and by listening carefully; Para and Story level partners help.","Letter":"Say the letters/sounds and give simple words they know.","Word":"Say and write words and short sentences for the game.","Para":"Write sentences with the words; help groups to record answers.","Story":"Write sentences or short stories with the words; help groups to record answers."}},{"activity":"Mind mapping 'sweets': level tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.14","tasks":{"Beginner":"Circle all the words that contain the letter 'A' on the board; make a list. See how many learners find the most words.","Letter":"Circle all the words that contain the letter 'A' and make a list of them.","Word":"Use 4-5 words (for example milk, rice, laddu, pitha, sugar) to form sentences, starting with words of one or two syllables. Example: Dream - I had a dream last night.","Para":"Choose any five words from the map and create a story with them. Use consonant clusters correctly, read the story aloud, correct mistakes of sentence structure, spelling or grammar, then display it on the wall.","Story":"Choose any five words from the map and create a story with them. Use consonant clusters correctly, read the story aloud, correct mistakes of sentence structure, spelling or grammar, then display it on the wall."}}],"organisation":[{"grouping":"Whole class (big group)","how":"All learners of all levels sit in a 'U' shape arranged by level (Beginner, Letter, Word, Para, Story) so that the move to small groups is easy.","activities":["Warm-up: Rhyme - 'I caught a Fish Alive'","Oral conversation: conversation on a picture","Story (Day 1 of the story): reading aloud and discussion","Language game: The Story Continued Slowly","Mind mapping (Day 1): the word 'sweets'"]},{"grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","how":"Learners of similar levels work together; the teacher gives each group a task for its level and spends more time with learners who need support. Rotate responsibilities (for example group leader).","activities":["Story: reading in small groups","Mind mapping: classify the words"]},{"grouping":"Individual","how":"Each learner works on a task for their own level; the teacher moves around, observes difficulties and supports individuals.","activities":["Story: level-wise individual tasks","Mind mapping: level-wise individual tasks","Daily reading (10 minutes)"]}],"materials":["Rhyme chart or board (optional)","Picture card of a cricket match in the field","A story from the school library (a story about a happy ending after a problem)","a copy for each learner","Story book copies","Story book","notebooks","board","Board","chalk (or floor)","chalk","word cards (optional)","Notebooks","Library books or storybooks"],"outcomes":["Learners take part in the oral conversation and speak without fear.","Learners show understanding of the story in the discussion and complete the task for their level.","Learners respond to the sound-symbol task for today (Language game: The Story Continued Slowly) at their own level.","Learners add words to the mind map and use them in sentences or a story at their level.","Each learner reads a book for 10 minutes."],"observation":["Observe each learner's reading and writing during the individual tasks; note who needs individual support and how many learners share the same difficulty.","Note any learner whose level is improving; move the learner to the next level group when you see steady progress (manual p.5).","Record each learner's progress for the day in the notebook, according to the learner's level (manual p.4).","Use today's observations to adjust tomorrow's plan (manual p.5)."],"teacherNotes":["Story selection: the manual asks teachers to use picture story books or stories in the school library. Today's suggested theme (a story about a happy ending after a problem) is a planning suggestion; use any suitable story you have.","The manual lists the letter and word games but does not fix the slot in the daily timetable where they are used. This plan places them in the 10-minute sound-symbol / alphabet slot (interpretation).","Mind mapping topic for this day: 'sweets'. The manual's example uses the word 'shop'; today's topic follows the same method.","Pace: the manual says not to assume all learners progress at the same speed. Repeat a day's activity with the groups that need it before moving on.","Special needs: give extra time and prepare materials for slower learners; seat learners with hearing or vision difficulty at the front; for learners who reverse or confuse letters, trace letters on the letter card with a finger and write with dots to trace with a pencil (manual p.6)."],"components":[{"no":1,"key":"warmup","name":"Warm-up activities","keywords":["Rhyme - 'I caught a Fish Alive'","two learners lead"],"rows":[1]},{"no":2,"key":"oral","name":"Oral Discussion","keywords":["conversation on a picture","every learner speaks"],"rows":[2]},{"no":3,"key":"story","name":"Story","keywords":["Day 1","title / picture talk","read aloud with expression","vocabulary-based questions","re-read pointing","group reading","level tasks"],"rows":[3,4,5]},{"no":4,"key":"sound","name":"Sound symbol games, Sound separation-pairing","keywords":["The Story Continued Slowly","play in turns","level support"],"rows":[6]},{"no":5,"key":"mindwrite","name":"Mind Mapping (Day 1)","keywords":["mind map: sweets","classify the words","level task: circle letter A / sentences / story"],"rows":[7,8,9]},{"no":6,"key":"reading","name":"Daily reading","keywords":["library book","read alone","teacher listens"],"rows":[10]}],"preLesson":null},{"programme":"TARL Literacy","id":"lit-090","day":90,"phase":2,"phaseLabel":"Phase 2 (Days 46-90)","title":"Saturday: drama presentation","dayType":"Saturday drama + Self-writing","focus":"Barakhadi / alphabet and phonics chart (line 1, letter 'g') | Self-writing: the story we acted out (a story about a happy ending after a problem)","duration":70,"objectives":["Listen, speak and answer in the oral conversation (listening and storytelling).","Express a story through role play, using voice, facial expressions and gestures.","Develop sound-symbol skills: Barakhadi / alphabet and phonics chart (line 1, letter 'g').","Write about the story and review the writing.","Read independently for 10 minutes every day."],"sequence":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Singing and Spinning","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Learners sit in a circle and pass a small object while you clap with your back turned; when the clapping stops, the learner holding it sings a song, recites a poem or tells a joke. Two learners lead the warm-up today (the pair changes every day so that all learners get a chance).","learners":"Pass the object round the circle; sing, recite or tell a joke when the clapping stops.","tlm":"A small object (chalk or pencil)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","n":1},{"activity":"Oral conversation: listening and storytelling","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":10,"teacher":"Tell an interesting story starter and involve the learners: 'A little cloud fell into our courtyard. What did we do?' Let learners imagine and continue the story.","learners":"Listen to the teacher, then imagine and continue the story. Learners can also recite a rhyme or story they know.","tlm":"None","source":"M","ref":"p.9","n":2},{"activity":"Dramatic presentation: introduction and reading","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Explain what a dramatic presentation is and how it is done. Provide stories discussed during the week and read one aloud once more. Para and Story level learners support Beginner and Letter level learners in reading.","learners":"Listen, read along, then each learner chooses a character.","tlm":"Stories discussed in the week (a story about a promise kept; a story about a happy ending after a problem)","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":3},{"activity":"Dramatic presentation: planning in small groups","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":8,"teacher":"Each group discusses and plans dialogues; Para or Story level learners write the dialogues. Groups prepare their dramatic presentation.","learners":"Choose characters, plan and rehearse dialogues with facial expressions and gestures.","tlm":"Story, paper for dialogues","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":4},{"activity":"Dramatic presentation: performances and feedback","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":7,"teacher":"Learners sit in a U shape. Each group presents; after each performance, watching learners say what they enjoyed and what could be improved.","learners":"Perform in turn; watch; give feedback.","tlm":"Open space (U-shape seating)","source":"M","ref":"p.11","n":5},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart: big group reading","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":3,"teacher":"Show the Barakhadi chart and ask which letter they like. Read the letter 'g' on the chart; learners listen carefully and point to it on their own chart (they do not repeat after you).","learners":"Listen and point to the letter on their own chart.","tlm":"Barakhadi chart, alphabet or phonics chart","source":"M","ref":"p.13","n":6},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart: small-group practice","grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Learners practise reading the alphabet or phonics chart in groups and help each other. One learner per group reads aloud. Occasionally ask learners to identify the sounds of letters. Give each level its group task.","learners":"Read the chart in groups; one learner reads aloud; do the level task.","tlm":"Alphabet or phonics chart, board or floor","source":"M","ref":"p.13","n":7},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart: individual tasks","grouping":"Individual","minutes":2,"teacher":"Give each learner an individual task for their level and observe closely; assist any learner who needs individual support.","learners":"Say and write a letter or word, a sentence or a short paragraph (by level).","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.13","n":8},{"activity":"Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on the story we acted out (a story about a happy ending after a problem)","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","minutes":5,"teacher":"Start a conversation about the story used for the drama: 'the story we acted out (a story about a happy ending after a problem)'. Involve all learners with open-ended questions.","learners":"Take part in the discussion and share thoughts freely.","tlm":"Picture card or topic on the board","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":9},{"activity":"Self-writing: individual writing","grouping":"Individual","minutes":7,"teacher":"Give each level its task (see level table). Let learners take ownership of what they draw and write; mistakes are fine.","learners":"Draw and write about the topic at their level.","tlm":"Notebooks, crayons or pencils","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":10},{"activity":"Self-writing: review and reading back","grouping":"Individual","minutes":3,"teacher":"Ask each learner 'What did you draw or write?' and have them read it aloud once. Word-level learners read to the group; discuss spelling, punctuation and sentence structure. Help beginners by writing their text in the notebook for them if needed.","learners":"Read what they wrote; correct mistakes after listening to their own reading.","tlm":"Notebooks","source":"M","ref":"p.15","n":11},{"activity":"Daily reading (10 minutes)","grouping":"Individual","minutes":10,"teacher":"Give each learner a library book or any storybook. Move around, listen to individual readers and note their level.","learners":"Read independently a book of their choice.","tlm":"Library books or storybooks","source":"M","ref":"p.7","n":12}],"procedures":[{"activity":"Warm-up: Singing and Spinning","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.8","steps":[{"teacher":"Seat the learners in a circle; give a small object to one learner.","learners":"Sit in a circle."},{"teacher":"Stand outside the circle with your back to them and clap steadily; they pass the object.","learners":"Pass the object while the clapping continues."},{"teacher":"Stop clapping; the learner holding the object sings, recites or tells a joke.","learners":"Perform, and everybody claps."}]},{"activity":"Oral conversation: listening and storytelling","grouping":"Whole class (big group)","source":"M","ref":"p.9","steps":[{"teacher":"Say the starter: 'A little cloud fell into our courtyard. What did we do?'","learners":"Listen and imagine."},{"teacher":"Ask learners to continue the story one by one. Encourage those who speak less.","learners":"Add ideas to the story."},{"teacher":"Invite a learner to recite a poem or rhyme they know.","learners":"Recite and listen to others."}]},{"activity":"Saturday special: dramatic presentation","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Small group (level-wise)","source":"M","ref":"p.11","steps":[{"teacher":"Explain what a dramatic presentation is and how it can be done. Give the groups the stories discussed during the week.","learners":"Listen to the explanation."},{"teacher":"Read a story aloud once more. Learners at story and paragraph level support those at beginner and letter level in reading.","learners":"Read along; helpers support their friends."},{"teacher":"After reading, each learner chooses a character from the story.","learners":"Choose a role (boys may play girl roles and girls may play boy roles)."},{"teacher":"In groups, learners discuss and plan the dialogues; paragraph or story level learners write the dialogues.","learners":"Plan and write dialogues together."},{"teacher":"Learners sit in a U shape. Each group presents its drama. After each performance, ask what the audience enjoyed and what could be improved.","learners":"Perform, watch and give kind feedback."}]},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart activity (line 1)","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Small group (level-wise) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.13","steps":[{"teacher":"Show the Barakhadi chart and ask the learners which letter they like. Where is the letter 'g'?","learners":"Look for the letter on the chart."},{"teacher":"Read the letter 'g' on the chart. Learners listen and point to it on their own chart. Make sure they do not repeat after you.","learners":"Listen and point to the letter."},{"teacher":"Learners read the alphabet or phonics chart in their groups and help each other; one learner from each group comes forward to read aloud.","learners":"Read in groups; the representative reads aloud."},{"teacher":"Occasionally ask them to identify the sounds of letters from the chart.","learners":"Say the sound of the letter you point to."},{"teacher":"As an extra activity, write some letters on the floor, call out each letter one by one and let the learners jump onto the correct letter.","learners":"Jump onto the letter that is called."}]},{"activity":"Self-writing: 'Discussion, Writing, Self-review'","grouping":"Whole class (big group) / Individual","source":"M","ref":"p.15","steps":[{"teacher":"Start a conversation about the story used for the drama: 'the story we acted out (a story about a happy ending after a problem)'. Involve all learners with open-ended questions.","learners":"Discuss and answer questions."},{"teacher":"Give writing time at each level: draw then write (Beginner), write about what they liked (Letter), a sentence (Word), a paragraph or story on a topic of their choice (Para/Story).","learners":"Write at their level and take ownership of the work."},{"teacher":"Review: ask 'What did you draw or write?' Have each learner read the text aloud once. Support with writing if needed.","learners":"Read aloud, listen to their pronunciation and correct mistakes."}]}],"levelTasks":[{"activity":"Drama: roles by level","source":"M","ref":"p.11","tasks":{"Beginner":"Take a character role and say or act short lines with help from Para and Story level learners.","Letter":"Take a character role and say or act short lines with help from Para and Story level learners.","Word":"Take a role and speak the dialogues; help rehearse.","Para":"Write the dialogues for the group and support Beginner, Letter and Word level learners throughout.","Story":"Write the dialogues for the group and support Beginner, Letter and Word level learners throughout."}},{"activity":"Barakhadi chart: level tasks","source":"M","ref":"p.13","tasks":{"Beginner":"Small group: read the chart in the group; find and write favourite letters from the line. Individual: say and write a letter of their choice.","Letter":"Small group: read the chart; find and write favourite letters or words from any line. Individual: say a word on their own that begins with any letter.","Word":"Small group: write one or two lines of letters on the board or floor and use them to form words. Individual: speak and write sentences using words they know.","Para":"Small group: prepare word lists using the Barakhadi chart (for example items found in a shop or in the kitchen). Individual: write short paragraphs using the words formed with the Barakhadi chart.","Story":"Small group: prepare word lists using the Barakhadi chart. Individual: write short paragraphs using the words formed with the Barakhadi chart."}},{"activity":"Self-writing: level tasks and review","source":"M","ref":"p.15","tasks":{"Beginner":"Draw a picture about the discussion and then write a few sentences about it, expressing thoughts freely. Review: say what they drew or wrote; read the text aloud once; the teacher may write the text in the notebook for them.","Letter":"Write about what they liked, using drawing and writing; write any words or sentences they can. Review: read the text aloud once; correct punctuation mistakes using the Barakhadi chart.","Word":"Write a sentence based on the conversation. Mistakes in spelling, punctuation and sentence structure are fine. Review: read it to the group; discuss and correct mistakes together.","Para":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation.","Story":"Choose their own topic and write about it (a paragraph or a story). Read it once and try to correct mistakes by listening to their own pronunciation. Review: discuss the beginning, middle and end; check sequence, spelling and punctuation."}}],"organisation":[{"grouping":"Whole class (big group)","how":"All learners of all levels sit in a 'U' shape arranged by level (Beginner, Letter, Word, Para, Story) so that the move to small groups is easy.","activities":["Warm-up: Singing and Spinning","Oral conversation: listening and storytelling","Dramatic presentation: introduction and reading","Dramatic presentation: performances and feedback","Barakhadi chart: big group reading","Self-writing (Day 2): discussion on the story we acted out (a story about a happy ending after a problem)"]},{"grouping":"Small group (level-wise)","how":"Learners of similar levels work together; the teacher gives each group a task for its level and spends more time with learners who need support. Rotate responsibilities (for example group leader).","activities":["Dramatic presentation: planning in small groups","Barakhadi chart: small-group practice"]},{"grouping":"Individual","how":"Each learner works on a task for their own level; the teacher moves around, observes difficulties and supports individuals.","activities":["Barakhadi chart: individual tasks","Self-writing: individual writing","Self-writing: review and reading back","Daily reading (10 minutes)"]}],"materials":["A small object (chalk or pencil)","Stories discussed in the week (a story about a promise kept; a story about a happy ending after a problem)","Story","paper for dialogues","Open space (U-shape seating)","Barakhadi chart","alphabet or phonics chart","Alphabet or phonics chart","board or floor","Notebooks","Picture card or topic on the board","crayons or pencils","Library books or storybooks"],"outcomes":["Learners take part in the oral conversation and speak without fear.","Learners present a role in the group drama and give feedback to others.","Learners respond to the sound-symbol task for today (Barakhadi / alphabet and phonics chart (line 1, letter 'g')) at their own level.","Learners write about the story at their level and read it aloud.","Each learner reads a book for 10 minutes."],"observation":["Observe each learner's reading and writing during the individual tasks; note who needs individual support and how many learners share the same difficulty.","Note any learner whose level is improving; move the learner to the next level group when you see steady progress (manual p.5).","Record each learner's progress for the day in the notebook, according to the learner's level (manual p.4).","Use today's observations to adjust tomorrow's plan (manual p.5)."],"teacherNotes":["Saturday: this plan assumes Day 1 is a Monday (six teaching days per week). If your school week is different, hold the drama presentation on your Saturday and keep the other days in sequence.","Barakhadi: learners who need extra time should get repeated practice using one or two sound units at a time. Topic-based discussion helps oral expression, thinking and understanding.","Writing has two parts, content and sequence: encourage learners to read what they wrote, improve it and rewrite it for clarity and correctness (manual p.15).","Day 90 is the last lesson of the programme. Conduct the endline assessment next (it is not a lesson day).","Pace: the manual says not to assume all learners progress at the same speed. Repeat a day's activity with the groups that need it before moving on.","Special needs: give extra time and prepare materials for slower learners; seat learners with hearing or vision difficulty at the front; for learners who reverse or confuse letters, trace letters on the letter card with a finger and write with dots to trace with a pencil (manual p.6)."],"components":[{"no":1,"key":"warmup","name":"Warm-up activities","keywords":["Singing and Spinning","two learners lead"],"rows":[1]},{"no":2,"key":"oral","name":"Oral Discussion","keywords":["listening and storytelling","every learner speaks"],"rows":[2]},{"no":3,"key":"story","name":"Story (Saturday: dramatic presentation)","keywords":["Saturday drama","choose a character","plan dialogues","perform in U shape","feedback"],"rows":[3,4,5]},{"no":4,"key":"sound","name":"Sound symbol games, Sound separation-pairing","keywords":["Barakhadi / alphabet chart","listen and point (no repeating)","group reading","level tasks"],"rows":[6,7,8]},{"no":5,"key":"mindwrite","name":"Individual-Writing (Day 2)","keywords":["discussion","write at own level","self-review (read aloud)"],"rows":[9,10,11]},{"no":6,"key":"reading","name":"Daily reading","keywords":["library book","read alone","teacher listens"],"rows":[12]}],"preLesson":null}]};
